on de compétences","Intégration avec Claude"],"de":["Spezialisierte Arbeitsabläufe","Prozedurale Kenntnisse und Tools","IA-Kontext und Schutzmechanismen","Governance und Fähigkeitsmanagement","Integration mit Claude"],"pt":["Criação de habilidades de IA personalizadas","Melhoria da eficiência do time de engenharia","Integração com fluxos de trabalho especializados","Governança e segurança de dados","Otimização de processos de engenharia","Análise de dados e relatórios personalizados"],"ru":["Создание индивидуальных навыков ИИ","Повышение эффективности инженерной команды","Интеграция со специализированными рабочими процессами","Управление и безопасность данных","Оптимизация инженерных процессов","Анализ данных и индивидуальные отчеты"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات ذكاء اصطناعي مخصصة","تحسين كفاءة فريق الهندسة","التكامل مع سلاسل عمل مخصصة","الحوكمة وأمن البيانات","تحسين عمليات الهندسة","تحليل البيانات وتقارير مخصصة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Packmind 创建技能","AI 工程智能","工程自动化","AI 守护","工程优化","模块化技能包","Claude 能力扩展"],"ja":["Packmind スキル作成","AI エンジニアリング インテリジェンス","エンジニアリングの自動化","AI ガードレール","エンジニアリングの最適化","モジュール化スキル パッケージ","Claude の機能拡張"],"ko":["Packmind 스킬 생성","AI 엔지니어링 인텔리전스","엔지니어링 자동화","AI 가드레일","엔지니어링 최적화","모듈화 스킬 패키지","Claude 의 기능 확장"],"es":["Packmind","creación de habilidades","IA","ingeniería","flujos de trabajo","conocimientos procedimentales"," Claude","desarrollo de software","automatización"],"fr":["Packmind","création de compétences","IA","ingénierie","flux de travail","connaissances procédurales"," Claude","développement de logiciels","automatisation"],"de":["Packmind","Erstellung von Fähigkeiten","IA","Ingenieurbuch","Arbeitsabläufe","prozedurale Kenntnisse"," Claude","Softwareentwicklung","Automatisierung"],"pt":["habilidades de IA","engenharia","eficiência","produtividade","Packmind","criação de habilidades","inteligência artificial","automatização de processos","análise de dados"],"ru":["навыки ИИ","инженерия","эффективность","производительность","Packmind","создание навыков","искусственный интеллект","автоматизация процессов","анализ данных"],"ar":["مهارات ذكاء اصطناعي","هندسة","كفاءة","نتاجية","Packmind","إنشاء مهارات","ذكاء اصطناعي","آليّة العمليات","تحليل البيانات"]}},"owner":"PackmindHub","repo":"packmind","repoPath":"PackmindHub/packmind","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.405Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"packmind-create-skill","description":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.","bodyPreview":"# Create skill\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-","body":"# Create skill\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains\n2. Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats or APIs\n3. Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic\n4. Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and repetitive tasks\n\n### Anatomy of a Skill\n\nEvery skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled resources:\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter metadata (required)\n│   │   ├── name: (required)\n│   │   └── description: (required)\n│   └── Markdown instructions (required)\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/          - Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.)\n    ├── references/       - Documentation intended to be loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/           - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts, etc.)\n```\n\n#### SKILL.md (required)\n\n**Metadata Quality:** The `name` and `description` in YAML frontmatter determine when Claude will use the skill. Be specific about what the skill does and when to use it. Use the third-person (e.g. \"This skill should be used when...\" instead of \"Use this skill when...\").\n\n#### Bundled Resources (optional)\n\n##### Scripts (`scripts/`)\n\nExecutable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic reliability or are repeatedly rewritten.\n\n- **When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or deterministic reliability is needed\n- **Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks\n- **Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without loading into context\n- **Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by Claude for patching or environment-specific adjustments\n\n##### References (`references/`)\n\nDocumentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into context to inform Claude''s process and thinking.\n\n- **When to include**: For documentation that Claude should reference while working\n- **Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, `references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications\n- **Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, company policies, detailed workflow guides\n- **Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when Claude determines it''s needed\n- **Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search patterns in SKILL.md\n- **Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed information unless it''s truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean while making information discoverable without hogging the context window. Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to references files.\n\n##### Assets (`assets/`)\n\nFiles not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the output Claude produces.\n\n- **When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the final output\n- **Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography\n- **Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample documents that get copied or modified\n- **Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables Claude to use files without loading them into context\n\n### Progressive Disclosure Design Principle\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:\n\n1. **Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed by Claude (Unlimited\\*)\n\n\\*Unlimited because scripts can be executed without reading into context window.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nBefore running any skill scripts, verify that the required tools are available:\n\n### Python 3\n\nCheck if Python 3 is installed:\n\n```bash\npython3 --version\n```\n\nIf not available, install it:\n\n- **macOS**: `brew install python3`\n- **Ubuntu/Debian**: `sudo apt-get install python3`\n- **Windows**: Download from https://python.org or use `winget install Python.Python.3`\n\n### Packmind CLI\n\nCheck if packmind-cli is installed:\n\n```bash\npackmind-cli --version\n```\n\nIf not available, install it:\n\n```bash\nnpm install -g packmind-cli\n```\n\n## Skill Creation Process\n\nTo create a skill, follow the \"Skill Creation Process\" in order, skipping steps only if there is a clear reason why they are not applicable.\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples\n\nSkip this step only when the skill''s usage patterns are already clearly understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill.\n\nTo create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct user examples or generated examples that are validated with user feedback.\n\nFor example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions include:\n\n- \"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, rotating, anything else?\"\n- \"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\"\n- \"I can imagine users asking for things like ''Remove the red-eye from this image'' or ''Rotate this image''. Are there other ways you imagine this skill being used?\"\n- \"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\"\n\nTo avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed for better effectiveness.\n\nConclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the skill should support.\n\n### Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example by:\n\n1. Considering how to execute on the example from scratch\n2. Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when executing these workflows repeatedly\n\nExample: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time\n2. A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my steps,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each time\n2. An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React project files would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and relationships each time\n2. A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nTo establish the skill''s contents, analyze each concrete example to create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, and assets.\n\n### Step 3: Initializing the Skill\n\nAt this point, it is time to actually create the skill.\n\nSkip this step only if the skill being developed already exists, and iteration or packaging is needed. In this case, continue to the next step.\n\n**Before running the script**, verify that python3 and packmind-cli are available (see Prerequisites section). If not installed, install them first.\n\nWhen creating a new skill from scratch, always run the `init_skill.py` script. The script conveniently generates a new template skill directory that automatically includes everything a skill requires, making the skill creation process much more efficient and reliable.\n\nUsage:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/init_skill.py <skill-name> --path <output-directory>\n```\n\nThe script:\n\n- Creates the skill directory at the specified path\n- Generates a SKILL.md template with proper frontmatter and TODO placeholders\n- Creates example resource directories: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/`\n- Adds example files in each directory that can be customized or deleted\n\nAfter initialization, customize or remove the generated SKILL.md and example files as needed.\n\n### Step 4: Edit the Skill\n\nWhen editing the (newly-generated or existing) skill, remember that the skill is being created for another instance of Claude to use. Focus on including information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to Claude. Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable assets would help another Claude instance execute these tasks more effectively.\n\n#### Start with Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`.\n\nAlso, delete any example files and directories not needed for the skill. The initialization script creates example files in `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` to demonstrate structure, but most skills won''t need all of them.\n\n#### Update SKILL.md\n\n**Writing Style:** Write the entire skill using **imperative/infinitive form** (verb-first instructions), not second person. Use objective, instructional language (e.g., \"To accomplish X, do Y\" rather than \"You should do X\" or \"If you need to do X\"). This maintains consistency and clarity for AI consumption.\n\nTo complete SKILL.md, answer the following questions:\n\n1. What is the purpose of the skill, in a few sentences?\n2. When should the skill be used?\n3. In practice, how should Claude use the skill? All reusable skill contents developed above should be referenced so that Claude knows how to use them.\n\n### Step 5: Validating a Skill\n\nBefore distributing, validate the skill to ensure it meets all requirements.\n\n**Before running the script**, verify that python3 is available (see Prerequisites section). If not installed, install it first.\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/quick_validate.py <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nThe validation script checks:\n\n- YAML frontmatter format and required fields\n- Skill naming conventions and directory structure\n- Description completeness and quality\n\nIf validation fails, fix the reported errors and run the validation again.\n\n### Step 6: Iterate\n\nAfter testing the skill, users may request improvements. Often this happens right after using the skill, with fresh context of how the skill performed.\n\n**Iteration workflow:**\n\n1. Use the skill on real tasks\n2. Notice struggles or inefficiencies\n3. Identify how SKILL.md or bundled resources should be updated\n4. Implement changes and test again\n\n### Step 7: Distributing a Skill\n\n**After successful validation, always run the distribution command** to register the skill with Packmind. Do not skip this step.\n\n**Before running the command**, verify that packmind-cli is available (see Prerequisites section). If not installed, install it first.\n\nRun the following command with the actual skill path:\n\n```bash\npackmind-cli skills add <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nThis registers the skill with Packmind, making it available for deployment to target repositories and AI coding agents.\n\n### Step 8: Offer to Add to Package\n\nAfter successful distribution, check if the skill fits an existing package:\n\n1. Run `packmind-cli install --list` to get available packages\n2. If no packages exist, skip this step silently and end the workflow\n3. Analyze the created skill''s name and description against each package''s name and description\n4. If a package is a clear semantic fit (the skill''s domain/technology aligns with the package''s purpose):\n   - Present to user: \"This skill seems to fit the `<package-slug>` package.\"\n   - Offer three options:\n     - Add to `<package-slug>`\n     - Choose a different package\n     - Skip\n5. If no clear fit is found, skip silently (do not mention packages)\n6. If user chooses to add:\n   - Run: `packmind-cli packages add --to <package-slug> --skill <skill-slug>`\n   - Ask: \"Would you like me to run `packmind-cli install` to sync the changes?\"\n   - If yes, run: `packmind-cli install`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:12:55.305Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude, Windsurf, and AutoGPT needing to capture engineering playbooks and turn them into AI context, guardrails, and governance.","zh":"适用于 Claude、Windsurf 和 AutoGPT 等需要捕获工程规程并将其转化为 AI 上下文、护栏和治理的 AI 代理。","ja":"Claude、Windsurf、AutoGPT などのエンジニアリングのプレイブックをキャプチャし、それを AI コンテキスト、ガードレール、ガバナンスに変換する必要がある AI エージェントに最適です。","ko":"클라우드, 윈드서프, 오토지피티 等의 엔지니어링 플레이북을 캡처하여 이를 AI 컨텍스트, 가드레일, 거버넌스로 변환해야 하는 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Claude, Windsurf y AutoGPT que necesitan capturar libros de juego de ingeniería y convertirlos en contexto de IA, guardias y gobernanza.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Claude, Windsurf et AutoGPT ayant besoin de capturer les carnets de jeu d''ingénierie et de les transformer en contexte d''IA, gardes-fous et gouvernance.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Claude, Windsurf und AutoGPT, die Ingenieurbücher erfassen und in KI-Kontext, Schutzvorkehrungen und Governance umwandeln müssen.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Claude, Windsurf e AutoGPT que precisam capturar planilhas de engenharia e transformá-las em contexto de IA, guardrails e governança.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude, Windsurf и AutoGPT, которые нуждаются в захвате инженерных книг рецептов и переводе их в контекст ИИ, ограничители и управление.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكيل الذكي مثل Claude و Windsurf و AutoGPT التي تحتاج إلى التقاط كتب هندسية وتحويلها إلى سياق ذكاء اصطناعي وضبط وحوكمة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create modular, self-contained skills that provide specialized knowledge, workflows, and tools, transforming them into specialized agents equipped with procedural knowledge, utilizing guardrails and governance for effective skill creation.","zh":"赋予代理创建模块化、自包含的技能，这些技能提供专门的知识、工作流程和工具，将其转化为配备程序化知识的专门代理，利用护栏和治理进行有效的技能创建。","ja":"エージェントがモジュール化された自己完結型のスキルを作成できるようにし、専門知識、ワークフロー、ツールを提供し、ガードレールとガバナンスを使用して効果的なスキル作成を行うことで、専門知識を備えたエージェントに変換します。","ko":"에이전트가 모듈화된 자체 완결형 스킬을 생성할 수 있도록 해주어 전문 지식, 워크플로우, 툴을 제공하고, 가드레일과 거버넌스를 활용하여 효과적인 스킬 생성을 통해 전문 지식을 갖춘 에이전트로 변환합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear habilidades modulares y autocontenidas que brindan conocimientos especializados, flujos de trabajo y herramientas, transformándolos en agentes especializados equipados con conocimientos procedimentales, utilizando guardias y gobernanza para una creación de habilidades efectiva.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des compétences modulaires et autonomes qui fournissent des connaissances spécialisées, des flux de travail et des outils, les transformant en agents spécialisés équipés de connaissances procédurales, en utilisant des gardes-fous et une gouvernance pour une création de compétences efficace.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, modulare, selbstenthaltene Fähigkeiten zu erstellen, die spezialisierte Kenntnisse, Arbeitsabläufe und Werkzeuge bereitstellen, und verwandelt sie in spezialisierte Agenten, die mit prozeduralem Wissen ausgestattet sind, und verwendet Schutzvorkehrungen und Governance für eine effektive Fähigkeitsbildung.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar habilidades modulares, autossuficientes que fornecem conhecimento especializado, fluxos de trabalho e ferramentas, transformando-os em agentes especializados equipados com conhecimento procedural, utilizando guardrails e governança para criação eficaz de habilidades.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать модульные, самодостаточные навыки, которые предоставляют специализированные знания, рабочие процессы и инструменты, превращая их в специализированных агентов, оснащенных процедурными знаниями, использующих ограничители и управление для эффективного создания навыков.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إنشاء مهارات مودULAR ومتكاملة توفر معرفة متخصصة وعمليات عمل وأدوات، وتحويلها إلى وكلاء متخصصين مجهزين بالمعرفة الإجرائية، باستخدام ضبط وحوكمة لإنشاء مهارات فعالة."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating effective skills with specialized workflows","Onboarding agents with domain-specific knowledge","Extending agent capabilities with modular skill packages"],"zh":["创建具有专业工作流程的有效技能","使用领域特定知识进行代理员工入职","使用模块化技能包扩展代理功能"],"ja":["専門のワークフローを備えた有効なスキルの作成","ドメイン固有の知識を使用したエージェントのオンボーディング","モジュール化されたスキルパッケージを使用したエージェント機能の拡張"],"ko":["전문 워크플로우를 갖춘 유효한 스킬 생성","도메인 특정 지식을 사용한 에이전트 온보딩","모듈화된 스킬 패키지를 사용한 에이전트 기능 확장"],"es":["Creación de habilidades efectivas con flujos de trabajo especializados","Integración de agentes con conocimientos específicos del dominio","Ampliación de las capacidades de los agentes con paquetes de habilidades modulares"],"fr":["Création de compétences efficaces avec des flux de travail spécialisés","Intégration d''agents avec des connaissances spécifiques au domaine","Élargissement des capacités des agents avec des packages de compétences modulaires"],"de":["Erstellung effektiver Fähigkeiten mit spezialisierten Arbeitsabläufen","Einbindung von Agenten mit domänen-spezifischem Wissen","Erweiterung der Fähigkeiten von Agenten mit modularen Fähigkeitspaketen"],"pt":["Criar habilidades eficazes com fluxos de trabalho especializados","Integrar agentes com conhecimento específico de domínio","Ampliar as capacidades dos agentes com pacotes de habilidades modulares"],"ru":["Создание эффективных навыков со специализированными рабочими процессами","Внедрение агентов с доменно-специфическими знаниями","Расширение возможностей агентов с помощью модульных пакетов навыков"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات فعالة مع عمليات عمل متخصصة","توفير وكلاء مع معرفة محددة للنطاق","توسيع قدرات الوكلاء مع حزمة مهارات مودULAR"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires engineering playbook capture","Claude or similar agent architecture needed"],"zh":["需要捕获工程规程","需要 Claude 或类似的代理架构"],"ja":["エンジニアリングのプレイブックのキャプチャが必要","Claude または同等のエージェントアーキテクチャが必要"],"ko":["엔지니어링 플레이북 캡처 필요","클라우드 또는 유사한 에이전트 아키텍처 필요"],"es":["Requiere captura de libro de juego de ingeniería","Se requiere arquitectura de agente Claude o similar"],"fr":["Nécessite la capture de carnets de jeu d''ingénierie","Nécessite une architecture d''agent Claude ou similaire"],"de":["Erfordert Erfassung von Ingenieurbüchern","Benötigt Claude- oder ähnliche Agenten-Architektur"],"pt":["Exige a captura de planilhas de engenharia","Arquitetura de agente Claude ou semelhante é necessária"],"ru":["Требуется захват инженерных книг рецептов","Требуется архитектура агента Claude или аналогичная"],"ar":["يتطلب التقاط كتب هندسية","هندسة وكيل Claude أو مشابهة مطلوبة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('kungfuai/CVlization/remote-run-ssh', 'community', 'kungfuai', 'CVlization', 'kungfuai/CVlization', 'remote-run-ssh', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.405Z', '2026-02-18T03:12:39.827Z', NULL, '{"id":"kungfuai/CVlization/remote-run-ssh","name":"remote-run-ssh","description":{"zh":"远程运行CV任务，支持CUDA加速，适用于大规模深度学习训练和评估","ja":"CVタスクをリモート実行し、CUDAアクセラレーションをサポートし、大規模な深層学習のトレーニングと評価に適しています","ko":"CV 태스크를 원격 실행하고 CUDA 가속을 지원하여 대규모 深層學習 학습과 평가에 적합","es":"El skill ''remote-run-ssh'' permite ejecutar modelos de visión y lenguaje de forma remota sobre SSH para entrenamientos intensivos y evaluaciones","fr":"Le skill ''remote-run-ssh'' permet d''exécuter des modèles de vision et de langage à distance sur SSH pour des entraînements et des évaluations intensifs","de":"Das Skill ''remote-run-ssh'' ermöglicht die Ausführung von Vision- und Sprachmodellen remote über SSH für intensive Trainings und Evaluierungen","pt":"O remote-run-ssh permite a execução de workflows práticos para treinamento de modelos de visão e linguagem em ambientes de GPU remotos","ru":"Remote-run-ssh позволяет выполнять практические рабочие процессы для обучения моделей компьютерного зрения и языка в удаленных средах GPU","ar":"يسمح remote-run-ssh بتنفيذ سلاسل عمل عملية لتدريب نماذج الرؤية واللغة في بيئات GPU عن بعد","en":"Practical workflows for using and training vision and language models."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"SSH远程运行CV任务","ja":"SSHリモートランCVタスク","ko":"SSH 원격 실행 CV 태스크","es":"Ejecución remota sobre SSH para modelos de visión y lenguaje","fr":"Exécution à distance sur SSH pour les modèles de vision e...","de":"Remote-Ausführung über SSH für Vision- und Sprachmodelle","pt":"Execução Remota SSH para Treinamento de Modelos","ru":"Удаленный запуск SSH для обучения моделей","ar":"تشغيل بعيد عبر SSH لتدريب النماذج","en":"remote-run-ssh"},"description":{"zh":"远程运行CV任务，支持CUDA加速，适用于大规模深度学习训练和评估","ja":"CVタスクをリモート実行し、CUDAアクセラレーションをサポートし、大規模な深層学習のトレーニングと評価に適しています","ko":"CV 태스크를 원격 실행하고 CUDA 가속을 지원하여 대규모 深層學習 학습과 평가에 적합","es":"El skill ''remote-run-ssh'' permite ejecutar modelos de visión y lenguaje de forma remota sobre SSH para entrenamientos intensivos y evaluaciones","fr":"Le skill ''remote-run-ssh'' permet d''exécuter des modèles de vision et de langage à distance sur SSH pour des entraînements et des évaluations intensifs","de":"Das Skill ''remote-run-ssh'' ermöglicht die Ausführung von Vision- und Sprachmodellen remote über SSH für intensive Trainings und Evaluierungen","pt":"O remote-run-ssh permite a execução de workflows práticos para treinamento de modelos de visão e linguagem em ambientes de GPU remotos","ru":"Remote-run-ssh позволяет выполнять практические рабочие процессы для обучения моделей компьютерного зрения и языка в удаленных средах GPU","ar":"يسمح remote-run-ssh بتنفيذ سلاسل عمل عملية لتدريب نماذج الرؤية واللغة في بيئات GPU عن بعد","en":"Practical workflows for using and training vision and language models."},"definition":{"en":"Practical workflows for using and training vision and language models."},"features":{"zh":["支持CUDA加速","远程运行CV任务","大规模深度学习训练和评估","SSH连接","简化的远程运行流程"],"ja":["CUDAアクセラレーションのサポート","CVタスクのリモート実行","大規模な深層学習のトレーニングと評価","SSH接続","簡素化されたリモート実行プロセス"],"ko":["CUDA 가속 지원","CV 태스크 원격 실행","대규모 深層學習 학습과 평가","SSH 연결","원격 실행 프로세스 단순화"],"es":["Ejecución remota de modelos de visión y lenguaje","Soporte para entrenamientos intensivos y evaluaciones","Uso de Docker para la ejecución de modelos","Compatibilidad con servidores remotos","Flexibilidad para configurar y personalizar la ejecución"],"fr":["Exécution à distance de modèles de vision et de langage","Prise en charge des entraînements et des évaluations intensifs","Utilisation de Docker pour l''exécution des modèles","Compatibilité avec les serveurs distants","Flexibilité pour configurer et personnaliser l''exécution"],"de":["Remote-Ausführung von Vision- und Sprachmodellen","Unterstützung für intensive Trainings und Evaluierungen","Verwendung von Docker für die Ausführung von Modellen","Kompatibilität mit Remote-Servern","Flexibilität zur Konfiguration und Anpassung der Ausführung"],"pt":["Execução de treinamentos de modelos em ambientes de GPU remotos","Utilização de Docker para helper de build e treinamento","Manutenção de uma cópia minimal do repositório remoto","Suporte a CUDA para treinamentos intensivos","Integração com bibliotecas de visão e linguagem"],"ru":["Выполнение обучения моделей в удаленных средах GPU","Использование Docker для помощи в сборке и обучении","Сохранение минимальной копии удаленного репозитория","Поддержка CUDA для интенсивных обучений","Интеграция с библиотеками компьютерного зрения и языка"],"ar":["تشغيل تدريبات النماذج في بيئات GPU عن بعد","استخدام Docker لمساعدة في بناء وتدريب","الحفاظ على نسخة mínima من المستودع البعيد","دعم CUDA لتدريبات مكثفة","التكامل مع مكتبات الرؤية واللغة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["SSH远程运行","CV任务","CUDA加速","深度学习训练","评估","计算机视觉","远程服务器"],"ja":["SSHリモートラン","CVタスク","CUDAアクセラレーション","深層学習トレーニング","評価","コンピュータビジョン","リモートサーバー"],"ko":["SSH 원격 실행","CV 태스크","CUDA 가속","深層學習 학습","평가","컴퓨터 비전","원격 서버"],"es":["ejecución remota","SSH","modelos de visión","modelos de lenguaje","entrenamientos intensivos","evaluaciones","Docker","servidores remotos"],"fr":["exécution à distance","SSH","modèles de vision","modèles de langage","entraînements intensifs","évaluations","Docker","serveurs distants"],"de":["Remote-Ausführung","SSH","Vision-Modelle","Sprachmodelle","intensive Trainings","Evaluierungen","Docker","Remote-Server"],"pt":["remote-run-ssh","treinamento de modelos","GPU remoto","Docker","CUDA","visão computacional","linguagem natural","desenvolvimento de machine learning"],"ru":["remote-run-ssh","обучение моделей","удаленный GPU","Docker","CUDA","компьютерное зрение","естественный язык","разработка машинного обучения"],"ar":["remote-run-ssh","تدريب النماذج","GPU عن بعد","Docker","CUDA","رؤية حاسوبية","لغة طبيعية","تطوير تعلم الآلة"]}},"owner":"kungfuai","repo":"CVlization","repoPath":"kungfuai/CVlization","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.405Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"remote-run-ssh","description":"Run CVlization examples on the `ssh l1` GPU host by copying only the needed example directory plus the shared `cvlization/` package into `/tmp`, then launching the example’s Docker scripts.","bodyPreview":"# Remote Run over SSH\n\nOperate CVlization examples on the remote GPU reachable as `ssh l1`. This playbook keeps the remote copy minimal—just the target example folder (e.g., `examples/perception/multimodal_multitask/recipe_analysis_torch`) and the `cvlization/` library—then relies on the example’s own `build.sh` / `train.sh` Docker helpers. The user’s long-lived checkout on the remote stays untouched.\n\n## When to Use\n- Heavy trainings or evaluations that require CUDA (CIFAR10 speed runs, multimo","body":"# Remote Run over SSH\n\nOperate CVlization examples on the remote GPU reachable as `ssh l1`. This playbook keeps the remote copy minimal—just the target example folder (e.g., `examples/perception/multimodal_multitask/recipe_analysis_torch`) and the `cvlization/` library—then relies on the example’s own `build.sh` / `train.sh` Docker helpers. The user’s long-lived checkout on the remote stays untouched.\n\n## When to Use\n- Heavy trainings or evaluations that require CUDA (CIFAR10 speed runs, multimodal pipelines, etc.).\n- Performance or regression measurements on the remote GPU after local code changes.\n- Producing reproducible logs / artifacts for discussions or CI baselines without pushing a branch first.\n\n## Prerequisites\n- Local repo state ready to sync (uncommitted changes acceptable).\n- SSH config already maps the GPU machine to `l1`.\n- Remote host provides NVIDIA GPU (currently A10) and Docker with GPU runtime enabled.\n- At least ~15 GB free under `/tmp` for the slim workspace, Docker context, and caches.\n- Hugging Face tokens or other creds available locally if the example pulls hub assets.\n\n## Quick Reference\n1. Choose the example to run.\n2. `rsync` only the example folder, `cvlization/`, and any required helper dirs to `/tmp/cvlization_remote` on `l1`.\n3. On `l1`, run `./build.sh` inside the example folder to build the Docker image.\n4. Run `./train.sh` (or the example’s equivalent) to launch the job with GPU access.\n5. Collect logs / metrics and record the run in `var/skills/remote-run-ssh/runs/<timestamp>/log.md`.\n\n## Detailed Procedure\n\n### 1. Identify the example and supporting files\n- Note the example path relative to repo root (e.g., `examples/perception/multimodal_multitask/recipe_analysis_torch`).\n- List any extra assets the run needs (custom configs under `examples`, top-level scripts, environment files, etc.).\n- Confirm `cvlization/` includes all library modules the example imports.\n\n### 2. Sync minimal workspace to `/tmp`\n```bash\nREMOTE_ROOT=/tmp/cvlization_remote\nrsync -az --delete \\\n  --include=''cvlization/***'' \\\n  --include=''examples/***'' \\\n  --include=''scripts/***'' \\\n  --include=''pyproject.toml'' \\\n  --include=''setup.cfg'' \\\n  --include=''README.md'' \\\n  --exclude=''*'' \\\n  ./ l1:${REMOTE_ROOT}/\n```\nTips:\n- Adjust the include list if the example needs additional files (e.g., `docker-compose.yml`, `requirements.txt`). The blanket `--exclude=''*''` prevents unrelated directories from syncing.\n- Keep the remote path structure (`${REMOTE_ROOT}/examples/...`) aligned with the local repo so relative paths like `../../../..` used inside scripts still resolve to the repo root.\n- Avoid syncing `.git`, local datasets, `.venv`, or heavy cache directories.\n\n### 3. Build the example image\n```bash\nssh l1 ''cd /tmp/cvlization_remote/examples/perception/multimodal_multitask/recipe_analysis_torch && ./build.sh''\n```\n- The Docker build context is limited to the example folder, keeping builds quick.\n- Edit `build.sh` locally if you need custom base images or dependency tweaks before re-syncing.\n\n### 4. Confirm GPU availability\n```bash\nssh l1 ''nvidia-smi''\n```\nEnsure no conflicting jobs are consuming the GPU before starting a long run.\n\n### 5. Run the training script (Docker)\n```bash\nssh l1 ''cd /tmp/cvlization_remote/examples/perception/multimodal_multitask/recipe_analysis_torch && ./train.sh > run.log 2>&1''\n```\n- Tail logs while the job runs:\n```bash\nssh l1 ''tail -f /tmp/cvlization_remote/examples/perception/multimodal_multitask/recipe_analysis_torch/run.log''\n```\n- `train.sh` already mounts the example directory at `/workspace`, mounts the synced repo root read-only at `/cvlization_repo`, and sets `PYTHONPATH=/cvlization_repo`.\n- Customize environment variables or extra mounts by editing `train.sh` locally (e.g., injecting dataset paths, WANDB keys) then re-syncing.\n- If an example lacks Docker scripts, fall back to running its entrypoint directly (`python train.py`) inside the container or a temporary venv—but document the deviation in the run log.\n\n### 6. Capture metrics\nLog files should include per-epoch summaries and final metrics. Record:\n- Wall-clock time / throughput.\n- Accuracy, loss, or other task metrics.\n- Warnings or notable log lines (e.g., retry downloads, CUDA warnings).\n\n### 7. Retrieve artifacts (optional)\n```bash\nrsync -az l1:/tmp/cvlization_remote/examples/perception/multimodal_multitask/recipe_analysis_torch/run.log \\\n  ./remote_runs/$(date +%Y%m%dT%H%M%S)_multimodal.log\n```\nCopy checkpoints, TensorBoard logs, or generated samples in the same manner if needed.\n\n### 8. Document the run\n- Create `var/skills/remote-run-ssh/runs/<timestamp>/log.md` summarizing:\n  - Example path, git commit or diff basis.\n  - Commands executed (`build.sh`, `train.sh` args).\n  - Key metrics / observations.\n  - Location of logs or artifacts (local paths or remote references).\n\n### 9. Cleanup (optional)\n- Delete `/tmp/cvlization_remote` when finished if the disk budget is tight (`ssh l1 ''rm -rf /tmp/cvlization_remote''`).\n- Clear cached datasets (`rm -rf /root/.cache/...` inside Docker) only if future runs should start fresh.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n- **Missing module inside container**: Ensure `train.sh` mounts the repo root and sets `PYTHONPATH`. Re-run `rsync` if files were added after the initial sync.\n- **Docker build fails**: Inspect the output of `./build.sh`. Some examples assume base images with CUDA toolkits—update the Dockerfile accordingly.\n- **CUDA OOM**: Reduce batch sizes or precision, or run one job at a time on `l1`.\n- **No GPU detected**: Confirm `--gpus=all` is present in `train.sh` and check `nvidia-smi` on the host.\n- **Long sync times**: Tighten the rsync include rules to the specific example and library folders required.\n\n## Outputs\nEvery run should leave:\n- Remote workspace at `/tmp/cvlization_remote` containing the synced example + library.\n- Local or remote logs with the captured metrics.\n- A run log under `var/skills/remote-run-ssh/runs/<timestamp>/log.md` documenting the session.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:12:39.827Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Cursor or AutoGPT needing to leverage remote GPU resources for heavy vision and language model training over SSH.","zh":"适用于像 Cursor 或 AutoGPT 这样的 AI 代理，它们需要利用远程 GPU 资源进行重度视觉和语言模型训练，通过 SSH 进行。","ja":"Cursor または AutoGPT のような AI エージェントに最適であり、SSH を介して遠距離の GPU リソースを利用して重度のビジョンと言語モデルをトレーニングする必要があります。","ko":"Cursor 또는 AutoGPT와 같은 AI 에이전트에 적합하며, SSH를 통해 원격 GPU 리소스를 활용하여 무거운 비전 및 언어 모델 훈련이 필요한 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Cursor o AutoGPT que necesitan aprovechar recursos de GPU remotos para entrenamiento intensivo de visión y lenguaje a través de SSH.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''IA comme Cursor ou AutoGPT ayant besoin d''utiliser des ressources de GPU distantes pour un entraînement intensif de vision et de langage via SSH.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Cursor oder AutoGPT, die Remote-GPU-Ressourcen für intensives Training von Bild- und Sprachmodellen über SSH nutzen müssen.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Cursor ou AutoGPT que precisam utilizar recursos de GPU remotos para treinamento pesado de visão e modelo de linguagem via SSH.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Cursor или AutoGPT, которым необходимо использовать удаленные ресурсы GPU для тяжелой тренировки моделей зрения и языка по SSH.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Cursor أو AutoGPT الذي يحتاج إلى استخدام موارد GPU عن بُعد للتدريب الثقيل لنماذج الرؤية واللغة عبر SSH."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to operate CVlization examples on remote GPUs via SSH, utilizing Docker helpers for efficient model training and evaluation with CUDA, specifically for tasks like CIFAR10 speed runs and multimodal multitask recipe analysis.","zh":"赋予代理在远程 GPU 上通过 SSH 运行 CVlization 示例的能力，利用 Docker 辅助工具实现高效的模型训练和评估，特别是使用 CUDA，用于任务如 CIFAR10 速度运行和多模态多任务食谱分析。","ja":"エージェントに、SSH 経由でリモート GPU 上で CVlization の例を実行する能力を与え、Docker ヘルパーを使用して CUDA を使用したモデル トレーニングと評価を効率的に実行することを可能にし、特に CIFAR10 の速度実行や多モーダル マルチタスク レシピ分析などのタスクで。","ko":"에이전트가 원격 GPU에서 SSH를 통해 CVlization 예제를 실행할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, Docker 헬퍼를 사용하여 CUDA와 함께 모델 훈련과 평가를 효율적으로 수행할 수 있으며, 특히 CIFAR10 속도 실행 및 다중 모드 다중 작업 레시피 분석과 같은 작업에 적합합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes operar ejemplos de CVlization en GPUs remotas a través de SSH, utilizando ayudantes de Docker para un entrenamiento y evaluación eficientes de modelos con CUDA, específicamente para tareas como pruebas de velocidad CIFAR10 y análisis de recetas multimodales y multitasque.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exploiter des exemples de CVlization sur des GPU distantes via SSH, en utilisant des aides Docker pour un entraînement et une évaluation efficaces de modèles avec CUDA, spécifiquement pour des tâches comme des courses de vitesse CIFAR10 et une analyse de recettes multimodales et multitasque.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, CVlization-Beispiele auf Remote-GPUs über SSH zu betreiben, indem Docker-Helfer für effizientes Modelltraining und -bewertung mit CUDA verwendet werden, insbesondere für Aufgaben wie CIFAR10-Geschwindigkeitstests und multimodale Multitask-Rezeptanalyse.","pt":"Habilita agentes a operar exemplos de CVlization em GPUs remotas via SSH, utilizando ajudantes do Docker para treinamento e avaliação de modelos eficientes com CUDA, especificamente para tarefas como execuções de velocidade CIFAR10 e análise de receitas multimodais multitarefa.","ru":"Позволяет агентам работать с примерами CVlization на удаленных GPU по SSH, используя помощников Docker для эффективной тренировки и оценки моделей с CUDA, в частности для задач, таких как запуски скорости CIFAR10 и анализ рецептов multimodal multitask.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تشغيل أمثلة CVlization على وحدات معالجة الرسومات عن بُعد عبر SSH، باستخدام مساعد Docker لتدريب نموذج كفء وتقييمه باستخدام CUDA، بشكل خاص لمهام مثل تشغيل سرعة CIFAR10 وتحليل وصفات متعددة المهام."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating heavy model trainings on remote GPUs","Evaluating vision models like multimodal multitask recipe analysis","Deploying language models on remote servers with CUDA support"],"zh":["在远程 GPU 上自动执行重度模型训练","评估像多模态多任务食谱分析这样的视觉模型","在支持 CUDA 的远程服务器上部署语言模型"],"ja":["リモート GPU 上での重度モデル トレーニングの自動化","多モーダル マルチタスク レシピ分析のようなビジョン モデルを評価する","CUDA 対応のリモート サーバー上に言語モデルを展開する"],"ko":["원격 GPU에서 무거운 모델 훈련 자동화","다중 모드 다중 작업 레시피 분석과 같은 비전 모델 평가","CUDA 지원 원격 서버에 언어 모델 배포"],"es":["Automatizar entrenamientos de modelos pesados en GPUs remotas","Evaluar modelos de visión como análisis de recetas multimodales y multitasque","Implementar modelos de lenguaje en servidores remotos con soporte CUDA"],"fr":["Automatiser les entraînements de modèles lourds sur des GPU distantes","Évaluer les modèles de vision comme l''analyse de recettes multimodales et multitasque","Déployer des modèles de langage sur des serveurs distants avec prise en charge CUDA"],"de":["Automatisierung von schweren Modelltrainings auf Remote-GPUs","Auswertung von Bildmodellen wie multimodale Multitask-Rezeptanalyse","Bereitstellung von Sprachmodellen auf Remote-Servern mit CUDA-Unterstützung"],"pt":["Automatizar treinamentos de modelos pesados em GPUs remotas","Avaliar modelos de visão como análise de receitas multimodais multitarefa","Implantar modelos de linguagem em servidores remotos com suporte a CUDA"],"ru":["Автоматизировать тяжелую тренировку моделей на удаленных GPU","Оценить модели зрения, такие как анализ рецептов multimodal multitask","Развернуть модели языка на удаленных серверах с поддержкой CUDA"],"ar":["أتمتة تدريب النماذج الثقيلة على وحدات معالجة الرسومات عن بُعد","تقييم نماذج الرؤية مثل تحليل وصفات متعددة المهام","نشر نماذج اللغة على الخواديم عن بُعد مع دعم CUDA"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires SSH access to a remote GPU-enabled machine","Dependent on Docker for containerization","Limited to CVlization examples and library"],"zh":["需要远程 GPU 机器的 SSH 访问","依赖 Docker 进行容器化","仅限 CVlization 示例和库"],"ja":["リモート GPU マシンの SSH アクセスが必要","コンテナ化のために Docker への依存","CVlization の例とライブラリに限定"],"ko":["원격 GPU 머신의 SSH 접근이 필요","컨테이너화에 대한 Docker 의존","CVlization 예제 및 라이브러리에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere acceso SSH a una máquina con GPU remota","Dependiente de Docker para la contenerización","Limitado a ejemplos y bibliotecas de CVlization"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès SSH à une machine avec GPU distante","Dépend de Docker pour la conteneurisation","Limité aux exemples et bibliothèques de CVlization"],"de":["Benötigt SSH-Zugriff auf eine Remote-GPU-Maschine","Abhängig von Docker für die Containerisierung","Begrenzt auf CVlization-Beispiele und -Bibliotheken"],"pt":["Exige acesso SSH a uma máquina com GPU habilitada remotamente","Depende do Docker para contenerização","Limitado a exemplos e biblioteca de CVlization"],"ru":["Требует доступа SSH к удаленной машине с включенным GPU","Зависит от Docker для контейнеризации","Ограничен примерами и библиотекой CVlization"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى SSH إلى جهاز معزز GPU عن بُعد","يعتمد على Docker لتحذیر الحاويات","محدود بأمثلة ومكتبة CVlization"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
