боснованных решений","Разработка навыков критического мышления","Применение шаблонов разработки","Использование инструментов разработки на Python"],"ar":["مبادئ تطوير بايثون","اتخاذ قرارات مدروسة","تطوير مهارات التفكير النقدي","تطبيق أنماط التطوير","استخدام أدوات تطوير بايثون"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Python 设计模式","Python 开发原则","代码质量","可维护性","决策","异步编程","同步编程","框架"],"ja":["Python パターン","Python 開発原則","コード品質","メンテナンス性","決定","异步プログラミング","同期プログラミング","フレームワーク"],"ko":["파이썬 패턴","파이썬 개발 원칙","코드 품질","유지 보수성","결정","비동기 프로그래밍","동기 프로그래밍","프레임워크"],"es":["patrones de python","desarrollo de software","principios de diseño","toma de decisiones","frameworks de python","programación asíncrona","programación síncrona","contexto de programación"],"fr":["modèles python","développement de logiciels","principes de conception","prise de décision","frameworks python","programmation asynchrone","programmation synchrone","contexte de programmation"],"de":["python-muster","softwareentwicklung","entwurfsprinzipien","entscheidungsfindung","python-frameworks","asynchrone programmierung","synchrone programmierung","programmierkontext"],"pt":["desenvolvimento python","padrões python","princípios de desenvolvimento","tomada de decisões","pensamento crítico","ferramentas de desenvolvimento python"],"ru":["разработка на python","шаблоны python","принципы разработки","принятие решений","критическое мышление","инструменты разработки на python"],"ar":["تطوير بايثون","نماذج بايثون","مبادئ التطوير","اتخاذ القرارات","التفكير النقدي","أدوات تطوير بايثون"]}},"owner":"darthlinuxer","repo":"Agentic-Skills","repoPath":"darthlinuxer/Agentic-Skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.405Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"python-patterns","description":"Python development principles and decision-making. Framework selection,","bodyPreview":"# Python Patterns\n\n> **💡 MCP Tool Available**: Use **Context7**, **Tavily**, **BraveSearch**, or **Serper.dev** first; only if those fail, use **WebSearch** or **WebFetch** as needed.\n\n> Python development principles and decision-making for 2025.\n> **Learn to THINK, not memorize patterns.**\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ How to Use This Skill\n\nThis skill teaches **decision-making principles**, not fixed code to copy.\n\n- ASK user for framework preference when unclear\n- Choose async vs sync based on CONTEXT\n- Don''t","body":"# Python Patterns\n\n> **💡 MCP Tool Available**: Use **Context7**, **Tavily**, **BraveSearch**, or **Serper.dev** first; only if those fail, use **WebSearch** or **WebFetch** as needed.\n\n> Python development principles and decision-making for 2025.\n> **Learn to THINK, not memorize patterns.**\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ How to Use This Skill\n\nThis skill teaches **decision-making principles**, not fixed code to copy.\n\n- ASK user for framework preference when unclear\n- Choose async vs sync based on CONTEXT\n- Don''t default to same framework every time\n\n---\n\n## 1. Framework Selection (2025)\n\n### Decision Tree\n\n```\nWhat are you building?\n│\n├── API-first / Microservices\n│   └── FastAPI (async, modern, fast)\n│\n├── Full-stack web / CMS / Admin\n│   └── Django (batteries-included)\n│\n├── Simple / Script / Learning\n│   └── Flask (minimal, flexible)\n│\n├── AI/ML API serving\n│   └── FastAPI (Pydantic, async, uvicorn)\n│\n└── Background workers\n    └── Celery + any framework\n```\n\n### Comparison Principles\n\n| Factor | FastAPI | Django | Flask |\n|--------|---------|--------|-------|\n| **Best for** | APIs, microservices | Full-stack, CMS | Simple, learning |\n| **Async** | Native | Django 5.0+ | Via extensions |\n| **Admin** | Manual | Built-in | Via extensions |\n| **ORM** | Choose your own | Django ORM | Choose your own |\n| **Learning curve** | Low | Medium | Low |\n\n### Selection Questions to Ask:\n1. Is this API-only or full-stack?\n2. Need admin interface?\n3. Team familiar with async?\n4. Existing infrastructure?\n\n---\n\n## 2. Async vs Sync Decision\n\n### When to Use Async\n\n```\nasync def is better when:\n├── I/O-bound operations (database, HTTP, file)\n├── Many concurrent connections\n├── Real-time features\n├── Microservices communication\n└── FastAPI/Starlette/Django ASGI\n\ndef (sync) is better when:\n├── CPU-bound operations\n├── Simple scripts\n├── Legacy codebase\n├── Team unfamiliar with async\n└── Blocking libraries (no async version)\n```\n\n### The Golden Rule\n\n```\nI/O-bound → async (waiting for external)\nCPU-bound → sync + multiprocessing (computing)\n\nDon''t:\n├── Mix sync and async carelessly\n├── Use sync libraries in async code\n└── Force async for CPU work\n```\n\n### Async Library Selection\n\n| Need | Async Library |\n|------|---------------|\n| HTTP client | httpx |\n| PostgreSQL | asyncpg |\n| Redis | aioredis / redis-py async |\n| File I/O | aiofiles |\n| Database ORM | SQLAlchemy 2.0 async, Tortoise |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Type Hints Strategy\n\n### When to Type\n\n```\nAlways type:\n├── Function parameters\n├── Return types\n├── Class attributes\n├── Public APIs\n\nCan skip:\n├── Local variables (let inference work)\n├── One-off scripts\n├── Tests (usually)\n```\n\n### Common Type Patterns\n\n```python\n\n# These are patterns, understand them:\n\n# Optional → might be None\nfrom typing import Optional\ndef find_user(id: int) -> Optional[User]: ...\n\n# Union → one of multiple types\ndef process(data: str | dict) -> None: ...\n\n# Generic collections\ndef get_items() -> list[Item]: ...\ndef get_mapping() -> dict[str, int]: ...\n\n# Callable\nfrom typing import Callable\ndef apply(fn: Callable[[int], str]) -> str: ...\n```\n\n### Pydantic for Validation\n\n```\nWhen to use Pydantic:\n├── API request/response models\n├── Configuration/settings\n├── Data validation\n├── Serialization\n\nBenefits:\n├── Runtime validation\n├── Auto-generated JSON schema\n├── Works with FastAPI natively\n└── Clear error messages\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Project Structure Principles\n\n### Structure Selection\n\n```\nSmall project / Script:\n├── main.py\n├── utils.py\n└── requirements.txt\n\nMedium API:\n├── app/\n│   ├── __init__.py\n│   ├── main.py\n│   ├── models/\n│   ├── routes/\n│   ├── services/\n│   └── schemas/\n├── tests/\n└── pyproject.toml\n\nLarge application:\n├── src/\n│   └── myapp/\n│       ├── core/\n│       ├── api/\n│       ├── services/\n│       ├── models/\n│       └── ...\n├── tests/\n└── pyproject.toml\n```\n\n### FastAPI Structure Principles\n\n```\nOrganize by feature or layer:\n\nBy layer:\n├── routes/ (API endpoints)\n├── services/ (business logic)\n├── models/ (database models)\n├── schemas/ (Pydantic models)\n└── dependencies/ (shared deps)\n\nBy feature:\n├── users/\n│   ├── routes.py\n│   ├── service.py\n│   └── schemas.py\n└── products/\n    └── ...\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Django Principles (2025)\n\n### Django Async (Django 5.0+)\n\n```\nDjango supports async:\n├── Async views\n├── Async middleware\n├── Async ORM (limited)\n└── ASGI deployment\n\nWhen to use async in Django:\n├── External API calls\n├── WebSocket (Channels)\n├── High-concurrency views\n└── Background task triggering\n```\n\n### Django Best Practices\n\n```\nModel design:\n├── Fat models, thin views\n├── Use managers for common queries\n├── Abstract base classes for shared fields\n\nViews:\n├── Class-based for complex CRUD\n├── Function-based for simple endpoints\n├── Use viewsets with DRF\n\nQueries:\n├── select_related() for FKs\n├── prefetch_related() for M2M\n├── Avoid N+1 queries\n└── Use .only() for specific fields\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. FastAPI Principles\n\n### async def vs def in FastAPI\n\n```\nUse async def when:\n├── Using async database drivers\n├── Making async HTTP calls\n├── I/O-bound operations\n└── Want to handle concurrency\n\nUse def when:\n├── Blocking operations\n├── Sync database drivers\n├── CPU-bound work\n└── FastAPI runs in threadpool automatically\n```\n\n### Dependency Injection\n\n```\nUse dependencies for:\n├── Database sessions\n├── Current user / Auth\n├── Configuration\n├── Shared resources\n\nBenefits:\n├── Testability (mock dependencies)\n├── Clean separation\n├── Automatic cleanup (yield)\n```\n\n### Pydantic v2 Integration\n\n```python\n\n# FastAPI + Pydantic are tightly integrated:\n\n# Request validation\n@app.post(\"/users\")\nasync def create(user: UserCreate) -> UserResponse:\n    # user is already validated\n    ...\n\n# Response serialization\n\n# Return type becomes response schema\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Background Tasks\n\n### Selection Guide\n\n| Solution | Best For |\n|----------|----------|\n| **BackgroundTasks** | Simple, in-process tasks |\n| **Celery** | Distributed, complex workflows |\n| **ARQ** | Async, Redis-based |\n| **RQ** | Simple Redis queue |\n| **Dramatiq** | Actor-based, simpler than Celery |\n\n### When to Use Each\n\n```\nFastAPI BackgroundTasks:\n├── Quick operations\n├── No persistence needed\n├── Fire-and-forget\n└── Same process\n\nCelery/ARQ:\n├── Long-running tasks\n├── Need retry logic\n├── Distributed workers\n├── Persistent queue\n└── Complex workflows\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Error Handling Principles\n\n### Exception Strategy\n\n```\nIn FastAPI:\n├── Create custom exception classes\n├── Register exception handlers\n├── Return consistent error format\n└── Log without exposing internals\n\nPattern:\n├── Raise domain exceptions in services\n├── Catch and transform in handlers\n└── Client gets clean error response\n```\n\n### Error Response Philosophy\n\n```\nInclude:\n├── Error code (programmatic)\n├── Message (human readable)\n├── Details (field-level when applicable)\n└── NOT stack traces (security)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. Testing Principles\n\n### Testing Strategy\n\n| Type | Purpose | Tools |\n|------|---------|-------|\n| **Unit** | Business logic | pytest |\n| **Integration** | API endpoints | pytest + httpx/TestClient |\n| **E2E** | Full workflows | pytest + DB |\n\n### Async Testing\n\n```python\n\n# Use pytest-asyncio for async tests\n\nimport pytest\nfrom httpx import AsyncClient\n\n@pytest.mark.asyncio\nasync def test_endpoint():\n    async with AsyncClient(app=app, base_url=\" as client:\n        response = await client.get(\"/users\")\n        assert response.status_code == 200\n```\n\n### Fixtures Strategy\n\n```\nCommon fixtures:\n├── db_session → Database connection\n├── client → Test client\n├── authenticated_user → User with token\n└── sample_data → Test data setup\n```\n\n---\n\n## 10. Decision Checklist\n\nBefore implementing:\n\n- [ ] **Asked user about framework preference?**\n- [ ] **Chosen framework for THIS context?** (not just default)\n- [ ] **Decided async vs sync?**\n- [ ] **Planned type hint strategy?**\n- [ ] **Defined project structure?**\n- [ ] **Planned error handling?**\n- [ ] **Considered background tasks?**\n\n---\n\n## 11. Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n### ❌ DON''T:\n- Default to Django for simple APIs (FastAPI may be better)\n- Use sync libraries in async code\n- Skip type hints for public APIs\n- Put business logic in routes/views\n- Ignore N+1 queries\n- Mix async and sync carelessly\n\n### ✅ DO:\n- Choose framework based on context\n- Ask about async requirements\n- Use Pydantic for validation\n- Separate concerns (routes → services → repos)\n- Test critical paths\n\n---\n\n> **Remember**: Python patterns are about decision-making for YOUR specific context. Don''t copy code—think about what serves your application best.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:15:20.004Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Analysis Agents needing advanced Python development principles and decision-making capabilities.","zh":"适合需要高级Python开发原则和决策能力的代码分析代理。","ja":"Python開発の高度な原則と意思決定能力が必要なコード分析エージェントに適しています。","ko":"고급 Python 개발 원칙과 의사 결정 능력이 필요한 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de análisis de código que necesitan principios avanzados de desarrollo de Python y capacidades de toma de decisiones.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de code ayant besoin de principes de développement Python avancés et de capacités de prise de décision.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Analyse-Agents, die erweiterte Python-Entwicklungsprinzipien und Entscheidungskapazitäten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Código que precisam de princípios avançados de desenvolvimento Python e capacidades de tomada de decisões.","ru":"Идеально для агентов анализа кода, которым необходимы продвинутые принципы разработки на Python и возможности принятия решений.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء قادرون على تحليل الشفرة الذين يحتاجون إلى مبادئ متقدمة لتطوير بايثون وقدرات اتخاذ القرارات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to make informed decisions about async vs sync programming based on context, and apply framework-agnostic principles to Python development, utilizing tools like Context7, Tavily, BraveSearch, or Serper.dev for web searches.","zh":"赋予代理根据上下文做出有关异步与同步编程的明智决策的能力，并将框架无关的原则应用于Python开发，利用像Context7、Tavily、BraveSearch或Serper.dev这样的工具进行网络搜索。","ja":"エージェントがコンテキストに基づいて非同期と同期プログラミングについて十分な情報に基づいた決定を下し、Python開発にフレームワークに依存しない原則を適用することを可能にし、Context7、Tavily、BraveSearch、またはSerper.devなどのツールを使用してWeb検索を行う。","ko":"에이전트가 문脈에 따라 비동기 및 동기 프로그래밍에 대해 정보에基づいた 의사 결정을 내릴 수 있도록 하며, Python 개발에 프레임워크에 종속되지 않는 원칙을 적용하며, Context7, Tavily, BraveSearch 또는 Serper.dev와 같은 도구를 사용하여 웹 검색을 수행할 수 있습니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes tomar decisiones informadas sobre programación asíncrona versus sincrónica en función del contexto y aplicar principios agnósticos de framework al desarrollo de Python, utilizando herramientas como Context7, Tavily, BraveSearch o Serper.dev para búsquedas web.","fr":"Permet aux agents de prendre des décisions éclairées sur la programmation asynchrone versus synchrone en fonction du contexte et d''appliquer des principes agnostiques de framework au développement Python, en utilisant des outils tels que Context7, Tavily, BraveSearch ou Serper.dev pour les recherches web.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, fundierte Entscheidungen über asynchrone versus synchrone Programmierung basierend auf dem Kontext zu treffen und framework-agnostische Prinzipien auf die Python-Entwicklung anzuwenden, indem Tools wie Context7, Tavily, BraveSearch oder Serper.dev für Web-Suchen verwendet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a tomar decisões informadas sobre programação async versus sync com base no contexto e aplicar princípios agnósticos de framework ao desenvolvimento Python, utilizando ferramentas como Context7, Tavily, BraveSearch ou Serper.dev para pesquisas na web.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью принимать обоснованные решения об асинхронном или синхронном программировании на основе контекста и применять принципы независимого от фреймворка развития Python, используя инструменты seperti Context7, Tavily, BraveSearch или Serper.dev для веб-поиска.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على اتخاذ قرارات مدروسة حول برمجة Async مقابل Sync بناءً على السياق وتطبيق مبادئ متقدمة لتطوير بايثون باستخدام أدوات مثل Context7 و Tavily و BraveSearch أو Serper.dev للبحث على الويب."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating Python code reviews for best practices","Generating framework-agnostic Python code snippets","Debugging synchronous vs asynchronous programming issues"],"zh":["自动执行Python代码审查以获取最佳实践","生成与框架无关的Python代码片段","调试同步与异步编程问题"],"ja":["ベストプラクティスを取得するためのPythonコードレビューの自動化","フレームワークに依存しないPythonコードスニペットの生成","同期と非同期プログラミングの問題のデバッグ"],"ko":["최선의 실践을 얻기 위한 Python 코드 리뷰의 자동화","프레임워크에 종속되지 않는 Python 코드 스니펫의 생성","동기화 및 비동기 프로그래밍 문제의 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización de revisiones de código Python para mejores prácticas","Generación de fragmentos de código Python agnósticos de framework","Depuración de problemas de programación sincrónica versus asíncrona"],"fr":["Automatisation des examens de code Python pour les meilleures pratiques","Génération de fragments de code Python agnostiques de framework","Débogage des problèmes de programmation synchrone versus asynchrone"],"de":["Automatisierung von Python-Code-Reviews für Best Practices","Generierung von framework-agnostischen Python-Code-Snippets","Fehlerbehebung bei synchroner versus asynchroner Programmierung"],"pt":["Automatizar revisões de código Python para as melhores práticas","Gerar trechos de código Python agnósticos de framework","Depurar problemas de programação síncrona versus assíncrona"],"ru":["Автоматизировать проверку кода Python на лучшие практики","Генерировать фрагменты кода Python независимого от фреймворка","Отлаживать проблемы синхронного и асинхронного программирования"],"ar":["تأتمتة مراجعة الشفرة بايثون لأفضل الممارسات","генерировать شفرة بايثون غير معتمدة على الإطار","تصحيح أخطاء البرمجة المتزامنة مقابل غير المتزامنة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Python development principles","Not a replacement for memorized code patterns"],"zh":["需要理解Python开发原则","不是替代记忆代码模式"],"ja":["Python開発の原則を理解する必要がある","記憶したコードパターンの代替ではない"],"ko":["Python 개발 원칙을 이해해야 함","기억된 코드 패턴의 대체가 아님"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los principios de desarrollo de Python","No reemplaza los patrones de código memorizados"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des principes de développement Python","Ne remplace pas les modèles de code mémorisés"],"de":["Erfordert Verständnis der Python-Entwicklungsprinzipien","Ist kein Ersatz für gemerkte Code-Muster"],"pt":["Exige compreensão dos princípios de desenvolvimento Python","Não é um substituto para padrões de código memorizados"],"ru":["Требует понимания принципов разработки Python","Не является заменой запомненных шаблонов кода"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم مبادئ تطوير بايثون","ليس بديلاً عن الأنماط الشفرية المحفوظة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
