portunidades","Transformação de solicitações vagas em especificações claras","Garantia de compreensão do problema real antes de propor soluções"],"ru":["Систематический сократический вопрос","Уточнение целей и задач","Определение ограничений и возможностей","Преобразование неясных запросов в ясные спецификации","Гарантия понимания реальной проблемы до предложения решений"],"ar":["استجواب سقراطي منهجي","توضيح الأهداف والغايات","تحديد القيود والفرص","تحويل الطلبات الغامضة إلى مواصفات واضحة","ضمان فهم المشكلة الحقيقية قبل اقتراح حلول"]},"keywords":{"zh":["探索技能","自适应任务阐明","索拉特问题","任务规范","解决方案","技术开发","软件开发"],"ja":["Exploreスキル","アダプティブタスク明確化","ソクラテス的疑問","タスク仕様","解決策","テクノロジー開発","ソフトウェア開発"],"ko":["탐색 스킬","적응형 작업 명확화","소크라테스식 질문","작업 명세","해결책","기술 개발","소프트웨어 개발"],"es":["clarificación de tareas","preguntas socráticas","desarrollo de soluciones","comprensión del problema","soluciones efectivas","reducción de errores","análisis de requisitos","especificaciones de tareas","adaptación de tareas"],"fr":["clarification des tâches","questions socratiques","développement de solutions","compréhension du problème","solutions efficaces","réduction des erreurs","analyse des exigences","spécifications des tâches","adaptation des tâches"],"de":["Klärung von Aufgaben","sokratische Fragen","Entwicklung von Lösungen","Verständnis des Problems","effektive Lösungen","Reduzierung von Fehlern","Anforderungsanalyse","Aufgabenbeschreibungen","Anpassung von Aufgaben"],"pt":["esclarecimento de tarefas","questionamento socrático","objetivos e metas","restrições e oportunidades","soluções eficazes","desenvolvimento de software","engenharia de requisitos"],"ru":["адаптивное уточнение задач","сократический вопрос","цели и задачи","ограничения и возможности","эффективные решения","разработка программного обеспечения","инженерия требований"],"ar":["توضيح مهام تعاوني","استجواب سقراطي","أهداف وغايات","قيود وفرص","حلول فعالة","تطوير البرمجيات","هندسة المتطلبات"]}},"owner":"dzhechko","repo":"2026-jan-pu-noom-clone-01","repoPath":"dzhechko/2026-jan-pu-noom-clone-01","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.406Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"explore","description":">","bodyPreview":"# Explore: Adaptive Task Clarification\n\nTransform vague requests into crystal-clear, actionable task specifications through systematic Socratic questioning.\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\n**Never solve before you understand.** Most failed solutions solve the wrong problem. This skill ensures the real problem is understood before any solution is proposed.\n\nKey principles:\n- Questions unlock understanding; answers often hide assumptions\n- The stated goal is rarely the real goal\n- Constraints reveal opportun","body":"# Explore: Adaptive Task Clarification\n\nTransform vague requests into crystal-clear, actionable task specifications through systematic Socratic questioning.\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\n**Never solve before you understand.** Most failed solutions solve the wrong problem. This skill ensures the real problem is understood before any solution is proposed.\n\nKey principles:\n- Questions unlock understanding; answers often hide assumptions\n- The stated goal is rarely the real goal\n- Constraints reveal opportunities\n- Success criteria prevent scope creep\n\n## Task Classification\n\nBefore asking questions, classify the task type to select appropriate exploration dimensions:\n\n| Task Type | Indicators | Primary Dimensions |\n|-----------|------------|-------------------|\n| **Product/Feature** | \"build\", \"create app\", \"develop\" | Outcome, Users, Constraints, Success |\n| **Problem Solving** | \"fix\", \"solve\", \"issue with\" | Root Cause, Constraints, Attempted Solutions |\n| **Decision Making** | \"should I\", \"choose between\", \"evaluate\" | Criteria, Tradeoffs, Timeline, Reversibility |\n| **Creative** | \"write\", \"design\", \"make content\" | Audience, Tone, Format, Examples |\n| **Research** | \"find out\", \"analyze\", \"understand\" | Scope, Depth, Sources, Deliverable |\n| **Process/Workflow** | \"how to\", \"improve process\" | Current State, Desired State, Blockers |\n\n## Exploration Dimensions\n\nSelect 3-5 dimensions based on task type. Each dimension has multiple question variants—choose the most natural for context.\n\n### 1. The Real Objective\nUncover what success truly looks like, beyond the stated request.\n\n**Questions:**\n- \"If this worked perfectly, what would be different in your [work/life/business]?\"\n- \"What outcome would make you say ''this was absolutely worth it''?\"\n- \"Is this goal a means to something else, or the end itself?\"\n- \"If you could wave a magic wand and have any result, what would you choose?\"\n\n**Red flags to probe:** Generic goals (\"make it better\"), proxy metrics, solutions presented as requirements.\n\n### 2. Constraints & Boundaries\nIdentify hard limits that shape the solution space.\n\n**Questions:**\n- \"What''s absolutely off the table—budget, time, technology, or approach-wise?\"\n- \"What existing systems, processes, or decisions must this work with?\"\n- \"Who needs to approve this, and what are their non-negotiables?\"\n- \"What would disqualify a solution, even if it technically works?\"\n\n**Red flags to probe:** No constraints mentioned (usually means hidden ones), unrealistic expectations.\n\n### 3. Available Resources\nUnderstand leverage points and existing assets.\n\n**Questions:**\n- \"What do you already have that we could build on—data, tools, people, prior work?\"\n- \"Who else is involved, and what can they contribute?\"\n- \"What similar problems have you solved before, and what worked?\"\n- \"What''s your actual capacity to implement this?\"\n\n**Red flags to probe:** Overestimated capabilities, unacknowledged dependencies.\n\n### 4. Timeline & Urgency\nDistinguish real deadlines from arbitrary ones.\n\n**Questions:**\n- \"What happens if this takes 2x longer than expected?\"\n- \"Is there a hard deadline, and what''s driving it?\"\n- \"Would you prefer a quick 80% solution or a slower 100% solution?\"\n- \"What''s the cost of delay vs. the cost of getting it wrong?\"\n\n**Red flags to probe:** Artificial urgency, no clear driver for deadline.\n\n### 5. Success Criteria\nDefine what \"done\" actually means.\n\n**Questions:**\n- \"How will you know this is successful? What will you measure?\"\n- \"Who decides if this is good enough, and what will they look for?\"\n- \"What''s the minimum viable outcome that would still be valuable?\"\n- \"In 6 months, what would make you regret the approach we took?\"\n\n**Red flags to probe:** Vague criteria (\"stakeholders will be happy\"), moving targets.\n\n### 6. Attempted Solutions (for problems)\nLearn from what hasn''t worked.\n\n**Questions:**\n- \"What have you already tried, and why didn''t it work?\"\n- \"What solutions have you considered but rejected?\"\n- \"What would the obvious solution be, and why isn''t that good enough?\"\n\n### 7. Audience & Stakeholders (for products/content)\nUnderstand who this serves.\n\n**Questions:**\n- \"Who specifically will use this, and what''s their context when they do?\"\n- \"What does your audience already know or believe about this?\"\n- \"Who might be negatively affected, and does that matter?\"\n\n## Execution Protocol\n\n### Phase 1: Initial Assessment (1 turn)\n\n1. Parse the user''s request\n2. Identify what''s already clear from context\n3. Classify task type\n4. Select 3-5 most critical dimensions\n5. Note any immediate red flags or assumptions\n\n### Phase 2: Adaptive Questioning (3-7 turns)\n\n**Rules:**\n- Ask ONE question at a time\n- Make questions specific and decision-shaping, not generic\n- Challenge vague answers: \"Can you be more specific about...?\"\n- Acknowledge answers before next question\n- Skip dimensions already clarified\n- Stop when you have enough to create a clear brief\n\n**Question Sequencing:**\n1. Start with Real Objective (reveals the most)\n2. Follow with Constraints (narrows solution space)\n3. Then Success Criteria (defines done)\n4. Fill gaps with other dimensions as needed\n\n**Adaptive behavior:**\n- If user gives detailed answer → compress follow-ups\n- If user seems frustrated → summarize and ask if they want to continue\n- If contradiction detected → gently probe: \"Earlier you mentioned X, but now Y—help me understand?\"\n\n### Phase 3: Task Brief Synthesis (1 turn)\n\nAfter sufficient exploration, synthesize into a **Task Brief**:\n\n```\n## Task Brief\n\n**Objective:** [Clear statement of what we''re actually solving]\n\n**Context:** [Relevant background and constraints]\n\n**Success Criteria:**\n- [Measurable criterion 1]\n- [Measurable criterion 2]\n\n**Constraints:**\n- [Hard constraint 1]\n- [Hard constraint 2]\n\n**Resources Available:** [What we can leverage]\n\n**Timeline:** [Deadline and urgency level]\n\n**Key Assumptions:** [Things we''re assuming that could change the approach]\n\n**Out of Scope:** [Explicitly excluded items]\n```\n\nAsk user: \"Does this capture what you need? Anything to add or correct?\"\n\n### Phase 4: Handoff\n\nOnce validated, either:\n- Proceed to solution (if user wants immediate help)\n- Export brief for later use\n- Suggest appropriate next steps/skills\n\n## Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n❌ **Interrogation mode:** Don''t fire questions robotically\n❌ **Assuming context:** Don''t skip clarification because you \"think\" you understand\n❌ **Premature solutions:** Don''t hint at solutions before exploration is complete\n❌ **Over-questioning:** Stop when you have enough clarity\n❌ **Generic questions:** Each question should be tailored to this specific task\n❌ **Ignoring signals:** If user provides info proactively, don''t re-ask\n\n## Example Flow\n\n**User:** \"I want to create a dashboard for my team\"\n\n**Claude (Phase 1 assessment):**\n- Task type: Product/Feature\n- Unclear: Who uses it, what data, what decisions it enables, timeline\n- Dimensions needed: Real Objective, Audience, Constraints, Success Criteria\n\n**Claude:** \"Before we dive in—what decisions will your team make differently once they have this dashboard? What''s the main insight they''re missing today?\"\n\n*[User answers about tracking project delays]*\n\n**Claude:** \"Got it—so the core need is visibility into project health to catch delays early. How do you know a project is delayed today? What''s the current process for catching these issues?\"\n\n*[Continues adaptively based on answers...]*\n\n## Integration Notes\n\nAfter exploration, this skill can hand off to:\n- problem-solver-enhanced (for complex problems)\n- goap-research (for research tasks)\n- frontend-design (for UI/product tasks)\n- Any implementation skill with the structured Task Brief\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:17:35.227Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Conversational Agents needing advanced task clarification capabilities through Socratic questioning.","zh":"非常适合需要通过苏格拉底式提问进行高级任务阐明能力的对话式代理。","ja":"会話エージェントが高度なタスクの明確化機能を必要とする場合に最適です。ソクラテス的質問を通じて。","ko":"대화형 에이전트가 소크라테스식 질문을 통해 고급 태스크澄清 기능을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de conversación que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de aclaración de tareas a través de preguntas socráticas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de conversation qui nécessitent des capacités avancées de clarification de tâches via des questions socratiques.","de":"Perfekt für Konversationsagenten, die erweiterte Aufgabenklärungsfähigkeiten durch sokratisches Fragen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Conversação que precisam de capacidades avançadas de esclarecimento de tarefas por meio de questionamento socrático.","ru":"Идеально подходит для разговорных агентов, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности разъяснения задач посредством сократического вопросования.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المحادثين الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة لتوضيح المهام من خلال الاستجواب السقراطي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform vague requests into crystal-clear task specifications using systematic questioning, unlocking understanding and revealing constraints through protocols like adaptive task clarification.","zh":"使代理能够通过系统化的提问将模糊的请求转化为清晰的任务规范，从而解锁理解并通过像自适应任务阐明这样的协议揭示约束。","ja":"エージェントが漠然としたリクエストを明確なタスク仕様に変換できるようにし、体系的な質問を通じて理解を解き放ち、適応タスクの明確化などのプロトコルを通じて制約を明らかにする。","ko":"에이전트가 모호한 요청을 명확한 태스크 사양으로 변환 할 수 있도록 하여 이해를 잠금 해제하고 적응형 태스크 澄清과 같은 프로토콜을 통해 제약 조건을 드러내는 것을 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformar solicitudes vagas en especificaciones de tareas cristalinamente claras utilizando un cuestionamiento sistemático, desbloqueando la comprensión y revelando restricciones a través de protocolos como la aclaración de tareas adaptativa.","fr":"Permet aux agents de transformer des demandes vagues en des spécifications de tâches cristallinement claires en utilisant un questionnement systématique, déverrouillant la compréhension et révélant les contraintes via des protocoles tels que la clarification de tâches adaptative.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, vage Anfragen in kristallklare Aufgabenbeschreibungen umzuwandeln, indem sie systematisches Fragen verwenden, um das Verständnis zu ermöglichen und Einschränkungen durch Protokolle wie adaptive Aufgabenklärung aufzudecken.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a transformar solicitações vagas em especificações de tarefas cristalinamente claras usando questionamento sistemático, desbloqueando a compreensão e revelando restrições por meio de protocolos como esclarecimento de tarefas adaptativo.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью преобразовывать неясные запросы в чрезвычайно ясные спецификации задач с помощью системного вопросования, открывая понимание и раскрывая ограничения посредством протоколов, таких как адаптивное разъяснение задач.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من تحويل الطلبات الغامضة إلى مواصفات المهام واضحة تمامًا باستخدام الاستجواب المنهجي ، وفك الحجب لفهم وإظهار القيود من خلال بروتوكولات مثل توضيح المهام التكيفي."},"useCases":{"en":["Clarifying ambiguous user requests","Generating actionable task specifications","Identifying hidden assumptions in user queries"],"zh":["阐明模糊的用户请求","生成可操作的任务规范","识别用户查询中的隐含假设"],"ja":["ユーザーの曖昧なリクエストを明確化する","実行可能なタスク仕様を生成する","ユーザーのクエリの中に隠れた仮定を特定する"],"ko":["사용자의 모호한 요청을 澄清하는こと","실행 가능한 태스크 사양을 생성하는 것","사용자의 쿼리에서 숨겨진 가정 식별"],"es":["Aclarar solicitudes de usuario ambiguas","Generar especificaciones de tareas realizables","Identificar suposiciones ocultas en consultas de usuario"],"fr":["Clarifier les demandes d''utilisateur ambigües","Générer des spécifications de tâches réalisables","Identifier les hypothèses cachées dans les requêtes d''utilisateur"],"de":["Ambigue Benutzersuchen klären","Handhabbare Aufgabenbeschreibungen generieren","Versteckte Annahmen in Benutzerabfragen identifizieren"],"pt":["Esclarecer solicitações de usuário ambíguas","Gerar especificações de tarefas executáveis","Identificar suposições ocultas em consultas de usuário"],"ru":["Ясное изложение неоднозначных запросов пользователя","Генерирование спецификаций задач, которые можно выполнить","Определение скрытых предположений в запросах пользователя"],"ar":["توضيح طلبات المستخدم الغامضة","إنتاج مواصفات المهام القابلة للتنفيذ","تحديد افتراضات خفية في استفسارات المستخدم"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires ability to engage in Socratic questioning","May not be effective with extremely vague or undefined goals"],"zh":["需要能够进行苏格拉底式提问","可能不适用于极其模糊或未定义的目标"],"ja":["ソクラテス的質問を行う能力が必要","極めて漠然とした、または未定義の目標に対しては効果的ではない"],"ko":["소크라테스식 질문을 할 수 있는 능력이 필요","극도로 모호하거나 정의되지 않은 목표에 대해 효과적이지 않을 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere la capacidad de participar en preguntas socráticas","Puede no ser efectivo con metas extremadamente vagas o indefinidas"],"fr":["Nécessite la capacité de participer à des questions socratiques","Peut ne pas être efficace avec des objectifs extrêmement vagues ou non définis"],"de":["Benötigt die Fähigkeit, an sokratischen Fragen teilzunehmen","Kann bei extrem vagen oder unbestimmten Zielen nicht wirksam sein"],"pt":["Exige a capacidade de se engajar em questionamento socrático","Pode não ser eficaz com metas extremamente vagas ou não definidas"],"ru":["Требует способности участвовать в сократическом вопросовании","Может быть неэффективным при работе с чрезвычайно неясными или неопределенными целями"],"ar":["يتطلب القدرة على المشاركة في الاستجواب السقراطي","يمكن أن يكون غير فعال مع الأهداف الغامضة بشكل خاص أو غير محددة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('AoEiuV020/flutter_melos_template/init-import-sorter', 'community', 'AoEiuV020', 'flutter_melos_template', 'AoEiuV020/flutter_melos_template', 'init-import-sorter', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.406Z', '2026-02-18T03:17:31.884Z', NULL, '{"id":"AoEiuV020/flutter_melos_template/init-import-sorter","name":"init-import-sorter","description":{"zh":"Init-Import-Sorter 是一个 melos 管理的 Flutter 多模块项目模板，用于简化 import 排序和 melos 工作流","ja":"Init-Import-Sorter は、Flutter マルチモジュールプロジェクトのテンプレートを melos で管理し、import の並べ替えと melos ワークフローを簡素化","ko":"Init-Import-Sorter는 melos에서 관리하는 Flutter 멀티 모듈 프로젝트 템플릿으로 import 정렬 및 melos 워크플ロー簡素화","es":"Init Import Sorter es una herramienta para ordenar importaciones en proyectos Flutter. Garantiza la organización y el orden de las importaciones.","fr":"Init Import Sorter est un outil pour classer les importations dans les projets Flutter. Il garantit l''organisation et l''ordre des importations.","de":"Init Import Sorter ist ein Tool zum Ordnen von Importen in Flutter-Projekten. Es gewährleistet die Organisation und Ordnung der Importe.","pt":"O init-import-sorter é uma ferramenta para organizar importações em projetos Flutter com melos. Ele garante que as importações sejam ordenadas corretamente","ru":"Init-import-sorter - это инструмент для организации импортов в проектах Flutter с melos. Он гарантирует, что импорт будет отсортирован правильно","ar":"init-import-sorter هو أداة لتنظيم الاستيرادات في مشاريع Flutter مع melos. يضمن أن تكون الاستيرادات مرتبة بشكل صحيح","en":"melos管理的flutter多模块项目模板，"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Init-Import-Sorter：Flutter 多模块项目模板管理","ja":"Init-Import-Sorter：Flutter マルチモジュールプロジェクトテンプレート管理","ko":"Init-Import-Sorter：Flutter 멀티 모듈 프로젝트 템플릿 관리","es":"Init Import Sorter para Flutter","fr":"Init Import Sorter pour Flutter","de":"Init Import Sorter für Flutter","pt":"Organizador de Importação para Flutter","ru":"Сортировщик импорта для Flutter","ar":"موزع الاستيراد لFlutter","en":"init-import-sorter"},"description":{"zh":"Init-Import-Sorter 是一个 melos 管理的 Flutter 多模块项目模板，用于简化 import 排序和 melos 工作流","ja":"Init-Import-Sorter は、Flutter マルチモジュールプロジェクトのテンプレートを melos で管理し、import の並べ替えと melos ワークフローを簡素化","ko":"Init-Import-Sorter는 melos에서 관리하는 Flutter 멀티 모듈 프로젝트 템플릿으로 import 정렬 및 melos 워크플ロー簡素화","es":"Init Import Sorter es una herramienta para ordenar importaciones en proyectos Flutter. Garantiza la organización y el orden de las importaciones.","fr":"Init Import Sorter est un outil pour classer les importations dans les projets Flutter. Il garantit l''organisation et l''ordre des importations.","de":"Init Import Sorter ist ein Tool zum Ordnen von Importen in Flutter-Projekten. Es gewährleistet die Organisation und Ordnung der Importe.","pt":"O init-import-sorter é uma ferramenta para organizar importações em projetos Flutter com melos. Ele garante que as importações sejam ordenadas corretamente","ru":"Init-import-sorter - это инструмент для организации импортов в проектах Flutter с melos. Он гарантирует, что импорт будет отсортирован правильно","ar":"init-import-sorter هو أداة لتنظيم الاستيرادات في مشاريع Flutter مع melos. يضمن أن تكون الاستيرادات مرتبة بشكل صحيح","en":"melos管理的flutter多模块项目模板，"},"definition":{"en":"melos管理的flutter多模块项目模板，"},"features":{"zh":["简化 import 排序","支持 melos 工作流","兼容 pub workspaces","支持 monorepo 项目","命令行工具","自动化 import 排序"],"ja":["import の並べ替えを簡素化","melos ワークフローをサポート","pub workspaces と互換性","monorepo プロジェクトをサポート","コマンドラインツール","自動化 import 並べ替え"],"ko":["import 정렬을 간소화","melos 워크플로우를 지원","pub workspaces와 호환","monorepo 프로젝트를 지원","명령줄 도구","자동 import 정렬"],"es":["Ordena importaciones en proyectos Flutter","Compatible con melos y pub workspaces","Soporte para monorepo","Facil instalación y uso","Mejora la organización del código"],"fr":["Classe les importations dans les projets Flutter","Compatible avec melos et pub workspaces","Prise en charge de monorepo","Installation et utilisation faciles","Améliore l''organisation du code"],"de":["Ordnet Importe in Flutter-Projekten","Kompatibel mit melos und pub workspaces","Unterstützung für monorepo","Einfache Installation und Verwendung","Verbessert die Codeorganisation"],"pt":["Organização de importações em projetos Flutter","Integração com melos","Suporte a monorepo pub workspaces","Instalação simples via dart pub global","Uso fácil com comandos bash"],"ru":["Организация импортов в проектах Flutter","Интеграция с melos","Поддержка monorepo pub workspaces","Простая установка через dart pub global","Легкое использование с помощью команд bash"],"ar":["تنظيم الاستيرادات في مشاريع Flutter","التكامل مع melos","دعم monorepo pub workspaces","تركيب بسيط عبر dart pub global","استخدام سهل مع أوامر bash"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Flutter","多模块项目","import 排序","melos","pub workspaces","monorepo","命令行工具","自动化"],"ja":["Flutter","マルチモジュールプロジェクト","import 並べ替え","melos","pub workspaces","monorepo","コマンドラインツール","自動化"],"ko":["Flutter","멀티 모듈 프로젝트","import 정렬","melos","pub workspaces","monorepo","명령줄 도구","자동화"],"es":["Init Import Sorter","Flutter","ordenamiento de importaciones","melos","pub workspaces","monorepo","desarrollo de aplicaciones móviles"],"fr":["Init Import Sorter","Flutter","classement d''importations","melos","pub workspaces","monorepo","développement d''applications mobiles"],"de":["Init Import Sorter","Flutter","Ordnen von Importen","melos","pub workspaces","monorepo","Mobile-App-Entwicklung"],"pt":["init-import-sorter","flutter","melos","organização de importações","monorepo pub workspaces","dart pub global"],"ru":["init-import-sorter","flutter","melos","организация импортов","monorepo pub workspaces","dart pub global"],"ar":["init-import-sorter","flutter","melos","تنظيم الاستيرادات","monorepo pub workspaces","dart pub global"]}},"owner":"AoEiuV020","repo":"flutter_melos_template","repoPath":"AoEiuV020/flutter_melos_template","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.406Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"init-import-sorter","description":"Install import_sorter for Dart import sorting. Use when user needs import sorting, wants to sort imports, or gets import_sorter not found. Triggers on install import_sorter, init import sorter, sort imports, setup import_sorter.","bodyPreview":"# 安装 Import Sorter\n\n确保 import_sorter 已安装并可用。使用支持 pub workspaces 的修复版本。\n\n## 安装步骤\n\n```bash\n# 1. 检查是否已安装\ndart pub global list | grep import_sorter\n\n# 2. 如果未安装，从修复分支安装（支持 monorepo pub workspaces）\ndart pub global activate --source git https://github.com/myConsciousness/import_sorter.git --git-ref fix/monorepo-pub-workspaces\n```\n\n## 使用\n\n```bash\n# 对单个文件排序\ndart pub global run import_sorter --no-comments\n\n# 通过 melos 对所有包排序\nmelos sort\n```","body":"# 安装 Import Sorter\n\n确保 import_sorter 已安装并可用。使用支持 pub workspaces 的修复版本。\n\n## 安装步骤\n\n```bash\n# 1. 检查是否已安装\ndart pub global list | grep import_sorter\n\n# 2. 如果未安装，从修复分支安装（支持 monorepo pub workspaces）\ndart pub global activate --source git https://github.com/myConsciousness/import_sorter.git --git-ref fix/monorepo-pub-workspaces\n```\n\n## 使用\n\n```bash\n# 对单个文件排序\ndart pub global run import_sorter --no-comments\n\n# 通过 melos 对所有包排序\nmelos sort\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:17:31.884Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Flutter Monorepo Maintenance Agents requiring automated import organization across multi-package workspaces.","zh":"适用于需要在多包工作空间中自动化导入组织的Flutter Monorepo维护代理的理想选择。","ja":"マルチパッケージワークスペースでの自動インポート整理を必要とするFlutter Monorepoメンテナンスエージェントに最適です。","ko":"다중 패키지 워크스페이스에서 자동화된 가져오기 조직이 필요한 Flutter Monorepo 유지 보수 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de mantenimiento de monorepo de Flutter que requieren organización automática de importaciones en espacios de trabajo de varios paquetes.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de maintenance de monorepo Flutter nécessitant une organisation automatisée des importations dans des espaces de travail à plusieurs packages.","de":"Ideal für Flutter-Monorepo-Wartungsagenten, die eine automatisierte Organisierung von Importen in Mehrpaket-Arbeitsbereichen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Manutenção de Monorepo Flutter que exigem organização de importação automatizada em espaços de trabalho de vários pacotes.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов обслуживания монорепозитория Flutter, требующих автоматизированной организации импорта в много-пакетных рабочих пространствах.","ar":"مثالي لعميل صيانة Monorepo Flutter الذي يتطلب تنظيم الاستيراد التلقائي عبر مساحات العمل متعددة الحزم."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables automated Dart import organization across pub workspaces using melos integration. Provides consistent code style enforcement through CLI-based file processing with optional comment stripping via --no-comments flag.","zh":"通过melos集成，实现Dart导入的自动化组织，并通过基于CLI的文件处理提供一致的代码样式强制执行，具有可选的注释剥离功能，通过--no-comments标志实现。","ja":"melos統合を使用してDartのインポートを自動的に整理し、CLIベースのファイル処理を通じて一貫したコードスタイルの適用を提供し、--no-commentsフラグを使用したコメントの剥離をオプションで提供します。","ko":"melos 통합을 사용하여 Dart 가져오기를 자동으로 정렬하고, CLI 기반 파일 처리를 통해 일관된 코드 스타일 적용을 제공하며, --no-comments 플래그를 사용하여 주석을剥离하는 옵션을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita la organización automática de importaciones de Dart en espacios de trabajo de pub mediante la integración de melos. Proporciona una aplicación coherente del estilo de código a través de la procesamiento de archivos basado en CLI con la opción de eliminación de comentarios a través de la marca --no-comments.","fr":"Permet l''organisation automatisée des importations Dart dans les espaces de travail pub à l''aide de l''intégration de melos. Fournit une application cohérente du style de code via le traitement de fichiers basé sur CLI avec l''option de suppression de commentaires via le drapeau --no-comments.","de":"Ermöglicht die automatisierte Organisation von Dart-Importen in pub-Arbeitsbereichen über die melos-Integration. Bietet eine konsistente Durchsetzung des Code-Stils durch CLI-basierte Dateiverarbeitung mit optionaler Kommentar-Entfernung über die --no-comments-Flagge.","pt":"Permite a organização automatizada de importações Dart em espaços de trabalho pub usando integração melos. Fornece aplicação de estilo de código consistente por meio do processamento de arquivos baseado em CLI com remoção opcional de comentários via sinalizador --no-comments.","ru":"Позволяет выполнять автоматизированную организацию импорта Dart в рабочих пространствах pub с помощью интеграции melos. Обеспечивает единый стиль кода через обработку файлов на основе CLI с возможным удалением комментариев через флаг --no-comments.","ar":"يسمح بتنظيم الاستيراد التلقائي Dart عبر مساحات العمل pub باستخدام تكامل melos. يوفر تنفيذ نمط код موحد من خلال معالجة الملفات القائمة على CLI مع إمكانية إزالة التعليقات عبر علامة --no-comments."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating import sorting across Flutter monorepo packages","Enforcing consistent code style in multi-module projects","Integrating import organization into CI/CD pipelines via melos commands"],"zh":["自动化Flutter单体仓库包的导入排序","在多模块项目中强制执行一致的代码样式","通过melos命令将导入组织集成到CI/CD管道中"],"ja":["Flutterモノリポパッケージのインポートの自動整理","マルチモジュールプロジェクトで一貫したコードスタイルを適用","melosコマンドを使用してインポートの整理をCI/CDパイプラインに統合"],"ko":["Flutter 모노레포 패키지의 가져오기 정렬 자동화","다중 모듈 프로젝트에서 일관된 코드 스타일 적용","melos 명령을 사용하여 가져오기 조직을 CI/CD 파이프라인에 통합"],"es":["Automatización de la organización de importaciones en paquetes de monorepo de Flutter","Aplicación de un estilo de código coherente en proyectos de varios módulos","Integración de la organización de importaciones en tuberías de CI/CD a través de comandos de melos"],"fr":["Automatisation du tri des importations dans les packages de monorepo Flutter","Application d''un style de code cohérent dans les projets multimodules","Intégration de l''organisation des importations dans les pipelines de CI/CD via des commandes melos"],"de":["Automatisierung der Organisierung von Importen in Flutter-Monorepo-Paketen","Durchsetzung eines konsistenten Code-Stils in Mehrmodul-Projekten","Integration der Import-Organisierung in CI/CD-Pipelines über melos-Befehle"],"pt":["Automatizar a organização de importações em pacotes de monorepo Flutter","Impor estilo de código consistente em projetos multi-módulos","Integrar a organização de importações em pipelines de CI/CD via comandos melos"],"ru":["Автоматизировать сортировку импортов в пакетах монорепозитория Flutter","Обеспечить единый стиль кода в много-модульных проектах","Интегрировать организацию импорта в конвейеры CI/CD с помощью команд melos"],"ar":["توفير تنظيم الاستيراد التلقائي عبر حزم Monorepo Flutter","فرض نمط код موحد في مشاريع متعددة الوحدات","دمج تنظيم الاستيراد في خطوط أنابيب CI/CD عبر أوامر melos"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires melos dependency management system","Needs git-based installation from specific fix branch","Dart-specific functionality only"],"zh":["需要melos的依赖管理系统","需要从特定修复分支通过git安装","仅Dart特定功能"],"ja":["melosの依存関係管理システムが必要","特定の修正ブランチからのgitインストールが必要","Dart固有の機能のみ"],"ko":["melos의 의존성 관리 시스템이 필요","특정 수정 브랜치에서 git을 통해 설치해야 함","Dart 전용 기능만"],"es":["Requiere el sistema de gestión de dependencias de melos","Necesita instalación basada en git desde una rama de corrección específica","Funcionalidad específica de Dart solo"],"fr":["Nécessite le système de gestion de dépendances melos","Nécessite une installation basée sur git à partir d''une branche de correction spécifique","Fonctionnalité spécifique à Dart uniquement"],"de":["Benötigt das Abhängigkeitsverwaltungssystem von melos","Benötigt eine git-basierte Installation von einem bestimmten Fix-Zweig","Nur Dart-spezifische Funktionalität"],"pt":["Exige sistema de gerenciamento de dependências melos","Necessita instalação baseada em git a partir de ramo de correção específico","Funcionalidade específica do Dart apenas"],"ru":["Требует системы управления зависимостями melos","Требует установки на основе git из определенной ветки исправления","Функциональность только для Dart"],"ar":["يتطلب نظام إدارة الاعتماد melos","يحتاج إلى تثبيت قائم على git من فرع تصحيح محدد","وظيفة محددة ل Dart فقط"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('paul-heyse/CodeAnatomy/dfdl_ref', 'community', 'paul-heyse', 'CodeAnatomy', 'paul-heyse/CodeAnatomy', 'dfdl_ref', 0, 0, 20, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.406Z', '2026-02-18T03:17:49.252Z', NULL, '{"id":"paul-heyse/CodeAnatomy/dfdl_ref","name":"dfdl_ref","description":{"es":"La guía de referencia DFDL proporciona pautas para el uso de DataFusion, DeltaLake y PyArrow","fr":"Le guide de référence DFDL fournit des directives pour l''utilisation de DataFusion, DeltaLake et PyArrow","de":"Das DFDL-Referenzhandbuch bietet Richtlinien für die Verwendung von DataFusion, DeltaLake und PyArrow","pt":"O dfdl_ref fornece diretrizes para usar as APIs de DataFusion, DeltaLake e PyArrow de forma eficaz.","ru":"dfdl_ref предоставляет руководство по эффективному использованию API DataFusion, DeltaLake и PyArrow.","ar":"يوفر dfdl_ref إرشادات لاستخدام برامج API DataFusion و DeltaLake و PyArrow بشكل فعال.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"es":"Guía de Referencia DFDL para Desarrolladores","fr":"Guide de Référence DFDL pour Développeurs","de":"DFDL-Referenzhandbuch für Entwickler","pt":"dfdl_ref: Melhor Prática para APIs de DataFusion","ru":"dfdl_ref: Лучшие практики для API DataFusion","ar":"dfdl_ref: أفضل الممارسات لبرامج API DataFusion","en":"dfdl_ref"},"description":{"es":"La guía de referencia DFDL proporciona pautas para el uso de DataFusion, DeltaLake y PyArrow","fr":"Le guide de référence DFDL fournit des directives pour l''utilisation de DataFusion, DeltaLake et PyArrow","de":"Das DFDL-Referenzhandbuch bietet Richtlinien für die Verwendung von DataFusion, DeltaLake und PyArrow","pt":"O dfdl_ref fornece diretrizes para usar as APIs de DataFusion, DeltaLake e PyArrow de forma eficaz.","ru":"dfdl_ref предоставляет руководство по эффективному использованию API DataFusion, DeltaLake и PyArrow.","ar":"يوفر dfdl_ref إرشادات لاستخدام برامج API DataFusion و DeltaLake و PyArrow بشكل فعال.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"es":["Uso efectivo de DataFusion","Integración con DeltaLake","Utilización de PyArrow","Referencia rápida para APIs","Patrones de implementación locales","Guía para la resolución de problemas"],"fr":["Utilisation efficace de DataFusion","Intégration avec DeltaLake","Utilisation de PyArrow","Référence rapide pour les APIs","Modèles d''implémentation locaux","Guide pour la résolution de problèmes"],"de":["Effektive Verwendung von DataFusion","Integration mit DeltaLake","Verwendung von PyArrow","Schnellreferenz für APIs","Lokale Implementierungsmuster","Handbuch für die Fehlerbehebung"],"pt":["Evite erros comuns ao usar APIs de DataFusion","Aprenda a usar as APIs de DeltaLake e PyArrow","Siga as melhores práticas para implementação","Use padrões locais existentes para implementação","Consulte a documentação de referência para ajuda adicional"],"ru":["Избегайте распространенных ошибок при использовании API DataFusion","Узнайте, как использовать API DeltaLake и PyArrow","Следуйте лучшим практикам для реализации","Используйте существующие локальные шаблоны для реализации","Используйте справочную документацию для дополнительной помощи"],"ar":["تجنب الأخطاء الشائعة عند استخدام برامج API DataFusion","تعرف على كيفية استخدام برامج API DeltaLake و PyArrow","اتبع أفضل الممارسات للتنفيذ","استخدم الأنماط المحلية الحالية للتنفيذ","استخدم وثائق المرجع للحصول على مساعدة إضافية"]},"keywords":{"es":["DataFusion","DeltaLake","PyArrow","DFDL","desarrollo de software","guías de referencia","APIs","implementación local","resolución de problemas"],"fr":["DataFusion","DeltaLake","PyArrow","DFDL","développement de logiciels","guides de référence","API","implémentation locale","résolution de problèmes"],"de":["DataFusion","DeltaLake","PyArrow","DFDL","Softwareentwicklung","Referenzhandbücher","APIs","lokale Implementierung","Fehlerbehebung"],"pt":["DataFusion","DeltaLake","PyArrow","API","Melhores práticas","Desenvolvimento de software","Programação","Tecnologia"],"ru":["DataFusion","DeltaLake","PyArrow","API","Лучшие практики","Разработка программного обеспечения","Программирование","Технологии"],"ar":["DataFusion","DeltaLake","PyArrow","API","أفضل الممارسات","تطوير البرمجيات","البرمجة","التكنولوجيا"]}},"owner":"paul-heyse","repo":"CodeAnatomy","repoPath":"paul-heyse/CodeAnatomy","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.406Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"dfdl_ref","description":"DataFusion + DeltaLake operations manual for this repo. DataFusion is the core query engine; DeltaLake provides the storage layer and integrates tightly via scan providers, schema bridging, and predicate pushdown. Use lookup + local probes; do not guess APIs.","bodyPreview":"## Operating rule: never guess DataFusion/DeltaLake/PyArrow/UDF APIs\nWhen uncertain:\n1) Probe local environment (versions + available methods).\n2) Search the repo for how we already use it.\n3) Open the relevant reference file below (only the section you need).\n4) Implement using *existing local patterns* unless the plan says otherwise.\n\n\n## Reference map (open these files as needed)\n- Core DataFusion Python surfaces (IO, catalog, SQL, DataFrame API): reference/datafusion.md\n- \"Best-in-class depl","body":"## Operating rule: never guess DataFusion/DeltaLake/PyArrow/UDF APIs\nWhen uncertain:\n1) Probe local environment (versions + available methods).\n2) Search the repo for how we already use it.\n3) Open the relevant reference file below (only the section you need).\n4) Implement using *existing local patterns* unless the plan says otherwise.\n\n\n## Reference map (open these files as needed)\n- Core DataFusion Python surfaces (IO, catalog, SQL, DataFrame API): reference/datafusion.md\n- \"Best-in-class deployment gaps\" (caching, stats, observability, planning knobs): reference/datafusion_addendum.md\n- Planning deep dive (logical/physical plan pipeline, introspection, optimization rules): reference/datafusion_planning.md\n- Rust UDF contracts (Scalar/UDAF/UDWF/Async/named args): reference/datafusion_rust_UDFs.md\n- Schema management + schema pitfalls: reference/datafusion_schema.md\n- DeltaLake ↔ DataFusion integration details: reference/deltalake_datafusion_integration.md\n- Advanced Rust integration (PyO3 packaging, wheels, CI, native module distribution): reference/datafusion_deltalake_advanced_rust_integration.md\n- DataFusionMixins trait (Delta snapshot schema + predicate parsing helpers): reference/deltalake_datafusionmixins.md\n- Plan combination (composing DataFusion plans via joins/unions/CTEs, Delta integration, parameterized queries, plan serialization): reference/datafusion_plan_combination.md\n- Rust LogicalPlan programmatic construction (LogicalPlanBuilder, Expr, schema/DFSchema, plan rewriting via TreeNode, extensibility, serialization): reference/Datafusion_logicplan_rust.md\n- DataFusion tracing (Rust community extension: execution spans, metrics capture, partial-result previews, rule-phase instrumentation, OpenTelemetry export): reference/datafusion-tracing.md\n- DeltaLake core (format/protocol, client APIs, 3-layer model): reference/deltalake.md\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:17:49.252Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Analysis Agents needing advanced DataFusion, DeltaLake, and PyArrow API navigation capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级DataFusion、DeltaLake和PyArrow API导航能力的数据分析代理。","ja":"データ分析エージェントが高度なDataFusion、DeltaLake、PyArrow APIナビゲーション機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"데이터 분석 에이전트가 고급 DataFusion, DeltaLake 및 PyArrow API 탐색 기능을 필요로 할 경우 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Análisis de Datos que necesitan capacidades de navegación avanzadas de DataFusion, DeltaLake y API de PyArrow.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de données nécessitant des capacités de navigation avancées de DataFusion, DeltaLake et API PyArrow.","de":"Perfekt für Data-Analytics-Agents, die erweiterte DataFusion-, DeltaLake- und PyArrow-API-Navigationsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Dados que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de navegação de APIs DataFusion, DeltaLake e PyArrow.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа данных, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности навигации по API DataFusion, DeltaLake и PyArrow.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تحليل البيانات التي تحتاج إلى قدرات متقدمة في ملاحة واجهات برمجة التطبيقات DataFusion و DeltaLake و PyArrow."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to accurately implement DataFusion, DeltaLake, and PyArrow APIs by probing local environments, searching existing code repositories, and referencing core API documentation for DataFusion Python surfaces, including IO, catalog, SQL, and DataFrame API, ensuring compliance with existing local patterns.","zh":"通过探测本地环境、搜索现有代码仓库以及参考DataFusion Python表面（包括IO、目录、SQL和DataFrame API）的核心API文档，赋予代理准确实现DataFusion、DeltaLake和PyArrow API的能力，确保遵守现有的本地模式。","ja":"ローカル環境をプローブし、既存のコードリポジトリを検索し、DataFusion Pythonサーフェス（IO、カタログ、SQL、DataFrame APIを含む）のコアAPIドキュメントを参照することで、エージェントがDataFusion、DeltaLake、PyArrow APIを正確に実装できるようにし、既存のローカルパターンに準拠します。","ko":"로컬 환경을 프로브하고 기존 코드 저장소를 검색하며 DataFusion Python 표면(IO, 카탈로그, SQL 및 DataFrame API 포함)의 핵심 API 문서를 참조하여 에이전트가 DataFusion, DeltaLake 및 PyArrow API를 정확하게 구현할 수 있도록 하며 기존 로컬 패턴을 준수합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar DataFusion, DeltaLake y PyArrow APIs de forma precisa, sondeando entornos locales, buscando en repositorios de código existentes y haciendo referencia a la documentación de superficies de Python de DataFusion, incluyendo IO, catálogo, SQL y API de DataFrame, garantizando el cumplimiento de los patrones locales existentes.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre avec précision les API DataFusion, DeltaLake et PyArrow en sonnant les environnements locaux, en recherchant dans les référentiels de code existants et en faisant référence à la documentation des surfaces Python de DataFusion, y compris IO, catalogue, SQL et API de DataFrame, garantissant ainsi le respect des modèles locaux existants.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, DataFusion-, DeltaLake- und PyArrow-APIs genau umzusetzen, indem sie lokale Umgebungen abfragen, in bestehenden Code-Repositorys suchen und auf die Kern-API-Dokumentation für DataFusion-Python-Oberflächen verweisen, einschließlich IO, Katalog, SQL und DataFrame-API, um die Einhaltung bestehender lokaler Muster sicherzustellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar com precisão as APIs DataFusion, DeltaLake e PyArrow, sondando ambientes locais, procurando repositórios de código existentes e referenciando a documentação de superfícies Python do DataFusion, incluindo IO, catálogo, SQL e API de DataFrame, garantindo a conformidade com os padrões locais existentes.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью точно реализовать API DataFusion, DeltaLake и PyArrow, зондировать локальные среды, искать существующие репозитории кода и ссылаться на документацию по поверхностям Python DataFusion, включая IO, каталог, SQL и API DataFrame, обеспечивая соответствие существующим местным шаблонам.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تنفيذ واجهات برمجة التطبيقات DataFusion و DeltaLake و PyArrow بدقة من خلال سондاج البيئات المحلية و البحث في مستودعات الشفرة الحالية و الإشارة إلى توثيق سطح python لبرنامج DataFusion، بما في ذلك IO و الفهرس و SQL و واجهة برمجة تطبيقات DataFrame، مما يضمن الامتثال للنماذج المحلية الحالية."},"useCases":{"en":["Probing local environments for available DataFusion methods","Searching code repositories for existing DeltaLake and PyArrow API usage patterns","Referencing DataFusion Python surfaces documentation for accurate API implementation"],"zh":["探测本地环境以获取可用的DataFusion方法","搜索代码仓库以获取现有的DeltaLake和PyArrow API使用模式","参考DataFusion Python表面文档以实现准确的API"],"ja":["利用可能なDataFusionメソッドを取得するためにローカル環境をプローブする","既存のDeltaLakeとPyArrow API使用パターンを取得するためにコードリポジトリを検索する","正確なAPI実装のためにDataFusion Pythonサーフェスドキュメントを参照する"],"ko":["사용 가능한 DataFusion 메서드를 얻기 위해 로컬 환경을 프로브하는 것","기존의 DeltaLake 및 PyArrow API 사용 패턴을 얻기 위해 코드 저장소를 검색하는 것","정확한 API 구현을 위해 DataFusion Python 표면 문서를 참조하는 것"],"es":["Sondear entornos locales para métodos de DataFusion disponibles","Buscar en repositorios de código para patrones de uso de API de DeltaLake y PyArrow existentes","Hacer referencia a la documentación de superficies de Python de DataFusion para una implementación de API precisa"],"fr":["Sonder les environnements locaux pour les méthodes DataFusion disponibles","Rechercher dans les référentiels de code pour les modèles d''utilisation de l''API DeltaLake et PyArrow existants","Faire référence à la documentation des surfaces Python de DataFusion pour une mise en œuvre précise de l''API"],"de":["Lokale Umgebungen auf verfügbare DataFusion-Methoden abfragen","In Code-Repositorys nach bestehenden NutzungsMustern für DeltaLake- und PyArrow-APIs suchen","Auf die Dokumentation von DataFusion-Python-Oberflächen verweisen, um eine genaue API-Implementierung sicherzustellen"],"pt":["Sondagem de ambientes locais para métodos DataFusion disponíveis","Pesquisa em repositórios de código para padrões de uso de API DeltaLake e PyArrow existentes","Referência à documentação de superfícies Python do DataFusion para implementação precisa de API"],"ru":["Зондирование локальных сред для доступных методов DataFusion","Поиск в репозиториях кода для существующих шаблонов использования API DeltaLake и PyArrow","Ссылка на документацию по поверхностям Python DataFusion для точной реализации API"],"ar":["سلسلة بيئات محلية للطرق المتاحة من DataFusion","البحث في مستودعات الشفرة عن أنماط استخدام واجهة برمجة التطبيقات DeltaLake و PyArrow الحالية","الإشارة إلى توثيق سطح python لبرنامج DataFusion من أجل تنفيذ واجهة برمجة التطبيقات بدقة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to local environment versions and available methods","Limited to DataFusion, DeltaLake, and PyArrow APIs","Needs existing code repository for reference"],"zh":["需要访问本地环境版本和可用方法","仅限DataFusion、DeltaLake和PyArrow API","需要现有的代码仓库作为参考"],"ja":["ローカル環境バージョンと利用可能なメソッドへのアクセスが必要","DataFusion、DeltaLake、PyArrow APIのみ","参照用の既存のコードリポジトリが必要"],"ko":["로컬 환경 버전 및 사용 가능한 메서드에 대한 액세스가 필요함","DataFusion, DeltaLake 및 PyArrow API에만 한정됨","참조용 기존 코드 저장소가 필요함"],"es":["Requiere acceso a versiones de entornos locales y métodos disponibles","Limitado a DataFusion, DeltaLake y PyArrow APIs","Necesita un repositorio de código existente para referencia"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès aux versions d''environnements locaux et aux méthodes disponibles","Limité aux API DataFusion, DeltaLake et PyArrow","Nécessite un référentiel de code existant pour référence"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf lokale Umgebungsversionen und verfügbare Methoden","Begrenzt auf DataFusion-, DeltaLake- und PyArrow-APIs","Benötigt ein bestehendes Code-Repository für Referenzen"],"pt":["Requer acesso às versões do ambiente local e métodos disponíveis","Limitado às APIs DataFusion, DeltaLake e PyArrow","Necessita de um repositório de código existente para referência"],"ru":["Требует доступа к версиям локальной среды и доступным методам","Ограничен API DataFusion, DeltaLake и PyArrow","Требует существующего репозитория кода для ссылки"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى الإصدارات البيئية المحلية و الطرق المتاحة","محدود بواجهات برمجة التطبيقات DataFusion و DeltaLake و PyArrow","يحتاج إلى مستودع شفرة حالي للإشارة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":20}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('grenos/gh-viewer/karpathy', 'community', 'grenos', 'gh-viewer', 'grenos/gh-viewer', 'karpathy', 0, 0, 30, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.406Z', '2026-02-18T03:17:51.633Z', NULL, '{"id":"grenos/gh-viewer/karpathy","name":"karpathy","description":{"zh":"Karpathy 编码原则是关于编写干净、简洁、有目的的代码的指导方针","ja":"Karpathy コーディング原則は、クリーンでミニマルで目的のあるコードを書くためのガイドラインです","ko":"Karpathy 코딩 원칙은 깨끗하고 최소하고 목적이 있는 코드를 작성하는 가이드라인입니다","es":"Los principios de Karpathy ofrecen pautas para escribir código limpio, minimalista y con propósito.","fr":"Les principes de Karpathy fournissent des lignes directrices pour écrire du code propre, minimaliste et à des fins précises.","de":"Die Karpathy-Prinzipien bieten Richtlinien für das Schreiben von sauberem, minimalistischem und zweckorientiertem Code.","pt":"Os princípios de Karpathy são diretrizes para escrever código limpo, minimalista e com propósito. Aprenda a pensar antes de codificar e a priorizar a simplicidade.","ru":"Принципы Карпатия - это руководство для написания чистого, минималистичного и целенаправленного кода. Узнайте, как думать перед кодированием и отдавать приоритет простоте.","ar":"مبادئ كارباتي هي إرشادات لكتابة الكود النظيف والمتواضع والغرضي. تعلم كيف تفكر قبل البرمجة وأعط الأولوية للبساطة.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Karpathy 编码原则","ja":"Karpathy コーディング原則","ko":"Karpathy 코딩 원칙","es":"Principios de codificación Karpathy","fr":"Principes de codage Karpathy","de":"Karpathy Codierprinzipien","pt":"Princípios de Karpathy para Codificação Limpa","ru":"Принципы Карпатия для чистого кода","ar":"مبادئ كارباتي لكتابة الكود النظيف","en":"karpathy"},"description":{"zh":"Karpathy 编码原则是关于编写干净、简洁、有目的的代码的指导方针","ja":"Karpathy コーディング原則は、クリーンでミニマルで目的のあるコードを書くためのガイドラインです","ko":"Karpathy 코딩 원칙은 깨끗하고 최소하고 목적이 있는 코드를 작성하는 가이드라인입니다","es":"Los principios de Karpathy ofrecen pautas para escribir código limpio, minimalista y con propósito.","fr":"Les principes de Karpathy fournissent des lignes directrices pour écrire du code propre, minimaliste et à des fins précises.","de":"Die Karpathy-Prinzipien bieten Richtlinien für das Schreiben von sauberem, minimalistischem und zweckorientiertem Code.","pt":"Os princípios de Karpathy são diretrizes para escrever código limpo, minimalista e com propósito. Aprenda a pensar antes de codificar e a priorizar a simplic...","ru":"Принципы Карпатия - это руководство для написания чистого, минималистичного и целенаправленного кода. Узнайте, как думать перед кодированием и отдавать приор...","ar":"مبادئ كارباتي هي إرشادات لكتابة الكود النظيف والمتواضع والغرضي. تعلم كيف تفكر قبل البرمجة وأعط الأولوية للبساطة.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["思考在编码前","简洁优先","明确假设","表达疑惑","推动简单的方法"],"ja":["コードを書く前に考える","シンプルさを優先する","仮定を明確にする","混乱を表現する","シンプルな方法を推進する"],"ko":["코딩하기 전에 생각하기","간결성을 우선시","가정들을 명확히","혼란을 표현","간단한 방법을推進"],"es":["Pensar antes de codificar","Priorizar la simplicidad","Explicitar las suposiciones","Presentar múltiples interpretaciones","Simplificar el enfoque"],"fr":["Réfléchir avant de coder","Donner la priorité à la simplicité","Expliciter les hypothèses","Présenter plusieurs interprétations","Simplifier l''approche"],"de":["Bevor Sie codieren, nachdenken","Einfachheit priorisieren","Annahmen explizit machen","Mehrere Interpretationen präsentieren","Ansatz vereinfachen"],"pt":["Pensar antes de codificar","Priorizar a simplicidade","Explicitar suposições","Apresentar interpretações múltiplas","Questionar a complexidade"],"ru":["Думать перед кодированием","Отдавать приоритет простоте","Явно выражать предположения","Представлять множественные интерпретации","Вопросить сложность"],"ar":["التفكير قبل البرمجة","إعطاء الأولوية للبساطة","توضيح الافتراضات","عرض التأويلات المتعددة","استجواب التعقيد"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Karpathy 编码原则","编码指导方针","简洁编码","明确编码","代码质量","编程最佳实践"],"ja":["Karpathy コーディング原則","コーディングガイドライン","シンプルコーディング","明確コーディング","コード品質","プログラミングベストプラクティス"],"ko":["Karpathy 코딩 원칙","코딩 가이드라인","간결 코딩","명확 코딩","코드 품질","프로그래밍 최선의 관행"],"es":["principios de codificación","código limpio","código minimalista","desarrollo de software","mejores prácticas de codificación","eficiencia del código"],"fr":["principes de codage","code propre","code minimaliste","développement de logiciels","meilleures pratiques de codage","efficacité du code"],"de":["Codierprinzipien","sauberer Code","minimalistischer Code","Software-Entwicklung","Best-Practices für Codierung","Code-Effizienz"],"pt":["princípios de karpathy","código limpo","codificação minimalista","desenvolvimento de software","melhores práticas de codificação","programação eficiente"],"ru":["принципы Карпатия","чистый код","минималистичное программирование","разработка программного обеспечения","лучшие практики кодирования","эффективное программирование"],"ar":["مبادئ كارباتي","الكود النظيف","البرمجة المتواضعة","تطوير البرمجيات","أفضل الممارسات لكتابة الكود","البرمجة الفعالة"]}},"owner":"grenos","repo":"gh-viewer","repoPath":"grenos/gh-viewer","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.406Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"karpathy","description":"Coding principles for simplicity, clarity, and surgical precision. Use when you want Claude to think before coding, keep solutions minimal, make surgical changes, and define verifiable success criteria. Triggers on: karpathy mode, think before coding, simplicity first, surgical changes.","bodyPreview":"# Karpathy Coding Principles\n\nPrinciples for writing clean, minimal, and purposeful code.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Think Before Coding\n\n**Don''t assume. Don''t hide confusion. Surface tradeoffs.**\n\nBefore implementing:\n\n- State your assumptions explicitly. If uncertain, ask.\n- If multiple interpretations exist, present them - don''t pick silently.\n- If a simpler approach exists, say so. Push back when warranted.\n- If something is unclear, stop. Name what''s confusing. Ask.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Simplicity First\n\n**Minimum","body":"# Karpathy Coding Principles\n\nPrinciples for writing clean, minimal, and purposeful code.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Think Before Coding\n\n**Don''t assume. Don''t hide confusion. Surface tradeoffs.**\n\nBefore implementing:\n\n- State your assumptions explicitly. If uncertain, ask.\n- If multiple interpretations exist, present them - don''t pick silently.\n- If a simpler approach exists, say so. Push back when warranted.\n- If something is unclear, stop. Name what''s confusing. Ask.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Simplicity First\n\n**Minimum code that solves the problem. Nothing speculative.**\n\n- No features beyond what was asked.\n- No abstractions for single-use code.\n- No \"flexibility\" or \"configurability\" that wasn''t requested.\n- No error handling for impossible scenarios.\n- If you write 200 lines and it could be 50, rewrite it.\n\nAsk yourself: \"Would a senior engineer say this is overcomplicated?\" If yes, simplify.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Surgical Changes\n\n**Touch only what you must. Clean up only your own mess.**\n\nWhen editing existing code:\n\n- Don''t \"improve\" adjacent code, comments, or formatting.\n- Don''t refactor things that aren''t broken.\n- Match existing style, even if you''d do it differently.\n- If you notice unrelated dead code, mention it - don''t delete it.\n\nWhen your changes create orphans:\n\n- Remove imports/variables/functions that YOUR changes made unused.\n- Don''t remove pre-existing dead code unless asked.\n\nThe test: Every changed line should trace directly to the user''s request.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Goal-Driven Execution\n\n**Define success criteria. Loop until verified.**\n\nTransform tasks into verifiable goals:\n\n- \"Add validation\" -> \"Write tests for invalid inputs, then make them pass\"\n- \"Fix the bug\" -> \"Write a test that reproduces it, then make it pass\"\n- \"Refactor X\" -> \"Ensure tests pass before and after\"\n\nFor multi-step tasks, state a brief plan:\n\n```\n1. [Step] -> verify: [check]\n2. [Step] -> verify: [check]\n3. [Step] -> verify: [check]\n```\n\nStrong success criteria let you loop independently. Weak criteria (\"make it work\") require constant clarification.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:17:51.633Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing adherence to clean coding principles.","zh":"非常适合需要遵循清晰编码原则的代码审查代理","ja":"クリーンなコーディングの原則に従う必要があるコードレビューエージェントに最適","ko":"클린 코딩 원칙을 준수해야 하는 코드 리뷰 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de revisión de código que necesitan adherirse a principios de codificación limpios.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''examen de code ayant besoin de respecter les principes de codage propres.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agents, die sich an saubere Programmierprinzipien halten müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam de aderência a princípios de codificação limpa.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов кодового обзора, которым необходима соблюдение принципов чистого кодирования.","ar":" مثالي لعميل استعراض الشفرة الذي يحتاج إلى الالتزام بمبادئ البرمجة النظيفة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write minimal and purposeful code by surfacing tradeoffs, pushing back on complexity, and stating assumptions explicitly, utilizing principles like ''Think Before Coding'' and ''Simplicity First''.","zh":"通过表面化权衡、抵制复杂性和明确说明假设，利用像 ''思考再编码'' 和 ''简洁优先'' 的原则，赋予代理编写最小化和有目的的代码的能力","ja":"トレードオフを浮き彫りにし、複雑さに抵抗し、仮定を明示的に述べることで、エージェントが最小限の目的のあるコードを書くことを可能にし、''コードを書く前に考える'' や ''シンプルさを第一に'' などの原則を利用する","ko":"트레이드오프를 노출시키고, 복잡성을 밀어내고, 가정을 명시적으로 설명함으로써, ''코딩하기 전에 생각하기'' 와 ''단순함을 먼저'' 같은 원리를 사용하여, 에이전트가 최소화된 목적있는 코드를 작성할 수 있도록 하는 능력을 부여","es":"Habilita a los agentes a escribir código mínimo y con propósito, resaltando las compensaciones, rechazando la complejidad y declarando las suposiciones explícitamente, utilizando principios como ''Pensar antes de codificar'' y ''Simplicidad primero''.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''écrire un code minimal et à dessein en mettant en évidence les compromis, en rejetant la complexité et en énonçant explicitement les hypothèses, en utilisant des principes comme ''Réfléchir avant de coder'' et ''Simplicité d''abord''.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, minimales und zweckmäßiges Code zu schreiben, indem es Kompromisse aufzeigt, die Komplexität zurückdrängt und Annahmen explizit macht, indem es Prinzipien wie ''Denken, bevor Sie coden'' und ''Einfachheit zuerst'' verwendet.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a escreverem códigos mínimos e propositais, ao trazer à tona compromissos, resistir à complexidade e declarar suposições explicitamente, utilizando princípios como ''Pense Antes de Codificar'' e ''Simplicidade em Primeiro Lugar''.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью писать минимальный и целесообразный код, выявляя компромиссы, сопротивляясь сложности и явно заявляя предположения, используя принципы, такие как ''Подумайте, прежде чем кодировать'' и ''Простота прежде всего''.","ar":"يمكّن العميل من كتابة شفرة صغيرة وغرضية من خلال إبراز التنازلات والضغط على التعقيد والتعبير الصريح عن الافتراضات، باستخدام مبادئ مثل ''افكر قبل البرمجة'' و ''البساطة أولا''."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging ambiguous code implementations","Generating transparent and interpretable code","Automating code review for simplicity and clarity"],"zh":["调试模糊的代码实现","生成透明和可解释的代码","自动化代码审查以实现简单性和明晰性"],"ja":["曖昧なコード実装のデバッグ","透明で解釈可能なコードの生成","シンプルさと明瞭さのためのコードレビューの自動化"],"ko":["模糊한 코드 구현 디버깅","투명하고 해석 가능한 코드 생성","단순성과 명확성을 위한 코드 리뷰 자동화"],"es":["Depuración de implementaciones de código ambiguas","Generación de código transparente e interpretable","Automatización de la revisión de código para simplicidad y claridad"],"fr":["Débogage d''implémentations de code ambiguës","Génération de code transparent et interprétable","Automatisation de l''examen de code pour la simplicité et la clarté"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung bei mehrdeutigen Codeimplementierungen","Erzeugung von transparentem und interpretierbarem Code","Automatisierung der Code-Überprüfung für Einfachheit und Klarheit"],"pt":["Depuração de implementações de código ambíguas","Geração de código transparente e interpretável","Automatização da revisão de código para simplicidade e clareza"],"ru":["Отладка неоднозначных реализаций кода","Генерация прозрачный и интерпретируемый код","Автоматизация обзора кода для простоты и ясности"],"ar":["تصحيح شفرة التطبيق الغامض","توليد شفرة شفافة وقابلة للتفسير","أتمتة استعراض الشفرة من أجل البساطة والوضوح"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires explicit assumption stating","Demands simplicity over complexity","Needs active feedback for unclear implementations"],"zh":["需要明确的假设说明","要求简单性优于复杂性","需要对不明确的实现进行主动反馈"],"ja":["明示的な仮定の説明が必要","シンプルさを複雑さよりも要求","不明確な実装に対するフィードバックが必要"],"ko":["명확한 가정이 필요","단순성을 복잡성보다 요구","불명확한 구현에 대한 피드백이 필요"],"es":["Requiere la declaración explícita de suposiciones","Exige simplicidad sobre complejidad","Necesita retroalimentación activa para implementaciones poco claras"],"fr":["Nécessite la déclaration explicite d''hypothèses","Exige la simplicité plutôt que la complexité","Nécessite une rétroaction active pour les implémentations peu claires"],"de":["Benötigt die explizite Angabe von Annahmen","Fordert Einfachheit vor Komplexität","Benötigt aktives Feedback für unklare Implementierungen"],"pt":["Exige declaração explícita de suposições","Exige simplicidade sobre complexidade","Necessita de feedback ativo para implementações não claras"],"ru":["Требует явного заявления предположений","Требует простоты над сложностью","Требует активной обратной связи для неясных реализаций"],"ar":["يتطلب بيان افتراض صريح","يتطلب بساطة أكثر من تعقيد","يحتاج إلى ملاحظات نشطة لتنفيذ غير واضح"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('gutierrezp22/administracion-departamentos/jira-epic', 'community', 'gutierrezp22', 'administracion-departamentos', 'gutierrezp22/administracion-departamentos', 'jira-epic', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.406Z', '2026-02-18T03:18:17.085Z', NULL, '{"id":"gutierrezp22/administracion-departamentos/jira-epic","name":"jira-epic","description":{"zh":"Jira ","ja":"Jira","ko":"Jira ","es":"El skill de Jira Epic ayuda a crear épicos para características grandes y refactorizaciones. Incluye una plantilla para describir requisitos y funcionalidades.","fr":"Le skill Jira Epic aide à créer des épics pour de grandes fonctionnalités et des refactorisations. Il inclut un modèle pour décrire les exigences et les fonctionnalités.","de":"Das Jira-Epic-Skill hilft bei der Erstellung von Epics für große Funktionen und Refactorings. Es enthält eine Vorlage zur Beschreibung von Anforderungen und Funktionalitäten.","pt":"O skill Jira Epic ajuda a criar epissódios para projetos complexos, melhorando a colaboração e a produtividade","ru":"Навык Jira Эпик помогает создавать эпизоды для сложных проектов, улучшая сотрудничество и производительность","ar":"مهارة جيرا إبك تساعد على إنشاء الحلقات للمشاريع المعقدة، وتحسين التعاون والإنتاجية","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Jira ","ja":"Jira","ko":"Jira ","es":"Creación de épicos en Jira para desarrolladores","fr":"Création d''épics Jira pour les développeurs","de":"Erstellung von Jira-Epics für Entwickler","pt":"Jira Epic: Criando Episódios para Projetos de Sucesso","ru":"Jira Эпик: Создание Эпизодов для Успешных Проектов","ar":"جيرا إبك: إنشاء الحلقات لنجاح المشاريع","en":"jira-epic"},"description":{"zh":"Jira ","ja":"Jira","ko":"Jira ","es":"El skill de Jira Epic ayuda a crear épicos para características grandes y refactorizaciones. Incluye una plantilla para describir requisitos y funcionalidades.","fr":"Le skill Jira Epic aide à créer des épics pour de grandes fonctionnalités et des refactorisations. Il inclut un modèle pour décrire les exigences et les fonc...","de":"Das Jira-Epic-Skill hilft bei der Erstellung von Epics für große Funktionen und Refactorings. Es enthält eine Vorlage zur Beschreibung von Anforderungen und ...","pt":"O skill Jira Epic ajuda a criar epissódios para projetos complexos, melhorando a colaboração e a produtividade","ru":"Навык Jira Эпик помогает создавать эпизоды для сложных проектов, улучшая сотрудничество и производительность","ar":"مهارة جيرا إبك تساعد على إنشاء الحلقات للمشاريع المعقدة، وتحسين التعاون والإنتاجية","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["Jira ","API+UI+SDK"," ","Figma"],"ja":["Jira","API+UI+SDK","","Figma"],"ko":["Jira ","API+UI+SDK","","Figma"],"es":["Plantilla para describir requisitos y funcionalidades","Creación de épicos para características grandes y refactorizaciones","Integración con Figma para diseño de interfaz de usuario","Secciones para describir la funcionalidad y los requisitos","Soporte para múltiples componentes y API"],"fr":["Modèle pour décrire les exigences et les fonctionnalités","Création d''épics pour de grandes fonctionnalités et des refactorisations","Intégration avec Figma pour la conception d''interface utilisateur","Sections pour décrire la fonctionnalité et les exigences","Prise en charge de plusieurs composants et API"],"de":["Vorlage zur Beschreibung von Anforderungen und Funktionalitäten","Erstellung von Epics für große Funktionen und Refactorings","Integration mit Figma für Benutzeroberflächendesign","Abschnitte zur Beschreibung der Funktionalität und der Anforderungen","Unterstützung für mehrere Komponenten und APIs"],"pt":["Criação de epissódios para projetos complexos","Melhoria da colaboração entre equipes","Aumento da produtividade","Gerenciamento de recursos","Integração com o Figma"],"ru":["Создание эпизодов для сложных проектов","Улучшение сотрудничества между командами","Повышение производительности","Управление ресурсами","Интеграция с Figma"],"ar":["إنشاء الحلقات للمشاريع المعقدة","تحسين التعاون بين الفرق","زيادة الإنتاجية","إدارة الموارد","التكامل مع الفيجما"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Jira ","Jira ","API","UI","SDK","Figma"," "],"ja":["Jira","Jira","API","UI","SDK","Figma",""],"ko":["Jira ","Jira ","API","UI","SDK","Figma",""],"es":["Jira Epic","creación de épicos","refactorización","desarrollo de software","plantilla de requisitos","Figma","API","SDK","UI"],"fr":["Jira Epic","création d''épics","refactoring","développement de logiciels","modèle d''exigences","Figma","API","SDK","UI"],"de":["Jira-Epic","Erstellung von Epics","Refactoring","Softwareentwicklung","Anforderungsvorlage","Figma","API","SDK","Benutzeroberfläche"],"pt":["Jira Epic","projetos complexos","colaboração","produtividade","gerenciamento de recursos","Figma","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["Jira Эпик","сложные проекты","сотрудничество","производительность","управление ресурсами","Figma","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["جيرا إبك","المشاريع المعقدة","التعاون","الإنتاجية","إدارة الموارد","الفيجما","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"gutierrezp22","repo":"administracion-departamentos","repoPath":"gutierrezp22/administracion-departamentos","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.406Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"jira-epic","description":">","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"## When to Use\n\nUse this skill when creating Jira epics for:\n- Large features spanning multiple components\n- New views/pages in the application\n- Major refactoring initiatives\n- Features requiring API + UI + SDK work\n\n## Epic Template\n\n```markdown\n# {Epic Title}\n\n**Figma:** {figma link if available}\n\n## Feature Overview\n\n{2-3 paragraph description of what this feature does and why it''s needed}\n\n## Requirements\n\n### {Section 1: Major Functionality Area}\n\n#### {Subsection}\n- Requirement 1\n- Requir","body":"## When to Use\n\nUse this skill when creating Jira epics for:\n- Large features spanning multiple components\n- New views/pages in the application\n- Major refactoring initiatives\n- Features requiring API + UI + SDK work\n\n## Epic Template\n\n```markdown\n# {Epic Title}\n\n**Figma:** {figma link if available}\n\n## Feature Overview\n\n{2-3 paragraph description of what this feature does and why it''s needed}\n\n## Requirements\n\n### {Section 1: Major Functionality Area}\n\n#### {Subsection}\n- Requirement 1\n- Requirement 2\n- Requirement 3\n\n#### {Another Subsection}\n- Requirement 1\n- Requirement 2\n\n### {Section 2: Another Major Area}\n\n#### {Subsection}\n- Requirement 1\n- Requirement 2\n\n## Technical Considerations\n\n### Performance\n- {Performance requirement 1}\n- {Performance requirement 2}\n\n### Data Integration\n- {Data source}\n- {Integration points}\n\n### UI Components\n- {Component 1}\n- {Component 2}\n\n## Implementation Checklist\n\n- [ ] {Major deliverable 1}\n- [ ] {Major deliverable 2}\n- [ ] {Major deliverable 3}\n\n## Diagrams\n\n{Mermaid diagrams for architecture, flow, data model, etc.}\n```\n\n## Epic Title Conventions\n\nFormat: `[EPIC] Feature Name`\n\n**Examples:**\n- `[EPIC] Findings View`\n- `[EPIC] Multi-tenant Support`\n- `[EPIC] Compliance Dashboard Redesign`\n- `[EPIC] GovCloud Support`\n\n## Required Sections\n\n### 1. Feature Overview\nBrief but complete description of:\n- What the feature does\n- Who uses it\n- Why it''s needed\n\n### 2. Requirements\nOrganized by functional area:\n- Group related requirements together\n- Use clear headers and subheaders\n- Be specific and testable\n\n### 3. Technical Considerations\nAlways include:\n- **Performance**: Large dataset handling, pagination, caching\n- **Data Integration**: Data sources, APIs, relationships\n- **UI Components**: Reusable components, design system usage\n\n### 4. Implementation Checklist\nHigh-level deliverables that will become individual tasks:\n- Each checkbox = potential Jira task\n- Order by dependency (API before UI)\n- Include testing milestones\n\n## Diagrams\n\nUse Mermaid for:\n\n### Architecture Diagrams\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    UI[UI Components] --> API[API Endpoints]\n    API --> SDK[Prowler SDK]\n    SDK --> Cloud[Cloud Providers]\n```\n\n### Data Flow Diagrams\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    User->>UI: Apply filters\n    UI->>API: GET /findings?filters\n    API->>DB: Query findings\n    DB-->>API: Results\n    API-->>UI: JSON response\n    UI-->>User: Render table\n```\n\n### State Diagrams\n```mermaid\nstateDiagram-v2\n    [*] --> Pending\n    Pending --> InProgress: Start triage\n    InProgress --> Resolved: Mark resolved\n    InProgress --> Pending: Reset\n    Resolved --> [*]\n```\n\n### Entity Relationship Diagrams\n```mermaid\nerDiagram\n    FINDING ||--o{ RESOURCE : affects\n    FINDING }|--|| CHECK : \"belongs to\"\n    RESOURCE }|--|| ACCOUNT : \"belongs to\"\n    ACCOUNT }|--|| PROVIDER : \"belongs to\"\n```\n\n## Splitting Epic into Tasks\n\nAfter creating the epic, generate individual tasks using the `jira-task` skill:\n\n### Task Naming Pattern\nFrom epic `[EPIC] Findings View`, create:\n- `[FEATURE] Findings table with pagination (UI)`\n- `[FEATURE] Findings filters - provider and account (UI)`\n- `[FEATURE] Findings detail panel - Overview tab (UI)`\n- `[FEATURE] Findings detail panel - Resources tab (UI)`\n- `[FEATURE] Findings bulk actions - mute/suppress (API + UI)`\n- `[FEATURE] Findings search functionality (API + UI)`\n\n### Task Dependencies\nAlways specify in each task:\n```markdown\n## Related Tasks\n- Epic: [EPIC] Findings View\n- Blocked by: [task if any]\n- Blocks: [task if any]\n```\n\n## Figma Integration\n\nWhen Figma links are provided:\n- Include main Figma link at top\n- Reference specific frames in relevant sections\n- Example: `https://www.figma.com/design/xxx?node-id=1830-44712&m=dev`\n\n## Output Format\n\n```markdown\n## Epic: [EPIC] {Title}\n\n{Full epic content following template}\n\n---\n\n## Suggested Tasks\n\nBased on this epic, create the following tasks:\n\n| # | Title | Component | Blocked By |\n|---|-------|-----------|------------|\n| 1 | [FEATURE] Task name | API | - |\n| 2 | [FEATURE] Task name | UI | Task 1 |\n| 3 | [FEATURE] Task name | UI | Task 2 |\n\nWould you like me to generate the full task descriptions?\n```\n\n## Checklist Before Submitting\n\n1. ✅ Title follows `[EPIC] Feature Name` format\n2. ✅ Feature Overview explains what/who/why\n3. ✅ Requirements are organized by functional area\n4. ✅ Technical Considerations cover performance, data, UI\n5. ✅ Implementation Checklist has high-level deliverables\n6. ✅ Diagrams included where helpful (Mermaid format)\n7. ✅ Figma links included if available\n8. ✅ Suggested tasks table provided at the end\n\n## Formatting Rules\n\n**CRITICAL:** All output MUST be in Markdown format, ready to paste into Jira.\n\n- Use `#` for epic title, `##` for main sections, `###` for subsections\n- Use `**bold**` for emphasis\n- Use `- [ ]` for checkboxes in Implementation Checklist\n- Use ``` for code blocks and Mermaid diagrams\n- Use `backticks` for file paths, commands, and code references\n- Use tables for Suggested Tasks section\n- Use `---` to separate epic from suggested tasks\n\n## Jira MCP Integration\n\n**CRITICAL:** When creating epics via MCP, use these exact parameters:\n\n### Required Fields\n\n```json\n{\n  \"project_key\": \"PROWLER\",\n  \"summary\": \"[EPIC] Feature name\",\n  \"issue_type\": \"Epic\",\n  \"additional_fields\": {\n    \"customfield_10359\": {\"value\": \"UI\"}\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Team Field (REQUIRED)\n\nThe `customfield_10359` (Team) field is **REQUIRED**. Options:\n- `\"UI\"` - Frontend epics\n- `\"API\"` - Backend epics\n- `\"SDK\"` - Prowler SDK epics\n\n### Work Item Description Field\n\n**IMPORTANT:** The project uses `customfield_10363` (Work Item Description) instead of the standard `description` field for display in the UI.\n\n**CRITICAL:** Use **Jira Wiki markup**, NOT Markdown:\n- `h2.` instead of `##`\n- `*text*` for bold instead of `**text**`\n- `* item` for bullets (same)\n- `** subitem` for nested bullets\n\nAfter creating the epic, update the description with:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"customfield_10363\": \"h2. Feature Overview\\n\\n{overview}\\n\\nh2. Requirements\\n\\n*{Section 1}*\\n* {requirement 1}\\n* {requirement 2}\\n\\n*{Section 2}*\\n* {requirement 1}\\n* {requirement 2}\\n\\nh2. Technical Considerations\\n\\n*Performance:*\\n* {consideration 1}\\n\\n*Data Integration:*\\n* {consideration 2}\\n\\nh2. Implementation Checklist\\n\\n* [ ] {deliverable 1}\\n* [ ] {deliverable 2}\\n* [ ] {deliverable 3}\"\n}\n```\n\n### Linking Tasks to Epic\n\nWhen creating child tasks, use the epic key as parent:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"additional_fields\": {\n    \"parent\": \"PROWLER-XXX\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Workflow Transitions\n\n```\nBacklog (10037) → To Do (14) → In Progress (11) → Done (21)\n                → Blocked (10)\n```\n\n### MCP Commands Sequence\n\n1. **Create epic:**\n```\nmcp__mcp-atlassian__jira_create_issue (issue_type: \"Epic\")\n```\n\n2. **Update Work Item Description:**\n```\nmcp__mcp-atlassian__jira_update_issue with customfield_10363\n```\n\n3. **Create child tasks:**\n```\nmcp__mcp-atlassian__jira_create_issue with parent: EPIC-KEY\n```\n\n4. **Assign and transition:**\n```\nmcp__mcp-atlassian__jira_update_issue (assignee)\nmcp__mcp-atlassian__jira_transition_issue (status)\n```\n\n## Keywords\njira, epic, feature, initiative, prowler, large feature\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:18:17.085Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Project Management Agents needing structured issue tracking and epic creation for Jira","zh":"非常适合需要结构化问题跟踪和史诗创建的Jira项目管理代理","ja":"Jiraの構造化された問題追跡とエピック作成が必要なプロジェクト管理エージェントに最適","ko":"지라에서 구조화된 문제 추적 및 에픽 생성이 필요한 프로젝트 관리 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de gestión de proyectos que necesitan un seguimiento de problemas estructurado y creación de epics para Jira","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de gestion de projet ayant besoin d''un suivi de problèmes structuré et de création d''épics pour Jira","de":"Perfekt für Projektmanagement-Agenten, die ein strukturiertes Problem-Tracking und die Erstellung von Epics für Jira benötigen","pt":"Perfect for Project Management Agents needing structured issue tracking and epic creation for Jira","ru":"Perfect for Project Management Agents needing structured issue tracking and epic creation for Jira","ar":"Perfect for Project Management Agents needing structured issue tracking and epic creation for Jira"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create and manage Jira epics for large features, new views, and refactoring initiatives, utilizing markdown templates and Figma links for detailed feature overviews and requirements","zh":"赋予代理创建和管理大型功能、新的视图和重构计划的Jira史诗的能力，利用Markdown模板和Figma链接进行详细的功能概述和需求","ja":"エージェントが大規模な機能、新しいビュー、リファクタリングイニシアチブのためのJiraエピックを作成および管理できるようにし、詳細な機能の概要と要件のためのMarkdownテンプレートとFigmaリンクを利用する","ko":"에이전트가 대형 기능, 새로운 뷰 및 리팩터링 계획을 위한 지라 에픽을 생성 및 관리할 수 있도록 하며, 자세한 기능 개요 및 요구 사항을 위한 마크다운 템플릿 및 피가마 링크를 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear y gestionar epics de Jira para características de gran tamaño, nuevas vistas y iniciativas de refactorización, utilizando plantillas de markdown y enlaces de Figma para descripciones detalladas de características y requisitos","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer et de gérer des épics Jira pour des fonctionnalités de grande taille, de nouvelles vues et des initiatives de refactoring, en utilisant des modèles de markdown et des liens Figma pour des descriptions détaillées des fonctionnalités et des exigences","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Jira-Epics für große Funktionen, neue Ansichten und Refactoring-Initiativen zu erstellen und zu verwalten, indem Markdown-Vorlagen und Figma-Links für detaillierte Funktionsübersichten und Anforderungen verwendet werden","pt":"Empowers agents to create and manage Jira epics for large features, new views, and refactoring initiatives, utilizing markdown templates and Figma links for detailed feature overviews and requirements","ru":"Empowers agents to create and manage Jira epics for large features, new views, and refactoring initiatives, utilizing markdown templates and Figma links for detailed feature overviews and requirements","ar":"Empowers agents to create and manage Jira epics for large features, new views, and refactoring initiatives, utilizing markdown templates and Figma links for detailed feature overviews and requirements"},"useCases":{"en":["Creating Jira epics for multi-component features","Managing major refactoring initiatives","Generating epic templates for new application views"],"zh":["为多组件功能创建Jira史诗","管理主要重构计划","为新应用程序视图生成史诗模板"],"ja":["マルチコンポーネント機能のためのJiraエピックの作成","主要なリファクタリングイニシアチブの管理","新しいアプリケーションビューのためのエピックテンプレートの生成"],"ko":["다중 구성 요소 기능을 위한 지라 에픽 생성","주요 리팩터링 계획 관리","새로운 애플리케이션 뷰를 위한 에픽 템플릿 생성"],"es":["Creación de epics de Jira para características de varios componentes","Gestión de iniciativas de refactorización importantes","Generación de plantillas de epics para nuevas vistas de aplicaciones"],"fr":["Création d''épics Jira pour des fonctionnalités à plusieurs composants","Gestion des initiatives de refactoring majeures","Génération de modèles d''épics pour de nouvelles vues d''applications"],"de":["Erstellung von Jira-Epics für Funktionen mit mehreren Komponenten","Verwaltung von großen Refactoring-Initiativen","Generierung von Epic-Vorlagen für neue Anwendungsansichten"],"pt":["Creating Jira epics for multi-component features","Managing major refactoring initiatives","Generating epic templates for new application views"],"ru":["Creating Jira epics for multi-component features","Managing major refactoring initiatives","Generating epic templates for new application views"],"ar":["Creating Jira epics for multi-component features","Managing major refactoring initiatives","Generating epic templates for new application views"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Jira access and credentials","Markdown formatting knowledge recommended"],"zh":["需要Jira访问和凭证","建议掌握Markdown格式知识"],"ja":["Jiraへのアクセスと資格情報が必要","Markdown形式の知識を習得することをお勧めします"],"ko":["지라 액세스 및 자격 증명 필요","마크다운 형식 지식을 권장"],"es":["Requiere acceso y credenciales de Jira","Conocimiento de formato de markdown recomendado"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès et des informations d''identification Jira","Connaissance de la mise en forme markdown recommandée"],"de":["Benötigt Jira-Zugang und -Anmeldeinformationen","Kenntnisse der Markdown-Formatierung werden empfohlen"],"pt":["Requires Jira access and credentials","Markdown formatting knowledge recommended"],"ru":["Requires Jira access and credentials","Markdown formatting knowledge recommended"],"ar":["Requires Jira access and credentials","Markdown formatting knowledge recommended"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
