educir el riesgo","Uso de CDK TypeScript para la configuración"],"fr":["Configuration de versions et d''alias de Lambda","Alarmes CloudWatch pour rollback automatique","Groupes de déploiement CodeDeploy pour changement de trafic","Déploiements canaris progressifs pour réduire le risque","Utilisation de CDK TypeScript pour la configuration"],"de":["Konfiguration von Lambda-Versionen und Aliases","CloudWatch-Alarma für automatischen Rollback","CodeDeploy-Deploy-Gruppen für Trafficschaltung","Progressive Canary-Deployments zur Risikoreduzierung","Verwendung von CDK TypeScript für die Konfiguration"],"pt":["Configuração de versões e aliases do Lambda","Alarmes do CloudWatch para rollback automático","Grupos de implantação do CodeDeploy para mudança de tráfego","Redução do risco de implantação com canary","Uso de CDK TypeScript para configuração","Integração com AWS Lambda"],"ru":["Настройка версий и псевдонимов Lambda","Сигналы CloudWatch для автоматического откат","Группы развертывания CodeDeploy для переключения трафика","Снижение риска развертывания с помощью канареечного развертывания","Использование CDK TypeScript для настройки","Интеграция с AWS Lambda"],"ar":["إعداد إصدارات واسماء مستعارة Lambda","إنذارات CloudWatch للتراجع التلقائي","مجموعات نشر CodeDeploy لتغيير Movement","تقليل مخاطر النشر مع تقنيات Canary","استخدام CDK TypeScript لإعداد","التكامل مع AWS Lambda"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AWS Canary 部署","CDK TypeScript","Lambda 版本和别名","CloudWatch 报警","CodeDeploy 部署组","自动回滚","流量转移","部署风险","系统稳定性"],"ja":["AWS Canary デプロイ","CDK TypeScript","Lambda バージョンとエイリアス","CloudWatch アラーム","CodeDeploy デプロイグループ","自動ロールバック","トラフィックの移行","デプロイリスク","システムの安定性"],"ko":["AWS Canary 배포","CDK TypeScript","Lambda 버전과 별칭","CloudWatch 알림","CodeDeploy 배포 그룹","자동 롤백","트래픽 이동","배포 위험","시스템 안정성"],"es":["despliegue canario","AWS Lambda","CDK TypeScript","CloudWatch","CodeDeploy","despliegue progresivo","reducción de riesgo","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["déploiement canari","AWS Lambda","CDK TypeScript","CloudWatch","CodeDeploy","déploiement progressif","réduction de risque","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Canary-Deploy","AWS Lambda","CDK TypeScript","CloudWatch","CodeDeploy","progressives Deploy","Risikoreduzierung","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["implantação de canary","AWS Lambda","CDK TypeScript","CloudWatch","CodeDeploy","redução de risco","novo código","tráfego"," rollout automático"],"ru":["канареечное развертывание","AWS Lambda","CDK TypeScript","CloudWatch","CodeDeploy","снижение риска","новый код","трафик","автоматический откат"],"ar":["نشر Canary","AWS Lambda","CDK TypeScript","CloudWatch","CodeDeploy","تقليل المخاطر","الكود الجديد","Movement","التراجع التلقائي"]}},"owner":"mariotoffia","repo":"gobridge","repoPath":"mariotoffia/gobridge","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.407Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"deployment-aws-canary-setup","description":"Step-by-step guide for setting up AWS Lambda canary deployments with CDK, CloudWatch alarms, and automated rollback.","bodyPreview":"# Skill: AWS Canary Deployment Setup\n\nThis skill teaches you how to set up progressive canary deployments for AWS Lambda using CDK TypeScript. You''ll configure Lambda versions and aliases, CloudWatch alarms for automated rollback, and CodeDeploy deployment groups for traffic shifting.\n\nCanary deployments reduce deployment risk by routing a small percentage of traffic to new code first. If the new version performs well (low errors, acceptable latency), traffic gradually shifts until 100% reaches","body":"# Skill: AWS Canary Deployment Setup\n\nThis skill teaches you how to set up progressive canary deployments for AWS Lambda using CDK TypeScript. You''ll configure Lambda versions and aliases, CloudWatch alarms for automated rollback, and CodeDeploy deployment groups for traffic shifting.\n\nCanary deployments reduce deployment risk by routing a small percentage of traffic to new code first. If the new version performs well (low errors, acceptable latency), traffic gradually shifts until 100% reaches the new version. If metrics fail, traffic automatically rolls back to the stable version.\n\nThis approach is essential for production workloads where zero-downtime deployments and automatic failure recovery are critical requirements.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- AWS CDK v2 installed (`npm install -g aws-cdk`)\n- TypeScript project with CDK configured\n- Lambda function deployed with proper IAM roles\n- CloudWatch configured for Lambda metrics\n- Understanding of Lambda versions and aliases\n\n## Overview\n\nIn this skill, you will:\n1. Create Lambda function with versioning and alias\n2. Configure CloudWatch alarms for error rate and latency\n3. Set up CodeDeploy deployment group with canary config\n4. Create CDK stack with all deployment infrastructure\n5. Implement rollback procedures\n6. Add monitoring dashboard for canary metrics\n\n## Step 1: Create Lambda with Versioning and Alias\n\nLambda versions are immutable snapshots of your function code and configuration. Aliases are mutable pointers that can route traffic between versions.\n\n### CDK Lambda Construct with Versioning\n\n```typescript\n// lib/constructs/versioned-lambda.ts\nimport * as cdk from ''aws-cdk-lib'';\nimport * as lambda from ''aws-cdk-lib/aws-lambda'';\nimport * as codedeploy from ''aws-cdk-lib/aws-codedeploy'';\nimport { Construct } from ''constructs'';\n\nexport interface VersionedLambdaProps {\n  functionName: string;\n  description: string;\n  codePath: string;\n  handler: string;\n  runtime: lambda.Runtime;\n  memorySize?: number;\n  timeout?: cdk.Duration;\n  environment?: { [key: string]: string };\n  reservedConcurrentExecutions?: number;\n}\n\nexport class VersionedLambda extends Construct {\n  public readonly function: lambda.Function;\n  public readonly alias: lambda.Alias;\n  public readonly currentVersion: lambda.Version;\n\n  constructor(scope: Construct, id: string, props: VersionedLambdaProps) {\n    super(scope, id);\n\n    // Create Lambda function with tracing enabled\n    this.function = new lambda.Function(this, ''Function'', {\n      functionName: props.functionName,\n      description: props.description,\n      runtime: props.runtime,\n      handler: props.handler,\n      code: lambda.Code.fromAsset(props.codePath),\n      memorySize: props.memorySize ?? 256,\n      timeout: props.timeout ?? cdk.Duration.seconds(30),\n      environment: props.environment,\n      tracing: lambda.Tracing.ACTIVE,\n      reservedConcurrentExecutions: props.reservedConcurrentExecutions,\n      // Enable versioning by setting currentVersionOptions\n      currentVersionOptions: {\n        removalPolicy: cdk.RemovalPolicy.RETAIN,\n        description: `Version deployed at ${new Date().toISOString()}`,\n      },\n    });\n\n    // Get the current version (creates new version on each deployment)\n    this.currentVersion = this.function.currentVersion;\n\n    // Create alias pointing to current version\n    // The alias is what API Gateway or other services invoke\n    this.alias = new lambda.Alias(this, ''LiveAlias'', {\n      aliasName: ''live'',\n      version: this.currentVersion,\n      description: ''Production traffic alias'',\n    });\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe key concepts here:\n- **Versions**: Each deployment creates an immutable version snapshot\n- **Alias**: The \"live\" alias is what clients invoke, not a specific version\n- **Traffic routing**: The alias can split traffic between two versions\n\n### Using the Construct\n\n```typescript\n// lib/stacks/api-stack.ts\nimport * as cdk from ''aws-cdk-lib'';\nimport * as lambda from ''aws-cdk-lib/aws-lambda'';\nimport { Construct } from ''constructs'';\nimport { VersionedLambda } from ''../constructs/versioned-lambda'';\n\nexport class ApiStack extends cdk.Stack {\n  public readonly apiHandler: VersionedLambda;\n\n  constructor(scope: Construct, id: string, props?: cdk.StackProps) {\n    super(scope, id, props);\n\n    const stage = this.node.tryGetContext(''stage'') || ''dev'';\n\n    this.apiHandler = new VersionedLambda(this, ''ApiHandler'', {\n      functionName: `my-service-api-${stage}`,\n      description: ''API handler for my-service'',\n      codePath: ''../dist/api'',\n      handler: ''bootstrap'',\n      runtime: lambda.Runtime.PROVIDED_AL2023,\n      memorySize: 256,\n      timeout: cdk.Duration.seconds(30),\n      environment: {\n        STAGE: stage,\n        LOG_LEVEL: stage === ''prod'' ? ''INFO'' : ''DEBUG'',\n      },\n    });\n\n    // Export alias ARN for API Gateway integration\n    new cdk.CfnOutput(this, ''ApiAliasArn'', {\n      value: this.apiHandler.alias.functionArn,\n      description: ''Lambda alias ARN for API Gateway'',\n    });\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Step 2: Configure CloudWatch Alarms\n\nCloudWatch alarms monitor your Lambda''s health during deployment. If metrics breach thresholds, CodeDeploy triggers automatic rollback.\n\n### Alarm Configuration Construct\n\n```typescript\n// lib/constructs/deployment-alarms.ts\nimport * as cdk from ''aws-cdk-lib'';\nimport * as cloudwatch from ''aws-cdk-lib/aws-cloudwatch'';\nimport * as lambda from ''aws-cdk-lib/aws-lambda'';\nimport { Construct } from ''constructs'';\n\nexport interface DeploymentAlarmsProps {\n  lambdaFunction: lambda.Function;\n  alias: lambda.Alias;\n  alarmNamePrefix: string;\n  // Thresholds\n  errorRateThreshold?: number;      // Default: 1%\n  latencyP99Threshold?: number;     // Default: 5000ms\n  throttleThreshold?: number;       // Default: 10 per minute\n  evaluationPeriods?: number;       // Default: 2\n}\n\nexport class DeploymentAlarms extends Construct {\n  public readonly errorAlarm: cloudwatch.Alarm;\n  public readonly latencyAlarm: cloudwatch.Alarm;\n  public readonly throttleAlarm: cloudwatch.Alarm;\n  public readonly allAlarms: cloudwatch.Alarm[];\n\n  constructor(scope: Construct, id: string, props: DeploymentAlarmsProps) {\n    super(scope, id);\n\n    const evaluationPeriods = props.evaluationPeriods ?? 2;\n\n    // Error rate alarm - triggers rollback if errors exceed threshold\n    this.errorAlarm = new cloudwatch.Alarm(this, ''ErrorAlarm'', {\n      alarmName: `${props.alarmNamePrefix}-errors`,\n      alarmDescription: ''Lambda error rate exceeded threshold during deployment'',\n      metric: props.alias.metricErrors({\n        period: cdk.Duration.minutes(1),\n        statistic: ''Sum'',\n      }),\n      threshold: props.errorRateThreshold ?? 10,\n      evaluationPeriods: evaluationPeriods,\n      comparisonOperator: cloudwatch.ComparisonOperator.GREATER_THAN_THRESHOLD,\n      treatMissingData: cloudwatch.TreatMissingData.NOT_BREACHING,\n    });\n\n    // P99 latency alarm - triggers rollback if latency too high\n    this.latencyAlarm = new cloudwatch.Alarm(this, ''LatencyAlarm'', {\n      alarmName: `${props.alarmNamePrefix}-latency-p99`,\n      alarmDescription: ''Lambda P99 latency exceeded threshold during deployment'',\n      metric: props.alias.metricDuration({\n        period: cdk.Duration.minutes(1),\n        statistic: ''p99'',\n      }),\n      threshold: props.latencyP99Threshold ?? 5000,\n      evaluationPeriods: evaluationPeriods,\n      comparisonOperator: cloudwatch.ComparisonOperator.GREATER_THAN_THRESHOLD,\n      treatMissingData: cloudwatch.TreatMissingData.NOT_BREACHING,\n    });\n\n    // Throttle alarm - indicates capacity issues\n    this.throttleAlarm = new cloudwatch.Alarm(this, ''ThrottleAlarm'', {\n      alarmName: `${props.alarmNamePrefix}-throttles`,\n      alarmDescription: ''Lambda throttling detected during deployment'',\n      metric: props.alias.metricThrottles({\n        period: cdk.Duration.minutes(1),\n        statistic: ''Sum'',\n      }),\n      threshold: props.throttleThreshold ?? 10,\n      evaluationPeriods: evaluationPeriods,\n      comparisonOperator: cloudwatch.ComparisonOperator.GREATER_THAN_THRESHOLD,\n      treatMissingData: cloudwatch.TreatMissingData.NOT_BREACHING,\n    });\n\n    this.allAlarms = [this.errorAlarm, this.latencyAlarm, this.throttleAlarm];\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThese alarms monitor the alias (which receives production traffic), not the function directly. This ensures we''re measuring the actual user experience during canary deployment.\n\n## Step 3: Configure CodeDeploy Deployment Group\n\nCodeDeploy manages the traffic shifting between Lambda versions. It supports multiple deployment strategies.\n\n### Deployment Configuration Options\n\n```typescript\n// lib/constructs/canary-deployment.ts\nimport * as cdk from ''aws-cdk-lib'';\nimport * as lambda from ''aws-cdk-lib/aws-lambda'';\nimport * as codedeploy from ''aws-cdk-lib/aws-codedeploy'';\nimport * as cloudwatch from ''aws-cdk-lib/aws-cloudwatch'';\nimport { Construct } from ''constructs'';\n\n// Available deployment configurations\nexport enum CanaryDeploymentConfig {\n  // Canary: Deploy to small percentage, wait, then 100%\n  CANARY_10_PERCENT_5_MINUTES = ''CANARY_10PERCENT_5MINUTES'',\n  CANARY_10_PERCENT_10_MINUTES = ''CANARY_10PERCENT_10MINUTES'',\n  CANARY_10_PERCENT_15_MINUTES = ''CANARY_10PERCENT_15MINUTES'',\n  \n  // Linear: Gradually increase traffic at fixed intervals\n  LINEAR_10_PERCENT_EVERY_1_MINUTE = ''LINEAR_10PERCENT_EVERY_1MINUTE'',\n  LINEAR_10_PERCENT_EVERY_2_MINUTES = ''LINEAR_10PERCENT_EVERY_2MINUTES'',\n  LINEAR_10_PERCENT_EVERY_3_MINUTES = ''LINEAR_10PERCENT_EVERY_3MINUTES'',\n  LINEAR_10_PERCENT_EVERY_10_MINUTES = ''LINEAR_10PERCENT_EVERY_10MINUTES'',\n  \n  // All at once (not recommended for production)\n  ALL_AT_ONCE = ''ALL_AT_ONCE'',\n}\n\nexport interface CanaryDeploymentProps {\n  alias: lambda.Alias;\n  deploymentConfig: CanaryDeploymentConfig;\n  alarms: cloudwatch.Alarm[];\n  applicationName?: string;\n  deploymentGroupName?: string;\n}\n\nexport class CanaryDeployment extends Construct {\n  public readonly application: codedeploy.LambdaApplication;\n  public readonly deploymentGroup: codedeploy.LambdaDeploymentGroup;\n\n  constructor(scope: Construct, id: string, props: CanaryDeploymentProps) {\n    super(scope, id);\n\n    // Create CodeDeploy application\n    this.application = new codedeploy.LambdaApplication(this, ''Application'', {\n      applicationName: props.applicationName,\n    });\n\n    // Map deployment config enum to CDK deployment config\n    const deploymentConfig = this.getDeploymentConfig(props.deploymentConfig);\n\n    // Create deployment group with automatic rollback\n    this.deploymentGroup = new codedeploy.LambdaDeploymentGroup(this, ''DeploymentGroup'', {\n      application: this.application,\n      deploymentGroupName: props.deploymentGroupName,\n      alias: props.alias,\n      deploymentConfig: deploymentConfig,\n      \n      // Attach alarms for automatic rollback\n      alarms: props.alarms,\n      \n      // Auto-rollback on deployment failure or alarm breach\n      autoRollback: {\n        failedDeployment: true,\n        stoppedDeployment: true,\n        deploymentInAlarm: true,\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  private getDeploymentConfig(\n    config: CanaryDeploymentConfig\n  ): codedeploy.ILambdaDeploymentConfig {\n    switch (config) {\n      case CanaryDeploymentConfig.CANARY_10_PERCENT_5_MINUTES:\n        return codedeploy.LambdaDeploymentConfig.CANARY_10PERCENT_5MINUTES;\n      case CanaryDeploymentConfig.CANARY_10_PERCENT_10_MINUTES:\n        return codedeploy.LambdaDeploymentConfig.CANARY_10PERCENT_10MINUTES;\n      case CanaryDeploymentConfig.CANARY_10_PERCENT_15_MINUTES:\n        return codedeploy.LambdaDeploymentConfig.CANARY_10PERCENT_15MINUTES;\n      case CanaryDeploymentConfig.LINEAR_10_PERCENT_EVERY_1_MINUTE:\n        return codedeploy.LambdaDeploymentConfig.LINEAR_10PERCENT_EVERY_1MINUTE;\n      case CanaryDeploymentConfig.LINEAR_10_PERCENT_EVERY_2_MINUTES:\n        return codedeploy.LambdaDeploymentConfig.LINEAR_10PERCENT_EVERY_2MINUTES;\n      case CanaryDeploymentConfig.LINEAR_10_PERCENT_EVERY_3_MINUTES:\n        return codedeploy.LambdaDeploymentConfig.LINEAR_10PERCENT_EVERY_3MINUTES;\n      case CanaryDeploymentConfig.LINEAR_10_PERCENT_EVERY_10_MINUTES:\n        return codedeploy.LambdaDeploymentConfig.LINEAR_10PERCENT_EVERY_10MINUTES;\n      case CanaryDeploymentConfig.ALL_AT_ONCE:\n        return codedeploy.LambdaDeploymentConfig.ALL_AT_ONCE;\n      default:\n        return codedeploy.LambdaDeploymentConfig.CANARY_10PERCENT_5MINUTES;\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Deployment Config Comparison\n\n| Config | Traffic Shift | Total Time | Use Case |\n|--------|---------------|------------|----------|\n| CANARY_10PERCENT_5MINUTES | 10% → 100% | 5 min | Quick validation |\n| CANARY_10PERCENT_10MINUTES | 10% → 100% | 10 min | Standard production |\n| LINEAR_10PERCENT_EVERY_1MINUTE | 10% increments | 10 min | Gradual rollout |\n| LINEAR_10PERCENT_EVERY_10MINUTES | 10% increments | 100 min | High-risk changes |\n\n## Step 4: Complete CDK Stack\n\nCombine all components into a production-ready deployment stack.\n\n```typescript\n// lib/stacks/canary-deployment-stack.ts\nimport * as cdk from ''aws-cdk-lib'';\nimport * as lambda from ''aws-cdk-lib/aws-lambda'';\nimport * as codedeploy from ''aws-cdk-lib/aws-codedeploy'';\nimport * as cloudwatch from ''aws-cdk-lib/aws-cloudwatch'';\nimport { Construct } from ''constructs'';\nimport { VersionedLambda } from ''../constructs/versioned-lambda'';\nimport { DeploymentAlarms } from ''../constructs/deployment-alarms'';\nimport { CanaryDeployment, CanaryDeploymentConfig } from ''../constructs/canary-deployment'';\n\nexport interface CanaryDeploymentStackProps extends cdk.StackProps {\n  stage: string;\n  serviceName: string;\n  codePath: string;\n  deploymentConfig?: CanaryDeploymentConfig;\n  errorRateThreshold?: number;\n  latencyP99Threshold?: number;\n}\n\nexport class CanaryDeploymentStack extends cdk.Stack {\n  public readonly lambdaFunction: lambda.Function;\n  public readonly alias: lambda.Alias;\n  public readonly deploymentGroup: codedeploy.LambdaDeploymentGroup;\n\n  constructor(scope: Construct, id: string, props: CanaryDeploymentStackProps) {\n    super(scope, id, props);\n\n    const alarmPrefix = `${props.serviceName}-${props.stage}`;\n\n    // Create versioned Lambda\n    const versionedLambda = new VersionedLambda(this, ''ApiHandler'', {\n      functionName: `${props.serviceName}-api-${props.stage}`,\n      description: `${props.serviceName} API handler`,\n      codePath: props.codePath,\n      handler: ''bootstrap'',\n      runtime: lambda.Runtime.PROVIDED_AL2023,\n      memorySize: 256,\n      timeout: cdk.Duration.seconds(30),\n      environment: {\n        STAGE: props.stage,\n        SERVICE_NAME: props.serviceName,\n      },\n    });\n\n    this.lambdaFunction = versionedLambda.function;\n    this.alias = versionedLambda.alias;\n\n    // Create deployment alarms\n    const alarms = new DeploymentAlarms(this, ''Alarms'', {\n      lambdaFunction: this.lambdaFunction,\n      alias: this.alias,\n      alarmNamePrefix: alarmPrefix,\n      errorRateThreshold: props.errorRateThreshold,\n      latencyP99Threshold: props.latencyP99Threshold,\n    });\n\n    // Determine deployment config based on stage\n    const deploymentConfig = props.deploymentConfig ?? \n      (props.stage === ''prod'' \n        ? CanaryDeploymentConfig.CANARY_10_PERCENT_10_MINUTES\n        : CanaryDeploymentConfig.ALL_AT_ONCE);\n\n    // Create canary deployment group\n    const canaryDeployment = new CanaryDeployment(this, ''CanaryDeploy'', {\n      alias: this.alias,\n      deploymentConfig: deploymentConfig,\n      alarms: alarms.allAlarms,\n      applicationName: `${props.serviceName}-${props.stage}`,\n      deploymentGroupName: `${props.serviceName}-${props.stage}-dg`,\n    });\n\n    this.deploymentGroup = canaryDeployment.deploymentGroup;\n\n    // Outputs\n    new cdk.CfnOutput(this, ''FunctionName'', {\n      value: this.lambdaFunction.functionName,\n    });\n\n    new cdk.CfnOutput(this, ''AliasArn'', {\n      value: this.alias.functionArn,\n    });\n\n    new cdk.CfnOutput(this, ''CurrentVersion'', {\n      value: versionedLambda.currentVersion.version,\n    });\n\n    new cdk.CfnOutput(this, ''DeploymentGroupName'', {\n      value: this.deploymentGroup.deploymentGroupName,\n    });\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### CDK App Entry Point\n\n```typescript\n// bin/app.ts\n#!/usr/bin/env node\nimport ''source-map-support/register'';\nimport * as cdk from ''aws-cdk-lib'';\nimport { CanaryDeploymentStack } from ''../lib/stacks/canary-deployment-stack'';\nimport { CanaryDeploymentConfig } from ''../lib/constructs/canary-deployment'';\n\nconst app = new cdk.App();\n\nconst stage = app.node.tryGetContext(''stage'') || ''dev'';\nconst serviceName = ''my-service'';\n\nnew CanaryDeploymentStack(app, `${serviceName}-${stage}`, {\n  stage: stage,\n  serviceName: serviceName,\n  codePath: ''../dist/api'',\n  deploymentConfig: stage === ''prod'' \n    ? CanaryDeploymentConfig.CANARY_10_PERCENT_10_MINUTES\n    : CanaryDeploymentConfig.ALL_AT_ONCE,\n  errorRateThreshold: 10,\n  latencyP99Threshold: 5000,\n  env: {\n    account: process.env.CDK_DEFAULT_ACCOUNT,\n    region: process.env.CDK_DEFAULT_REGION || ''eu-west-1'',\n  },\n});\n```\n\n## Step 5: Test Rollback Scenarios\n\nImplement scripts and procedures for testing rollback behavior.\n\n### Metrics Check Script\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n# scripts/check-metrics.sh\n# Validates Lambda metrics for canary deployment health\n\nset -euo pipefail\n\nSERVICE=$1\nSTAGE=$2\nFUNCTION_NAME=\"${SERVICE}-api-${STAGE}\"\nALIAS_NAME=\"live\"\n\necho \"Checking metrics for ${FUNCTION_NAME}:${ALIAS_NAME}...\"\n\n# Time range: last 5 minutes\nEND_TIME=$(date -u +\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\nSTART_TIME=$(date -u -v-5M +\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\" 2>/dev/null || \\\n             date -u -d \"5 minutes ago\" +\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n\n# Get error count\nERRORS=$(aws cloudwatch get-metric-statistics \\\n  --namespace AWS/Lambda \\\n  --metric-name Errors \\\n  --dimensions Name=FunctionName,Value=$FUNCTION_NAME Name=Resource,Value=\"${FUNCTION_NAME}:${ALIAS_NAME}\" \\\n  --start-time \"$START_TIME\" \\\n  --end-time \"$END_TIME\" \\\n  --period 300 \\\n  --statistics Sum \\\n  --query ''Datapoints[0].Sum'' \\\n  --output text 2>/dev/null || echo \"0\")\n\n# Get invocation count  \nINVOCATIONS=$(aws cloudwatch get-metric-statistics \\\n  --namespace AWS/Lambda \\\n  --metric-name Invocations \\\n  --dimensions Name=FunctionName,Value=$FUNCTION_NAME Name=Resource,Value=\"${FUNCTION_NAME}:${ALIAS_NAME}\" \\\n  --start-time \"$START_TIME\" \\\n  --end-time \"$END_TIME\" \\\n  --period 300 \\\n  --statistics Sum \\\n  --query ''Datapoints[0].Sum'' \\\n  --output text 2>/dev/null || echo \"1\")\n\n# Get P99 duration\nDURATION_P99=$(aws cloudwatch get-metric-statistics \\\n  --namespace AWS/Lambda \\\n  --metric-name Duration \\\n  --dimensions Name=FunctionName,Value=$FUNCTION_NAME Name=Resource,Value=\"${FUNCTION_NAME}:${ALIAS_NAME}\" \\\n  --start-time \"$START_TIME\" \\\n  --end-time \"$END_TIME\" \\\n  --period 300 \\\n  --extended-statistics p99 \\\n  --query ''Datapoints[0].ExtendedStatistics.p99'' \\\n  --output text 2>/dev/null || echo \"0\")\n\n# Handle None values\nERRORS=${ERRORS//None/0}\nINVOCATIONS=${INVOCATIONS//None/1}\nDURATION_P99=${DURATION_P99//None/0}\n\n# Calculate error rate\nif [[ \"$INVOCATIONS\" != \"0\" ]]; then\n  ERROR_RATE=$(echo \"scale=4; $ERRORS / $INVOCATIONS\" | bc)\nelse\n  ERROR_RATE=\"0\"\nfi\n\necho \"==========================================\"\necho \"Errors:       $ERRORS\"\necho \"Invocations:  $INVOCATIONS\"\necho \"Error Rate:   $ERROR_RATE\"\necho \"P99 Duration: ${DURATION_P99}ms\"\necho \"==========================================\"\n\n# Validate against thresholds\nFAILED=0\n\nif (( $(echo \"$ERROR_RATE > 0.01\" | bc -l) )); then\n  echo \"❌ FAIL: Error rate $ERROR_RATE > 1%\"\n  FAILED=1\nfi\n\nif (( $(echo \"$DURATION_P99 > 5000\" | bc -l) )); then\n  echo \"❌ FAIL: P99 latency ${DURATION_P99}ms > 5000ms\"\n  FAILED=1\nfi\n\nif [[ $FAILED -eq 1 ]]; then\n  echo \"\"\n  echo \"Metrics validation FAILED - rollback recommended\"\n  exit 1\nfi\n\necho \"✅ PASS: All metrics within thresholds\"\nexit 0\n```\n\n### Manual Rollback Commands\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n# scripts/rollback.sh\n# Manually rollback to previous Lambda version\n\nset -euo pipefail\n\nSERVICE=$1\nSTAGE=$2\nFUNCTION_NAME=\"${SERVICE}-api-${STAGE}\"\nALIAS_NAME=\"live\"\n\necho \"Rolling back ${FUNCTION_NAME}...\"\n\n# Get previous version (second to last)\nPREVIOUS_VERSION=$(aws lambda list-versions-by-function \\\n  --function-name \"$FUNCTION_NAME\" \\\n  --query ''Versions[-2].Version'' \\\n  --output text)\n\nif [[ \"$PREVIOUS_VERSION\" == \"None\" || \"$PREVIOUS_VERSION\" == \"\\$LATEST\" ]]; then\n  echo \"Error: No previous version found to rollback to\"\n  exit 1\nfi\n\necho \"Rolling back to version: $PREVIOUS_VERSION\"\n\n# Update alias to point to previous version (100% traffic)\naws lambda update-alias \\\n  --function-name \"$FUNCTION_NAME\" \\\n  --name \"$ALIAS_NAME\" \\\n  --function-version \"$PREVIOUS_VERSION\" \\\n  --routing-config ''AdditionalVersionWeights={}''\n\necho \"✅ Rollback complete. Alias now points to version $PREVIOUS_VERSION\"\n\n# Verify\nCURRENT=$(aws lambda get-alias \\\n  --function-name \"$FUNCTION_NAME\" \\\n  --name \"$ALIAS_NAME\" \\\n  --query ''FunctionVersion'' \\\n  --output text)\n\necho \"Current alias version: $CURRENT\"\n```\n\n### Stop In-Progress Deployment\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\n# scripts/stop-deployment.sh\n# Stop an in-progress CodeDeploy deployment\n\nset -euo pipefail\n\nSERVICE=$1\nSTAGE=$2\nAPPLICATION_NAME=\"${SERVICE}-${STAGE}\"\nDEPLOYMENT_GROUP=\"${SERVICE}-${STAGE}-dg\"\n\n# Get current deployment ID\nDEPLOYMENT_ID=$(aws deploy list-deployments \\\n  --application-name \"$APPLICATION_NAME\" \\\n  --deployment-group-name \"$DEPLOYMENT_GROUP\" \\\n  --include-only-statuses \"InProgress\" \\\n  --query ''deployments[0]'' \\\n  --output text)\n\nif [[ \"$DEPLOYMENT_ID\" == \"None\" ]]; then\n  echo \"No in-progress deployment found\"\n  exit 0\nfi\n\necho \"Stopping deployment: $DEPLOYMENT_ID\"\n\naws deploy stop-deployment \\\n  --deployment-id \"$DEPLOYMENT_ID\" \\\n  --auto-rollback-enabled\n\necho \"✅ Deployment stopped and rollback initiated\"\n```\n\n## Step 6: Monitor Canary Metrics\n\nCreate a CloudWatch dashboard for monitoring canary deployments in real-time.\n\n```typescript\n// lib/constructs/canary-dashboard.ts\nimport * as cdk from ''aws-cdk-lib'';\nimport * as cloudwatch from ''aws-cdk-lib/aws-cloudwatch'';\nimport * as lambda from ''aws-cdk-lib/aws-lambda'';\nimport { Construct } from ''constructs'';\n\nexport interface CanaryDashboardProps {\n  dashboardName: string;\n  lambdaFunction: lambda.Function;\n  alias: lambda.Alias;\n}\n\nexport class CanaryDashboard extends Construct {\n  public readonly dashboard: cloudwatch.Dashboard;\n\n  constructor(scope: Construct, id: string, props: CanaryDashboardProps) {\n    super(scope, id);\n\n    this.dashboard = new cloudwatch.Dashboard(this, ''Dashboard'', {\n      dashboardName: props.dashboardName,\n    });\n\n    // Error rate widget\n    this.dashboard.addWidgets(\n      new cloudwatch.GraphWidget({\n        title: ''Error Rate'',\n        left: [\n          props.alias.metricErrors({\n            period: cdk.Duration.minutes(1),\n            statistic: ''Sum'',\n            label: ''Errors'',\n          }),\n        ],\n        right: [\n          props.alias.metricInvocations({\n            period: cdk.Duration.minutes(1),\n            statistic: ''Sum'',\n            label: ''Invocations'',\n          }),\n        ],\n        width: 12,\n      }),\n      new cloudwatch.GraphWidget({\n        title: ''Latency (P50, P90, P99)'',\n        left: [\n          props.alias.metricDuration({\n            period: cdk.Duration.minutes(1),\n            statistic: ''p50'',\n            label: ''P50'',\n          }),\n          props.alias.metricDuration({\n            period: cdk.Duration.minutes(1),\n            statistic: ''p90'',\n            label: ''P90'',\n          }),\n          props.alias.metricDuration({\n            period: cdk.Duration.minutes(1),\n            statistic: ''p99'',\n            label: ''P99'',\n          }),\n        ],\n        width: 12,\n      })\n    );\n\n    // Throttles and concurrent executions\n    this.dashboard.addWidgets(\n      new cloudwatch.GraphWidget({\n        title: ''Throttles'',\n        left: [\n          props.alias.metricThrottles({\n            period: cdk.Duration.minutes(1),\n            statistic: ''Sum'',\n          }),\n        ],\n        width: 8,\n      }),\n      new cloudwatch.GraphWidget({\n        title: ''Concurrent Executions'',\n        left: [\n          props.lambdaFunction.metric(''ConcurrentExecutions'', {\n            period: cdk.Duration.minutes(1),\n            statistic: ''Maximum'',\n          }),\n        ],\n        width: 8,\n      }),\n      new cloudwatch.SingleValueWidget({\n        title: ''Current Error Rate'',\n        metrics: [\n          props.alias.metricErrors({\n            period: cdk.Duration.minutes(5),\n            statistic: ''Sum'',\n          }),\n        ],\n        width: 8,\n      })\n    );\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Makefile Targets\n\nAdd deployment targets to your Makefile for easy canary operations.\n\n```makefile\n# Makefile for canary deployment operations\n\nSERVICE_NAME := my-service\nSTAGE ?= dev\nCDK_DIR := deploy/cdk\nVERSION ?= $(shell git describe --tags --always)\n\n.PHONY: deploy deploy-canary promote rollback check-metrics stop-deployment\n\n# Standard deployment (uses stage-appropriate config)\ndeploy: build\n\t@echo \"Deploying $(SERVICE_NAME) to $(STAGE)...\"\n\tcd $(CDK_DIR) && cdk deploy --context stage=$(STAGE) --require-approval never\n\n# Deploy with specific canary weight (0.1 = 10%, 0.5 = 50%)\ndeploy-canary: build\nifndef WEIGHT\n\t$(error WEIGHT is required, e.g., make deploy-canary WEIGHT=0.1)\nendif\n\t@echo \"Deploying canary at $(WEIGHT) weight...\"\n\tcd $(CDK_DIR) && CANARY_WEIGHT=$(WEIGHT) cdk deploy --context stage=$(STAGE)\n\n# Promote canary to 100%\npromote:\n\t@echo \"Promoting $(SERVICE_NAME) to 100% in $(STAGE)...\"\n\t./scripts/promote.sh $(SERVICE_NAME) $(STAGE)\n\n# Rollback to previous version\nrollback:\n\t@echo \"Rolling back $(SERVICE_NAME) in $(STAGE)...\"\n\t./scripts/rollback.sh $(SERVICE_NAME) $(STAGE)\n\n# Check deployment metrics\ncheck-metrics:\n\t@./scripts/check-metrics.sh $(SERVICE_NAME) $(STAGE)\n\n# Stop in-progress deployment\nstop-deployment:\n\t@./scripts/stop-deployment.sh $(SERVICE_NAME) $(STAGE)\n\n# Build Lambda binary\nbuild:\n\tGOOS=linux GOARCH=arm64 CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -o bootstrap ./cmd/api\n\tzip -j dist/api.zip bootstrap\n\trm bootstrap\n```\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\nAfter setting up canary deployments, verify:\n\n- [ ] Lambda function publishes new version on each deployment\n- [ ] Alias \"live\" exists and points to current version\n- [ ] CloudWatch alarms configured for errors, latency, and throttles\n- [ ] CodeDeploy deployment group created with correct config\n- [ ] Alarms attached to deployment group for auto-rollback\n- [ ] autoRollback enabled for failedDeployment and deploymentInAlarm\n- [ ] Metrics check script validates error rate < 1%\n- [ ] Metrics check script validates P99 latency < 5000ms\n- [ ] Manual rollback script updates alias to previous version\n- [ ] Stop deployment script halts in-progress deployments\n- [ ] Dashboard shows real-time canary metrics\n- [ ] Makefile has deploy, rollback, and check-metrics targets\n- [ ] Different deployment configs used per environment (ALL_AT_ONCE for dev, CANARY for prod)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:24:47.521Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Cloud Agents needing automated canary deployment setups for AWS Lambda using CDK TypeScript.","zh":"适合需要自动化金丝雀部署设置的云代理，使用AWS Lambda和CDK TypeScript。","ja":"AWS Lambdaを使用してCDK TypeScriptで自動化されたカナリアデプロイセットアップが必要なクラウドエージェントに最適。","ko":"AWS Lambda를 사용하여 CDK TypeScript로 자동화된 카나리아 배포 설정이 필요한 클라우드 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Nube que necesitan configuraciones de implementación de canario automatizadas para AWS Lambda utilizando CDK TypeScript.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Cloud nécessitant des configurations de déploiement de canari automatisées pour AWS Lambda en utilisant CDK TypeScript.","de":"Perfekt für Cloud-Agents, die automatisierte Canary-Deployments für AWS Lambda mit CDK TypeScript benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Nuvem que precisam de configurações de implantação canary automatizadas para AWS Lambda usando CDK TypeScript.","ru":"Идеально подходит для облачных агентов, которым необходимы автоматические настройки развертывания canary для AWS Lambda с использованием CDK TypeScript.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل السحابة التي تحتاج إلى إعدادات تثبيت كاناري автомاتيكي لآي دبليو إس لامدا باستخدام سي دي كي تا입 سكريبت."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to configure Lambda versions and aliases, set up CloudWatch alarms for automated rollback, and create CodeDeploy deployment groups for traffic shifting using AWS CDK and TypeScript, reducing deployment risk with progressive canary deployments.","zh":"赋予代理配置Lambda版本和别名，设置CloudWatch报警以实现自动回滚，并使用AWS CDK和TypeScript创建CodeDeploy部署组以实现流量转移，减少部署风险并实现渐进式金丝雀部署。","ja":"エージェントがLambdaバージョンとエイリアスを構成し、CloudWatchアラームを使用して自動ロールバックを設定し、AWS CDKとTypeScriptを使用してCodeDeployデプロイグループを作成してトラフィックシフトを実行することを可能にし、デプロイのリスクを減らすことで_progressiveカナリアデプロイを実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 람다 버전 및 별칭을 구성하고 CloudWatch 알람을 사용하여 자동 롤백을 설정하며 AWS CDK 및 TypeScript를 사용하여 CodeDeploy 배포 그룹을 생성하여 트래픽 전환을 수행할 수 있도록 하여 배포 위험을 줄이고 점진적인 카나리아 배포를 구현합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a configurar versiones y alias de Lambda, configurar alarmas de CloudWatch para reversión automática y crear grupos de implementación de CodeDeploy para cambio de tráfico utilizando AWS CDK y TypeScript, reduciendo el riesgo de implementación con despliegues de canario progresivos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de configurer les versions et les alias de Lambda, de configurer des alarmes de CloudWatch pour une réversibilité automatisée et de créer des groupes de déploiement de CodeDeploy pour le changement de trafic en utilisant AWS CDK et TypeScript, en réduisant le risque de déploiement avec des déploiements de canari progressifs.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Lambda-Versionen und Aliase zu konfigurieren, CloudWatch-Alarmanlagen für automatisches Rollback einzurichten und CodeDeploy-Deploymentsgruppen für Traffikumschaltung mit AWS CDK und TypeScript zu erstellen, wodurch das Risiko von Deployments durch progressive Canary-Deployments reduziert wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a configurar versões e aliases do Lambda, configurar alarmes do CloudWatch para rollback automatizado e criar grupos de implantação do CodeDeploy para alteração de tráfego usando AWS CDK e TypeScript, reduzindo o risco de implantação com implantações canary progressivas.","ru":"Позволяет агентам настраивать версии и псевдонимы Lambda, устанавливать сигналы тревоги CloudWatch для автоматического откатا и создавать группы развертывания CodeDeploy для переключения трафика с помощью AWS CDK и TypeScript, снижая риск развертывания с помощью прогрессивных развертываний canary.","ar":"يُمكّن الوكيل من تكوين إصدارات وأسماء مستعارة لامدا، وتكوين إنذارات كلاود ووتش للأستعادة التلقائية، وإنشاء مجموعات تثبيت للكود ديبلي باستخدام آي دبليو إس سي دي كي وتايب سكريبت، مما يقلل من مخاطر التثبيت باستخدام تثبيتات كاناري تدريجية."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating rollback of faulty Lambda versions using CloudWatch alarms","Configuring traffic shifting for canary deployments with CodeDeploy","Setting up Lambda aliases for version control and testing"],"zh":["使用CloudWatch报警自动回滚有故障的Lambda版本","使用CodeDeploy配置金丝雀部署的流量转移","设置Lambda别名以实现版本控制和测试"],"ja":["CloudWatchアラームを使用して故障のあるLambdaバージョンを自動ロールバックする","CodeDeployを使用してカナリアデプロイのトラフィックシフトを構成する","バージョン管理とテストのためにLambdaエイリアスを設定する"],"ko":["CloudWatch 알람을 사용하여 잘못된 람다 버전을 자동으로 롤백합니다.","CodeDeploy를 사용하여 카나리아 배포를 위한 트래픽 전환을 구성합니다.","버전 관리 및 테스트를 위해 람다 별칭을 설정합니다."],"es":["Automatización de la reversión de versiones de Lambda defectuosas utilizando alarmas de CloudWatch","Configuración del cambio de tráfico para despliegues de canario con CodeDeploy","Configuración de alias de Lambda para control de versiones y pruebas"],"fr":["Automatisation du rollback de versions de Lambda défectueuses à l''aide d''alarmes de CloudWatch","Configuration du changement de trafic pour les déploiements de canari avec CodeDeploy","Configuration des alias de Lambda pour la gestion de versions et les tests"],"de":["Automatisierung des Rollbacks fehlerhafter Lambda-Versionen mithilfe von CloudWatch-Alarmanlagen","Konfiguration des Traffikumschaltens für Canary-Deployments mit CodeDeploy","Einrichtung von Lambda-Aliasen für Versionskontrolle und Tests"],"pt":["Automatizar o rollback de versões defeituosas do Lambda usando alarmes do CloudWatch","Configurar a alteração de tráfego para implantações canary com CodeDeploy","Configurar aliases do Lambda para controle de versão e teste"],"ru":["Автоматизировать откат неисправных версий Lambda с помощью сигналов тревоги CloudWatch","Настроить переключение трафика для развертываний canary с помощью CodeDeploy","Настроить псевдонимы Lambda для контроля версий и тестирования"],"ar":["أتمتة الإستعادة من إصدارات لامدا المعيبة باستخدام إنذارات كلاود ووتش","تكوين تبديل حركة المرور لتثبيتات كاناري مع كود ديبلي","تكوين أسماء مستعارة لامدا للتحكم في الإصدارات والاختبار"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires AWS account and CDK setup","Limited to AWS Lambda and CDK TypeScript","Needs CloudWatch and CodeDeploy configuration"],"zh":["需要AWS账户和CDK设置","仅限于AWS Lambda和CDK TypeScript","需要CloudWatch和CodeDeploy配置"],"ja":["AWSアカウントとCDKの設定が必要","AWS LambdaとCDK TypeScriptに限定","CloudWatchとCodeDeployの設定が必要"],"ko":["AWS 계정 및 CDK 설정이 필요합니다.","AWS 람다 및 CDK TypeScript로 제한됩니다.","CloudWatch 및 CodeDeploy 구성이 필요합니다."],"es":["Requiere cuenta de AWS y configuración de CDK","Limitado a AWS Lambda y CDK TypeScript","Requiere configuración de CloudWatch y CodeDeploy"],"fr":["Nécessite un compte AWS et une configuration de CDK","Limité à AWS Lambda et CDK TypeScript","Nécessite une configuration de CloudWatch et CodeDeploy"],"de":["Benötigt ein AWS-Konto und CDK-Konfiguration","Begrenzt auf AWS Lambda und CDK TypeScript","Benötigt eine CloudWatch- und CodeDeploy-Konfiguration"],"pt":["Exige conta da AWS e configuração do CDK","Limitado ao AWS Lambda e CDK TypeScript","Necessita de configuração do CloudWatch e CodeDeploy"],"ru":["Требует учетной записи AWS и настройки CDK","Ограничен для AWS Lambda и CDK TypeScript","Требует настройки CloudWatch и CodeDeploy"],"ar":["يتطلب حساب آي دبليو إس وإعداد سي دي كي","محدود لآي دبليو إس لامدا وسي دي كي تا입 سكريبت","يحتاج إلى إعداد كلاود ووتش وكود ديبلي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Maple-and-Spruce/maple-and-spruce/local-development', 'community', 'Maple-and-Spruce', 'maple-and-spruce', 'Maple-and-Spruce/maple-and-spruce', 'local-development', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.407Z', '2026-02-18T03:24:51.436Z', NULL, '{"id":"Maple-and-Spruce/maple-and-spruce/local-development","name":"local-development","description":{"zh":"本地开发环境设置允许您在本地运行函数和Web应用程序，方便测试和调试","ja":"ローカル開発環境の設定により、関数とWebアプリケーションをローカルで実行してテストおよびデバッグできます","ko":"로컬 개발 환경 설정을 통해 함수 및 웹 애플리케이션을 로컬에서 실행하여 테스트 및 디버깅할 수 있습니다","es":"El desarrollo local te permite probar y depurar aplicaciones web de forma local antes de implementarlas. Utiliza comandos como ''npx nx run functions:serve'' para ejecutar funciones y aplicaciones web en tu entorno local.","fr":"Le développement local vous permet de tester et de déboguer des applications web en local avant de les déployer. Utilisez des commandes comme ''npx nx run functions:serve'' pour exécuter des fonctions et des applications web dans votre environnement local.","de":"Die lokale Entwicklung ermöglicht es Ihnen, Webanwendungen lokal zu testen und zu debuggen, bevor Sie sie bereitstellen. Verwenden Sie Befehle wie ''npx nx run functions:serve'', um Funktionen und Webanwendungen in Ihrer lokalen Umgebung auszuführen.","pt":"O desenvolvimento local permite executar aplicativos web e funções localmente para testes e depuração","ru":"Местное развитие позволяет запускать веб-приложения и функции локально для тестирования и отладки","ar":"التطوير المحلي يسمح بتشغيل تطبيقات الويب والوظائف محليًا للاختبار والتصحيح","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"本地开发环境设置","ja":"ローカル開発環境の設定","ko":"로컬 개발 환경 설정","es":"Desarrollo Local: Entorno de Pruebas para Aplicaciones Web","fr":"Développement Local : Environnement de Test pour Applicat...","de":"Lokale Entwicklung: Testumgebung für Webanwendungen","pt":"Desenvolvimento Local: Guia de Início Rápido","ru":"Местное развитие: быстрый старт","ar":"التطوير المحلي: دليل البداية السريعة","en":"local-development"},"description":{"zh":"本地开发环境设置允许您在本地运行函数和Web应用程序，方便测试和调试","ja":"ローカル開発環境の設定により、関数とWebアプリケーションをローカルで実行してテストおよびデバッグできます","ko":"로컬 개발 환경 설정을 통해 함수 및 웹 애플리케이션을 로컬에서 실행하여 테스트 및 디버깅할 수 있습니다","es":"El desarrollo local te permite probar y depurar aplicaciones web de forma local antes de implementarlas. Utiliza comandos como ''npx nx run functions:serve'' p...","fr":"Le développement local vous permet de tester et de déboguer des applications web en local avant de les déployer. Utilisez des commandes comme ''npx nx run fun...","de":"Die lokale Entwicklung ermöglicht es Ihnen, Webanwendungen lokal zu testen und zu debuggen, bevor Sie sie bereitstellen. Verwenden Sie Befehle wie ''npx nx ru...","pt":"O desenvolvimento local permite executar aplicativos web e funções localmente para testes e depuração","ru":"Местное развитие позволяет запускать веб-приложения и функции локально для тестирования и отладки","ar":"التطوير المحلي يسمح بتشغيل تطبيقات الويب والوظائف محليًا للاختبار والتصحيح","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["在本地运行函数","在本地运行Web应用程序","排除模拟器问题","运行Storybook","使用npx nx run functions:serve命令","自动构建和复制环境变量"],"ja":["関数をローカルで実行","Webアプリケーションをローカルで実行","エミュレータの問題を解決","Storybookを実行","npx nx run functions:serveコマンドを使用","自動ビルドと環境変数のコピー"],"ko":["함수를 로컬에서 실행","웹 애플리케이션을 로컬에서 실행","에뮬레이터 문제 해결","스토리북 실행","npx nx run functions:serve 명령어 사용","자동 빌드 및 환경 변수 복사"],"es":["Ejecución de funciones y aplicaciones web en un entorno local","Utiliza el comando ''npx nx run functions:serve'' para iniciar el servidor de desarrollo","Construye y copia archivos de configuración para el entorno de desarrollo","Permite la depuración y prueba de aplicaciones web antes de implementarlas","Integra con herramientas de desarrollo como Storybook"],"fr":["Exécution de fonctions et d''applications web dans un environnement local","Utilisez la commande ''npx nx run functions:serve'' pour démarrer le serveur de développement","Construit et copie les fichiers de configuration pour l''environnement de développement","Permet le débogage et les tests d''applications web avant de les déployer","Intègre avec des outils de développement comme Storybook"],"de":["Ausführung von Funktionen und Webanwendungen in einer lokalen Umgebung","Verwenden Sie den Befehl ''npx nx run functions:serve'', um den Entwicklungsserver zu starten","Baut und kopiert Konfigurationsdateien für die Entwicklungsumgebung","Ermöglicht das Debugging und Testen von Webanwendungen vor der Bereitstellung","Integriert mit Entwicklungstools wie Storybook"],"pt":["Executa aplicativos web e funções localmente","Permite testes e depuração","Utiliza o comando npx nx run functions:serve","Copia .env.dev para dist/apps/functions/.env","Inicia o watch"],"ru":["Запускает веб-приложения и функции локально","Позволяет тестировать и отлаживать","Использует команду npx nx run functions:serve","Копирует .env.dev в dist/apps/functions/.env","Запускает watch"],"ar":["تشغل تطبيقات الويب والوظائف محليًا","يسمح باختبار والتصحيح","يستخدم الأمر npx nx run functions:serve","ينسخ .env.dev إلى dist/apps/functions/.env","يبدأ التشغيل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["本地开发环境","函数运行","Web应用程序运行","模拟器问题","Storybook","npx nx run functions:serve","自动构建","环境变量","开发环境配置"],"ja":["ローカル開発環境","関数実行","Webアプリケーション実行","エミュレータ問題","Storybook","npx nx run functions:serve","自動ビルド","環境変数","開発環境構成"],"ko":["로컬 개발 환경","함수 실행","웹 애플리케이션 실행","에뮬레이터 문제","스토리북","npx nx run functions:serve","자동 빌드","환경 변수","개발 환경 구성"],"es":["desarrollo local","entorno de pruebas","aplicaciones web","depuración","pruebas","Storybook","nx","functions:serve"],"fr":["développement local","environnement de test","applications web","débogage","tests","Storybook","nx","functions:serve"],"de":["lokale Entwicklung","Testumgebung","Webanwendungen","Debugging","Tests","Storybook","nx","functions:serve"],"pt":["desenvolvimento local","testes local","depuração local","npx nx run functions:serve","desenvolvimento web","funções locais"],"ru":["местное развитие","локальное тестирование","локальная отладка","npx nx run functions:serve","веб-разработка","локальные функции"],"ar":["التطوير المحلي","اختبار محلي","تصحيح محلي","npx nx run functions:serve","تطوير الويب","وظائف محلية"]}},"owner":"Maple-and-Spruce","repo":"maple-and-spruce","repoPath":"Maple-and-Spruce/maple-and-spruce","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.407Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"local-development","description":"Running functions and web app locally, troubleshooting emulator issues, Storybook. Use when running or debugging locally.","bodyPreview":"# Local Development\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this skill when running the web app or functions locally, troubleshooting emulator issues, or running Storybook.\n\n## Important\n\nThe user runs functions and web app locally for testing. Claude writes code and creates PRs -- Claude does NOT deploy or run dev servers.\n\n## Running Functions Locally (user runs this)\n\n```bash\nnpx nx run functions:serve\n```\n\nThis command:\n1. Builds the functions\n2. Copies `.env.dev` to `dist/apps/functions/.env`\n3. Starts watch","body":"# Local Development\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this skill when running the web app or functions locally, troubleshooting emulator issues, or running Storybook.\n\n## Important\n\nThe user runs functions and web app locally for testing. Claude writes code and creates PRs -- Claude does NOT deploy or run dev servers.\n\n## Running Functions Locally (user runs this)\n\n```bash\nnpx nx run functions:serve\n```\n\nThis command:\n1. Builds the functions\n2. Copies `.env.dev` to `dist/apps/functions/.env`\n3. Starts watch mode for rebuilds (background)\n4. Runs `firebase serve --only functions --project=dev` on port 5001\n\n## Running Web App Locally (user runs this)\n\n```bash\nnpx nx run maple-spruce:serve\n```\n\nRuns on http://localhost:3000\n\n## Running Storybook\n\n```bash\nnpx nx run maple-spruce:storybook\n# Opens http://localhost:6006\n```\n\nBuilding Storybook:\n```bash\nnpx nx run maple-spruce:build-storybook\n# Output: dist/storybook/maple-spruce\n```\n\n## Running Tests\n\n```bash\nnpm test\n```\n\n## Deployment\n\nUser decides when to deploy to dev. Production deploys automatically via CI/CD on merge to main.\n\n## Troubleshooting Local Functions\n\n### Emulator prompts for environment variables\n\nThe Firebase emulator is not finding the `.env` file. This happens when:\n- The build clears `dist/apps/functions/` before the `.env` is copied\n- A stale watch process is interfering\n\n**Fix:**\n```bash\n# Kill any stale processes\npkill -f \"firebase serve\"\npkill -f \"nx run functions\"\n\n# Clean and restart\nrm -rf dist/apps/functions\nnpx nx run functions:serve\n```\n\n**Why this happens:**\n- Firebase reads `.env` from `dist/apps/functions/`\n- The `nx run functions:build` clears this directory\n- The serve command copies `.env.dev` after build, before starting the emulator\n- If ordering is wrong or stale processes exist, the emulator starts without the `.env`\n\n**Key indicator it''s working:**\n```\ni  functions: Loaded environment variables from .env.\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:24:51.436Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Full Stack Agents requiring streamlined local development workflows with Nx and Storybook.","zh":"适用于需要使用Nx和Storybook实现本地开发工作流的全栈代理。","ja":"NxとStorybookを使用してローカル開発ワークフローをストリームライン化する必要があるフルスタックエージェントに最適です。","ko":"Nx와 Storybook를 사용하여 로컬 개발 워크플로를 간소화해야 하는 풀스택 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Stack Completo que requieren flujos de trabajo de desarrollo local optimizados con Nx y Storybook.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents Full Stack nécessitant des flux de travail de développement local rationalisés avec Nx et Storybook.","de":"Ideal für Full-Stack-Agents, die optimierte lokale Entwicklungswerkflüsse mit Nx und Storybook erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Pilha Completa que exigem fluxos de trabalho de desenvolvimento local otimizados com Nx e Storybook.","ru":"Идеально для полнофункциональных агентов, требующих упрощенных локальных рабочих процессов разработки с Nx и Storybook.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التكنولوجيا الكاملة الذين يتطلبون تدفقات عمل محلية محسنة مع Nx و Storybook."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to run web apps and functions locally using Nx, leveraging `.env.dev` for development environments and enabling watch mode for real-time updates, while utilizing Storybook for UI component testing.","zh":"赋予代理在本地运行Web应用和函数的能力，利用`.env.dev`进行开发环境配置，并启用监视模式以实现实时更新，同时利用Storybook进行UI组件测试。","ja":"エージェントが`.env.dev`を使用して開発環境を設定し、ウォッチモードを有効にしてリアルタイム更新を実行しながら、Nxを使用してローカルでWebアプリと関数を実行する機能を提供し、Storybookを使用してUIコンポーネントのテストを実行します。","ko":"에이전트가 `.env.dev`를 사용하여 개발 환경을 구성하고 감시 모드를 활성화하여 실시간 업데이트를 수행하는 동시에 Nx를 사용하여 로컬에서 웹 애플리케이션과 함수를 실행할 수 있는 기능을 제공하며, Storybook를 사용하여 UI 컴포넌트 테스트를 수행합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes para ejecutar aplicaciones web y funciones localmente con Nx, aprovechando `.env.dev` para entornos de desarrollo y habilitando el modo de vigilancia para actualizaciones en tiempo real, mientras utiliza Storybook para pruebas de componentes de interfaz de usuario.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter des applications Web et des fonctions localement à l''aide de Nx, en exploitant `.env.dev` pour les environnements de développement et en activant le mode de surveillance pour des mises à jour en temps réel, tout en utilisant Storybook pour les tests de composants d''interface utilisateur.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Web-Apps und Funktionen lokal mit Nx auszuführen, indem `.env.dev` für Entwicklungsumgebungen genutzt und der Wachtmodus für Echtzeit-Updates aktiviert wird, während Storybook für Benutzeroberflächenkomponententests verwendet wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a executar aplicativos web e funções localmente usando Nx, aproveitando `.env.dev` para ambientes de desenvolvimento e habilitando o modo de observação para atualizações em tempo real, ao mesmo tempo em que utiliza Storybook para testes de componentes de interface do usuário.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью запускать веб-приложения и функции локально с помощью Nx, используя `.env.dev` для сред разработки и включая режим наблюдения для обновлений в реальном времени, а также использует Storybook для тестирования компонентов пользовательского интерфейса.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل khảية تشغيل التطبيقات الويب والوظائف محليًا باستخدام Nx ، مستفيدًا من `.env.dev` للبيئات التطويرية وتفعيل وضع المراقبة للتحديثات في الوقت الفعلي ، وفي الوقت نفسه يستخدم Storybook لاختبار مكونات واجهة المستخدم."},"useCases":{"en":["Running functions locally with `npx nx run functions:serve`","Troubleshooting emulator issues","Testing UI components with Storybook"],"zh":["使用`npx nx run functions:serve`在本地运行函数","排除模拟器问题","使用Storybook测试UI组件"],"ja":["`npx nx run functions:serve`を使用してローカルで関数を実行する","エミュレータの問題をトラブルシューティングする","Storybookを使用してUIコンポーネントをテストする"],"ko":["`npx nx run functions:serve`를 사용하여 로컬에서 함수를 실행하는 것","에뮬레이터 문제를 해결하는 것","Storybook를 사용하여 UI 컴포넌트를 테스트하는 것"],"es":["Ejecutar funciones localmente con `npx nx run functions:serve`","Depurar problemas del emulador","Probar componentes de interfaz de usuario con Storybook"],"fr":["Exécuter des fonctions localement avec `npx nx run functions:serve`","Dépanner les problèmes d''émulateur","Tester les composants d''interface utilisateur avec Storybook"],"de":["Funktionen lokal mit `npx nx run functions:serve` ausführen","Emulator-Probleme beheben","Benutzeroberflächenkomponenten mit Storybook testen"],"pt":["Executar funções localmente com `npx nx run functions:serve`","Solucionar problemas do emulador","Testar componentes de interface do usuário com Storybook"],"ru":["Запуск функций локально с `npx nx run functions:serve`","Устранение неполадок эмулятора","Тестирование компонентов пользовательского интерфейса с Storybook"],"ar":["تشغيل الوظائف محليًا مع `npx nx run functions:serve`","معالجة مشاكل المحاكي","اختبار مكونات واجهة المستخدم مع Storybook"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires local development environment setup","Does not deploy or run dev servers","Limited to Nx and Storybook ecosystems"],"zh":["需要本地开发环境设置","不部署或运行开发服务器","仅限于Nx和Storybook生态系统"],"ja":["ローカル開発環境の設定が必要","開発サーバーをデプロイまたは実行しない","NxとStorybookのエコシステムに限定される"],"ko":["로컬 개발 환경 설정이 필요합니다","개발 서버를 배포 또는 실행하지 않음","Nx와 Storybook의 에코시스템으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere configuración de entorno de desarrollo local","No implementa ni ejecuta servidores de desarrollo","Limitado a los ecosistemas de Nx y Storybook"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration d''environnement de développement local","Ne déploie ni n''exécute de serveurs de développement","Limité aux écosystèmes Nx et Storybook"],"de":["Benötigt Einrichtung einer lokalen Entwicklungsumgebung","Stellt keine Entwicklungsserver bereit oder führt sie aus","Begrenzt auf die Nx- und Storybook-Ökosysteme"],"pt":["Exige configuração de ambiente de desenvolvimento local","Não implanta ou executa servidores de desenvolvimento","Limitado aos ecossistemas Nx e Storybook"],"ru":["Требует настройки локальной среды разработки","Не развертывает и не запускает серверы разработки","Ограничен экосистемами Nx и Storybook"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد بيئة تطوير محلية","لا ي نشر أو تشغيل خوادم التطوير","محدود بنطاقات Nx و Storybook"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Awannaphasch2016/jousef-landing/infrastructure-verification', 'community', 'Awannaphasch2016', 'jousef-landing', 'Awannaphasch2016/jousef-landing', 'infrastructure-verification', 0, 0, 80, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.407Z', '2026-02-18T03:24:49.661Z', NULL, '{"id":"Awannaphasch2016/jousef-landing/infrastructure-verification","name":"infrastructure-verification","description":{"zh":"基础设施验证技能用于验证 AWS Lambda 部署和网络连接的可靠性和稳定性。它支持 AWS CLI、Terraform 和 CloudWatch 等技术栈","ja":"インフラストラクチャ検証スキルは、AWS Lambda のデプロイとネットワーク接続の信頼性と安定性を検証するために使用されます。AWS CLI、Terraform、CloudWatch などのテクノロジースタックをサポートしています","ko":"인프라스트럭처 검증 스킬은 AWS Lambda 배포 및 네트워크 연결의 안정성과 신뢰성을 검증하는 데 사용됩니다. AWS CLI, Terraform, CloudWatch 등의 기술 스택을 지원합니다","es":"La verificación de infraestructura es una habilidad crucial para los desarrolladores que trabajan con AWS, especialmente al depurar tiempos de espera de Lambda y validar rutas de red","fr":"La vérification d''infrastructure est une compétence essentielle pour les développeurs qui travaillent avec AWS, en particulier lors du débogage des temps d''attente de Lambda et de la validation des chemins réseau","de":"Die Infrastruktur-Verifizierung ist eine wichtige Fähigkeit für Entwickler, die mit AWS arbeiten, insbesondere beim Debuggen von Lambda-Timeouts und der Überprüfung von Netzwerkwegen","pt":"A verificação de infraestrutura é uma habilidade essencial para desenvolvedores que trabalham com AWS e Lambda. Ela ajuda a identificar problemas de conectividade e tempo limite.","ru":"Проверка инфраструктуры является необходимым навыком для разработчиков, работающих с AWS и Lambda. Она помогает выявить проблемы подключения и таймаута.","ar":"تحقق البنية التحتية هو مهارة أساسية لمطوري البرمجيات الذين يعملون مع AWS و Lambda. يساعد على تحديد مشاكل الاتصال وانتهاء الوقت.","en":"Landing page for Jousef Murad - B2B Process Architecture"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"基础设施验证技能 - AWS CLI 和 Terraform","ja":"インフラストラクチャ検証スキル - AWS CLI と Terraform","ko":"인프라스트럭처 검증 스킬 - AWS CLI 및 Terraform","es":"Verificación de Infraestructura para Desarrolladores","fr":"Vérification d''Infrastructure pour les Développeurs","de":"Infrastruktur-Verifizierung für Entwickler","pt":"Verificação de Infraestrutura para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Проверка инфраструктуры для разработчиков","ar":"تحقق البنية التحتية لمطوري البرمجيات","en":"infrastructure-verification"},"description":{"zh":"基础设施验证技能用于验证 AWS Lambda 部署和网络连接的可靠性和稳定性。它支持 AWS CLI、Terraform 和 CloudWatch 等技术栈","ja":"インフラストラクチャ検証スキルは、AWS Lambda のデプロイとネットワーク接続の信頼性と安定性を検証するために使用されます。AWS CLI、Terraform、CloudWatch などのテクノロジースタックをサポートしています","ko":"인프라스트럭처 검증 스킬은 AWS Lambda 배포 및 네트워크 연결의 안정성과 신뢰성을 검증하는 데 사용됩니다. AWS CLI, Terraform, CloudWatch 등의 기술 스택을 지원합니다","es":"La verificación de infraestructura es una habilidad crucial para los desarrolladores que trabajan con AWS, especialmente al depurar tiempos de espera de Lamb...","fr":"La vérification d''infrastructure est une compétence essentielle pour les développeurs qui travaillent avec AWS, en particulier lors du débogage des temps d''a...","de":"Die Infrastruktur-Verifizierung ist eine wichtige Fähigkeit für Entwickler, die mit AWS arbeiten, insbesondere beim Debuggen von Lambda-Timeouts und der Über...","pt":"A verificação de infraestrutura é uma habilidade essencial para desenvolvedores que trabalham com AWS e Lambda. Ela ajuda a identificar problemas de conectiv...","ru":"Проверка инфраструктуры является необходимым навыком для разработчиков, работающих с AWS и Lambda. Она помогает выявить проблемы подключения и таймаута.","ar":"تحقق البنية التحتية هو مهارة أساسية لمطوري البرمجيات الذين يعملون مع AWS و Lambda. يساعد على تحديد مشاكل الاتصال وانتهاء الوقت.","en":"Landing page for Jousef Murad - B2B Process Architecture"},"definition":{"en":"Landing page for Jousef Murad - B2B Process Architecture"},"features":{"zh":["支持 AWS CLI 和 Terraform","验证 Lambda 部署和网络连接","支持 CloudWatch 和 VPC","调试和排除故障","验证网络路径到 AWS"],"ja":["AWS CLI と Terraform をサポート","Lambda デプロイとネットワーク接続を検証","CloudWatch と VPC をサポート","デバッグとトラブルシューティング","AWS へのネットワークパスを検証"],"ko":["AWS CLI 및 Terraform 지원","Lambda 배포 및 네트워크 연결 검증","CloudWatch 및 VPC 지원","디버깅 및 문제 해결","AWSへの 네트워크 경로 검증"],"es":["Depuración de tiempos de espera de Lambda","Validación de rutas de red a AWS","Uso de AWS CLI y Terraform","Integración con CloudWatch y bash","Aplicación del principio de contrato de infraestructura-aplicación"],"fr":["Débogage des temps d''attente de Lambda","Validation des chemins réseau vers AWS","Utilisation de AWS CLI et Terraform","Intégration avec CloudWatch et bash","Application du principe de contrat d''infrastructure-application"],"de":["Debuggen von Lambda-Timeouts","Überprüfung von Netzwerkwegen zu AWS","Verwendung von AWS CLI und Terraform","Integration mit CloudWatch und bash","Anwendung des Prinzips des Infrastruktur-Anwendungsvertrags"],"pt":["Verificação de infraestrutura antes de implantar código Lambda em VPC","Investigação de problemas de tempo limite de conexão","Depuração de padrões de falha determinística","Validação do caminho de rede para AWS"],"ru":["Проверка инфраструктуры перед развертыванием кода Lambda в VPC","Расследование проблем с таймаутом соединения","Отладка детерминированных моделей отказов","Валидация сетевого пути к AWS"],"ar":["تحقق البنية التحتية قبل نشر 코드 Lambda في VPC","التحقيق في مشاكل انتهاء وقت الاتصال","تصحيح أخطاء أنماط الفشل المتعلمة","التحقق من مسار الشبكة إلى AWS"]},"keywords":{"zh":["基础设施验证","AWS Lambda","AWS CLI","Terraform","CloudWatch","VPC","网络连接","部署","调试"],"ja":["インフラストラクチャ検証","AWS Lambda","AWS CLI","Terraform","CloudWatch","VPC","ネットワーク接続","デプロイ","デバッグ"],"ko":["인프라스트럭처 검증","AWS Lambda","AWS CLI","Terraform","CloudWatch","VPC","네트워크 연결","배포","디버깅"],"es":["verificación de infraestructura","depuración de Lambda","validación de rutas de red","AWS CLI","Terraform","CloudWatch","bash","desarrollo de software","infraestructura en la nube"],"fr":["vérification d''infrastructure","débogage de Lambda","validation des chemins réseau","AWS CLI","Terraform","CloudWatch","bash","développement de logiciels","infrastructure cloud"],"de":["Infrastruktur-Verifizierung","Debuggen von Lambda","Überprüfung von Netzwerkwegen","AWS CLI","Terraform","CloudWatch","bash","Software-Entwicklung","Cloud-Infrastruktur"],"pt":["verificação de infraestrutura","desenvolvedores","AWS","Lambda","VPC","tempo limite de conexão","depuração"],"ru":["проверка инфраструктуры","разработчики","AWS","Lambda","VPC","таймаут соединения","отладка"],"ar":["تحقق البنية التحتية","مطوري البرمجيات","AWS","Lambda","VPC","انتهاء وقت الاتصال","تصحيح الأخطاء"]}},"owner":"Awannaphasch2016","repo":"jousef-landing","repoPath":"Awannaphasch2016/jousef-landing","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.407Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"infrastructure-verification","description":"Verify AWS infrastructure configuration before deployment. Use when validating VPC endpoints, NAT Gateway capacity, security groups, or debugging network path issues that cause Lambda connection timeouts.","bodyPreview":"# Infrastructure Verification Skill\n\n**Tech Stack**: AWS CLI, Terraform, VPC, CloudWatch, bash\n\n**Source**: Extracted from PDF S3 upload timeout investigation (2026-01-05) and Infrastructure-Application Contract principle.\n\n---\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse the infrastructure-verification skill when:\n- ✓ Before deploying Lambda-in-VPC code\n- ✓ Investigating Lambda connection timeouts\n- ✓ Debugging deterministic failure patterns (first N succeed, last M fail)\n- ✓ Validating network path to AWS","body":"# Infrastructure Verification Skill\n\n**Tech Stack**: AWS CLI, Terraform, VPC, CloudWatch, bash\n\n**Source**: Extracted from PDF S3 upload timeout investigation (2026-01-05) and Infrastructure-Application Contract principle.\n\n---\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse the infrastructure-verification skill when:\n- ✓ Before deploying Lambda-in-VPC code\n- ✓ Investigating Lambda connection timeouts\n- ✓ Debugging deterministic failure patterns (first N succeed, last M fail)\n- ✓ Validating network path to AWS services (S3, DynamoDB, RDS)\n- ✓ After adding VPC endpoints\n- ✓ Before concurrent Lambda executions\n\n**DO NOT use this skill for:**\n- ✗ Application code debugging (use error-investigation)\n- ✗ Performance optimization (different focus)\n- ✗ IAM permission issues (use AWS CLI directly)\n\n---\n\n## Core Verification Principles\n\n### Principle 1: Infrastructure Dependency Validation\n\n**From CLAUDE.md Principle #15:**\n> \"Before deploying code that depends on AWS infrastructure (S3, VPC endpoints, NAT Gateway), verify infrastructure exists and is correctly configured. Network path issues cause deterministic failure patterns.\"\n\n**When to validate:**\n- Before deploying Lambda functions that make AWS service calls\n- After Terraform infrastructure changes\n- When investigating Lambda timeout patterns\n- Before increasing concurrency limits\n\n### Principle 2: Pattern Recognition\n\n**Failure Pattern Types:**\n\n| Pattern | Root Cause | Investigation Priority |\n|---------|------------|----------------------|\n| **First N succeed, last M fail** | Infrastructure bottleneck (NAT, connection limits) | HIGH - VPC endpoint missing |\n| **Random scattered failures** | Performance issue (slow API, memory) | MEDIUM - Optimize code |\n| **All operations fail** | Configuration issue (permissions, endpoint) | HIGH - Fix config |\n| **Intermittent failures** | Rate limiting, transient network | LOW - Add retries |\n\n**Deterministic pattern** (first N succeed, last M fail) is strongest signal of infrastructure bottleneck.\n\n---\n\n## Verification Workflows\n\n### Workflow 1: VPC Endpoint Verification\n\n**Use when:** Lambda-in-VPC needs to access S3 or DynamoDB\n\n**Steps:**\n\n```bash\n# 1. Check if VPC endpoint exists\naws ec2 describe-vpc-endpoints \\\n  --filters \"Name=vpc-id,Values=vpc-xxx\" \\\n            \"Name=service-name,Values=com.amazonaws.ap-southeast-1.s3\" \\\n  --query ''VpcEndpoints[*].{ID:VpcEndpointId,State:State,Service:ServiceName}'' \\\n  --output table\n\n# Expected output (if endpoint exists):\n# -----------------------------------------\n# | DescribeVpcEndpoints                  |\n# +-------+-------+------------------------+\n# | ID    | State | Service                |\n# +-------+-------+------------------------+\n# | vpce-xxx | available | com.amazonaws.ap-southeast-1.s3 |\n# +-------+-------+------------------------+\n\n# If empty → No S3 VPC Endpoint (traffic goes through NAT Gateway)\n\n# 2. Verify endpoint state\naws ec2 describe-vpc-endpoints \\\n  --vpc-endpoint-ids vpce-xxx \\\n  --query ''VpcEndpoints[0].State'' \\\n  --output text\n\n# Expected: \"available\"\n# If \"pending\" → Wait for creation\n# If \"failed\" → Check Terraform logs\n\n# 3. Verify route table attachment\naws ec2 describe-vpc-endpoints \\\n  --vpc-endpoint-ids vpce-xxx \\\n  --query ''VpcEndpoints[0].RouteTableIds'' \\\n  --output table\n\n# Expected: List of route table IDs (must include Lambda subnet route tables)\n\n# 4. Check Lambda subnet route tables\naws lambda get-function-configuration \\\n  --function-name my-function \\\n  --query ''VpcConfig.SubnetIds'' \\\n  --output text | xargs -I {} aws ec2 describe-subnets --subnet-ids {}\n\n# Compare: Lambda subnets'' route tables should be in VPC endpoint''s RouteTableIds\n\n# 5. Verify S3 prefix list in route tables\nROUTE_TABLE_ID=$(aws ec2 describe-route-tables \\\n  --filters \"Name=vpc-id,Values=vpc-xxx\" \\\n  --query ''RouteTables[0].RouteTableId'' \\\n  --output text)\n\naws ec2 describe-route-tables \\\n  --route-table-ids $ROUTE_TABLE_ID \\\n  --query ''RouteTables[*].Routes[?GatewayId==`vpce-xxx`]''\n\n# Expected: Route with DestinationPrefixListId (S3 prefix list)\n```\n\n**Verification checklist:**\n- [ ] VPC endpoint exists (`describe-vpc-endpoints` returns result)\n- [ ] State is \"available\" (not \"pending\" or \"failed\")\n- [ ] Route tables attached (includes Lambda subnet route tables)\n- [ ] S3 prefix list routes created (check route tables)\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Missing VPC endpoint → Create with Terraform\n- State \"pending\" → Wait 2-3 minutes\n- Route tables not attached → Update Terraform `route_table_ids`\n- Lambda subnets not covered → Verify subnet route table IDs\n\n### Workflow 2: NAT Gateway Diagnosis\n\n**Use when:** Investigating Lambda connection timeouts with external services\n\n**Steps:**\n\n```bash\n# 1. Check NAT Gateway exists\naws ec2 describe-nat-gateways \\\n  --filter \"Name=vpc-id,Values=vpc-xxx\" \\\n  --query ''NatGateways[*].{ID:NatGatewayId,State:State,PublicIp:NatGatewayAddresses[0].PublicIp}'' \\\n  --output table\n\n# Expected: State \"available\"\n\n# 2. Check route tables using NAT Gateway\naws ec2 describe-route-tables \\\n  --filters \"Name=vpc-id,Values=vpc-xxx\" \\\n  --query ''RouteTables[*].Routes[?NatGatewayId!=`null`].[RouteTableId,DestinationCidrBlock,NatGatewayId]'' \\\n  --output table\n\n# Expected: Route 0.0.0.0/0 → nat-xxx (default route through NAT)\n\n# 3. Analyze connection saturation pattern\n# Run this during concurrent Lambda executions\naws logs filter-log-events \\\n  --log-group-name /aws/lambda/my-function \\\n  --start-time $(date -d ''5 minutes ago'' +%s)000 \\\n  --filter-pattern \"START RequestId\" \\\n  --query ''events[*].timestamp'' \\\n  --output text | xargs -n1 date -d @\n\n# Check execution pattern:\n# - All start within 1 second → Concurrent execution\n# - Some timeout after 600s → NAT Gateway saturation\n\n# 4. Check for connection timeout errors\naws logs filter-log-events \\\n  --log-group-name /aws/lambda/my-function \\\n  --filter-pattern \"ConnectTimeoutError\" \\\n  --query ''events[*].message'' \\\n  --output text\n\n# If errors found → NAT Gateway connection limit reached\n\n# 5. Calculate concurrent connection demand\nCONCURRENT_LAMBDAS=$(aws logs filter-log-events \\\n  --log-group-name /aws/lambda/my-function \\\n  --start-time $(date -d ''1 minute ago'' +%s)000 \\\n  --filter-pattern \"START RequestId\" \\\n  --query ''length(events)'' \\\n  --output text)\n\necho \"Concurrent Lambdas: $CONCURRENT_LAMBDAS\"\necho \"NAT Gateway connection limit: ~55,000 (but establishment rate limited)\"\n```\n\n**NAT Gateway saturation indicators:**\n- ✅ Deterministic pattern (first N succeed, last M fail)\n- ✅ ConnectTimeoutError in logs\n- ✅ Long execution times (600s = boto3 default timeout)\n- ✅ Timeline shows concurrent starts → split success/failure\n\n**Solution:** Add VPC Gateway Endpoint for S3/DynamoDB to bypass NAT\n\n### Workflow 3: Network Path Validation\n\n**Use when:** Verifying Lambda can reach AWS services\n\n**Steps:**\n\n```bash\n# 1. Identify Lambda VPC configuration\naws lambda get-function-configuration \\\n  --function-name my-function \\\n  --query ''VpcConfig.{VpcId:VpcId,SubnetIds:SubnetIds,SecurityGroupIds:SecurityGroupIds}'' \\\n  --output json\n\n# Save VPC ID, Subnet IDs, Security Group IDs\n\n# 2. Check security group egress rules\naws ec2 describe-security-groups \\\n  --group-ids sg-xxx \\\n  --query ''SecurityGroups[*].IpPermissionsEgress[*].{Proto:IpProtocol,Port:FromPort,Dest:IpRanges[0].CidrIp}'' \\\n  --output table\n\n# Expected: 0.0.0.0/0 allowed (all egress)\n# If restricted → Add rule for destination service\n\n# 3. Check route table for Lambda subnet\nSUBNET_ID=$(aws lambda get-function-configuration \\\n  --function-name my-function \\\n  --query ''VpcConfig.SubnetIds[0]'' \\\n  --output text)\n\nROUTE_TABLE_ID=$(aws ec2 describe-route-tables \\\n  --filters \"Name=association.subnet-id,Values=$SUBNET_ID\" \\\n  --query ''RouteTables[0].RouteTableId'' \\\n  --output text)\n\naws ec2 describe-route-tables \\\n  --route-table-ids $ROUTE_TABLE_ID \\\n  --query ''RouteTables[*].Routes[*].[DestinationCidrBlock,GatewayId,NatGatewayId]'' \\\n  --output table\n\n# Expected routes:\n# - local → vpc-xxx (VPC internal)\n# - 0.0.0.0/0 → nat-xxx (internet via NAT) OR vpce-xxx (S3 via endpoint)\n\n# 4. Test actual network path (requires test Lambda invocation)\n# Deploy temporary test Lambda:\n# - Attempts connection to S3\n# - Logs connection details\n# - Reports success/failure\n\n# 5. Analyze test results\naws logs tail /aws/lambda/network-test --since 1m\n\n# Look for:\n# - Connection established (success)\n# - Connection timeout (NAT saturated)\n# - Connection refused (security group blocked)\n# - DNS resolution failure (VPC DNS issue)\n```\n\n**Network path checklist:**\n- [ ] Lambda in VPC (`VpcConfig` not empty)\n- [ ] Security group allows egress to destination\n- [ ] Route table has path to destination (NAT or VPC endpoint)\n- [ ] VPC endpoint exists for AWS service (S3, DynamoDB)\n- [ ] Test invocation confirms connectivity\n\n### Workflow 4: Post-Deployment Infrastructure Validation\n\n**Use when:** After deploying infrastructure changes (VPC endpoints, security groups)\n\n**Steps:**\n\n```bash\n# 1. Verify Terraform outputs\ncd terraform\nterraform output s3_vpc_endpoint_id        # Should return vpce-xxx\nterraform output s3_vpc_endpoint_state     # Should return \"available\"\n\n# 2. Run smoke test Lambda invocation\naws lambda invoke \\\n  --function-name my-function \\\n  --payload ''{\"test\": true}'' \\\n  /tmp/response.json\n\n# Check response\ncat /tmp/response.json | jq .\n\n# 3. Verify CloudWatch logs show success\naws logs tail /aws/lambda/my-function --since 1m --follow\n\n# Expected:\n# - No ConnectTimeoutError\n# - Operation completes in expected time (2-3s not 600s)\n# - Success message logged\n\n# 4. Test concurrent execution (simulate production load)\nfor i in {1..10}; do\n  aws lambda invoke \\\n    --function-name my-function \\\n    --payload \"{\\\"id\\\": $i}\" \\\n    --invocation-type Event \\\n    /tmp/response_$i.json &\ndone\nwait\n\n# 5. Analyze concurrent execution results\naws logs filter-log-events \\\n  --log-group-name /aws/lambda/my-function \\\n  --start-time $(date -d ''5 minutes ago'' +%s)000 \\\n  --filter-pattern \"ConnectTimeoutError\" \\\n  --query ''length(events)'' \\\n  --output text\n\n# Expected: 0 (no timeout errors)\n# If > 0 → Infrastructure issue still exists\n\n# 6. Verify 100% success rate\naws logs filter-log-events \\\n  --log-group-name /aws/lambda/my-function \\\n  --start-time $(date -d ''5 minutes ago'' +%s)000 \\\n  --filter-pattern \"✅\" \\\n  --query ''length(events)'' \\\n  --output text\n\n# Expected: 10 (all concurrent executions succeeded)\n```\n\n**Post-deployment checklist:**\n- [ ] Terraform outputs confirm resource created\n- [ ] Smoke test invocation succeeds\n- [ ] CloudWatch logs show no errors\n- [ ] Concurrent execution test (10+ invocations)\n- [ ] 100% success rate (no timeouts)\n- [ ] Execution time within expected range (2-3s not 600s)\n\n---\n\n## Common Infrastructure Issues\n\n### Issue 1: Missing S3 VPC Endpoint\n\n**Symptom:**\n- Lambda timeout after 600s\n- Error: `ConnectTimeoutError: Connect timeout on endpoint URL: \"https://bucket.s3.region.amazonaws.com/...\"`\n- Pattern: First N concurrent operations succeed, last M timeout\n\n**Diagnosis:**\n\n```bash\n# Check for S3 VPC endpoint\naws ec2 describe-vpc-endpoints \\\n  --filters \"Name=vpc-id,Values=vpc-xxx\" \\\n            \"Name=service-name,Values=com.amazonaws.region.s3\"\n\n# If empty → No endpoint (S3 traffic goes through NAT)\n```\n\n**Fix:**\n\n```hcl\n# terraform/s3_vpc_endpoint.tf\ndata \"aws_route_tables\" \"vpc_route_tables\" {\n  vpc_id = data.aws_vpc.default.id\n}\n\nresource \"aws_vpc_endpoint\" \"s3\" {\n  vpc_id            = data.aws_vpc.default.id\n  service_name      = \"com.amazonaws.${var.aws_region}.s3\"\n  vpc_endpoint_type = \"Gateway\"\n\n  route_table_ids = data.aws_route_tables.vpc_route_tables.ids\n\n  policy = jsonencode({\n    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    Statement = [{\n      Effect    = \"Allow\"\n      Principal = \"*\"\n      Action    = \"s3:*\"\n      Resource  = \"*\"\n    }]\n  })\n\n  tags = {\n    Name = \"s3-endpoint\"\n  }\n}\n\noutput \"s3_vpc_endpoint_id\" {\n  value = aws_vpc_endpoint.s3.id\n}\n\noutput \"s3_vpc_endpoint_state\" {\n  value = aws_vpc_endpoint.s3.state\n}\n```\n\n**Verification:**\n\n```bash\ncd terraform\nterraform apply\nterraform output s3_vpc_endpoint_state  # Should be \"available\"\n\n# Test Lambda invocation\naws lambda invoke --function-name my-function --payload ''{}'' /tmp/response.json\naws logs tail /aws/lambda/my-function --since 1m\n# Expected: No timeout, completes in 2-3s\n```\n\n### Issue 2: NAT Gateway Connection Saturation\n\n**Symptom:**\n- Deterministic failure pattern (first 5 succeed, last 5 timeout)\n- All timeouts occur after ~10 minutes (boto3 default + retries)\n- Timeline analysis shows concurrent Lambda starts\n\n**Diagnosis:**\n\n```bash\n# Check timeline of Lambda executions\naws logs filter-log-events \\\n  --log-group-name /aws/lambda/my-function \\\n  --start-time $(date -d ''30 minutes ago'' +%s)000 \\\n  --filter-pattern \"START RequestId\" \\\n  | jq -r ''.events[] | .timestamp as $ts | ($ts/1000 | strftime(\"%H:%M:%S\")) + \" \" + (.message | split(\" \")[2])''\n\n# Look for:\n# - All start within 1 second (concurrent)\n# - Check which RequestIds have errors\naws logs filter-log-events \\\n  --log-group-name /aws/lambda/my-function \\\n  --filter-pattern \"ConnectTimeoutError\" \\\n  | jq -r ''.events[].message'' | grep -o \"RequestId: [a-z0-9-]*\"\n\n# Pattern: Last N RequestIds consistently fail\n```\n\n**Root Cause:**\n- NAT Gateway has limited connection establishment rate\n- Concurrent Lambdas try to establish S3 connections simultaneously\n- First N connections succeed → Upload completes in 2-3s\n- Last M connections queued → Eventually timeout after 600s\n\n**Fix:** Add S3 VPC Gateway Endpoint (see Issue 1)\n\n**Why this works:**\n- VPC Gateway Endpoint bypasses NAT Gateway\n- S3 traffic routed directly within AWS network\n- No connection establishment limits\n- Free (Gateway endpoints have no hourly charge)\n\n### Issue 3: Security Group Blocking Egress\n\n**Symptom:**\n- Lambda unable to connect to AWS service\n- Error: Connection refused or timeout\n- All invocations fail (not deterministic pattern)\n\n**Diagnosis:**\n\n```bash\n# Check security group egress rules\naws lambda get-function-configuration \\\n  --function-name my-function \\\n  --query ''VpcConfig.SecurityGroupIds[0]'' \\\n  --output text | xargs -I {} aws ec2 describe-security-groups --group-ids {}\n\n# Look for egress rules allowing HTTPS (port 443)\n# Expected: 0.0.0.0/0 or specific AWS service prefix list\n```\n\n**Fix:**\n\n```hcl\n# terraform/security_groups.tf\nresource \"aws_security_group_rule\" \"lambda_egress_https\" {\n  type              = \"egress\"\n  from_port         = 443\n  to_port           = 443\n  protocol          = \"tcp\"\n  cidr_blocks       = [\"0.0.0.0/0\"]\n  security_group_id = aws_security_group.lambda.id\n}\n```\n\n### Issue 4: Route Table Not Attached to VPC Endpoint\n\n**Symptom:**\n- VPC endpoint exists and is \"available\"\n- Lambda still times out connecting to S3\n- Deterministic or random failures\n\n**Diagnosis:**\n\n```bash\n# Check VPC endpoint route table attachment\naws ec2 describe-vpc-endpoints \\\n  --vpc-endpoint-ids vpce-xxx \\\n  --query ''VpcEndpoints[0].RouteTableIds'' \\\n  --output table\n\n# Get Lambda subnet route table\naws lambda get-function-configuration \\\n  --function-name my-function \\\n  --query ''VpcConfig.SubnetIds[0]'' \\\n  --output text | xargs -I {} aws ec2 describe-route-tables \\\n  --filters \"Name=association.subnet-id,Values={}\" \\\n  --query ''RouteTables[0].RouteTableId'' \\\n  --output text\n\n# Compare: Lambda''s route table should be in endpoint''s RouteTableIds\n```\n\n**Fix:**\n\n```hcl\n# terraform/s3_vpc_endpoint.tf\ndata \"aws_route_tables\" \"vpc_route_tables\" {\n  vpc_id = data.aws_vpc.default.id\n}\n\nresource \"aws_vpc_endpoint\" \"s3\" {\n  # ... other config ...\n\n  # Attach to ALL route tables (includes Lambda subnets)\n  route_table_ids = data.aws_route_tables.vpc_route_tables.ids\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Integration with Other Skills\n\n### With error-investigation\n- Use infrastructure-verification BEFORE error-investigation when:\n  - Investigating Lambda timeout patterns\n  - Debugging connection failures\n  - Analyzing deterministic failure patterns\n- Use error-investigation AFTER infrastructure-verification when:\n  - Infrastructure confirmed correct but errors persist\n  - Need to analyze application logs\n  - Debugging business logic failures\n\n### With deployment skill\n- Use infrastructure-verification:\n  - BEFORE deploying Lambda-in-VPC code\n  - AFTER deploying infrastructure changes (Terraform apply)\n  - During post-deployment validation\n- Complements deployment smoke tests with infrastructure-specific checks\n\n### With testing-workflow\n- Infrastructure verification is a form of pre-deployment testing\n- Validates infrastructure-application contract (CLAUDE.md Principle #15)\n- Catches configuration issues before code deployment\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### VPC Endpoint Types\n\n| Type | Services | Cost | Use Case |\n|------|----------|------|----------|\n| **Gateway** | S3, DynamoDB | FREE | High-throughput data access |\n| **Interface** | Most AWS services | ~$7.50/month | Other services (Secrets Manager, etc.) |\n\n### NAT Gateway Limits\n\n| Limit | Value | Impact |\n|-------|-------|--------|\n| **Concurrent connections** | 55,000 | Theoretical max |\n| **Connection establishment rate** | Limited | Causes saturation with concurrent Lambdas |\n| **Data transfer cost** | $0.045/GB | Expensive for large transfers |\n\n**Recommendation:** Use VPC Gateway Endpoints for S3/DynamoDB (free, unlimited, faster)\n\n### Common AWS CLI Commands\n\n```bash\n# VPC endpoint\naws ec2 describe-vpc-endpoints --vpc-endpoint-ids vpce-xxx\n\n# NAT Gateway\naws ec2 describe-nat-gateways --nat-gateway-ids nat-xxx\n\n# Security groups\naws ec2 describe-security-groups --group-ids sg-xxx\n\n# Route tables\naws ec2 describe-route-tables --route-table-ids rtb-xxx\n\n# Lambda VPC config\naws lambda get-function-configuration --function-name my-function --query ''VpcConfig''\n```\n\n---\n\n## File Organization\n\n```\n.claude/skills/infrastructure-verification/\n└── SKILL.md              # This file (complete skill)\n```\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n- [VPC Endpoints](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/vpc-endpoints.html)\n- [NAT Gateway](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-nat-gateway.html)\n- [Lambda VPC Configuration](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-vpc.html)\n- [Bug Hunt Report](../../bug-hunts/2026-01-05-pdf-s3-upload-timeout.md) - Real-world investigation\n- CLAUDE.md Principle #15 (Infrastructure-Application Contract)\n- CLAUDE.md Principle #2 (Progressive Evidence Strengthening)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:24:49.661Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Cloud Agents needing advanced infrastructure validation capabilities using AWS CLI and Terraform","zh":"非常适合需要使用 AWS CLI 和 Terraform 进行高级基础设施验证的云代理","ja":"AWS CLI と Terraform を使用した高度なインフラストラクチャの検証機能が必要なクラウドエージェントに最適","ko":"AWS CLI와 Terraform을 사용하여 고급 인프라スト럭처 검증 기능이 필요한 클라우드 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Nube que necesitan capacidades de validación de infraestructura avanzadas utilizando AWS CLI y Terraform","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Cloud nécessitant des capacités de validation d''infrastructure avancées utilisant AWS CLI et Terraform","de":"Perfekt für Cloud-Agents, die erweiterte Infrastrukturvalidierungsfunktionen unter Verwendung von AWS CLI und Terraform benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Nuvem que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de validação de infraestrutura usando AWS CLI e Terraform","ru":"Идеально для облачных агентов, которым требуются расширенные возможности проверки инфраструктуры с использованием AWS CLI и Terraform","ar":"مثالي لوسائل وكلاء السحابي الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات متقدمة للتحقق من البنية التحتية باستخدام AWS CLI و Terraform"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to verify infrastructure setups using Terraform, monitor performance with CloudWatch, and debug network issues within VPCs, all while leveraging bash scripting for automation","zh":"赋予代理验证基础设施设置、使用 CloudWatch 监控性能、在 VPC 中调试网络问题的能力，同时利用 bash 脚本进行自动化","ja":"エージェントに Terraform を使用してインフラストラクチャの設定を検証し、CloudWatch を使用してパフォーマンスを監視し、VPC 内のネットワークの問題をデバッグする機能を提供し、同時に bash スクリプティングを使用して自動化する","ko":"에이전트에게 Terraform을 사용하여 인프라스트럭처 설정을 검증하고 CloudWatch를 사용하여 성능을 모니터링하며 VPC 내의 네트워크 문제를 디버깅할 수 있는 기능을 제공하며,同時に bash 스크립팅을 사용하여 자동화하는 기능을 제공","es":"Habilita a los agentes a verificar configuraciones de infraestructura utilizando Terraform, monitorear el rendimiento con CloudWatch y depurar problemas de red dentro de las VPC, todo mientras aprovecha la programación bash para la automatización","fr":"Permet aux agents de vérifier les configurations d''infrastructure à l''aide de Terraform, de surveiller les performances avec CloudWatch et de déboguer les problèmes de réseau au sein des VPC, le tout en exploitant la programmation bash pour l''automatisation","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Infrastrukturkonfigurationen mit Terraform zu überprüfen, die Leistung mit CloudWatch zu überwachen und Netzwerkprobleme innerhalb von VPCs zu debuggen, während sie gleichzeitig die bash-Programmierung für die Automatisierung nutzen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a verificar configurações de infraestrutura usando Terraform, monitorar o desempenho com CloudWatch e depurar problemas de rede dentro de VPCs, tudo isso aproveitando a automação de scripts bash","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проверять настройки инфраструктуры с использованием Terraform, контролировать производительность с помощью CloudWatch и устранять сбои в работе сети внутри VPC, все это при помощи автоматизации скриптов bash","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من التحقق من إعدادات البنية التحتية باستخدام Terraform ومراقبة الأداء مع CloudWatch وتصحيح مشاكل الشبكة داخل VPCs، وكل ذلك بالاستفادة من自动ية البرمجة باستخدام bash"},"useCases":{"en":["Validating network paths to AWS","Debugging Lambda connection timeouts","Investigating deterministic failure patterns in Lambda-in-VPC deployments","Automating infrastructure verification before deploying Lambda-in-VPC code"],"zh":["验证 AWS 的网络路径","调试 Lambda 连接超时","调查 VPC 中的 Lambda 部署中的确定性故障模式","在部署 Lambda-in-VPC 代码之前自动化基础设施验证"],"ja":["AWS のネットワークパスを検証する","Lambda の接続タイムアウトをデバッグする","VPC 内の Lambda デプロイメントにおける決定的な故障パターンを調査する","Lambda-in-VPC コードをデプロイする前にインフラストラクチャの検証を自動化する"],"ko":["AWS의 네트워크 경로를 검증","Lambda 연결 시간 초과를 디버깅","VPC 내의 Lambda 배포에서 결정적인 실패 패턴을 조사","Lambda-in-VPC 코드를 배포하기 전에 인프라스트럭처 검증을 자동화"],"es":["Validar rutas de red a AWS","Depurar tiempos de espera de conexión de Lambda","Investigar patrones de fallo deterministas en implementaciones de Lambda en VPC","Automatizar la verificación de infraestructura antes de implementar código Lambda en VPC"],"fr":["Valider les chemins de réseau vers AWS","Déboguer les délais d''attente de connexion de Lambda","Enquêter sur les modèles de défaillance déterministes dans les déploiements de Lambda dans les VPC","Automatiser la vérification de l''infrastructure avant de déployer du code Lambda dans les VPC"],"de":["Netzpfade zu AWS überprüfen","Lambda-Verbindungszeitüberschreitungen debuggen","Bestimmte Ausfallmuster in Lambda-in-VPC-Implementierungen untersuchen","Infrastrukturüberprüfung vor der Bereitstellung von Lambda-in-VPC-Code automatisieren"],"pt":["Validar caminhos de rede para AWS","Depurar tempos limite de conexão Lambda","Investigar padrões de falha determinística em implantações Lambda-in-VPC","Automatizar verificação de infraestrutura antes de implantar código Lambda-in-VPC"],"ru":["Проверять сетевые пути до AWS","Отлаживать таймауты подключения Lambda","Изучать детерминированные шаблоны сбоев в развертываниях Lambda-in-VPC","Автоматизировать проверку инфраструктуры перед развертыванием кода Lambda-in-VPC"],"ar":["التحقق من مسارات الشبكة إلى AWS","تصحيح مهلات الاتصال لامبدا","تحقيق أنماط الفشل المحدد في عمليات نشر لامبدا-داخل-VPCs","تأتمتة التحقق من البنية التحتية قبل نشر رمز لامبدا-داخل-VPC"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires AWS CLI setup","Terraform configuration needed","Limited to AWS infrastructure"],"zh":["需要 AWS CLI 设置","需要 Terraform 配置","仅限于 AWS 基础设施"],"ja":["AWS CLI の設定が必要","Terraform の設定が必要","AWS インフラストラクチャのみに限定"],"ko":["AWS CLI 설정이 필요","Terraform 설정이 필요","AWS 인프라스트럭처에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere configuración de AWS CLI","Se necesita configuración de Terraform","Limitado a la infraestructura de AWS"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration AWS CLI","Une configuration Terraform est nécessaire","Limité à l''infrastructure AWS"],"de":["Benötigt AWS-CLI-Setup","Terraform-Konfiguration erforderlich","Begrenzt auf AWS-Infrastruktur"],"pt":["Requer configuração do AWS CLI","Configuração do Terraform necessária","Limitado à infraestrutura da AWS"],"ru":["Требуется настройка AWS CLI","Необходима конфигурация Terraform","Ограниченная инфраструктура AWS"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد AWS CLI","الإعداد مطلوب لشركة Terraform","محدود بالبنية التحتية لشركة AWS"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
