o","ru":"Завершение ветки разработки","ar":"إكمال فرع التطوير","en":"finishing-a-development-branch"},"description":{"zh":"完成开发分支技能是通过验证测试、呈现选项、执行选择和清理来指导开发工作的完成","ja":"開発ブランチの完了スキルは、テストの検証、オプションの提示、選択の実行、クリーンアップによって開発作業を完了するためのガイドです","ko":"개발 분기 완료 가이드는 테스트 검증, 옵션 제공, 선택 실행 및 정리 등을 통해 개발 작업을 완료하는 데 도움을 줍니다","es":"Nuestro enfoque para finalizar ramas de desarrollo implica la verificación de pruebas, la presentación de opciones y la ejecución de la elección, para garant...","fr":"Notre approche pour terminer les branches de développement implique la vérification des tests, la présentation des options et l''exécution du choix, pour gara...","de":"Unser Ansatz zum Abschließen von Entwicklungszweigen umfasst die Überprüfung von Tests, die Darstellung von Optionen und die Ausführung der Auswahl, um einen...","pt":"O skill finishing-a-development-branch ajuda a concluir o trabalho de desenvolvimento apresentando opções claras e manipulando workflows escolhidos.","ru":"Навык finishing-a-development-branch помогает завершить работу по разработке, представляя rõкие варианты и обрабатывая выбранные рабочие процессы.","ar":"مهارة finishing-a-development-branch تساعد على إكمال عمل التطوير من خلال تقديم خيارات واضحة ومعالجة سير العمل المحدد.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["验证测试","呈现选项","执行选择","清理","提高开发效率","简化工作流程"],"ja":["テストの検証","オプションの提示","選択の実行","クリーンアップ","開発効率の向上","ワークフローの簡素化"],"ko":["테스트 검증","옵션 제공","선택 실행","정리","개발 효율성 향상","작업 흐름 간소화"],"es":["Verificación de pruebas antes de presentar opciones","Presentación de opciones de flujo de trabajo","Ejecución de la elección del usuario","Limpieza de recursos después de la ejecución","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo populares"],"fr":["Vérification des tests avant de présenter des options","Présentation des options de flux de travail","Exécution du choix de l''utilisateur","Nettoyage des ressources après l''exécution","Intégration avec des outils de développement populaires"],"de":["Überprüfung von Tests vor der Darstellung von Optionen","Darstellung von Workflow-Optionen","Ausführung der Benutzerauswahl","Bereinigung von Ressourcen nach der Ausführung","Integration mit beliebten Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["Verificação de testes","Apresentação de opções","Execução de workflows","Limpeza de recursos","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Проверка тестов","Представление вариантов","Выполнение рабочих процессов","Очистка ресурсов","Интеграция с инструментами разработки"],"ar":["التحقق من الاختبارات","تقديم الخيارات","تشغيل سير العمل","تنظيف الموارد","التكامل مع أدوات التطوير"]},"keywords":{"zh":["完成开发分支","开发工作流程","验证测试","呈现选项","执行选择","清理","开发效率","工作流程简化"],"ja":["開発ブランチの完了","開発ワークフロー","テストの検証","オプションの提示","選択の実行","クリーンアップ","開発効率","ワークフローの簡素化"],"ko":["개발 분기 완료","개발 작업 흐름","테스트 검증","옵션 제공","선택 실행","정리","개발 효율성","작업 흐름 간소화"],"es":["finalizar ramas de desarrollo","verificación de pruebas","opciones de flujo de trabajo","desarrollo de software","eficiencia en el desarrollo","herramientas de desarrollo","integración de herramientas","pruebas automatizadas","desarrollo ágil"],"fr":["terminer les branches de développement","vérification des tests","options de flux de travail","développement de logiciels","efficacité dans le développement","outils de développement","intégration d''outils","tests automatisés","développement agile"],"de":["Entwicklungszweige abschließen","Überprüfung von Tests","Workflow-Optionen","Software-Entwicklung","Effizienz im Entwicklung","Entwicklungstools","Integration von Tools","automatisierte Tests","agiles Entwicklung"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de software","finalizar ramo de desenvolvimento","verificar testes","executar workflows","limpeza de recursos","integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["разработка программного обеспечения","завершение ветки разработки","проверка тестов","выполнение рабочих процессов","очистка ресурсов","интеграция с инструментами разработки"],"ar":["تطوير البرمجيات","إكمال فرع التطوير","التحقق من الاختبارات","تشغيل سير العمل","تنظيف الموارد","التكامل مع أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"mbcoalson","repo":"skills","repoPath":"mbcoalson/skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.407Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"finishing-a-development-branch","description":"Use when implementation is complete, all tests pass, and you need to decide how to integrate the work - guides completion of development work by presenting structured options for merge, PR, or cleanup","bodyPreview":"# Finishing a Development Branch\n\n## Overview\n\nGuide completion of development work by presenting clear options and handling chosen workflow.\n\n**Core principle:** Verify tests → Present options → Execute choice → Clean up.\n\n**Announce at start:** \"I''m using the finishing-a-development-branch skill to complete this work.\"\n\n## The Process\n\n### Step 1: Verify Tests\n\n**Before presenting options, verify tests pass:**\n\n```bash\n# Run project''s test suite\nnpm test / cargo test / pytest / go test ./...\n`","body":"# Finishing a Development Branch\n\n## Overview\n\nGuide completion of development work by presenting clear options and handling chosen workflow.\n\n**Core principle:** Verify tests → Present options → Execute choice → Clean up.\n\n**Announce at start:** \"I''m using the finishing-a-development-branch skill to complete this work.\"\n\n## The Process\n\n### Step 1: Verify Tests\n\n**Before presenting options, verify tests pass:**\n\n```bash\n# Run project''s test suite\nnpm test / cargo test / pytest / go test ./...\n```\n\n**If tests fail:**\n```\nTests failing (<N> failures). Must fix before completing:\n\n[Show failures]\n\nCannot proceed with merge/PR until tests pass.\n```\n\nStop. Don''t proceed to Step 2.\n\n**If tests pass:** Continue to Step 2.\n\n### Step 2: Determine Base Branch\n\n```bash\n# Try common base branches\ngit merge-base HEAD main 2>/dev/null || git merge-base HEAD master 2>/dev/null\n```\n\nOr ask: \"This branch split from main - is that correct?\"\n\n### Step 3: Present Options\n\nPresent exactly these 4 options:\n\n```\nImplementation complete. What would you like to do?\n\n1. Merge back to <base-branch> locally\n2. Push and create a Pull Request\n3. Keep the branch as-is (I''ll handle it later)\n4. Discard this work\n\nWhich option?\n```\n\n**Don''t add explanation** - keep options concise.\n\n### Step 4: Execute Choice\n\n#### Option 1: Merge Locally\n\n```bash\n# Switch to base branch\ngit checkout <base-branch>\n\n# Pull latest\ngit pull\n\n# Merge feature branch\ngit merge <feature-branch>\n\n# Verify tests on merged result\n<test command>\n\n# If tests pass\ngit branch -d <feature-branch>\n```\n\nThen: Cleanup worktree (Step 5)\n\n#### Option 2: Push and Create PR\n\n```bash\n# Push branch\ngit push -u origin <feature-branch>\n\n# Create PR\ngh pr create --title \"<title>\" --body \"$(cat <<''EOF''\n## Summary\n<2-3 bullets of what changed>\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] <verification steps>\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\nThen: Cleanup worktree (Step 5)\n\n#### Option 3: Keep As-Is\n\nReport: \"Keeping branch <name>. Worktree preserved at <path>.\"\n\n**Don''t cleanup worktree.**\n\n#### Option 4: Discard\n\n**Confirm first:**\n```\nThis will permanently delete:\n- Branch <name>\n- All commits: <commit-list>\n- Worktree at <path>\n\nType ''discard'' to confirm.\n```\n\nWait for exact confirmation.\n\nIf confirmed:\n```bash\ngit checkout <base-branch>\ngit branch -D <feature-branch>\n```\n\nThen: Cleanup worktree (Step 5)\n\n### Step 5: Cleanup Worktree\n\n**For Options 1, 2, 4:**\n\nCheck if in worktree:\n```bash\ngit worktree list | grep $(git branch --show-current)\n```\n\nIf yes:\n```bash\ngit worktree remove <worktree-path>\n```\n\n**For Option 3:** Keep worktree.\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Option | Merge | Push | Keep Worktree | Cleanup Branch |\n|--------|-------|------|---------------|----------------|\n| 1. Merge locally | ✓ | - | - | ✓ |\n| 2. Create PR | - | ✓ | ✓ | - |\n| 3. Keep as-is | - | - | ✓ | - |\n| 4. Discard | - | - | - | ✓ (force) |\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n**Skipping test verification**\n- **Problem:** Merge broken code, create failing PR\n- **Fix:** Always verify tests before offering options\n\n**Open-ended questions**\n- **Problem:** \"What should I do next?\" → ambiguous\n- **Fix:** Present exactly 4 structured options\n\n**Automatic worktree cleanup**\n- **Problem:** Remove worktree when might need it (Option 2, 3)\n- **Fix:** Only cleanup for Options 1 and 4\n\n**No confirmation for discard**\n- **Problem:** Accidentally delete work\n- **Fix:** Require typed \"discard\" confirmation\n\n## Red Flags\n\n**Never:**\n- Proceed with failing tests\n- Merge without verifying tests on result\n- Delete work without confirmation\n- Force-push without explicit request\n\n**Always:**\n- Verify tests before offering options\n- Present exactly 4 options\n- Get typed confirmation for Option 4\n- Clean up worktree for Options 1 & 4 only\n\n## Integration\n\n**Called by:**\n- **subagent-driven-development** (Step 7) - After all tasks complete\n- **executing-plans** (Step 5) - After all batches complete\n\n**Pairs with:**\n- **using-git-worktrees** - Cleans up worktree created by that skill\n\n\n## Saving Next Steps\n\nWhen finishing-a-development-branch work is complete or paused:\n\n```bash\nnode .claude/skills/work-command-center/tools/add-skill-next-steps.js \\\n  --skill \"finishing-a-development-branch\" \\\n  --content \"## Priority Tasks\n1. Complete final testing on feature branch\n2. Decide merge strategy (PR vs direct merge)\n3. Clean up development branch\"\n```\n\nSee: `.claude/skills/work-command-center/skill-next-steps-convention.md`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:26:33.898Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents requiring streamlined workflow management and test verification.","zh":"适用于需要简化工作流管理和测试验证的开发代理。","ja":"開発エージェントがストリームライン化されたワークフローの管理とテストの検証を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"개발 에이전트가 스트림 라인 된 워크 플로우 관리와 테스트 확인을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo que requieren una gestión de flujo de trabajo optimizada y verificación de pruebas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement nécessitant une gestion de workflow rationalisée et une vérification de tests.","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine optimierte Workflow-Verwaltung und Testverifizierung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de desenvolvimento que exigem gestão de fluxo de trabalho simplificada e verificação de teste.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, требующих упрощенного управления рабочим процессом и проверки тестов.","ar":"مثالية للوكلاء النموزجيين الذين يتطلبون إدارة تدفق العمل المبسطة وتأكيد الاختبار."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to execute chosen workflows after verifying tests pass using npm test, cargo test, pytest, or go test, ensuring a clean and reliable development process with protocols like bash.","zh":"使代理能够在使用npm test、cargo test、pytest或go test验证测试通过后执行所选工作流，确保使用bash等协议的干净可靠的开发过程。","ja":"エージェントがnpm test、cargo test、pytest、またはgo testを使用してテストを検証した後、選択したワークフローを実行できるようにし、bashなどのプロトコルを使用してクリーンで信頼性の高い開発プロセスを保証します。","ko":"에이전트가 npm 테스트, 카고 테스트, pytest 또는 고 테스트를 사용하여 테스트를 검증한 후 선택한 워크 플로우를 실행할 수 있도록 하여 bash와 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 깨끗하고 신뢰할 수 있는 개발 프로세스를 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a ejecutar flujos de trabajo elegidos después de verificar que las pruebas pasen usando npm test, cargo test, pytest o go test, asegurando un proceso de desarrollo limpio y confiable con protocolos como bash.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter les workflows choisis après avoir vérifié que les tests passent en utilisant npm test, cargo test, pytest ou go test, garantissant un processus de développement propre et fiable avec des protocoles comme bash.","de":"Ermächtigt die Mittel, ausgewählte Workflows nach Überprüfung der erfolgreichen Durchführung von Tests mit npm test, cargo test, pytest oder go test auszuführen, um so einen sauberen und zuverlässigen Entwicklungsprozess mit Protokollen wie bash sicherzustellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a executar fluxos de trabalho escolhidos após verificar se os testes passam usando npm test, cargo test, pytest ou go test, garantindo um processo de desenvolvimento limpo e confiável com protocolos como bash.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выполнять выбранные рабочие процессы после проверки успешного прохождения тестов с помощью npm test, cargo test, pytest или go test, обеспечивая чистый и надежный процесс разработки с использованием протоколов, таких как bash.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من تشغيل سلاسل العمل المختارة بعد التحقق من نجاح الاختبارات باستخدام npm test ، cargo test ، pytest أو go test ، مما يضمن عملية تطوير نظيفة وموثوقة باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل bash."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating development branch completion","Verifying test suites with npm test or cargo test","Executing workflow choices and handling cleanup"],"zh":["自动完成开发分支","使用npm test或cargo test验证测试套件","执行工作流选择并处理清理"],"ja":["開発ブランチの自動完了","npm testまたはcargo testを使用したテストスイートの検証","ワークフローの選択とクリーンアップの実行"],"ko":["개발 지점 자동 완성","npm 테스트 또는 카고 테스트를 사용한 테스트套件 확인","워크 플로우 선택 및 정리 처리"],"es":["Automatización de la finalización de la rama de desarrollo","Verificación de conjuntos de pruebas con npm test o cargo test","Ejecución de opciones de flujo de trabajo y manejo de limpieza"],"fr":["Automatisation de la finalisation de la branche de développement","Vérification des ensembles de tests avec npm test ou cargo test","Exécution des options de workflow et gestion de la suppression"],"de":["Automatisierung der Fertigstellung des Entwicklungszweigs","Verifizierung von Test-Suiten mit npm test oder cargo test","Ausführung von Workflow-Optionen und Bereinigung"],"pt":["Automatizar a conclusão da branch de desenvolvimento","Verificar conjuntos de testes com npm test ou cargo test","Executar escolhas de fluxo de trabalho e lidar com a limpeza"],"ru":["Автоматизация завершения ветки разработки","Проверка наборов тестов с помощью npm test или cargo test","Выполнение выбранных рабочих процессов и обработка очистки"],"ar":["تحسين إكمال فرع التطوير","التحقق من مجموعات الاختبار باستخدام npm test أو cargo test","تشغيل خيارات سلاسل العمل ومعالجة التنظيف"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires project test suite setup","Limited to bash-compatible environments"],"zh":["需要项目测试套件设置","仅限bash兼容环境"],"ja":["プロジェクトのテストスイートの設定が必要","bashと互換性のある環境に限定される"],"ko":["프로젝트 테스트套件 설정이 필요","bash와互換性 있는 환경에限定"],"es":["Requiere configuración del conjunto de pruebas del proyecto","Limitado a entornos compatibles con bash"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration du jeu de tests du projet","Limité aux environnements compatibles bash"],"de":["Erfordert die Einrichtung des Test-Suiten des Projekts","Begrenzt auf bash-kompatible Umgebungen"],"pt":["Exige configuração do conjunto de testes do projeto","Limitado a ambientes compatíveis com bash"],"ru":["Требует настройки набора тестов проекта","Ограничен средами, совместимыми с bash"],"ar":["يتطلب تهيئة مجموعة اختبار المشروع","محدود بالبيئات المتوافقة مع bash"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('avvale/aurora-back/aurora-tools-scripts', 'community', 'avvale', 'aurora-back', 'avvale/aurora-back', 'aurora-tools-scripts', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.407Z', '2026-02-18T03:27:01.255Z', NULL, '{"id":"avvale/aurora-back/aurora-tools-scripts","name":"aurora-tools-scripts","description":{"es":"La habilidad aurora-tools-scripts permite definir dónde poner el código para migraciones y procedimientos de base de datos","fr":"La compétence aurora-tools-scripts permet de définir où placer le code pour les migrations et les procédures de base de données","de":"Die Fähigkeit aurora-tools-scripts ermöglicht es, zu definieren, wo der Code für Migrationen und Datenbankprozeduren platziert werden soll","pt":"O skill aurora-tools-scripts define onde colocar o código para modificações de esquema de banco de dados, enquanto o skill postgresql define como escrever as instruções SQL.","ru":"Навык aurora-tools-scripts определяет, где размещать код для изменений схемы базы данных, а навык postgresql определяет, как писать инструкции SQL.","ar":"المهارة aurora-tools-scripts تحدد حيث وضع الكود لتعديلات مخطط قاعدة البيانات، بينما تحدد مهارة postgresql كيفية كتابة تعليمات SQL.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"es":"Herramientas de Aurora: Scripts y migraciones de base de ...","fr":"Outils Aurora : Scripts et migrations de base de données","de":"Aurora-Tools: Skripte und Datenbankmigrationen","pt":"Ferramentas Aurora: Scripts para Modificações de Esquema","ru":"Аурора-инструменты: Скрипты для изменений схемы","ar":"أدوات أورورا: سكريبتات لتعديلات مخطط قاعدة البيانات","en":"aurora-tools-scripts"},"description":{"es":"La habilidad aurora-tools-scripts permite definir dónde poner el código para migraciones y procedimientos de base de datos","fr":"La compétence aurora-tools-scripts permet de définir où placer le code pour les migrations et les procédures de base de données","de":"Die Fähigkeit aurora-tools-scripts ermöglicht es, zu definieren, wo der Code für Migrationen und Datenbankprozeduren platziert werden soll","pt":"O skill aurora-tools-scripts define onde colocar o código para modificações de esquema de banco de dados, enquanto o skill postgresql define como escrever as...","ru":"Навык aurora-tools-scripts определяет, где размещать код для изменений схемы базы данных, а навык postgresql определяет, как писать инструкции SQL.","ar":"المهارة aurora-tools-scripts تحدد حيث وضع الكود لتعديلات مخطط قاعدة البيانات، بينما تحدد مهارة postgresql كيفية كتابة تعليمات SQL.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"es":["Definir la ubicación del código para migraciones y procedimientos de base de datos","Gestionar scripts para modificaciones de esquema de base de datos","Crear y eliminar índices de base de datos","Agregar y eliminar columnas de tablas de base de datos"],"fr":["Définir l''emplacement du code pour les migrations et les procédures de base de données","Gérer les scripts pour les modifications de schéma de base de données","Créer et supprimer des index de base de données","Ajouter et supprimer des colonnes de tables de base de données"],"de":["Die Position des Codes für Migrationen und Datenbankprozeduren definieren","Skripte für Schema-Änderungen an Datenbanken verwalten","Datenbank-Indizes erstellen und löschen","Spalten in Datenbank-Tabellen hinzufügen und entfernen"],"pt":["Definição de local para código de modificações de esquema","Uso em conjunto com o skill postgresql","Suporte a modificações de tabela e índice","Criação e exclusão de índices","Modificações de colunas de tabela"],"ru":["Определение места для кода изменений схемы","Использование в паре с навыком postgresql","Поддержка изменений таблицы и индекса","Создание и удаление индексов","Изменения столбцов таблицы"],"ar":["تحديد موقع للكود لتعديلات مخطط","استخدامه مع مهارة postgresql","دعم تعديلات الجدول والفهرس","إنشاء وحذف الفهارس","تعديلات أعمدة الجدول"]},"keywords":{"es":["aurora tools scripts","migraciones de base de datos","procedimientos de base de datos","modificaciones de esquema de base de datos","gestión de scripts de base de datos","desarrollo de base de datos"],"fr":["outils aurora scripts","migrations de base de données","procédures de base de données","modifications de schéma de base de données","gestion de scripts de base de données","développement de base de données"],"de":["aurora tools skripte","datenbankmigrationen","datenbankprozeduren","schema-änderungen an datenbanken","skript-verwaltung für datenbanken","datenbank-entwicklung"],"pt":["ferramentas aurora","modificações de esquema","banco de dados","postgresql","skill aurora-tools-scripts","desenvolvimento de software","engenharia de dados"],"ru":["инструменты аурора","изменения схемы","база данных","postgresql","навык aurora-tools-scripts","разработка программного обеспечения","инженерия данных"],"ar":["أدوات أورورا","تعديلات مخطط","قاعدة البيانات","postgresql","مهارة aurora-tools-scripts","تطوير البرمجيات","هندسة البيانات"]}},"owner":"avvale","repo":"aurora-back","repoPath":"avvale/aurora-back","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.407Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"aurora-tools-scripts","description":">","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"## Required Companion Skill\n\n> **IMPORTANT**: Always use this skill together with `postgresql` skill.\n>\n> - This skill defines **WHERE** to put the code (migrations.ts vs procedures.ts)\n> - The `postgresql` skill defines **HOW** to write the SQL statements\n>\n> Read `.claude/skills/postgresql/SKILL.md` before writing any SQL.\n\n---\n\n## When to Use\n\n### migrations.ts - Schema Changes (DDL)\n\nUse for **database schema modifications**:\n\n- ALTER TABLE (add/drop/modify columns)\n- CREATE/DROP INDEX\n- Add","body":"## Required Companion Skill\n\n> **IMPORTANT**: Always use this skill together with `postgresql` skill.\n>\n> - This skill defines **WHERE** to put the code (migrations.ts vs procedures.ts)\n> - The `postgresql` skill defines **HOW** to write the SQL statements\n>\n> Read `.claude/skills/postgresql/SKILL.md` before writing any SQL.\n\n---\n\n## When to Use\n\n### migrations.ts - Schema Changes (DDL)\n\nUse for **database schema modifications**:\n\n- ALTER TABLE (add/drop/modify columns)\n- CREATE/DROP INDEX\n- Add constraints (UNIQUE, FOREIGN KEY, CHECK)\n- Add rowId pattern to existing tables\n- Any structural change to tables\n\n### procedures.ts - Programmable Objects\n\nUse for **stored logic and automation**:\n\n- Stored procedures (PROCEDURE)\n- Functions (FUNCTION)\n- Triggers (TRIGGER)\n- Sequences (via FUNCTION that creates them)\n\n---\n\n## Critical Patterns\n\n### File Structure\n\n| File                             | Purpose                                                     |\n| -------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/assets/tools/migrations.ts` | **Schema changes only**: ALTER TABLE, CREATE INDEX, DDL     |\n| `src/assets/tools/procedures.ts` | **Programmable objects**: procedures, functions, triggers   |\n| `src/@api/graphql.ts`            | Types and ToolsProcedureType enum                           |\n\n### Migration Object Structure\n\n```typescript\n{\n  id: ''UUID'',           // Generate with crypto.randomUUID()\n  name: string,         // English description: \"Verb + Object + Table\"\n  version: string,      // Semver matching package.json, e.g., ''0.0.7''\n  sort: number,         // Execution order within version\n  upScript: `SQL`,      // Pure PostgreSQL SQL in template literal\n  downScript: `SQL`,    // Exact inverse of upScript\n}\n```\n\n### Procedure Object Structure\n\n```typescript\n{\n  id: ''UUID'',\n  name: string,                    // Descriptive name\n  type: ToolsProcedureType,        // PROCEDURE | FUNCTION | TRIGGER\n  version: string,\n  sort: number,\n  upScript: `SQL`,                 // Pure SQL: CREATE OR REPLACE...\n  downScript: `SQL`,               // Pure SQL: DROP...\n}\n```\n\n### SQL Conventions\n\n| Rule                           | Example              |\n| ------------------------------ | -------------------- |\n| Table names use double quotes  | `\"TableName\"`        |\n| Always prefix with schema      | `public.\"TableName\"` |\n| Use IF EXISTS/IF NOT EXISTS    | Idempotent scripts   |\n| Environment vars interpolation | `${process.env.VAR}` |\n\n### Naming Conventions\n\n| Element    | Pattern                | Example                   |\n| ---------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| Functions  | `set_{entity}_{field}` | `set_load_order_code`     |\n| Triggers   | `trg_{function_name}`  | `trg_set_load_order_code` |\n| Sequences  | `{purpose}_seq`        | `load_order_code_seq`     |\n| Indexes    | `{table_snake}_{col}`  | `message_outbox_row_id`   |\n| Local vars | `v_` prefix            | `v_code`                  |\n| Counters   | `t_` prefix            | `t_counter`               |\n\n### Decision Tree\n\n```\nWhat do you need?\n│\n├─ Schema/Structure change (DDL)?\n│   └─ YES → migrations.ts\n│       ├─ ALTER TABLE (add/drop/modify columns)\n│       ├─ CREATE/DROP INDEX\n│       ├─ ADD CONSTRAINT\n│       └─ Any table structure change\n│\n└─ Programmable logic?\n    └─ YES → procedures.ts\n        ├─ Stored procedure (no return)     → type: PROCEDURE\n        ├─ Function (returns value/table)   → type: FUNCTION\n        ├─ Trigger + trigger function       → type: TRIGGER\n        └─ Sequence (created via function)  → type: FUNCTION\n```\n\n---\n\n## Code Examples\n\n### Migration: Add Column\n\n```typescript\n{\n  id: ''98978f96-b617-469f-b80c-2a30c5516f47'',\n  name: ''Add defaultRedirection to IamRole'',\n  version: ''0.0.6'',\n  sort: 8,\n  upScript: `\n    ALTER TABLE public.\"IamRole\" ADD COLUMN \"defaultRedirection\" VARCHAR(2046) NULL;\n  `,\n  downScript: `\n    ALTER TABLE public.\"IamRole\" DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS \"defaultRedirection\";\n  `,\n}\n```\n\n### Migration: Add rowId (Aurora Standard Pattern)\n\n```typescript\n{\n  id: ''bf177b46-6671-410b-bf49-4ce97c29884e'',\n  name: ''Add rowId to MessageOutbox'',\n  version: ''0.0.5'',\n  sort: 5,\n  upScript: `\n    ALTER TABLE public.\"MessageOutbox\" ADD COLUMN \"rowId\" BIGINT GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY;\n    WITH ordered AS (\n        SELECT id AS uuid_pk, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY \"createdAt\", id) AS rn FROM public.\"MessageOutbox\"\n    )\n    UPDATE public.\"MessageOutbox\" t\n        SET \"rowId\" = o.rn\n    FROM ordered o\n        WHERE t.id = o.uuid_pk\n            AND t.\"rowId\" IS NULL;\n\n    SELECT setval(pg_get_serial_sequence(''public.\"MessageOutbox\"'',''rowId''), (SELECT MAX(\"rowId\") FROM public.\"MessageOutbox\"), true);\n\n    ALTER TABLE public.\"MessageOutbox\" ALTER COLUMN \"rowId\" SET NOT NULL;\n    CREATE UNIQUE INDEX message_outbox_row_id ON public.\"MessageOutbox\" USING btree (\"rowId\");\n  `,\n  downScript: `\n    DROP INDEX IF EXISTS \"message_outbox_row_id\";\n    ALTER TABLE public.\"MessageOutbox\" DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS \"rowId\";\n  `,\n}\n```\n\n### Procedure: Basic\n\n```typescript\n{\n  id: ''1cd0c79e-b83b-4ebf-b112-063669703cdc'',\n  name: ''insert_user'',\n  type: ToolsProcedureType.PROCEDURE,\n  version: ''0.0.1'',\n  sort: 1,\n  upScript: `\nCREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE insert_user(name_input VARCHAR, age_input INTEGER)\nLANGUAGE plpgsql\nAS $$\nBEGIN\n    INSERT INTO users (name, age) VALUES (name_input, age_input);\nEND;\n$$;\n  `,\n  downScript: `DROP PROCEDURE IF EXISTS insert_user(VARCHAR, INTEGER);`,\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Commands\n\n```bash\n# Generate UUID for new entry\nuuidgen | tr ''[:upper:]'' ''[:lower:]''\n\n# Or in Node.js\nnode -e \"console.log(crypto.randomUUID())\"\n\n# Check current package version\njq -r ''.version'' package.json\n```\n\n---\n\n## Resources\n\n- **Templates**: See [assets/templates.ts](assets/templates.ts) for copy-paste\n  templates\n- **Migrations**: See `src/assets/tools/migrations.ts` for real examples\n- **Procedures**: See `src/assets/tools/procedures.ts` for procedure examples\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:27:01.255Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Database Management Agents requiring structured schema modifications and SQL statement management.","zh":"适用于需要结构化模式修改和SQL语句管理的数据库管理代理。","ja":"構造化スキーマの変更とSQLステートメントの管理が必要なデータベース管理エージェントに適しています。","ko":"구조화된 스키마 수정 및 SQL 문 관리가 필요한 데이터베이스 관리 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de administración de bases de datos que requieren modificaciones de esquema estructuradas y administración de instrucciones SQL.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de gestion de bases de données nécessitant des modifications de schéma structurées et une gestion d''instructions SQL.","de":"Ideal für Datenbankverwaltungsagenten, die strukturierte Schemamodifikationen und SQL-Anweisungsverwaltung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Gerenciamento de Banco de Dados que requerem modificações de esquema estruturadas e gerenciamento de instruções SQL.","ru":"Идеально для агентов управления базами данных, требующих структурированных изменений схемы и управления операторами SQL.","ar":"مثالي لعميل إدارة قواعد البيانات التي تتطلب تعديلات مخطط منظم و إدارة عبارات SQL."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage database schema changes through migrations.ts, defining where to put the code, while leveraging the postgresql skill for writing SQL statements, utilizing files like migrations.ts and procedures.ts.","zh":"赋予代理管理数据库模式更改的能力，通过migrations.ts定义代码放置位置，同时利用postgresql技能编写SQL语句，使用诸如migrations.ts和procedures.ts的文件。","ja":"エージェントがデータベーススキーマの変更を管理できるようにし、migrations.tsでコードを配置する場所を定義しながら、postgresqlスキルを利用してSQLステートメントを書き、migrations.tsやprocedures.tsのようなファイルを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 데이터베이스 스키마 변경을 관리할 수 있도록 하며, migrations.ts에서 코드를 배치할 위치를 정의하면서 postgresql 스킬을 활용하여 SQL 문을 작성하고, migrations.ts 및 procedures.ts와 같은 파일을 사용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar cambios en el esquema de la base de datos a través de migrations.ts, definiendo dónde poner el código, aprovechando al mismo tiempo la habilidad postgresql para escribir instrucciones SQL, utilizando archivos como migrations.ts y procedures.ts.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer les modifications du schéma de base de données via migrations.ts, en définissant où placer le code, tout en exploitant la compétence postgresql pour écrire des instructions SQL, en utilisant des fichiers tels que migrations.ts et procedures.ts.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Änderungen an der Datenbankschema über migrations.ts zu verwalten, indem sie definieren, wo der Code platziert werden soll, während sie gleichzeitig die postgresql-Fähigkeit für das Schreiben von SQL-Anweisungen nutzen, unter Verwendung von Dateien wie migrations.ts und procedures.ts.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar alterações no esquema do banco de dados por meio de migrations.ts, definindo onde colocar o código, aproveitando a habilidade postgresql para escrever instruções SQL, utilizando arquivos como migrations.ts e procedures.ts.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять изменениями схемы базы данных через migrations.ts, определяя, где размещать код, используя навык postgresql для написания операторов SQL, используя файлы, такие как migrations.ts и procedures.ts.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل khảية لإدارة تغييرات مخطط قاعدة البيانات من خلال migrations.ts، و تحديد مكان وضع الكود، و الاستفادة من مهارة postgresql لكتابة عبارات SQL، و استخدام الملفات مثل migrations.ts و procedures.ts."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating database schema modifications using migrations.ts","Generating SQL statements for database interactions","Managing database indexes and tables through ALTER TABLE and CREATE/DROP INDEX statements"],"zh":["使用migrations.ts自动执行数据库模式修改","生成用于数据库交互的SQL语句","通过ALTER TABLE和CREATE/DROP INDEX语句管理数据库索引和表"],"ja":["migrations.tsを使用してデータベーススキーマの変更を自動化する","データベースとのやりとりに使用するSQLステートメントを生成する","ALTER TABLEおよびCREATE/DROP INDEXステートメントを使用してデータベースのインデックスとテーブルを管理する"],"ko":["migrations.ts를 사용하여 데이터베이스 스키마 수정을 자동화합니다","데이터베이스 상호 작용을 위한 SQL 문을 생성합니다","ALTER TABLE 및 CREATE/DROP INDEX 문을 사용하여 데이터베이스 인덱스 및 테이블을 관리합니다"],"es":["Automatizar las modificaciones del esquema de base de datos utilizando migrations.ts","Generar instrucciones SQL para interacciones con la base de datos","Administrar índices y tablas de base de datos a través de instrucciones ALTER TABLE y CREATE/DROP INDEX"],"fr":["Automatiser les modifications du schéma de base de données à l''aide de migrations.ts","Générer des instructions SQL pour les interactions avec la base de données","Gérer les index et les tables de base de données via des instructions ALTER TABLE et CREATE/DROP INDEX"],"de":["Automatisieren von Datenbankschemamodifikationen mit Hilfe von migrations.ts","Generieren von SQL-Anweisungen für Datenbankinteraktionen","Verwalten von Datenbankindizes und -tabellen über ALTER TABLE- und CREATE/DROP INDEX-Anweisungen"],"pt":["Automatizar modificações de esquema de banco de dados usando migrations.ts","Gerar instruções SQL para interações de banco de dados","Gerenciar índices e tabelas de banco de dados por meio de instruções ALTER TABLE e CREATE/DROP INDEX"],"ru":["Автоматизировать изменения схемы базы данных с помощью migrations.ts","Генерировать операторы SQL для взаимодействия с базой данных","Управлять индексами и таблицами базы данных с помощью операторов ALTER TABLE и CREATE/DROP INDEX"],"ar":["أتمتة تعديلات مخطط قاعدة البيانات باستخدام migrations.ts","إنتاج عبارات SQL للتفاعلات مع قاعدة البيانات","إدارة فهارس و جداول قاعدة البيانات من خلال عبارات ALTER TABLE و CREATE/DROP INDEX"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires companion postgresql skill","Specific to PostgreSQL databases","Needs careful reading of .claude/skills/postgresql/SKILL.md for SQL writing guidelines"],"zh":["需要postgresql技能作为伴侣","仅适用于PostgreSQL数据库","需要仔细阅读.claude/skills/postgresql/SKILL.md以获取SQL编写指南"],"ja":["postgresqlスキルが必要な伴侶スキルです","PostgreSQLデータベースのみに対応しています","SQLの書き方に関するガイドラインを得るために、.claude/skills/postgresql/SKILL.mdを慎重に読む必要があります"],"ko":["postgresql 스킬이 필요한 동반 스킬입니다","PostgreSQL 데이터베이스만 지원합니다","SQL 작성 지침을 얻으려면 .claude/skills/postgresql/SKILL.md를 주의해서 읽어야 합니다"],"es":["Requiere la habilidad postgresql companion","Específico para bases de datos PostgreSQL","Necesita una lectura cuidadosa de .claude/skills/postgresql/SKILL.md para las pautas de escritura de SQL"],"fr":["Nécessite la compétence postgresql companion","Spécifique aux bases de données PostgreSQL","Nécessite une lecture attentive de .claude/skills/postgresql/SKILL.md pour les directives d''écriture de SQL"],"de":["Benötigt die postgresql-Begleitfähigkeit","Spezifisch für PostgreSQL-Datenbanken","Benötigt eine sorgfältige Lektüre von .claude/skills/postgresql/SKILL.md für die SQL-Schreibanleitungen"],"pt":["Exige habilidade postgresql companion","Específico para bancos de dados PostgreSQL","Necessita leitura cuidadosa de .claude/skills/postgresql/SKILL.md para diretrizes de escrita de SQL"],"ru":["Требует компаньонского навыка postgresql","Специфичен для баз данных PostgreSQL","Требует тщательного чтения .claude/skills/postgresql/SKILL.md для рекомендаций по написанию SQL"],"ar":["يتطلب مهارة postgresql مرافقة","محدد لقواعد البيانات PostgreSQL","يحتاج إلى قراءة متأنية من .claude/skills/postgresql/SKILL.md لإرشادات كتابة SQL"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('lucidlabs-hq/agent-kit/design-system-guard', 'community', 'lucidlabs-hq', 'agent-kit', 'lucidlabs-hq/agent-kit', 'design-system-guard', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.407Z', '2026-02-18T03:26:09.447Z', NULL, '{"id":"lucidlabs-hq/agent-kit/design-system-guard","name":"design-system-guard","description":{"zh":"Design System Guard - AI, Next.js, Mastra, Convex, n8n","ja":"Design System Guard - AI, Next.js, Mastra, Convex, n8n","ko":"Design System Guard - AI, Next.js, Mastra, Convex, n8n","es":"El Design System Guard es un kit de inicio para aplicaciones AI que proporciona una validación estricta de diseño y UX. Está construido con Next.js, Mastra, Convex y n8n","fr":"Design System Guard est un kit de démarrage pour applications IA qui offre une validation stricte de conception et UX. Il est construit avec Next.js, Mastra, Convex et n8n","de":"Design System Guard ist ein Starter-Kit für KI-Anwendungen, der eine strenge Validierung von Design und UX bietet. Es ist mit Next.js, Mastra, Convex und n8n erstellt","pt":"O Design System Guard é um kit de início para aplicações AI que valida a conformidade com as regras do sistema de design da Lucid Labs.","ru":"Design System Guard — стартовый комплект для AI-приложений, который проверяет соответствие правилам системы дизайна Lucid Labs.","ar":"ديزاين سيستيم جارد هو كيت إطلاق للتقويمات الذكية التي تدقق في مطابقة قواعد نظام التصميم في مختبرات لوسيد.","en":"AI Agent Starter Kit - Production-ready boilerplate for AI-powered applications with Next.js, Mastra, Convex, and n8n"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Design System Guard - AI ","ja":"Design System Guard - AI","ko":"Design System Guard - AI","es":"Design System Guard: Kit de inicio para aplicaciones AI","fr":"Design System Guard : Kit de démarrage pour applications IA","de":"Design System Guard: Starter-Kit für KI-Anwendungen","pt":"Design System Guard: Kit de Início para Aplicativos AI","ru":"Design System Guard: Стартовый комплект для AI-приложений","ar":"ديزاين سيستيم جارد: كيت إطلاق للتقويمات الذكية","en":"design-system-guard"},"description":{"zh":"Design System Guard - AI, Next.js, Mastra, Convex, n8n","ja":"Design System Guard - AI, Next.js, Mastra, Convex, n8n","ko":"Design System Guard - AI, Next.js, Mastra, Convex, n8n","es":"El Design System Guard es un kit de inicio para aplicaciones AI que proporciona una validación estricta de diseño y UX. Está construido con Next.js, Mastra, ...","fr":"Design System Guard est un kit de démarrage pour applications IA qui offre une validation stricte de conception et UX. Il est construit avec Next.js, Mastra,...","de":"Design System Guard ist ein Starter-Kit für KI-Anwendungen, der eine strenge Validierung von Design und UX bietet. Es ist mit Next.js, Mastra, Convex und n8n...","pt":"O Design System Guard é um kit de início para aplicações AI que valida a conformidade com as regras do sistema de design da Lucid Labs.","ru":"Design System Guard — стартовый комплект для AI-приложений, который проверяет соответствие правилам системы дизайна Lucid Labs.","ar":"ديزاين سيستيم جارد هو كيت إطلاق للتقويمات الذكية التي تدقق في مطابقة قواعد نظام التصميم في مختبرات لوسيد.","en":"AI Agent Starter Kit - Production-ready boilerplate for AI-powered applications with Next.js, Mastra, Convex, and n8n"},"definition":{"en":"AI Agent Starter Kit - Production-ready boilerplate for AI-powered applications with Next.js, Mastra, Convex, and n8n"},"features":{"zh":["AI","Next.js","Mastra","Convex","n8n","Design System"],"ja":["AI","Next.js","Mastra","Convex","n8n","Design System"],"ko":["AI","Next.js","Mastra","Convex","n8n","Design System"],"es":["Kit de inicio para aplicaciones AI","Validación estricta de diseño y UX","Construido con Next.js, Mastra, Convex y n8n","Compatible con aplicaciones web y móviles","Fácil de integrar y personalizar"],"fr":["Kit de démarrage pour applications IA","Validation stricte de conception et UX","Construit avec Next.js, Mastra, Convex et n8n","Compatible avec les applications web et mobiles","Facile à intégrer et personnaliser"],"de":["Starter-Kit für KI-Anwendungen","Strenge Validierung von Design und UX","Erstellt mit Next.js, Mastra, Convex und n8n","Kompatibel mit Web- und Mobilanwendungen","Einfach zu integrieren und anzupassen"],"pt":["Kit de início para aplicações AI","Integração com Next.js, Mastra, Convex e n8n","Validação de conformidade com as regras do sistema de design da Lucid Labs","Análise de telas para detecção de erros","Relatórios detalhados de erros e sugestões de melhoria"],"ru":["Стартовый комплект для AI-приложений","Интеграция с Next.js, Mastra, Convex и n8n","Проверка соответствия правилам системы дизайна Lucid Labs","Анализ экранов для обнаружения ошибок","Детальные отчеты об ошибках и建议ениях по улучшению"],"ar":["كيت إطلاق للتقويمات الذكية","التكامل مع Next.js، Mastra، Convex و n8n","تدقيق مطابقة الشاشات لقواعد نظام التصميم في مختبرات لوسيد","تحليل الشاشات لاكتشاف الأخطاء","تقارير مفصلة عن الأخطاء وتوصيات التحسين"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Design System Guard","AI","Next.js","Mastra","Convex","n8n","Design System","AI","Validation"],"ja":["Design System Guard","AI","Next.js","Mastra","Convex","n8n","Design System","AI","Validation"],"ko":["Design System Guard","AI","Next.js","Mastra","Convex","n8n","Design System","AI","Validation"],"es":["design system guard","kit de inicio para aplicaciones ai","validación de diseño y ux","next.js","mastra","convex","n8n","desarrollo de aplicaciones ai"],"fr":["design system guard","kit de démarrage pour applications ia","validation de conception et ux","next.js","mastra","convex","n8n","développement d''applications ia"],"de":["design system guard","starter-kit für ki-anwendungen","validierung von design und ux","next.js","mastra","convex","n8n","entwicklung von ki-anwendungen"],"pt":["Design System Guard","Kit de início para aplicações AI","Next.js","Mastra","Convex","n8n","Sistema de design da Lucid Labs","Validação de conformidade","Análise de telas"],"ru":["Design System Guard","Стартовый комплект для AI-приложений","Next.js","Mastra","Convex","n8n","Система дизайна Lucid Labs","Проверка соответствия","Анализ экранов"],"ar":["ديزاين سيستيم جارد","كيت إطلاق للتقويمات الذكية","Next.js","Mastra","Convex","n8n","نظام التصميم في مختبرات لوسيد","تدقيق مطابقة","تحليل الشاشات"]}},"owner":"lucidlabs-hq","repo":"agent-kit","repoPath":"lucidlabs-hq/agent-kit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.407Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"design-system-guard","description":"Validate UI screens against Lucid Labs design system rules. Use after implementing UI components to verify adherence to brand colors, typography, layout patterns, and service board logic.","bodyPreview":"# Design System Guard\n\nYou are a **Lucid Labs Design & UX Validator Agent**.\n\nYour task is **not to redesign**, **not to optimize creatively**, and **not to guess intent**.\n\nYour sole responsibility is to **validate** whether a given screen follows the **Lucid Labs design system rules**.\n\nYou must be **strict, explicit, and rule-based**.\n\nIf something is unclear, assume it is **incorrect** and flag it.\n\n---\n\n## INPUT YOU RECEIVE\n\nYou will receive one or more of the following:\n\n* Screenshots of a","body":"# Design System Guard\n\nYou are a **Lucid Labs Design & UX Validator Agent**.\n\nYour task is **not to redesign**, **not to optimize creatively**, and **not to guess intent**.\n\nYour sole responsibility is to **validate** whether a given screen follows the **Lucid Labs design system rules**.\n\nYou must be **strict, explicit, and rule-based**.\n\nIf something is unclear, assume it is **incorrect** and flag it.\n\n---\n\n## INPUT YOU RECEIVE\n\nYou will receive one or more of the following:\n\n* Screenshots of a UI\n* File paths to components\n* ASCII layouts\n* Short textual descriptions of a screen\n\nWhen given file paths, read the component code to understand the UI structure.\n\n---\n\n## VALIDATION SCOPE\n\nValidate the screen against **all** of the following dimensions:\n\n---\n\n## 1. BRAND & COLOR RULES\n\n### Must be true\n\n* Indigo/purple tones (`indigo-500`, `indigo-600`) are the dominant accent colors\n* White (`bg-white`) is used for content cards\n* Off-white/light gray (`bg-[#F7F8FA]`, `bg-slate-50`) for section backgrounds\n* Slate tones for text hierarchy (`text-slate-900`, `text-slate-700`, `text-slate-500`)\n\n### Must NOT be true\n\n* No dark mode as default (bg-slate-800, bg-slate-900 for main panels)\n* No black backgrounds\n* No semantic colors for status (red/green/yellow) - use indigo intensity instead\n* No shadows on cards (use borders only)\n\n### Output\n\n* PASS / FAIL\n* Short explanation\n\n---\n\n## 2. TYPOGRAPHY ROLES\n\n### Must be true\n\n* Section titles: `text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900`\n* Labels: `text-sm font-medium text-slate-700`\n* Meta/muted: `text-xs text-slate-500`\n* Uppercase tracking for category labels: `text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500`\n\n### Must NOT be true\n\n* No mixed font weights without purpose\n* No excessive font sizes (max `text-xl` for page titles)\n\n### Output\n\n* PASS / FAIL\n* What typography is wrong if failing\n\n---\n\n## 3. LAYOUT PATTERNS\n\n### Must be true\n\n* Generous spacing (`p-6`, `gap-4`, `mb-6`)\n* Border-based separation (`border border-slate-200`)\n* Rounded corners (`rounded-lg`, `rounded-md`)\n* Empty states have dashed borders (`border-dashed border-slate-300`)\n\n### Must NOT be true\n\n* No tight spacing (p-2, gap-1 for main sections)\n* No heavy visual dividers\n* No card shadows\n\n### Output\n\n* PASS / FAIL\n* Which elements violate layout rules\n\n---\n\n## 4. INTERACTIVE ELEMENTS\n\n### Must be true\n\n* All clickable elements have `cursor-pointer`\n* Buttons use indigo as primary color\n* Secondary buttons have borders, not fills\n* Hover states are subtle (slate-50, slate-100)\n\n### Must NOT be true\n\n* No aggressive hover effects\n* No multiple primary actions competing\n\n### Output\n\n* PASS / FAIL\n* Specific violation if present\n\n---\n\n## 5. STATUS & CONFIDENCE DISPLAY\n\n### Must be true\n\n* Confidence uses IntensityBar (1-5 scale, indigo gradient)\n* Status badges use neutral colors (slate, indigo)\n* Processing states use `Loader2` with `animate-spin`\n\n### Must NOT be true\n\n* No traffic light colors (red/green/yellow badges)\n* No progress bars for confidence\n* No percentage badges\n\n### Output\n\n* PASS / FAIL\n* Explain mismatch if failing\n\n---\n\n## 6. EMPTY STATES\n\n### Must be true\n\n* Centered content\n* Muted icon (`text-slate-300`)\n* Short, helpful text\n* Dashed border container\n\n### Must NOT be true\n\n* No empty states without visual indicator\n* No error-styled empty states\n\n### Output\n\n* PASS / FAIL\n* Missing empty state handling if failing\n\n---\n\n## 7. CALMNESS & READABILITY\n\n### Must be true\n\n* The screen feels calm and structured\n* Visual noise is low\n* No unnecessary borders, lines, or decorations\n* Content is scannable\n\n### Must NOT be true\n\n* No dashboard clutter\n* No dense tables without purpose\n* No aggressive visual density\n\n### Output\n\n* PASS / FAIL\n* What causes overload if failing\n\n---\n\n## REQUIRED FINAL OUTPUT FORMAT\n\nAlways respond in this structure:\n\n```\nLucid Labs Design System Validation\n\n1. Brand & Color: PASS / FAIL\n   - Reason\n\n2. Typography Roles: PASS / FAIL\n   - Reason\n\n3. Layout Patterns: PASS / FAIL\n   - Reason\n\n4. Interactive Elements: PASS / FAIL\n   - Reason\n\n5. Status & Confidence: PASS / FAIL\n   - Reason\n\n6. Empty States: PASS / FAIL\n   - Reason\n\n7. Calmness & Readability: PASS / FAIL\n   - Reason\n\nOverall Verdict:\n- APPROVED\n- APPROVED WITH ISSUES\n- REJECTED\n\nCritical Violations (if any):\n- Bullet list\n\nSuggested Fixes:\n- Bullet list (only if REJECTED or APPROVED WITH ISSUES)\n```\n\n---\n\n## IMPORTANT CONSTRAINTS\n\n* Do **not** suggest redesigns unless asked\n* Do **not** invent intent\n* Do **not** optimize copy\n* Validate **only** against design system rules\n* Be specific about which Tailwind classes are wrong\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:26:09.447Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for UX Validator Agents needing strict design system rule enforcement in Next.js applications","zh":"非常适合需要在 Next.js 应用程序中严格执行设计系统规则的 UX Validator Agents","ja":"Next.js アプリケーションで厳格なデザインシステムルールの適用が必要な UX Validator エージェントに最適","ko":"Next.js 애플리케이션에서 엄격한 디자인 시스템 규칙 적용이 필요한 UX Validator 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes validadores de UX que necesitan una aplicación estricta de las reglas del sistema de diseño en aplicaciones Next.js","fr":"Parfait pour les agents validateurs d''UX nécessitant une application stricte des règles du système de conception dans les applications Next.js","de":"Perfekt für UX-Validator-Agents, die eine strikte Durchsetzung der Design-System-Regeln in Next.js-Anwendungen benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Validadores de UX que necessitam de aplicação estrita de regras de sistema de design em aplicações Next.js","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов-валидаторов UX, которым требуется严格ое соблюдение правил системы дизайна в приложениях Next.js","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المحققين لتحقق UX الذين يحتاجون إلى تنفيذ قواعد نظام التصميم بشكل صارم في تطبيقات Next.js"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to validate screens against Lucid Labs design system rules using explicit and rule-based checks, ensuring consistency with Mastra, Convex, and n8n integrations","zh":"赋予代理人使用明确和基于规则的检查来验证屏幕是否符合 Lucid Labs 设计系统规则，确保与 Mastra、Convex 和 n8n 集成的一致性","ja":"エージェントに明示的およびルールベースのチェックを使用して、スクリーンが Lucid Labs デザインシステムルールに準拠していることを検証する権限を与え、Mastra、Convex、n8n 統合との一致性を確保する","ko":"에이전트에게 명시적이고 규칙 기반 체크를 사용하여 화면이 Lucid Labs 디자인 시스템 규칙에 준수하는지 검증할 수 있는 권한을 부여하여 Mastra, Convex 및 n8n 통합과 일관성을 보장","es":"Habilita a los agentes a validar pantallas contra las reglas del sistema de diseño de Lucid Labs utilizando comprobaciones explícitas y basadas en reglas, garantizando la consistencia con las integraciones de Mastra, Convex y n8n","fr":"Habilite les agents à valider les écrans contre les règles du système de conception de Lucid Labs en utilisant des vérifications explicites et basées sur des règles, garantissant la cohérence avec les intégrations de Mastra, Convex et n8n","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Bildschirme gegen die Regeln des Design-Systems von Lucid Labs zu validieren, indem explizite und regelbasierte Überprüfungen verwendet werden, um die Konsistenz mit den Integrationen von Mastra, Convex und n8n sicherzustellen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a validar telas contra as regras do sistema de design da Lucid Labs usando verificações explícitas e baseadas em regras, garantindo a consistência com as integrações Mastra, Convex e n8n","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проверять экраны на соответствие правилам системы дизайна Lucid Labs с помощью явных и основанных на правилах проверок, обеспечивая согласованность с интеграциями Mastra, Convex и n8n","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على التحقق من الشاشات ضد قواعد نظام التصميم في مختبرات لوكيد باستخدام عمليات التحقق الصريحة والقائمة على القواعد، وضمان الاتساق مع التكاملات Mastra و Convex و n8n"},"useCases":{"en":["Validating design system compliance in Next.js projects","Flagging incorrect design elements in screenshots","Enforcing strict design rules for AI-powered applications"],"zh":["验证 Next.js 项目的设计系统合规性","标记屏幕截图中的不正确设计元素","为 AI 驱动的应用程序施加严格的设计规则"],"ja":["Next.js プロジェクトのデザインシステムの準拠を検証する","スクリーンショットの不正なデザイン要素をフラグする","AI ドライブのアプリケーションに厳格なデザインルールを適用する"],"ko":["Next.js 프로젝트의 디자인 시스템 규칙 준수를 검증","스크린샷의 잘못된 디자인 요소를 플래그","AI 구동 애플리케이션에 엄격한 디자인 규칙을 적용"],"es":["Validar la conformidad del sistema de diseño en proyectos Next.js","Marcar elementos de diseño incorrectos en capturas de pantalla","Aplicar reglas de diseño estrictas para aplicaciones impulsadas por IA"],"fr":["Valider la conformité du système de conception dans les projets Next.js","Marquer les éléments de conception incorrects dans les captures d''écran","Appliquer des règles de conception strictes pour les applications alimentées par l''IA"],"de":["Überprüfen der Konformität des Design-Systems in Next.js-Projekten","Markieren von fehlerhaften Design-Elementen in Screenshots","Durchsetzen strenger Design-Regeln für künstlich intelligente Anwendungen"],"pt":["Validar a conformidade do sistema de design em projetos Next.js","Sinalizar elementos de design incorretos em capturas de tela","Aplicar regras de design estritas para aplicações impulsionadas por IA"],"ru":["Проверка соответствия системы дизайна в проектах Next.js","Помечание неправильных элементов дизайна на скриншотах","Применение строгих правил дизайна для приложений, работающих на ИИ"],"ar":["التحقق من مطابقة نظام التصميم في مشاريع Next.js","تأشير عناصر التصميم غير الصحيحة في لقطات الشاشة","تنفيذ قواعد التصميم الصارمة للتطبيقات التي تعمل بالذكاء الاصطناعي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Lucid Labs design system rules to be well-defined","Limited to validating existing designs, not redesigning or optimizing creatively"],"zh":["需要 Lucid Labs 设计系统规则明确定义","仅限验证现有设计，不创造性地重新设计或优化"],"ja":["Lucid Labs デザインシステムルールが明確に定義されている必要がある","既存のデザインの検証のみに限定され、創造的に再設計または最適化することはできない"],"ko":["Lucid Labs 디자인 시스템 규칙이 명확하게 정의되어야 함","既存 디자인의 검증만 가능하며, 창의적으로 다시 설계하거나 최적화할 수 없음"],"es":["Requiere que las reglas del sistema de diseño de Lucid Labs estén bien definidas","Limitado a la validación de diseños existentes, no a la recreación o optimización creativa"],"fr":["Nécessite que les règles du système de conception de Lucid Labs soient bien définies","Limité à la validation des conceptions existantes, et non à la recreation ou à l''optimisation créative"],"de":["Erfordert, dass die Regeln des Design-Systems von Lucid Labs gut definiert sind","Begrenzt auf die Validierung bestehender Designs, nicht auf das kreative Neu- oder Optimierungsdesign"],"pt":["Exige que as regras do sistema de design da Lucid Labs estejam bem definidas","Limitado à validação de designs existentes, não redesenho ou otimização criativa"],"ru":["Требует, чтобы правила системы дизайна Lucid Labs были хорошо определены","Ограничен проверкой существующих дизайнов, не переработкой или творческой оптимизацией"],"ar":["يتطلب أن تكون قواعد نظام التصميم في مختبرات لوكيد محددة جيدًا","محدود بالتحقق من التصاميم الحالية، وليس إعادة التصميم أو التحسين الإبداعي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
