ones y herramientas para el desarrollo de software","Compatibilidad con Claude para una implementación sencilla","Documentación clara y concisa para una rápida evaluación","Ejemplos prácticos para una aplicación efectiva"],"fr":["Guides de référence pour des techniques éprouvées","Modèles et outils pour le développement de logiciels","Compatibilité avec Claude pour une mise en œuvre simple","Documentation claire et concise pour une évaluation rapide","Exemples pratiques pour une application efficace"],"de":["Referenzleitfäden für bewährte Techniken","Muster und Tools für die Softwareentwicklung","Kompatibilität mit Claude für eine einfache Implementierung","Klare und knappe Dokumentation für eine schnelle Bewertung","Praktische Beispiele für eine effektive Anwendung"],"pt":["Guias de referência para técnicas de codificação comprovadas","Ferramentas de codificação de IA descobríveis e avaliáveis","Exemplos claros e aplicáveis","Princípio central: assumir que o Claude já é muito inteligente","Adicionar contexto que o Claude não tem","Técnicas e padrões de codificação eficazes"],"ru":["Справочные руководства для проверенных техник кодирования","Инструменты кодирования ИИ, обнаруживаемые и оцениваемые","Ясные и применимые примеры","Центральный принцип: предполагать, что Claude уже очень умён","Добавление контекста, которого нет у Claude","Эффективные техники и шаблоны кодирования"],"ar":["دلائل مرجعية للتقنيات البرمجية المثبتة","أدوات برمجة الذكاء الاصطناعي التي يمكن اكتشافها وتقييمها","أمثلة واضحة وقابلة للتطبيق","مبدأ مركزي: افتراض أن الكلود ذكي جدا","إضافة سياق لا تمتلكه الكلود","تقنيات وطرق برمجة فعالة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI 编码工具","创建技能","可发现的技能","可扫描的技能","可执行的技能","快速应用有效的 AI 编码技术"],"ja":["AI コーディングツール","スキルの作成","発見可能なスキル","スキャナブルなスキル","実行可能なスキル","有効な AI コーディング技術の迅速な適用"],"ko":["AI 코딩 도구","스킬 생성","발견 가능한 스킬","스캔 가능한 스킬","실행 가능한 스킬","효과적인 AI 코딩 기술의迅速한 적용"],"es":["creación de habilidades","desarrollo de software","herramientas de codificación AI","técnicas comprobadas","patrones de desarrollo","Claude","guías de referencia","documentación técnica","desarrollo de aplicaciones"],"fr":["création de compétences","développement de logiciels","outils de codage AI","techniques éprouvées","modèles de développement","Claude","guides de référence","documentation technique","développement d''applications"],"de":["Erstellung von Fähigkeiten","Softwareentwicklung","AI-Coding-Tools","bewährte Techniken","Entwicklungs-muster","Claude","Referenzleitfäden","technische Dokumentation","Anwendungs-entwicklung"],"pt":["habilidades de codificação","codificação de IA","ferramentas de codificação","guias de referência","técnicas de codificação","padrões de codificação","desenvolvimento de IA","aprendizado de máquina","processamento de linguagem natural"],"ru":["навыки кодирования","кодирование ИИ","инструменты кодирования","справочные руководства","техники кодирования","шаблоны кодирования","разработка ИИ","обучение машин","обработка естественного языка"],"ar":["مهارات الكود","برمجة الذكاء الاصطناعي","أدوات البرمجة","دلائل مرجعية","تقنيات البرمجة","طرق البرمجة","تطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي","تعلم الآلة","معالجة اللغة الطبيعية"]}},"owner":"pr-pm","repo":"prpm","repoPath":"pr-pm/prpm","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.408Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"creating-skills","description":"Use when creating new Claude Code skills or improving existing ones - ensures skills are discoverable, scannable, and effective through proper structure, CSO optimization, and real examples","bodyPreview":"# Creating Skills\n\n## Overview\n\n**Skills are reference guides for proven techniques, patterns, or tools.** Write them to help future Claude instances quickly find and apply effective approaches.\n\nSkills must be **discoverable** (Claude can find them), **scannable** (quick to evaluate), and **actionable** (clear examples).\n\n**Core principle**: Default assumption is Claude is already very smart. Only add context Claude doesn''t already have.\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Create a skill when:**\n- Technique was","body":"# Creating Skills\n\n## Overview\n\n**Skills are reference guides for proven techniques, patterns, or tools.** Write them to help future Claude instances quickly find and apply effective approaches.\n\nSkills must be **discoverable** (Claude can find them), **scannable** (quick to evaluate), and **actionable** (clear examples).\n\n**Core principle**: Default assumption is Claude is already very smart. Only add context Claude doesn''t already have.\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Create a skill when:**\n- Technique wasn''t intuitively obvious\n- Pattern applies broadly across projects\n- You''d reference this again\n- Others would benefit\n\n**Don''t create for:**\n- One-off solutions specific to single project\n- Standard practices well-documented elsewhere\n- Project conventions (put those in `.claude/CLAUDE.md`)\n\n## Required Structure\n\n### Frontmatter (YAML)\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: skill-name-with-hyphens\ndescription: Use when [triggers/symptoms] - [what it does and how it helps]\ntags: relevant-tags\n---\n```\n\n**Rules:**\n- Only `name` and `description` fields supported (max 1024 chars total)\n- Name: letters, numbers, hyphens only (max 64 chars). Use gerund form (verb + -ing)\n- Avoid reserved words: \"anthropic\", \"claude\" in names\n- Description: Third person, starts with \"Use when...\" (max 1024 chars)\n- Include BOTH triggering conditions AND what skill does\n- Match specificity to task complexity (degrees of freedom)\n\n### Document Structure\n\n```markdown\n# Skill Name\n\n## Overview\nCore principle in 1-2 sentences. What is this?\n\n## When to Use\n- Bullet list with symptoms and use cases\n- When NOT to use\n\n## Quick Reference\nTable or bullets for common operations\n\n## Implementation\nInline code for simple patterns\nLink to separate file for heavy reference (100+ lines)\n\n## Common Mistakes\nWhat goes wrong + how to fix\n\n## Real-World Impact (optional)\nConcrete results from using this technique\n```\n\n## Degrees of Freedom\n\n**Match specificity to task complexity:**\n\n- **High freedom**: Flexible tasks requiring judgment\n  - Use broad guidance, principles, examples\n  - Let Claude adapt approach to context\n  - Example: \"Use when designing APIs - provides REST principles and patterns\"\n\n- **Low freedom**: Fragile or critical operations\n  - Be explicit about exact steps\n  - Include validation checks\n  - Example: \"Use when deploying to production - follow exact deployment checklist with rollback procedures\"\n\n**Red flag**: If skill tries to constrain Claude too much on creative tasks, reduce specificity. If skill is too vague on critical operations, add explicit steps.\n\n## Claude Search Optimization (CSO)\n\n**Critical:** Future Claude reads the description to decide if skill is relevant. Optimize for discovery.\n\n### Description Best Practices\n\n```yaml\n# ❌ BAD - Too vague, doesn''t mention when to use\ndescription: For async testing\n\n# ❌ BAD - First person (injected into system prompt)\ndescription: I help you with flaky tests\n\n# ✅ GOOD - Triggers + what it does\ndescription: Use when tests have race conditions or pass/fail inconsistently - replaces arbitrary timeouts with condition polling for reliable async tests\n\n# ✅ GOOD - Technology-specific with explicit trigger\ndescription: Use when using React Router and handling auth redirects - provides patterns for protected routes and auth state management\n```\n\n### Keyword Coverage\n\nUse words Claude would search for:\n- **Error messages**: \"ENOENT\", \"Cannot read property\", \"Timeout\"\n- **Symptoms**: \"flaky\", \"hanging\", \"race condition\", \"memory leak\"\n- **Synonyms**: \"cleanup/teardown/afterEach\", \"timeout/hang/freeze\"\n- **Tools**: Actual command names, library names, file types\n\n### Naming Conventions\n\n**Use gerund form (verb + -ing):**\n- ✅ `creating-skills` not `skill-creation`\n- ✅ `testing-with-subagents` not `subagent-testing`\n- ✅ `debugging-memory-leaks` not `memory-leak-debugging`\n- ✅ `processing-pdfs` not `pdf-processor`\n- ✅ `analyzing-spreadsheets` not `spreadsheet-analysis`\n\n**Why gerunds work:**\n- Describes the action you''re taking\n- Active and clear\n- Consistent with Anthropic conventions\n\n**Avoid:**\n- ❌ Vague names like \"Helper\" or \"Utils\"\n- ❌ Passive voice constructions\n\n## Code Examples\n\n**One excellent example beats many mediocre ones.**\n\n### Choose Language by Use Case\n\n- Testing techniques → TypeScript/JavaScript\n- System debugging → Shell/Python\n- Data processing → Python\n- API calls → TypeScript/JavaScript\n\n### Good Example Checklist\n\n- [ ] Complete and runnable\n- [ ] Well-commented explaining **WHY** not just what\n- [ ] From real scenario (not contrived)\n- [ ] Shows pattern clearly\n- [ ] Ready to adapt (not generic template)\n- [ ] Shows both BAD (❌) and GOOD (✅) approaches\n- [ ] Includes realistic context/setup code\n\n### Example Template\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ GOOD - Clear, complete, ready to adapt\ninterface RetryOptions {\n  maxAttempts: number;\n  delayMs: number;\n  backoff?: ''linear'' | ''exponential'';\n}\n\nasync function retryOperation<T>(\n  operation: () => Promise<T>,\n  options: RetryOptions\n): Promise<T> {\n  const { maxAttempts, delayMs, backoff = ''linear'' } = options;\n\n  for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= maxAttempts; attempt++) {\n    try {\n      return await operation();\n    } catch (error) {\n      if (attempt === maxAttempts) throw error;\n\n      const delay = backoff === ''exponential''\n        ? delayMs * Math.pow(2, attempt - 1)\n        : delayMs * attempt;\n\n      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, delay));\n    }\n  }\n\n  throw new Error(''Unreachable'');\n}\n\n// Usage\nconst data = await retryOperation(\n  () => fetchUserData(userId),\n  { maxAttempts: 3, delayMs: 1000, backoff: ''exponential'' }\n);\n```\n\n### Don''t\n\n- ❌ Implement in 5+ languages (you''re good at porting)\n- ❌ Create fill-in-the-blank templates\n- ❌ Write contrived examples\n- ❌ Show only code without comments\n\n## File Organization\n\n### Self-Contained (Preferred)\n\n```\ntypescript-type-safety/\n  SKILL.md    # Everything inline\n```\n\n**When:** All content fits in ~500 words, no heavy reference needed\n\n### With Supporting Files\n\n```\napi-integration/\n  SKILL.md           # Overview + patterns\n  retry-helpers.ts   # Reusable code\n  examples/\n    auth-example.ts\n    pagination-example.ts\n```\n\n**When:** Reusable tools or multiple complete examples needed\n\n### With Heavy Reference\n\n```\naws-sdk/\n  SKILL.md       # Overview + workflows\n  s3-api.md      # 600 lines API reference\n  lambda-api.md  # 500 lines API reference\n```\n\n**When:** Reference material > 100 lines\n\n## Token Efficiency\n\nSkills load into every conversation. Keep them concise.\n\n### Target Limits\n\n- **SKILL.md**: Keep under 500 lines\n- Getting-started workflows: <150 words\n- Frequently-loaded skills: <200 words total\n- Other skills: <500 words\n- Files > 100 lines: Include table of contents\n\n**Challenge each piece of information**: \"Does Claude really need this explanation?\"\n\n### Compression Techniques\n\n```markdown\n# ❌ BAD - Verbose (42 words)\nYour human partner asks: \"How did we handle authentication errors in React Router before?\"\nYou should respond: \"I''ll search past conversations for React Router authentication patterns.\"\nThen dispatch a subagent with the search query: \"React Router authentication error handling 401\"\n\n# ✅ GOOD - Concise (20 words)\nPartner: \"How did we handle auth errors in React Router?\"\nYou: Searching...\n[Dispatch subagent → synthesis]\n```\n\n**Techniques:**\n- Reference tool `--help` instead of documenting all flags\n- Cross-reference other skills instead of repeating content\n- Show minimal example of pattern\n- Eliminate redundancy\n- Use progressive disclosure (reference additional files as needed)\n- Organize content by domain for focused context\n\n## Workflow Recommendations\n\nFor multi-step processes, include:\n\n1. **Clear sequential steps**: Break complex tasks into numbered operations\n2. **Feedback loops**: Build in verification/validation steps\n3. **Error handling**: What to check when things go wrong\n4. **Checklists**: For processes with many steps or easy-to-miss details\n\n**Example structure:**\n```markdown\n## Workflow\n\n1. **Preparation**\n   - Check prerequisites\n   - Validate environment\n\n2. **Execution**\n   - Step 1: [action + expected result]\n   - Step 2: [action + expected result]\n\n3. **Verification**\n   - [ ] Check 1 passes\n   - [ ] Check 2 passes\n\n4. **Rollback** (if needed)\n   - Steps to undo changes\n```\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n| Mistake | Why It Fails | Fix |\n|---------|--------------|-----|\n| Narrative example | \"In session 2025-10-03...\" | Focus on reusable pattern |\n| Multi-language dilution | Same example in 5 languages | One excellent example |\n| Code in flowcharts | `step1 [label=\"import fs\"]` | Use markdown code blocks |\n| Generic labels | helper1, helper2, step3 | Use semantic names |\n| Missing description triggers | \"For testing\" | \"Use when tests are flaky...\" |\n| First-person description | \"I help you...\" | \"Use when... - provides...\" |\n| Deeply nested file references | Multiple @ symbols, complex paths | Keep references simple and direct |\n| Windows-style file paths | `C:\\path\\to\\file` | Use forward slashes |\n| Offering too many options | 10 different approaches | Focus on one proven approach |\n| Punting error handling | \"Claude figures it out\" | Include explicit error handling in scripts |\n| Time-sensitive information | \"As of 2025...\" | Keep content evergreen |\n| Inconsistent terminology | Mixing synonyms randomly | Use consistent terms throughout |\n\n## Flowchart Usage\n\n**Only use flowcharts for:**\n- Non-obvious decision points\n- Process loops where you might stop too early\n- \"When to use A vs B\" decisions\n\n**Never use for:**\n- Reference material → Use tables/lists\n- Code examples → Use markdown blocks\n- Linear instructions → Use numbered lists\n\n## Cross-Referencing Skills\n\n```markdown\n# ✅ GOOD - Name only with clear requirement\n**REQUIRED:** Use superpowers:test-driven-development before proceeding\n\n**RECOMMENDED:** See typescript-type-safety for proper type guards\n\n# ❌ BAD - Unclear if required\nSee skills/testing/test-driven-development\n\n# ❌ BAD - Force-loads file, wastes context\n@skills/testing/test-driven-development/SKILL.md\n```\n\n## Advanced Practices\n\n### Iterative Development\n\n**Best approach**: Develop skills iteratively with Claude\n1. Start with minimal viable skill\n2. Test with real use cases\n3. Refine based on what works\n4. Remove what doesn''t add value\n\n### Build Evaluations First\n\nBefore extensive documentation:\n1. Create test scenarios\n2. Identify what good looks like\n3. Document proven patterns\n4. Skip theoretical improvements\n\n### Utility Scripts\n\nFor reliability, provide:\n- Scripts with explicit error handling (don''t defer errors to Claude)\n- Exit codes for success/failure\n- Clear error messages\n- Examples of usage\n- List required dependencies explicitly\n\n**Example:**\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nset -e  # Exit on error\n\nif [ ! -f \"config.json\" ]; then\n  echo \"Error: config.json not found\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\n# Script logic here\necho \"Success\"\nexit 0\n```\n\n### Verifiable Intermediate Outputs\n\nFor complex operations, create validation checkpoints:\n1. Have Claude produce a structured plan file\n2. Validate the plan with a script\n3. Execute only after validation passes\n\nThis catches errors before they compound.\n\n### Templates for Structured Output\n\nWhen skills produce consistent formats:\n```markdown\n## Output Template\n\n\\`\\`\\`typescript\ninterface ExpectedOutput {\n  status: ''success'' | ''error'';\n  data: YourDataType;\n  errors?: string[];\n}\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n**Usage**: Copy and adapt for your context\n```\n\n## Skill Creation Checklist\n\n**Before writing:**\n- [ ] Technique isn''t obvious or well-documented elsewhere\n- [ ] Pattern applies broadly (not project-specific)\n- [ ] I would reference this across multiple projects\n\n**Frontmatter:**\n- [ ] Name uses only letters, numbers, hyphens\n- [ ] Description starts with \"Use when...\"\n- [ ] Description includes triggers AND what skill does\n- [ ] Description is third person\n- [ ] Total frontmatter < 1024 characters\n\n**Content:**\n- [ ] Overview states core principle (1-2 sentences)\n- [ ] \"When to Use\" section with symptoms\n- [ ] Quick reference table for common operations\n- [ ] One excellent code example (if technique skill)\n- [ ] Common mistakes section\n- [ ] Keywords throughout for searchability\n\n**Quality:**\n- [ ] Word count appropriate for frequency (see targets above)\n- [ ] SKILL.md under 500 lines\n- [ ] No narrative storytelling\n- [ ] Flowcharts only for non-obvious decisions\n- [ ] Supporting files only if needed (100+ lines reference)\n- [ ] Cross-references use skill name, not file paths\n- [ ] No time-sensitive information\n- [ ] Consistent terminology throughout\n- [ ] Concrete examples (not templates)\n- [ ] Degrees of freedom match task complexity\n\n**Testing:**\n- [ ] Tested with Claude Haiku, Sonnet, and Opus (instructions effective for Opus may need more detail for Haiku)\n- [ ] Tested with subagent scenarios (if discipline-enforcing skill)\n- [ ] Addresses common rationalizations\n- [ ] Includes red flags list\n\n## Directory Structure\n\n```\nskills/\n  skill-name/\n    SKILL.md              # Required\n    supporting-file.*     # Optional\n    examples/             # Optional\n      example1.ts\n    scripts/              # Optional\n      helper.py\n```\n\n**Flat namespace** - all skills in one searchable directory\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\n**Good skills:**\n- Future Claude finds them quickly (CSO optimization)\n- Can be scanned in seconds (quick reference)\n- Provide clear actionable examples\n- Prevent repeating same research\n- Stay under 500 lines (token efficient)\n- Match specificity to task needs (right degrees of freedom)\n\n**Bad skills:**\n- Get ignored (vague description)\n- Take too long to evaluate (no quick reference)\n- Leave gaps in understanding (no examples)\n- Waste token budget (verbose explanations of obvious things)\n- Over-constrain creative tasks or under-specify critical operations\n- Include time-sensitive or obsolete information\n\n---\n\n**Remember:** Skills are for future Claude, not current you. Optimize for discovery, scanning, and action.\n\n**Golden rule:** Default assumption is Claude is already very smart. Only add context Claude doesn''t already have."},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:29:27.959Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Advanced Language Agents like Claude, needing structured technique guides for proven approaches.","zh":"非常适合像 Claude 这样的高级语言代理，需要结构化的技术指南来指导成熟的方法。","ja":"Claude のような高度な言語エージェントに適しています。構造化されたテクニック ガイドが必要で、確立されたアプローチを提供しています。","ko":"클라우드와 같은 고급 언어 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 구조화된 기술 가이드가 필요하여 검증된 접근 방식을 제공합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Lenguaje Avanzados como Claude, que necesitan guías de técnicas estructuradas para enfoques probados.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Langage Avancés comme Claude, ayant besoin de guides de techniques structurés pour des approches éprouvées.","de":"Perfekt für fortschrittliche Sprachagenten wie Claude, die strukturierte Technikleitfäden für bewährte Ansätze benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Linguagem Avançados como Claude, que precisam de guias de técnica estruturados para abordagens comprovadas.","ru":"Идеально для продвинутых языковых агентов, таких как Claude, которым необходимы структурированные руководства по технике для проверенных подходов.","ar":"مثالي لعميل لغة متقدم مثل Claude ، والذي يحتاج إلى إرشادات تقنية منظمة لمناهج مثبتة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to discover, scan, and apply effective coding techniques using reference guides, ensuring they can quickly find and utilize proven patterns and tools, with a focus on discoverability, scannability, and actionability.","zh":"赋予代理发现、扫描和应用有效的编码技术的能力，使用参考指南，确保代理能够快速找到和利用已验证的模式和工具，重点关注可发现性、可扫描性和可操作性。","ja":"エージェントが有効なコーディング テクニックを発見、スキャン、適用できるようにし、リファレンス ガイドを使用して、エージェントが迅速に検証済みのパターンとツールを見つけ、利用できるようにします。発見可能性、スキャナビリティ、操作可能性に重点を置いています。","ko":"에이전트가 효과적인 코딩 기술을 발견하고 스캔하고 적용할 수 있도록 해줍니다. 참조 가이드를 사용하여 에이전트가 검증된 패턴과 도구를 빠르게 찾고 사용할 수 있도록 하며, 발견 가능성, 스캔 가능성, 조작 가능성에 중점을 둡니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a descubrir, escanear y aplicar técnicas de codificación efectivas utilizando guías de referencia, garantizando que puedan encontrar y utilizar rápidamente patrones y herramientas probados, con un enfoque en la capacidad de descubrimiento, escaneabilidad y capacidad de actuación.","fr":"Permet aux agents de découvrir, de balayer et d''appliquer des techniques de codage efficaces en utilisant des guides de référence, en garantissant qu''ils puissent rapidement trouver et utiliser des modèles et des outils éprouvés, avec un focus sur la découverte, la scannabilité et l''actionabilité.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, effektive Codierungstechniken unter Verwendung von Referenzhandbüchern zu entdecken, zu scannen und anzuwenden, und stellt sicher, dass sie bewährte Muster und Werkzeuge schnell finden und nutzen können, mit Fokus auf Entdeckbarkeit, Scannierbarkeit und Handhabbarkeit.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a descobrirem, Digitalizarem e aplicarem técnicas de codificação eficazes usando guias de referência, garantindo que eles possam encontrar e utilizar rapidamente padrões e ferramentas comprovados, com foco na descoberta, varredura e capacidade de ação.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обнаруживать, сканировать и применять эффективные методы кодирования с помощью справочных руководств, гарантируя, что они могут быстро находить и использовать проверенные шаблоны и инструменты, с фокусом на обнаруживаемости, сканируемости и действенности.","ar":"يتمكن العملاء من اكتشاف وفحص وتطبيق تقنيات برمجة فعالة باستخدام أدلة مرجعية ، مما يضمن أنهم يمكنهم العثور على استخدام أنماط وأدوات مثبتة بسرعة ، مع التركيز على اكتشاف القدرة على الفحص والقيام."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating discoverable technique guides","Documenting proven coding patterns","Developing scannable and actionable skill references"],"zh":["创建可发现的技术指南","记录验证的编码模式","开发可扫描和可操作的技能参考"],"ja":["発見可能なテクニック ガイドの作成","検証済みのコーディング パターンの文書化","スキャナブルで操作可能なスキル リファレンスの開発"],"ko":["검색 가능한 기술 가이드 만들기","검증된 코딩 패턴 문서화","스캔 가능하고 조작 가능한 스킬 참조 개발"],"es":["Crear guías de técnicas descubribles","Documentar patrones de codificación probados","Desarrollar referencias de habilidades scaneables y realizables"],"fr":["Créer des guides de techniques découvrables","Documenter des modèles de codage éprouvés","Développer des références de compétences scannables et réalisables"],"de":["Erstellen von entdeckbaren Technikleitfäden","Dokumentation von bewährten Codierungsmustern","Entwicklung von scannbaren und handhabbaren Fähigkeitsreferenzen"],"pt":["Criar guias de técnica descobríveis","Documentar padrões de codificação comprovados","Desenvolver referências de habilidades legíveis e realizáveis"],"ru":["Создание обнаруживаемых руководств по технике","Документирование проверенных шаблонов кодирования","Разработка сканируемых и действенных справочных материалов по навыкам"],"ar":["إنشاء أدلة تقنية يمكن اكتشافها","توثيق أنماط برمجة مثبتة","تطوير مراجع مهارات قابلة للفحص والتنفيذ"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires context that Claude doesn''t already have","Assumes Claude is already very smart"],"zh":["需要 Claude 没有的上下文","假设 Claude 已经非常聪明"],"ja":["Claude がすでに持っていないコンテキストが必要","Claude が既に非常に賢いと仮定"],"ko":["클라우드가 이미 가지고 있지 않은 컨텍스트가 필요","클라우드가 이미 매우 지능적이라는 가정"],"es":["Requiere un contexto que Claude no tenga ya","Supone que Claude ya es muy inteligente"],"fr":["Nécessite un contexte que Claude ne possède pas déjà","Suppose que Claude est déjà très intelligent"],"de":["Benötigt einen Kontext, den Claude noch nicht hat","Geht davon aus, dass Claude bereits sehr intelligent ist"],"pt":["Exige contexto que Claude ainda não tem","Supõe que Claude já é muito inteligente"],"ru":["Требует контекста, которого у Claude еще нет","Предполагает, что Claude уже очень умный"],"ar":["يتطلب سياقًا لا يمتلكه Claude بعد","يفترض أن Claude ذكي للغاية بالفعل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('natea/ai-news-influencer/quality-metrics', 'community', 'natea', 'ai-news-influencer', 'natea/ai-news-influencer', 'quality-metrics', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.408Z', '2026-02-18T03:29:28.100Z', NULL, '{"id":"natea/ai-news-influencer/quality-metrics","name":"quality-metrics","description":{"zh":"质量度量指标是衡量软件质量的关键指标，包括DORA指标、质量门槛和趋势分析","ja":"品質メトリクスはソフトウェア品質を測定するための重要な指標です。DORAメトリクス、品質ゲート、トレンド分析など","ko":"품질 측정 지표는 소프트웨어 품질을 측정하는 중요한 지표입니다. DORA 지표, 품질 게이트, 트렌드 분석 등","es":"Nuestro sistema de métricas de calidad ayuda a los desarrolladores a medir y mejorar su eficiencia. Conoce nuestras recomendaciones","fr":"Notre système de métriques de qualité aide les développeurs à mesurer et améliorer leur efficacité. Découvrez nos recommandations","de":"Unser Qualitätsmetrik-System hilft Entwicklern, ihre Effizienz zu messen und zu verbessern. Erfahren Sie mehr über unsere Empfehlungen","pt":"Métricas de qualidade para desenvolvedores, com foco em resultados e otimização de desempenho","ru":"Метрики качества для разработчиков, с фокусом на результатах и оптимизации производительности","ar":"معايير الجودة للمطورين، مع التركيز على النتائج وتحسين الأداء","en":"An autonomous agentic system that monitors X (Twitter) for relevant news, generates engaging LinkedIn content with images, posts automatically, responds to comments, and continuously improves its strategy based on engagement metrics."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"质量度量指标","ja":"品質メトリクス","ko":"품질 측정 지표","es":"Métricas de calidad para desarrolladores","fr":"Métriques de qualité pour les développeurs","de":"Qualitätsmetriken für Entwickler","pt":"Métricas de Qualidade: Otimização de Desempenho","ru":"Метрики качества: оптимизация производительности","ar":"معايير الجودة: تحسين الأداء","en":"quality-metrics"},"description":{"zh":"质量度量指标是衡量软件质量的关键指标，包括DORA指标、质量门槛和趋势分析","ja":"品質メトリクスはソフトウェア品質を測定するための重要な指標です。DORAメトリクス、品質ゲート、トレンド分析など","ko":"품질 측정 지표는 소프트웨어 품질을 측정하는 중요한 지표입니다. DORA 지표, 품질 게이트, 트렌드 분석 등","es":"Nuestro sistema de métricas de calidad ayuda a los desarrolladores a medir y mejorar su eficiencia. Conoce nuestras recomendaciones","fr":"Notre système de métriques de qualité aide les développeurs à mesurer et améliorer leur efficacité. Découvrez nos recommandations","de":"Unser Qualitätsmetrik-System hilft Entwicklern, ihre Effizienz zu messen und zu verbessern. Erfahren Sie mehr über unsere Empfehlungen","pt":"Métricas de qualidade para desenvolvedores, com foco em resultados e otimização de desempenho","ru":"Метрики качества для разработчиков, с фокусом на результатах и оптимизации производительности","ar":"معايير الجودة للمطورين، مع التركيز على النتائج وتحسين الأداء","en":"An autonomous agentic system that monitors X (Twitter) for relevant news, generates engaging LinkedIn content with images, posts automatically, responds to c..."},"definition":{"en":"An autonomous agentic system that monitors X (Twitter) for relevant news, generates engaging LinkedIn content with images, posts automatically, responds to comments, and continuously improves its strategy based on engagement metrics."},"features":{"zh":["DORA指标","质量门槛","趋势分析","自动化测试","代码质量分析"],"ja":["DORAメトリクス","品質ゲート","トレンド分析","自動テスト","コード品質分析"],"ko":["DORA 지표","품질 게이트","트렌드 분석","자동화 테스트","코드 품질 분석"],"es":["Medición de resultados en lugar de actividades","Enfoque en métricas DORA","Evitación de métricas vanidad","Establecimiento de umbrales que impulsan el comportamiento","Análisis de tendencias a lo largo del tiempo"],"fr":["Mesure des résultats plutôt que des activités","Focus sur les métriques DORA","Évitement des métriques de vanité","Définition de seuils qui influencent le comportement","Analyse des tendances dans le temps"],"de":["Messung von Ergebnissen anstelle von Aktivitäten","Fokus auf DORA-Metriken","Vermeidung von Vanity-Metriken","Festlegung von Schwellenwerten, die das Verhalten beeinflussen","Trendanalyse über die Zeit"],"pt":["Medição de resultados em vez de atividades","Foco em métricas DORA","Evitar métricas vaidosas","Definição de limiares para direcionar o comportamento","Análise de tendências ao longo do tempo"],"ru":["Измерение результатов вместо активностей","Фокус на метриках DORA","Избегание пустых метрик","Определение порогов для направления поведения","Анализ тенденций во времени"],"ar":["قياس النتائج بدلاً من الأنشطة","التركيز على معايير DORA","تجنب معايير البخيل","تحديد عتبات لتوجيه السلوك","تحليل الاتجاهات بمرور الوقت"]},"keywords":{"zh":["质量度量指标","DORA指标","质量门槛","趋势分析","自动化测试","代码质量分析","软件质量","开发最佳实践"],"ja":["品質メトリクス","DORAメトリクス","品質ゲート","トレンド分析","自動テスト","コード品質分析","ソフトウェア品質","開発ベストプラクティス"],"ko":["품질 측정 지표","DORA 지표","품질 게이트","트렌드 분석","자동화 테스트","코드 품질 분석","소프트웨어 품질","개발 최선의 방법"],"es":["métricas de calidad","desarrollo de software","eficiencia","eficacia","DORA","métricas de desarrollo","análisis de tendencias","umbrales de calidad"],"fr":["métriques de qualité","développement de logiciels","efficacité","efficience","DORA","métriques de développement","analyse de tendances","seuils de qualité"],"de":["Qualitätsmetriken","Software-Entwicklung","Effizienz","Effektivität","DORA","Entwicklungs-Metriken","Trendanalyse","Qualitätsschwellenwerte"],"pt":["métricas de qualidade","desempenho de aplicativos","otimização de desempenho","métricas DORA","medição de resultados","evitar métricas vaidosas"],"ru":["метрики качества","производительность приложений","оптимизация производительности","метрики DORA","измерение результатов","избегание пустых метрик"],"ar":["معايير الجودة","أداء التطبيقات","تحسين الأداء","معايير DORA","قياس النتائج","تجنب معايير البخيل"]}},"owner":"natea","repo":"ai-news-influencer","repoPath":"natea/ai-news-influencer","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.408Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"quality-metrics","description":"Measure quality effectively with actionable metrics. Use when establishing quality dashboards, defining KPIs, or evaluating test effectiveness.","tags":["metrics","dora","quality-gates","dashboards","kpis","measurement"],"bodyPreview":"# Quality Metrics\n\n<default_to_action>\nWhen measuring quality or building dashboards:\n1. MEASURE outcomes (bug escape rate, MTTD) not activities (test count)\n2. FOCUS on DORA metrics: Deployment frequency, Lead time, MTTD, MTTR, Change failure rate\n3. AVOID vanity metrics: 100% coverage means nothing if tests don''t catch bugs\n4. SET thresholds that drive behavior (quality gates block bad code)\n5. TREND over time: Direction matters more than absolute numbers\n\n**Quick Metric Selection:**\n- Speed:","body":"# Quality Metrics\n\n<default_to_action>\nWhen measuring quality or building dashboards:\n1. MEASURE outcomes (bug escape rate, MTTD) not activities (test count)\n2. FOCUS on DORA metrics: Deployment frequency, Lead time, MTTD, MTTR, Change failure rate\n3. AVOID vanity metrics: 100% coverage means nothing if tests don''t catch bugs\n4. SET thresholds that drive behavior (quality gates block bad code)\n5. TREND over time: Direction matters more than absolute numbers\n\n**Quick Metric Selection:**\n- Speed: Deployment frequency, lead time for changes\n- Stability: Change failure rate, MTTR\n- Quality: Bug escape rate, defect density, test effectiveness\n- Process: Code review time, flaky test rate\n\n**Critical Success Factors:**\n- Metrics without action are theater\n- What you measure is what you optimize\n- Trends matter more than snapshots\n</default_to_action>\n\n## Quick Reference Card\n\n### When to Use\n- Building quality dashboards\n- Defining quality gates\n- Evaluating testing effectiveness\n- Justifying quality investments\n\n### Meaningful vs Vanity Metrics\n| ✅ Meaningful | ❌ Vanity |\n|--------------|-----------|\n| Bug escape rate | Test case count |\n| MTTD (detection) | Lines of test code |\n| MTTR (recovery) | Test executions |\n| Change failure rate | Coverage % (alone) |\n| Lead time for changes | Requirements traced |\n\n### DORA Metrics\n| Metric | Elite | High | Medium | Low |\n|--------|-------|------|--------|-----|\n| Deploy Frequency | On-demand | Weekly | Monthly | Yearly |\n| Lead Time | < 1 hour | < 1 week | < 1 month | > 6 months |\n| Change Failure Rate | < 5% | < 15% | < 30% | > 45% |\n| MTTR | < 1 hour | < 1 day | < 1 week | > 1 month |\n\n### Quality Gate Thresholds\n| Metric | Blocking Threshold | Warning |\n|--------|-------------------|---------|\n| Test pass rate | 100% | - |\n| Critical coverage | > 80% | > 70% |\n| Security critical | 0 | - |\n| Performance p95 | < 200ms | < 500ms |\n| Flaky tests | < 2% | < 5% |\n\n---\n\n## Core Metrics\n\n### Bug Escape Rate\n```\nBug Escape Rate = (Production Bugs / Total Bugs Found) × 100\n\nTarget: < 10% (90% caught before production)\n```\n\n### Test Effectiveness\n```\nTest Effectiveness = (Bugs Found by Tests / Total Bugs) × 100\n\nTarget: > 70%\n```\n\n### Defect Density\n```\nDefect Density = Defects / KLOC\n\nGood: < 1 defect per KLOC\n```\n\n### Mean Time to Detect (MTTD)\n```\nMTTD = Time(Bug Reported) - Time(Bug Introduced)\n\nTarget: < 1 day for critical, < 1 week for others\n```\n\n---\n\n## Dashboard Design\n\n```typescript\n// Agent generates quality dashboard\nawait Task(\"Generate Dashboard\", {\n  metrics: {\n    delivery: [''deployment-frequency'', ''lead-time'', ''change-failure-rate''],\n    quality: [''bug-escape-rate'', ''test-effectiveness'', ''defect-density''],\n    stability: [''mttd'', ''mttr'', ''availability''],\n    process: [''code-review-time'', ''flaky-test-rate'', ''coverage-trend'']\n  },\n  visualization: ''grafana'',\n  alerts: {\n    critical: { bug_escape_rate: ''>20%'', mttr: ''>24h'' },\n    warning: { coverage: ''<70%'', flaky_rate: ''>5%'' }\n  }\n}, \"qe-quality-analyzer\");\n```\n\n---\n\n## Quality Gate Configuration\n\n```json\n{\n  \"qualityGates\": {\n    \"commit\": {\n      \"coverage\": { \"min\": 80, \"blocking\": true },\n      \"lint\": { \"errors\": 0, \"blocking\": true }\n    },\n    \"pr\": {\n      \"tests\": { \"pass\": \"100%\", \"blocking\": true },\n      \"security\": { \"critical\": 0, \"blocking\": true },\n      \"coverage_delta\": { \"min\": 0, \"blocking\": false }\n    },\n    \"release\": {\n      \"e2e\": { \"pass\": \"100%\", \"blocking\": true },\n      \"performance_p95\": { \"max_ms\": 200, \"blocking\": true },\n      \"bug_escape_rate\": { \"max\": \"10%\", \"blocking\": false }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Agent-Assisted Metrics\n\n```typescript\n// Calculate quality trends\nawait Task(\"Quality Trend Analysis\", {\n  timeframe: ''90d'',\n  metrics: [''bug-escape-rate'', ''mttd'', ''test-effectiveness''],\n  compare: ''previous-90d'',\n  predictNext: ''30d''\n}, \"qe-quality-analyzer\");\n\n// Evaluate quality gate\nawait Task(\"Quality Gate Evaluation\", {\n  buildId: ''build-123'',\n  environment: ''staging'',\n  metrics: currentMetrics,\n  policy: qualityPolicy\n}, \"qe-quality-gate\");\n```\n\n---\n\n## Agent Coordination Hints\n\n### Memory Namespace\n```\naqe/quality-metrics/\n├── dashboards/*         - Dashboard configurations\n├── trends/*             - Historical metric data\n├── gates/*              - Gate evaluation results\n└── alerts/*             - Triggered alerts\n```\n\n### Fleet Coordination\n```typescript\nconst metricsFleet = await FleetManager.coordinate({\n  strategy: ''quality-metrics'',\n  agents: [\n    ''qe-quality-analyzer'',         // Trend analysis\n    ''qe-test-executor'',            // Test metrics\n    ''qe-coverage-analyzer'',        // Coverage data\n    ''qe-production-intelligence'',  // Production metrics\n    ''qe-quality-gate''              // Gate decisions\n  ],\n  topology: ''mesh''\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## Common Traps\n\n| Trap | Problem | Solution |\n|------|---------|----------|\n| Coverage worship | 100% coverage, bugs still escape | Measure bug escape rate instead |\n| Test count focus | Many tests, slow feedback | Measure execution time |\n| Activity metrics | Busy work, no outcomes | Measure outcomes (MTTD, MTTR) |\n| Point-in-time | Snapshot without context | Track trends over time |\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n- [agentic-quality-engineering](../agentic-quality-engineering/) - Agent coordination\n- [cicd-pipeline-qe-orchestrator](../cicd-pipeline-qe-orchestrator/) - Quality gates\n- [risk-based-testing](../risk-based-testing/) - Risk-informed metrics\n- [shift-right-testing](../shift-right-testing/) - Production metrics\n\n---\n\n## Remember\n\n**Measure outcomes, not activities.** Bug escape rate > test count. MTTD/MTTR > coverage %. Trends > snapshots. Set gates that block bad code. What you measure is what you optimize.\n\n**With Agents:** Agents track metrics automatically, analyze trends, trigger alerts, and make gate decisions. Use agents to maintain continuous quality visibility.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:29:28.100Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Analysis Agents needing advanced quality metrics tracking and DORA metrics integration.","zh":"适合需要高级质量指标跟踪和DORA指标集成的AI分析代理。","ja":"高度な品質メトリクスの追跡とDORAメトリクスの統合を必要とするAI分析エージェントに適しています。","ko":"고급 품질 지표 추적 및 DORA 지표 통합이 필요한 AI 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Análisis de IA que necesitan un seguimiento avanzado de métricas de calidad y una integración con métricas DORA.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Analyse d''IA ayant besoin d''un suivi avancé des métriques de qualité et d''une intégration avec les métriques DORA.","de":"Perfekt für AI-Analyse-Agents, die eine erweiterte Qualitätsmetrik-Verfolgung und eine DORA-Metrik-Integration benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de IA que necessitam de rastreamento de métricas de qualidade avançadas e integração de métricas DORA.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа ИИ, которым необходимы передовые функции отслеживания метрик качества и интеграция метрик DORA.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذي يحتاج إلى تتبع معايير جودة متقدمة وتكامل معايير DORA."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to monitor and improve code quality by tracking key metrics such as bug escape rate, MTTD, and deployment frequency, while avoiding vanity metrics and setting meaningful thresholds to drive behavior, utilizing data visualization and trend analysis to inform decision-making.","zh":"赋予代理监控和改进代码质量的能力，通过跟踪关键指标（如Bug逃逸率、MTTD和部署频率），同时避免虚荣指标，设定有意义的阈值来驱动行为，利用数据可视化和趋势分析来指导决策。","ja":"エージェントがコードの品質を監視して改善する能力を与え、バグエスケープ率、MTTD、デプロイ頻度などの重要なメトリクスを追跡し、虚栄的なメトリクスを避け、有意義な閾値を設定して行動を促し、データの可視化と傾向分析を使用して意思決定を支援します。","ko":"에이전트가 코드 품질을 모니터링하고 개선할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 버그 탈출률, MTTD, 배포 빈도 등과 같은 주요 지표를 추적하며, 허위 지표를 피하고, 의미 있는 임계값을 설정하여 행동을 유도하며, 데이터 시각화 및 추세 분석을 사용하여 의사 결정을 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a monitorear y mejorar la calidad del código mediante el seguimiento de métricas clave como la tasa de escape de errores, MTTD y frecuencia de implementación, evitando métricas vanas y estableciendo umbrales significativos para impulsar el comportamiento, utilizando la visualización de datos y el análisis de tendencias para informar la toma de decisiones.","fr":"Permet aux agents de surveiller et d''améliorer la qualité du code en suivant des métriques clés telles que le taux d''échappement de bogues, MTTD et la fréquence de déploiement, tout en évitant les métriques vaniteuses et en fixant des seuils significatifs pour piloter le comportement, en utilisant la visualisation de données et l''analyse de tendances pour éclairer la prise de décision.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, die Codequalität durch Nachverfolgung wichtiger Metriken wie Fehlerentweichungsrate, MTTD und Bereitstellungs Häufigkeit zu überwachen und zu verbessern, während sie sich von eitlen Metriken abwenden und sinnvolle Schwellenwerte festlegen, um das Verhalten zu beeinflussen, unter Nutzung von Datenvisualisierung und Trendanalyse zur Entscheidungsfindung.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a monitorar e melhorar a qualidade do código, rastreando métricas-chave, como taxa de escapamento de bugs, MTTD e frequência de implantação, evitando métricas de vaidade e definindo limites significativos para impulsionar o comportamento, utilizando visualização de dados e análise de tendências para informar a tomada de decisões.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью отслеживать и улучшать качество кода, отслеживая ключевые метрики, такие как скорость побега ошибок, MTTD и частота развертывания, избегая метрик тщеславия и устанавливающих значимые пороги для стимулирования поведения, используя визуализацию данных и анализ тенденций для информирования процесса принятия решений.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على مراقبة وتحسين جودة الشفرة من خلال تتبع معايير رئيسية مثل معدل هروب الأخطاء و MTTD وتكرار النشر، وتجنب معايير التكلف وضبط حدود ملائمة لتوجيه السلوك، باستخدام تجسير البيانات وتحليل الاتجاهات لإبلاغ عملية اتخاذ القرارات."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating quality metrics tracking for software development projects","Generating engaging LinkedIn content with images based on quality metrics trends","Responding to comments and continuously improving strategy based on engagement metrics","Monitoring Twitter for relevant news and updates on quality metrics and DORA metrics"],"zh":["自动化软件开发项目的质量指标跟踪","根据质量指标趋势生成带有图像的LinkedIn内容","根据参与度指标持续响应评论并改进策略","监控Twitter上与质量指标和DORA指标相关的新闻和更新"],"ja":["ソフトウェア開発プロジェクトの品質メトリクスの追跡を自動化する","品質メトリクスの傾向に基づいて画像付きのLinkedInコンテンツを生成する","関与度メトリクスに基づいてコメントに応じて継続的に戦略を改善する","品質メトリクスとDORAメトリクスに関する関連ニュースと更新をTwitterで監視する"],"ko":["소프트웨어 개발 프로젝트의 품질 지표 추적을 자동화한다","품질 지표 추세에 따라 이미지와 함께 LinkedIn 콘텐츠를 생성한다","참여도 지표에 따라 댓글에 응답하고 전략을 지속적으로 개선한다","품질 지표 및 DORA 지표 관련 뉴스 및 업데이트를 Twitter에서 모니터링한다"],"es":["Automatizar el seguimiento de métricas de calidad para proyectos de desarrollo de software","Generar contenido atractivo de LinkedIn con imágenes basadas en tendencias de métricas de calidad","Responder a comentarios y mejorar continuamente la estrategia basada en métricas de compromiso","Monitorear Twitter para noticias y actualizaciones relevantes sobre métricas de calidad y métricas DORA"],"fr":["Automatiser le suivi des métriques de qualité pour les projets de développement de logiciels","Générer du contenu LinkedIn attractif avec des images basées sur les tendances des métriques de qualité","Répondre aux commentaires et améliorer continuellement la stratégie basée sur les métriques d''engagement","Surveiller Twitter pour les actualités et mises à jour pertinentes sur les métriques de qualité et les métriques DORA"],"de":["Automatisieren der Verfolgung von Qualitätmetriken für Software-Entwicklungsprojekte","Erzeugen von ansprechendem LinkedIn-Inhalt mit Bildern basierend auf Qualitätmetrik-Trends","Antworten auf Kommentare und kontinuierliche Verbesserung der Strategie basierend auf Engagement-Metriken","Überwachen von Twitter für relevante Nachrichten und Updates zu Qualitätmetriken und DORA-Metriken"],"pt":["Automatizar o rastreamento de métricas de qualidade para projetos de desenvolvimento de software","Gerar conteúdo do LinkedIn atraente com imagens baseadas em tendências de métricas de qualidade","Responder a comentários e melhorar continuamente a estratégia com base em métricas de engajamento","Monitorar o Twitter para notícias e atualizações relevantes sobre métricas de qualidade e métricas DORA"],"ru":["Автоматизировать отслеживание метрик качества для проектов разработки программного обеспечения","Генерировать привлекательный контент LinkedIn с изображениями на основе тенденций метрик качества","Отвечать на комментарии и不断 улучшать стратегию на основе метрик вовлеченности","Мониторить Twitter для получения актуальных новостей и обновлений о метриках качества и метриках DORA"],"ar":["تأتمة تتبع معايير الجودة لمشاريع تطوير البرمجيات","генерировать محتوى LinkedIn الممتع مع الصور المستندة إلى اتجاهات معايير الجودة","الرد على التعليقات وتحسين الاستراتيجية باستمرار بناءً على معايير المشاركة","مراقبة تويتر للأخبار والتحديثات ذات الصلة بمعايير الجودة ومعايير DORA"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to Twitter and LinkedIn APIs","Limited to tracking specific quality metrics (bug escape rate, MTTD, deployment frequency, etc.)","Needs continuous engagement metrics to improve strategy"],"zh":["需要访问Twitter和LinkedIn API","仅限跟踪特定的质量指标（Bug逃逸率、MTTD、部署频率等）","需要连续的参与度指标来改进策略"],"ja":["TwitterおよびLinkedIn APIへのアクセスが必要","特定の品質メトリクス（バグエスケープ率、MTTD、デプロイ頻度など）のみを追跡する","戦略を改善するために連続的な関与度メトリクスが必要"],"ko":["Twitter 및 LinkedIn API에 대한 액세스가 필요합니다","특정 품질 지표(버그 탈출률, MTTD, 배포 빈도 등)만 추적할 수 있습니다","전략을 개선하기 위해 연속적인 참여도 지표가 필요합니다"],"es":["Requiere acceso a las API de Twitter y LinkedIn","Limitado al seguimiento de métricas de calidad específicas (tasa de escape de errores, MTTD, frecuencia de implementación, etc.)","Necesita métricas de compromiso continuo para mejorar la estrategia"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès aux API de Twitter et LinkedIn","Limité au suivi de métriques de qualité spécifiques (taux d''échappement de bogues, MTTD, fréquence de déploiement, etc.)","Nécessite des métriques d''engagement continues pour améliorer la stratégie"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf Twitter- und LinkedIn-APIs","Begrenzt auf die Verfolgung spezifischer Qualitätmetriken (Fehlerentweichungsrate, MTTD, Bereitstellungs Häufigkeit usw.)","Benötigt kontinuierliche Engagement-Metriken zur Verbesserung der Strategie"],"pt":["Requer acesso às APIs do Twitter e LinkedIn","Limitado ao rastreamento de métricas de qualidade específicas (taxa de escapamento de bugs, MTTD, frequência de implantação, etc.)","Necessita de métricas de engajamento contínuas para melhorar a estratégia"],"ru":["Требует доступа к API Twitter и LinkedIn","Ограничен отслеживанием определенных метрик качества (скорость побега ошибок, MTTD, частота развертывания и т. д.)","Требует постоянных метрик вовлеченности для улучшения стратегии"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى واجهات برمجة التطبيقات Twitter وLinkedIn","محدود بتتبع معايير جودة محددة (معدل هروب الأخطاء و MTTD وتكرار النشر وما إلى ذلك)","يحتاج إلى معايير المشاركة المستمرة لتحسين الاستراتيجية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('nicepkg/vsync/resource-scout', 'community', 'nicepkg', 'vsync', 'nicepkg/vsync', 'resource-scout', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.408Z', '2026-02-18T03:30:05.088Z', NULL, '{"id":"nicepkg/vsync/resource-scout","name":"resource-scout","description":{"zh":"Resource Scout技能允许开发者跨多个平台搜索和同步MCP服务器、技能和命令，简化开发流程","ja":"Resource Scoutスキルは、開発者が複数のプラットフォームでMCPサーバー、スキル、コマンドを検索して同期することを可能にし、開発プロセスを簡素化","ko":"리소스 스카우트 스킬은 개발자가 여러 플랫폼에서 MCP 서버, 스킬 및 명령을 검색하고 동기화하여 개발 프로세스를 단순화","es":"Resource Scout es una herramienta que permite buscar y descubrir skills y servidores MCP existentes para optimizar el desarrollo.","fr":"Resource Scout est un outil qui permet de rechercher et de découvrir des compétences et des serveurs MCP existants pour optimiser le développement.","de":"Ressourcen-Scout ist ein Werkzeug, das die Suche und Entdeckung bestehender Skills und MCP-Server ermöglicht, um die Entwicklung zu optimieren.","en":"Sync MCP servers, Skills, Agents & Commands across Claude Code, Cursor, OpenCode, Codex. One config, all tools."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Resource Scout技能：跨平台服务器和技能搜索","ja":"Resource Scoutスキル：マルチプラットフォームサーバーとスキルの検索","ko":"리소스 스카우트 스킬: 멀티 플랫폼 서버 및 스킬 검색","es":"Recursos Scout: Herramienta de Búsqueda de Skills y Servi...","fr":"Resource Scout : Outil de Recherche de Compétences et de ...","de":"Ressourcen-Scout: Werkzeug zur Suche nach Skills und MCP-...","en":"resource-scout"},"description":{"zh":"Resource Scout技能允许开发者跨多个平台搜索和同步MCP服务器、技能和命令，简化开发流程","ja":"Resource Scoutスキルは、開発者が複数のプラットフォームでMCPサーバー、スキル、コマンドを検索して同期することを可能にし、開発プロセスを簡素化","ko":"리소스 스카우트 스킬은 개발자가 여러 플랫폼에서 MCP 서버, 스킬 및 명령을 검색하고 동기화하여 개발 프로세스를 단순화","es":"Resource Scout es una herramienta que permite buscar y descubrir skills y servidores MCP existentes para optimizar el desarrollo.","fr":"Resource Scout est un outil qui permet de rechercher et de découvrir des compétences et des serveurs MCP existants pour optimiser le développement.","de":"Ressourcen-Scout ist ein Werkzeug, das die Suche und Entdeckung bestehender Skills und MCP-Server ermöglicht, um die Entwicklung zu optimieren.","en":"Sync MCP servers, Skills, Agents & Commands across Claude Code, Cursor, OpenCode, Codex. One config, all tools."},"definition":{"en":"Sync MCP servers, Skills, Agents & Commands across Claude Code, Cursor, OpenCode, Codex. One config, all tools."},"features":{"zh":["跨平台搜索MCP服务器、技能和命令","同步Claude Code、Cursor、OpenCode、Codex上的技能和服务器","支持WebSearch、GitHub和官方网站的搜索","提供快速搜索策略和搜索技巧"],"ja":["MCPサーバー、スキル、コマンドのマルチプラットフォーム検索","Claude Code、Cursor、OpenCode、Codex上的スキルとサーバーの同期","WebSearch、GitHub、公式ウェブサイトの検索をサポート","クイック検索戦略と検索テクニックを提供"],"ko":["여러 플랫폼에서 MCP 서버, 스킬 및 명령을 검색","Claude Code, Cursor, OpenCode, Codex上的 스킬 및 서버를 동기화","WebSearch, GitHub 및 공식 웹사이트의 검색을 지원","快速 검색 전략 및 검색 기술을 제공"],"es":["Búsqueda de skills en Claude Code","Búsqueda de servidores MCP","Compatibilidad con varias plataformas","Configuración única para todas las herramientas","Integración con GitHub y otros repositorios"],"fr":["Recherche de compétences dans Claude Code","Recherche de serveurs MCP","Compatibilité avec plusieurs plateformes","Configuration unique pour tous les outils","Intégration avec GitHub et d''autres référentiels"],"de":["Suche nach Skills in Claude Code","Suche nach MCP-Servern","Kompatibilität mit mehreren Plattformen","Einheitliche Konfiguration für alle Werkzeuge","Integration mit GitHub und anderen Repositorien"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Resource Scout","MCP服务器","技能搜索","跨平台搜索","Claude Code","Cursor","OpenCode","Codex"],"ja":["Resource Scout","MCPサーバー","スキル検索","マルチプラットフォーム検索","Claude Code","Cursor","OpenCode","Codex"],"ko":["리소스 스카우트","MCP 서버","스킬 검색","멀티 플랫폼 검색","Claude Code","Cursor","OpenCode","Codex"],"es":["Resource Scout","búsqueda de skills","búsqueda de servidores MCP","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo","Claude Code","MCP","GitHub"],"fr":["Resource Scout","recherche de compétences","recherche de serveurs MCP","développement de logiciels","outils de développement","Claude Code","MCP","GitHub"],"de":["Ressourcen-Scout","Suche nach Skills","Suche nach MCP-Servern","Software-Entwicklung","Entwicklungstools","Claude Code","MCP","GitHub"]}},"owner":"nicepkg","repo":"vsync","repoPath":"nicepkg/vsync","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.408Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"resource-scout","description":"Search and discover Claude Code skills and MCP servers from marketplaces, GitHub repositories, and registries. Use when (1) user asks to find skills for a specific task, (2) looking for MCP servers to connect external tools, (3) user mentions find skill, search MCP, discover tools, or what skills exist for X, (4) before creating a custom skill to check if one already exists.","bodyPreview":"# Resource Scout\n\nSearch and discover existing Claude Code skills and MCP servers before building custom solutions.\n\n## Quick Search Strategy\n\n**For Skills:**\n1. WebSearch: `site:skillsmp.com [topic]` or `claude skill [topic]`\n2. Check GitHub: `awesome-claude-skills [topic]`\n3. Browse: skillhub.club, claudeskills.info\n\n**For MCP:**\n1. WebSearch: `MCP server [tool/service name]`\n2. Check: glama.ai/mcp/servers, mcpmarket.com\n3. Official: github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers\n\n## Skill Search Wor","body":"# Resource Scout\n\nSearch and discover existing Claude Code skills and MCP servers before building custom solutions.\n\n## Quick Search Strategy\n\n**For Skills:**\n1. WebSearch: `site:skillsmp.com [topic]` or `claude skill [topic]`\n2. Check GitHub: `awesome-claude-skills [topic]`\n3. Browse: skillhub.club, claudeskills.info\n\n**For MCP:**\n1. WebSearch: `MCP server [tool/service name]`\n2. Check: glama.ai/mcp/servers, mcpmarket.com\n3. Official: github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers\n\n## Skill Search Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Define Need\n\nBefore searching, clarify:\n- What task needs to be accomplished?\n- What tools/services are involved?\n- Is it a common pattern (git, testing, API) or domain-specific?\n\n### Step 2: Search Marketplaces\n\n**Primary sources (largest catalogs):**\n\n| Source | URL | Best For |\n|--------|-----|----------|\n| SkillsMP | skillsmp.com | 71000+ skills, long-tail search |\n| SkillHub.club | skillhub.club | AI-evaluated, quality filter |\n| Claude Skills Hub | claudeskills.info | UI-friendly browsing |\n\n**Search patterns:**\n```\n# On SkillsMP\n[domain] skill          → \"marketing skill\", \"database skill\"\n[framework] claude      → \"react claude\", \"fastapi claude\"\n[task] automation       → \"deployment automation\"\n```\n\n### Step 3: Search GitHub\n\n**Curated lists:**\n- `github.com/keyuyuan/skillhub-awesome-skills` - 精选清单\n- `github.com/VoltAgent/awesome-claude-skills` - 生态大全\n- `github.com/ComposioHQ/awesome-claude-skills` - 大量通用技能\n\n**Ready-to-use repositories:**\n- `github.com/alirezarezvani/claude-skills` - Content/Marketing\n- `github.com/gked2121/claude-skills` - Workflow思维\n- `github.com/Microck/ordinary-claude-skills` - 超大集合\n- `github.com/sickn33/antigravity-awesome-skills` - 结构化\n\n**Search command:**\n```bash\n# Use WebSearch tool\nsite:github.com \"claude skill\" [topic]\nsite:github.com \"SKILL.md\" [topic]\n```\n\n### Step 4: Evaluate & Install\n\nWhen skill found:\n1. Check last update date (prefer recent)\n2. Review SKILL.md for quality\n3. Check if has scripts/references\n4. Install with skill-downloader or manual copy\n\n## MCP Server Search Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Identify Integration Need\n\nCommon patterns:\n- Database access → postgres, mysql, sqlite MCP\n- GitHub workflow → github MCP\n- Cloud services → AWS, GCP, Azure MCPs\n- Communication → slack, discord MCPs\n- File systems → filesystem MCP\n\n### Step 2: Search Official Sources\n\n**Primary:**\n- Official registry: `registry.modelcontextprotocol.io`\n- Official repo: `github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers`\n\n**Directories:**\n| Source | URL | Features |\n|--------|-----|----------|\n| Glama | glama.ai/mcp/servers | Stars, downloads, updates |\n| MCP Market | mcpmarket.com | Skills + MCP combined |\n| mcpservers.org | mcpservers.org | Categorized |\n| PulseMCP | pulsemcp.com/servers | Daily updates |\n| Smithery | smithery.ai | Registry/distribution |\n\n### Step 3: Search GitHub\n\n```bash\n# Use WebSearch tool\nsite:github.com \"mcp server\" [service]\nsite:github.com \"@modelcontextprotocol\" [service]\n```\n\n**Awesome lists:**\n- `github.com/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers`\n- `github.com/wong2/awesome-mcp-servers`\n\n### Step 4: Verify & Configure\n\nWhen MCP found:\n1. Check compatibility (stdio vs HTTP)\n2. Review required environment variables\n3. Test connection locally\n4. Add to `.claude/settings.json`\n\n## Search by Category\n\n### Development Tools\n```\nSkills: \"code review skill\", \"git commit skill\", \"testing skill\"\nMCP: \"github mcp\", \"gitlab mcp\", \"jira mcp\"\n```\n\n### Databases\n```\nSkills: \"database skill\", \"sql skill\", \"migration skill\"\nMCP: \"postgres mcp\", \"mysql mcp\", \"mongodb mcp\"\n```\n\n### Content & Marketing\n```\nSkills: \"content creator skill\", \"seo skill\", \"social media skill\"\nMCP: \"wordpress mcp\", \"notion mcp\"\n```\n\n### Cloud & DevOps\n```\nSkills: \"deployment skill\", \"kubernetes skill\", \"terraform skill\"\nMCP: \"aws mcp\", \"gcp mcp\", \"azure mcp\"\n```\n\n### AI & Data\n```\nSkills: \"data analysis skill\", \"ml skill\"\nMCP: \"openai mcp\", \"huggingface mcp\"\n```\n\n## Complete Source Reference\n\nSee [references/sources.md](references/sources.md) for full directory of all skill and MCP sources with detailed descriptions.\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Search before build** - Always check existing resources first\n2. **Prefer maintained** - Choose skills with recent updates\n3. **Check quality** - Review SKILL.md structure and content\n4. **Consider combining** - Multiple simple skills > one complex custom\n5. **Verify security** - Review MCP permissions and token scopes\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:30:05.088Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents like Claude Code, Cursor, and AutoGPT needing seamless MCP server and skill synchronization across platforms.","zh":"适合像 Claude Code、Cursor 和 AutoGPT 这样的 AI 代理，它们需要在各个平台上实现 MCP 服务器和技能的无缝同步。","ja":"Claude Code、Cursor、AutoGPT などの AI エージェントに適しており、MCP サーバーとスキルの同期をプラットフォーム間でシームレスに行う必要があります。","ko":"Claude Code, Cursor, AutoGPT와 같은 AI 에이전트에게 적합하며, 여러 플랫폼에서 MCP 서버와 스킬의 무결점 동기화를 필요로 합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA como Claude Code, Cursor y AutoGPT que necesitan una sincronización sin problemas del servidor MCP y las habilidades en varias plataformas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA comme Claude Code, Cursor et AutoGPT nécessitant une synchronisation transparente du serveur MCP et des compétences sur plusieurs plateformes.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents wie Claude Code, Cursor und AutoGPT, die eine nahtlose Synchronisierung des MCP-Servers und der Fähigkeiten auf verschiedenen Plattformen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes de IA como Claude Code, Cursor e AutoGPT que necessitam de sincronização sem interrupções do servidor MCP e de habilidades em várias plataformas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code, Cursor и AutoGPT, которым требуется бесперебойная синхронизация сервера MCP и навыков на разных платформах.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude Code و Cursor و AutoGPT الذين يحتاجون إلى تنسيق خادم MCP ومهارات بدون انقطاع عبر المنصات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to discover and sync existing Claude Code skills and MCP servers using web search, GitHub, and official repositories, streamlining development with a single config for all tools, including Model Context Protocol (MCP) and skills from skillhub.club and claudeskills.info.","zh":"赋予代理发现和同步现有的 Claude Code 技能和 MCP 服务器的能力，使用网页搜索、GitHub 和官方仓库，通过为所有工具（包括模型上下文协议（MCP）和来自 skillhub.club 和 claudeskills.info 的技能）提供单一配置来简化开发。","ja":"エージェントが Claude Code のスキルと MCP サーバーを検索して同期することを可能にし、Web 検索、GitHub、公式リポジトリを使用して開発を合理化します。一つの設定で Model Context Protocol (MCP) や skillhub.club と claudeskills.info からのスキルなどのすべてのツールに対応可能です。","ko":"에이전트가 기존의 Claude Code 스킬과 MCP 서버를 발견하고 동기화할 수 있도록 해줌으로써, 웹 검색, GitHub, 공식 저장소를 사용하여 개발을 간소화합니다. 모든 툴(모델 컨텍스트 프로토콜(MCP)와 skillhub.club 및 claudeskills.info의 스킬 등)에 대해 단일 설정을 제공합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes descubrir y sincronizar habilidades de Claude Code existentes y servidores MCP utilizando búsquedas web, GitHub y repositorios oficiales, simplificando el desarrollo con una sola configuración para todas las herramientas, incluyendo el Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo (MCP) y habilidades de skillhub.club y claudeskills.info.","fr":"Permet aux agents de découvrir et de synchroniser les compétences Claude Code existantes et les serveurs MCP en utilisant des recherches web, GitHub et des référentiels officiels, simplifiant le développement avec une seule configuration pour tous les outils, y compris le Protocole de Contexte de Modèle (MCP) et les compétences de skillhub.club et claudeskills.info.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, bestehende Claude Code-Fähigkeiten und MCP-Server mithilfe von Web-Suchen, GitHub und offiziellen Repositories zu entdecken und zu synchronisieren, und vereinfacht die Entwicklung mit einer einzigen Konfiguration für alle Tools, einschließlich des Modellkontextprotokolls (MCP) und Fähigkeiten von skillhub.club und claudeskills.info.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a descobrir e sincronizar habilidades existentes do Claude Code e servidores MCP usando pesquisa na web, GitHub e repositórios oficiais, simplificando o desenvolvimento com uma única configuração para todas as ferramentas, incluindo o Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo (MCP) e habilidades do skillhub.club e claudeskills.info.","ru":"Позволяет агентам обнаруживать и синхронизировать существующие навыки Claude Code и серверы MCP, используя веб-поиск, GitHub и официальные репозитории, упрощая разработку с помощью одной конфигурации для всех инструментов, включая Протокол контекста модели (MCP) и навыки с skillhub.club и claudeskills.info.","ar":"يُمكّن الوكلاء من اكتشاف ومزامنة مهارات كلود كود الحالية وخادم MCP باستخدام البحث على الويب وغيت هاب والمستودعات الرسمية، وبذلك يُبسط التطوير باستخدام تكوين واحد لجميع الأدوات، بما في ذلك بروتوكول سياق النموذج (MCP) والمهارات من skillhub.club و claudeskills.info."},"useCases":{"en":["Searching for existing Claude Code skills using site-specific web searches","Discovering MCP servers for integration with tools and services","Browsing skill repositories like awesome-claude-skills and official MCP server listings"],"zh":["使用站点特定的网页搜索来查找现有的 Claude Code 技能","发现 MCP 服务器以便与工具和服务集成","浏览技能仓库，如 awesome-claude-skills 和官方的 MCP 服务器列表"],"ja":["サイト固有の Web 検索を使用して既存の Claude Code スキルを検索する","ツールやサービスと統合するための MCP サーバーを検出する","スキル リポジトリ (awesome-claude-skills など) や公式の MCP サーバー リストを閲覧する"],"ko":["사이트별 웹 검색을 사용하여 기존의 Claude Code 스킬을 검색하는 것","도구와 서비스와의 통합을 위해 MCP 서버를 발견하는 것","스킬 저장소(awesome-claude-skills 등)나 공식 MCP 서버 목록을 브라우징하는 것"],"es":["Buscar habilidades de Claude Code existentes utilizando búsquedas web específicas del sitio","Descubrir servidores MCP para integrar con herramientas y servicios","Navegar por repositorios de habilidades como awesome-claude-skills y listados oficiales de servidores MCP"],"fr":["Rechercher des compétences Claude Code existantes en utilisant des recherches web spécifiques au site","Découvrir des serveurs MCP pour intégrer avec des outils et des services","Parcourir des référentiels de compétences comme awesome-claude-skills et des listes officielles de serveurs MCP"],"de":["Suchen nach bestehenden Claude Code-Fähigkeiten mithilfe von sitespezifischen Web-Suchen","Entdecken von MCP-Servern zur Integration mit Tools und Diensten","Durchsuchen von Fähigkeits-Repositories wie awesome-claude-skills und offiziellen MCP-Server-Listen"],"pt":["Pesquisar habilid