markdown 文件。","ja":"Hookify ルールは、パターンとメッセージを定義する markdown ファイルです。","ko":"Hookify 규칙은 패턴과 메시지를 정의하는 markdown 파일입니다.","es":"Las reglas Hookify son archivos markdown con YAML que definen patrones y mensajes para ZOE Solar Accounting OCR.","fr":"Les règles Hookify sont des fichiers markdown avec YAML qui définissent des modèles et des messages pour ZOE Solar Accounting OCR.","de":"Hookify-Regeln sind Markdown-Dateien mit YAML, die Muster und Nachrichten für ZOE Solar Accounting OCR definieren.","pt":"As regras do Hookify são arquivos markdown com frontmatter YAML que definem padrões para monitorar e mensagens para exibir quando esses padrões são detectados.","ru":"Правила Hookify представляют собой файлы markdown с YAML-frontend, которые определяют шаблоны для отслеживания и сообщения для отображения, когда эти шаблоны...","ar":"قواعد Hookify هي ملفات markdown مع YAML-frontend التي تعرف أنماطاً للمراقبة ورسائل لعرضها عند مطابقة هذه الأنماط","en":"ZOE Solar Accounting OCR"},"definition":{"en":"ZOE Solar Accounting OCR"},"features":{"zh":["基于 YAML 的前置格式","支持正则表达式模式","自定义显示消息","支持多种事件类型","存储在 `.claude` 目录中"],"ja":["YAML 前置形式を使用","正規表現パターンのサポート","カスタム表示メッセージ","複数のイベントタイプのサポート",".claude ディレクトリに保存"],"ko":["YAML 전위 형식을 사용","정규식 패턴 지원","사용자 정의 표시 메시지","여러 이벤트 유형 지원",".claude 디렉토리에 저장"],"es":["Archivos markdown con YAML","Definición de patrones y mensajes","Almacenamiento en `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md`","Compatibilidad con regex","Formato de mensaje con markdown","Soporte para eventos como bash, file, stop, prompt y all"],"fr":["Fichiers markdown avec YAML","Définition de modèles et de messages","Stockage dans `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md`","Compatibilité avec regex","Format de message avec markdown","Prise en charge d''événements tels que bash, file, stop, prompt et all"],"de":["Markdown-Dateien mit YAML","Definition von Mustern und Nachrichten","Speicherung in `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md`","Kompatibilität mit regex","Nachrichtenformat mit markdown","Unterstützung für Ereignisse wie bash, file, stop, prompt und all"],"pt":["Crie regras personalizadas para automatizar tarefas","Defina padrões para monitorar com expressões regulares","Exiba mensagens personalizadas quando os padrões são detectados","Armazene regras em arquivos markdown com frontmatter YAML","Habilite ou desabilite regras conforme necessário"],"ru":["Создавайте индивидуальные правила для автоматизации задач","Определите шаблоны для отслеживания с помощью регулярных выражений","Отображайте индивидуальные сообщения, когда шаблоны совпадают","Храните правила в файлах markdown с YAML-frontend","Включайте или выключайте правила по мере необходимости"],"ar":["أنشئ قواعد مخصصة لتحسين الإنتاجية","عرف أنماطاً للمراقبة باستخدام التعبيرات العادية","اعرض رسائل مخصصة عند مطابقة الأنماط","احفظ القواعد في ملفات markdown مع YAML-frontend","فعّل أو عطل القواعد حسب الحاجة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Hookify 规则","markdown 文件","YAML 前置格式","正则表达式","代码质量","开发效率"],"ja":["Hookify ルール","markdown ファイル","YAML 前置形式","正規表現","コード品質","開発効率"],"ko":["Hookify 규칙","markdown 파일","YAML 전위 형식","정규식","코드 품질","개발 효율"],"es":["reglas Hookify","ZOE Solar Accounting OCR","markdown","YAML","automatización","patrones","mensajes","regex","desarrollo"],"fr":["règles Hookify","ZOE Solar Accounting OCR","markdown","YAML","automatisation","modèles","messages","regex","développement"],"de":["Hookify-Regeln","ZOE Solar Accounting OCR","Markdown","YAML","Automatisierung","Muster","Nachrichten","regex","Entwicklung"],"pt":["Regras do Hookify","Automatização de tarefas","ZOE Solar Accounting OCR","Expressões regulares","Markdown","YAML","Produtividade","Eficiência"],"ru":["Правила Hookify","Автоматизация задач","ZOE Solar Accounting OCR","Регулярные выражения","Markdown","YAML","Производительность","Эффективность"],"ar":["قواعد Hookify","أتمتة المهام","ZOE Solar Accounting OCR","التعبيرات العادية","Markdown","YAML","الإنتاجية","الفعالية"]}},"owner":"Delqhi","repo":"ZOE-Solar-Accounting-OCR","repoPath":"Delqhi/ZOE-Solar-Accounting-OCR","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.409Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Writing Hookify Rules","description":"This skill should be used when the user asks to create a hookify rule, write a hook rule, configure hookify, add a hookify rule, or needs guidance on hookify rule syntax and patterns.","version":"0.1.0","bodyPreview":"# Writing Hookify Rules\n\n## Overview\n\nHookify rules are markdown files with YAML frontmatter that define patterns to watch for and messages to show when those patterns match. Rules are stored in `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md` files.\n\n## Rule File Format\n\n### Basic Structure\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: rule-identifier\nenabled: true\nevent: bash|file|stop|prompt|all\npattern: regex-pattern-here\n---\n\nMessage to show Claude when this rule triggers.\nCan include markdown formatting, warnings, suggest","body":"# Writing Hookify Rules\n\n## Overview\n\nHookify rules are markdown files with YAML frontmatter that define patterns to watch for and messages to show when those patterns match. Rules are stored in `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md` files.\n\n## Rule File Format\n\n### Basic Structure\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: rule-identifier\nenabled: true\nevent: bash|file|stop|prompt|all\npattern: regex-pattern-here\n---\n\nMessage to show Claude when this rule triggers.\nCan include markdown formatting, warnings, suggestions, etc.\n```\n\n### Frontmatter Fields\n\n**name** (required): Unique identifier for the rule\n- Use kebab-case: `warn-dangerous-rm`, `block-console-log`\n- Be descriptive and action-oriented\n- Start with verb: warn, prevent, block, require, check\n\n**enabled** (required): Boolean to activate/deactivate\n- `true`: Rule is active\n- `false`: Rule is disabled (won''t trigger)\n- Can toggle without deleting rule\n\n**event** (required): Which hook event to trigger on\n- `bash`: Bash tool commands\n- `file`: Edit, Write, MultiEdit tools\n- `stop`: When agent wants to stop\n- `prompt`: When user submits a prompt\n- `all`: All events\n\n**action** (optional): What to do when rule matches\n- `warn`: Show message but allow operation (default)\n- `block`: Prevent operation (PreToolUse) or stop session (Stop events)\n- If omitted, defaults to `warn`\n\n**pattern** (simple format): Regex pattern to match\n- Used for simple single-condition rules\n- Matches against command (bash) or new_text (file)\n- Python regex syntax\n\n**Example:**\n```yaml\nevent: bash\npattern: rm\\s+-rf\n```\n\n### Advanced Format (Multiple Conditions)\n\nFor complex rules with multiple conditions:\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: warn-env-file-edits\nenabled: true\nevent: file\nconditions:\n  - field: file_path\n    operator: regex_match\n    pattern: \\.env$\n  - field: new_text\n    operator: contains\n    pattern: API_KEY\n---\n\nYou''re adding an API key to a .env file. Ensure this file is in .gitignore!\n```\n\n**Condition fields:**\n- `field`: Which field to check\n  - For bash: `command`\n  - For file: `file_path`, `new_text`, `old_text`, `content`\n- `operator`: How to match\n  - `regex_match`: Regex pattern matching\n  - `contains`: Substring check\n  - `equals`: Exact match\n  - `not_contains`: Substring must NOT be present\n  - `starts_with`: Prefix check\n  - `ends_with`: Suffix check\n- `pattern`: Pattern or string to match\n\n**All conditions must match for rule to trigger.**\n\n## Message Body\n\nThe markdown content after frontmatter is shown to Claude when the rule triggers.\n\n**Good messages:**\n- Explain what was detected\n- Explain why it''s problematic\n- Suggest alternatives or best practices\n- Use formatting for clarity (bold, lists, etc.)\n\n**Example:**\n```markdown\n⚠️ **Console.log detected!**\n\nYou''re adding console.log to production code.\n\n**Why this matters:**\n- Debug logs shouldn''t ship to production\n- Console.log can expose sensitive data\n- Impacts browser performance\n\n**Alternatives:**\n- Use a proper logging library\n- Remove before committing\n- Use conditional debug builds\n```\n\n## Event Type Guide\n\n### bash Events\n\nMatch Bash command patterns:\n\n```markdown\n---\nevent: bash\npattern: sudo\\s+|rm\\s+-rf|chmod\\s+777\n---\n\nDangerous command detected!\n```\n\n**Common patterns:**\n- Dangerous commands: `rm\\s+-rf`, `dd\\s+if=`, `mkfs`\n- Privilege escalation: `sudo\\s+`, `su\\s+`\n- Permission issues: `chmod\\s+777`, `chown\\s+root`\n\n### file Events\n\nMatch Edit/Write/MultiEdit operations:\n\n```markdown\n---\nevent: file\npattern: console\\.log\\(|eval\\(|innerHTML\\s*=\n---\n\nPotentially problematic code pattern detected!\n```\n\n**Match on different fields:**\n```markdown\n---\nevent: file\nconditions:\n  - field: file_path\n    operator: regex_match\n    pattern: \\.tsx?$\n  - field: new_text\n    operator: regex_match\n    pattern: console\\.log\\(\n---\n\nConsole.log in TypeScript file!\n```\n\n**Common patterns:**\n- Debug code: `console\\.log\\(`, `debugger`, `print\\(`\n- Security risks: `eval\\(`, `innerHTML\\s*=`, `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`\n- Sensitive files: `\\.env$`, `credentials`, `\\.pem$`\n- Generated files: `node_modules/`, `dist/`, `build/`\n\n### stop Events\n\nMatch when agent wants to stop (completion checks):\n\n```markdown\n---\nevent: stop\npattern: .*\n---\n\nBefore stopping, verify:\n- [ ] Tests were run\n- [ ] Build succeeded\n- [ ] Documentation updated\n```\n\n**Use for:**\n- Reminders about required steps\n- Completion checklists\n- Process enforcement\n\n### prompt Events\n\nMatch user prompt content (advanced):\n\n```markdown\n---\nevent: prompt\nconditions:\n  - field: user_prompt\n    operator: contains\n    pattern: deploy to production\n---\n\nProduction deployment checklist:\n- [ ] Tests passing?\n- [ ] Reviewed by team?\n- [ ] Monitoring ready?\n```\n\n## Pattern Writing Tips\n\n### Regex Basics\n\n**Literal characters:** Most characters match themselves\n- `rm` matches \"rm\"\n- `console.log` matches \"console.log\"\n\n**Special characters need escaping:**\n- `.` (any char) → `\\.` (literal dot)\n- `(` `)` → `\\(` `\\)` (literal parens)\n- `[` `]` → `\\[` `\\]` (literal brackets)\n\n**Common metacharacters:**\n- `\\s` - whitespace (space, tab, newline)\n- `\\d` - digit (0-9)\n- `\\w` - word character (a-z, A-Z, 0-9, _)\n- `.` - any character\n- `+` - one or more\n- `*` - zero or more\n- `?` - zero or one\n- `|` - OR\n\n**Examples:**\n```\nrm\\s+-rf         Matches: rm -rf, rm  -rf\nconsole\\.log\\(   Matches: console.log(\n(eval|exec)\\(    Matches: eval( or exec(\nchmod\\s+777      Matches: chmod 777, chmod  777\nAPI_KEY\\s*=      Matches: API_KEY=, API_KEY =\n```\n\n### Testing Patterns\n\nTest regex patterns before using:\n\n```bash\npython3 -c \"import re; print(re.search(r''your_pattern'', ''test text''))\"\n```\n\nOr use online regex testers (regex101.com with Python flavor).\n\n### Common Pitfalls\n\n**Too broad:**\n```yaml\npattern: log    # Matches \"log\", \"login\", \"dialog\", \"catalog\"\n```\nBetter: `console\\.log\\(|logger\\.`\n\n**Too specific:**\n```yaml\npattern: rm -rf /tmp  # Only matches exact path\n```\nBetter: `rm\\s+-rf`\n\n**Escaping issues:**\n- YAML quoted strings: `\"pattern\"` requires double backslashes `\\\\s`\n- YAML unquoted: `pattern: \\s` works as-is\n- **Recommendation**: Use unquoted patterns in YAML\n\n## File Organization\n\n**Location:** All rules in `.claude/` directory\n**Naming:** `.claude/hookify.{descriptive-name}.local.md`\n**Gitignore:** Add `.claude/*.local.md` to `.gitignore`\n\n**Good names:**\n- `hookify.dangerous-rm.local.md`\n- `hookify.console-log.local.md`\n- `hookify.require-tests.local.md`\n- `hookify.sensitive-files.local.md`\n\n**Bad names:**\n- `hookify.rule1.local.md` (not descriptive)\n- `hookify.md` (missing .local)\n- `danger.local.md` (missing hookify prefix)\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Creating a Rule\n\n1. Identify unwanted behavior\n2. Determine which tool is involved (Bash, Edit, etc.)\n3. Choose event type (bash, file, stop, etc.)\n4. Write regex pattern\n5. Create `.claude/hookify.{name}.local.md` file in project root\n6. Test immediately - rules are read dynamically on next tool use\n\n### Refining a Rule\n\n1. Edit the `.local.md` file\n2. Adjust pattern or message\n3. Test immediately - changes take effect on next tool use\n\n### Disabling a Rule\n\n**Temporary:** Set `enabled: false` in frontmatter\n**Permanent:** Delete the `.local.md` file\n\n## Examples\n\nSee `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/examples/` for complete examples:\n- `dangerous-rm.local.md` - Block dangerous rm commands\n- `console-log-warning.local.md` - Warn about console.log\n- `sensitive-files-warning.local.md` - Warn about editing .env files\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n**Minimum viable rule:**\n```markdown\n---\nname: my-rule\nenabled: true\nevent: bash\npattern: dangerous_command\n---\n\nWarning message here\n```\n\n**Rule with conditions:**\n```markdown\n---\nname: my-rule\nenabled: true\nevent: file\nconditions:\n  - field: file_path\n    operator: regex_match\n    pattern: \\.ts$\n  - field: new_text\n    operator: contains\n    pattern: any\n---\n\nWarning message\n```\n\n**Event types:**\n- `bash` - Bash commands\n- `file` - File edits\n- `stop` - Completion checks\n- `prompt` - User input\n- `all` - All events\n\n**Field options:**\n- Bash: `command`\n- File: `file_path`, `new_text`, `old_text`, `content`\n- Prompt: `user_prompt`\n\n**Operators:**\n- `regex_match`, `contains`, `equals`, `not_contains`, `starts_with`, `ends_with`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:34:09.320Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Advanced AI Agents like Claude, needing customized event handling and notification capabilities through markdown-based Hookify rules.","zh":"非常适合像 Claude 这样的高级 AI 代理，需要通过基于 markdown 的 Hookify 规则自定义事件处理和通知功能。","ja":"Claude のような高度な AI エージェントに最適で、markdown ベースの Hookify ルールを使用したカスタム イベント ハンドリングと通知機能が必要です。","ko":"Claude 와 같은 고급 AI 에이전트에 적합하며, markdown 기반의 Hookify 규칙을 통해 사용자 지정 이벤트 처리 및 알림 기능이 필요합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA avanzados como Claude, que necesitan un manejo de eventos personalizado y capacidades de notificación a través de reglas de Hookify basadas en markdown.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''IA avancés comme Claude, nécessitant une gestion d''événements personnalisée et des capacités de notification via des règles Hookify basées sur markdown.","de":"Perfekt für erweiterte KI-Agents wie Claude, die ein benutzerdefiniertes Ereignishandling und Benachrichtigungsfunktionen über markdown-basierte Hookify-Regeln benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA Avançados como Claude, que necessitam de tratamento de eventos personalizados e capacidades de notificação por meio de regras baseadas em markdown do Hookify.","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых агентов ИИ, таких как Claude, требующих индивидуальной обработки событий и возможностей уведомления через правила Hookify на основе markdown.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكيل الذكي المتقدمة مثل Claude ، التي تحتاج إلى معالجة أحداث مخصصة وقدرات إشعار من خلال قواعد Hookify المعتمدة على markdown."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to define patterns and messages using YAML frontmatter and regex patterns, enabling tailored interactions through files stored in `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md` format, leveraging markdown formatting for dynamic notifications.","zh":"赋予代理定义使用 YAML 前置内容和正则表达式模式的模式和消息的能力，通过以 `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md` 格式存储的文件实现定制化的交互，利用 markdown 格式实现动态通知。","ja":"エージェントが YAML フロントマターと正則表現パターンを使用してパターンとメッセージを定義できるようにし、`.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md` 形式で保存されたファイルを介してカスタマイズされたインタラクションを可能にし、markdown フォーマットを使用して動的な通知を実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 YAML 프론트매터와 정규 표현식 패턴을 사용하여 패턴과 메시지를 정의할 수 있도록 하여, `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md` 형식으로 저장된 파일을 통해 사용자 지정된 상호 작용을 가능하게 하고, markdown 형식을 사용하여 동적 알림을 구현합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a definir patrones y mensajes utilizando frontmatter YAML y patrones de regex, lo que permite interacciones personalizadas a través de archivos almacenados en formato `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md`, aprovechando la formación de markdown para notificaciones dinámicas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de définir des modèles et des messages en utilisant le frontmatter YAML et des modèles de regex, ce qui permet des interactions personnalisées via des fichiers stockés au format `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md`, en exploitant la mise en forme markdown pour des notifications dynamiques.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Muster und Nachrichten mithilfe von YAML-Frontmatter und Regex-Mustern zu definieren, wodurch maßgeschneiderte Interaktionen durch Dateien im Format `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md` ermöglicht werden, die markdown-Formatierung für dynamische Benachrichtigungen nutzt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a definir padrões e mensagens usando frontmatter YAML e padrões regex, permitindo interações personalizadas por meio de arquivos armazenados no formato `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md`, utilizando formatação markdown para notificações dinâmicas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью определять шаблоны и сообщения с помощью YAML frontmatter и шаблонов regex, что позволяет создавать адаптированные взаимодействия через файлы, хранящиеся в формате `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md`, используя markdown-форматирование для динамических уведомлений.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من تعريف الأنماط والرسائل باستخدام YAML frontmatter ونماذج regex، مما يتيح تفاعلات مخصصة من خلال الملفات المخزنة في تنسيق `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md` ، باستخدام تنسيق markdown للتنبيهات الديناميكية."},"useCases":{"en":["Defining custom event handlers for bash, file, or prompt events","Creating notifications with markdown formatting for enhanced user experience","Developing regex patterns to match specific conditions and trigger targeted messages"],"zh":["定义用于 bash、文件或提示事件的自定义事件处理程序","使用 markdown 格式创建增强的用户体验的通知","开发正则表达式模式以匹配特定条件并触发目标消息"],"ja":["bash、ファイル、またはプロンプト イベント用のカスタム イベント ハンドラーを定義する","markdown フォーマットを使用して、ユーザー エクスペリエンスを強化する通知を作成する","特定の条件に一致し、ターゲット メッセージをトリガーする正則表現パターンを開発する"],"ko":["bash, 파일 또는 프롬프트 이벤트를 위한 사용자 지정 이벤트 핸들러를 정의하기","markdown 형식을 사용하여 사용자 경험을 향상시키는 알림을 생성하기","특정 조건과 일치하고 대상 메시지를 트리거하는 정규 표현식 패턴을 개발하기"],"es":["Definir controladores de eventos personalizados para eventos de bash, archivo o prompt","Crear notificaciones con formateo de markdown para una experiencia de usuario mejorada","Desarrollar patrones de regex para coincidir con condiciones específicas y desencadenar mensajes dirigidos"],"fr":["Définir des contrôleurs d''événements personnalisés pour les événements bash, fichier ou invite","Créer des notifications avec une mise en forme markdown pour une expérience utilisateur améliorée","Développer des modèles de regex pour correspondre à des conditions spécifiques et déclencher des messages ciblés"],"de":["Definieren von benutzerdefinierten Ereignishandlern für bash-, Datei- oder Prompt-Ereignisse","Erstellen von Benachrichtigungen mit markdown-Formatierung für eine verbesserte Benutzererfahrung","Entwickeln von Regex-Mustern, um bestimmte Bedingungen zu erfüllen und gezielte Nachrichten auszulösen"],"pt":["Definir manipuladores de eventos personalizados para eventos bash, arquivo ou prompt","Criar notificações com formatação markdown para experiência do usuário aprimorada","Desenvolver padrões regex para corresponder a condições específicas e acionar mensagens direcionadas"],"ru":["Определение индивидуальных обработчиков событий для событий bash, файла или приглашения","Создание уведомлений с форматированием markdown для улучшения пользовательского опыта","Разработка шаблонов regex для соответствия конкретным условиям и запуска целевых сообщений"],"ar":["تعريف معالجات أحداث مخصصة لأحداث bash أو ملف أو سطر الأوامر","إنشاء إشعارات بالتنسيق markdown لتحسين تجربة المستخدم","تطوير أنماط regex لتطابق الشروط المحددة وإرسال رسائل مستهدفة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of YAML frontmatter and regex patterns","Limited to `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md` file format","Dependent on agent''s ability to read and process markdown files"],"zh":["需要 YAML 前置内容和正则表达式模式的知识","仅限于 `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md` 文件格式","依赖于代理的 markdown 文件读取和处理能力"],"ja":["YAML フロントマターと正則表現パターンの知識が必要","`.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md` ファイル形式に限定される","エージェントの markdown ファイルの読み取りと処理能力に依存する"],"ko":["YAML 프론트매터와 정규 표현식 패턴에 대한 지식이 필요합니다","`.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md` 파일 형식으로 제한됩니다","에이전트의 markdown 파일 읽기 및 처리 능력에 의존합니다"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de frontmatter YAML y patrones de regex","Limitado al formato de archivo `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md`","Dependiente de la capacidad del agente para leer y procesar archivos de markdown"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances en frontmatter YAML et modèles de regex","Limité au format de fichier `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md`","Dépend de la capacité de l''agent à lire et traiter les fichiers markdown"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse von YAML-Frontmatter und Regex-Mustern","Begrenzt auf das Dateiformat `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md`","Abhängig von der Fähigkeit des Agents, markdown-Dateien zu lesen und zu verarbeiten"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento de frontmatter YAML e padrões regex","Limitado ao formato de arquivo `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md`","Dependente da capacidade do agente de ler e processar arquivos markdown"],"ru":["Требует знания YAML frontmatter и шаблонов regex","Ограничен форматом файла `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md`","Зависит от способности агента читать и обрабатывать файлы markdown"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة YAML frontmatter ونماذج regex","محدود بتنسيق ملف `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md`","يعتمد على قدرة الوكيل على قراءة ومعالجة ملفات markdown"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('opensesh/BOS-2.0/Writing Hookify Rules', 'community', 'opensesh', 'BOS-2.0', 'opensesh/BOS-2.0', 'Writing Hookify Rules', 0, 0, 85, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.409Z', '2026-02-18T03:33:56.843Z', NULL, '{"id":"opensesh/BOS-2.0/Writing Hookify Rules","name":"Writing Hookify Rules","description":{"zh":"Hookify 规则是用于定义模式和显示消息的 markdown 文件，通过 YAML 前置数据存储在 .claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md 文件中","ja":"Hookify ルールは、パターンとメッセージを定義するための markdown ファイルであり、YAML フロントマターを使用して .claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md ファイルに保存されます","ko":"Hookify 규칙은 패턴과 메시지를 정의하는 마크다운 파일로서 YAML 전면 데이터를 사용하여 .claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md 파일에 저장됩니다","es":"Las reglas Hookify permiten automatizar tareas en Brand Operating System 2.0 mediante patrones y mensajes personalizados.","fr":"Les règles Hookify permettent d''automatiser des tâches dans Brand Operating System 2.0 à l''aide de modèles et de messages personnalisés.","de":"Hookify-Regeln ermöglichen die Automatisierung von Aufgaben in Brand Operating System 2.0 mithilfe von Mustern und benutzerdefinierten Nachrichten.","pt":"O Hookify permite criar regras personalizadas para automatizar tarefas no Brand Operating System 2.0. Aprenda a escrever regras com markdown e YAML.","ru":"Hookify позволяет создавать индивидуальные правила для автоматизации задач в Brand Operating System 2.0. Узнайте, как писать правила с помощью markdown и YAML.","ar":"يسمح Hookify بإنشاء قواعد مخصصة لتأتمة المهام في Brand Operating System 2.0. تعلم كيفية كتابة القواعد باستخدام markdown و YAML.","en":"Brand Operating System 2.0 — A systems UI prototype application for AI-powered brand management, moving beyond Figma MCP toward code-first design infrastructure."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Hookify 规则编写","ja":"Hookify ルールの作成","ko":"Hookify 규칙 작성","es":"Crear Reglas Hookify para Gestión de Marcas","fr":"Écrire des Règles Hookify pour la Gestion de Marque","de":"Erstellen von Hookify-Regeln für Markenmanagement","pt":"Regras do Hookify: Automatize Tarefas com Markdown","ru":"Правила Hookify: Автоматизируйте задачи с помощью Markdown","ar":"قواعد Hookify: أوتوماتيك المهام باستخدام Markdown","en":"Writing Hookify Rules"},"description":{"zh":"Hookify 规则是用于定义模式和显示消息的 markdown 文件，通过 YAML 前置数据存储在 .claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md 文件中","ja":"Hookify ルールは、パターンとメッセージを定義するための markdown ファイルであり、YAML フロントマターを使用して .claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md ファイルに保存されます","ko":"Hookify 규칙은 패턴과 메시지를 정의하는 마크다운 파일로서 YAML 전면 데이터를 사용하여 .claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md 파일에 저장됩니다","es":"Las reglas Hookify permiten automatizar tareas en Brand Operating System 2.0 mediante patrones y mensajes personalizados.","fr":"Les règles Hookify permettent d''automatiser des tâches dans Brand Operating System 2.0 à l''aide de modèles et de messages personnalisés.","de":"Hookify-Regeln ermöglichen die Automatisierung von Aufgaben in Brand Operating System 2.0 mithilfe von Mustern und benutzerdefinierten Nachrichten.","pt":"O Hookify permite criar regras personalizadas para automatizar tarefas no Brand Operating System 2.0. Aprenda a escrever regras com markdown e YAML.","ru":"Hookify позволяет создавать индивидуальные правила для автоматизации задач в Brand Operating System 2.0. Узнайте, как писать правила с помощью markdown и YAML.","ar":"يسمح Hookify بإنشاء قواعد مخصصة لتأتمة المهام في Brand Operating System 2.0. تعلم كيفية كتابة القواعد باستخدام markdown و YAML.","en":"Brand Operating System 2.0 — A systems UI prototype application for AI-powered brand management, moving beyond Figma MCP toward code-first design infrastruct..."},"definition":{"en":"Brand Operating System 2.0 — A systems UI prototype application for AI-powered brand management, moving beyond Figma MCP toward code-first design infrastructure."},"features":{"zh":["支持 markdown 格式","使用 YAML 前置数据","定义模式和显示消息","存储在 .claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md 文件中","支持正则表达式模式"],"ja":["markdown 形式をサポート","YAML フロントマターを使用","パターンとメッセージを定義",".claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md ファイルに保存","正規表現パターンをサポート"],"ko":["마크다운 형식 지원","YAML 전면 데이터 사용","패턴과 메시지 정의",".claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md 파일에 저장","정규식 패턴 지원"],"es":["Automatización de tareas","Patrones personalizados","Mensajes personalizados","Compatibilidad con markdown","Almacenamiento en archivos .claude"],"fr":["Automatisation de tâches","Modèles personnalisés","Messages personnalisés","Compatibilité avec markdown","Stockage dans des fichiers .claude"],"de":["Automatisierung von Aufgaben","Benutzerdefinierte Muster","Benutzerdefinierte Nachrichten","Kompatibilität mit markdown","Speicherung in .claude-Dateien"],"pt":["Crie regras personalizadas com markdown e YAML","Automatize tarefas no Brand Operating System 2.0","Defina padrões e mensagens para exibir","Armazene regras em arquivos `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md`","Inclua formatação markdown e avisos nas mensagens"],"ru":["Создайте индивидуальные правила с помощью markdown и YAML","Автоматизируйте задачи в Brand Operating System 2.0","Определите шаблоны и сообщения для отображения","Храните правила в файлах `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md`","Включайте форматирование markdown и предупреждения в сообщениях"],"ar":["أنشئ قواعد مخصصة باستخدام markdown و YAML","أوتوماتيك المهام في Brand Operating System 2.0","عرف الأنماط والرسائل لعرضها","احفظ القواعد في ملفات `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md`","شمل التنسيق markdown والتحذيرات في الرسائل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Hookify 规则","代码管理","markdown 格式","YAML 前置数据","正则表达式模式","代码质量","开发效率"],"ja":["Hookify ルール","コード管理","markdown 形式","YAML フロントマター","正規表現パターン","コード品質","開発効率"],"ko":["Hookify 규칙","코드 관리","마크다운 형식","YAML 전면 데이터","정규식 패턴","코드 품질","개발 효율성"],"es":["reglas Hookify","gestión de marcas","automatización de tareas","patrones personalizados","mensajes personalizados","Brand Operating System 2.0","desarrollo de software","integración de AI"],"fr":["règles Hookify","gestion de marque","automatisation de tâches","modèles personnalisés","messages personnalisés","Brand Operating System 2.0","développement de logiciels","intégration de l''IA"],"de":["Hookify-Regeln","Markenmanagement","Automatisierung von Aufgaben","benutzerdefinierte Muster","benutzerdefinierte Nachrichten","Brand Operating System 2.0","Softwareentwicklung","KI-Integration"],"pt":["Hookify","Regras do Hookify","Automatizar tarefas","Brand Operating System 2.0","Markdown","YAML","Desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["Hookify","Правила Hookify","Автоматизация задач","Brand Operating System 2.0","Markdown","YAML","Разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["Hookify","قواعد Hookify","تأتمة المهام","Brand Operating System 2.0","Markdown","YAML","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"opensesh","repo":"BOS-2.0","repoPath":"opensesh/BOS-2.0","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.409Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Writing Hookify Rules","description":"This skill should be used when the user asks to create a hookify rule, write a hook rule, configure hookify, add a hookify rule, or needs guidance on hookify rule syntax and patterns.","version":"0.1.0","bodyPreview":"# Writing Hookify Rules\n\n## Overview\n\nHookify rules are markdown files with YAML frontmatter that define patterns to watch for and messages to show when those patterns match. Rules are stored in `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md` files.\n\n## Rule File Format\n\n### Basic Structure\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: rule-identifier\nenabled: true\nevent: bash|file|stop|prompt|all\npattern: regex-pattern-here\n---\n\nMessage to show Claude when this rule triggers.\nCan include markdown formatting, warnings, suggest","body":"# Writing Hookify Rules\n\n## Overview\n\nHookify rules are markdown files with YAML frontmatter that define patterns to watch for and messages to show when those patterns match. Rules are stored in `.claude/hookify.{rule-name}.local.md` files.\n\n## Rule File Format\n\n### Basic Structure\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: rule-identifier\nenabled: true\nevent: bash|file|stop|prompt|all\npattern: regex-pattern-here\n---\n\nMessage to show Claude when this rule triggers.\nCan include markdown formatting, warnings, suggestions, etc.\n```\n\n### Frontmatter Fields\n\n**name** (required): Unique identifier for the rule\n- Use kebab-case: `warn-dangerous-rm`, `block-console-log`\n- Be descriptive and action-oriented\n- Start with verb: warn, prevent, block, require, check\n\n**enabled** (required): Boolean to activate/deactivate\n- `true`: Rule is active\n- `false`: Rule is disabled (won''t trigger)\n- Can toggle without deleting rule\n\n**event** (required): Which hook event to trigger on\n- `bash`: Bash tool commands\n- `file`: Edit, Write, MultiEdit tools\n- `stop`: When agent wants to stop\n- `prompt`: When user submits a prompt\n- `all`: All events\n\n**action** (optional): What to do when rule matches\n- `warn`: Show message but allow operation (default)\n- `block`: Prevent operation (PreToolUse) or stop session (Stop events)\n- If omitted, defaults to `warn`\n\n**pattern** (simple format): Regex pattern to match\n- Used for simple single-condition rules\n- Matches against command (bash) or new_text (file)\n- Python regex syntax\n\n**Example:**\n```yaml\nevent: bash\npattern: rm\\s+-rf\n```\n\n### Advanced Format (Multiple Conditions)\n\nFor complex rules with multiple conditions:\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: warn-env-file-edits\nenabled: true\nevent: file\nconditions:\n  - field: file_path\n    operator: regex_match\n    pattern: \\.env$\n  - field: new_text\n    operator: contains\n    pattern: API_KEY\n---\n\nYou''re adding an API key to a .env file. Ensure this file is in .gitignore!\n```\n\n**Condition fields:**\n- `field`: Which field to check\n  - For bash: `command`\n  - For file: `file_path`, `new_text`, `old_text`, `content`\n- `operator`: How to match\n  - `regex_match`: Regex pattern matching\n  - `contains`: Substring check\n  - `equals`: Exact match\n  - `not_contains`: Substring must NOT be present\n  - `starts_with`: Prefix check\n  - `ends_with`: Suffix check\n- `pattern`: Pattern or string to match\n\n**All conditions must match for rule to trigger.**\n\n## Message Body\n\nThe markdown content after frontmatter is shown to Claude when the rule triggers.\n\n**Good messages:**\n- Explain what was detected\n- Explain why it''s problematic\n- Suggest alternatives or best practices\n- Use formatting for clarity (bold, lists, etc.)\n\n**Example:**\n```markdown\n⚠️ **Console.log detected!**\n\nYou''re adding console.log to production code.\n\n**Why this matters:**\n- Debug logs shouldn''t ship to production\n- Console.log can expose sensitive data\n- Impacts browser performance\n\n**Alternatives:**\n- Use a proper logging library\n- Remove before committing\n- Use conditional debug builds\n```\n\n## Event Type Guide\n\n### bash Events\n\nMatch Bash command patterns:\n\n```markdown\n---\nevent: bash\npattern: sudo\\s+|rm\\s+-rf|chmod\\s+777\n---\n\nDangerous command detected!\n```\n\n**Common patterns:**\n- Dangerous commands: `rm\\s+-rf`, `dd\\s+if=`, `mkfs`\n- Privilege escalation: `sudo\\s+`, `su\\s+`\n- Permission issues: `chmod\\s+777`, `chown\\s+root`\n\n### file Events\n\nMatch Edit/Write/MultiEdit operations:\n\n```markdown\n---\nevent: file\npattern: console\\.log\\(|eval\\(|innerHTML\\s*=\n---\n\nPotentially problematic code pattern detected!\n```\n\n**Match on different fields:**\n```markdown\n---\nevent: file\nconditions:\n  - field: file_path\n    operator: regex_match\n    pattern: \\.tsx?$\n  - field: new_text\n    operator: regex_match\n    pattern: console\\.log\\(\n---\n\nConsole.log in TypeScript file!\n```\n\n**Common patterns:**\n- Debug code: `console\\.log\\(`, `debugger`, `print\\(`\n- Security risks: `eval\\(`, `innerHTML\\s*=`, `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`\n- Sensitive files: `\\.env$`, `credentials`, `\\.pem$`\n- Generated files: `node_modules/`, `dist/`, `build/`\n\n### stop Events\n\nMatch when agent wants to stop (completion checks):\n\n```markdown\n---\nevent: stop\npattern: .*\n---\n\nBefore stopping, verify:\n- [ ] Tests were run\n- [ ] Build succeeded\n- [ ] Documentation updated\n```\n\n**Use for:**\n- Reminders about required steps\n- Completion checklists\n- Process enforcement\n\n### prompt Events\n\nMatch user prompt content (advanced):\n\n```markdown\n---\nevent: prompt\nconditions:\n  - field: user_prompt\n    operator: contains\n    pattern: deploy to production\n---\n\nProduction deployment checklist:\n- [ ] Tests passing?\n- [ ] Reviewed by team?\n- [ ] Monitoring ready?\n```\n\n## Pattern Writing Tips\n\n### Regex Basics\n\n**Literal characters:** Most characters match themselves\n- `rm` matches \"rm\"\n- `console.log` matches \"console.log\"\n\n**Special characters need escaping:**\n- `.` (any char) → `\\.` (literal dot)\n- `(` `)` → `\\(` `\\)` (literal parens)\n- `[` `]` → `\\[` `\\]` (literal brackets)\n\n**Common metacharacters:**\n- `\\s` - whitespace (space, tab, newline)\n- `\\d` - digit (0-9)\n- `\\w` - word character (a-z, A-Z, 0-9, _)\n- `.` - any character\n- `+` - one or more\n- `*` - zero or more\n- `?` - zero or one\n- `|` - OR\n\n**Examples:**\n```\nrm\\s+-rf         Matches: rm -rf, rm  -rf\nconsole\\.log\\(   Matches: console.log(\n(eval|exec)\\(    Matches: eval( or exec(\nchmod\\s+777      Matches: chmod 777, chmod  777\nAPI_KEY\\s*=      Matches: API_KEY=, API_KEY =\n```\n\n### Testing Patterns\n\nTest regex patterns before using:\n\n```bash\npython3 -c \"import re; print(re.search(r''your_pattern'', ''test text''))\"\n```\n\nOr use online regex testers (regex101.com with Python flavor).\n\n### Common Pitfalls\n\n**Too broad:**\n```yaml\npattern: log    # Matches \"log\", \"login\", \"dialog\", \"catalog\"\n```\nBetter: `console\\.log\\(|logger\\.`\n\n**Too specific:**\n```yaml\npattern: rm -rf /tmp  # Only matches exact path\n```\nBetter: `rm\\s+-rf`\n\n**Escaping issues:**\n- YAML quoted strings: `\"pattern\"` requires double backslashes `\\\\s`\n- YAML unquoted: `pattern: \\s` works as-is\n- **Recommendation**: Use unquoted patterns in YAML\n\n## File Organization\n\n**Location:** All rules in `.claude/` directory\n**Naming:** `.claude/hookify.{descriptive-name}.local.md`\n**Gitignore:** Add `.claude/*.local.md` to `.gitignore`\n\n**Good names:**\n- `hookify.dangerous-rm.local.md`\n- `hookify.console-log.local.md`\n- `hookify.require-tests.local.md`\n- `hookify.sensitive-files.local.md`\n\n**Bad names:**\n- `hookify.rule1.local.md` (not descriptive)\n- `hookify.md` (missing .local)\n- `danger.local.md` (missing hookify prefix)\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Creating a Rule\n\n1. Identify unwanted behavior\n2. Determine which tool is involved (Bash, Edit, etc.)\n3. Choose event type (bash, file, stop, etc.)\n4. Write regex pattern\n5. Create `.claude/hookify.{name}.local.md` file in project root\n6. Test immediately - rules are read dynamically on next tool use\n\n### Refining a Rule\n\n1. Edit the `.local.md` file\n2. Adjust pattern or message\n3. Test immediately - changes take effect on next tool use\n\n### Disabling a Rule\n\n**Temporary:** Set `enabled: false` in frontmatter\n**Permanent:** Delete the `.local.md` file\n\n## Examples\n\nSee `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/examples/` for complete examples:\n- `dangerous-rm.local.md` - Block dangerous rm commands\n- `console-log-warning.local.md` - Warn about console.log\n- `sensitive-files-warning.local.md` - Warn about editing .env files\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n**Minimum viable rule:**\n```markdown\n---\nname: my-rule\nenabled: true\nevent: bash\npattern: dangerous_command\n---\n\nWarning message here\n```\n\n**Rule with conditions:**\n```markdown\n---\nname: my-rule\nenabled: true\nevent: file\nconditions:\n  - field: file_path\n    operator: regex_match\n    pattern: \\.ts$\n  - field: new_text\n    operator: contains\n    pattern: any\n---\n\nWarning message\n```\n\n**Event types:**\n- `bash` - Bash commands\n- `file` - File edits\n- `stop` - Completion checks\n- `prompt` - User input\n- `all` - All events\n\n**Field options:**\n- Bash: `command`\n- File: `file_path`, `new_text`, `old_text`, `content`\n- Prompt: `user_prompt`\n\n**Operators:**\n- `regex_match`, `contains`, `equals`, `not_contains`, `starts_with`, `ends_with`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:33:56.843Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents like Claude, AutoGPT, and LangChain needing custom event-driven messaging capabilities.","zh":"非常适合Claude、AutoGPT和LangChain等需要自定义事件驱动消息能力的AI代理。","ja":"Claude、AutoGPT、LangChainなどのカスタムイベント駆動メッセージ機能を必要とするAIエージェントに最適です。","ko":"Claude, AutoGPT, LangChain 등의 이벤트 驱动 메시지 기능을 필요로 하는 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA como Claude, AutoGPT y LangChain que necesitan capacidades de mensajería personalizadas basadas en eventos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA comme Claude, AutoGPT et LangChain ayant besoin de capacités de messagerie personnalisées basées sur les événements.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agenten wie Claude, AutoGPT und LangChain, die benutzerdefinierte ereignisgesteuerte Messaging-Funktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes de IA como Claude, AutoGPT e LangChain que necessitam de capacidades de mensagens personalizadas baseadas em eventos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude, AutoGPT и LangChain, требующих настраиваемых возможностей обмена сообщениями, основанных на событиях.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude و AutoGPT و LangChain الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات رسائل مخصصة مدفوعة بالأحداث."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to define patterns and messages using markdown files with YAML frontmatter, leveraging regex patterns and event triggers like bash, file, stop, prompt, or all, to display customized messages.","zh":"赋予代理定义使用Markdown文件和YAML前置内容的模式和消息的能力，利用正则表达式模式和事件触发器，如bash、文件、停止、提示或全部，来显示自定义消息。","ja":"エージェントがマークダウンファイルとYAMLフロントマターを使用してパターンとメッセージを定義する能力を提供します。正規表現パターンとイベントトリガー（bash、ファイル、停止、プロンプト、またはすべて）を利用して、カスタムメッセージを表示します。","ko":"에이전트가 마크다운 파일과 YAML 전면 물질을 사용하여 패턴과 메시지를 정의 할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다. 정규 표현식 패턴과 이벤트 트리거 (bash, 파일, 중지, 프롬프트 또는 모든)를 사용하여 사용자 지정 메시지를 표시합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes definir patrones y mensajes utilizando archivos markdown con frontmatter YAML, aprovechando patrones regex y desencadenadores de eventos como bash, archivo, detener, prompt o todos, para mostrar mensajes personalizados.","fr":"Permet aux agents de définir des modèles et des messages en utilisant des fichiers markdown avec frontmatter YAML, en exploitant des modèles regex et des déclencheurs d''événements tels que bash, fichier, arrêter, invite ou tous, pour afficher des messages personnalisés.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Muster und Nachrichten mithilfe von Markdown-Dateien mit YAML-Frontmatter zu definieren, indem Regex-Muster und Ereignisauslöser wie bash, Datei, Stop, Prompt oder alle verwendet werden, um benutzerdefinierte Nachrichten anzuzeigen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a definir padrões e mensagens usando arquivos markdown com frontmatter YAML, aproveitando padrões regex e gatilhos de eventos como bash, arquivo, parar, prompt ou todos, para exibir mensagens personalizadas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью определять шаблоны и сообщения, используя файлы markdown с YAML-заголовком, используя шаблоны regex и триггеры событий, такие как bash, файл, остановка, приглашение или все, для отображения настраиваемых сообщений.","ar":"يتمكن العميل من تعريف الأنماط والرسائل باستخدام ملفات markdown مع YAML frontmatter، واستخدام أنماط regex ومحفزات الأحداث مثل bash وملف وايقاف وتنبيه أو جميعها، لعرض رسائل مخصصة."},"useCases":{"en":["Defining event-driven messages for AI-powered brand management","Creating custom rules for code-first design infrastructure","Triggering messages based on regex patterns in markdown files"],"zh":["为AI驱动的品牌管理定义事件驱动消息","为代码优先设计基础设施创建自定义规则","在Markdown文件中基于正则表达式模式触发消息"],"ja":["AI駆動のブランド管理のためのイベント駆動メッセージの定義","コードファースト設計インフラストラクチャのためのカスタムルールの作成","マークダウンファイル内の正規表現パターンに基づいてメッセージをトリガーする"],"ko":["AI 구동 브랜드 관리를 위한 이벤트 驱动 메시지 정의","코드 우선 설계 인프라를 위한 사용자 지정 규칙 생성","마크다운 파일 내의 정규식 패턴을 기반으로 메시지 트리거"],"es":["Definir mensajes basados en eventos para la gestión de marcas impulsada por IA","Crear reglas personalizadas para infraestructuras de diseño de código","Desencadenar mensajes en función de patrones regex en archivos markdown"],"fr":["Définir des messages basés sur les événements pour la gestion de marques propulsée par l''IA","Créer des règles personnalisées pour les infrastructures de conception de code","Déclencher des messages en fonction de modèles regex dans des fichiers markdown"],"de":["Ereignisgesteuerte Nachrichten für die KI-gestützte Markenverwaltung definieren","Benutzerdefinierte Regeln für Code-First-Design-Infrastrukturen erstellen","Nachrichten basierend auf Regex-Mustern in Markdown-Dateien auslösen"],"pt":["Definir mensagens baseadas em eventos para gerenciamento de marca impulsionado por IA","Criar regras personalizadas para infraestrutura de design code-first","Acionar mensagens com base em padrões regex em arquivos markdown"],"ru":["Определение сообщений, основанных на событиях, для управления брендом, основанным на ИИ","Создание пользовательских правил для инфраструктуры code-first","Активация сообщений на основе шаблонов regex в файлах markdown"],"ar":["تعريف رسائل مدفوعة بالأحداث لإدارة العلامة التجارية التي ي驱ها الذكاء الاصطناعي","إنشاء قواعد مخصصة للبنية التحتية لتصميم الكود أولاً","تشغيل الرسائل بناءً على الأنماط regex في ملفات markdown"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires .claude directory for rule storage","Markdown files with YAML frontmatter for rule definition","Regex pattern knowledge for effective pattern matching"],"zh":["需要.claude目录用于规则存储","需要Markdown文件和YAML前置内容用于规则定义","需要正则表达式知识才能有效地匹配模式"],"ja":["ルールストレージに.claudeディレクトリが必要","ルール定義にマークダウンファイルとYAMLフロントマターが必要","パターンを効果的にマッチングするには正規表現の知識が必要"],"ko":["규칙 저장을 위한 .claude 디렉토리가 필요함","규칙 정의를 위한 마크다운 파일과 YAML 전면 물질이 필요함","패턴을 효과적으로 일치시키기 위해 정규식 지식이 필요함"],"es":["Requiere un directorio .claude para el almacenamiento de reglas","Archivos markdown con frontmatter YAML para la definición de reglas","Conocimiento de patrones regex para la coincidencia de patrones efectiva"],"fr":["Nécessite un répertoire .claude pour le stockage des règles","Fichiers markdown avec frontmatter YAML pour la définition des règles","Connaissance des modèles regex pour une correspondance de modèles efficace"],"de":["Benötigt ein .claude-Verzeichnis für die Speicherung von Regeln","Markdown-Dateien mit YAML-Frontmatter für die Regeldéfinition","Kenntnisse von Regex-Mustern für eine effektive Musterabgleich"],"pt":["Requer diretório .claude para armazenamento de regras","Arquivos markdown com frontmatter YAML para definição de regras","Conhecimento de padrões regex para correspondência de padrões eficaz"],"ru":["Требуется目录 .claude для хранения правил","Файлы markdown с YAML-заголовком для определения правил","Знание шаблонов regex для эффективного сопоставления шаблонов"],"ar":["يتطلب ملف .claude لتخزين القواعد","ملفات markdown مع YAML frontmatter لتعريف القواعد","معرفة أنماط regex للمطابقة الفعالة للنماط"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":85}');
