ル構成と委任パターンのサポート","エージェント呼び出しの問題のトラブルシューティングを支援","既存のエージェントのパフォーマンスを改善"],"ko":["Claude Code 서브 에이전트의 생성 및 관리","에이전트 설계 및 시스템 프롬프트 엔지니어링에 대한 전문가 지침 제공","도구 구성 및 위임 패턴 지원","에이전트 호출 문제의 문제 해결을支援","既存 에이전트의 성능을 개선"],"es":["Diseño de agentes experto","Ingeniería de prompts de sistema","Configuración de herramientas","Patrones de delegación","Solución de problemas de invocación de agentes"],"fr":["Conception d''agents experte","Ingénierie de prompts de système","Configuration d''outils","Modèles de délégation","Dépannage des problèmes d''invocation d''agents"],"de":["Experten-Design für Agenten","System-Prompt-Engineering","Tool-Konfiguration","Delegationsmuster","Fehlerbehebung bei Agenten-Aufrufen"],"pt":["Orientação especializada em design de agente","Engenharia de prompts de sistema","Configuração de ferramentas","Padrões de delegação","Criação e melhoria de subagentes"],"ru":["Экспертные рекомендации по проектированию агентов","Инженерия системных подсказок","Настройка инструментов","Паттерны делегирования","Создание и улучшение субагентов"],"ar":["توجيه متخصص في تصميم الوكيل","هندسة الإشارات النصية للنظام","تكوين الأدوات","أنماط التفويض","إنشاء وتحسين الوكلاء الفرعيين"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI 代理","Claude Code","子代理","代理设计","系统提示工程","工具配置","委托模式","AI 编码工具"],"ja":["AI エージェント","Claude Code","サブエージェント","エージェント設計","システムプロンプトエンジニアリング","ツール構成","委任パターン","AI コーディング ツール"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","Claude Code","서브 에이전트","에이전트 설계","시스템 프롬프트 엔지니어링","도구 구성","위임 패턴","AI 코딩 도구"],"es":["constructor de agentes","herramientas de codificación AI","subagentes de Claude Code","diseño de agentes","configuración de sistemas","patrones de delegación"],"fr":["constructeur d''agents","outils de codage IA","sous-agents de Claude Code","conception d''agents","configuration de systèmes","modèles de délégation"],"de":["Agenten-Builder","KI-Coding-Tools","Subagenten von Claude Code","Agenten-Design","Systemkonfiguration","Delegationsmuster"],"pt":["Construtor de Agentes","Ferramenta de registro universal","Ferramentas de codificação de IA","Desenvolvimento de subagentes","Engenharia de prompts de sistema","Configuração de ferramentas"],"ru":["Построитель агентов","Универсальный реестр","Инструменты кодирования ИИ","Разработка субагентов","Инженерия системных подсказок","Настройка инструментов"],"ar":["بناء الوكيل","السجل الشامل","أدوات البرمجة الإصطناعية","تطوير الوكلاء الفرعيين","هندسة الإشارات النصية للنظام","تكوين الأدوات"]}},"owner":"pr-pm","repo":"prpm","repoPath":"pr-pm/prpm","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.410Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"agent-builder","description":"Use when creating, improving, or troubleshooting Claude Code subagents. Expert guidance on agent design, system prompts, tool access, model selection, and best practices for building specialized AI assistants.","bodyPreview":"# Agent Builder - Claude Code Subagent Expert\n\nUse this skill when creating, improving, or troubleshooting Claude Code subagents. Provides expert guidance on agent design, system prompt engineering, tool configuration, and delegation patterns.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nActivate this skill when:\n- User asks to create a new subagent\n- User wants to improve an existing agent\n- User needs help with agent configuration or tool access\n- User is troubleshooting agent invocation issues\n- User wants to","body":"# Agent Builder - Claude Code Subagent Expert\n\nUse this skill when creating, improving, or troubleshooting Claude Code subagents. Provides expert guidance on agent design, system prompt engineering, tool configuration, and delegation patterns.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nActivate this skill when:\n- User asks to create a new subagent\n- User wants to improve an existing agent\n- User needs help with agent configuration or tool access\n- User is troubleshooting agent invocation issues\n- User wants to understand when to use agents vs skills vs commands\n- User asks about agent chaining or delegation patterns\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Agent File Structure\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: agent-name\ndescription: When and why to use this agent\ntools: Read, Write, Bash(git *)\nmodel: sonnet\n---\n\nYour detailed system prompt defining:\n- Agent role and expertise\n- Problem-solving approach\n- Output format expectations\n- Specific constraints or requirements\n```\n\n### File Locations\n\n**Project agents** (shared with team, highest priority):\n```\n.claude/agents/my-agent.md\n```\n\n**Personal agents** (individual use, lower priority):\n```\n~/.claude/agents/my-agent.md\n```\n\n**Plugin agents** (from installed plugins):\n```\n<plugin-dir>/agents/agent-name.md\n```\n\n## Creating Effective Subagents\n\n### Step 1: Identify the Use Case\n\n**Good candidates for subagents:**\n- Complex, multi-step workflows\n- Specialized expertise (debugging, security review, data analysis)\n- Tasks requiring focused context\n- Repeatable processes with specific quality bars\n- Code review and analysis workflows\n\n**NOT good for subagents (use Skills/Commands instead):**\n- Simple one-off prompts (use Slash Commands)\n- Context-aware automatic activation (use Skills)\n- Quick transformations or formatting\n\n### Step 2: Design Agent Scope\n\n**Best practices:**\n- **Single responsibility** - Each agent does ONE thing exceptionally well\n- **Clear boundaries** - Define what''s in/out of scope\n- **Specific expertise** - Don''t create \"general helper\" agents\n- **Measurable outcomes** - Agent should produce concrete deliverables\n\n**Examples:**\n- ✅ **code-reviewer** - Reviews code changes for quality, security, and best practices\n- ✅ **debugger** - Root cause analysis and minimal fixes for errors\n- ✅ **data-scientist** - SQL query optimization and data analysis\n- ❌ **helper** - Too vague, no clear scope\n- ❌ **everything** - Defeats purpose of specialization\n\n### Step 3: Write the System Prompt\n\nThe system prompt is the most critical part of your agent. It defines the agent''s personality, capabilities, and approach.\n\n**Structure for effective prompts:**\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: code-reviewer\ndescription: Analyzes code changes for quality, security, and maintainability\ntools: Read, Grep, Bash(git *)\nmodel: sonnet\n---\n\n# Code Reviewer Agent\n\nYou are an expert code reviewer specializing in [language/framework].\n\n## Your Role\n\nReview code changes thoroughly for:\n1. Code quality and readability\n2. Security vulnerabilities\n3. Performance issues\n4. Best practices adherence\n5. Test coverage\n\n## Review Process\n\n1. **Read the changes**\n   - Get recent git diff or specified files\n   - Understand the context and purpose\n\n2. **Analyze systematically**\n   - Check each category (quality, security, performance, etc.)\n   - Provide specific file:line references\n   - Explain why something is an issue\n\n3. **Provide actionable feedback**\n   Format:\n   ### 🔴 Critical Issues\n   - [Issue] (file.ts:42) - [Explanation] - [Fix]\n\n   ### 🟡 Suggestions\n   - [Improvement] (file.ts:67) - [Rationale] - [Recommendation]\n\n   ### ✅ Good Practices\n   - [What was done well]\n\n4. **Summarize**\n   - Overall assessment\n   - Top 3 priorities\n   - Approval status (approve, approve with comments, request changes)\n\n## Quality Standards\n\n**Code must:**\n- [ ] Follow language/framework conventions\n- [ ] Have proper error handling\n- [ ] Include necessary tests\n- [ ] Not expose secrets or sensitive data\n- [ ] Use appropriate abstractions (not over-engineered)\n\n**Flag immediately:**\n- SQL injection risks\n- XSS vulnerabilities\n- Hardcoded credentials\n- Memory leaks\n- O(n²) or worse algorithms in hot paths\n\n## Output Format\n\nAlways provide:\n1. Summary (1-2 sentences)\n2. Categorized findings with file:line refs\n3. Approval decision\n4. Top 3 action items\n\nBe thorough but concise. Focus on what matters.\n```\n\n### Step 4: Configure Tools Access\n\n**Available tools:**\n- `Read` - Read files\n- `Write` - Create new files\n- `Edit` - Modify existing files\n- `Bash` - Execute shell commands\n- `Grep` - Search file contents\n- `Glob` - Find files by pattern\n- `WebFetch` - Fetch web content\n- `WebSearch` - Search the web\n- Plus any connected MCP tools\n\n**Tool configuration patterns:**\n\n**Inherit all tools** (omit `tools` field):\n```yaml\n---\nname: full-access-agent\ndescription: Agent needs access to everything\n# No tools field = inherits all\n---\n```\n\n**Specific tools only**:\n```yaml\n---\nname: read-only-reviewer\ndescription: Reviews code without making changes\ntools: Read, Grep, Bash(git *)\n---\n```\n\n**Bash with restrictions**:\n```yaml\n---\nname: git-helper\ndescription: Git operations only\ntools: Bash(git *), Read\n---\n```\n\n**Security best practice:** Grant minimum necessary tools. Don''t give `Write` or `Bash` unless required.\n\n### Step 5: Choose Model\n\n**Model options:**\n- `sonnet` - Balanced, good for most agents (default)\n- `opus` - Complex reasoning, architectural decisions\n- `haiku` - Fast, simple tasks (formatting, quick checks)\n- `inherit` - Use main conversation''s model\n\n**When to use each:**\n\n**Sonnet (most agents):**\n```yaml\nmodel: sonnet\n```\n- Code review\n- Debugging\n- Data analysis\n- General problem-solving\n\n**Opus (complex reasoning):**\n```yaml\nmodel: opus\n```\n- Architecture decisions\n- Complex refactoring\n- Deep security analysis\n- Novel problem-solving\n\n**Haiku (speed matters):**\n```yaml\nmodel: haiku\n```\n- Syntax checks\n- Simple formatting\n- Quick validations\n- Low-latency needs\n\n**Inherit (context-dependent):**\n```yaml\nmodel: inherit\n```\n- Agent should match user''s model choice\n- Cost sensitivity\n\n### Step 6: Write Clear Description\n\nThe `description` field determines when Claude invokes your agent automatically.\n\n**Best practices:**\n- Start with \"Use when...\" or \"Analyzes...\" or \"Helps with...\"\n- Be specific about the agent''s domain\n- Mention key capabilities\n- Include when NOT to use (if helpful)\n\n**Examples:**\n\n✅ **Good descriptions:**\n```yaml\ndescription: Analyzes code changes for quality, security, and maintainability issues\ndescription: Use when debugging errors - performs root cause analysis and suggests minimal fixes\ndescription: Helps with SQL query optimization and data analysis tasks\n```\n\n❌ **Poor descriptions:**\n```yaml\ndescription: A helpful agent  # Too vague\ndescription: Does code stuff  # Not specific enough\ndescription: Reviews, debugs, refactors, tests, documents, and deploys code  # Too broad\n```\n\n## Agent Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Code Reviewer\n\n**Purpose:** Systematic code review with quality gates\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: code-reviewer\ndescription: Reviews code changes for quality, security, performance, and best practices\ntools: Read, Grep, Bash(git *)\nmodel: sonnet\n---\n\n# Code Reviewer\n\nExpert code reviewer for [your tech stack].\n\n## Review Categories\n\n### 1. Code Quality (0-10)\n- Readability and clarity\n- Naming conventions\n- Function/class size\n- Comments and documentation\n\n### 2. Security (0-10)\n- Input validation\n- SQL injection risks\n- XSS vulnerabilities\n- Secrets exposure\n- Authentication/authorization\n\n### 3. Performance (0-10)\n- Algorithm efficiency\n- Resource usage\n- Caching strategy\n- Database queries\n\n### 4. Testing (0-10)\n- Test coverage\n- Edge cases\n- Integration tests\n- Test quality\n\n## Process\n\n1. Get changes: `git diff main...HEAD`\n2. Review each file systematically\n3. Score each category\n4. Provide specific file:line feedback\n5. Recommend: Approve | Approve with comments | Request changes\n\n## Output Template\n\n**Overall: X/40**\n\n### Critical Issues (must fix)\n- [Issue] (file:line) - [Why] - [How to fix]\n\n### Suggestions (should fix)\n- [Improvement] (file:line) - [Rationale]\n\n### Positive Notes\n- [What was done well]\n\n**Decision:** [Approve/Approve with comments/Request changes]\n**Top 3 Priorities:**\n1. [Action]\n2. [Action]\n3. [Action]\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Debugger\n\n**Purpose:** Root cause analysis and targeted fixes\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: debugger\ndescription: Specializes in root cause analysis and minimal fixes for bugs and errors\ntools: Read, Edit, Bash, Grep\nmodel: sonnet\n---\n\n# Debugger Agent\n\nExpert at finding and fixing bugs through systematic analysis.\n\n## Debugging Process\n\n### 1. Capture Context\n- What error/unexpected behavior occurred?\n- Error messages and stack traces\n- Steps to reproduce\n- Expected vs actual behavior\n\n### 2. Isolate the Problem\n- Read relevant files\n- Trace execution path\n- Identify failure point\n- Determine root cause (not just symptoms)\n\n### 3. Minimal Fix\n- Fix the root cause, not symptoms\n- Make smallest change that works\n- Don''t refactor unrelated code\n- Preserve existing behavior\n\n### 4. Verify\n- How to test the fix\n- Edge cases to check\n- Potential side effects\n\n## Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n❌ Fixing symptoms instead of root cause\n❌ Large refactoring during debugging\n❌ Adding features while fixing bugs\n❌ Changing working code unnecessarily\n\n## Output Format\n\n**Root Cause:** [Clear explanation]\n\n**Location:** file.ts:line\n\n**Fix:** [Minimal code change]\n\n**Verification:** [How to test]\n\n**Side Effects:** [Potential impacts]\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Data Scientist\n\n**Purpose:** SQL optimization and data analysis\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: data-scientist\ndescription: Optimizes SQL queries and performs data analysis with cost-awareness\ntools: Read, Write, Bash, WebSearch\nmodel: sonnet\n---\n\n# Data Scientist Agent\n\nExpert in SQL optimization and data analysis.\n\n## SQL Query Guidelines\n\n### Performance\n- Always include WHERE clauses with indexed columns\n- Use appropriate JOINs (avoid cartesian products)\n- Limit result sets with LIMIT\n- Use EXPLAIN to verify query plans\n\n### Cost Awareness\n- Estimate query cost before running\n- Prefer indexed lookups over full table scans\n- Use materialized views for expensive aggregations\n- Sample large datasets when appropriate\n\n### Best Practices\n- Use CTEs for readability\n- Parameterize queries (prevent SQL injection)\n- Document complex queries\n- Format for readability\n\n## Analysis Process\n\n1. **Understand the question**\n   - What insights are needed?\n   - What''s the business context?\n\n2. **Design query**\n   - Choose appropriate tables\n   - Apply necessary filters\n   - Optimize for performance\n\n3. **Run and validate**\n   - Check results make sense\n   - Verify data quality\n   - Note any anomalies\n\n4. **Present findings**\n   - Summary (key insights)\n   - Visualizations (if helpful)\n   - Recommendations\n   - Query for reproducibility\n\n## Output Template\n\n**Question:** [What we''re analyzing]\n\n**Query:**\n\\`\\`\\`sql\n-- [Comment explaining approach]\nSELECT ...\nFROM ...\nWHERE ...\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n**Results:** [Summary]\n\n**Insights:**\n- [Key finding 1]\n- [Key finding 2]\n- [Key finding 3]\n\n**Recommendations:** [Data-driven suggestions]\n\n**Cost Estimate:** [Expected query cost]\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: Test Generator\n\n**Purpose:** Generate comprehensive test suites\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: test-generator\ndescription: Generates comprehensive test cases covering happy path, edge cases, and errors\ntools: Read, Write\nmodel: sonnet\n---\n\n# Test Generator Agent\n\nGenerates thorough test suites for code.\n\n## Test Coverage Strategy\n\n### 1. Happy Path (40%)\n- Normal inputs\n- Expected outputs\n- Standard workflows\n- Common use cases\n\n### 2. Edge Cases (30%)\n- Empty inputs\n- Null/undefined\n- Boundary values\n- Maximum values\n- Minimum values\n- Unicode/special characters\n\n### 3. Error Cases (20%)\n- Invalid inputs\n- Type mismatches\n- Missing required fields\n- Network failures\n- Permission errors\n\n### 4. Integration (10%)\n- Component interaction\n- API contracts\n- Database operations\n- External dependencies\n\n## Test Structure\n\n\\`\\`\\`typescript\ndescribe(''[Component/Function]'', () => {\n  describe(''Happy Path'', () => {\n    it(''should [expected behavior]'', () => {\n      // Arrange\n      // Act\n      // Assert\n    })\n  })\n\n  describe(''Edge Cases'', () => {\n    it(''should handle empty input'', () => {})\n    it(''should handle null'', () => {})\n    it(''should handle boundary values'', () => {})\n  })\n\n  describe(''Error Cases'', () => {\n    it(''should throw on invalid input'', () => {})\n    it(''should handle network failure'', () => {})\n  })\n})\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n## Test Quality Checklist\n\n- [ ] Descriptive test names (\"should...\" format)\n- [ ] Clear arrange-act-assert structure\n- [ ] One assertion per test (generally)\n- [ ] No test interdependencies\n- [ ] Fast execution (<100ms per test ideally)\n- [ ] Easy to understand failures\n\n## Output\n\nGenerate complete test file with:\n- Imports and setup\n- Test suites organized by category\n- All test cases with assertions\n- Cleanup/teardown if needed\n```\n\n## Using Agents\n\n### Automatic Delegation\n\nClaude will automatically invoke agents when:\n- Task matches agent description\n- Agent is appropriate for context\n- More efficient than main conversation\n\n**Example:**\n```\nUser: \"Can you review my recent code changes?\"\n→ Claude invokes code-reviewer agent\n```\n\n### Explicit Invocation\n\nRequest specific agents:\n```\n\"Use the debugger subagent to find why this test is failing\"\n\"Have the data-scientist subagent analyze user retention\"\n\"Ask the code-reviewer to check this PR\"\n```\n\n### Agent Chaining\n\nSequence multiple agents for complex workflows:\n```\n\"First use code-analyzer to find performance bottlenecks,\nthen use optimizer to fix them,\nfinally use test-generator to verify the changes\"\n```\n\n## Agents vs Skills vs Commands\n\n### Use Subagents When:\n- ✅ Complex multi-step workflows\n- ✅ Specialized expertise needed\n- ✅ Delegation improves main context efficiency\n- ✅ Repeatable process with quality standards\n- ✅ Need focused context window\n\n### Use Skills When:\n- ✅ Context-aware automatic activation\n- ✅ Reference documentation and patterns\n- ✅ Multiple supporting files needed\n- ✅ Team standardization required\n\n### Use Slash Commands When:\n- ✅ Simple, focused tasks\n- ✅ Frequent manual invocation\n- ✅ Prompt fits in one file\n- ✅ Personal productivity shortcuts\n\n**Decision Tree:**\n\n```\nNeed specialized AI behavior?\n├─ Yes → Complex workflow?\n│         ├─ Yes → Use Subagent\n│         └─ No → Simple prompt?\n│                 ├─ Yes → Use Slash Command\n│                 └─ No → Use Skill (reference docs)\n└─ No → Just need documentation? → Use Skill\n```\n\n## Managing Agents\n\n### View Agents\n\nUse `/agents` command to:\n- List all available agents\n- See agent descriptions\n- Check tool permissions\n- View model configurations\n\n### Create Agent with Claude\n\nRecommended approach:\n```\n\"Create a subagent for [purpose] that [capabilities]\"\n```\n\nClaude will generate:\n- Appropriate name\n- Clear description\n- System prompt\n- Tool configuration\n- Model selection\n\nThen review and customize as needed.\n\n### Edit Agents\n\n1. Open agent file (`.claude/agents/agent-name.md`)\n2. Modify frontmatter or system prompt\n3. Save file\n4. Changes apply immediately (no restart needed)\n\n### Test Agents\n\nVerify agent works as expected:\n```\n\"Use the [agent-name] subagent to [test task]\"\n```\n\nCheck:\n- Agent activates correctly\n- Has necessary tool access\n- Produces expected output format\n- Handles edge cases\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### 1. Single Responsibility\n\nEach agent should do ONE thing exceptionally well.\n\n❌ **Anti-pattern:**\n```yaml\nname: code-helper\ndescription: Reviews, debugs, tests, refactors, and documents code\n```\n\n✅ **Better:**\n```yaml\nname: code-reviewer\ndescription: Reviews code for quality, security, and best practices\n```\n```yaml\nname: debugger\ndescription: Root cause analysis and minimal fixes for bugs\n```\n\n### 2. Detailed System Prompts\n\nInclude:\n- Role definition\n- Step-by-step process\n- Output format\n- Quality standards\n- Examples\n- Anti-patterns to avoid\n\n### 3. Minimum Tool Access\n\nGrant only necessary tools:\n\n❌ **Anti-pattern:**\n```yaml\ntools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob, WebSearch, WebFetch\n# Agent only needs Read and Grep\n```\n\n✅ **Better:**\n```yaml\ntools: Read, Grep\n```\n\n### 4. Clear Output Formats\n\nDefine expected structure in system prompt:\n\n```markdown\n## Output Format\n\n**Summary:** [1-2 sentence overview]\n\n**Findings:**\n- [Category]: [Specific finding] (file:line)\n\n**Recommendations:**\n1. [Priority action]\n2. [Priority action]\n3. [Priority action]\n```\n\n### 5. Version Control\n\nStore project agents in git:\n- `.claude/agents/` committed to repo\n- Team can collaborate on improvements\n- Track changes over time\n- Share best practices\n\n### 6. Iterative Improvement\n\nStart simple, refine based on usage:\n\n**v1:** Basic functionality\n```yaml\ndescription: Reviews code\n```\n\n**v2:** More specific\n```yaml\ndescription: Reviews code for security vulnerabilities\n```\n\n**v3:** Comprehensive\n```yaml\ndescription: Reviews code for security vulnerabilities including SQL injection, XSS, CSRF, and secrets exposure\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Agent Not Activating\n\n**Problem:** Agent doesn''t get invoked when expected\n\n**Solutions:**\n1. Check description is specific and matches use case\n2. Verify agent file is in `.claude/agents/`\n3. Request explicitly: \"Use the [agent-name] subagent\"\n4. Check for file syntax errors in frontmatter\n\n### Tool Permission Denied\n\n**Problem:** Agent can''t access needed tools\n\n**Solutions:**\n1. Add tools to frontmatter: `tools: Read, Write, Bash`\n2. Check Bash patterns: `Bash(git *)` not just `Bash`\n3. Omit `tools` field to inherit all tools\n4. Use `/agents` to verify tool configuration\n\n### Agent Output Format Wrong\n\n**Problem:** Agent doesn''t produce expected format\n\n**Solutions:**\n1. Add explicit format to system prompt\n2. Include example output\n3. Use template/checklist in prompt\n4. Test with various inputs\n\n### Agent Too Slow\n\n**Problem:** Agent takes too long to respond\n\n**Solutions:**\n1. Use `model: haiku` for faster responses\n2. Limit tool usage in prompt\n3. Reduce scope of agent responsibility\n4. Consider if task better suited for skill/command\n\n## Advanced Patterns\n\n### Conditional Agent Chains\n\n```\n\"If the code-reviewer finds critical issues,\nuse the auto-fixer subagent to resolve them,\nthen re-review with code-reviewer\"\n```\n\n### Dynamic Tool Access\n\nSome agents may need different tools for different tasks:\n\n```yaml\ntools: Read, Grep, Bash(git *), Bash(npm test:*)\n```\n\n### Multi-Model Workflow\n\n```\nUse opus for architecture decisions →\nUse sonnet for implementation →\nUse haiku for formatting checks\n```\n\n## Example Agent Library\n\n### code-reviewer\n**Purpose:** Code quality, security, and best practices\n**Tools:** Read, Grep, Bash(git *)\n**Model:** sonnet\n\n### debugger\n**Purpose:** Root cause analysis and minimal fixes\n**Tools:** Read, Edit, Bash, Grep\n**Model:** sonnet\n\n### test-generator\n**Purpose:** Comprehensive test suite generation\n**Tools:** Read, Write\n**Model:** sonnet\n\n### data-scientist\n**Purpose:** SQL optimization and data analysis\n**Tools:** Read, Write, Bash, WebSearch\n**Model:** sonnet\n\n### security-auditor\n**Purpose:** Deep security vulnerability analysis\n**Tools:** Read, Grep, WebSearch\n**Model:** opus\n\n### performance-optimizer\n**Purpose:** Performance bottleneck identification and fixes\n**Tools:** Read, Edit, Bash\n**Model:** sonnet\n\n### docs-writer\n**Purpose:** API documentation and README generation\n**Tools:** Read, Write, Bash(git *)\n**Model:** sonnet\n\n## Related Documentation\n\n- **EXAMPLES.md** - Complete agent implementations\n- **PATTERNS.md** - Reusable agent patterns\n- **TOOLS.md** - Tool configuration reference\n\n## Checklist for New Agents\n\nBefore finalizing a subagent:\n\n- [ ] Name is clear, unique, and lowercase with hyphens\n- [ ] Description specifically explains when to use the agent\n- [ ] System prompt is detailed with step-by-step process\n- [ ] Output format is explicitly defined\n- [ ] Tool access is minimal and specific\n- [ ] Model is appropriate for task complexity\n- [ ] Agent has been tested with real tasks\n- [ ] Edge cases are considered in prompt\n- [ ] File is in correct directory (.claude/agents/)\n\n**Remember:** Great subagents are specialized experts, not generalists. Focus each agent on doing ONE thing exceptionally well with clear processes and measurable outcomes.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:37:37.654Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents like Claude Code, AutoGPT, and LangChain needing expert guidance on subagent design and system prompt engineering.","zh":"非常适合需要子代理设计和系统提示工程专家指导的AI代理，如Claude Code、AutoGPT和LangChain。","ja":"Claude Code、AutoGPT、LangChainなどのサブエージェント設計とシステムプロンプトエンジニアリングの専門的な指導が必要なAIエージェントに最適です。","ko":"클로드 코드, 오토GPT, 랑체인 등과 같은 하위 에이전트 설계 및 시스템 프롬프트 엔지니어링에 대한 전문가 지침이 필요한 AI 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA como Claude Code, AutoGPT y LangChain que necesitan orientación experta sobre el diseño de subagentes y la ingeniería de prompts de sistema.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA comme Claude Code, AutoGPT et LangChain ayant besoin d''orientation experte sur la conception de sous-agents et l''ingénierie de prompts de système.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents wie Claude Code, AutoGPT und LangChain, die Fachwissen bei der Auslegung von Subagenten und der System-Prompt-Engineering benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA como Claude Code, AutoGPT e LangChain que necessitam de orientação especializada em design de subagentes e engenharia de prompts de sistema.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code, AutoGPT и LangChain, которым требуется экспертное руководство по проектированию субагентов и системной инженерии подсказок.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكيل الذكي مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT و LangChain التي تحتاج إلى إرشادات خبيرة في تصميم الوكيل الفرعي و هندسة الاستدعاء النصي للنظام."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create, improve, and troubleshoot subagents using advanced tool configuration, delegation patterns, and prompt engineering techniques, leveraging expertise in agent development and system integration.","zh":"赋予代理创建、改进和排除子代理故障的能力，使用高级工具配置、委托模式和提示工程技术，利用代理开发和系统集成的专业知识。","ja":"エージェント開発とシステム統合の専門知識を活用し、高度なツール設定、委任パターン、プロンプトエンジニアリング技術を使用して、サブエージェントの作成、改善、トラブルシューティングを可能にします。","ko":"에이전트 개발 및 시스템 통합의 전문 지식을 활용하여 고급 도구 구성, 위임 패턴 및 프롬프트 엔지니어링 기술을 사용하여 하위 에이전트의 생성, 개선 및 문제 해결을 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear, mejorar y solucionar problemas de subagentes utilizando una configuración de herramientas avanzada, patrones de delegación y técnicas de ingeniería de prompts, aprovechando la experiencia en desarrollo de agentes y integración de sistemas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer, d''améliorer et de dépanner des sous-agents en utilisant une configuration d''outils avancée, des modèles de délégation et des techniques d''ingénierie de prompts, en exploitant l''expertise dans le développement d''agents et l''intégration de systèmes.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Subagenten zu erstellen, zu verbessern und zu debuggen, indem sie eine erweiterte Werkzeugkonfiguration, Delegationsmuster und Prompt-Engineering-Techniken nutzen und dabei das Fachwissen in der Agentenentwicklung und Systemintegration nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar, melhorar e solucionar problemas de subagentes usando configuração de ferramentas avançada, padrões de delegação e técnicas de engenharia de prompts, aproveitando a expertise em desenvolvimento de agentes e integração de sistemas.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать, улучшать и устранять неполадки субагентов, используя расширенную конфигурацию инструментов, шаблоны делегирования и методы инженерии подсказок, используя опыт в разработке агентов и системной интеграции.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من إنشاء و تحسين و حل مشاكل الوكيل الفرعي باستخدام تكوين أدوات متقدم و أنماط من tomu و تقنيات هندسة الاستدعاء النصي، مستفيداً من الخبرة في تطوير الوكيل و دمج النظام."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating new subagents with optimized system prompts","Improving existing agent performance through configuration tuning","Troubleshooting subagent invocation issues with expert guidance"],"zh":["使用优化的系统提示创建新的子代理","通过配置微调提高现有代理的性能","使用专家指导排除子代理调用问题"],"ja":["最適化されたシステムプロンプトを使用して新しいサブエージェントを作成する","構成の微調整により、既存のエージェントのパフォーマンスを向上させる","専門家の指導により、サブエージェントの呼び出しに関する問題をトラブルシューティングする"],"ko":["최적화된 시스템 프롬프트를 사용하여 새로운 하위 에이전트를 생성하는 것","구성 조정을 통해 기존 에이전트의 성능을 향상시키는 것","전문가의 지침을 사용하여 하위 에이전트 호출 문제를 해결하는 것"],"es":["Crear nuevos subagentes con prompts de sistema optimizados","Mejorar el rendimiento de los agentes existentes mediante la ajuste de la configuración","Solucionar problemas de invocación de subagentes con orientación experta"],"fr":["Créer de nouveaux sous-agents avec des prompts de système optimisés","Améliorer les performances des agents existants en ajustant la configuration","Résoudre les problèmes d''invocation de sous-agents avec une orientation experte"],"de":["Erstellen von neuen Subagenten mit optimierten System-Prompts","Verbesserung der Leistung bestehender Agenten durch Konfigurationsfeinabstimmung","Behebung von Subagenten-Aufrufproblemen mit Hilfe von Fachwissen"],"pt":["Criar novos subagentes com prompts de sistema otimizados","Melhorar o desempenho de agentes existentes por meio de ajustes de configuração","Solucionar problemas de invocação de subagentes com orientação especializada"],"ru":["Создание новых субагентов с оптимизированными системными подсказками","Улучшение производительности существующих агентов за счет настройки конфигурации","Устранение неполадок вызова субагентов с помощью экспертного руководства"],"ar":["إنشاء وكلاء فرعيين جدد مع استدعاءات نصية محسّنة للنظام","تحسين أداء الوكلاء الحاليين من خلال ضبط التكوين","حل مشاكل استدعاء الوكيل الفرعي مع إرشادات خبيرة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Claude Code subagent setup","Limited to AI agents with subagent architecture"],"zh":["需要克劳德代码子代理设置","仅限具有子代理架构的AI代理"],"ja":["クラウドコードサブエージェントの設定が必要","サブエージェントアーキテクチャを持つAIエージェントのみ"],"ko":["클라우드 코드 하위 에이전트 설정이 필요합니다","하위 에이전트 아키텍처를 갖춘 AI 에이전트만 해당"],"es":["Requiere la configuración de subagentes de Claude Code","Limitado a agentes de IA con arquitectura de subagentes"],"fr":["Nécessite la configuration de sous-agents de Claude Code","Limité aux agents IA avec une architecture de sous-agents"],"de":["Benötigt die Einrichtung von Claude Code-Subagenten","Begrenzt auf KI-Agents mit Subagenten-Architektur"],"pt":["Requer configuração de subagente do Claude Code","Limitado a agentes de IA com arquitetura de subagente"],"ru":["Требует настройки субагента Claude Code","Ограничен агентами ИИ с архитектурой субагента"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد الوكيل الفرعي Claude Code","محدود بالوكلاء الذكيين ذوي هندسة الوكيل الفرعي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('sfc-gh-dflippo/snowflake-dbt-demo/dbt-migration-vertica', 'community', 'sfc-gh-dflippo', 'snowflake-dbt-demo', 'sfc-gh-dflippo/snowflake-dbt-demo', 'dbt-migration-vertica', 0, 0, 80, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.410Z', '2026-02-18T03:37:54.875Z', NULL, '{"id":"sfc-gh-dflippo/snowflake-dbt-demo/dbt-migration-vertica","name":"dbt-migration-vertica","description":{"zh":"本项目演示了 dbt 在 Snowflake Data Cloud 中的众多功能，包括将 Vertica DDL 转换为 dbt 模型","ja":"このプロジェクトでは、Snowflake Data Cloud で dbt を使用する際の多くの機能を紹介し、Vertica DDL を dbt モデルに変換します","ko":"이 프로젝트는 Snowflake Data Cloud에서 dbt를 사용하는 다양한 기능을展示하며 Vertica DDL을 dbt 모델로 변환","es":"Convierta vistas, tablas y procedimientos almacenados de Vertica en modelos dbt de producción para Snowflake","fr":"Convertissez des vues, des tables et des procédures stockées Vertica en modèles dbt de production pour Snowflake","de":"Wandeln Sie Ansichten, Tabellen und gespeicherte Prozeduren von Vertica in dbt-Produktionsmodelle für Snowflake um","pt":"Converte vistas e tabelas Vertica em modelos dbt de produção compatíveis com Snowflake, mantendo a lógica de negócios e etapas de transformação de dados","ru":"Преобразует представления и таблицы Vertica в модели dbt, совместимые с Snowflake, сохраняя бизнес-логику и шаги трансформации данных","ar":"يحول العروض والجداول Vertica إلى نماذج dbt متوافقة مع Snowflake مع الحفاظ على المنطق التجاري وخطوات تحويل البيانات","en":"This project demonstrates many of dbt''s features when used with the Snowflake Data Cloud"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Vertica 到 dbt 模型迁移","ja":"Vertica から dbt モデルへの移行","ko":"Vertica에서 dbt 모델로 마이그레이션","es":"Migración dbt Vertica: Conversión de modelos","fr":"Migration dbt Vertica: Conversion de modèles","de":"dbt-Migration Vertica: Modellkonvertierung","pt":"Migração dbt-Vertica: Conversão de Modelos","ru":"dbt-Миграция Vertica: Конвертация Моделей","ar":"هجرة dbt-Vertica: تحويل النماذج","en":"dbt-migration-vertica"},"description":{"zh":"本项目演示了 dbt 在 Snowflake Data Cloud 中的众多功能，包括将 Vertica DDL 转换为 dbt 模型","ja":"このプロジェクトでは、Snowflake Data Cloud で dbt を使用する際の多くの機能を紹介し、Vertica DDL を dbt モデルに変換します","ko":"이 프로젝트는 Snowflake Data Cloud에서 dbt를 사용하는 다양한 기능을展示하며 Vertica DDL을 dbt 모델로 변환","es":"Convierta vistas, tablas y procedimientos almacenados de Vertica en modelos dbt de producción para Snowflake","fr":"Convertissez des vues, des tables et des procédures stockées Vertica en modèles dbt de production pour Snowflake","de":"Wandeln Sie Ansichten, Tabellen und gespeicherte Prozeduren von Vertica in dbt-Produktionsmodelle für Snowflake um","pt":"Converte vistas e tabelas Vertica em modelos dbt de produção compatíveis com Snowflake, mantendo a lógica de negócios e etapas de transformação de dados","ru":"Преобразует представления и таблицы Vertica в модели dbt, совместимые с Snowflake, сохраняя бизнес-логику и шаги трансформации данных","ar":"يحول العروض والجداول Vertica إلى نماذج dbt متوافقة مع Snowflake مع الحفاظ على المنطق التجاري وخطوات تحويل البيانات","en":"This project demonstrates many of dbt''s features when used with the Snowflake Data Cloud"},"definition":{"en":"This project demonstrates many of dbt''s features when used with the Snowflake Data Cloud"},"features":{"zh":["将 Vertica 视图和表转换为 dbt 模型","将 Vertica 存储过程迁移到 dbt","将 Vertica SQL 语法转换为 Snowflake","生成 schema"],"ja":["Vertica のビューとテーブルを dbt モデルに変換","Vertica のストアドプロシージャを dbt に移行","Vertica SQL 構文を Snowflake に変換","スキーマの生成"],"ko":["Vertica 뷰와 테이블을 dbt 모델로 변환","Vertica 저장 프로시저를 dbt로 마이그레이션","Vertica SQL 구문을 Snowflake로 변환","스키마 생성"],"es":["Conversión de vistas y tablas de Vertica en modelos dbt","Migración de procedimientos almacenados de Vertica a dbt","Traducción de sintaxis SQL de Vertica a Snowflake","Generación de esquemas para dbt"],"fr":["Conversion de vues et de tables Vertica en modèles dbt","Migration de procédures stockées Vertica vers dbt","Traduction de la syntaxe SQL Vertica en Snowflake","Génération de schémas pour dbt"],"de":["Umwandlung von Ansichten und Tabellen von Vertica in dbt-Modelle","Migration von gespeicherten Prozeduren von Vertica zu dbt","Übersetzung von Vertica-SQL-Syntax in Snowflake","Erzeugung von Schemata für dbt"],"pt":["Conversão de vistas e tabelas Vertica em modelos dbt","Manutenção da lógica de negócios e etapas de transformação de dados","Compatibilidade com Snowflake","Seguimento das melhores práticas dbt","Geração de esquemas"],"ru":["Преобразование представлений и таблиц Vertica в модели dbt","Сохранение бизнес-логики и шагов трансформации данных","Совместимость с Snowflake","Следование рекомендациям dbt","Генерация схем"],"ar":["تحويل العروض والجداول Vertica إلى نماذج dbt","الحفاظ على المنطق التجاري وخطوات تحويل البيانات","التوافق مع Snowflake","متابعة أفضل الممارسات dbt","توليد مخططات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["dbt","Vertica","Snowflake","数据库迁移","dbt 模型","数据转换"],"ja":["dbt","Vertica","Snowflake","データベース移行","dbt モデル","データ変換"],"ko":["dbt","Vertica","Snowflake","데이터베이스 마이그레이션","dbt 모델","데이터 변환"],"es":["migración dbt","Vertica a dbt"," Snowflake","conversión de modelos","procedimientos almacenados","sintaxis SQL"],"fr":["migration dbt","Vertica vers dbt","Snowflake","conversion de modèles","procédures stockées","syntaxe SQL"],"de":["dbt-Migration","Vertica zu dbt","Snowflake","Modellkonvertierung","gespeicherte Prozeduren","SQL-Syntax"],"pt":["dbt-migration-vertica","conversão de modelos","vertica para dbt","snowflake","dbt best practices","geração de esquemas"],"ru":["dbt-Миграция Vertica","конвертация моделей","vertica в dbt","snowflake","рекомендации dbt","генерация схем"],"ar":["هجرة dbt-Vertica","تحويل النماذج","vertica إلى dbt","snowflake","أفضل الممارسات dbt","توليد مخططات"]}},"owner":"sfc-gh-dflippo","repo":"snowflake-dbt-demo","repoPath":"sfc-gh-dflippo/snowflake-dbt-demo","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.410Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"dbt-migration-vertica","description":"","bodyPreview":"# Vertica to dbt Model Conversion\n\n## Purpose\n\nTransform Vertica DDL (views, tables, stored procedures) into production-quality dbt models\ncompatible with Snowflake, maintaining the same business logic and data transformation steps while\nfollowing dbt best practices.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nActivate this skill when users ask about:\n\n- Converting Vertica views or tables to dbt models\n- Migrating Vertica stored procedures to dbt\n- Translating Vertica SQL syntax to Snowflake\n- Generating schema","body":"# Vertica to dbt Model Conversion\n\n## Purpose\n\nTransform Vertica DDL (views, tables, stored procedures) into production-quality dbt models\ncompatible with Snowflake, maintaining the same business logic and data transformation steps while\nfollowing dbt best practices.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nActivate this skill when users ask about:\n\n- Converting Vertica views or tables to dbt models\n- Migrating Vertica stored procedures to dbt\n- Translating Vertica SQL syntax to Snowflake\n- Generating schema.yml files with tests and documentation\n- Handling Vertica-specific syntax (projections, flex tables, ANY/ALL predicates)\n\n---\n\n## Task Description\n\nYou are a database engineer working for a hospital system. You need to convert Vertica DDL to\nequivalent dbt code compatible with Snowflake, maintaining the same business logic and data\ntransformation steps while following dbt best practices.\n\n## Input Requirements\n\nI will provide you the Vertica DDL to convert.\n\n## Audience\n\nThe code will be executed by data engineers who are learning Snowflake and dbt.\n\n## Output Requirements\n\nGenerate the following:\n\n1. One or more dbt models with complete SQL for every column\n2. A corresponding schema.yml file with appropriate tests and documentation\n3. A config block with materialization strategy\n4. Explanation of key changes and architectural decisions\n5. Inline comments highlighting any syntax that was converted\n\n## Conversion Guidelines\n\n### General Principles\n\n- Replace procedural logic with declarative SQL where possible\n- Break down complex procedures into multiple modular dbt models\n- Implement appropriate incremental processing strategies\n- Maintain data quality checks through dbt tests\n- Use Snowflake SQL functions rather than macros whenever possible\n\n### Sample Response Format\n\n```sql\n-- dbt model: models/[domain]/[target_schema_name]/model_name.sql\n{{ config(materialized=''view'') }}\n\n/* Original Object: [schema].[object_name]\n   Source Platform: Vertica\n   Purpose: [brief description]\n   Conversion Notes: [key changes]\n   Description: [SQL logic description] */\n\nWITH source_data AS (\n    SELECT\n        customer_id::INTEGER AS customer_id,\n        customer_name::VARCHAR(100) AS customer_name,\n        account_balance::NUMBER(18,2) AS account_balance,\n        -- TIMESTAMPTZ converted to TIMESTAMP_TZ\n        created_date::TIMESTAMP_TZ AS created_date\n    FROM {{ ref(''upstream_model'') }}\n),\n\ntransformed_data AS (\n    SELECT\n        customer_id,\n        UPPER(customer_name)::VARCHAR(100) AS customer_name_upper,\n        account_balance,\n        created_date,\n        CURRENT_TIMESTAMP()::TIMESTAMP_NTZ AS loaded_at\n    FROM source_data\n)\n\nSELECT\n    customer_id,\n    customer_name_upper,\n    account_balance,\n    created_date,\n    loaded_at\nFROM transformed_data\n```\n\n```yaml\n## models/[domain]/[target_schema_name]/_models.yml\nversion: 2\n\nmodels:\n  - name: model_name\n    description: \"Table description; converted from Vertica [Original object name]\"\n    columns:\n      - name: customer_id\n        description: \"Primary key - unique customer identifier\"\n        tests:\n          - unique\n          - not_null\n      - name: customer_name_upper\n        description: \"Customer name in uppercase\"\n      - name: account_balance\n        description: \"Current account balance; Foreign key to OTHER_TABLE\"\n        tests:\n          - relationships:\n              to: ref(''OTHER_TABLE'')\n              field: OTHER_TABLE_KEY\n      - name: created_date\n        description: \"Date the customer record was created\"\n      - name: loaded_at\n        description: \"Timestamp when the record was loaded by dbt\"\n```\n\n```yaml\n## dbt_project.yml (excerpt)\nmodels:\n  my_project:\n    +materialized: view\n    domain_name:\n      +schema: target_schema_name\n```\n\n### Specific Translation Rules\n\n#### dbt Specific Requirements\n\n- If the source is a view, use a view materialization in dbt\n- Include appropriate dbt model configuration (materialization type)\n- Add documentation blocks for a schema.yml\n- Add descriptions for tables and columns\n- Include relevant tests\n- Define primary keys and relationships\n- Assume that upstream objects are models\n- Comprehensively provide all the columns in the output\n- Break complex procedures into multiple models if needed\n- Implement appropriate incremental strategies for large tables\n- Use Snowflake SQL functions rather than macros whenever possible\n- **Always cast columns with explicit precision/scale** using `::TYPE` syntax (e.g.,\n  `column_name::VARCHAR(100)`, `amount::NUMBER(18,2)`) to ensure output matches expected data types\n- **Always provide explicit column aliases** for clarity and documentation\n\n#### Performance Optimization\n\n- Suggest clustering keys if needed\n- Recommend materialization strategy (view vs table)\n- Identify potential performance improvements\n\n#### Vertica to Snowflake Syntax Conversion\n\n- Remove projection specifications\n- Handle flex table conversions\n- Convert case sensitivity with quoted identifiers\n- Replace ANY/ALL array predicates with Snowflake equivalents\n- Convert Vertica-specific functions\n- Handle COPY syntax differences\n- Remove SEGMENTED BY clauses\n\n#### Key Data Type Mappings\n\n| Vertica                             | Snowflake              | Notes |\n| ----------------------------------- | ---------------------- | ----- |\n| INT/INTEGER/BIGINT/SMALLINT/TINYINT | Same                   |       |\n| NUMERIC/DECIMAL                     | Same                   |       |\n| FLOAT/REAL/DOUBLE PRECISION         | FLOAT                  |       |\n| CHAR/VARCHAR                        | Same                   |       |\n| LONG VARCHAR                        | VARCHAR                |       |\n| BINARY/VARBINARY/LONG VARBINARY     | BINARY                 |       |\n| BOOLEAN                             | BOOLEAN                |       |\n| DATE                                | DATE                   |       |\n| TIME/TIMETZ                         | TIME                   |       |\n| TIMESTAMP/TIMESTAMPTZ               | TIMESTAMP/TIMESTAMP_TZ |       |\n| INTERVAL                            | VARCHAR                |       |\n| UUID                                | VARCHAR                |       |\n\n#### Key Syntax Conversions\n\n```sql\n-- Projections -> Remove (Snowflake auto-manages)\nCREATE PROJECTION proj AS SELECT ... -> (remove entirely)\n\n-- SEGMENTED BY -> CLUSTER BY\nCREATE TABLE t (...) SEGMENTED BY HASH(id) ->\nCREATE TABLE t (...) CLUSTER BY (id)\n\n-- Flex tables -> VARIANT columns\nCREATE FLEX TABLE t() -> CREATE TABLE t (data VARIANT)\n\n-- Case sensitivity (Vertica folds to lowercase)\nSELECT Col -> SELECT \"Col\"  -- if case matters\n\n-- ANY/ALL array predicates\ncol = ANY(ARRAY[1,2,3]) -> col IN (1,2,3)\ncol <> ALL(ARRAY[1,2,3]) -> col NOT IN (1,2,3)\n```\n\n#### Common Function Mappings\n\n| Vertica                  | Snowflake                  | Notes |\n| ------------------------ | -------------------------- | ----- |\n| `NVL(a, b)`              | `NVL(a, b)`                | Same  |\n| `NVL2(a, b, c)`          | `IFF(a IS NOT NULL, b, c)` |       |\n| `COALESCE(...)`          | `COALESCE(...)`            | Same  |\n| `NULLIF(a, b)`           | `NULLIF(a, b)`             | Same  |\n| `DECODE(expr, ...)`      | `CASE expr WHEN ... END`   |       |\n| `GETDATE()`              | `CURRENT_TIMESTAMP()`      |       |\n| `SYSDATE`                | `CURRENT_TIMESTAMP()`      |       |\n| `ADD_MONTHS(d, n)`       | `DATEADD(''month'', n, d)`   |       |\n| `DATEDIFF(unit, d1, d2)` | `DATEDIFF(unit, d1, d2)`   | Same  |\n| `TO_CHAR(d, fmt)`        | `TO_CHAR(d, fmt)`          | Same  |\n| `TO_DATE(s, fmt)`        | `TO_DATE(s, fmt)`          | Same  |\n| `INSTR(str, search)`     | `POSITION(search IN str)`  |       |\n| `SUBSTR(s, pos, len)`    | `SUBSTR(s, pos, len)`      | Same  |\n| `REGEXP_LIKE(s, p)`      | `REGEXP_LIKE(s, p)`        | Same  |\n| `LISTAGG(col, delim)`    | `LISTAGG(col, delim)`      | Same  |\n| `SPLIT_PART(s, d, n)`    | `SPLIT_PART(s, d, n)`      | Same  |\n\n#### Dependencies\n\n- List any upstream dependencies\n- Suggest model organization in dbt project\n\n---\n\n## Validation Checklist\n\n- [] Every DDL statement has been accounted for in the dbt models\n- [] SQL in models is compatible with Snowflake\n- [] Vertica-specific syntax converted (projections removed, case sensitivity handled)\n- [] All business logic preserved\n- [] All columns included in output\n- [] Data types correctly mapped\n- [] Functions translated to Snowflake equivalents\n- [] Materialization strategy selected\n- [] Tests added\n- [] SQL logic description complete\n- [] Table descriptions added\n- [] Column descriptions added\n- [] Dependencies correctly mapped\n- [] Incremental logic (if applicable) verified\n- [] Inline comments added for converted syntax\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- $dbt-migration - For the complete migration workflow (discovery, planning, placeholder models,\n  testing, deployment)\n- $dbt-modeling - For CTE patterns and SQL structure guidance\n- $dbt-testing - For implementing comprehensive dbt tests\n- $dbt-architecture - For project organization and folder structure\n- $dbt-materializations - For choosing materialization strategies (view, table, incremental,\n  snapshots)\n- $dbt-performance - For clustering keys, warehouse sizing, and query optimization\n- $dbt-commands - For running dbt commands and model selection syntax\n- $dbt-core - For dbt installation, configuration, and package management\n- $snowflake-cli - For executing SQL and managing Snowflake objects\n\n---\n\n## Supported Source Database\n\n| Database    | Key Considerations                                                               |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Vertica** | Projections, flex tables, case sensitivity with quotes, ANY/ALL array predicates |\n\n## Translation References\n\nDetailed syntax translation guides are available in the `translation-references/` folder.\n\n> **Copyright Notice:** The translation reference documentation in this repository is derived from\n> [Snowflake SnowConvert Documentation](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/migrations/snowconvert-docs)\n> and is © Copyright Snowflake Inc. All rights reserved. Used for reference purposes only.\n\n### Reference Index\n\n- [Create Table](translation-references/vertica-create-table.md)\n- [Create View](translation-references/vertica-create-view.md)\n- [Data Types](translation-references/vertica-data-types.md)\n- [Identifier Between Vertica And Snowflake](translation-references/vertica-identifier-between-vertica-and-snowflake.md)\n- [Operators](translation-references/vertica-operators.md)\n- [Predicates](translation-references/vertica-predicates.md)\n- [Overview (README)](translation-references/vertica-readme.md)\n- [Subqueries](translation-references/vertica-subqueries.md)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:37:54.875Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Engineering Agents needing Vertica to dbt model conversion capabilities for Snowflake Data Cloud","zh":"非常适合需要将Vertica转换为dbt模型以用于Snowflake Data Cloud的数据工程代理","ja":"Verticaをdbtモデルに変換する機能がSnowflake Data Cloudで必要なデータエンジニアリングエージェントに最適","ko":"Snowflake Data Cloud에서 Vertica를 dbt 모델로 변환하는 기능이 필요한 데이터 엔지니어링 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Ingeniería de Datos que necesitan capacidades de conversión de modelos de Vertica a dbt para Snowflake Data Cloud","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''ingénierie de données ayant besoin de capacités de conversion de modèles Vertica en modèles dbt pour Snowflake Data Cloud","de":"Perfekt für Data-Engineering-Agents, die Vertica-zu-dbt-Modell-Konvertierungsfunktionen für Snowflake Data Cloud benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Engenharia de Dados que necessitam de capacidades de conversão de modelo Vertica para dbt para Snowflake Data Cloud","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов инженерии данных, которым необходимы возможности преобразования модели Vertica в dbt для Snowflake Data Cloud","ar":"مثالي لعميل هندسة البيانات الذين يحتاجون إلىقدرات تحويل نموذج Vertica إلى dbt ل سحابة بيانات Snowflake"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform Vertica DDL into production-quality dbt models compatible with Snowflake, maintaining business logic and data transformation steps while following dbt best practices, utilizing Vertica SQL syntax translation and schema generation","zh":"赋予代理将Vertica DDL转换为生产级的dbt模型的能力，兼容Snowflake，保持业务逻辑和数据转换步骤，同时遵循dbt的最佳实践，利用Vertica SQL语法翻译和模式生成","ja":"エージェントがVertica DDLをSnowflakeと互換性のあるプロダクションレベルのdbtモデルに変換できるようにし、ビジネスロジックとデータ変換ステップを維持しながらdbtのベストプラクティスに従い、Vertica SQL構文の翻訳とスキーマ生成を利用する","ko":"에이전트가 Vertica DDL을 Snowflake와 호환되는 프로덕션 레벨의 dbt 모델로 변환할 수 있도록 하여 비즈니스 논리와 데이터 변환 단계를 유지하면서 dbt의 모범 사례를 따르며 Vertica SQL 구문 번역과 스키마 생성을 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformar DDL de Vertica en modelos dbt de producción compatible con Snowflake, manteniendo la lógica empresarial y los pasos de transformación de datos mientras sigue las mejores prácticas de dbt, utilizando la traducción de sintaxis SQL de Vertica y la generación de esquemas","fr":"Permet aux agents de transformer le DDL Vertica en des modèles dbt de production compatible avec Snowflake, en conservant la logique métier et les étapes de transformation de données tout en suivant les meilleures pratiques de dbt, en utilisant la traduction de la syntaxe SQL Vertica et la génération de schémas","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Vertica-DDL in produktionsreife dbt-Modelle kompatibel mit Snowflake zu transformieren, wobei die Geschäftslogik und die DatenTransformationsschritte beibehalten werden, während die dbt-Best-Practices befolgt und die Vertica-SQL-Syntaxübersetzung und die Schemagenerierung genutzt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a transformar DDL Vertica em modelos dbt de produção compatíveis com Snowflake, mantendo a lógica de negócios e os passos de transformação de dados, seguindo as melhores práticas dbt, utilizando a tradução da sintaxe SQL Vertica e geração de esquema","ru":"Позволяет агентам преобразовывать DDL Vertica в modelos dbt производственного качества, совместимые с Snowflake, сохраняя бизнес-логику и шаги преобразования данных, следуя лучшим практикам dbt, используя перевод синтаксиса SQL Vertica и генерацию схемы","ar":"يتمكن الوكلاء من تحويل DDL Vertica إلى نماذج dbt من الإنتاج ذوي الجودة العالية المتوافقة مع Snowflake ، مع الحفاظ على منطق الأعمال وخطوات تحويل البيانات ، اتباعا لأفضل الممارسات dbt ، واستخدام ترجمة بناء جملة SQL Vertica وتوليد مخطط"},"useCases":{"en":["Converting Vertica views or tables to dbt models","Migrating Vertica stored procedures to dbt","Translating Vertica SQL syntax to Snowflake","Generating schema for dbt models"],"zh":["将Vertica视图或表转换为dbt模型","将Vertica存储过程迁移到dbt","将Vertica SQL语法翻译为Snowflake","为dbt模型生成模式"],"ja":["Verticaビューまたはテーブルをdbtモデルに変換する","Verticaストアドプロシージャをdbtに移行する","Vertica SQL構文をSnowflakeに翻訳する","dbtモデル用のスキーマを生成する"],"ko":["Vertica 뷰 또는 테이블을 dbt 모델로 변환","Vertica 저장 프로시저를 dbt로 마이그레이션","Vertica SQL 구문을 Snowflake로 번역","dbt 모델을 위한 스키마 생성"],"es":["Conversión de vistas o tablas de Vertica en modelos dbt","Migración de procedimientos almacenados de Vertica a dbt","Traducción de la sintaxis SQL de Vertica a Snowflake","Generación de esquema para modelos dbt"],"fr":["Conversion de vues ou de tables Vertica en modèles dbt","Migration de procédures stockées Vertica vers dbt","Traduction de la syntaxe SQL Vertica en Snowflake","Génération de schéma pour les modèles dbt"],"de":["Konvertierung von Vertica-Views oder -Tabellen in dbt-Modelle","Migration von gespeicherten Vertica-Prozeduren zu dbt","Übersetzung der Vertica-SQL-Syntax in Snowflake","Generierung von Schemata für dbt-Modelle"],"pt":["Conversão de visualizações ou tabelas Vertica em modelos dbt","Migração de procedimentos armazenados Vertica para dbt","Tradução da sintaxe SQL Vertica para Snowflake","Geração de esquema para modelos dbt"],"ru":["Преобразование представлений или таблиц Vertica в модели dbt","Миграция хранимых процедур Vertica в dbt","Перевод синтаксиса SQL Vertica в Snowflake","Генерация схемы для моделей dbt"],"ar":["تحويل عارضات أو جداول Vertica إلى نماذج dbt","هجرة إجراءات مخزنة Vertica إلى dbt","ترجمة بناء جملة SQL Vertica إلى Snowflake","توليد مخطط لنماذج dbt"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of Vertica DDL and dbt","Specific to Snowflake Data Cloud","Limited to transforming Vertica views, tables, and stored procedures"],"zh":["需要了解Vertica DDL和dbt","仅限于Snowflake Data Cloud","仅限于转换Vertica视图、表和存储过程"],"ja":["Vertica DDLとdbtの知識が必要","Snowflake Data Cloudに限定","Verticaビュー、テーブル、ストアドプロシージャの変換のみ"],"ko":["Vertica DDL과 dbt에 대한 지식이 필요","Snowflake Data Cloud에만 국한","Vertica 뷰, 테이블 및 저장 프로시저의 변환만"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de DDL de Vertica y dbt","Específico para Snowflake Data Cloud","Limitado a la transformación de vistas, tablas y procedimientos almacenados de Vertica"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance du DDL Vertica et de dbt","Spécifique à Snowflake Data Cloud","Limité à la transformation de vues, de tables et de procédures stockées Vertica"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse von Vertica-DDL und dbt","Spezifisch für Snowflake Data Cloud","Begrenzt auf die Transformation von Vertica-Views, -Tabellen und gespeicherten Prozeduren"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento de DDL Vertica e dbt","Específico para Snowflake Data Cloud","Limitado à transformação de visualizações, tabelas e procedimentos armazenados Vertica"],"ru":["Требует знания DDL Vertica и dbt","Специфичен для Snowflake Data Cloud","Ограничен преобразованием представлений, таблиц и хранимых процедур Vertica"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة DDL Vertica و dbt","محدد لسحابة بيانات Snowflake","محدود بتحويل عارضات وجداول وإجراءات مخزنة Vertica"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('binjuhor/shadcn-lar/ui-ux-pro-max', 'community', 'binjuhor', 'shadcn-lar', 'binjuhor/shadcn-lar', 'ui-ux-pro-max', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.410Z', '2026-02-18T03:37:47.140Z', NULL, '{"id":"binjuhor/shadcn-lar/ui-ux-pro-max","name":"ui-ux-pro-max","description":{"zh":"UI/UX Pro Max 是一个设计智能解决方案，提供可搜索的 UI 风格、色彩调色板和 UX 指南等设计资源。它可以帮助开发者提高设计效率和质量","ja":"UI/UX Pro Max はデザインインテリジェンスソリューションで、検索可能な UI スタイル、カラーパレット、UX ガイドラインなどのデザイン リソースを提供します。これにより、開発者はデザインの効率と品質を向上させることができます","ko":"UI/UX Pro Max는 디자인 인텔리전스 솔루션으로, 검색 가능한 UI 스타일, 색상 팔레트 및 UX 가이드라인 등의 디자인 리소스를 제공합니다. 이는 개발자가 디자인의 효율과 품질을 향상시키는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"UI/UX Pro Max es una herramienta de diseño inteligente que ofrece una base de datos de estilos UI, paletas de colores y mejores prácticas para desarrolladores","fr":"UI/UX Pro Max est un outil de design intelligent qui propose une base de données de styles UI, de palettes de couleurs et de meilleures pratiques pour les développeurs","de":"UI/UX Pro Max ist ein Design-Intelligenz-Tool, das eine Datenbank von UI-Stilen, Farbpaletten und Best Practices für Entwickler bietet","pt":"O UI/UX Pro Max é uma ferramenta para desenvolvedores que busca melhorar a experiência do usuário através do design de interfaces.","ru":"UI/UX Pro Max - это инструмент для разработчиков, который помогает улучшить опыт пользователя через проектирование интерфейсов.","ar":"UI/UX برو ماكس هو أداة لمطوري البرمجيات تسعى لتحسين تجربة المستخدم من خلال تصميم الواجهات.","en":"Made an shadcn/ui admin for Laravel with 🤍 "},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"UI/UX Pro Max - 设计智能解决方案","ja":"UI/UX Pro Max - デザインインテリジェンスソリューション","ko":"UI/UX Pro Max - 디자인 인텔리전스 솔루션","es":"UI/UX Pro Max: Diseño Inteligente para Desarrolladores","fr":"UI/UX Pro Max: Intelligence de Design pour Développeurs","de":"UI/UX Pro Max: Design-Intelligenz für Entwickler","pt":"UI/UX Pro Max: Desenvolvimento de Interfaces","ru":"UI/UX Pro Max: Разработка Интерфейсов","ar":"UI/UX برو ماكس: تطوير الواجهات","en":"ui-ux-pro-max"},"description":{"zh":"UI/UX Pro Max 是一个设计智能解决方案，提供可搜索的 UI 风格、色彩调色板和 UX 指南等设计资源。它可以帮助开发者提高设计效率和质量","ja":"UI/UX Pro Max はデザインインテリジェンスソリューションで、検索可能な UI スタイル、カラーパレット、UX ガイドラインなどのデザイン リソースを提供します。これにより、開発者はデザインの効率と品質を向上させることができます","ko":"UI/UX Pro Max는 디자인 인텔리전스 솔루션으로, 검색 가능한 UI 스타일, 색상 팔레트 및 UX 가이드라인 등의 디자인 리소스를 제공합니다. 이는 개발자가 디자인의 효율과 품질을 향상시키는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"UI/UX Pro Max es una herramienta de diseño inteligente que ofrece una base de datos de estilos UI, paletas de colores y mejores prácticas para desarrolladores","fr":"UI/UX Pro Max est un outil de design intelligent qui propose une base de données de styles UI, de palettes de couleurs et de meilleures pratiques pour les dé...","de":"UI/UX Pro Max ist ein Design-Intelligenz-Tool, das eine Datenbank von UI-Stilen, Farbpaletten und Best Practices für Entwickler bietet","pt":"O UI/UX Pro Max é uma ferramenta para desenvolvedores que busca melhorar a experiência do usuário através do design de interfaces.","ru":"UI/UX Pro Max - это инструмент для разработчиков, который помогает улучшить опыт пользователя через проектирование интерфейсов.","ar":"UI/UX برو ماكس هو أداة لمطوري البرمجيات تسعى لتحسين تجربة المستخدم من خلال تصميم الواجهات.","en":"Made an shadcn/ui admin for Laravel with 🤍 "},"definition":{"en":"Made an shadcn/ui admin for Laravel with 🤍 "},"features":{"zh":["可搜索的 UI 风格","色彩调色板","字体配对","图表类型","UX 指南"],"ja":["検索可能な UI スタイル","カラーパレット","フォントのペア","チャートの種類","UX ガイドライン"],"ko":["검색 가능한 UI 스타일","색상 팔레트","글꼴 쌍","차트 유형","UX 가이드라인"],"es":["Base de datos de estilos UI","Paletas de colores personalizables","Mejores prácticas para desarrolladores","Recomendaciones de productos","Pautas de UX"],"fr":["Base de données de styles UI","Palettes de couleurs personnalisables","Meilleures pratiques pour les développeurs","Recommandations de produits","Directives d''UX"],"de":["Datenbank von UI-Stilen","Anpassbare Farbpaletten","Best Practices für Entwickler","Produktempfehlungen","UX-Richtlinien"],"pt":["Biblioteca de estilos de UI","Paletas de cores personalizadas","Pares de fontes recomendados","Tipos de gráficos","Recomendações de produtos","Diretrizes de UX"],"ru":["Библиотека стилей UI","Пользовательские цветовые палитры","Рекомендуемые пары шрифтов","Типы графиков","Рекомендации продуктов","Руководства по UX"],"ar":["مكتبة أنماط واجهة المستخدم","لوحات ألوان مخصصة","أزواج الخطوط الموصى بها","أنواع الرسومات","توصيات المنتجات","إرشادات تجربة المستخدم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["UI 设计","UX 设计","设计智能","开发工具","可搜索数据库"],"ja":["UI デザイン","UX デザイン","デザインインテリジェンス","開発ツール","検索可能なデータベース"],"ko":["UI 디자인","UX 디자인","디자인 인텔리전스","개발 도구","검색 가능한 데이터베이스"],"es":["diseño ui","ux","desarrollo web","estilos ui","paletas de colores","mejores prácticas","recomendaciones de productos"],"fr":["design ui","ux","développement web","styles ui","palettes de couleurs","meilleures pratiques","recommandations de produits"],"de":["ui-design","ux","webentwicklung","ui-stile","farbpaletten","best practices","produktempfehlungen"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de interfaces","ui/ux","design de interfaces","experiência do usuário","ferramentas de design","recursos de ui","biblioteca de estilos","paletas de cores","pares de fontes"],"ru":["разработка интерфейсов","ui/ux","проектирование интерфейсов","опыт пользователя","инструменты дизайна","ресурсы ui","библиотека стилей","цветовые палитры","пары шрифтов"],"ar":["تطوير الواجهات","ui/ux","تصميم الواجهات","تجربة المستخدم","أدوات التصميم","موارد واجهة المستخدم","مكتبة الأنماط","لوحات الألوان","أزواج الخطوط"]}},"owner":"binjuhor","repo":"shadcn-lar","repoPath":"binjuhor/shadcn-lar","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.410Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"ui-ux-pro-max","description":"Frontend UI/UX design intelligence - activate FIRST when user requests beautiful, stunning, gorgeous, or aesthetic interfaces. The primary skill for design decisions before implementation. 50 styles, 21 palettes, 50 font pairings, 20 charts, 8 stacks (React, Next.js, Vue, Svelte, SwiftUI, React Native, Flutter, Tailwind). Actions: plan, build, create, design, implement, review, fix, improve, optimize, enhance, refactor, check frontend UI/UX code. Projects: website, landing page, dashboard, admin panel, e-commerce, SaaS, portfolio, blog, mobile app, .html, .tsx, .vue, .svelte. Elements: button, modal, navbar, sidebar, card, table, form, chart. Styles: glassmorphism, claymorphism, minimalism, brutalism, neumorphism, bento grid, dark mode, responsive, skeuomorphism, flat design. Topics: color palette, accessibility, animation, layout, typography, font pairing, spacing, hover, shadow, gradient.","bodyPreview":"# UI/UX Pro Max - Design Intelligence\n\nSearchable database of UI styles, color palettes, font pairings, chart types, product recommendations, UX guidelines, and stack-specific best practices.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nCheck if Python is installed:\n\n```bash\npython3 --version || python --version\n```\n\nIf Python is not installed, install it based on user''s OS:\n\n**macOS:**\n```bash\nbrew install python3\n```\n\n**Ubuntu/Debian:**\n```bash\nsudo apt update && sudo apt install python3\n```\n\n**Windows:**\n```powershell","body":"# UI/UX Pro Max - Design Intelligence\n\nSearchable database of UI styles, color palettes, font pairings, chart types, product recommendations, UX guidelines, and stack-specific best practices.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nCheck if Python is installed:\n\n```bash\npython3 --version || python --version\n```\n\nIf Python is not installed, install it based on user''s OS:\n\n**macOS:**\n```bash\nbrew install python3\n```\n\n**Ubuntu/Debian:**\n```bash\nsudo apt update && sudo apt install python3\n```\n\n**Windows:**\n```powershell\nwinget install Python.Python.3.12\n```\n\n---\n\n## How to Use This Skill\n\nWhen user requests UI/UX work (design, build, create, implement, review, fix, improve), follow this workflow:\n\n### Step 1: Analyze User Requirements\n\nExtract key information from user request:\n- **Product type**: SaaS, e-commerce, portfolio, dashboard, landing page, etc.\n- **Style keywords**: minimal, playful, professional, elegant, dark mode, etc.\n- **Industry**: healthcare, fintech, gaming, education, etc.\n- **Stack**: React, Vue, Next.js, or default to `html-tailwind`\n\n### Step 2: Search Relevant Domains\n\nUse `search.py` multiple times to gather comprehensive information. Search until you have enough context.\n\n```bash\npython3 .claude/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"<keyword>\" --domain <domain> [-n <max_results>]\n```\n\n**Recommended search order:**\n\n1. **Product** - Get style recommendations for product type\n2. **Style** - Get detailed style guide (colors, effects, frameworks)\n3. **Typography** - Get font pairings with Google Fonts imports\n4. **Color** - Get color palette (Primary, Secondary, CTA, Background, Text, Border)\n5. **Landing** - Get page structure (if landing page)\n6. **Chart** - Get chart recommendations (if dashboard/analytics)\n7. **UX** - Get best practices and anti-patterns\n8. **Stack** - Get stack-specific guidelines (default: html-tailwind)\n\n### Step 3: Stack Guidelines (Default: html-tailwind)\n\nIf user doesn''t specify a stack, **default to `html-tailwind`**.\n\n```bash\npython3 .claude/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"<keyword>\" --stack html-tailwind\n```\n\nAvailable stacks: `html-tailwind`, `react`, `nextjs`, `vue`, `svelte`, `swiftui`, `react-native`, `flutter`\n\n---\n\n## Search Reference\n\n### Available Domains\n\n| Domain | Use For | Example Keywords |\n|--------|---------|------------------|\n| `product` | Product type recommendations | SaaS, e-commerce, portfolio, healthcare, beauty, service |\n| `style` | UI styles, colors, effects | glassmorphism, minimalism, dark mode, brutalism |\n| `typography` | Font pairings, Google Fonts | elegant, playful, professional, modern |\n| `color` | Color palettes by product type | saas, ecommerce, healthcare, beauty, fintech, service |\n| `landing` | Page structure, CTA strategies | hero, hero-centric, testimonial, pricing, social-proof |\n| `chart` | Chart types, library recommendations | trend, comparison, timeline, funnel, pie |\n| `ux` | Best practices, anti-patterns | animation, accessibility, z-index, loading |\n| `prompt` | AI prompts, CSS keywords | (style name) |\n\n### Available Stacks\n\n| Stack | Focus |\n|-------|-------|\n| `html-tailwind` | Tailwind utilities, responsive, a11y (DEFAULT) |\n| `react` | State, hooks, performance, patterns |\n| `nextjs` | SSR, routing, images, API routes |\n| `vue` | Composition API, Pinia, Vue Router |\n| `svelte` | Runes, stores, SvelteKit |\n| `swiftui` | Views, State, Navigation, Animation |\n| `react-native` | Components, Navigation, Lists |\n| `flutter` | Widgets, State, Layout, Theming |\n\n---\n\n## Example Workflow\n\n**User request:** \"Làm landing page cho dịch vụ chăm sóc da chuyên nghiệp\"\n\n**AI should:**\n\n```bash\n# 1. Search product type\npython3 .claude/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"beauty spa wellness service\" --domain product\n\n# 2. Search style (based on industry: beauty, elegant)\npython3 .claude/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"elegant minimal soft\" --domain style\n\n# 3. Search typography\npython3 .claude/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"elegant luxury\" --domain typography\n\n# 4. Search color palette\npython3 .claude/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"beauty spa wellness\" --domain color\n\n# 5. Search landing page structure\npython3 .claude/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"hero-centric social-proof\" --domain landing\n\n# 6. Search UX guidelines\npython3 .claude/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"animation\" --domain ux\npython3 .claude/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"accessibility\" --domain ux\n\n# 7. Search stack guidelines (default: html-tailwind)\npython3 .claude/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"layout responsive\" --stack html-tailwind\n```\n\n**Then:** Synthesize all search results and implement the design.\n\n---\n\n## Tips for Better Results\n\n1. **Be specific with keywords** - \"healthcare SaaS dashboard\" > \"app\"\n2. **Search multiple times** - Different keywords reveal different insights\n3. **Combine domains** - Style + Typography + Color = Complete design system\n4. **Always check UX** - Search \"animation\", \"z-index\", \"accessibility\" for common issues\n5. **Use stack flag** - Get implementation-specific best practices\n6. **Iterate** - If first search doesn''t match, try different keywords\n\n---\n\n## Common Rules for Professional UI\n\nThese are frequently overlooked issues that make UI look unprofessional:\n\n### Icons & Visual Elements\n\n| Rule | Do | Don''t |\n|------|----|----- |\n| **No emoji icons** | Use SVG icons (Heroicons, Lucide, Simple Icons) | Use emojis like 🎨 🚀 ⚙️ as UI icons |\n| **Stable hover states** | Use color/opacity transitions on hover | Use scale transforms that shift layout |\n| **Correct brand logos** | Research official SVG from Simple Icons | Guess or use incorrect logo paths |\n| **Consistent icon sizing** | Use fixed viewBox (24x24) with w-6 h-6 | Mix different icon sizes randomly |\n\n### Interaction & Cursor\n\n| Rule | Do | Don''t |\n|------|----|----- |\n| **Cursor pointer** | Add `cursor-pointer` to all clickable/hoverable cards | Leave default cursor on interactive elements |\n| **Hover feedback** | Provide visual feedback (color, shadow, border) | No indication element is interactive |\n| **Smooth transitions** | Use `transition-colors duration-200` | Instant state changes or too slow (>500ms) |\n\n### Light/Dark Mode Contrast\n\n| Rule | Do | Don''t |\n|------|----|----- |\n| **Glass card light mode** | Use `bg-white/80` or higher opacity | Use `bg-white/10` (too transparent) |\n| **Text contrast light** | Use `#0F172A` (slate-900) for text | Use `#94A3B8` (slate-400) for body text |\n| **Muted text light** | Use `#475569` (slate-600) minimum | Use gray-400 or lighter |\n| **Border visibility** | Use `border-gray-200` in light mode | Use `border-white/10` (invisible) |\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n\n| Rule | Do | Don''t |\n|------|----|----- |\n| **Floating navbar** | Add `top-4 left-4 right-4` spacing | Stick navbar to `top-0 left-0 right-0` |\n| **Content padding** | Account for fixed navbar height | Let content hide behind fixed elements |\n| **Consistent max-width** | Use same `max-w-6xl` or `max-w-7xl` | Mix different container widths |\n\n---\n\n## Pre-Delivery Checklist\n\nBefore delivering UI code, verify these items:\n\n### Visual Quality\n- [ ] No emojis used as icons (use SVG instead)\n- [ ] All icons from consistent icon set (Heroicons/Lucide)\n- [ ] Brand logos are correct (verified from Simple Icons)\n- [ ] Hover states don''t cause layout shift\n\n### Interaction\n- [ ] All clickable elements have `cursor-pointer`\n- [ ] Hover states provide clear visual feedback\n- [ ] Transitions are smooth (150-300ms)\n- [ ] Focus states visible for keyboard navigation\n\n### Light/Dark Mode\n- [ ] Light mode text has sufficient contrast (4.5:1 minimum)\n- [ ] Glass/transparent elements visible in light mode\n- [ ] Borders visible in both modes\n- [ ] Test both modes before delivery\n\n### Layout\n- [ ] Floating elements have proper spacing from edges\n- [ ] No content hidden behind fixed navbars\n- [ ] Responsive at 320px, 768px, 1024px, 1440px\n- [ ] No horizontal scroll on mobile\n\n### Accessibility\n- [ ] All images have alt text\n- [ ] Form inputs have labels\n- [ ] Color is not the only indicator\n- [ ] `prefers-reduced-motion` respected\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:37:47.140Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Design-focused Agents needing advanced UI/UX intelligence with searchable databases of UI styles and color palettes.","zh":"非常适合需要高级 UI/UX 智能和可搜索的 UI 样式及色彩板数据库的设计导向型代理。","ja":"デザイン中心のエージェントが高度な UI/UX インテリジェンスと検索可能な UI スタイルおよび色パレットのデータベースを必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 UI/UX 지능 및 검색 가능한 UI 스타일 및 색상 팔레트 데이터베이스가 필요한 디자인 중심 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes enfocados en diseño que necesitan inteligencia avanzada de UI/UX con bases de datos de estilos de interfaz de usuario y paletas de colores que se pueden buscar.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents axés sur la conception nécessitant une intelligence UI/UX avancée avec des bases de données de styles d''interface utilisateur et de palettes de couleurs recherchables.","de":"Perfekt für designorientierte Agenten, die erweiterte UI/UX-Intelligenz mit durchsuchbaren Datenbanken von Benutzeroberflächenstilen und Farbpaletten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes focados em Design que necessitam de inteligência avançada de UI/UX com bancos de dados pesquisáveis de estilos de UI e paletas de cores.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов, ориентированных на дизайн, которым требуется продвинутая интеллект UI/UX с поисковыми базами данных стилей UI и цветовых палитр.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذين يركزون على التصميم وهم في حاجة إلى ذكاء متقدم لوي/UX مع قواعد بيانات قابلة للبحث من أنماط واجهة المستخدم وألوان البالت"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage a searchable database of UI styles, color palettes, font pairings, and UX guidelines, utilizing Python for seamless integration and analysis, including stack-specific best practices and product recommendations.","zh":"赋予代理利用可搜索的 UI 风格、色彩板、字体配对和 UX 指南数据库的能力，利用 Python 实现无缝集成和分析，包括特定堆栈的最佳实践和产品推荐。","ja":"エージェントが検索可能な UI スタイル、色パレット、フォントのペア、UX ガイドラインのデータベースを利用できるようにし、Python を使用してシームレスな統合と分析を実現し、スタック固有のベストプラクティスと製品の推奨事項を含む。","ko":"에이전트가 검색 가능한 UI 스타일, 색상 팔레트, 글꼴 페어 및 UX 가이드ライン 데이터베이스를 활용할 수 있도록 하며, Python을 사용하여 무결점 통합 및 분석을 구현하며, 스택 특정 최선의 관행 및 제품 추천을 포함합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aprovechar una base de datos de estilos de interfaz de usuario, paletas de colores, combinaciones de fuentes y pautas de UX, utilizando Python para una integración y análisis sin problemas, incluyendo las mejores prácticas y recomendaciones de productos específicas de la pila.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''utiliser une base de données de styles d''interface utilisateur, de palettes de couleurs, de combinaisons de polices et de lignes directrices UX, en utilisant Python pour une intégration et une analyse sans effort, y compris les meilleures pratiques et les recommandations de produits spécifiques à la pile.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, eine Datenbank von Benutzeroberflächenstilen, Farbpaletten, Schriftkombinationen und UX-Richtlinien zu nutzen, unter Verwendung von Python für eine nahtlose Integration und Analyse, einschließlich stapelspezifischer Best Practices und Produktempfehlungen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aproveitar um banco de dados pesquisável de estilos de UI, paletas de cores, combinações de fontes e diretrizes de UX, utilizando Python para integração e análise sem problemas, incluindo as melhores práticas específicas de pilha e recomendações de produtos.","ru":"Позволяет агентам использовать поисковую базу данных стилей UI, цветовых палитр, пар(font) шрифтов и руководств по UX, используя Python для бесшовной интеграции и анализа, включая рекомендации по лучшим практикам для конкретных стеков и продуктах.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من الاستفادة من قاعدة بيانات قابلة للبحث من أنماط واجهة المستخدم وألوان البالت وتركيبات الخطوط وإرشادات تجربة المستخدم، باستخدام بايثون من أجل التكامل السلس والتحليل، بما في ذلك أفضل الممارسات المحددة للكومة وتوصيات المنتجات"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating UI design suggestions","Generating compatible color palettes for brand consistency","Debugging UX issues with guidelines and best practices"],"zh":["自动化 UI 设计建议","生成与品牌一致的兼容色彩板","使用指南和最佳实践调试 UX 问题"],"ja":["UI デザインの提案を自動化する","ブランドの統一性を保つための互換性のある色パレットを生成する","ガイドラインとベストプラクティスを使用して UX の問題をデバッグする"],"ko":["UI 디자인 제안 자동화","브랜드 일관성을 위한 호환 색상 팔레트 생성","가이드라인 및 최선의 관행을 사용하여 UX 문제 디버깅"],"es":["Automatizar sugerencias de diseño de interfaz de usuario","Generar paletas de colores compatibles para la coherencia de la marca","Depurar problemas de UX con pautas y mejores prácticas"],"fr":["Automatiser les suggestions de conception d''interface utilisateur","Générer des palettes de couleurs compatibles pour la cohérence de la marque","Déboguer les problèmes d''UX avec des lignes directrices et des meilleures pratiques"],"de":["Automatisieren von Vorschlägen für die Benutzeroberflächengestaltung","Erzeugen von kompatiblen Farbpaletten für Markenkontinuität","Fehlerbehebung bei UX-Problemen mit Richtlinien und Best Practices"],"pt":["Automatizar sugestões de design de UI","Gerar paletas de cores compatíveis para consistência da marca","Depurar problemas de UX com diretrizes e melhores práticas"],"ru":["Автоматизировать предложения по дизайну UI","Генерировать совместимые цветовые палитры для согласованности бренда","Отладить проблемы UX с помощью руководств и лучших практик"],"ar":["أتمتة اقتراحات تصميم واجهة المستخدم","توليد ألوان البالت المتوافقة لاتساق العلامة التجارية","تصحيح أخطاء UX باستخدام الإرشادات وأفضل الممارسات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python installation","Limited to design and UI/UX analysis tasks"],"zh":["需要 Python 安装","仅限设计和 UI/UX 分析任务"],"ja":["Python のインストールが必要","デザインと UI/UX 分析タスクのみに限定される"],"ko":["Python 설치 필요","디자인 및 UI/UX 분석 작업만 해당"],"es":["Requiere instalación de Python","Limitado a tareas de análisis de diseño y UI/UX"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de Python","Limité aux tâches d''analyse de conception et d''UX/UI"],"de":["Benötigt Python-Installation","Begrenzt auf Design- und UI/UX-Analyseaufgaben"],"pt":["Requer instalação do Python","Limitado a tarefas de análise de design e UI/UX"],"ru":["Требует установку Python","Ограничен задачами анализа дизайна и UI/UX"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت بايثون","محدود بمهام تحليل التصميم وتجربة المستخدم"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('vechain/inspector-app/karpathy-guidelines', 'community', 'vechain', 'inspector-app', 'vechain/inspector-app', 'karpathy-guidelines', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.410Z', '2026-02-18T03:37:54.818Z', NULL, '{"id":"vechain/inspector-app/karpathy-guidelines","name":"karpathy-guidelines","description":{"zh":"Karpathy 指南提供智能合约开发最佳实践，帮助开发者减少常见的 LLM 编码错误","ja":"Karpathy ガイドラインは、スマートコントラクト開発のベストプラクティスを提供し、開発者が一般的な LLM コーディング エラーを減らすのに役立ちます","ko":"Karpathy 가이드라인은 스마트 계약 개발 모범 사례를 제공하여 개발자가 일반적인 LLM 코딩 오류를 줄일 수 있습니다","es":"Herramienta de exploración de contratos inteligentes para interactuar con contratos en redes VeChain, basada en las guías de Karpathy.","fr":"Outil d''exploration de contrats intelligents pour interagir avec des contrats sur les réseaux VeChain, basé sur les lignes directrices de Karpathy.","de":"Smart-Contract-Explorer-Tool zum Interagieren mit Verträgen in VeChain-Netzwerken, basierend auf den Karpathy-Richtlinien.","pt":"As diretrizes Karpathy são um conjunto de orientações para reduzir erros comuns de codificação em LLM, derivadas das observações de Andrej Karpathy","ru":"Руководство Karpathy - это набор рекомендаций для снижения распространенных ошибок кодирования в LLM, основанный на наблюдениях Андрея Карпатья","ar":"إرشادات Karpathy هي مجموعة من الإرشادات لخفض الأخطاء الشائعة في ترميز LLM، المشتق من ملاحظات أندريه كارباثي","en":"Smart contract explorer tool: interact with contracts on VeChain networks"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Karpathy 指南：智能合约开发最佳实践","ja":"Karpathy ガイドライン：スマートコントラクト開発のベストプラクティス","ko":"Karpathy 가이드라인: 스마트 계약 개발 모범 사례","es":"Explorador de contratos inteligentes en VeChain","fr":"Outil d''exploration de contrats intelligents sur VeChain","de":"Smart-Contract-Explorer für VeChain-Netzwerke","pt":"Karpathy Guidelines: Ferramenta de Exploração de Contrato...","ru":"Руководство Karpathy: Инструмент для работы с умными конт...","ar":"إرشادات Karpathy: أداة استكشاف العقد الذكي","en":"karpathy-guidelines"},"description":{"zh":"Karpathy 指南提供智能合约开发最佳实践，帮助开发者减少常见的 LLM 编码错误","ja":"Karpathy ガイドラインは、スマートコントラクト開発のベストプラクティスを提供し、開発者が一般的な LLM コーディング エラーを減らすのに役立ちます","ko":"Karpathy 가이드라인은 스마트 계약 개발 모범 사례를 제공하여 개발자가 일반적인 LLM 코딩 오류를 줄일 수 있습니다","es":"Herramienta de exploración de contratos inteligentes para interactuar con contratos en redes VeChain, basada en las guías de Karpathy.","fr":"Outil d''exploration de contrats intelligents pour interagir avec des contrats sur les réseaux VeChain, basé sur les lignes directrices de Karpathy.","de":"Smart-Contract-Explorer-Tool zum Interagieren mit Verträgen in VeChain-Netzwerken, basierend auf den Karpathy-Richtlinien.","pt":"As diretrizes Karpathy são um conjunto de orientações para reduzir erros comuns de codificação em LLM, derivadas das observações de Andrej Karpathy","ru":"Руководство Karpathy - это набор рекомендаций для снижения распространенных ошибок кодирования в LLM, основанный на наблюдениях Андрея Карпатья","ar":"إرشادات Karpathy هي مجموعة من الإرشادات لخفض الأخطاء الشائعة في ترميز LLM، المشتق من ملاحظات أندريه كارباثي","en":"Smart contract explorer tool: interact with contracts on VeChain networks"},"definition":{"en":"Smart contract explorer tool: interact with contracts on VeChain networks"},"features":{"zh":["明确假设","避免混淆","表面化权衡","智能合约开发最佳实践","减少 LLM 编码错误"],"ja":["仮定を明確にする","混乱を避ける","トレードオフを表面化する","スマートコントラクト開発のベストプラクティス","LLM コーディング エラーを減らす"],"ko":["가정 사항을 명확히 한다","혼란을 피한다","트레이드 오프를 표면화한다","스마트 계약 개발 모범 사례","LLM 코딩 오류를 줄인다"],"es":["Interacción con contratos en redes VeChain","Guías de Karpathy para reducir errores de codificación","Análisis de tradeoffs y suposiciones explícitas","Interfaz de usuario intuitiva para desarrolladores","Compatibilidad con múltiples interpretaciones de contratos","Enfoque en la cautela y la claridad en el codificado"],"fr":["Interaction avec des contrats sur les réseaux VeChain","Lignes directrices de Karpathy pour réduire les erreurs de codage","Analyse des compromis et des suppositions explicites","Interface utilisateur intuitive pour les développeurs","Compatibilité avec plusieurs interprétations de contrats","Focus sur la prudence et la clarté dans le codage"],"de":["Interaktion mit Verträgen in VeChain-Netzwerken","Karpathy-Richtlinien zur Reduzierung von Codierfehlern","Analyse von Tradeoffs und expliziten Annahmen","Benutzerfreundliche Oberfläche für Entwickler","Kompatibilität mit mehreren Vertragsinterpretationen","Fokus auf Vorsicht und Klarheit im Codieren"],"pt":["Interaja com contratos na rede VeChain","Reduza erros comuns de codificação em LLM","Aprenda com as observações de Andrej Karpathy","Melhore a segurança dos seus contratos inteligentes","Otimize a eficiência do seu código"],"ru":["Работайте с умными контрактами в сети VeChain","Снизьте распространенные ошибки кодирования в LLM","Изучите наблюдения Андрея Карпатья","Улучшите безопасность своих умных контрактов","Оптимизируйте эффективность своего кода"],"ar":["التفاعل مع العقود الذكية على شبكة في تشين","خفض الأخطاء الشائعة في ترميز LLM","تعلم من ملاحظات أندريه كارباثي","تحسين أمان العقود الذكية الخاصة بك","تحسين كفاءة الكود الخاص بك"]},"keywords":{"zh":["智能合约","LLM","编码错误","开发最佳实践","Karpathy 指南","VeChain"],"ja":["スマートコントラクト","LLM","コーディング エラー","開発ベストプラクティス","Karpathy ガイドライン","VeChain"],"ko":["스마트 계약","LLM","코딩 오류","개발 모범 사례","Karpathy 가이드라인","VeChain"],"es":["contratos inteligentes","VeChain","Karpathy","codificación","desarrollo de blockchain","herramientas de desarrollo","explorador de contratos","seguridad de contratos","mejores prácticas de codificación"],"fr":["contrats intelligents","VeChain","Karpathy","codage","développement de blockchain","outils de développement","outil d''exploration de contrats","sécurité des contrats","meilleures pratiques de codage"],"de":["Smart-Contrakt","VeChain","Karpathy","Codieren","Blockchain-Entwicklung","Entwicklungstools","Smart-Contract-Explorer","Vertragsicherheit","Best-Practices-Codieren"],"pt":["Karpathy Guidelines","Contratos Inteligentes","VeChain","LLM","Codificação","Segurança","Eficiência","Desenvolvimento de Software"],"ru":["Руководство Karpathy","Умные контракты","VeChain","LLM","Кодирование","Безопасность","Эффективность","Разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["إرشادات Karpathy","العقود الذكية","في تشين","LLM","الترميز","الأمان","الكفاءة","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"vechain","repo":"inspector-app","repoPath":"vechain/inspector-app","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.410Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"karpathy-guidelines","description":"Behavioral guidelines to reduce common LLM coding mistakes. Use when writing, reviewing, or refactoring code to avoid overcomplication, make surgical changes, surface assumptions, and define verifiable success criteria.","bodyPreview":"# Karpathy Guidelines\n\nBehavioral guidelines to reduce common LLM coding mistakes, derived from [Andrej Karpathy''s observations](https://x.com/karpathy/status/2015883857489522876) on LLM coding pitfalls.\n\n**Tradeoff:** These guidelines bias toward caution over speed. For trivial tasks, use judgment.\n\n## 1. Think Before Coding\n\n**Don''t assume. Don''t hide confusion. Surface tradeoffs.**\n\nBefore implementing:\n\n- State your assumptions explicitly. If uncertain, ask.\n- If multiple interpretations exi","body":"# Karpathy Guidelines\n\nBehavioral guidelines to reduce common LLM coding mistakes, derived from [Andrej Karpathy''s observations](https://x.com/karpathy/status/2015883857489522876) on LLM coding pitfalls.\n\n**Tradeoff:** These guidelines bias toward caution over speed. For trivial tasks, use judgment.\n\n## 1. Think Before Coding\n\n**Don''t assume. Don''t hide confusion. Surface tradeoffs.**\n\nBefore implementing:\n\n- State your assumptions explicitly. If uncertain, ask.\n- If multiple interpretations exist, present them - don''t pick silently.\n- If a simpler approach exists, say so. Push back when warranted.\n- If something is unclear, stop. Name what''s confusing. Ask.\n\n## 2. Simplicity First\n\n**Minimum code that solves the problem. Nothing speculative.**\n\n- No features beyond what was asked.\n- No abstractions for single-use code.\n- No \"flexibility\" or \"configurability\" that wasn''t requested.\n- No error handling for impossible scenarios.\n- If you write 200 lines and it could be 50, rewrite it.\n\nAsk yourself: \"Would a senior engineer say this is overcomplicated?\" If yes, simplify.\n\n## 3. Surgical Changes\n\n**Touch only what you must. Clean up only your own mess.**\n\nWhen editing existing code:\n\n- Don''t \"improve\" adjacent code, comments, or formatting.\n- Don''t refactor things that aren''t broken.\n- Match existing style, even if you''d do it differently.\n- If you notice unrelated dead code, mention it - don''t delete it.\n\nWhen your changes create orphans:\n\n- Remove imports/variables/functions that YOUR changes made unused.\n- Don''t remove pre-existing dead code unless asked.\n\nThe test: Every changed line should trace directly to the user''s request.\n\n## 4. Goal-Driven Execution\n\n**Define success criteria. Loop until verified.**\n\nTransform tasks into verifiable goals:\n\n- \"Add validation\" → \"Write tests for invalid inputs, then make them pass\"\n- \"Fix the bug\" → \"Write a test that reproduces it, then make it pass\"\n- \"Refactor X\" → \"Ensure tests pass before and after\"\n\nFor multi-step tasks, state a brief plan:\n\n```\n1. [Step] → verify: [check]\n2. [Step] → verify: [check]\n3. [Step] → verify: [check]\n```\n\nStrong success criteria let you loop independently. Weak criteria (\"make it work\") require constant clarification.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:37:54.818Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for LLM Coding Agents needing behavioral guidelines to reduce common coding mistakes","zh":"非常适合需要行为指南以减少常见编码错误的 LLM 编码代理","ja":"LLM コーディング エージェントが一般的なコーディング ミスを減らすために行動ガイドラインを必要とする場合に最適","ko":"일반적인 코딩 실수를 줄이기 위한 행동 지침이 필요한 LLM 코딩 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de codificación LLM que necesitan pautas de comportamiento para reducir errores de codificación comunes","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de codage LLM ayant besoin de lignes directrices de comportement pour réduire les erreurs de codage courantes","de":"Perfekt für LLM-Coding-Agents, die Verhaltensrichtlinien benötigen, um häufige Codierfehler zu reduzieren","pt":"Perfect for LLM Coding Agents needing behavioral guidelines to reduce common coding mistakes","ru":"Perfect for LLM Coding Agents needing behavioral guidelines to reduce common coding mistakes","ar":"Perfect for LLM Coding Agents needing behavioral guidelines to reduce common coding mistakes"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to surface tradeoffs, state assumptions explicitly, and avoid hidden confusion by following Andrej Karpathy''s observations on LLM coding pitfalls, utilizing caution over speed for non-trivial tasks and judgment for trivial ones","zh":"赋予代理能力以表面化权衡、明确说明假设并避免通过遵循 Andrej Karpathy 关于 LLM 编码陷阱的观察来避免隐藏的混淆，利用谨慎而非速度来处理非平凡任务，并利用判断来处理平凡任务","ja":"エージェントにトレードオフを浮き彫りにし、仮定を明示的に記述し、Andrej Karpathy の LLM コーディングの落とし穴に関する観察に従うことで隠れた混乱を避ける能力を与え、非自明なタスクには慎重さを、自明なタスクには判断力を優先する","ko":"에이전트가 트레이드 오프를 표면화하고 가정을 명시적으로说明하고 Andrej Karpathy의 LLM 코딩 함정에 대한 관찰을 따라 숨겨진 혼란을 피하며 비자명한 작업에는 신중함을 자명한 작업에는 판단력을 우선하여 활용할 수 있도록 해줌","es":"Habilita a los agentes a mostrar compensaciones, declarar suposiciones explícitamente y evitar confusiones ocultas siguiendo las observaciones de Andrej Karpathy sobre las trampas de codificación LLM, utilizando la precaución sobre la velocidad para tareas no triviales y el juicio para las triviales","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en évidence les compromis, de déclarer explicitement les hypothèses et d''éviter les confusions cachées en suivant les observations d''Andrej Karpathy sur les pièges de codage LLM, en utilisant la prudence plutôt que la vitesse pour les tâches non triviales et le jugement pour les tâches triviales","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Kompromisse zu offenbaren, Annahmen explizit zu machen und versteckte Verwirrung zu vermeiden, indem sie die Beobachtungen von Andrej Karpathy zu LLM-Coding-Fallen befolgen, Vorsicht vor Geschwindigkeit bei nicht trivialem Aufgaben und Urteilsvermögen bei trivialen Aufgaben","pt":"Empowers agents to surface tradeoffs, state assumptions explicitly, and avoid hidden confusion by following Andrej Karpathy''s observations on LLM coding pitfalls, utilizing caution over speed for non-trivial tasks and judgment for trivial ones","ru":"Empowers agents to surface tradeoffs, state assumptions explicitly, and avoid hidden confusion by following Andrej Karpathy''s observations on LLM coding pitfalls, utilizing caution over speed for non-trivial tasks and judgment for trivial ones","ar":"Empowers agents to surface tradeoffs, state assumptions explicitly, and avoid hidden confusion by following Andrej Karpathy''s observations on LLM coding pitfalls, utilizing caution over speed for non-trivial tasks and judgment for trivial ones"},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging LLM generated code","Generating explicit assumptions for coding tasks","Avoiding hidden confusion in contract interactions on VeChain networks"],"zh":["调试 LLM 生成的代码","为编码任务生成明确的假设","避免 VeChain 网络上合同交互中的隐藏混淆"],"ja":["LLM によって生成されたコードのデバッグ","コーディング タスクのための明示的な仮定の生成","VeChain ネットワーク上の契約のやり取りにおける隠れた混乱の回避"],"ko":["LLM이 생성한 코드 디버깅","코딩 작업을 위한 명시적 가설 생성","VeChain 네트워크上的 계약 상호작용에서 숨겨진 혼란 피하기"],"es":["Depuración de código generado por LLM","Generación de suposiciones explícitas para tareas de codificación","Evitación de confusión oculta en interacciones de contrato en redes VeChain"],"fr":["Débogage de code généré par LLM","Génération d''hypothèses explicites pour les tâches de codage","Évitement de confusion cachée dans les interactions de contrat sur les réseaux VeChain"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung von LLM-generiertem Code","Erzeugung von expliziten Annahmen für Codierungsaufgaben","Vermeidung von versteckter Verwirrung bei Vertragsinteraktionen in VeChain-Netzwerken"],"pt":["Debugging LLM generated code","Generating explicit assumptions for coding tasks","Avoiding hidden confusion in contract interactions on VeChain networks"],"ru":["Debugging LLM generated code","Generating explicit assumptions for coding tasks","Avoiding hidden confusion in contract interactions on VeChain networks"],"ar":["Debugging LLM generated code","Generating explicit assumptions for coding tasks","Avoiding hidden confusion in contract interactions on VeChain networks"]},"limitations":{"en":["Biases toward caution over speed","Requires judgment for trivial tasks","Derived from specific observations on LLM coding pitfalls"],"zh":["偏向谨慎而非速度","需要对自明任务进行判断","源自对 LLM 编码陷阱的特定观察"],"ja":["速度よりも慎重さへの偏り","自明なタスクには判断が必要","LLM コーディングの落とし穴に関する特定の観察に基づく"],"ko":["속도보다 신중함으로의 편향","자명한 작업에는 판단력이 필요","LLM 코딩 함정에 대한 특정 관찰에서 파생"],"es":["Sesgos hacia la precaución sobre la velocidad","Requiere juicio para tareas triviales","Derivado de observaciones específicas sobre trampas de codificación LLM"],"fr":["Biais en faveur de la prudence plutôt que de la vitesse","Nécessite un jugement pour les tâches triviales","Dérivé d''observations spécifiques sur les pièges de codage LLM"],"de":["Voreingenommenheit gegenüber Vorsicht vor Geschwindigkeit","Erfordert Urteilsvermögen für triviale Aufgaben","Abgeleitet aus spezifischen Beobachtungen zu LLM-Coding-Fallen"],"pt":["Biases toward caution over speed","Requires judgment for trivial tasks","Derived from specific observations on LLM coding pitfalls"],"ru":["Biases toward caution over speed","Requires judgment for trivial tasks","Derived from specific observations on LLM coding pitfalls"],"ar":["Biases toward caution over speed","Requires judgment for trivial tasks","Derived from specific observations on LLM coding pitfalls"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
