para sistemas distribuidos","Inclusión de timestamps en cada tabla","Diseño de esquemas de base de datos escalables","Prácticas de seguridad para bases de datos"],"fr":["Normalisation des schémas de base de données","Utilisation de UUIDs pour les systèmes distribués","Inclusion de timestamps dans chaque tableau","Conception de schémas de base de données évolutifs","Pratiques de sécurité pour les bases de données"],"de":["Normalisierung von Datenbankschemata","Verwendung von UUIDs für verteilte Systeme","Einclusion von Timestamps in jede Tabelle","Entwurf von skalierbaren Datenbankschemata","Sicherheitspraktiken für Datenbanken"],"pt":["Normalização de esquemas de banco de dados","Uso de UUIDs em vez de auto-incremento","Inclusão de carimbos de data e hora em todas as tabelas","Projeto de banco de dados para sistemas distribuídos","Garantia de consistência e escalabilidade dos dados"],"ru":["Нормализация схем баз данных","Использование UUID вместо авто-инкремента","Включение временных штампов во все таблицы","Проектирование баз данных для распределенных систем","Гарантия согласованности и масштабируемости данных"],"ar":["تطبيقات التطبيقات للمخططات قواعد البيانات","استخدام UUID بدلاً من التزايد التلقائي","إدراج طوابع التاريخ والوقت في جميع الجداول","تصميم قواعد البيانات لأنظمة موزعة","ضمان الاتساق والقابلية للتحجيم للبيانات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["数据库模式","数据库设计","模式设计原则","UUID","时间戳","数据表 normalization","数据库安全性","数据库性能"],"ja":["データベースパターン","データベース設計","スキーマ設計原則","UUID","タイムスタンプ","テーブルの正規化","データベースセキュリティ","データベースパフォーマンス"],"ko":["데이터베이스 패턴","데이터베이스 설계","스키마 설계 원칙","UUID","타임스탬프","테이블의 정규화","데이터베이스 보안성","데이터베이스 성능"],"es":["patrones de base de datos","diseño de esquemas de base de datos","normalización de base de datos","UUIDs en base de datos","seguridad de base de datos","desarrollo de aplicaciones","base de datos relacional","bases de datos NoSQL"],"fr":["modèles de base de données","conception de schémas de base de données","normalisation de base de données","UUIDs dans les bases de données","sécurité des bases de données","développement d''applications","base de données relationnelle","bases de données NoSQL"],"de":["Datenbankmuster","Entwurf von Datenbankschemata","Normalisierung von Datenbanken","UUIDs in Datenbanken","Datenbanksicherheit","Anwendungsentwicklung","relationale Datenbank","NoSQL-Datenbanken"],"pt":["padrões de banco de dados","desenvolvimento de software","normalização de esquemas","UUID","carimbos de data e hora","sistemas distribuídos","consistência de dados","escalabilidade de dados"],"ru":["шаблоны баз данных","разработка программного обеспечения","нормализация схем","UUID","временные штампы","распределенные системы","согласованность данных","масштабируемость данных"],"ar":["أنماط قواعد البيانات","تطوير البرمجيات","تطبيقات المخططات","UUID","طوابع التاريخ والوقت","نظم موزعة","اتساق البيانات","قابلية التحجيم للبيانات"]}},"owner":"Wania-Kazmi","repo":"claude-code-autonomous-agent-workflow","repoPath":"Wania-Kazmi/claude-code-autonomous-agent-workflow","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.411Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"database-patterns","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# Database Patterns & Best Practices\n\n## Schema Design Principles\n\n### 1. Normalization (3NF minimum)\n- No repeating groups\n- No partial dependencies\n- No transitive dependencies\n\n### 2. Use UUIDs vs Auto-Increment\n```sql\n-- GOOD: UUID for distributed systems\nid UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()\n\n-- OK: Auto-increment for simple cases\nid SERIAL PRIMARY KEY\n```\n\n### 3. Timestamps on Every Table\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE users (\n  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  name VARCHAR(10","body":"# Database Patterns & Best Practices\n\n## Schema Design Principles\n\n### 1. Normalization (3NF minimum)\n- No repeating groups\n- No partial dependencies\n- No transitive dependencies\n\n### 2. Use UUIDs vs Auto-Increment\n```sql\n-- GOOD: UUID for distributed systems\nid UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()\n\n-- OK: Auto-increment for simple cases\nid SERIAL PRIMARY KEY\n```\n\n### 3. Timestamps on Every Table\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE users (\n  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,\n  email VARCHAR(255) UNIQUE NOT NULL,\n  created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW(),\n  updated_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW()\n);\n```\n\n## Prisma ORM Patterns\n\n### Schema Definition\n\n```prisma\n// prisma/schema.prisma\ngenerator client {\n  provider = \"prisma-client-js\"\n}\n\ndatasource db {\n  provider = \"postgresql\"\n  url      = env(\"DATABASE_URL\")\n}\n\nmodel User {\n  id        String   @id @default(uuid())\n  email     String   @unique\n  name      String\n  role      Role     @default(USER)\n  posts     Post[]\n  profile   Profile?\n  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt\n\n  @@index([email])\n  @@map(\"users\")\n}\n\nmodel Post {\n  id        String   @id @default(uuid())\n  title     String\n  content   String?\n  published Boolean  @default(false)\n  author    User     @relation(fields: [authorId], references: [id])\n  authorId  String\n  tags      Tag[]\n  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt\n\n  @@index([authorId])\n  @@index([published])\n  @@map(\"posts\")\n}\n\nenum Role {\n  USER\n  ADMIN\n}\n```\n\n### CRUD Operations\n\n```typescript\nimport { PrismaClient } from ''@prisma/client''\n\nconst prisma = new PrismaClient()\n\n// Create\nasync function createUser(data: { name: string; email: string }) {\n  return prisma.user.create({\n    data,\n    select: {\n      id: true,\n      name: true,\n      email: true,\n      createdAt: true\n    }\n  })\n}\n\n// Read with relations\nasync function getUserWithPosts(id: string) {\n  return prisma.user.findUnique({\n    where: { id },\n    include: {\n      posts: {\n        where: { published: true },\n        orderBy: { createdAt: ''desc'' },\n        take: 10\n      },\n      profile: true\n    }\n  })\n}\n\n// Update\nasync function updateUser(id: string, data: Partial<User>) {\n  return prisma.user.update({\n    where: { id },\n    data\n  })\n}\n\n// Delete (soft delete pattern)\nasync function deleteUser(id: string) {\n  return prisma.user.update({\n    where: { id },\n    data: { deletedAt: new Date() }\n  })\n}\n```\n\n### Transactions\n\n```typescript\n// Interactive transaction\nasync function transferFunds(fromId: string, toId: string, amount: number) {\n  return prisma.$transaction(async (tx) => {\n    const from = await tx.account.update({\n      where: { id: fromId },\n      data: { balance: { decrement: amount } }\n    })\n\n    if (from.balance < 0) {\n      throw new Error(''Insufficient funds'')\n    }\n\n    await tx.account.update({\n      where: { id: toId },\n      data: { balance: { increment: amount } }\n    })\n\n    return tx.transaction.create({\n      data: { fromId, toId, amount }\n    })\n  })\n}\n\n// Sequential transaction\nasync function createUserWithProfile(data: CreateUserInput) {\n  return prisma.$transaction([\n    prisma.user.create({ data: data.user }),\n    prisma.profile.create({ data: data.profile })\n  ])\n}\n```\n\n### Pagination\n\n```typescript\n// Cursor-based (recommended for large datasets)\nasync function getUsers(cursor?: string, limit = 20) {\n  const users = await prisma.user.findMany({\n    take: limit + 1,\n    cursor: cursor ? { id: cursor } : undefined,\n    orderBy: { createdAt: ''desc'' },\n    skip: cursor ? 1 : 0 // Skip the cursor itself\n  })\n\n  const hasMore = users.length > limit\n  const data = hasMore ? users.slice(0, -1) : users\n\n  return {\n    data,\n    nextCursor: hasMore ? data[data.length - 1].id : null\n  }\n}\n\n// Offset-based\nasync function getUsersWithOffset(page = 1, limit = 20) {\n  const [users, total] = await Promise.all([\n    prisma.user.findMany({\n      skip: (page - 1) * limit,\n      take: limit\n    }),\n    prisma.user.count()\n  ])\n\n  return {\n    data: users,\n    meta: { total, page, limit, totalPages: Math.ceil(total / limit) }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Query Optimization\n\n### Avoid N+1 Queries\n\n```typescript\n// BAD: N+1 problem\nconst users = await prisma.user.findMany()\nfor (const user of users) {\n  const posts = await prisma.post.findMany({\n    where: { authorId: user.id }\n  })\n}\n\n// GOOD: Include in single query\nconst users = await prisma.user.findMany({\n  include: { posts: true }\n})\n\n// GOOD: Select only needed fields\nconst users = await prisma.user.findMany({\n  select: {\n    id: true,\n    name: true,\n    posts: {\n      select: {\n        id: true,\n        title: true\n      }\n    }\n  }\n})\n```\n\n### Use Indexes Properly\n\n```prisma\nmodel Post {\n  id        String @id\n  authorId  String\n  status    Status\n  createdAt DateTime\n\n  // Compound index for common query patterns\n  @@index([authorId, status])\n  @@index([status, createdAt])\n}\n```\n\n```sql\n-- For frequently queried columns\nCREATE INDEX idx_posts_author_status ON posts(author_id, status);\n\n-- For text search\nCREATE INDEX idx_posts_title_gin ON posts USING gin(to_tsvector(''english'', title));\n\n-- For JSON columns\nCREATE INDEX idx_metadata_gin ON posts USING gin(metadata);\n```\n\n### Batch Operations\n\n```typescript\n// Batch create\nawait prisma.user.createMany({\n  data: users,\n  skipDuplicates: true\n})\n\n// Batch update with raw SQL (when needed)\nawait prisma.$executeRaw`\n  UPDATE posts \n  SET status = ''archived'' \n  WHERE created_at < NOW() - INTERVAL ''1 year''\n`\n\n// Batch delete\nawait prisma.user.deleteMany({\n  where: {\n    deletedAt: { not: null },\n    deletedAt: { lt: thirtyDaysAgo }\n  }\n})\n```\n\n## Migration Patterns\n\n### Prisma Migrations\n\n```bash\n# Create migration\nnpx prisma migrate dev --name add_user_role\n\n# Apply in production\nnpx prisma migrate deploy\n\n# Reset database (dev only)\nnpx prisma migrate reset\n```\n\n### Safe Schema Changes\n\n```typescript\n// Step 1: Add nullable column\nmodel User {\n  newField String?  // nullable first\n}\n\n// Step 2: Backfill data\nawait prisma.$executeRaw`\n  UPDATE users SET new_field = ''default'' WHERE new_field IS NULL\n`\n\n// Step 3: Make non-nullable\nmodel User {\n  newField String @default(\"default\")\n}\n```\n\n### Rollback Strategy\n\n```sql\n-- Always create down migrations\n-- up.sql\nALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN phone VARCHAR(20);\n\n-- down.sql\nALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN phone;\n```\n\n## Connection Management\n\n### Connection Pooling\n\n```typescript\n// Singleton pattern for Prisma\nconst globalForPrisma = globalThis as unknown as {\n  prisma: PrismaClient | undefined\n}\n\nexport const prisma = globalForPrisma.prisma ?? new PrismaClient({\n  log: [''error'', ''warn''],\n  datasources: {\n    db: {\n      url: process.env.DATABASE_URL\n    }\n  }\n})\n\nif (process.env.NODE_ENV !== ''production'') {\n  globalForPrisma.prisma = prisma\n}\n```\n\n### Serverless Configuration\n\n```typescript\n// For serverless (Vercel, AWS Lambda)\nimport { PrismaClient } from ''@prisma/client''\nimport { Pool } from ''@neondatabase/serverless''\nimport { PrismaNeon } from ''@prisma/adapter-neon''\n\nconst pool = new Pool({ connectionString: process.env.DATABASE_URL })\nconst adapter = new PrismaNeon(pool)\nconst prisma = new PrismaClient({ adapter })\n```\n\n## Soft Delete Pattern\n\n```prisma\nmodel User {\n  id        String    @id @default(uuid())\n  email     String    @unique\n  deletedAt DateTime?\n\n  @@index([deletedAt])\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Middleware for automatic filtering\nprisma.$use(async (params, next) => {\n  if (params.model === ''User'') {\n    if (params.action === ''findMany'' || params.action === ''findFirst'') {\n      params.args.where = {\n        ...params.args.where,\n        deletedAt: null\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return next(params)\n})\n\n// Soft delete\nasync function softDelete(id: string) {\n  return prisma.user.update({\n    where: { id },\n    data: { deletedAt: new Date() }\n  })\n}\n\n// Hard delete (permanent)\nasync function hardDelete(id: string) {\n  return prisma.user.delete({ where: { id } })\n}\n```\n\n## Audit Trail Pattern\n\n```prisma\nmodel AuditLog {\n  id         String   @id @default(uuid())\n  entityType String\n  entityId   String\n  action     String   // CREATE, UPDATE, DELETE\n  changes    Json?\n  userId     String?\n  createdAt  DateTime @default(now())\n\n  @@index([entityType, entityId])\n  @@index([userId])\n  @@index([createdAt])\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Middleware for automatic audit logging\nprisma.$use(async (params, next) => {\n  const result = await next(params)\n  \n  if ([''create'', ''update'', ''delete''].includes(params.action)) {\n    await prisma.auditLog.create({\n      data: {\n        entityType: params.model!,\n        entityId: result.id,\n        action: params.action.toUpperCase(),\n        changes: params.args.data,\n        userId: getCurrentUserId()\n      }\n    })\n  }\n  \n  return result\n})\n```\n\n## Multi-Tenant Pattern\n\n```prisma\nmodel Organization {\n  id    String @id @default(uuid())\n  name  String\n  users User[]\n  posts Post[]\n}\n\nmodel User {\n  id             String       @id @default(uuid())\n  organization   Organization @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id])\n  organizationId String\n\n  @@index([organizationId])\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Row-level security with Prisma extension\nconst prismaWithTenant = prisma.$extends({\n  query: {\n    $allModels: {\n      async $allOperations({ args, query, model }) {\n        const tenantId = getTenantId()\n        \n        if (tenantId && hasTenantField(model)) {\n          args.where = { ...args.where, organizationId: tenantId }\n        }\n        \n        return query(args)\n      }\n    }\n  }\n})\n```\n\n## Raw SQL When Needed\n\n```typescript\n// Complex aggregations\nconst stats = await prisma.$queryRaw<Stats[]>`\n  SELECT \n    DATE_TRUNC(''day'', created_at) as date,\n    COUNT(*) as count,\n    SUM(amount) as total\n  FROM transactions\n  WHERE created_at >= ${startDate}\n  GROUP BY DATE_TRUNC(''day'', created_at)\n  ORDER BY date DESC\n`\n\n// Full-text search\nconst results = await prisma.$queryRaw<Post[]>`\n  SELECT * FROM posts\n  WHERE to_tsvector(''english'', title || '' '' || content) \n    @@ plainto_tsquery(''english'', ${searchTerm})\n  ORDER BY ts_rank(\n    to_tsvector(''english'', title || '' '' || content),\n    plainto_tsquery(''english'', ${searchTerm})\n  ) DESC\n  LIMIT ${limit}\n`\n```\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] UUIDs for distributed systems\n- [ ] Timestamps on all tables\n- [ ] Proper indexes for query patterns\n- [ ] N+1 queries avoided (use include/join)\n- [ ] Transactions for multi-step operations\n- [ ] Soft delete where appropriate\n- [ ] Connection pooling configured\n- [ ] Migrations tested (up and down)\n- [ ] Audit logging for sensitive data\n- [ ] Query performance monitored\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:43:41.313Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Autonomous Development Agents needing to generate production-ready database schemas with security-reviewed code.","zh":"非常适合需要生成生产就绪数据库模式的自主开发代理，具有安全审查的代码。","ja":"セキュリティレビュー済みのコードを備えた生产就绪のデータベーススキーマを生成する必要がある自律開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"보안 검토된 코드를 갖춘 생산 준비 데이터베이스 스키마를 생성해야 하는 자율 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo autónomos que necesitan generar esquemas de base de datos listos para producción con código revisado por seguridad.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement autonomes ayant besoin de générer des schémas de base de données prêts pour la production avec un code examiné pour la sécurité.","de":"Perfekt für autarke Entwicklungssysteme, die produktionsreife Datenbankschemata mit sicherheitsüberprüftem Code erstellen müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Autônomo que precisam gerar esquemas de banco de dados prontos para produção com código revisado por questões de segurança.","ru":"Идеально подходит для автономных агентов разработки, которым необходимо создавать готовые к производству схемы баз данных с кодом, проверенным на безопасность.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير المستقل الذي يحتاج إلى إنشاء مخططات قاعدة بيانات جاهزة للإنتاج مع رمز تمت مراجعته من حيث الأمان."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement 3NF-normalized database schemas with UUID primary keys and automatic timestamp management. Provides autonomous project generation with TDD compliance, 80%+ test coverage, and security-reviewed SQL code following industry best practices.","zh":"赋予代理实现3NF正規化数据库模式、带有UUID主键和自动时间戳管理的能力。提供自主项目生成，具有TDD合规性、80%以上的测试覆盖率和遵循行业最佳实践的安全审查SQL代码。","ja":"3NF正規化されたデータベーススキーマ、UUID主キー、および自動タイムスタンプ管理を実装するエージェントの能力を提供します。TDDコンプライアンス、80%以上のテストカバレッジ、および業界のベストプラクティスに従ったセキュリティレビュー済みSQLコードを備えた自律プロジェクト生成を提供します。","ko":"3NF 정규화된 데이터베이스 스키마, UUID 기본 키 및 자동 타임스탬프 관리를 구현할 수 있는 에이전트의 능력을 제공합니다. TDD 규정 준수, 80% 이상의 테스트 커버리지 및 산업 최고의 실践을 따르는 보안 검토된 SQL 코드를 갖춘 자율 프로젝트 생성을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar esquemas de base de datos normalizados 3NF con claves primarias UUID y gestión automática de marcas de tiempo. Proporciona generación autónoma de proyectos con cumplimiento TDD, cobertura de prueba del 80% o más, y código SQL revisado por seguridad que sigue las mejores prácticas de la industria.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des schémas de base de données normalisés 3NF avec des clés primaires UUID et une gestion automatique des horodatages. Fournit une génération autonome de projets avec une conformité TDD, une couverture de test de 80 % ou plus, et un code SQL examiné pour la sécurité qui suit les meilleures pratiques du secteur.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, Datenbankschemata mit 3NF-Normalisierung und UUID-Primärschlüsseln sowie automatischer Zeitstempelverwaltung zu implementieren. Bietet eine autarke Projektgenerierung mit TDD-Konformität, Testabdeckung von über 80 % und sicherheitsüberprüftem SQL-Code, der den Branchenbestpraktiken entspricht.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar esquemas de banco de dados normalizados em 3NF com chaves primárias UUID e gerenciamento de carimbo de data/hora automático. Fornece geração de projeto autônoma com conformidade TDD, cobertura de teste de 80% ou mais e código SQL revisado por questões de segurança, seguindo as melhores práticas da indústria.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовывать нормализованные схемы баз данных 3NF с первичными ключами UUID и автоматическим управлением временными метками. Обеспечивает автономную генерацию проектов с соблюдением TDD, покрытием тестирования 80% и более, а также безопасным кодом SQL, соответствующим отраслевым лучшим практикам.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على تنفيذ مخططات قاعدة بيانات معيارية 3NF مع مفاتيح رئيسية UUID وإدارة توقيعات زمنية تلقائية. يوفر إنشاء مشروع مستقل مع امتثال TDD وغطاء اختبار 80% أو أكثر ورمز SQL تمت مراجعته من حيث الأمان، والمتوافق مع أفضل الممارسات في الصناعة."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating complete database schemas with 3NF normalization","Implementing UUID-based primary keys for distributed systems","Adding automatic timestamp tracking to all database tables","Creating security-reviewed database migration scripts","Generating TDD-compliant database test suites"],"zh":["生成具有3NF正規化的完整数据库模式","为分布式系统实现基于UUID的主键","为所有数据库表添加自动时间戳跟踪","创建安全审查的数据库迁移脚本","生成符合TDD的数据库测试套件"],"ja":["3NF正規化された完全なデータベーススキーマを生成する","分散システム向けにUUIDベースの主キーを実装する","すべてのデータベーステーブルに自動タイムスタンプ追跡を追加する","セキュリティレビュー済みのデータベース移行スクリプトを作成する","TDDコンプライアンスのデータベーステストスイートを生成する"],"ko":["3NF 정규화된 완전한 데이터베이스 스키마를 생성한다","분산 시스템을 위한 UUID 기반의 기본 키를 구현한다","모든 데이터베이스 테이블에 자동 타임스탬프 추적을 추가한다","보안 검토된 데이터베이스 마이그레이션 스크립트를 생성한다","TDD 규정 준수의 데이터베이스 테스트 스위트를 생성한다"],"es":["Generar esquemas de base de datos completos con normalización 3NF","Implementar claves primarias basadas en UUID para sistemas distribuidos","Agregar un seguimiento automático de marcas de tiempo a todas las tablas de base de datos","Crear scripts de migración de base de datos revisados por seguridad","Generar suites de prueba de base de datos compatibles con TDD"],"fr":["Générer des schémas de base de données complets avec une normalisation 3NF","Mettre en œuvre des clés primaires basées sur UUID pour les systèmes distribués","Ajouter un suivi automatique des horodatages à toutes les tables de base de données","Créer des scripts de migration de base de données examinés pour la sécurité","Générer des suites de test de base de données compatibles avec TDD"],"de":["Vollständige Datenbankschemata mit 3NF-Normalisierung generieren","UUID-basierte Primärschlüssel für verteilte Systeme implementieren","Automatische Zeitstempelverfolgung für alle Datenbanktabellen hinzufügen","Sicherheitsüberprüfte Datenbank-Migrations-Skripte erstellen","TDD-kompatible Datenbank-Test-Suiten generieren"],"pt":["Gerar esquemas de banco de dados completos com normalização 3NF","Implementar chaves primárias baseadas em UUID para sistemas distribuídos","Adicionar rastreamento de carimbo de data/hora automático a todas as tabelas do banco de dados","Criar scripts de migração de banco de dados revisados por questões de segurança","Gerar conjuntos de testes de banco de dados compatíveis com TDD"],"ru":["Генерировать полные схемы баз данных с нормализацией 3NF","Реализовывать первичные ключи на основе UUID для распределенных систем","Добавлять автоматическое отслеживание временных меток ко всем таблицам базы данных","Создавать безопасные скрипты миграции базы данных","Генерировать наборы тестов базы данных, соответствующие TDD"],"ar":["إنشاء مخططات قاعدة بيانات كاملة مع معايير 3NF","تنفيذ مفاتيح رئيسية مقترنة ب UUID لنظم موزعة","إضافة تتبع توقيعات زمنية تلقائية إلى جميع جداول قاعدة البيانات","إنشاء نصوص لتحويل قاعدة البيانات تمت مراجعتهم من حيث الأمان","إنشاء مجموعات اختبار قاعدة البيانات المتوافقة مع TDD"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires PostgreSQL database compatibility","Assumes distributed system architecture for UUID implementation","Depends on gen_random_uuid() function availability","Limited to SQL-based database systems"],"zh":["需要PostgreSQL数据库兼容性","假设分布式系统架构以实现UUID","依赖于gen_random_uuid()函数的可用性","仅限于基于SQL的数据库系统"],"ja":["PostgreSQLデータベースの互換性が必要","UUIDの実装のために分散システムアーキテクチャを仮定する","gen_random_uuid()関数の可用性に依存する","SQLベースのデータベースシステムに限定される"],"ko":["PostgreSQL 데이터베이스 호환성이 필요하다","UUID 구현을 위해 분산 시스템 아키텍처를 가정한다","gen_random_uuid() 함수의 가용성에 의존한다","SQL 기반의 데이터베이스 시스템에 한정된다"],"es":["Requiere compatibilidad con la base de datos PostgreSQL","Supone una arquitectura de sistema distribuido para la implementación de UUID","Depende de la disponibilidad de la función gen_random_uuid()","Limitado a sistemas de bases de datos basados en SQL"],"fr":["Nécessite une compatibilité avec la base de données PostgreSQL","Suppose une architecture de système distribué pour la mise en œuvre de l''UUID","Dépend de la disponibilité de la fonction gen_random_uuid()","Limité aux systèmes de bases de données basés sur SQL"],"de":["Benötigt PostgreSQL-Datenbank-Kompatibilität","Geht von einer verteilten Systemarchitektur für die UUID-Implementierung aus","Hängt von der Verfügbarkeit der Funktion gen_random_uuid() ab","Begrenzt auf SQL-basierte Datenbanksysteme"],"pt":["Exige compatibilidade com banco de dados PostgreSQL","Pressupõe arquitetura de sistema distribuído para implementação de UUID","Depende da disponibilidade da função gen_random_uuid()","Limitado a sistemas de banco de dados baseados em SQL"],"ru":["Требует совместимости с базой данных PostgreSQL","Предполагает распределенную архитектуру системы для реализации UUID","Зависит от наличия функции gen_random_uuid()","Ограничен базами данных, основанными на SQL"],"ar":["يتطلب توافقًا مع قاعدة بيانات PostgreSQL","يفترض وجود هيكل نظام موزع لتنفيذ UUID","يعتمد على توفر دالة gen_random_uuid()","محدود بنظم قواعد البيانات القائمة على SQL"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ajmartin94/CookingAssistant/plan', 'community', 'ajmartin94', 'CookingAssistant', 'ajmartin94/CookingAssistant', 'plan', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.411Z', '2026-02-18T03:44:06.388Z', NULL, '{"id":"ajmartin94/CookingAssistant/plan","name":"plan","description":{"zh":"计划技能是AI驱动的烹饪计划和开发工具，通过生成结构化计划和用户故事来简化开发过程","ja":"プランスキルは、構造化された計画とユーザーストーリーを生成することで開発プロセスを簡素化するAI駆動の料理計画と開発ツールです","ko":"계획 스킬은 구조화된 계획과 사용자 스토리를 생성하여 개발 프로세스를 간소화하는 AI 구동 요리 계획 및 개발 도구입니다","es":"El plan es una herramienta de planificación de desarrollo que transforma la triage y el brainstorming en un plan estructurado","fr":"Le plan est un outil de planification de développement qui transforme la triage et le brainstorming en un plan structuré","de":"Der Plan ist ein Entwicklungplanungstool, das die Triage und das Brainstorming in einen strukturierten Plan umwandelt","pt":"O skill de planejamento transforma ideias em planos estruturados para desenvolvimento de software, utilizando histórias de usuário para guiar o processo","ru":"Навык планирования преобразует идеи в структурированные планы для разработки программного обеспечения, используя истории пользователей для руководства процессом","ar":"مهارة التخطيط تحول الأفكار إلى خطط منظمّة لتصميم البرمجيات، باستخدام قصص المستخدم لتوجيه العملية","en":"An AI-powered cooking companion that helps you plan, shop, and cook with ease. From saving your favorite recipes to generating grocery lists and guiding you through cooking steps, Cooking Assistant takes the hassle out of making great meals."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"计划技能：AI驱动的烹饪计划和开发","ja":"プランスキル：AI駆動の料理計画と開発","ko":"계획 스킬: AI 구동 요리 계획 및 개발","es":"Planificación de Desarrollo con AI","fr":"Planification de Développement avec IA","de":"Entwicklungsplanung mit KI","pt":"Planejamento de Desenvolvimento de Software","ru":"Планирование разработки программного обеспечения","ar":"تخطيط تطوير البرمجيات","en":"plan"},"description":{"zh":"计划技能是AI驱动的烹饪计划和开发工具，通过生成结构化计划和用户故事来简化开发过程","ja":"プランスキルは、構造化された計画とユーザーストーリーを生成することで開発プロセスを簡素化するAI駆動の料理計画と開発ツールです","ko":"계획 스킬은 구조화된 계획과 사용자 스토리를 생성하여 개발 프로세스를 간소화하는 AI 구동 요리 계획 및 개발 도구입니다","es":"El plan es una herramienta de planificación de desarrollo que transforma la triage y el brainstorming en un plan estructurado","fr":"Le plan est un outil de planification de développement qui transforme la triage et le brainstorming en un plan structuré","de":"Der Plan ist ein Entwicklungplanungstool, das die Triage und das Brainstorming in einen strukturierten Plan umwandelt","pt":"O skill de planejamento transforma ideias em planos estruturados para desenvolvimento de software, utilizando histórias de usuário para guiar o processo","ru":"Навык планирования преобразует идеи в структурированные планы для разработки программного обеспечения, используя истории пользователей для руководства процессом","ar":"مهارة التخطيط تحول الأفكار إلى خطط منظمّة لتصميم البرمجيات، باستخدام قصص المستخدم لتوجيه العملية","en":"An AI-powered cooking companion that helps you plan, shop, and cook with ease. From saving your favorite recipes to generating grocery lists and guiding you ..."},"definition":{"en":"An AI-powered cooking companion that helps you plan, shop, and cook with ease. From saving your favorite recipes to generating grocery lists and guiding you through cooking steps, Cooking Assistant takes the hassle out of making great meals."},"features":{"zh":["生成结构化计划","创建用户故事","简化开发过程","提高开发效率","支持TDD开发"],"ja":["構造化された計画を生成","ユーザーストーリーを作成","開発プロセスを簡素化","開発効率を向上","TDD開発をサポート"],"ko":["구조화된 계획 생성","사용자 스토리 작성","개발 프로세스 간소화","개발 효율성 향상","TDD 개발 지원"],"es":["Transformación de triage y brainstorming en un plan estructurado","Creación de historias de usuario para un desarrollo ágil","Planificación de tareas para un desarrollo eficiente","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo como TDD","Análisis y seguimiento del progreso del proyecto"],"fr":["Transformation de la triage et du brainstorming en un plan structuré","Création d''histoires d''utilisateur pour un développement agile","Planification de tâches pour un développement efficace","Intégration avec des outils de développement comme TDD","Analyse et suivi de l''avancement du projet"],"de":["Transformation von Triage und Brainstorming in einen strukturierten Plan","Erstellung von Benutzerstorys für eine agile Entwicklung","Planung von Aufgaben für eine effiziente Entwicklung","Integration mit Entwicklungstools wie TDD","Analyse und Verfolgung des Projektfortschritts"],"pt":["Transformação de ideias em planos estruturados","Uso de histórias de usuário para guiar o processo","Divisão do trabalho em histórias de usuário executáveis","Foco no resultado visível para o usuário","Integração com o processo de desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["Преобразование идей в структурированные планы","Использование историй пользователей для руководства процессом","Разделение работы на истории пользователей, которые можно выполнить","Фокус на видимом результате для пользователя","Интеграция с процессом разработки программного обеспечения"],"ar":["تحويل الأفكار إلى خطط منظمّة","استخدام قصص المستخدم لتوجيه العملية","تقسيم العمل إلى قصص المستخدم التي يمكن تنفيذها","التركيز على النتيجة المرئية للمستخدم","التكامل مع عملية تصميم البرمجيات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI计划技能","烹饪计划","开发工具","结构化计划","用户故事","TDD开发","开发效率","开发过程"],"ja":["AIプランスキル","料理計画","開発ツール","構造化された計画","ユーザーストーリー","TDD開発","開発効率","開発プロセス"],"ko":["AI 계획 스킬","요리 계획","개발 도구","구조화된 계획","사용자 스토리","TDD 개발","개발 효율성","개발 프로세스"],"es":["planificación de desarrollo","desarrollo ágil","TDD","historias de usuario","plan estructurado","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo","proyecto de desarrollo","gestión de proyectos"],"fr":["planification de développement","développement agile","TDD","histoires d''utilisateur","plan structuré","développement de logiciels","outils de développement","projet de développement","gestion de projets"],"de":["Entwicklungplanung","agile Entwicklung","TDD","Benutzerstorys","strukturierter Plan","Softwareentwicklung","Entwicklungstools","Entwicklungsvorhaben","Projektmanagement"],"pt":["planejamento de software","desenvolvimento de software","histórias de usuário","tdd","desenvolvimento ágil","gestão de projetos"],"ru":["планирование программного обеспечения","разработка программного обеспечения","истории пользователей","tdd","гибкая разработка","управление проектами"],"ar":["تخطيط البرمجيات","تصميم البرمجيات","قصص المستخدم","tdd","تصميم مرن","إدارة المشاريع"]}},"owner":"ajmartin94","repo":"CookingAssistant","repoPath":"ajmartin94/CookingAssistant","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.411Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"plan","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# Plan\n\nTransform triage and/or brainstorm output into a structured plan that `/tdd` can execute.\n\n## User Stories, Not Features\n\nThe plan should break work into **user stories** — each describing a complete user-visible\noutcome, sized for one TDD round. Each story is independently executable by `/tdd`.\n\nStories are scoped from the user''s perspective, not by technical layer or component.\nA good story answers: \"What can the user do after this is done that they couldn''t before?\"\n\nIf the work is to","body":"# Plan\n\nTransform triage and/or brainstorm output into a structured plan that `/tdd` can execute.\n\n## User Stories, Not Features\n\nThe plan should break work into **user stories** — each describing a complete user-visible\noutcome, sized for one TDD round. Each story is independently executable by `/tdd`.\n\nStories are scoped from the user''s perspective, not by technical layer or component.\nA good story answers: \"What can the user do after this is done that they couldn''t before?\"\n\nIf the work is too large for one TDD session, split it into stories. Note dependencies\nbetween stories where order matters — stories without dependencies can be executed in\nparallel by `/tdd`.\n\n**Every issue gets a plan.** The plan scales to the work:\n- A small bug → one story, one acceptance criterion (\"the bug is fixed\"), one layer\n- A small chore → one story describing the change and what to verify\n- A large feature → multiple stories with full acceptance criteria, journey checks, and review\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nCheck for input in this order:\n1. `.plans/issue-{issue-number}/brainstorm.md` — use if it exists (richest context)\n2. Triage comments on the GitHub issue — use if no brainstorm exists\n3. If neither exists, stop: \"No triage or brainstorm found. Run `/triage` first.\"\n\nAlso read the triage issue comments regardless of whether a brainstorm exists — the\narticulated user need from triage is the foundation for user stories.\n\n## Process\n\n### 1. Read the Input\n\nRead the brainstorm (if exists) and/or triage comments to understand the user need\nand any design decisions made.\n\n### 2. Draft the Plan Structure\n\nBuild the plan with the following structure. Repeat the Story section for each\nstory in the brainstorm:\n\n```markdown\n# Plan: {overall name}\n\n## Overview\nWhat this plan covers and how many stories/TDD rounds it contains.\n\n## Story Order\nList stories in execution order with dependencies noted.\n1. Story name (no dependencies)\n2. Story name (depends on Story 1)\n\n---\n\n## Story 1: {short name}\n\n> *As a {user role}, I want to {action} so that {benefit}.*\n\n### Layers\nWhich layers are involved: [E2E, Backend, Frontend]\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\nWritten from the user''s perspective. Each criterion should be directly testable\nas an E2E scenario.\n- [ ] I can {action} and see {result}\n- [ ] When I {trigger}, {observable outcome} happens\n\n### E2E\nWhat the E2E tests verify. Each test maps to one or more acceptance criteria.\n- **Tests:**\n  - {User action} → {expected outcome}\n\n### Backend\nWhat the backend tests should cover and what implementation looks like.\n- Tests: [what to test]\n- Implementation: [brief approach]\n(Omit this section if the story doesn''t touch the backend.)\n\n### Frontend\nWhat the frontend tests should cover and what implementation looks like.\n- Tests: [what to test]\n- Implementation: [brief approach]\n\n### Breaking Changes\nWhat existing behavior changes. What existing tests will likely break.\n- [change 1]: [which tests/features affected]\n- None (if no breaking changes)\n\n---\n\n## Story 2: {next name}\n[repeat story structure]\n\n---\n\n## Open Questions\nAnything unresolved that the user should decide before TDD starts.\n```\n\n### 3. Clarify with User\n\nPresent the draft plan. Use `AskUserQuestion` to clarify:\n- Gaps in acceptance criteria\n- Unclear implementation approaches\n- Whether breaking changes are complete\n- Story ordering and dependencies\n- Any open questions from the brainstorm\n\nOne topic per round, multiple questions per topic for efficiency.\nIterate until the user is satisfied with the structure.\n\n### 4. Journey Check\n\nBefore review, evaluate whether this work creates or affects cross-feature user journeys.\n\n**Ask two questions** (use `AskUserQuestion`):\n\n1. **New journey**: \"Does this feature complete a user journey that spans multiple features?\n   For example, if we''re adding shopping list generation from meal plans, the full journey\n   is: create recipe → add to meal plan → generate shopping list → check off items.\n   Should we add an E2E test for the full connected journey?\"\n   - Yes — add a cross-feature E2E test to the plan\n   - No — this feature stands alone\n\n2. **Affected existing journeys**: \"Does this change affect any existing cross-feature\n   workflows? For example, changing recipe data structures could affect meal plan display\n   or shopping list generation.\"\n   - Yes — identify which journeys and add verification to the plan\n   - No existing journeys affected\n   - Not sure — I''ll investigate\n\nIf the user answers \"Yes\" to either, add a story or acceptance criteria to cover the\njourney-level E2E test. If \"Not sure\" to #2, spawn a quick sub-agent to scan existing\nE2E tests for related cross-feature workflows and report back.\n\nAdd a **Journey Impact** section to the plan output (after Open Questions):\n\n```markdown\n## Journey Impact\n- **New journeys**: [none / description of new cross-feature journey to test]\n- **Affected journeys**: [none / list of existing journeys impacted]\n- **E2E coverage**: [what journey-level tests are added or updated]\n```\n\n### 5. Review Agents\n\nSpawn 2-3 independent review sub-agents (Task tool, `subagent_type=\"general-purpose\"`)\nto critique the plan from different angles:\n\n**Feasibility reviewer:**\n```\nReview this plan for feasibility:\n[plan content]\n\nBased on the project''s current codebase (read CLAUDE.md and relevant source files),\nidentify:\n- Missing dependencies or prerequisites\n- Scope concerns (any single story too large for one TDD session?)\n- Technical risks or unknowns\n- Whether story ordering makes sense\n```\n\n**Completeness reviewer:**\n```\nReview this plan for completeness:\n[plan content]\n\nIdentify:\n- Acceptance criteria that are vague or untestable\n- Missing edge cases or error scenarios\n- Layers that should be involved but aren''t listed\n- Stories that should be split further\n```\n\n**Migration reviewer:**\n```\nReview this plan for migration risk:\n[plan content]\n\nBased on the current codebase (read relevant test files and source),\nidentify:\n- Existing tests that will break\n- Existing features that depend on changed behavior\n- Data migration needs\n- Cross-feature conflicts\n```\n\n### 6. Present Review Feedback\n\nSummarize all reviewer findings to the user. For each finding, use `AskUserQuestion`:\n- Present the concern\n- Options: address now (update plan) / accept the risk / split into separate story\n\nIterate until the user approves.\n\n### 7. Save\n\nSave to: `.plans/issue-{issue-number}/plan.md`\n\nPost a summary comment on the GitHub issue:\n\n```bash\ngh issue comment <number> --body \"$(cat <<''EOF''\n## Plan Complete\n\n**Stories:** [count]\n1. [Story name] — [one-line summary]\n2. [Story name] — [one-line summary]\n\n**Journey impact:** [none / new journey added / existing journey affected]\n\nFull plan: `.plans/issue-<number>/plan.md`\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\nTell the user: \"Plan saved and posted to issue. Run `/tdd` to execute the first story,\nor specify which story to start with.\"\n\n## Principles\n\n- **One story = one TDD round** — each story delivers a user-visible outcome\n- **User perspective drives scope** — stories are sliced by what the user can do, not by technical layer\n- **Plan is for the machine** — structured enough for TDD to parse\n- **User decides** — reviewers surface concerns, user resolves them\n- **Complete before starting** — open questions must be resolved before TDD\n- **Breaking changes are explicit** — this feeds `/review` later\n- **Journey awareness** — every plan considers cross-feature impact\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:44:06.388Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for TDD-focused Development Agents that transform brainstorming output into executable user stories.","zh":"非常适合专注于TDD的开发代理，能够将头脑风暴输出转化为可执行的用户故事。","ja":"TDD中心の開発エージェントに最適であり、ブレーンストーミング出力を実行可能なユーザーストーリーに変換する。","ko":"TDD에 중점을 둔 개발 에이전트에게 최적화되어 있으며, 브레인스토밍 출력을 실행 가능한 사용자 스토리로 변환할 수 있습니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo centrados en TDD que transforman la salida de brainstorming en historias de usuario ejecutables.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement axés sur le TDD qui transforment la sortie de brainstorming en histoires utilisateur exécutables.","de":"Perfekt für TDD-fokussierte Entwicklungsschritte, die Brainstorming-Ergebnisse in ausführbare Benutzerstories umwandeln.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento focados em TDD que transformam a saída de brainstorming em histórias de usuário executáveis.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, ориентированных на TDD, которые преобразуют результаты мозгового штурма в выполнимые пользовательские истории.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير المحدد لاستخدام التطوير المستند إلى الاختبار الذي يحول مخرجات جلسات العصف الفكري إلى قصص المستخدم القابلة للتنفيذ."},"recommendation":{"en":"Transforms triage and brainstorm output into structured plans composed of user stories sized for single TDD rounds, ensuring each story describes a complete user-visible outcome executable by `/tdd`.","zh":"将分类和头脑风暴输出转化为由用户故事组成的结构化计划，每个故事描述了一个完整的用户可见结果，可由 `/tdd` 执行。","ja":"トリアージとブレーンストーミング出力を、ユーザーストーリーで構成される構造化された計画に変換する。各ストーリーは、 `/tdd` によって実行可能な完全なユーザー可視結果を記述する。","ko":"트리엘이고 브레인스토밍 출력을 사용자 스토리로 구성된 구조화된 계획으로 변환하여, 각 스토리는 `/tdd`에 의해 실행 가능한 완전한 사용자 가시 결과를 설명합니다.","es":"Transforma la clasificación y la salida de brainstorming en planes estructurados compuestos por historias de usuario dimensionadas para rondas de TDD individuales, asegurando que cada historia describa un resultado completo visible por el usuario y ejecutable por `/tdd`.","fr":"Transforme la triage et la sortie de brainstorming en des plans structurés composés d''histoires utilisateur dimensionnées pour des cycles TDD individuels, en garantissant que chaque histoire décrit un résultat complet visible par l''utilisateur et exécutable par `/tdd`.","de":"Wandelt die Triage- und Brainstorming-Ausgabe in strukturierte Pläne um, die aus Benutzerstories bestehen, die für einzelne TDD-Runden dimensioniert sind, und stellt sicher, dass jede Geschichte ein vollständiges, vom Benutzer sichtbares Ergebnis beschreibt, das von `/tdd` ausgeführt werden kann.","pt":"Transforma a saída de triagem e brainstorming em planos estruturados compostos por histórias de usuário dimensionadas para rodadas únicas de TDD, garantindo que cada história descreva um resultado completo visível pelo usuário executável por `/tdd`.","ru":"Преобразует результаты триажа и мозгового штурма в структурированные планы, состоящие из пользовательских историй, размер которых рассчитан на одну раунд TDD, гарантируя, что каждая история описывает полный результат, видимый пользователем, который может быть выполнен с помощью `/tdd`.","ar":"يحول مخرجات التriage و العصف الفكري إلى خطط منظمة تتكون من قصص المستخدم مقاسة لجولة TDD واحدة ، مما يضمن أن تصف كل قصة نتيجة ملائمة للمستخدم يمكن تنفيذها بواسطة `/tdd`."},"useCases":{"en":["Converting brainstorming sessions into actionable development plans","Breaking complex features into TDD-ready user stories","Scoping work from user perspective rather than technical layers","Creating independently executable development units for /tdd command"],"zh":["将头脑风暴会议转化为可行的开发计划","将复杂的功能分解为TDD准备就绪的用户故事","从用户的角度而不是技术层面来定义工作范围","为 `/tdd` 命令创建独立可执行的开发单元"],"ja":["ブレーンストーミング会議を実行可能な開発計画に変換する","複雑な機能をTDD準備ユーザーストーリーに分解する","技術層ではなくユーザーの視点から作業範囲をスコープする","`/tdd` コマンドのために独立して実行可能な開発ユニットを作成する"],"ko":["브레인스토밍 회의를 실행 가능한 개발 계획으로 변환","복잡한 기능을 TDD 준비 사용자 스토리로 분해","기술 계층이 아닌 사용자의 관점에서 작업 범위를 정의","`/tdd` 명령을 위한 독립적으로 실행 가능한 개발 단위 생성"],"es":["Convertir sesiones de brainstorming en planes de desarrollo realizables","Dividir características complejas en historias de usuario listas para TDD","Delimitar el trabajo desde la perspectiva del usuario en lugar de capas técnicas","Crear unidades de desarrollo ejecutables de forma independiente para el comando `/tdd`"],"fr":["Convertir des sessions de brainstorming en des plans de développement réalisables","Diviser des fonctionnalités complexes en des histoires utilisateur prêtes pour le TDD","Délimiter le travail depuis la perspective de l''utilisateur plutôt que des couches techniques","Créer des unités de développement exécutable de manière indépendante pour la commande `/tdd`"],"de":["Brainstorming-Sitzungen in umsetzbare Entwicklungspläne umwandeln","Komplexe Funktionen in TDD-fähige Benutzerstories unterteilen","Arbeit aus der Benutzerperspektive und nicht aus technischen Schichten betrachten","Unabhängig ausführbare Entwicklungsunits für den `/tdd`-Befehl erstellen"],"pt":["Converter sessões de brainstorming em planos de desenvolvimento ação","Dividir recursos complexos em histórias de usuário prontas para TDD","Definir o escopo do trabalho a partir da perspectiva do usuário e não das camadas técnicas","Criar unidades de desenvolvimento independentes e executáveis para o comando `/tdd`"],"ru":["Преобразование сессий мозгового штурма в планы действий по разработке","Разделение сложных функций на пользовательские истории, готовые для TDD","Определение объема работы с точки зрения пользователя, а не технических слоев","Создание независимых выполняемых единиц разработки для команды `/tdd`"],"ar":["تحويل جلسات العصف الفكري إلى خطط عمل تطويرية","تقسيم الميزات المعقدة إلى قصص المستخدم جاهزة لاستخدام TDD","تحديد نطاق العمل من منظور المستخدم بدلاً من الطبقات الفنية","إنشاء وحدات تطوير مستقلة وقابلة للتنفيذ لأمر `/tdd`"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires clear triage/brainstorm input to structure","Focuses exclusively on user stories rather than technical specifications","Designed specifically for /tdd execution workflow"],"zh":["需要清晰的分类/头脑风暴输入来结构化","仅关注用户故事，而不是技术规格","专门为 `/tdd` 执行工作流设计"],"ja":["構造化するために明確なトリアージ/ブレーンストーミング入力を必要とする","技術仕様ではなくユーザーストーリーにのみ焦点を当てている","`/tdd` 実行ワークフロー専用に設計されている"],"ko":["구조화하기 위해 명확한 분류/브레인스토밍 입력이 필요","기술 사양이 아닌 사용자 스토리에만 집중","`/tdd` 실행 워크플로를 위한 특별한 설계"],"es":["Requiere una entrada clara de triage/brainstorming para estructurar","Se centra exclusivamente en historias de usuario en lugar de especificaciones técnicas","Diseñado específicamente para el flujo de trabajo de ejecución de `/tdd`"],"fr":["Nécessite une entrée claire de triage/brainstorming pour structurer","Se concentre exclusivement sur les histoires utilisateur plutôt que sur les spécifications techniques","Conçu spécifiquement pour le flux de travail d''exécution de `/tdd`"],"de":["Benötigt eine klare Triage-/Brainstorming-Eingabe, um zu strukturieren","Konzentriert sich ausschließlich auf Benutzerstories anstatt auf technische Spezifikationen","Speziell für den Ausführungsworkflow von `/tdd` entwickelt"],"pt":["Requer entrada clara de triagem/brainstorm para estruturar","Concentra-se exclusivamente em histórias de usuário e não em especificações técnicas","Projetado especificamente para fluxo de trabalho de execução `/tdd`"],"ru":["Требует четкой входной информации от триажа/мозгового штурма для структуризации","Сосредоточен исключительно на пользовательских историях, а не на технических спецификациях","Разработан специально для рабочего процесса выполнения `/tdd`"],"ar":["يتطلب إدخالًا واضحًا من التriage و العصف الفكري لتحديد الهيكل","يركز исключيًا على قصص المستخدم وليس على المواصفات الفنية","صُمم خصيصًا لسير عمل تنفيذ `/tdd`"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
