ンをデプロイする方法を説明します。フロントエンドの相対URLパターンとApache ProxyPassの設定を含みます","ko":"이 가이드에서는 Apache 리버스 프록시 서버에서 웹 애플리케이션을 배포하는 방법을 설명합니다. 프론트엔드 상대 URL 패턴 및 Apache ProxyPass 구성 포함","es":"Guía técnica para implementar aplicaciones web detrás de un proxy inverso Apache en rivsprod01.","fr":"Guide technique pour déployer des applications web derrière un proxy inverse Apache sur rivsprod01.","de":"Technische Anleitung zum Deployen von Webanwendungen hinter einem Apache-Reverse-Proxy auf rivsprod01.","pt":"Guia de implantação de proxy reverso para aplicações web em rivsprod01, abordando URLs relativas e configuração de ProxyPass","ru":"Руководство по развертыванию обратного прокси для веб-приложений на rivsprod01, рассматривающее относительные URL и настройку ProxyPass","ar":"دليل لتثبيت وكيل الويب العكسي لتطبيقات الويب على rivsprod01، يغطي عناوين URL النسبية وتكوين ProxyPass","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["使用相对URL","配置Apache ProxyPass","支持前端相对URL模式","提高安全性和性能","适用于Apache反向代理服务器"],"ja":["相対URLの使用","Apache ProxyPassの設定","フロントエンドの相対URLパターンのサポート","セキュリティとパフォーマンスの向上","Apacheリバースプロキシサーバーに対応"],"ko":["상대 URL 사용","Apache ProxyPass 구성","프론트엔드 상대 URL 패턴 지원","보안성과 성능 향상","Apache 리버스 프록시 서버 지원"],"es":["Uso de URLs relativas","Configuración de ProxyPass en Apache","Implementación de aplicaciones web en rivsprod01","Compatibilidad con frontend","Seguridad mejorada","Flexibilidad en la configuración"],"fr":["Utilisation d''URL relatives","Configuration de ProxyPass sur Apache","Déploiement d''applications web sur rivsprod01","Compatibilité avec le frontend","Sécurité améliorée","Flexibilité de configuration"],"de":["Verwendung relativer URLs","Konfiguration von ProxyPass in Apache","Deployen von Webanwendungen auf rivsprod01","Kompatibilität mit dem Frontend","Erhöhte Sicherheit","Flexibilität bei der Konfiguration"],"pt":["Uso de URLs relativas","Configuração de ProxyPass no Apache","Implantação de aplicações web em rivsprod01","Suporte a frontend de aplicações web","Configuração de servidor proxy reverso"],"ru":["Использование относительных URL","Настройка ProxyPass в Apache","Развертывание веб-приложений на rivsprod01","Поддержка frontend веб-приложений","Настройка сервера обратного прокси"],"ar":["استخدام عناوين URL النسبية","تكوين ProxyPass في Apache","تثبيت تطبيقات الويب على rivsprod01","دعم واجهة المستخدم الأمامية لتطبيقات الويب","تكوين خادم وكيل الويب العكسي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["反向代理部署","Apache反向代理","Web应用程序部署","相对URL","ProxyPass配置","安全性和性能"],"ja":["リバースプロキシデプロイメント","Apacheリバースプロキシ","Webアプリケーションデプロイ","相対URL","ProxyPass設定","セキュリティとパフォーマンス"],"ko":["리버스 프록시 배포","Apache 리버스 프록시","웹 애플리케이션 배포","상대 URL","ProxyPass 구성","보안성과 성능"],"es":["proxy inverso","apache reverse proxy","despliegue de aplicaciones web","rivsprod01","urls relativas","proxy pass","seguridad web","frontend","desarrollo web"],"fr":["proxy inverse","apache reverse proxy","déploiement d''applications web","rivsprod01","urls relatives","proxy pass","sécurité web","frontend","développement web"],"de":["reverse proxy","apache reverse proxy","webanwendung deployen","rivsprod01","relative urls","proxy pass","web sicherheit","frontend","webentwicklung"],"pt":["proxy reverso","apache","rivsprod01","urls relativas","configuração de proxy","implantação de aplicações web","desenvolvimento web","servidor proxy"],"ru":["обратный прокси","apache","rivsprod01","относительные url","настройка прокси","развертывание веб-приложений","веб-разработка","сервер прокси"],"ar":["وكيل الويب العكسي","apache","rivsprod01","عناوين url النسبية","تكوين وكيل","تثبيت تطبيقات الويب","تطوير الويب","خادم وكيل"]}},"owner":"lawless-m","repo":"claude-skills","repoPath":"lawless-m/claude-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.411Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Reverse Proxy Deployment","description":"Deploy web applications behind Apache reverse proxy on rivsprod01 with relative URLs and proper path configuration","bodyPreview":"# Reverse Proxy Deployment\n\nGuide for deploying web applications behind the Apache reverse proxy on rivsprod01 (dw.ramsden-international.com). Covers frontend relative URL patterns and Apache ProxyPass configuration.\n\n## Instructions\n\nWhen deploying a web application that will be accessed through the reverse proxy:\n\n1. **Use Relative URLs**: Frontend code must use relative URLs (not absolute localhost URLs) to work behind the proxy\n2. **Configure ProxyPass on rivsprod01**: Create Apache config i","body":"# Reverse Proxy Deployment\n\nGuide for deploying web applications behind the Apache reverse proxy on rivsprod01 (dw.ramsden-international.com). Covers frontend relative URL patterns and Apache ProxyPass configuration.\n\n## Instructions\n\nWhen deploying a web application that will be accessed through the reverse proxy:\n\n1. **Use Relative URLs**: Frontend code must use relative URLs (not absolute localhost URLs) to work behind the proxy\n2. **Configure ProxyPass on rivsprod01**: Create Apache config in `/etc/apache2/proxy-conf.d/` with proper path stripping\n3. **Order Matters**: More specific paths must come before general paths in Apache config\n4. **Test Locally First**: Verify services are accessible from rivsprod01 before configuring proxy\n5. **Use Trailing Slashes**: Both source and target URLs need trailing slashes for path stripping to work\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1: Deploy Web Application with API Backend\n\n```\nUser: I have a web app with frontend on port 9273 and API on port 8765. Deploy it behind the proxy at /myapp/\n\nClaude: I''ll set up your application for reverse proxy deployment:\n\n1. **Update Frontend URLs**: Change API calls to use relative URLs\n   - Before: `fetch(''http://localhost:8765/api/status'')`\n   - After: `fetch(''api/status'')`  // Relative to current path\n\n2. **Create Apache Config**: SSH to rivsprod01 and create `/etc/apache2/proxy-conf.d/myapp.conf`\n   - API path: `/myapp/api/` → backend on port 8765\n   - Frontend path: `/myapp/` → frontend on port 9273\n   - API location must come FIRST (more specific)\n\n3. **Reload Apache**: `sudo systemctl reload apache2`\n\n[Provides implementation using the ProxyPass Configuration pattern below]\n```\n\n### Example 2: Frontend Uses Absolute URLs\n\n```\nUser: My frontend has `fetch(''http://localhost:3000/api/data'')` hardcoded. How do I make it work behind a proxy?\n\nClaude: Absolute URLs won''t work behind a reverse proxy. You need to update the frontend to use relative URLs:\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Best: Use relative URLs** - `fetch(''api/data'')` - works anywhere\n2. **Alternative: Use base path** - Store base path in config, prepend to all API calls\n3. **Hidden input method** - Store proxy path in HTML, read in JavaScript\n\nFor option 1 (recommended):\n- Replace all `http://localhost:3000/api/` with `api/`\n- The browser resolves relative to current page path\n- If page is at `/myapp/`, API call goes to `/myapp/api/`\n\n[Shows the Relative URL Pattern implementation below]\n```\n\n### Example 3: Multiple Services on Same Machine\n\n```\nUser: I have 3 services running on ports 8001, 8002, 8003. Deploy all at /service1/, /service2/, /service3/\n\nClaude: I''ll configure all three services in a single Apache config file:\n\n1. **Create single config file**: `/etc/apache2/proxy-conf.d/services.conf`\n2. **Add ProxyPass for each**: More specific paths first (doesn''t matter here since no overlap)\n3. **Each service gets clean URLs**: Paths are stripped before forwarding\n4. **Reload once**: All services go live together\n\n[Provides implementation using the Multi-Service Configuration pattern below]\n```\n\n### Example 4: API Calls Return 404\n\n```\nUser: My frontend loads but API calls return 404. Frontend is at /rabbit/, API should be at /rabbit/api/\n\nClaude: The issue is likely ProxyPass configuration. Let me check:\n\n1. **Verify services are reachable**: From rivsprod01, can you curl the backend directly?\n   - `curl http://10.99.0.3:8765/status` should work\n\n2. **Check ProxyPass order**: API location must come BEFORE frontend location\n   - Wrong order: frontend `/rabbit/` catches `/rabbit/api/` requests\n   - Right order: API `/rabbit/api/` catches first, then frontend `/rabbit/`\n\n3. **Verify trailing slashes**: Both paths need trailing slashes for stripping\n   - `ProxyPass /rabbit/api/ http://10.99.0.3:8765/`\n   - Without trailing slash, path isn''t stripped properly\n\n[Shows debugging steps from Troubleshooting section below]\n```\n\n---\n\n# Reference Implementation Details\n\nThe sections below contain proven working configurations from production deployments.\n\n**Reference Files in This Folder**:\n- `rabbit.conf` - Example Apache config from Invoice OCR deployment\n\n## Relative URL Pattern\n\n**Purpose**: Make frontend work behind any reverse proxy path without hardcoding URLs\n\n### HTML Method (Recommended for Simple Cases)\n\n```html\n<!-- Hidden input stores the API base path -->\n<input type=\"hidden\" id=\"serverUrl\" value=\"api\">\n\n<script>\nfunction getServerUrl() {\n    return document.getElementById(''serverUrl'').value.trim();\n}\n\n// Use in fetch calls\nasync function checkStatus() {\n    const res = await fetch(`${getServerUrl()}/status`);\n    const data = await res.json();\n    // ...\n}\n</script>\n```\n\n**Key Points**:\n- Value is `\"api\"` (relative) not `\"http://localhost:8765\"` (absolute)\n- Browser resolves `api/status` relative to current page\n- If page is at `https://example.com/rabbit/`, request goes to `https://example.com/rabbit/api/status`\n- Proxy strips `/rabbit/` and forwards to backend\n\n### JavaScript Config Method (For Complex Applications)\n\n```javascript\n// config.js\nconst CONFIG = {\n    API_BASE: ''api'',  // Relative to current path\n    WS_BASE: ''ws''     // WebSocket endpoint if needed\n};\n\n// Use throughout app\nfetch(`${CONFIG.API_BASE}/endpoint`)\n```\n\n**When to use**:\n- Multiple API endpoints\n- Different base paths for dev/staging/prod\n- Need to change paths without editing HTML\n\n## ProxyPass Configuration Pattern\n\n**Purpose**: Configure Apache to forward requests from public path to internal service\n\n### Basic Single-Service Configuration\n\n**File**: `/etc/apache2/proxy-conf.d/myservice.conf`\n\n```apache\n# Single service on custom path\nProxyPass /myservice/ http://10.99.0.3:8080/\nProxyPassReverse /myservice/ http://10.99.0.3:8080/\n```\n\n**Key Points**:\n- Simple ProxyPass directives (no `<Location>` blocks needed)\n- Trailing slashes on both source and target strip the path prefix\n- Request to `/myservice/page` becomes `/page` at backend\n- `ProxyPassReverse` rewrites response headers (redirects, etc.)\n\n### API + Frontend Configuration\n\n**File**: `/etc/apache2/proxy-conf.d/service-with-api.conf`\n\n```apache\n# Backend API - Must come FIRST (more specific path)\nProxyPass /rabbit/api/ http://10.99.0.3:8765/\nProxyPassReverse /rabbit/api/ http://10.99.0.3:8765/\n\n# Frontend - Comes SECOND (less specific path)\nProxyPass /rabbit/ http://10.99.0.3:9273/\nProxyPassReverse /rabbit/ http://10.99.0.3:9273/\n```\n\n**Key Points**:\n- API location MUST be listed first (more specific)\n- If frontend is listed first, it catches API requests → 404\n- Both locations strip their prefix before forwarding\n- Request flow:\n  - `GET /rabbit/api/status` → matches first rule → `GET /status` to port 8765\n  - `GET /rabbit/index.html` → matches second rule → `GET /index.html` to port 9273\n\n### Large File Upload Configuration\n\n```apache\n# Service that handles file uploads (PDFs, images, etc.)\nProxyPass /uploads/ http://10.99.0.3:7000/\nProxyPassReverse /uploads/ http://10.99.0.3:7000/\n\n# Important for large PDF uploads\n<Location /uploads/>\n    ProxyPass http://10.99.0.3:7000/\n    ProxyPassReverse http://10.99.0.3:7000/\n\n    # Allow 50MB uploads\n    LimitRequestBody 52428800\n</Location>\n```\n\n**When to use**:\n- File upload services\n- PDF/image processing\n- Any endpoint that receives large request bodies\n\n## Multi-Service Configuration Pattern\n\n**Purpose**: Deploy multiple independent services in one config file\n\n**File**: `/etc/apache2/proxy-conf.d/all-services.conf`\n\n```apache\n# Service 1: API Gateway\nProxyPass /api/ http://10.99.0.3:8001/\nProxyPassReverse /api/ http://10.99.0.3:8001/\n\n# Service 2: Admin Dashboard\nProxyPass /admin/ http://10.99.0.3:8002/\nProxyPassReverse /admin/ http://10.99.0.3:8002/\n\n# Service 3: Public Website\nProxyPass /site/ http://10.99.0.3:8003/\nProxyPassReverse /site/ http://10.99.0.3:8003/\n```\n\n**Key Points**:\n- Each service is completely independent\n- Order doesn''t matter if paths don''t overlap\n- All go live together when Apache reloads\n- Can comment out individual services to disable temporarily\n\n## Deployment Workflow\n\n**Standard deployment process for new service:**\n\n### 1. Verify Local Service Accessibility\n\n```bash\n# From local machine where service runs\ncurl http://10.99.0.3:8765/status  # Test your port\n\n# From rivsprod01 (SSH in)\nssh rivsprod01 \"curl -s http://10.99.0.3:8765/status\"\n```\n\n**Expected**: JSON response or HTML, not connection refused\n\n### 2. Create Apache Configuration\n\n```bash\n# SSH to rivsprod01\nssh rivsprod01\n\n# Create config file (as root or with sudo)\nsudo nano /etc/apache2/proxy-conf.d/myservice.conf\n\n# Add ProxyPass configuration (see patterns above)\n\n# Verify syntax (optional, but recommended)\n# apache2ctl configtest   # May not be available\n# Just proceed to reload if command not found\n```\n\n### 3. Reload Apache\n\n```bash\nsudo systemctl reload apache2\n\n# Verify Apache is still running\nsudo systemctl status apache2\n```\n\n### 4. Test Public Access\n\n```bash\n# From any machine\ncurl https://dw.ramsden-international.com/myservice/\n\n# Or open in browser\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### 404 Not Found - Service Works Locally\n\n**Cause**: ProxyPass configuration issue\n\n**Diagnostic Steps**:\n1. Verify service is accessible from rivsprod01:\n   ```bash\n   ssh rivsprod01 \"curl -s http://10.99.0.3:PORT/endpoint\"\n   ```\n\n2. Check Apache config order:\n   ```bash\n   ssh rivsprod01 \"cat /etc/apache2/proxy-conf.d/myservice.conf\"\n   ```\n   - API paths must come before frontend paths\n   - Verify trailing slashes on both source and target\n\n3. Check Apache error logs:\n   ```bash\n   ssh rivsprod01 \"sudo tail -50 /var/log/apache2/error.log | grep myservice\"\n   ```\n\n**Solution**:\n- Fix ProxyPass order (more specific first)\n- Add missing trailing slashes\n- Reload Apache: `sudo systemctl reload apache2`\n\n### 404 on API Calls, Frontend Works\n\n**Cause**: Frontend path is catching API requests\n\n**Example of Wrong Configuration**:\n```apache\n# WRONG - Frontend catches everything\nProxyPass /app/ http://10.99.0.3:9000/\nProxyPass /app/api/ http://10.99.0.3:8000/\n```\n\n**Solution - Put API First**:\n```apache\n# CORRECT - API catches specific path first\nProxyPass /app/api/ http://10.99.0.3:8000/\nProxyPass /app/ http://10.99.0.3:9000/\n```\n\n### Connection Refused from rivsprod01\n\n**Cause**: Service not listening on accessible IP\n\n**Diagnostic**:\n```bash\n# On machine running service\nnetstat -tlnp | grep PORT\n# or\nss -tlnp | grep PORT\n```\n\n**Look for**:\n- `127.0.0.1:PORT` - Only listening on localhost (wrong)\n- `10.99.0.3:PORT` - Listening on network IP (correct)\n- `0.0.0.0:PORT` - Listening on all interfaces (also correct)\n\n**Solution**: Configure service to bind to `0.0.0.0` or specific IP `10.99.0.3`\n\n### Service Stops Working After Apache Reload\n\n**Cause**: Configuration syntax error\n\n**Diagnostic**:\n```bash\nssh rivsprod01 \"sudo systemctl status apache2\"\n```\n\n**Solution**:\n1. Check for typos in ProxyPass URLs\n2. Verify no missing quotes or slashes\n3. Look at error log: `sudo tail /var/log/apache2/error.log`\n4. Fix config and reload again\n\n### CORS Errors in Browser Console\n\n**Cause**: Backend not configured for CORS, or wrong origin\n\n**Solution (Backend)**: Enable CORS in your service\n\n```python\n# FastAPI example\nfrom fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware\n\napp.add_middleware(\n    CORSMiddleware,\n    allow_origins=[\"*\"],  # Or specific domain\n    allow_credentials=True,\n    allow_methods=[\"*\"],\n    allow_headers=[\"*\"],\n)\n```\n\n**Note**: Proxy handles forwarding; backend sees requests from proxy IP, not client\n\n## IP Addresses Reference\n\n| Hostname | IP Address | Purpose |\n|----------|-----------|---------|\n| rivsprod01 | 10.99.0.2 | Reverse proxy server (Apache) |\n| pogs (local) | 10.99.0.3 | Development machine running services |\n\n**Service Configuration**:\n- Services should bind to `10.99.0.3` or `0.0.0.0` to be accessible from rivsprod01\n- Use `http://10.99.0.3:PORT` in ProxyPass target URLs\n- Never use `localhost` or `127.0.0.1` in ProxyPass targets\n\n## File Locations on rivsprod01\n\n| Path | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `/etc/apache2/proxy-conf.d/*.conf` | Proxy configurations (add yours here) |\n| `/etc/apache2/sites-available/default-ssl.conf` | Main SSL site config (includes proxy-conf.d) |\n| `/var/log/apache2/error.log` | Apache error log |\n| `/var/log/apache2/access.log` | Access log (if needed) |\n\n**Important**: Configs in `/etc/apache2/proxy-conf.d/` are automatically included by the SSL site configuration.\n\n## Best Practices Summary\n\n1. **Always use relative URLs** in frontend code for proxy compatibility\n2. **Test service accessibility** from rivsprod01 before configuring proxy\n3. **Put specific paths first** in Apache config (API before frontend)\n4. **Use trailing slashes** on both ProxyPass source and target for path stripping\n5. **Reload Apache** after config changes: `sudo systemctl reload apache2`\n6. **Keep configs organized** - one file per application or related service group\n7. **Document your paths** - add comments explaining what each ProxyPass does\n8. **Test both frontend and API** after deployment to verify routing\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:44:48.688Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Web Development Agents needing secure and scalable reverse proxy configurations with Apache ProxyPass","zh":"非常适合需要安全且可扩展的反向代理配置的Web开发代理，支持Apache ProxyPass","ja":"Apache ProxyPassを使用した安全でスケーラブルなリバースプロキシ構成を必要とするWeb開発エージェントに最適","ko":"Apache ProxyPass를 사용하는 보안이 가능하고 확장 가능한 리버스 프록시 구성이 필요한 웹 개발 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo web que necesitan configuraciones de proxy inverso seguras y escalables con Apache ProxyPass","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement Web nécessitant des configurations de proxy inversé sécurisées et évolutives avec Apache ProxyPass","de":"Perfekt für Webentwicklungsagenten, die sichere und skalierbare Reverse-Proxy-Konfigurationen mit Apache ProxyPass benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Web que necessitam de configurações de proxy reverso seguras e escaláveis com Apache ProxyPass","ru":"Идеально для агентов веб-разработки, требующих безопасных и масштабируемых конфигураций обратного прокси с Apache ProxyPass","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذين يحتاجون إلى تكوين وكيل متوازي مع Apache ProxyPass آمنและมُوسّع"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to deploy web applications behind the Apache reverse proxy, leveraging relative URL patterns and Apache ProxyPass configuration for secure and efficient routing, utilizing protocols like HTTP and HTTPS","zh":"赋予代理部署Web应用程序在Apache反向代理后面的能力，利用相对URL模式和Apache ProxyPass配置实现安全高效的路由，使用如HTTP和HTTPS的协议","ja":"エージェントがApacheのリバースプロキシの後ろにWebアプリケーションを展開することを可能にし、相対URLパターンとApache ProxyPass構成を使用して安全で効率的なルーティングを実現し、HTTPやHTTPSなどのプロトコルを使用","ko":"에이전트가 Apache 리버스 프록시 뒤에 웹 애플리케이션을 배포할 수 있도록 하며, 상대 URL 패턴 및 Apache ProxyPass 구성으로 보안 및 효율적인 라우팅을 사용하여 HTTP 및 HTTPS와 같은 프로토콜을 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar aplicaciones web detrás del proxy inverso de Apache, aprovechando patrones de URL relativos y configuración de Apache ProxyPass para enrutamiento seguro y eficiente, utilizando protocolos como HTTP y HTTPS","fr":"Permet aux agents de déployer des applications Web derrière le proxy inversé Apache, en exploitant les modèles d''URL relatifs et la configuration d''Apache ProxyPass pour un routage sécurisé et efficace, en utilisant des protocoles tels que HTTP et HTTPS","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Webanwendungen hinter dem Apache-Reverse-Proxy zu bereitstellen, indem relative URL-Muster und die Apache-ProxyPass-Konfiguration für sichere und effiziente Routing verwendet werden, wobei Protokolle wie HTTP und HTTPS genutzt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implantar aplicações web por trás do proxy reverso do Apache, aproveitando padrões de URL relativos e configuração do Apache ProxyPass para roteamento seguro e eficiente, utilizando protocolos como HTTP e HTTPS","ru":"Позволяет агентам развертывать веб-приложения за обратным прокси Apache, используя относительные шаблоны URL и конфигурацию Apache ProxyPass для безопасного и эффективного маршрутизации, используя протоколы seperti HTTP и HTTPS","ar":"يمكن للوكلاء من خلاله نشر التطبيقات الويب خلف وكيل Apache المتوازي، واستخدام أنماط عنوان URL النسبي وتكوين Apache ProxyPass لنظام التوجيه الآمن والفعال، باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل HTTP و HTTPS"},"useCases":{"en":["Deploying web applications with relative URL patterns","Configuring Apache ProxyPass for secure routing","Optimizing frontend code for reverse proxy compatibility"],"zh":["使用相对URL模式部署Web应用程序","配置Apache ProxyPass实现安全路由","优化前端代码以适应反向代理兼容性"],"ja":["相対URLパターンを使用したWebアプリケーションの展開","Apache ProxyPassの構成によるセキュアなルーティング","リバースプロキシの互換性のためにフロントエンドコードの最適化"],"ko":["상대 URL 패턴을 사용하여 웹 애플리케이션 배포","Apache ProxyPass 구성으로 보안 라우팅","리버스 프록시 호환성을 위한 프론트엔드 코드 최적화"],"es":["Implementación de aplicaciones web con patrones de URL relativos","Configuración de Apache ProxyPass para enrutamiento seguro","Optimización del código del frontend para la compatibilidad con el proxy inverso"],"fr":["Déploiement d''applications Web avec des modèles d''URL relatifs","Configuration d''Apache ProxyPass pour un routage sécurisé","Optimisation du code frontal pour la compatibilité du proxy inversé"],"de":["Bereitstellung von Webanwendungen mit relativen URL-Mustern","Konfiguration von Apache ProxyPass für sicheres Routing","Optimierung des Frontend-Codes für die Kompatibilität mit dem Reverse-Proxy"],"pt":["Implantação de aplicações web com padrões de URL relativos","Configuração do Apache ProxyPass para roteamento seguro","Otimização do código frontend para compatibilidade com proxy reverso"],"ru":["Развертывание веб-приложений с относительными шаблонами URL","Настройка Apache ProxyPass для безопасного маршрутизации","Оптимизация frontend-кода для совместимости с обратным прокси"],"ar":["نشر تطبيقات الويب ذات الأنماط النسبي للعنوان","تكوين Apache ProxyPass لنظام التوجيه الآمن","تحسين код البرنامج الأمامي للتوافق مع وكيل متوازي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Apache server access","Specific to rivsprod01 (dw.ramsden-international.com) environment","Frontend code must use relative URLs"],"zh":["需要Apache服务器访问","特定于rivsprod01 (dw.ramsden-international.com)环境","前端代码必须使用相对URL"],"ja":["Apacheサーバーのアクセスが必要","rivsprod01 (dw.ramsden-international.com)環境に特有","フロントエンドコードは相対URLを使用する必要がある"],"ko":["Apache 서버 접근이 필요","rivsprod01 (dw.ramsden-international.com) 환경에 고유","프론트엔드 코드는 상대 URL을 사용해야 함"],"es":["Requiere acceso al servidor Apache","Específico del entorno rivsprod01 (dw.ramsden-international.com)","El código del frontend debe usar URLs relativas"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au serveur Apache","Spécifique à l''environnement rivsprod01 (dw.ramsden-international.com)","Le code frontal doit utiliser des URL relatives"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf den Apache-Server","Spezifisch für die rivsprod01-Umgebung (dw.ramsden-international.com)","Der Frontend-Code muss relative URLs verwenden"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao servidor Apache","Específico para o ambiente rivsprod01 (dw.ramsden-international.com)","O código frontend deve usar URLs relativos"],"ru":["Требует доступа к серверу Apache","Специфичен для среды rivsprod01 (dw.ramsden-international.com)","Код frontend должен использовать относительные URL"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى خادم Apache","محدد لبيئة rivsprod01 (dw.ramsden-international.com)","يجب أن يستخدم رمز البرنامج الأمامي عناوين URL نسبي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('K9i-0/flutter_claude_sandbox/flutter-ui-design', 'community', 'K9i-0', 'flutter_claude_sandbox', 'K9i-0/flutter_claude_sandbox', 'flutter-ui-design', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.411Z', '2026-02-18T03:44:04.450Z', NULL, '{"id":"K9i-0/flutter_claude_sandbox/flutter-ui-design","name":"flutter-ui-design","description":{"zh":"本指南提供了 Flutter UI 设计最佳实践，帮助您创建专业且令人印象深刻的应用程序界面","ja":"このガイドラインは、プロフェッショナルで印象的な Flutter アプリの UI を実現するためのベストプラクティスを提供します","ko":"이 가이드라인은 전문가적이고 인상적인 플러터 UI 디자인을 위한 최고의 실践을 제공합니다","es":"Nuestras pautas de diseño de interfaz de usuario de Flutter ayudan a crear aplicaciones móviles profesionales y atractivas. Aprende a mejorar la experiencia del usuario.","fr":"Nos lignes directrices de conception d''interface utilisateur Flutter aident à créer des applications mobiles professionnelles et attractives. Découvrez comment améliorer l''expérience utilisateur.","de":"Unsere Richtlinien für das Benutzeroberflächendesign von Flutter helfen bei der Erstellung professioneller und ansprechender mobiler Anwendungen. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie die Benutzererfahrung verbessern.","pt":"As diretrizes de design de UI do Flutter ajudam a criar interfaces do usuário profissionais e impressionantes para aplicativos móveis.","ru":"Руководства по дизайну UI для Flutter помогают создавать профессиональные и впечатляющие интерфейсы пользователя для мобильных приложений.","ar":"توجيهات تصميم الواجهة لمؤسسة Flutter تساعد على إنشاء واجهات مستخدم احترافية وملفتة لانتباه لتطبيقات الهاتف المحمول.","en":"Claude Code による Flutter アプリ開発の完全自動化検証。Maestro MCP + Dart MCP で設計・実装・E2Eテストまで AI が実行。"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Flutter UI 设计指南","ja":"Flutter UI デザインガイドライン","ko":"플러터 UI 디자인 가이드라인","es":"Diseño de interfaz de usuario de Flutter","fr":"Conception d''interface utilisateur Flutter","de":"Flutter-Benutzeroberflächendesign","pt":"D