ioration de l''expérience utilisateur","Conception d''interface utilisateur professionnelle"],"de":["Benutzerdefinierte Typografie","Anpassbares Benutzeroberflächendesign","Verwendung moderner Schriftarten","Verbesserung der Benutzererfahrung","Professionelles Benutzeroberflächendesign"],"pt":["Diretrizes de tipografia para texto claro e legível","Uso de fontes modernas do Google Fonts","Dicas para criar layouts atraentes e funcionais","Implementação de cores e espaçamento eficazes","Otimização para dispositivos móveis e tablets"],"ru":["Руководства по типографике для четкого и читаемого текста","Использование современных шрифтов Google Fonts","Советы по созданию привлекательных и функциональных макетов","Реализация эффективного использования цвета и间距","Оптимизация для мобильных устройств и планшетов"],"ar":["إرشادات لتصميم النصوص لجعلها واضحة وقابلة للقراءة","استخدام خطوط moderne من Google Fonts","نصائح لإنشاء تخطيطات جذابة ووظيفية","تنفيذ ألوان وفواصل فعالة","تحسين الأداء لتطبيقات الهاتف المحمول والألواح"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Flutter UI 设计","移动应用设计","用户界面设计","Google Fonts","字体设计","布局设计"],"ja":["Flutter UI デザイン","モバイルアプリ設計","ユーザーインターフェイス設計","Google Fonts","フォントデザイン","レイアウト設計"],"ko":["플러터 UI 디자인","모바일 애플리케이션 디자인","사용자 인터페이스 디자인","구글 폰트","글꼴 디자인","레이아웃 디자인"],"es":["diseño de interfaz de usuario de Flutter","desarrollo de aplicaciones móviles","tipografía en Flutter","diseño de interfaz de usuario adaptable","mejora de la experiencia del usuario","fuentes modernas en Flutter"],"fr":["conception d''interface utilisateur Flutter","développement d''applications mobiles","typographie dans Flutter","conception d''interface utilisateur adaptable","amélioration de l''expérience utilisateur","polices modernes dans Flutter"],"de":["Benutzeroberflächendesign von Flutter","Entwicklung mobiler Anwendungen","Typografie in Flutter","anpassbares Benutzeroberflächendesign","Verbesserung der Benutzererfahrung","moderne Schriftarten in Flutter"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de UI do Flutter","design de interface do usuário","tipografia para aplicativos móveis","Google Fonts","layouts atraentes","cores e espaçamento eficazes","otimização para dispositivos móveis"],"ru":["разработка интерфейса Flutter","дизайн интерфейса пользователя","типография для мобильных приложений","Google Fonts","привлекательные макеты","эффективное использование цвета и间距","оптимизация для мобильных устройств"],"ar":["تصميم واجهة المستخدم في Flutter","تصميم الواجهة","تصميم النصوص لتطبيقات الهاتف المحمول","Google Fonts","تخطيطات جذابة","ألوان وفواصل فعالة","تحسين الأداء لتطبيقات الهاتف المحمول"]}},"owner":"K9i-0","repo":"flutter_claude_sandbox","repoPath":"K9i-0/flutter_claude_sandbox","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.411Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"flutter-ui-design","description":"FlutterアプリのモダンUIデザインガイドライン。Material Design 3をベースに、洗練されたビジュアルを実現。","bodyPreview":"# Flutter UI Design Guidelines\n\n## Purpose\n\nこのスキルは、FlutterアプリのUIを「ありきたりなデフォルト」から脱却させ、プロフェッショナルで印象的なデザインを実現するためのガイドラインを提供します。\n\n## Typography（タイポグラフィ）\n\n### 避けるべきパターン\n- デフォルトの`Roboto`のみの使用\n- 単調なフォントウェイト（Regular/Boldのみ）\n- 均一なテキストサイズ\n\n### 推奨アプローチ\n\n```dart\n// Google Fontsでモダンなフォントを使用\nimport ''package:google_fonts/google_fonts.dart'';\n\n// タイトル用: 個性的なディスプレイフォント\nGoogleFonts.poppins(fontWeight: FontWeight.w700)\nGoogleFonts.inter(fontWeight: FontWeight.w800)\nGoogleFonts.plusJakartaSans()\n\n// 本文用: 読みやすいサンセリフ","body":"# Flutter UI Design Guidelines\n\n## Purpose\n\nこのスキルは、FlutterアプリのUIを「ありきたりなデフォルト」から脱却させ、プロフェッショナルで印象的なデザインを実現するためのガイドラインを提供します。\n\n## Typography（タイポグラフィ）\n\n### 避けるべきパターン\n- デフォルトの`Roboto`のみの使用\n- 単調なフォントウェイト（Regular/Boldのみ）\n- 均一なテキストサイズ\n\n### 推奨アプローチ\n\n```dart\n// Google Fontsでモダンなフォントを使用\nimport ''package:google_fonts/google_fonts.dart'';\n\n// タイトル用: 個性的なディスプレイフォント\nGoogleFonts.poppins(fontWeight: FontWeight.w700)\nGoogleFonts.inter(fontWeight: FontWeight.w800)\nGoogleFonts.plusJakartaSans()\n\n// 本文用: 読みやすいサンセリフ\nGoogleFonts.inter()\nGoogleFonts.dmSans()\n\n// コントラストを意識したサイズ階層\nheadlineLarge: 32sp, weight: 800\nheadlineMedium: 24sp, weight: 700\ntitleLarge: 20sp, weight: 600\nbodyLarge: 16sp, weight: 400\nlabelSmall: 12sp, weight: 500\n```\n\n### フォントウェイトの活用\n- 極端なコントラスト: `w300` と `w800` を組み合わせる\n- 見出しは太く（w600-w800）、本文は通常（w400）\n\n## Color & Theme（カラー・テーマ）\n\n### 避けるべきパターン\n- Material Design のデフォルト青/紫\n- 控えめで均等なカラーパレット\n- 灰色ばかりの無難なUI\n\n### 推奨アプローチ\n\n```dart\n// ダークテーマ: 深みのある背景 + 鮮やかなアクセント\nColorScheme.dark(\n  surface: Color(0xFF0F0F14),        // 深いダークグレー\n  surfaceContainerHighest: Color(0xFF1A1A23),\n  primary: Color(0xFF6366F1),         // 鮮やかなインディゴ\n  secondary: Color(0xFF22D3EE),       // シアンアクセント\n  tertiary: Color(0xFFF472B6),        // ピンクアクセント\n)\n\n// ライトテーマ: クリーンな白 + ビビッドなアクセント\nColorScheme.light(\n  surface: Color(0xFFFAFAFC),\n  surfaceContainerHighest: Color(0xFFF1F5F9),\n  primary: Color(0xFF4F46E5),         // インディゴ\n  secondary: Color(0xFF0EA5E9),       // スカイブルー\n  tertiary: Color(0xFFEC4899),        // ピンク\n)\n```\n\n### カラー活用のポイント\n- **Dominant Color**: 1つのプライマリカラーを大胆に使用\n- **Sharp Accents**: セカンダリカラーはアクセントとして控えめに\n- **Semantic Colors**: 成功=緑、エラー=赤、警告=黄は直感的に\n\n## Elevation & Depth（立体感）\n\n### 避けるべきパターン\n- フラットすぎるデザイン\n- 均一なelevation\n- 影の乱用\n\n### 推奨アプローチ\n\n```dart\n// カードに微妙な立体感\nCard(\n  elevation: 0,\n  shape: RoundedRectangleBorder(\n    borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(16),\n  ),\n  color: theme.colorScheme.surfaceContainerHighest,\n  child: ...\n)\n\n// ソフトシャドウ（コントラスト控えめ）\nBoxDecoration(\n  borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(16),\n  boxShadow: [\n    BoxShadow(\n      color: Colors.black.withOpacity(0.04),\n      blurRadius: 10,\n      offset: Offset(0, 4),\n    ),\n  ],\n)\n\n// グラスモーフィズム効果\nClipRRect(\n  borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(16),\n  child: BackdropFilter(\n    filter: ImageFilter.blur(sigmaX: 10, sigmaY: 10),\n    child: Container(\n      color: Colors.white.withOpacity(0.1),\n      child: ...\n    ),\n  ),\n)\n```\n\n## Motion & Animation（アニメーション）\n\n### 避けるべきパターン\n- アニメーションなしの硬いUI\n- 過剰で散漫なアニメーション\n- 一貫性のないタイミング\n\n### 推奨アプローチ\n\n```dart\n// ページ遷移: スムーズなフェード+スライド\nPageRouteBuilder(\n  transitionDuration: Duration(milliseconds: 300),\n  pageBuilder: (_, __, ___) => DestinationPage(),\n  transitionsBuilder: (_, animation, __, child) {\n    return FadeTransition(\n      opacity: animation,\n      child: SlideTransition(\n        position: Tween<Offset>(\n          begin: Offset(0, 0.05),\n          end: Offset.zero,\n        ).animate(CurvedAnimation(\n          parent: animation,\n          curve: Curves.easeOutCubic,\n        )),\n        child: child,\n      ),\n    );\n  },\n)\n\n// リスト項目: Staggered Animation\nAnimatedList + interval-based delays\n\n// タップフィードバック: 微細なスケール\nTransform.scale(\n  scale: isPressed ? 0.98 : 1.0,\n  child: AnimatedContainer(\n    duration: Duration(milliseconds: 100),\n    ...\n  ),\n)\n```\n\n### タイミングの指針\n- **短い操作（タップ）**: 100-150ms\n- **画面遷移**: 250-350ms\n- **複雑なアニメーション**: 400-600ms\n- **Curve**: `easeOutCubic`、`easeInOutCubic` を基本に\n\n## Layout & Spacing（レイアウト・余白）\n\n### 避けるべきパターン\n- 詰まりすぎたUI\n- 不規則なパディング\n- 要素間の余白不足\n\n### 推奨アプローチ\n\n```dart\n// 8px基準のスペーシングシステム\nconst spacing = (\n  xs: 4.0,\n  sm: 8.0,\n  md: 16.0,\n  lg: 24.0,\n  xl: 32.0,\n  xxl: 48.0,\n);\n\n// コンテンツエリアの余白\nPadding(\n  padding: EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 20, vertical: 16),\n  child: ...\n)\n\n// カード内の余白は外より大きく\nCard(\n  child: Padding(\n    padding: EdgeInsets.all(20),\n    child: ...\n  ),\n)\n\n// 要素間のギャップ\nSizedBox(height: 16) // 関連要素間\nSizedBox(height: 32) // セクション間\n```\n\n## Components（コンポーネント）\n\n### ボタン\n\n```dart\n// プライマリボタン: 角丸 + 十分なパディング\nFilledButton(\n  style: FilledButton.styleFrom(\n    padding: EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 24, vertical: 16),\n    shape: RoundedRectangleBorder(\n      borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(12),\n    ),\n  ),\n  child: Text(''Action''),\n)\n\n// アウトラインボタン\nOutlinedButton(\n  style: OutlinedButton.styleFrom(\n    side: BorderSide(color: theme.colorScheme.outline, width: 1.5),\n    shape: RoundedRectangleBorder(\n      borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(12),\n    ),\n  ),\n)\n```\n\n### 入力フィールド\n\n```dart\nTextField(\n  decoration: InputDecoration(\n    filled: true,\n    fillColor: theme.colorScheme.surfaceContainerHighest,\n    border: OutlineInputBorder(\n      borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(12),\n      borderSide: BorderSide.none,\n    ),\n    focusedBorder: OutlineInputBorder(\n      borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(12),\n      borderSide: BorderSide(\n        color: theme.colorScheme.primary,\n        width: 2,\n      ),\n    ),\n    contentPadding: EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 16, vertical: 16),\n  ),\n)\n```\n\n### FAB\n\n```dart\nFloatingActionButton(\n  elevation: 2,\n  shape: RoundedRectangleBorder(\n    borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(16),\n  ),\n  child: Icon(Icons.add),\n)\n```\n\n## Background（背景）\n\n### 推奨テクニック\n\n```dart\n// グラデーション背景\nContainer(\n  decoration: BoxDecoration(\n    gradient: LinearGradient(\n      begin: Alignment.topLeft,\n      end: Alignment.bottomRight,\n      colors: [\n        theme.colorScheme.surface,\n        theme.colorScheme.surface.withOpacity(0.95),\n      ],\n    ),\n  ),\n)\n\n// サブトルなパターン（ドット、グリッド）\nCustomPaint(\n  painter: DotPatternPainter(\n    color: theme.colorScheme.outline.withOpacity(0.05),\n    spacing: 20,\n  ),\n)\n```\n\n## Checklist\n\nUIを実装する際のチェックリスト:\n\n- [ ] デフォルトフォント以外を使用しているか\n- [ ] カラーパレットにアクセントカラーがあるか\n- [ ] 適切な余白・パディングが設定されているか\n- [ ] インタラクションにフィードバック（アニメーション）があるか\n- [ ] コンポーネントの角丸が統一されているか（12-16px推奨）\n- [ ] テキストの階層（サイズ・ウェイト）が明確か\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:44:04.450Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Mobile App Development Agents needing advanced Flutter UI design capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级 Flutter UI 设计能力的移动应用开发代理。","ja":"モバイルアプリ開発エージェントが高度なFlutter UI設計機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 Flutter UI 디자인 기능이 필요한 모바일 앱 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo de aplicaciones móviles que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de diseño de interfaz de usuario de Flutter.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement d''applications mobiles ayant besoin de capacités avancées de conception d''interface utilisateur Flutter.","de":"Perfekt für Mobile App Development Agents, die erweiterte Flutter Benutzeroberflächendesign-Funktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento de Aplicativos Móveis que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de design de UI do Flutter.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки мобильных приложений, которым требуются продвинутые возможности проектирования UI Flutter.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تطبيق الجوال الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات تصميم واجهة المستخدم Flutter متقدمة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create professional and impressive Flutter app designs using modern typography with Google Fonts, such as Poppins and Inter, and implement best practices for typography, including variable font weights and sizes, while leveraging Dart and the Flutter framework.","zh":"赋予代理创建使用现代字体（如Poppins和Inter）和Google Fonts的专业且令人印象深刻的Flutter应用设计能力，并实施最佳的字体实践，包括可变字体权重和大小，同时利用Dart和Flutter框架。","ja":"エージェントがGoogle Fonts（PoppinsやInterなど）を使用したモダンなタイポグラフィーでプロフェッショナルで印象的なFlutterアプリのデザインを作成し、ベストプラクティスを実施する能力を提供します。可変フォントの重さやサイズなどを利用してDartやFlutterフレームワークを活用します。","ko":"에이전트가 구글 폰트(Poppins, Inter 등)를 사용한 모던한 타이포그래피로 전문적이고 인상적인 Flutter 앱 디자인을 생성하도록 하며, 가변 폰트 크기 및 두께 등을 포함한 타이포그래피의 모범 사례를 구현하면서 다트와 Flutter 프레임워크를 활용할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear diseños de aplicaciones Flutter profesionales e impresionantes utilizando tipografía moderna con Google Fonts, como Poppins e Inter, e implementar las mejores prácticas para la tipografía, incluyendo pesos y tamaños de fuente variables, aprovechando Dart y el marco de trabajo Flutter.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des conceptions d''applications Flutter professionnelles et impressionnantes en utilisant une typographie moderne avec Google Fonts, tels que Poppins et Inter, et de mettre en œuvre les meilleures pratiques pour la typographie, notamment les poids et les tailles de police variables, en exploitant Dart et le framework Flutter.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, professionelle und beeindruckende Flutter-App-Designs mit moderner Typografie unter Verwendung von Google-Schriften wie Poppins und Inter zu erstellen und bewährte Verfahren für die Typografie umzusetzen, einschließlich variabler Schriftgewichte und -größen, unter Nutzung von Dart und dem Flutter-Framework.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar projetos de design de aplicativos Flutter profissionais e impressionantes usando moderna tipografia com Google Fonts, como Poppins e Inter, e implementar as melhores práticas para tipografia, incluindo pesos e tamanhos de fonte variáveis, aproveitando Dart e o framework Flutter.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать профессиональные и впечатляющие проекты дизайна приложений Flutter с использованием современной типографики и шрифтов Google, таких как Poppins и Inter, и реализовывать лучшие практики типографики, включая переменные веса и размеры шрифта, используя Dart и фреймворк Flutter.","ar":"يمكن للعميل إنشاء تصاميم تطبيقات Flutter احترافية وملفتة باستخدام الطباعة الحديثة مع خطوط جوجل مثل Poppins و Inter، وتنفيذ أفضل الممارسات للطباعة، بما في ذلك أحجام وأوزان خط متغيرة، مع استخدام Dart و إطار Flutter."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing visually appealing Flutter app interfaces","Implementing consistent typography across Flutter apps","Automating Flutter UI testing with Maestro MCP and Dart MCP"],"zh":["为Flutter应用设计视觉上吸引人的界面","在Flutter应用中实现一致的字体样式","使用Maestro MCP和Dart MCP自动化Flutter UI测试"],"ja":["Flutterアプリの視覚的に魅力的なインターフェイスを設計する","Flutterアプリ全体で一貫したタイポグラフィーを実装する","Maestro MCPとDart MCPを使用してFlutter UIテストを自動化する"],"ko":["Flutter 앱의 시각적으로 매력적인 인터페이스를 디자인하는 것","Flutter 앱 전체에서 일관된 타이포그래피를 구현하는 것","Maestro MCP와 Dart MCP를 사용하여 Flutter UI 테스트를 자동화하는 것"],"es":["Diseñar interfaces de aplicaciones Flutter visualmente atractivas","Implementar una tipografía coherente en aplicaciones Flutter","Automatizar las pruebas de interfaz de usuario de Flutter con Maestro MCP y Dart MCP"],"fr":["Concevoir des interfaces d''applications Flutter visuellement attrayantes","Mettre en œuvre une typographie cohérente dans les applications Flutter","Automatiser les tests d''interface utilisateur Flutter avec Maestro MCP et Dart MCP"],"de":["Visuell ansprechende Flutter-App-Oberflächen entwerfen","Eine konsistente Typografie in Flutter-Apps implementieren","Flutter-Benutzeroberflächentests mit Maestro MCP und Dart MCP automatisieren"],"pt":["Projetar interfaces de aplicativos Flutter visualmente atraentes","Implementar tipografia consistente em aplicativos Flutter","Automatizar testes de UI do Flutter com Maestro MCP e Dart MCP"],"ru":["Проектирование визуально привлекательных интерфейсов приложений Flutter","Реализация последовательной типографики в приложениях Flutter","Автоматизация тестирования UI Flutter с помощью Maestro MCP и Dart MCP"],"ar":["تصميم واجهات تطبيقات Flutter بصريًا جذابة","تنفيذ طباعة متسقة عبر تطبيقات Flutter","الاستفادة من تلقين اختبار واجهة المستخدم Flutter مع Maestro MCP و Dart MCP"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Dart and Flutter installation","Limited to Flutter app development"],"zh":["需要安装Dart和Flutter","仅限Flutter应用开发"],"ja":["DartとFlutterのインストールが必要","Flutterアプリ開発のみに限定される"],"ko":["다트와 Flutter의 설치가 필요함","Flutter 애플리케이션 개발에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de Dart y Flutter","Limitado al desarrollo de aplicaciones Flutter"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de Dart et Flutter","Limité au développement d''applications Flutter"],"de":["Benötigt die Installation von Dart und Flutter","Begrenzt auf die Entwicklung von Flutter-Apps"],"pt":["Requer instalação do Dart e do Flutter","Limitado ao desenvolvimento de aplicativos Flutter"],"ru":["Требует установки Dart и Flutter","Ограничен разработкой приложений Flutter"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت Dart و Flutter","محدود بتطوير تطبيقات Flutter"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('hippocampus-dev/hippocampus/kubernetes-operations', 'community', 'hippocampus-dev', 'hippocampus', 'hippocampus-dev/hippocampus', 'kubernetes-operations', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.411Z', '2026-02-18T03:44:49.670Z', NULL, '{"id":"hippocampus-dev/hippocampus/kubernetes-operations","name":"kubernetes-operations","description":{"zh":"Kubernetes操作指南，涵盖Grafana和ArgoCD的使用，帮助开发者高效运维","ja":"Kubernetes操作マニュアル。GrafanaとArgoCDの使用方法を解説し、開発者の効率的な運用を支援","ko":"쿠버네티스 운영 가이드. Grafana 및 ArgoCD 사용 방법을 설명하고 개발자의 효율적인 운영을 지원합니다","es":"El skill de operaciones de Kubernetes te permite acceder a herramientas de monitoreo y depuración como Grafana y kubectl","fr":"Le skill d''opérations Kubernetes vous permet d''accéder à des outils de surveillance et de débogage tels que Grafana et kubectl","de":"Das Kubernetes-Operations-Skill ermöglicht Ihnen den Zugriff auf Überwachungs- und Debugging-Tools wie Grafana und kubectl","pt":"Aprenda a gerenciar e depurar operações em clusters Kubernetes com acesso a ferramentas como Grafana e kubectl","ru":"Узнайте, как управлять и отладить операции в кластерах Kubernetes с доступом к инструментам seperti Grafana и kubectl","ar":"تعلم كيفية إدارة وتصحيح عمليات في مجموعات كوبيرنتس مع الوصول إلى أدوات مثل Grafana و kubectl","en":"Mirror of hippocampus"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Kubernetes操作指南","ja":"Kubernetes操作マニュアル","ko":"쿠버네티스 운영 가이드","es":"Operaciones de Kubernetes","fr":"Opérations Kubernetes","de":"Kubernetes-Betrieb","pt":"Operações Kubernetes: Guia de Depuração","ru":"Операции Kubernetes: Руководство по отладке","ar":"عمليات كوبيرنتس: دليل التصحيح","en":"kubernetes-operations"},"description":{"zh":"Kubernetes操作指南，涵盖Grafana和ArgoCD的使用，帮助开发者高效运维","ja":"Kubernetes操作マニュアル。GrafanaとArgoCDの使用方法を解説し、開発者の効率的な運用を支援","ko":"쿠버네티스 운영 가이드. Grafana 및 ArgoCD 사용 방법을 설명하고 개발자의 효율적인 운영을 지원합니다","es":"El skill de operaciones de Kubernetes te permite acceder a herramientas de monitoreo y depuración como Grafana y kubectl","fr":"Le skill d''opérations Kubernetes vous permet d''accéder à des outils de surveillance et de débogage tels que Grafana et kubectl","de":"Das Kubernetes-Operations-Skill ermöglicht Ihnen den Zugriff auf Überwachungs- und Debugging-Tools wie Grafana und kubectl","pt":"Aprenda a gerenciar e depurar operações em clusters Kubernetes com acesso a ferramentas como Grafana e kubectl","ru":"Узнайте, как управлять и отладить операции в кластерах Kubernetes с доступом к инструментам seperti Grafana и kubectl","ar":"تعلم كيفية إدارة وتصحيح عمليات في مجموعات كوبيرنتس مع الوصول إلى أدوات مثل Grafana و kubectl","en":"Mirror of hippocampus"},"definition":{"en":"Mirror of hippocampus"},"features":{"zh":["访问Grafana仪表盘","禁用ArgoCD自愈功能","查看Pod启动失败事件","使用kubectl调试","查看容器内过程和网络信息"],"ja":["Grafanaダッシュボードへのアクセス","ArgoCDのセルフヒール機能の無効化","Podの起動失敗イベントの表示","kubectlによるデバッグ","コンテナ内のプロセスとネットワーク情報の表示"],"ko":["Grafana 대시보드로 이동","ArgoCD 자동복구 기능 비활성화","Pod 시작 실패 이벤트 보기","kubectl로 디버깅","컨테이너 내 프로세스 및 네트워크 정보 보기"],"es":["Acceso a Grafana","Depuración con kubectl","Monitoreo de clusters","Análisis de registros","Detección de errores"],"fr":["Accès à Grafana","Débogage avec kubectl","Surveillance de clusters","Analyse de journaux","Détection d''erreurs"],"de":["Zugriff auf Grafana","Fehlersuche mit kubectl","Überwachung von Clustern","Analyse von Protokollen","Fehlererkennung"],"pt":["Acesso a Grafana para monitoramento","Depuração de falhas de inicialização de pods","Análise de logs e métricas","Uso de kubectl para gerenciar clusters","Desativação de selfHeal do ArgoCD","Reabilitação do ArgoCD após alterações manuais"],"ru":["Доступ к Grafana для мониторинга","Отладка сбоя при запуске pods","Анализ логов и метрик","Использование kubectl для управления кластерами","Отключение selfHeal ArgoCD","Восстановление ArgoCD после ручных изменений"],"ar":["الوصول إلى Grafana لمراقبة الأداء","تصحيح أخطاء بدء تشغيل الحاويات","تحليل السجلات والقياسات","استخدام kubectl لإدارة المجموعات","تعطيل خاصية selfHeal في ArgoCD","إعادة تمكين ArgoCD بعد التغييرات اليدوية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Kubernetes操作","Grafana","ArgoCD","kubectl","Pod启动失败","容器内过程","网络信息","DevOps"],"ja":["Kubernetes操作","Grafana","ArgoCD","kubectl","Podの起動失敗","コンテナ内のプロセス","ネットワーク情報","DevOps"],"ko":["쿠버네티스 운영","Grafana","ArgoCD","kubectl","Pod 시작 실패","컨테이너 내 프로세스","네트워크 정보","DevOps"],"es":["Kubernetes","operaciones de Kubernetes","Grafana","kubectl","monitoreo de clusters","depuración de contenedores","orquestación de contenedores"],"fr":["Kubernetes","opérations Kubernetes","Grafana","kubectl","surveillance de clusters","débogage de conteneurs","orchestration de conteneurs"],"de":["Kubernetes","Kubernetes-Betrieb","Grafana","kubectl","Überwachung von Clustern","Fehlersuche in Containern","Container-Orchestrierung"],"pt":["Kubernetes","Operações","Depuração","Grafana","kubectl","ArgoCD","selfHeal","Monitoramento","Logs","Métricas"],"ru":["Kubernetes","Операции","Отладка","Grafana","kubectl","ArgoCD","selfHeal","Мониторинг","Логи","Метрики"],"ar":["كوبيرنتس","عمليات","تصحيح","Grafana","kubectl","ArgoCD","selfHeal","مراقبة","سجلات","قياسات"]}},"owner":"hippocampus-dev","repo":"hippocampus","repoPath":"hippocampus-dev/hippocampus","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.411Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"kubernetes-operations","description":"Kubernetes cluster operations on minikube including observability (Grafana, Prometheus, Alertmanager, Loki, Tempo), debugging (kubectl debug, ephemeral containers), and cluster management (ArgoCD). Use when working with cluster/manifests/, Kubernetes workloads, pods, deployments, operators, controllers, or cluster components.","bodyPreview":"* Access Grafana at `https://grafana.minikube.127.0.0.1.nip.io`\n* Disable ArgoCD selfHeal before manual changes, re-enable after\n\n## Debugging\n\n| Investigating | Tool | Entry Point                                 |\n|---------------|------|---------------------------------------------|\n| Traces, metrics, logs, profiles | Grafana | `https://grafana.minikube.127.0.0.1.nip.io` |\n| Pod startup failures, events | kubectl | `kubectl get events -n <namespace>`         |\n| In-container process/network |","body":"* Access Grafana at `https://grafana.minikube.127.0.0.1.nip.io`\n* Disable ArgoCD selfHeal before manual changes, re-enable after\n\n## Debugging\n\n| Investigating | Tool | Entry Point                                 |\n|---------------|------|---------------------------------------------|\n| Traces, metrics, logs, profiles | Grafana | `https://grafana.minikube.127.0.0.1.nip.io` |\n| Pod startup failures, events | kubectl | `kubectl get events -n <namespace>`         |\n| In-container process/network | kubectl debug | Ephemeral container                         |\n\n### Observability Investigation (via Grafana)\n\nUse Grafana for all observability signals. Do NOT query backends (Tempo, Mimir, Loki) directly.\n\n1. **Get query parameters** - Check `cluster/manifests/<app>/` for namespace, labels, `OTEL_SERVICE_NAME` (see [Queries](reference/queries.md) for parameter locations)\n2. **Open Grafana** - Access `https://grafana.minikube.127.0.0.1.nip.io` in browser\n3. **Select datasource and query** - Use appropriate signal:\n\n| Signal | Backend | Datasource | Query Language | Use Case |\n|--------|---------|------------|----------------|----------|\n| Traces | Tempo | Tempo | TraceQL | Request flow, latency, access destinations |\n| Metrics | Mimir (Prometheus) | Mimir | PromQL | Resource usage, HTTP rates, alerting |\n| Logs | Loki | Loki | LogQL | Error investigation, audit |\n| Profiles | Pyroscope | Pyroscope | Flamegraph UI | CPU/memory hotspots |\n| Probes | Blackbox Exporter | Mimir | PromQL | Endpoint reachability |\n\n| Symptom | Signal | Query Approach |\n|---------|--------|----------------|\n| Errors in logs | Loki → Tempo | Extract traceid from logs, trace in Tempo |\n| Latency/5xx | Tempo | Search traces with `status = error` |\n| Unknown outbound dependencies | Tempo | Search traces, inspect spans for outbound calls |\n| Resource saturation | Mimir | Query CPU/memory metrics |\n| High CPU/memory | Pyroscope | Check flamegraphs |\n\n### Pod Direct Investigation (via kubectl)\n\nUse kubectl when Grafana cannot answer the question (e.g., pod not starting, container-level inspection).\n\n| Symptom | Action |\n|---------|--------|\n| Pod not starting | `kubectl get events -n <namespace>` |\n| CrashLoopBackOff | `kubectl logs <pod> -n <namespace> --previous` |\n| Network connectivity | `kubectl debug` with ephemeral container |\n| Process inspection | `kubectl debug` with ephemeral container |\n\n#### Ephemeral Container\n\n```bash\nkubectl debug <pod-name> -n <namespace> \\\n  --profile=restricted \\\n  --image=ghcr.io/hippocampus-dev/hippocampus/ephemeral-container:main \\\n  --target=<container-name> \\\n  -- <command>\n```\n\nNote: Do not use `-it` flag when executing commands. It causes output streaming issues.\n\n## Manual Changes\n\nRequired when directly modifying live cluster resources (e.g., `kubectl apply`, `kubectl patch`, `kubectl delete`) outside of the GitOps workflow.\n\n| Operation | Requires Manual Changes |\n|-----------|------------------------|\n| `kubectl apply/patch/delete` | Yes |\n| Debugging (read-only: logs, events, debug) | No |\n| Grafana queries | No |\n| Editing manifests in repo | No (ArgoCD syncs automatically) |\n\n### ArgoCD selfHeal Control\n\nArgoCD reverts manual changes unless selfHeal is disabled first. Always re-enable after.\n\n```bash\n# Disable selfHeal\nkubectl patch application <app-name> -n argocd --type=merge \\\n  -p ''{\"spec\":{\"syncPolicy\":{\"selfHeal\":false}}}''\n\n# Re-enable selfHeal (after work is complete)\nkubectl patch application <app-name> -n argocd --type=merge \\\n  -p ''{\"spec\":{\"syncPolicy\":{\"selfHeal\":true}}}''\n```\n\n## Observability Stack Manifests\n\n| Component | Path |\n|-----------|------|\n| Grafana | `cluster/manifests/grafana/` |\n| Tempo | `cluster/manifests/tempo/` |\n| Mimir | `cluster/manifests/mimir/` |\n| Loki | `cluster/manifests/loki/` |\n| Pyroscope | `cluster/manifests/pyroscope/` |\n| Prometheus | `cluster/manifests/prometheus/` |\n| Fluentd | `cluster/manifests/fluentd/` |\n| OpenTelemetry | `cluster/manifests/otel-agent/`, `cluster/manifests/otel-collector/` |\n\n## Reference\n\nIf writing observability queries:\n  See [Queries](reference/queries.md)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:44:49.670Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Cloud Native Agents needing advanced Kubernetes debugging and monitoring capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级 Kubernetes 调试和监控功能的云原生代理。","ja":"クラウドネイティブエージェントが高度なKubernetesデバッグと監視機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 Kubernetes 디버깅 및 모니터링 기능이 필요한 클라우드 네이티브 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes nativos de la nube que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de depuración y monitoreo de Kubernetes.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Cloud Native nécessitant des capacités de débogage et de surveillance avancées de Kubernetes.","de":"Perfekt für Cloud Native Agents, die erweiterte Kubernetes-Debugging- und Überwachungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Nativos em Nuvem que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de depuração e monitoramento do Kubernetes.","ru":"Идеально подходит для облачных агентов, которым необходимы расширенные возможности отладки и мониторинга Kubernetes.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الأصليين في السحابة الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات متقدمة لتصحيح الأخطاء وتحليل أداء كوبيرنتس."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to monitor and debug Kubernetes clusters using tools like Grafana for metrics and logs, and kubectl for pod management and event analysis, while leveraging ArgoCD for automated deployment management.","zh":"赋予代理监控和调试Kubernetes集群的能力，使用类似Grafana的工具进行指标和日志监控，使用kubectl进行容器管理和事件分析，同时利用ArgoCD进行自动化部署管理。","ja":"Grafanaなどのツールを使用してメトリクスとログを監視したり、kubectlを使用してポッドの管理とイベント分析を行ったりすることで、Kubernetesクラスタを監視およびデバッグするエージェントの能力を提供し、ArgoCDを使用して自動化されたデプロイ管理を活用します。","ko":"Grafana와 같은 도구를 사용하여 메트릭스와 로그를 모니터링하거나, kubectl을 사용하여 포드 관리 및 이벤트 분석을 수행하여 Kubernetes 클러스터를 모니터링 및 디버깅할 수 있는 에이전트의 능력을 제공하며, ArgoCD를 사용하여 자동화된 배포 관리를 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a monitorear y depurar clústeres de Kubernetes utilizando herramientas como Grafana para métricas y registros, y kubectl para la administración de pods y el análisis de eventos, aprovechando ArgoCD para la administración de implementaciones automatizadas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de surveiller et de déboguer des clusters Kubernetes en utilisant des outils comme Grafana pour les métriques et les journaux, et kubectl pour la gestion des pods et l''analyse des événements, tout en exploitant ArgoCD pour la gestion des déploiements automatiques.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Kubernetes-Cluster mit Tools wie Grafana für Metriken und Protokolle sowie kubectl für Pod-Verwaltung und Ereignisanalyse zu überwachen und zu debuggen, während ArgoCD für die automatisierte Bereitstellungsverwaltung genutzt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a monitorar e depurar clusters do Kubernetes usando ferramentas como Grafana para métricas e logs, e kubectl para gerenciamento de pods e análise de eventos, aproveitando ArgoCD para gerenciamento de implantação automatizada.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью мониторить и отлаживать кластеры Kubernetes с помощью инструментов, таких как Grafana для метрик и журналов, и kubectl для управления подами и анализа событий, используя ArgoCD для автоматизированного управления развертыванием.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على مراقبة وتحليل أخطاء مجموعات كوبيرنتس باستخدام أدوات مثل جرافانا لتحليل البيانات والسجلات، وكوبيكتيل لادارة الحاويات وتحليل الأحداث، مع الاستفادة من ارغو سي دي لإدارة التثبيت التلقائي."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging pod startup failures and events","Monitoring cluster performance with Grafana","Disabling ArgoCD self-healing for manual changes"],"zh":["调试容器启动失败和事件","使用Grafana监控集群性能","禁用ArgoCD的自愈功能以进行手动更改"],"ja":["ポッドの起動失敗やイベントのデバッグ","Grafanaを使用したクラスタパフォーマンスの監視","ArgoCDの自己回復機能を無効にして手動で変更する"],"ko":["포드 시작 실패 및 이벤트 디버깅","Grafana를 사용한 클러스터 성능 모니터링","ArgoCD의 자가 치유 기능을 비활성화하여 수동으로 변경"],"es":["Depuración de fallos de inicio de pods y eventos","Monitoreo del rendimiento del clúster con Grafana","Deshabilitación de la autoreparación de ArgoCD para cambios manuales"],"fr":["Débogage des échecs de démarrage de pods et des événements","Surveillance des performances du cluster avec Grafana","Désactivation de l''auto-réparation d''ArgoCD pour les modifications manuelles"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung bei Pod-Startfehlern und Ereignissen","Überwachung der Clusterleistung mit Grafana","Deaktivierung der Selbstheilungsfunktion von ArgoCD für manuelle Änderungen"],"pt":["Depuração de falhas de inicialização de pods e eventos","Monitoramento do desempenho do cluster com Grafana","Desabilitação da autoreparação do ArgoCD para alterações manuais"],"ru":["Отладка сбоев запуска подов и событий","Мониторинг производительности кластера с помощью Grafana","Отключение самоисцеления ArgoCD для ручных изменений"],"ar":["تصحيح أخطاء بدء تشغيل الحاويات والأحداث","مراقبة أداء المجموعة باستخدام جرافانا","تعطيل إصلاح ارغو سي دي التلقائي للتعديلات اليدوية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires minikube or Kubernetes cluster access","Grafana and kubectl setup needed","ArgoCD installation required for automated deployment management"],"zh":["需要minikube或Kubernetes集群访问","需要Grafana和kubectl设置","需要ArgoCD安装以进行自动化部署管理"],"ja":["minikubeまたはKubernetesクラスタへのアクセスが必要","Grafanaとkubectlの設定が必要","自動化されたデプロイ管理を行うにはArgoCDのインストールが必要"],"ko":["minikube 또는 Kubernetes 클러스터 액세스가 필요","Grafana 및 kubectl 설정이 필요","자동화된 배포 관리를 위해 ArgoCD 설치가 필요"],"es":["Requiere acceso a minikube o clúster de Kubernetes","Configuración de Grafana y kubectl necesaria","Instalación de ArgoCD requerida para la administración de implementaciones automatizadas"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à minikube ou à un cluster Kubernetes","Configuration de Grafana et kubectl nécessaire","Installation d''ArgoCD requise pour la gestion des déploiements automatiques"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf minikube oder Kubernetes-Cluster","Grafana- und kubectl-Setup erforderlich","ArgoCD-Installation erforderlich für die automatisierte Bereitstellungsverwaltung"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao minikube ou ao cluster do Kubernetes","Configuração do Grafana e kubectl necessária","Instalação do ArgoCD necessária para gerenciamento de implantação automatizada"],"ru":["Требует доступа к minikube или кластеру Kubernetes","Необходима настройка Grafana и kubectl","Требуется установка ArgoCD для автоматизированного управления развертыванием"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى ميني كيوب أو مجموعة كوبيرنتس","تتطلب إعداد جرافانا وكوبيكتيل","يتطلب تثبيت ارغو سي دي لإدارة التثبيت التلقائي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('oimiragieo/agent-studio/brainstorming', 'community', 'oimiragieo', 'agent-studio', 'oimiragieo/agent-studio', 'brainstorming', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.411Z', '2026-02-18T03:44:56.667Z', NULL, '{"id":"oimiragieo/agent-studio/brainstorming","name":"brainstorming","description":{"zh":"AI 辅助头脑风暴可以帮助您将想法转化为成熟的设计和规格。通过自然协作对话，了解项目背景，提出问题并完善您的想法","ja":"AI ブレインストーミングは、アイデアを設計と仕様に変えることができます。プロジェクトの背景を理解し、質問を提案してアイデアを洗練します","ko":"AI 브레인스토밍은 아이디어를 디자인과 사양으로 변환할 수 있습니다. 프로젝트의 배경을 이해하고 질문을 제안하여 아이디어를 다듬습니다","es":"El proceso de brainstorming permite a los desarrolladores convertir ideas en diseños completos a través de un diálogo colaborativo.","fr":"Le processus de brainstorming permet aux développeurs de convertir des idées en conceptions complètes grâce à un dialogue collaboratif.","de":"Der Brainstorming-Prozess ermöglicht es Entwicklern, Ideen in vollständige Designs umzusetzen, indem sie einen kollaborativen Dialog führen.","pt":"O brainstorming é uma técnica de desenvolvimento de ideias em design através do diálogo colaborativo","ru":"Мозговой штурм - это метод разработки идей в дизайне через сотрудничество","ar":"التحليل الذهني هو تقنية لتطوير الأفكار في التصميم من خلال الحوار التعاوني","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI 辅助头脑风暴：将想法转化为设计","ja":"アイデアを設計に変える AI ブレインストーミング","ko":"아이디어를 디자인으로 변환하는 AI 브레인스토밍","es":"Generación de ideas de diseño con diálogo colaborativo","fr":"Création de conceptions de design par dialogue collaboratif","de":"Erstellung von Designideen durch kollaborativen Dialog","pt":"Brainstorming: Desenvolvimento de Ideias em Design","ru":"Мозговой штурм: разработка идей в дизайн","ar":"التحليل الذهني: تطوير الأفكار في التصميم","en":"brainstorming"},"description":{"zh":"AI 辅助头脑风暴可以帮助您将想法转化为成熟的设计和规格。通过自然协作对话，了解项目背景，提出问题并完善您的想法","ja":"AI ブレインストーミングは、アイデアを設計と仕様に変えることができます。プロジェクトの背景を理解し、質問を提案してアイデアを洗練します","ko":"AI 브레인스토밍은 아이디어를 디자인과 사양으로 변환할 수 있습니다. 프로젝트의 배경을 이해하고 질문을 제안하여 아이디어를 다듬습니다","es":"El proceso de brainstorming permite a los desarrolladores convertir ideas en diseños completos a través de un diálogo colaborativo.","fr":"Le processus de brainstorming permet aux développeurs de convertir des idées en conceptions complètes grâce à un dialogue collaboratif.","de":"Der Brainstorming-Prozess ermöglicht es Entwicklern, Ideen in vollständige Designs umzusetzen, indem sie einen kollaborativen Dialog führen.","pt":"O brainstorming é uma técnica de desenvolvimento de ideias em design através do diálogo colaborativo","ru":"Мозговой штурм - это метод разработки идей в дизайне через сотрудничество","ar":"التحليل الذهني هو تقنية لتطوير الأفكار في التصميم من خلال الحوار التعاوني","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["自然协作对话","项目背景理解","逐步提问","设计和规格输出","实时反馈"],"ja":["自然なコラボレーションによる対話","プロジェクトの背景理解","逐次的な質問","設計と仕様の出力","リアルタイムのフィードバック"],"ko":["자연스러운 협력 대화","프로젝트의 배경 이해","逐步적인 질문","디자인과 사양의 출력","실시간 피드백"],"es":["Diálogo colaborativo para desarrollar ideas","Estructuración de proyectos de manera efectiva","Presentación de diseños en secciones pequeñas","Verificación continua del progreso del proyecto","Refinamiento de la idea a través de preguntas y respuestas","Creación de especificaciones detalladas"],"fr":["Dialogue collaboratif pour développer des idées","Structuration de projets de manière efficace","Présentation de conceptions en petites sections","Vérification continue de l''avancement du projet","Affinement de l''idée à travers des questions et des réponses","Création de spécifications détaillées"],"de":["Kollaborativer Dialog zur Entwicklung von Ideen","Strukturierung von Projekten auf effektive Weise","Präsentation von Designs in kleinen Abschnitten","Kontinuierliche Überprüfung des Projektfortschritts","Verfeinerung der Idee durch Fragen und Antworten","Erstellung detaillierter Spezifikationen"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de ideias em design","Diálogo colaborativo natural","Refinamento de ideias através de perguntas","Apresentação de designs em seções","Verificação de designs em cada seção"],"ru":["Разработка идей в дизайне","Естественное сотрудничество","Уточнение идей через вопросы","Представление дизайна по секциям","Проверка дизайна в каждой секции"],"ar":["تطوير الأفكار في التصميم","الحوار التعاوني الطبيعي","تحسين الأفكار من خلال الأسئلة","عرض التصاميم في أقسام","التحقق من التصاميم في كل قسم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI 辅助头脑风暴","设计和规格","自然协作对话","项目背景理解","开发者工具","AI 设计"],"ja":["AI ブレインストーミング","設計と仕様","自然なコラボレーションによる対話","プロジェクトの背景理解","開発者ツール","AI 設計"],"ko":["AI 브레인스토밍","디자인과 사양","자연스러운 협력 대화","프로젝트의 배경 이해","개발자 도구","AI 디자인"],"es":["brainstorming","diseño colaborativo","desarrollo de ideas","proyectos de diseño","diálogo natural","especificaciones detalladas","desarrollo de software","metodologías ágiles"],"fr":["brainstorming","conception collaborative","développement d''idées","projets de conception","dialogue naturel","spécifications détaillées","développement de logiciels","méthodologies agiles"],"de":["Brainstorming","kollaboratives Design","Ideenentwicklung","Designprojekte","natürlicher Dialog","detaillierte Spezifikationen","Software-Entwicklung","Agile Methoden"],"pt":["brainstorming","desenvolvimento de ideias","design","diálogo colaborativo","refinamento de ideias","apresentação de designs"],"ru":["мозговой штурм","разработка идей","дизайн","сотрудничество","уточнение идей","представление дизайна"],"ar":["التحليل الذهني","تطوير الأفكار","التصميم","الحوار التعاوني","تحسين الأفكار","عرض التصاميم"]}},"owner":"oimiragieo","repo":"agent-studio","repoPath":"oimiragieo/agent-studio","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.411Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"brainstorming","description":"Socratic design refinement before implementation. Use when planning creative work or designing features.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"# Brainstorming Ideas Into Designs\n\n## Overview\n\nHelp turn ideas into fully formed designs and specs through natural collaborative dialogue.\n\nStart by understanding the current project context, then ask questions one at a time to refine the idea. Once you understand what you''re building, present the design in small sections (200-300 words), checking after each section whether it looks right so far.\n\n## The Process\n\n**Understanding the idea:**\n\n- Check out the current project state first (files,","body":"# Brainstorming Ideas Into Designs\n\n## Overview\n\nHelp turn ideas into fully formed designs and specs through natural collaborative dialogue.\n\nStart by understanding the current project context, then ask questions one at a time to refine the idea. Once you understand what you''re building, present the design in small sections (200-300 words), checking after each section whether it looks right so far.\n\n## The Process\n\n**Understanding the idea:**\n\n- Check out the current project state first (files, docs, recent commits)\n- Ask questions one at a time to refine the idea\n- Prefer multiple choice questions when possible, but open-ended is fine too\n- Only one question per message - if a topic needs more exploration, break it into multiple questions\n- Focus on understanding: purpose, constraints, success criteria\n\n**Exploring approaches:**\n\n- Propose 2-3 different approaches with trade-offs\n- Present options conversationally with your recommendation and reasoning\n- Lead with your recommended option and explain why\n\n**Presenting the design:**\n\n- Once you believe you understand what you''re building, present the design\n- Break it into sections of 200-300 words\n- Ask after each section whether it looks right so far\n- Cover: architecture, components, data flow, error handling, testing\n- Be ready to go back and clarify if something doesn''t make sense\n\n## After the Design\n\n**Documentation:**\n\n- Write the validated design to `docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>-design.md`\n- Use context-compressor skill if available for efficient documentation\n- Commit the design document to git\n\n**Implementation (if continuing):**\n\n- Ask: \"Ready to set up for implementation?\"\n- Use writing-plans skill to create detailed implementation plan\n\n## Key Principles\n\n- **One question at a time** - Don''t overwhelm with multiple questions\n- **Multiple choice preferred** - Easier to answer than open-ended when possible\n- **YAGNI ruthlessly** - Remove unnecessary features from all designs\n- **Explore alternatives** - Always propose 2-3 approaches before settling\n- **Incremental validation** - Present design in sections, validate each\n- **Be flexible** - Go back and clarify when something doesn''t make sense\n\n## Memory Protocol (MANDATORY)\n\n**Before starting:**\nRead `.claude/context/memory/learnings.md`\n\n**After completing:**\n\n- New pattern -> `.claude/context/memory/learnings.md`\n- Issue found -> `.claude/context/memory/issues.md`\n- Decision made -> `.claude/context/memory/decisions.md`\n\n> ASSUME INTERRUPTION: If it''s not in memory, it didn''t happen.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:44:56.667Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Collaborative Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT needing natural dialogue-based design refinement capabilities.","zh":"适合于需要自然对话基于设计改进能力的协作式代理，如Claude Code和AutoGPT。","ja":"自然な対話に基づく設計改良機能が必要な共同エージェント seperti Claude CodeやAutoGPTに適しています。","ko":"자연어 대화 기반의 디자인 개선 기능이 필요한 협업 에이전트 seperti Claude Code와 AutoGPT에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes colaborativos como Claude Code y AutoGPT que necesitan capacidades de refinamiento de diseño basado en diálogo natural.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents collaboratifs comme Claude Code et AutoGPT nécessitant des capacités de raffinement de conception basées sur un dialogue naturel.","de":"Ideal für kollaborative Agenten wie Claude Code und AutoGPT, die eine Design-Verfeinerung mit natürlichen Dialogfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Colaborativos, como Claude Code e AutoGPT, que necessitam de capacidades de refinamento de design baseadas em diálogo natural.","ru":"Идеально подходит для Коллаборативных Агентов, таких как Claude Code и AutoGPT, требующих естественного диалогового проектирования улучшения возможностей.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التعاون مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT الذين يحتاجون إلى تصميم حوار طبيعي لتحسين القدرات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to engage in iterative design specification through natural language dialogue, utilizing collaborative questioning and incremental design presentation in 200-300 word sections, checking for accuracy after each section, and potentially integrating with file formats and project management protocols.","zh":"使代理能够通过自然语言对话进行迭代设计规范，利用协作式提问和增量设计展示，每个部分200-300字，检查每个部分的准确性，并可能集成文件格式和项目管理协议。","ja":"エージェントが自然言語による対話を通じて設計仕様の反復的な精査を行えるようにし、共同の質問とインクリメンタルな設計の提示を行い、各セクションごとに200-300語で正確性を確認し、ファイル形式やプロジェクト管理プロトコルとの統合も可能にします。","ko":"에이전트가 자연어 대화로 반복적인 디자인 명세를 수행할 수 있게 하며, 협업적인 질문과 증분적인 디자인 프레젠테이션을 통해 200-300 단어로 구분하여 각 섹션의 정확성을 확인하고, 파일 형식 및 프로젝트 관리 프로토콜과 통합할 수 있습니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes participar en la especificación iterativa de diseño a través del diálogo en lenguaje natural, utilizando cuestionamiento colaborativo y presentación de diseño incremental en secciones de 200-300 palabras, comprobando la precisión después de cada sección, e integrándose potencialmente con formatos de archivo y protocolos de gestión de proyectos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de s''engager dans une spécification de conception itérative via un dialogue en langage naturel, en utilisant des questions collaboratives et une présentation de conception incrémentale en sections de 200-300 mots, en vérifiant l''exactitude après chaque section, et en intégrant potentiellement des formats de fichiers et des protocoles de gestion de projet.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, sich an der iterativen Design-Spezifikation durch natürliche Sprachdialoge zu beteiligen, indem sie kollaboratives Fragenstellen und inkrementale Designpräsentation in Abschnitten von 200-300 Wörtern nutzen, die Genauigkeit nach jedem Abschnitt überprüfen und potenziell in Dateiformate und Projektmanagementprotokolle integrieren.","pt":"Habilita agentes a se engajarem em especificação de design iterativa por meio de diálogo de linguagem natural, utilizando questionamento colaborativo e apresentação de design incremental em seções de 200-300 palavras, verificando a precisão após cada seção, e potencialmente integrando-se com formatos de arquivo e protocolos de gerenciamento de projetos.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью участвовать в итеративной спецификации дизайна через естественный языковой диалог, используя коллаборативные вопросы и инкрементальное представление дизайна в разделах по 200-300 слов, проверяя точность после каждого раздела, и потенциально интегрируясь с форматами файлов и протоколами управления проектами.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من المشاركة في تحديد مواصفات التصميم التكراري من خلال حوار اللغة الطبيعية، استخدام الاستفهام التعاوني والتقديم التصميمي المتزايد في أقسام 200-300 كلمة، وفحص الدقة بعد كل قسم، والدمج المحتمل مع تنسيقات الملفات وبروتوكولات إدارة المشروع."},"useCases":{"en":["Refining project ideas through collaborative dialogue","Generating detailed design specifications incrementally","Validating design sections for accuracy and consistency"],"zh":["通过协作对话来改进项目创意","增量生成详细的设计规范","验证设计部分的准确性和一致性"],"ja":["共同の対話を通じてプロジェクトアイデアを洗練する","詳細な設計仕様をインクリメンタルに生成する","設計部分の正確性と一貫性を検証する"],"ko":["협업 대화를 통해 프로젝트 아이디어를 다듬는こと","詳細한 디자인 명세를 증분적으로 생성하는 것","디자인 섹션의 정확성 및 일관성을 검증하는 것"],"es":["Perfeccionar ideas de proyecto a través del diálogo colaborativo","Generar especificaciones de diseño detalladas de forma incremental","Validar secciones de diseño para precisión y coherencia"],"fr":["Affiner les idées de projet via un dialogue collaboratif","Générer des spécifications de conception détaillées de manière incrémentale","Valider les sections de conception pour l''exactitude et la cohérence"],"de":["Projektideen durch kollaborativen Dialog verfeinern","Detaillierte Designspezifikationen inkrementell generieren","Designabschnitte auf Genauigkeit und Konsistenz überprüfen"],"pt":["Aprimorar ideias de projeto por meio de diálogo colaborativo","Gerar especificações de design detalhadas de forma incremental","Validar seções de design para precisão e consistência"],"ru":["Уточнение идей проекта через коллаборативный диалог","Постепенное生成 подробных спецификаций дизайна","Проверка разделов дизайна на точность и последовательность"],"ar":["تحسين أفكار المشروع من خلال حوار تعاوني","توليد مواصفات تصميم مفصلة بشكل متزايد","التحقق من أقسام التصميم على الدقة والاتساق"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of the current project context and state","Dependent on effective questioning and feedback mechanisms"],"zh":["需要了解当前项目的背景和状态","依赖于有效的提问和反馈机制"],"ja":["現在のプロジェクトの状況と状態を理解する必要がある","効果的な質問とフィードバックメカニズムに依存する"],"ko":["현재 프로젝트의 상황 및 상태를 이해해야 함","유효한 질문 및 피드백 메커니즘에 의존"],"es":["Requiere comprensión del contexto y estado actual del proyecto","Depende de mecanismos de preguntas y comentarios efectivos"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension du contexte et de l''état actuel du projet","Dépend de mécanismes de questions et de commentaires efficaces"],"de":["Benötigt das Verständnis des aktuellen Projektkontexts und -zustands","Hängt von effektiven Frage- und Feedbackmechanismen ab"],"pt":["Requer entendimento do contexto e estado atual do projeto","Depende de mecanismos de questionamento e feedback eficazes"],"ru":["Требует понимания текущего контекста и состояния проекта","Зависит от эффективных механизмов вопросов и обратной связи"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم السياق والحالة الحالية للمشروع","يعتمد على آليات الاستفهام والتعليق الفعالة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('kbaseincubator/BERIL-research-observatory/berdl_start', 'community', 'kbaseincubator', 'BERIL-research-observatory', 'kbaseincubator/BERIL-research-observatory', 'berdl_start', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.411Z', '2026-02-18T03:45:07.468Z', NULL, '{"id":"kbaseincubator/BERIL-research-observatory/berdl_start","name":"berdl_start","description":{"zh":"BERIL 研究观测站是一个用于探索微生物生态学的平台，基于 KBase Data Lakehouse。它提供了 35 个数据库和 9 个租户的访问","ja":"BERIL 研究観測所は、マイクロビアル生態学を探索するためのプラットフォームです。KBase Data Lakehouse に基づいています。35 のデータベースと 9 のテナントにアクセスできます","ko":"BERIL 연구 관측소는 미생물 생태학을 탐구하기 위한 플랫폼입니다. KBase Data Lakehouse를 기반으로 하며 35개의 데이터베이스와 9개의 테넌트에 접근할 수 있습니다","es":"El Observatorio de Investigación BERIL explora la ecología microbiana utilizando el lago de datos KBase, alojando 35 bases de datos en 9 inquilinos","fr":"L''Observatoire de Recherche BERIL explore l''écologie microbienne en utilisant le lac de données KBase, hébergeant 35 bases de données dans 9 locataires","de":"Das Forschungsobservatorium BERIL erkundet die mikrobielle Ökologie unter Verwendung des KBase-Datensees, der 35 Datenbanken in 9 Mietern hostet","pt":"O BERIL Research Observatory utiliza o KBase Data Lakehouse para explorar a ecologia microbiana. Aprenda sobre essa plataforma inovadora","ru":"BERIL Research Observatory использует KBase Data Lakehouse для изучения микробной экологии. Узнайте об этой инновационной платформе","ar":"يستخدم مرصد BERIL البحثي KBase Data Lakehouse لاستكشاف علم البيئة الميكروبية. تعرف على هذه المنصة المبتكرة","en":"BERIL Research Observatory - Exploring microbial ecology with the KBase Data Lakehouse"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"BERIL 研究观测站 - 探索微生物生态学","ja":"BERIL 研究観測所 - マイクロビアル生態学の探索","ko":"BERIL 연구 관측소 - 미생물 생태학 탐구","es":"BERIL: Observatorio de Investigación de Ecología Microbiana","fr":"BERIL: Observatoire de Recherche en Écologie Microbienne","de":"BERIL: Forschungsobservatorium für Mikrobielle Ökologie","pt":"BERIL: Explorando Ecologia Microbiana com KBase Data Lake...","ru":"BERIL: Исследование микробной экологии с помощью KBase Da...","ar":"BERIL: استكشاف علم البيئة الميكروبية مع KBase Data Lakehouse","en":"berdl_start"},"description":{"zh":"BERIL 研究观测站是一个用于探索微生物生态学的平台，基于 KBase Data Lakehouse。它提供了 35 个数据库和 9 个租户的访问","ja":"BERIL 研究観測所は、マイクロビアル生態学を探索するためのプラットフォームです。KBase Data Lakehouse に基づいています。35 のデータベースと 9 のテナントにアクセスできます","ko":"BERIL 연구 관측소는 미생물 생태학을 탐구하기 위한 플랫폼입니다. KBase Data Lakehouse를 기반으로 하며 35개의 데이터베이스와 9개의 테넌트에 접근할 수 있습니다","es":"El Observatorio de Investigación BERIL explora la ecología microbiana utilizando el lago de datos KBase, alojando 35 bases de datos en 9 inquilinos","fr":"L''Observatoire de Recherche BERIL explore l''écologie microbienne en utilisant le lac de données KBase, hébergeant 35 bases de données dans 9 locataires","de":"Das Forschungsobservatorium BERIL erkundet die mikrobielle Ökologie unter Verwendung des KBase-Datensees, der 35 Datenbanken in 9 Mietern hostet","pt":"O BERIL Research Observatory utiliza o KBase Data Lakehouse para explorar a ecologia microbiana. Aprenda sobre essa plataforma inovadora","ru":"BERIL Research Observatory использует KBase Data Lakehouse для изучения микробной экологии. Узнайте об этой инновационной платформе","ar":"يستخدم مرصد BERIL البحثي KBase Data Lakehouse لاستكشاف علم البيئة الميكروبية. تعرف على هذه المنصة المبتكرة","en":"BERIL Research Observatory - Exploring microbial ecology with the KBase Data Lakehouse"},"definition":{"en":"BERIL Research Observatory - Exploring microbial ecology with the KBase Data Lakehouse"},"features":{"zh":["35 个数据库","9 个租户","基于 Spark SQL 的 Delta Lakehouse","支持微生物生态学研究","提供数据 lakehouse 功能","支持多租户访问"],"ja":["35 のデータベース","9 のテナント","Spark SQL に基づく Delta Lakehouse","マイクロビアル生態学研究をサポート","データ lakehouse 機能を提供","マルチテナントアクセスをサポート"],"ko":["35개의 데이터베이스","9개의 테넌트","Spark SQL 기반의 Delta Lakehouse","미생물 생태학 연구 지원","데이터 레이크하우스 기능 제공","멀티 테넌트 접근 지원"],"es":["35 bases de datos en 9 inquilinos","Lago de datos Delta en premises","Spark SQL para consultas","Colecciones clave: kbase_ke_pa","Análisis de ecología microbiana","Integración con KBase"],"fr":["35 bases de données dans 9 locataires","Lac de données Delta sur site","Spark SQL pour les requêtes","Collections clés: kbase_ke_pa","Analyse de l''écologie microbienne","Intégration avec KBase"],"de":["35 Datenbanken in 9 Mietern","Delta-Datensee vor Ort","Spark SQL für Abfragen","Schlüsselsammlungen: kbase_ke_pa","Analyse der mikrobiellen Ökologie","Integration mit KBase"],"pt":["Plataforma de dados de lakehouse","35 bancos de dados em 9 locatários","Coleções de dados de microbiologia","Análise de dados com Spark SQL","Integração com o KBase Data Lakehouse"],"ru":["Платформа данных lakehouse","35 баз данных в 9 арендаторах","Коллекции микробиологических данных","Анализ данных с помощью Spark SQL","Интеграция с KBase Data Lakehouse"],"ar":["منصة بيانات بحيرة","35 قاعدة بيانات في 9 مستأجرين","مجموعات بيانات ميكروبيولوجية","تحليل البيانات باستخدام Spark SQL","التكامل مع KBase Data Lakehouse"]},"keywords":{"zh":["BERIL 研究观测站","KBase Data Lakehouse","微生物生态学","Delta Lakehouse","Spark SQL","数据 lakehouse","多租户访问","研究平台"],"ja":["BERIL 研究観測所","KBase Data Lakehouse","マイクロビアル生態学","Delta Lakehouse","Spark SQL","データ lakehouse","マルチテナントアクセス","研究プラットフォーム"],"ko":["BERIL 연구 관측소","KBase Data Lakehouse","미생물 생태학","Delta Lakehouse","Spark SQL","데이터 레이크하우스","멀티 테넌트 접근","연구 플랫폼"],"es":["ecología microbiana","lago de datos KBase","BERDL","Delta Lakehouse","Spark SQL","análisis de datos","investigación científica","ciencia de datos","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["écologie microbienne","lac de données KBase","BERDL","Delta Lakehouse","Spark SQL","analyse de données","recherche scientifique","science des données","développement de logiciels"],"de":["mikrobielle Ökologie","KBase-Datensee","BERDL","Delta-Datensee","Spark SQL","Datenanalyse","wissenschaftliche Forschung","Datenwissenschaft","Softwareentwicklung"],"pt":["BERIL","KBase Data Lakehouse","ecologia microbiana","plataforma de dados","análise de dados","mikrobiologia","Spark SQL","lakehouse"],"ru":["BERIL","KBase Data Lakehouse","микробная экология","платформа данных","анализ данных","микробиология","Spark SQL","lakehouse"],"ar":["BERIL","KBase Data Lakehouse","علم البيئة الميكروبية","منصة بيانات","تحليل البيانات","ميكروبيولوجيا","Spark SQL","بحيرة البيانات"]}},"owner":"kbaseincubator","repo":"BERIL-research-observatory","repoPath":"kbaseincubator/BERIL-research-observatory","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.411Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"berdl_start","description":"Get started with the BERIL Research Observatory. Use when a user is new, wants orientation, or asks what they can do.","bodyPreview":"# BERIL Research Observatory - Onboarding\n\nWelcome the user and orient them to the system, then route them to the right context based on their goal.\n\n## Phase 1: System Overview\n\nPresent this information directly (no file reads needed):\n\n### What is BERDL?\n\nThe **KBase BER Data Lakehouse (BERDL)** is an on-prem Delta Lakehouse (Spark SQL) hosting **35 databases across 9 tenants**. Key collections:\n\n| Collection | Scale | What it contains |\n|------------|-------|------------------|\n| `kbase_ke_pa","body":"# BERIL Research Observatory - Onboarding\n\nWelcome the user and orient them to the system, then route them to the right context based on their goal.\n\n## Phase 1: System Overview\n\nPresent this information directly (no file reads needed):\n\n### What is BERDL?\n\nThe **KBase BER Data Lakehouse (BERDL)** is an on-prem Delta Lakehouse (Spark SQL) hosting **35 databases across 9 tenants**. Key collections:\n\n| Collection | Scale | What it contains |\n|------------|-------|------------------|\n| `kbase_ke_pangenome` | 293K genomes, 1B genes, 27K species | Species-level pangenomes from GTDB r214: gene clusters, ANI, functional annotations (eggNOG), pathway predictions (GapMind), environmental embeddings (AlphaEarth) |\n| `kbase_genomes` | 293K genomes, 253M proteins | Structural genomics (contigs, features, protein sequences) in CDM format |\n| `kbase_msd_biochemistry` | 56K reactions, 46K molecules | ModelSEED biochemical reactions and compounds for metabolic modeling |\n| `kescience_fitnessbrowser` | 48 organisms, 27M fitness scores | Genome-wide mutant fitness from RB-TnSeq experiments |\n| `enigma_coral` | 3K taxa, 7K genomes | ENIGMA SFA environmental microbiology |\n| `nmdc_arkin` | 48 studies, 3M+ metabolomics | NMDC multi-omics (annotations, embeddings, metabolomics, proteomics) |\n| PhageFoundry (5 DBs) | Various | Species-specific genome browsers for phage-host research |\n| `planetmicrobe_planetmicrobe` | 2K samples, 6K experiments | Marine microbial ecology |\n\n### Repo Structure\n\n```\nprojects/           # Science projects (each has README.md + notebooks/ + data/)\ndocs/               # Shared knowledge base\n  collections.md    # Full database inventory\n  schemas/          # Per-collection schema docs\n  pitfalls.md       # SQL gotchas, data sparsity, common errors\n  performance.md    # Query strategies for large tables\n  research_ideas.md # Future research directions\n  overview.md       # Scientific context and data generation workflow\n  discoveries.md    # Running log of insights\n.claude/skills/     # Agent skills\ndata/               # Shared data extracts reusable across projects\n```\n\n### Available Skills\n\n| Skill | What it does |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `/berdl` | Query BERDL databases via REST API or Spark SQL |\n| `/berdl-query` | Run SQL queries locally with remote Spark compute (CLI tools + notebook support) |\n| `/berdl-minio` | Transfer files between BERDL MinIO and local machine |\n| `/berdl-discover` | Explore and document a new BERDL database |\n| `/literature-review` | Search PubMed, bioRxiv, arXiv, Semantic Scholar, and Google Scholar for relevant biological literature |\n| `/synthesize` | Read analysis outputs, compare against literature, and draft findings |\n| `/submit` | Submit a project for automated review |\n| `/cts` | Run batch compute jobs on the CTS cluster |\n\n> **Note**: Hypothesis generation, research planning, and notebook creation are handled automatically as part of the research workflow (Path 1 below). You don''t need to invoke them separately.\n\n### Existing Projects\n\nDiscover projects dynamically — run `ls projects/` to list them. Read the first line of each `projects/*/README.md` to get titles. Present the list to the user so they can see what''s been done.\n\n### How Projects Work\n\nEach project lives in `projects/<name>/` with a three-file structure plus supporting directories:\n\n```\nprojects/<name>/\n├── README.md            — Project overview, reproduction, authors\n├── RESEARCH_PLAN.md     — Hypothesis, approach, query strategy, revision history\n├── REPORT.md            — Findings, interpretation, supporting evidence\n├── REVIEW.md            — Automated review (generated by /submit)\n├── notebooks/           — Analysis notebooks with saved outputs\n├── data/                — Extracted/processed data\n├── figures/             — Key visualizations\n└── requirements.txt     — Python dependencies\n```\n\n**Reproducibility is required**: notebooks must be committed with outputs, figures must be saved to `figures/`, and README must include a `## Reproduction` section. See PROJECT.md for full standards.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1.5: Environment Detection\n\nBefore routing the user, run environment detection to ensure prerequisites are met:\n\n**Run the detection script:**\n```bash\npython scripts/detect_berdl_environment.py\n```\n\nThis script automatically:\n1. **Detects location**: Tests connectivity to `spark.berdl.kbase.us:443` to determine if you''re on-cluster (BERDL JupyterHub) or off-cluster (local machine)\n2. **On-cluster path**:\n   - Automatically retrieves `KBASE_AUTH_TOKEN` from the environment and saves it to `.env`\n   - Confirms direct access works (no proxy needed)\n   - Reports ready status\n3. **Off-cluster path**:\n   - Checks `.env` for `KBASE_AUTH_TOKEN`\n   - Checks `.venv-berdl` exists\n   - Checks SSH tunnels on ports 1337 and 1338\n   - Checks pproxy on port 8123\n   - Provides specific next steps for anything missing\n\n**Present the output to the user** and help them resolve any issues before proceeding to Phase 2.\n\n**Common resolutions:**\n- **Missing .venv-berdl**: `bash scripts/bootstrap_client.sh`\n- **Missing KBASE_AUTH_TOKEN**: Get token from https://narrative.kbase.us/#auth2/account and add to `.env`\n- **Off-cluster without proxy**: User must start SSH tunnels (requires credentials). See `.claude/skills/berdl-query/references/proxy-setup.md` for full guide. Claude can start pproxy once tunnels are up.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Interactive Routing\n\nAsk the user which of these they want to do:\n\n1. **Start a new research project**\n2. **Explore BERDL data**\n3. **Review published literature**\n4. **Continue an existing project**\n5. **Understand the system**\n\nThen follow the appropriate path below.\n\n---\n\n### Path 1: Start a New Research Project (Orchestrated Workflow)\n\nWhen the user wants to start a new research project, the agent drives the entire process — from ideation through review — checking in with the user at natural decision points rather than requiring manual skill invocations.\n\n#### Phase A: Orientation & Ideation\n\n**Required reading before anything else:**\n1. Read `PROJECT.md` — understand dual goals (science + knowledge capture), project structure requirements, reproducibility standards, JupyterHub workflow, Spark notebook patterns\n2. Read `docs/overview.md` — understand the data architecture, key tables, data generation workflow, known limitations\n3. Read `docs/collections.md` — full database inventory (35 databases, 9 tenants), what data is actually available\n4. Read `docs/pitfalls.md` and `docs/performance.md` — **critical: read these before designing any queries or analysis**\n5. Read `docs/research_ideas.md` — check for existing ideas, avoid duplicating work\n\n**Additional setup (Phase 1.5 should have already checked KBASE_AUTH_TOKEN and proxy):**\n6. Check `gh auth status` — needed for creating branches, PRs, and pushing code. If not authenticated, prompt the user to run `gh auth login`\n7. Note the user''s ORCID and affiliation for the Authors section — ask once, remember for future projects\n\n**Then engage with the user:**\n9. Chat with the user about their research interest\n10. Explore BERDL data (use `/berdl` queries) to check data availability, row counts, column types\n11. Check existing projects (`ls projects/`) — read READMEs of related projects to understand what''s been done\n12. Develop 2-3 testable hypotheses with H0/H1\n13. Search literature (use `/literature-review` internally) for context\n\n#### Phase B: Research Plan\n\n14. Write `RESEARCH_PLAN.md` with: Research Question, Hypothesis, Literature Context, Approach, Data Sources, Query Strategy, Analysis Plan, Expected Outcomes, Revision History (v1)\n15. Write slim `README.md` with: Title, Research Question, Status (In Progress), Overview, Quick Links, Reproduction placeholder, Authors\n16. Create project directory structure: `notebooks/`, `data/`, `figures/`\n17. **Ask user**: \"Here''s the research plan. Should I create a new branch and check in before starting the analysis?\"\n18. If yes: create branch `projects/{project_id}`, commit README + RESEARCH_PLAN\n\n#### Phase C: Analysis (Notebooks)\n\n19. Write numbered notebooks (`01_data_exploration.ipynb`, `02_analysis.ipynb`, etc.) following the analysis plan\n20. Notebooks are the primary audit trail — do as much work as possible in notebooks so humans can inspect intermediate results\n21. When parallel execution or complex pipelines are needed, write scripts in `src/` but call them from notebooks\n22. **Run notebooks** — execute cells, inspect outputs, iterate\n23. As new information emerges, update `RESEARCH_PLAN.md` with a revision tag: `- **v2** ({date}): {what changed and why}`\n24. **Check in code frequently** — commit after each major milestone (plan written, notebooks created, data extracted, analysis complete)\n25. Re-read `docs/pitfalls.md` when something doesn''t work as expected\n\n#### Phase D: Synthesis & Writeup\n\n26. Chat with the user about results — discuss interpretation, identify gaps, add analysis for clarity\n27. Run `/synthesize` to create `REPORT.md` with findings, interpretation, supporting evidence\n28. Commit the report\n29. Chat with user about the report — revise if needed\n\n#### Phase E: Review & Submission\n\n30. Run `/submit` to validate documentation and generate `REVIEW.md`\n31. Fix any issues flagged by the review\n32. Commit fixes\n33. Chat with user about next steps\n\n#### Throughout the Entire Workflow:\n- **Check in code often** — don''t let work accumulate uncommitted\n- **Update `docs/discoveries.md`** when you find something interesting (tag with `[project_id]`)\n- **Update `docs/pitfalls.md`** when you hit a gotcha (follow pitfall-capture protocol from `.claude/skills/pitfall-capture/SKILL.md`)\n- **Update `docs/performance.md`** when you learn a query optimization\n- **Re-read `docs/pitfalls.md`** when debugging failures — the answer may already be documented\n- **Re-read `docs/performance.md`** when queries are slow — check for existing optimization patterns\n- **Follow `PROJECT.md` standards** — notebooks with saved outputs, figures as standalone PNGs, requirements.txt, Reproduction section in README\n\n### Path 2: Explore BERDL Data\n\nRead these files:\n- `docs/collections.md` — full database inventory\n- `docs/pitfalls.md` — critical gotchas before querying\n\nThen:\n- Summarize what databases are available and their scale\n- Highlight cross-collection relationships (pangenome <-> genomes <-> biochemistry <-> fitness)\n- Suggest using `/berdl` to start querying\n- Suggest using `/berdl-discover` if they want to explore a database not yet documented in `docs/schemas/`\n- Warn about the key pitfalls (see Critical Pitfalls below)\n\n### Path 3: Review Published Literature\n\nSuggest using `/literature-review` to search biological databases. This is useful for:\n- Checking what''s already known about an organism or pathway before querying BERDL\n- Finding published pangenome analyses to compare against BERDL data\n- Supporting a hypothesis with existing citations\n- Discovering methods and approaches used in similar studies\n\n**MCP setup check**: The `paper-search-mcp` ([openags/paper-search-mcp](https://github.com/openags/paper-search-mcp)) is configured in `.mcp.json`. It runs via `uvx paper-search-mcp`. If it''s not working:\n1. Ensure Python 3.10+ and [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) are installed\n2. Test: `uvx --from paper-search-mcp python -m paper_search_mcp.server`\n3. Optionally set `SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR_API_KEY` in your environment for enhanced Semantic Scholar features\n4. The skill falls back to WebSearch if the MCP server is unavailable\n\n### Path 4: Continue an Existing Project\n\nSteps:\n1. Run `ls projects/` and list all projects for the user to choose from\n2. Read the chosen project''s `README.md`\n3. Check if a `REVIEW.md` exists in that project directory (read it if so)\n4. Summarize where the project stands: what''s done, what''s next\n5. Suggest using `/submit` when the project is ready for review\n\n### Path 5: Understand the System\n\nRead these files:\n- `PROJECT.md` — high-level goals and structure\n- `docs/collections.md` — database inventory\n- `docs/overview.md` — scientific context and data workflow\n\nThen:\n- Walk through the dual goals (science + knowledge capture)\n- Explain the documentation workflow (tag discoveries, update pitfalls)\n- Mention the UI can be browsed at the BERDL JupyterHub\n- List the available skills and what each does\n- Point to `docs/research_ideas.md` for future directions\n\n---\n\n## Key Principles (for the agent)\n\n1. **Read the docs first** — `PROJECT.md`, `docs/overview.md`, `docs/collections.md`, `docs/pitfalls.md`, and `docs/performance.md` before designing anything. Check existing `projects/` to avoid duplicating work.\n2. **Notebooks are the audit trail** — numbered sequentially (01, 02, 03...), each self-contained with a clear purpose. Commit with saved outputs per `PROJECT.md` reproducibility standards.\n3. **Commit early and often** — after plan, after notebooks, after data extraction, after analysis, after synthesis.\n4. **Ask before branching** — always ask the user before creating a new branch.\n5. **Update the plan** — when the analysis reveals something that changes the approach, update RESEARCH_PLAN.md with a dated revision tag explaining what changed and why.\n6. **Don''t stop and wait** — drive the process forward, checking in with the user at decision points rather than stopping after each step.\n7. **Document as you go** — discoveries go in `docs/discoveries.md`, pitfalls in `docs/pitfalls.md`, performance tips in `docs/performance.md` — captured in real-time, tagged with `[project_id]`.\n8. **Use Spark patterns from PROJECT.md** — `get_spark_session()`, PySpark-first, `.toPandas()` only for final small results.\n\n---\n\n## Critical Pitfalls (always mention)\n\nRegardless of path chosen, surface these early:\n\n1. **Species IDs contain `--`** — This is fine inside quoted strings in SQL. Use exact equality (`WHERE id = ''s__Escherichia_coli--RS_GCF_000005845.2''`), not LIKE patterns.\n2. **Large tables need filters** — Never full-scan `gene` (1B rows) or `genome_ani` (420M rows). Always filter by species or genome ID.\n3. **AlphaEarth embeddings cover only 28%** of genomes (83K/293K) — check coverage before relying on them.\n4. **Notebooks can run on JupyterHub or locally** — On JupyterHub, `get_spark_session()` is injected into kernels. Locally, use `from get_spark_session import get_spark_session` with the `.venv-berdl` environment and proxy chain running. See `.claude/skills/berdl-query/SKILL.md` for local setup.\n5. **Auth token** — stored in `.env` as `KBASE_AUTH_TOKEN` (not `KB_AUTH_TOKEN`).\n6. **String-typed numeric columns** — Many databases store numbers as strings. Always CAST before comparisons.\n7. **Gene clusters are species-specific** — Cannot compare cluster IDs across species. Use COG/KEGG/PFAM for cross-species comparisons.\n8. **Avoid unnecessary `.toPandas()`** — `.toPandas()` pulls all data to the driver node and can be very slow or cause OOM errors. Use PySpark DataFrame operations for filtering, joins, and aggregations. Only convert to pandas for final small results (plotting, CSV export).\n\n---\n\n## Templates\n\n### RESEARCH_PLAN.md\n\n```markdown\n# Research Plan: {Title}\n\n## Research Question\n{Refined question after literature review}\n\n## Hypothesis\n- **H0**: {Null hypothesis}\n- **H1**: {Alternative hypothesis}\n\n## Literature Context\n{Summary of what''s known, key references, identified gaps}\n\n## Query Strategy\n\n### Tables Required\n| Table | Purpose | Estimated Rows | Filter Strategy |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| {table} | {why needed} | {count} | {how to filter} |\n\n### Key Queries\n1. **{Description}**:\n\\```sql\n{query}\n\\```\n\n### Performance Plan\n- **Tier**: {REST API / JupyterHub}\n- **Estimated complexity**: {simple / moderate / complex}\n- **Known pitfalls**: {list from pitfalls.md}\n\n## Analysis Plan\n\n### Notebook 1: Data Exploration\n- **Goal**: {what to verify/explore}\n- **Expected output**: {CSV/figures}\n\n### Notebook 2: Main Analysis\n- **Goal**: {core analysis}\n- **Expected output**: {CSV/figures}\n\n### Notebook 3: Visualization (if needed)\n- **Goal**: {figures for findings}\n\n## Expected Outcomes\n- **If H1 supported**: {interpretation}\n- **If H0 not rejected**: {interpretation}\n- **Potential confounders**: {list}\n\n## Revision History\n- **v1** ({date}): Initial plan\n\n## Authors\n{ORCID, affiliation}\n```\n\n### README.md\n\n```markdown\n# {Title}\n\n## Research Question\n{Refined question}\n\n## Status\nIn Progress — research plan created, awaiting analysis.\n\n## Overview\n{One-paragraph summary of the hypothesis and approach}\n\n## Quick Links\n- [Research Plan](RESEARCH_PLAN.md) — hypothesis, approach, query strategy\n- [Report](REPORT.md) — findings, interpretation, supporting evidence\n\n## Reproduction\n*TBD — add prerequisites and step-by-step instructions after analysis is complete.*\n\n## Authors\n{Authors}\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:45:07.468Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Analysis Agents needing advanced microbial ecology insights with the KBase Data Lakehouse","zh":"适用于需要高级微生物生态学见解的KBase Data Lakehouse数据分析代理","ja":"KBase Data Lakehouseの高度な微生物生態学の洞察が必要なデータ分析エージェントに最適","ko":"고급 미생물 생태학 정보가 필요한 KBase Data Lakehouse 데이터 분석 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de análisis de datos que necesitan conocimientos avanzados de ecología microbiana con el lago de datos KBase","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de données ayant besoin d''informations avancées sur l''écologie microbienne avec le lac de données KBase","de":"Perfekt für Data-Analytics-Agents, die erweiterte Einblicke in die mikrobielle Ökologie mit dem KBase Data Lakehouse benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Dados que necessitam de insights avançados em ecologia microbiana com o KBase Data Lakehouse","ru":"Идеально для агентов анализа данных, которым необходимы углубленные сведения по микробной экологии с помощью KBase Data Lakehouse","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المحللين للبيانات الذين يحتاجون إلى رؤى متقدمة في علم البيئة الدقيقة مع مخزن البيانات KBase"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to explore microbial ecology with the KBase BER Data Lakehouse, leveraging Spark SQL and 35 databases across 9 tenants, including key collections like `kbase_ke_pa`","zh":"赋予代理探索微生物生态学的能力，利用KBase BER Data Lakehouse、Spark SQL和35个数据库跨9个租户，包括关键集合如`kbase_ke_pa`","ja":"KBase BER Data Lakehouse、Spark SQL、9つのテナント跨ぐ35のデータベースを利用して、エージェントが微生物生態学を探索できるようにする。重要なコレクションとして`kbase_ke_pa`が含まれる","ko":"KBase BER Data Lakehouse, Spark SQL 및 9개의 테넌트에 걸친 35개의 데이터베이스를 활용하여 에이전트가 미생물 생태학을 탐색할 수 있도록 함. 주요 컬렉션으로 `kbase_ke_pa`가 포함됨","es":"Habilita a los agentes a explorar la ecología microbiana con el lago de datos KBase BER, aprovechando Spark SQL y 35 bases de datos en 9 inquilinos, incluyendo colecciones clave como `kbase_ke_pa`","fr":"Permet aux agents d''explorer l''écologie microbienne avec le lac de données KBase BER, en exploitant Spark SQL et 35 bases de données sur 9 locataires, notamment des collections clés comme `kbase_ke_pa`","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, die mikrobielle Ökologie mit dem KBase BER Data Lakehouse zu erkunden, indem sie Spark SQL und 35 Datenbanken über 9 Mandanten nutzen, einschließlich wichtiger Sammlungen wie `kbase_ke_pa`","pt":"Habilita os agentes a explorar a ecologia microbiana com o KBase BER Data Lakehouse, utilizando Spark SQL e 35 bancos de dados em 9 locatários, incluindo coleções-chave como `kbase_ke_pa`","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью изучать микробную экологию с помощью KBase BER Data Lakehouse, используя Spark SQL и 35 баз данных в 9 арендаторах, включая ключевые коллекции, такие как `kbase_ke_pa`","ar":"يتمكّن الوكلاء من استكشاف علم البيئة الدقيقة باستخدام مخزن البيانات KBase BER، مستخدمين Spark SQL و35 قاعدة بيانات عبر 9 مستأجرين، بما في ذلك المجموعات الرئيسية مثل `kbase_ke_pa`"},"useCases":{"en":["Onboarding users to the BERIL Research Observatory","Routing users to the right context based on their goals","Presenting system overviews of the KBase BER Data Lakehouse"],"zh":["将用户引导至BERIL Research Observatory的入门过程","根据用户目标将用户引导至正确的上下文","呈现KBase BER Data Lakehouse的系统概览"],"ja":["BERIL Research Observatoryへのユーザーオンボーディング","ユーザーの目標に基づいてユーザーを正しいコンテキストにルーティングする","KBase BER Data Lakehouseのシステムの概要を提示する"],"ko":["BERIL Research Observatory에 대한 사용자 온보딩","사용자의 목표에 따라 사용자를 올바른 컨텍스트로 라우팅","KBase BER Data Lakehouse의 시스템 개요를 제공"],"es":["Incorporación de usuarios al Observatorio de Investigación BERIL","Enrutamiento de usuarios al contexto adecuado en función de sus objetivos","Presentación de descripciones generales del lago de datos KBase BER"],"fr":["Intégration des utilisateurs à l''Observatoire de Recherche BERIL","Acheminement des utilisateurs vers le contexte approprié en fonction de leurs objectifs","Présentation des descriptions générales du lac de données KBase BER"],"de":["Onboarding von Benutzern in das BERIL-Forschungsobservatorium","Weiterleitung von Benutzern an den richtigen Kontext basierend auf ihren Zielen","Präsentation von Systemübersichten des KBase BER Data Lakehouse"],"pt":["Integração de usuários ao Observatório de Pesquisa BERIL","Encaminhamento de usuários para o contexto correto com base em seus objetivos","Apresentação de visões gerais do sistema do KBase BER Data Lakehouse"],"ru":["Ввод пользователей в обсерваторию BERIL","Направление пользователей в правильный контекст на основе их целей","Представление обзоров системы KBase BER Data Lakehouse"],"ar":["تنسيق المستخدمين مع مرصد BERIL البحثي","توجيه المستخدمين إلى السياق الصحيح بناءً على أهدافهم","عرض نظرة عامة على نظام مخزن البيانات KBase BER"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to the KBase Data Lakehouse","Limited to on-prem Delta Lakehouse (Spark SQL)"],"zh":["需要访问KBase Data Lakehouse","仅限本地Delta Lakehouse（Spark SQL）"],"ja":["KBase Data Lakehouseへのアクセスが必要","オンプレミスのDelta Lakehouse（Spark SQL）のみ"],"ko":["KBase Data Lakehouse에 대한 액세스가 필요","온프레미스 Delta Lakehouse(Spark SQL)만 해당"],"es":["Requiere acceso al lago de datos KBase","Limitado a Delta Lakehouse local (Spark SQL)"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au lac de données KBase","Limité au lac de données Delta local (Spark SQL)"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf das KBase Data Lakehouse","Begrenzt auf lokales Delta Lakehouse (Spark SQL)"],"pt":["Exige acesso ao KBase Data Lakehouse","Limitado ao Delta Lakehouse local (Spark SQL)"],"ru":["Требует доступа к KBase Data Lakehouse","Ограничен локальным Delta Lakehouse (Spark SQL)"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى مخزن البيانات KBase","محدود بمخزن Delta المحلي (Spark SQL)"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
