qualité du logiciel","de":"Die Code-Überprüfung ist ein entscheidender Prozess, um die Qualität der Software zu gewährleisten","pt":"Revisão de código é um processo que ajuda a garantir a qualidade do código-fonte, seguindo padrões e melhores práticas","ru":"Обзор кода - это процесс, который помогает обеспечить качество исходного кода, следуя стандартам и лучшим практикам","ar":"مراجعة الكود هي عملية تساعد على ضمان جودة الكود المصدري باتباع المعايير وأفضل الممارسات","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["确定代码审查范围","检查代码质量和可维护性","提供专业代码审查反馈","确保代码符合编码标准","提高代码可读性和可维护性"],"ja":["コードレビューの範囲を決定する","コードの品質とメンテナンス性をチェックする","プロフェッショナルなコードレビューのフィードバックを提供する","コードがコーディング規約に準拠していることを確認する","コードの可読性とメンテナンス性を向上させる"],"ko":["코드 리뷰 범위를 결정한다","코드의 품질과 유지 보수성을 확인한다","전문가 코드 리뷰의 피드백을 제공한다","코드가 코드 표준에 부합하는지 확인한다","코드의 가독성과 유지 보수성을 향상시킨다"],"es":["Identificar el alcance del código que necesita revisión","Verificar los cambios con git status y git diff","Revisar los commits desde la última revisión","Detectar errores y mejoras en el código","Realizar una revisión de código profesional"],"fr":["Identifier la portée du code à réviser","Vérifier les modifications avec git status et git diff","Réviser les commits depuis la dernière révision","Détecter les erreurs et les améliorations dans le code","Effectuer une révision de code professionnelle"],"de":["Den Umfang des zu überprüfenden Codes identifizieren","Die Änderungen mit git status und git diff überprüfen","Die Commits seit der letzten Überprüfung überprüfen","Fehler und Verbesserungsmöglichkeiten im Code erkennen","Eine professionelle Code-Überprüfung durchführen"],"pt":["Identificação do escopo da revisão","Análise do código-fonte","Verificação da conformidade com os padrões","Melhoria da qualidade do código","Redução de erros e bugs"],"ru":["Определение объема обзора","Анализ исходного кода","Проверка соответствия стандартам","Улучшение качества кода","Снижение ошибок и багов"],"ar":["تحديد نطاق المراجعة","تحليل الكود المصدري","التحقق من الامتثال للمعايير","تحسين جودة الكود","تقليل الأخطاء والعيوب"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码审查","代码质量","代码可维护性","编码标准","代码审查流程","代码审查工具"],"ja":["コードレビュー","コード品質","コードメンテナンス性","コーディング規約","コードレビューのプロセス","コードレビューツール"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","코드 품질","코드 유지 보수성","코드 표준","코드 리뷰 프로세스","코드 리뷰 도구"],"es":["revisión de código","calidad del software","desarrollo de software","git status","git diff","revisión de código profesional"],"fr":["révision de code","qualité du logiciel","développement de logiciel","git status","git diff","révision de code professionnelle"],"de":["Code-Überprüfung","Software-Qualität","Software-Entwicklung","git status","git diff","professionelle Code-Überprüfung"],"pt":["revisão de código","qualidade do código","padrões de código","melhoria do código","desenvolvimento de software","equipe de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["обзор кода","качество кода","стандарты кода","улучшение кода","разработка программного обеспечения","команда разработчиков"],"ar":["مراجعة الكود","جودة الكود","معايير الكود","تحسين الكود","تطوير البرمجيات","فريق التطوير"]}},"owner":"MQFacultyOfArts","repo":"PromptGrimoireTool","repoPath":"MQFacultyOfArts/PromptGrimoireTool","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.411Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"code-review","description":"Perform a maximally picky and professional code review of recent changes. Reviews all code added since the last review, checking for thread safety, async safety, security vulnerabilities, data integrity, test quality, and code smells. Use before committing significant changes.","bodyPreview":"# Code Review Skill\n\nPerform a professional code review following the standards in `prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md`.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Before committing significant code changes\n- After completing a spike or feature\n- When the Stop hook reminds you\n- When explicitly requested by user\n\n## Process\n\n1. **Identify scope** - Determine what code needs review:\n   - Check `git status` and `git diff` for uncommitted changes\n   - Check `git log` to find commits since last review\n   - Look for any existing code r","body":"# Code Review Skill\n\nPerform a professional code review following the standards in `prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md`.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Before committing significant code changes\n- After completing a spike or feature\n- When the Stop hook reminds you\n- When explicitly requested by user\n\n## Process\n\n1. **Identify scope** - Determine what code needs review:\n   - Check `git status` and `git diff` for uncommitted changes\n   - Check `git log` to find commits since last review\n   - Look for any existing code review documents to find the last review point\n\n2. **Read the review template** - Load `prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md` for the full criteria\n\n3. **Perform the review** - Apply all criteria from the template:\n   - MANDATORY: No Quick Hacks policy\n   - Race Condition Audit Checklist\n   - Critical issues (thread safety, async safety, security, data integrity)\n   - High priority (type hints, input validation, logging, test coverage)\n   - Medium priority (magic numbers, hard-coded config, duplication)\n   - Test quality (primary use cases tested, no anti-patterns)\n\n4. **Write the review document** - Save to `.claude/plans/` with:\n   - Executive summary\n   - Issues grouped by severity with file:line references\n   - Specific code fixes (before/after)\n   - Checklist of items to fix\n   - Verification steps\n   - Notes for future work\n\n5. **Report the path** - Tell the user where to find the review document\n\n## Key Principles\n\n- Be specific and critical\n- Every issue needs a file:line reference\n- Provide concrete fixes, not just descriptions\n- Consider whether code enables future architectural goals\n- Quick hacks are absolutely forbidden\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:45:10.490Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents requiring rigorous code validation and improvement through git-based code reviews.","zh":"适用于需要通过基于 Git 的代码审查进行严格代码验证和改进的开发代理。","ja":"Git ベースのコードレビューを通じて厳格なコード検証と改善が必要な開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Git 기반 코드 리뷰를 통해 엄격한 코드 검증 및 개선이 필요한 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Desarrollo que requieren una validación de código rigurosa y mejora a través de revisiones de código basadas en git.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents de Développement nécessitant une validation de code rigoureuse et une amélioration via des revues de code basées sur git.","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungs-Agents, die eine rigorose Code-Validierung und Verbesserung durch git-basierte Code-Reviews benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que exigem uma validação rigorosa de código e melhoria por meio de revisões de código baseadas em git.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, требующих тщательной проверки и улучшения кода посредством git-ревизий кода.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء النموزجيون الذين يتطلبون التحقق الدقيق من صحة الشفرة وتحسينها من خلال مراجعات الشفرة المعتمدة على جيت."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to scrutinize code changes using git status, git diff, and git log, ensuring adherence to standards outlined in prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md, thereby enhancing code quality and reliability.","zh":"赋予代理人使用 git 状态、git 差异和 git 日志来审查代码更改的能力，确保遵守 prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md 中概述的标准，从而提高代码质量和可靠性。","ja":"Git 状態、Git 差分、Git ログを使用してコード変更を検証する機能をエージェントに与え、prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md に概説された基準に従ってコードの品質と信頼性を高めます。","ko":"에이전트가 Git 상태, Git 차이, Git 로그를 사용하여 코드 변경을 검토할 수 있는 기능을 제공하여 prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md에 정의된 기준을 준수하여 코드 품질과 신뢰성을 향상합니다.","es":"Empodera a los agentes para escudriñar los cambios de código usando git status, git diff y git log, asegurando el cumplimiento de los estándares descritos en prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md, mejorando así la calidad y fiabilidad del código.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''examiner les modifications de code à l''aide de git status, git diff et git log, en veillant au respect des normes décrites dans prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md, améliorant ainsi la qualité et la fiabilité du code.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Code-Änderungen mit git status, git diff und git log zu prüfen, um die Einhaltung der in prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md festgelegten Standards zu gewährleisten und so die Code-Qualität und Zuverlässigkeit zu verbessern.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a examinar alterações de código usando git status, git diff e git log, garantindo a adesão aos padrões descritos em prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md, melhorando assim a qualidade e confiabilidade do código.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проверять изменения кода с помощью git status, git diff и git log, обеспечивая соблюдение стандартов, изложенных в prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md, тем самым повышая качество и надежность кода.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على فحص تغييرات الشفرة باستخدام git status و git diff و git log، مما يضمن الامتثال للمعايير المحددة في prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md، وبالتالي تعزيز جودة الشفرة وموثوقيتها."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating pre-commit code checks","Validating feature implementations post-completion","Debugging code discrepancies through thorough review"],"zh":["自动执行提交前代码检查","完成后验证功能实现","通过彻底审查调试代码差异"],"ja":["コミット前のコードチェックを自動化する","機能の実装を完了後に検証する","徹底的なレビューを通じてコードの差異をデバッグする"],"ko":["提交 전 코드 검사 자동화","기능 구현 완료 후 검증","코드 불일치를 철저하게 검토하여 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización de comprobaciones de código pre-commit","Validación de implementaciones de características tras su finalización","Depuración de discrepancias de código mediante una revisión exhaustiva"],"fr":["Automatisation des vérifications de code pré-commit","Validation des implémentations de fonctionnalités après leur achèvement","Débogage des écarts de code par un examen approfondi"],"de":["Automatisierung von Pre-Commit-Code-Prüfungen","Validierung von Feature-Implementierungen nach deren Abschluss","Debugging von Code-Diskrepanzen durch gründliche Überprüfung"],"pt":["Automatizar verificações de código pré-envio","Validar implementações de recursos após conclusão","Depurar discrepâncias de código por meio de revisão minuciosa"],"ru":["Автоматизировать проверки кода до фиксации","Проверять реализацию функций после завершения","Отлаживать несоответствия кода посредством тщательного обзора"],"ar":["تأتمتة التحقق من الشفرة قبل الإرسال"," التحقق من تنفيذ الميزات بعد الانتهاء","تصحيح الشفرة من خلال المراجعة الشاملة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to git repository","Must follow standards in prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md"],"zh":["需要访问 Git 仓库","必须遵循 prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md 中的标准"],"ja":["Git リポジトリへのアクセスが必要","prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md に記載された基準に従う必要がある"],"ko":["Git 저장소에 대한 액세스가 필요함","prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md에 정의된 기준을 따라야 함"],"es":["Requiere acceso al repositorio git","Debe seguir los estándares en prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au dépôt git","Doit suivre les normes dans prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf das Git-Repository","Muss den Standards in prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md folgen"],"pt":["Exige acesso ao repositório git","Deve seguir os padrões em prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md"],"ru":["Требует доступа к репозиторию git","Должно следовать стандартам, изложенным в prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى مستودع جيت","يجب اتباع المعايير المحددة في prompts/CODE_REVIEW.md"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('H2OSLabs/SynnovatorZero/api-builder', 'community', 'H2OSLabs', 'SynnovatorZero', 'H2OSLabs/SynnovatorZero', 'api-builder', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.411Z', '2026-02-18T03:45:36.199Z', NULL, '{"id":"H2OSLabs/SynnovatorZero/api-builder","name":"api-builder","description":{"zh":"API Builder 是一个从 OpenAPI 3.x 规范自动生成完整的 FastAPI 后端脚手架的工具，支持数据库模型、API 路由、测试和 Next.js 客户端","ja":"API Builder は、OpenAPI 3.x 仕様から完全な FastAPI バックエンドのスケルトンを自動生成するツールです。データベースモデル、API ルーティング、テスト、Next.js クライアントをサポートしています","ko":"API Builder는 OpenAPI 3.x 사양에서 완전한 FastAPI 백엔드 스켈레톤을 자동 생성하는 도구입니다. 데이터베이스 모델, API 라우팅, 테스트 및 Next.js 클라이언트를 지원합니다","es":"El constructor de API genera backends FastAPI completos desde la especificación OpenAPI 3.x, incluyendo modelos de base de datos, rutas de API y tests.","fr":"Le constructeur d''API génère des backends FastAPI complets à partir de la spécification OpenAPI 3.x, y compris des modèles de base de données, des routes d''API et des tests.","de":"Der API-Builder generiert vollständige FastAPI-Backends aus der OpenAPI 3.x-Spezifikation, einschließlich Datenbankmodellen, API-Routen und Tests.","en":"Synnovator Rebuild from Scratch"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"API Builder：从 OpenAPI 3.x 自动生成 FastAPI 后端","ja":"API Builder: OpenAPI 3.x から FastAPI バックエンドを自動生成","ko":"API Builder: OpenAPI 3.x 에서 FastAPI 백엔드 자동 생성","es":"Constructor de API: Genera backends FastAPI con OpenAPI 3.x","fr":"Constructeur d''API : Générez des backends FastAPI avec Op...","de":"API-Builder: Erstellen Sie FastAPI-Backends mit OpenAPI 3.x","en":"api-builder"},"description":{"zh":"API Builder 是一个从 OpenAPI 3.x 规范自动生成完整的 FastAPI 后端脚手架的工具，支持数据库模型、API 路由、测试和 Next.js 客户端","ja":"API Builder は、OpenAPI 3.x 仕様から完全な FastAPI バックエンドのスケルトンを自動生成するツールです。データベースモデル、API ルーティング、テスト、Next.js クライアントをサポートしています","ko":"API Builder는 OpenAPI 3.x 사양에서 완전한 FastAPI 백엔드 스켈레톤을 자동 생성하는 도구입니다. 데이터베이스 모델, API 라우팅, 테스트 및 Next.js 클라이언트를 지원합니다","es":"El constructor de API genera backends FastAPI completos desde la especificación OpenAPI 3.x, incluyendo modelos de base de datos, rutas de API y tests.","fr":"Le constructeur d''API génère des backends FastAPI complets à partir de la spécification OpenAPI 3.x, y compris des modèles de base de données, des routes d''A...","de":"Der API-Builder generiert vollständige FastAPI-Backends aus der OpenAPI 3.x-Spezifikation, einschließlich Datenbankmodellen, API-Routen und Tests.","en":"Synnovator Rebuild from Scratch"},"definition":{"en":"Synnovator Rebuild from Scratch"},"features":{"zh":["从 OpenAPI 3.x 规范自动生成 FastAPI 后端代码","支持数据库模型、API 路由、测试和 Next.js 客户端","自动验证 OpenAPI 3.x 规范格式","支持自定义生成范围"],"ja":["OpenAPI 3.x 仕様から FastAPI バックエンドのコードを自動生成","データベースモデル、API ルーティング、テスト、Next.js クライアントをサポート","OpenAPI 3.x 仕様のフォーマットを自動で検証","生成範囲のカスタマイズをサポート"],"ko":["OpenAPI 3.x 사양에서 FastAPI 백엔드 코드를 자동 생성","데이터베이스 모델, API 라우팅, 테스트 및 Next.js 클라이언트를 지원","OpenAPI 3.x 사양의 형식을 자동으로 검증","생성 범위의 사용자 지정 지원"],"es":["Generación automática de backends FastAPI","Soporte para OpenAPI 3.x","Inclusión de modelos de base de datos y rutas de API","Generación de tests para el backend","Integración con Next.js"],"fr":["Génération automatique de backends FastAPI","Prise en charge d''OpenAPI 3.x","Inclusion de modèles de base de données et de routes d''API","Génération de tests pour le backend","Intégration avec Next.js"],"de":["Automatische Erstellung von FastAPI-Backends","Unterstützung für OpenAPI 3.x","Einbeziehung von Datenbankmodellen und API-Routen","Erstellung von Tests für das Backend","Integration mit Next.js"]},"keywords":{"zh":["API Builder","OpenAPI 3.x","FastAPI","后端代码生成","自动化工具","数据库模型","API 路由","测试","Next.js 客户端"],"ja":["API Builder","OpenAPI 3.x","FastAPI","バックエンドコード生成","自動化ツール","データベースモデル","API ルーティング","テスト","Next.js クライアント"],"ko":["API Builder","OpenAPI 3.x","FastAPI","백엔드 코드 생성","자동화 도구","데이터베이스 모델","API 라우팅","테스트","Next.js 클라이언트"],"es":["constructor de API","OpenAPI 3.x","FastAPI","backend","automatización","desarrollo de API","Next.js"],"fr":["constructeur d''API","OpenAPI 3.x","FastAPI","backend","automatisation","développement d''API","Next.js"],"de":["API-Builder","OpenAPI 3.x","FastAPI","Backend","Automatisierung","API-Entwicklung","Next.js"]}},"owner":"H2OSLabs","repo":"SynnovatorZero","repoPath":"H2OSLabs/SynnovatorZero","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.411Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"api-builder","description":"Generate complete FastAPI backend scaffolds from OpenAPI 3.x specifications. Automatically creates SQLAlchemy models, Pydantic schemas, FastAPI routers, CRUD operations, database migrations, pytest tests, and Next.js TypeScript clients. Use when user provides an OpenAPI/OpenSpec file (.yaml/.json) or pastes spec content, and wants to generate API code. Triggers on phrases like generate API from spec, build backend from OpenAPI, create FastAPI from this spec, implement these endpoints, or when user shares OpenAPI specification files. Supports Python 3.12+, FastAPI, SQLite, SQLAlchemy, Alembic, pytest, and Next.js App Router.","bodyPreview":"# API Builder\n\n从 OpenAPI 3.x 规范自动生成完整的 FastAPI 后端脚手架，包括数据库模型、API 路由、测试和 Next.js client。\n\n## 工作流程\n\n### 阶段 1：验证输入\n\n1. **获取 OpenAPI Spec**\n   - 询问用户提供 OpenAPI spec：\n     - 文件路径（.yaml 或 .json）\n     - 粘贴 spec 内容（保存为临时文件）\n     - URL（如果可访问，先下载）\n\n2. **验证 Spec 格式**\n   - 运行 `scripts/validate_spec.py`：\n     ```bash\n     python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/validate_spec.py <spec-file>\n     ```\n   - 检查 exit code：0=成功，1=失败\n\n   **如果验证失败**：停止并告知用户具体错误，询问是否修正\n\n3. **选择生成范围**\n   - 运行 `scripts/parse_openapi.py` 查","body":"# API Builder\n\n从 OpenAPI 3.x 规范自动生成完整的 FastAPI 后端脚手架，包括数据库模型、API 路由、测试和 Next.js client。\n\n## 工作流程\n\n### 阶段 1：验证输入\n\n1. **获取 OpenAPI Spec**\n   - 询问用户提供 OpenAPI spec：\n     - 文件路径（.yaml 或 .json）\n     - 粘贴 spec 内容（保存为临时文件）\n     - URL（如果可访问，先下载）\n\n2. **验证 Spec 格式**\n   - 运行 `scripts/validate_spec.py`：\n     ```bash\n     python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/validate_spec.py <spec-file>\n     ```\n   - 检查 exit code：0=成功，1=失败\n\n   **如果验证失败**：停止并告知用户具体错误，询问是否修正\n\n3. **选择生成范围**\n   - 运行 `scripts/parse_openapi.py` 查看可用 endpoints：\n     ```bash\n     python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/parse_openapi.py <spec-file>\n     ```\n   - 询问用户：\n     - 生成全部 endpoints？\n     - 只生成特定的endpoints？（让用户选择，使用 `--resources` 参数）\n\n### 阶段 2：检测现有项目结构\n\n1. **检查是否为现有项目**\n   - 查找 `app/` 或 `src/` 目录\n   - 检查 `pyproject.toml`\n   - 检查是否已有 `database.py`、`routers/`、`models/` 等\n\n2. **确定集成策略**\n   - **如果是现有项目**：\n     - 复用现有的 `database.py`\n     - 检查文件冲突（如 `app/routers/users.py` 已存在）\n     - 询问用户如何处理冲突：覆盖/合并/重命名/跳过\n   - **如果是新项目**：\n     - 从 `assets/fastapi-template/` 复制基础结构\n     - 创建完整的项目脚手架\n\n### 阶段 3：生成后端代码\n\n**使用 CLI 脚本（推荐）**：\n\n运行完整的生成流程：\n```bash\ncd ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts\npython3 cli.py \\\n  --spec <spec-file> \\\n  --output <output-dir> \\\n  [--resources users,posts]  # 可选：只生成特定资源\n  [--conflict-strategy skip|backup|overwrite]  # 默认: skip\n  [--dry-run]  # 预览模式，不写入文件\n```\n\n**冲突处理策略**：\n- `skip`（默认）：跳过已存在的文件，不覆盖\n- `backup`：备份已存在的文件后覆盖（推荐用于更新）\n- `overwrite`：直接覆盖（危险！）\n\n**预览模式**：使用 `--dry-run` 可以预览将要生成的文件，而不实际写入。\n\n**生成内容**：\n- `models/` - SQLAlchemy 数据库模型\n- `schemas/` - Pydantic API schemas\n- `routers/` - FastAPI 路由\n- `__init__.py` - 包初始化文件\n- `parsed.json` - 解析后的 spec 数据\n\n**关键点**：\n- 脚本自动处理类型映射（参考 `references/type-mapping.md`）\n- 使用 Jinja2 模板（`assets/templates/`）生成代码\n- 生成的代码包含 TODO comments 标记业务逻辑部分\n- 添加时间戳字段（created_at, updated_at）\n- Email 字段自动添加 unique 和 index\n\n**手动步骤执行（高级）**：\n\n如果需要更细粒度控制，可分步执行：\n\n```bash\ncd ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts\n\n# 1. 解析 spec\npython3 parse_openapi.py <spec-file> --output parsed.json\n\n# 2. 生成代码\npython3 generate_code.py \\\n  --parsed-data parsed.json \\\n  --output-dir <output-dir> \\\n  --templates-dir ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/assets/templates\n```\n\n**参考文档**：\n- `references/type-mapping.md` - 类型映射规则\n- `references/fastapi-patterns.md` - FastAPI 最佳实践\n\n#### 3.5 更新 Main.py\n\n如果不存在 `app/main.py`，创建它：\n- 从 `assets/fastapi-template/app/main.py` 复制基础结构\n- 注册所有生成的 routers\n- 配置 CORS 中间件\n- 添加根路由\n\n如果已存在，询问用户是否添加新的 router 注册代码。\n\n#### 3.6 配置和运行数据库迁移（可选）\n\n**使用 CLI（推荐）**：\n\n```bash\n# 自动配置并运行迁移\ncd ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts\npython3 cli.py \\\n  --spec <spec-file> \\\n  --output <output-dir> \\\n  --setup-alembic \\\n  --run-migrations\n```\n\n**手动执行**：\n\n如果用户想手动控制：\n```bash\n# 1. 配置 Alembic\ncd ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts\npython3 cli.py --spec <spec-file> --output <output-dir> --setup-alembic\n\n# 2. 进入项目目录手动运行迁移\ncd <output-dir>\nalembic revision --autogenerate -m \"Initial tables\"\nalembic upgrade head\n```\n\n**生成内容**：\n- `alembic.ini` - Alembic 配置文件\n- `alembic/env.py` - 迁移环境配置\n- `alembic/versions/` - 迁移文件目录\n- `alembic/script.py.mako` - 迁移模板\n\n**何时使用迁移**：\n- 全新项目：使用 `--setup-alembic --run-migrations` 立即创建数据库\n- 已有项目更新schema：手动运行 `alembic revision --autogenerate`\n- 生产环境：先测试迁移，再手动应用\n\n### 阶段 4：生成测试\n\n#### 4.1 更新 conftest.py\n\n- 检查 `tests/conftest.py` 是否存在\n- 如果不存在，从 `assets/fastapi-template/tests/conftest.py` 复制\n- 为每个资源添加 fixtures：\n  - `sample_{resource}_data`\n  - `create_sample_{resource}`\n- 使用 `assets/templates/conftest_fixture.py.j2` 模板\n\n#### 4.2 生成 API 集成测试\n\n- 使用 `assets/templates/test_api.py.j2` 模板\n- 生成到 `tests/test_api/test_{resource}_api.py`\n- 包含测试：\n  - CRUD 操作（create, get, update, delete）\n  - 错误处理（404, 400, 422）\n  - 分页、验证\n\n**参考**：`references/testing-patterns.md`\n\n#### 4.3 生成 CRUD 单元测试\n\n- 使用 `assets/templates/test_crud.py.j2` 模板\n- 生成到 `tests/test_crud/test_{resource}_crud.py`\n\n### 阶段 5：生成 Next.js Client（可选）\n\n询问用户是否需要生成 Next.js TypeScript client。\n\n如果需要：\n\n**使用 CLI（推荐）**：\n\n```bash\ncd ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts\npython3 cli.py \\\n  --spec <spec-file> \\\n  --output <backend-output-dir> \\\n  --generate-client \\\n  [--client-output <frontend-path>/api-client.ts]\n```\n\n**单独生成Client**：\n\n```bash\ncd ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts\npython3 generate_client.py \\\n  --parsed-data parsed.json \\\n  --output <client-output-file>\n```\n\n**生成内容**：\n- TypeScript接口定义（从OpenAPI schemas）\n- API调用方法（从OpenAPI paths）\n- ApiClient类（包含错误处理）\n- 便捷的函数导出\n\n**参考**：`references/type-mapping.md` 的 TypeScript 映射\n\n**生成的client使用示例**：\n```typescript\n// Next.js App Router\nimport { apiClient } from ''@/lib/api/api-client''\n\nexport default async function Page() {\n  const users = await apiClient.list_users()\n  return <div>{users.map(u => <div>{u.name}</div>)}</div>\n}\n```\n\n### 阶段 6：验证和测试\n\n1. **安装依赖**：\n   ```bash\n   uv add fastapi sqlalchemy alembic pydantic[email] python-multipart\n   uv add --dev pytest pytest-cov httpx\n   ```\n\n2. **运行类型检查**：\n   ```bash\n   mypy app/\n   ```\n   如果有错误，修复后重新检查。\n\n3. **运行迁移**：\n   ```bash\n   alembic upgrade head\n   ```\n\n4. **运行测试**：\n   ```bash\n   pytest tests/ -v\n   ```\n   **目标**：所有测试通过\n\n5. **手动验证**：\n   - 启动服务器：`uvicorn app.main:app --reload`\n   - 访问 API 文档：http://localhost:8000/docs\n   - 测试几个 endpoints\n\n### 阶段 7：完成\n\n1. **生成总结文档**：\n   - 列出所有生成的文件\n   - 标记需要用户补充的 TODO 项\n   - 提供下一步指南\n\n2. **TODO 清单**：\n   - [ ] 实现业务逻辑（routers 中的 TODO comments）\n   - [ ] 添加认证/授权\n   - [ ] 配置环境变量（`.env` 文件）\n   - [ ] 补充关系字段（如果有）\n   - [ ] 添加自定义验证逻辑\n\n## 类型映射\n\n详细的 OpenAPI 到 Python/TypeScript 类型映射见：**[references/type-mapping.md](references/type-mapping.md)**\n\n快速参考：\n- `string` → `str` / `string`\n- `integer` → `int` / `number`\n- `string(email)` → `EmailStr` / `string`\n- `string(date-time)` → `datetime` / `string`\n- `array` → `List[T]` / `Array<T>`\n- `enum` → `Enum` / `enum` 或 `union type`\n\n## 项目结构\n\n生成的项目结构（模块化）：\n\n```\nproject/\n├── app/\n│   ├── main.py              # FastAPI 应用入口\n│   ├── database.py          # 数据库配置\n│   ├── models/              # SQLAlchemy 模型\n│   │   ├── __init__.py\n│   │   └── {resource}.py\n│   ├── schemas/             # Pydantic schemas\n│   │   ├── __init__.py\n│   │   └── {resource}.py\n│   ├── routers/             # API 路由\n│   │   ├── __init__.py\n│   │   └── {resource}.py\n│   └── crud/                # CRUD 操作\n│       ├── __init__.py\n│       ├── base.py\n│       └── {resource}.py\n├── alembic/                 # 数据库迁移\n│   ├── versions/\n│   └── env.py\n├── tests/                   # 测试\n│   ├── conftest.py\n│   ├── test_api/\n│   └── test_crud/\n├── .env.example             # 环境变量示例\n├── alembic.ini              # Alembic 配置\n└── pyproject.toml           # 项目配置\n```\n\n详见：**[references/project-structure.md](references/project-structure.md)**\n\n## 最佳实践\n\n详细的 FastAPI 最佳实践见：**[references/fastapi-patterns.md](references/fastapi-patterns.md)**\n\n关键模式：\n- 使用依赖注入（`Depends(get_db)`）\n- CRUD 基类继承模式\n- 统一错误处理\n- 响应模型验证\n- 分页和查询参数\n\n## 测试模式\n\n详细的测试模式见：**[references/testing-patterns.md](references/testing-patterns.md)**\n\n测试结构：\n- `conftest.py` - 共享 fixtures（DB session, test client）\n- `test_api/` - API 集成测试\n- `test_crud/` - CRUD 单元测试\n\n运行测试：\n```bash\npytest tests/ -v --cov=app\n```\n\n## 错误处理\n\n### 无效的 OpenAPI Spec\n**症状**：YAML 解析错误、缺少必需字段\n\n**处理**：\n1. 停止生成\n2. 显示具体错误信息\n3. 询问用户是否修正或提供新 spec\n\n### 文件冲突\n**症状**：要生成的文件已存在\n\n**处理**：\n1. 列出冲突文件\n2. 询问用户：覆盖/合并/重命名/跳过\n3. 按用户选择执行\n\n### 类型映射失败\n**症状**：OpenAPI 类型无法映射到 Python\n\n**处理**：\n1. 使用默认类型（`Any`）\n2. 添加 TODO comment\n3. 提醒用户检查\n\n### 测试失败\n**症状**：pytest 报错\n\n**处理**：\n1. 分析错误信息\n2. 修复代码\n3. 重新运行测试\n4. 如果 3 次尝试失败，询问用户\n\n## 技术栈\n\n- **Python**: 3.12+\n- **Framework**: FastAPI\n- **Database**: SQLite (via SQLAlchemy)\n- **ORM**: SQLAlchemy\n- **Migration**: Alembic\n- **Validation**: Pydantic\n- **Testing**: pytest, httpx\n- **Package Manager**: uv\n- **Frontend** (可选): Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript\n\n## 示例使用场景\n\n### 场景 1：从头创建新项目\n\n**用户**：\"我有一个 petstore.yaml OpenAPI spec，帮我生成完整的 FastAPI 后端\"\n\n**执行**：\n1. 读取 petstore.yaml\n2. 验证格式\n3. 询问是否生成全部 endpoints\n4. 创建项目结构（从 assets/fastapi-template/）\n5. 生成所有代码（models, schemas, routers, crud, tests）\n6. 生成迁移\n7. 运行测试验证\n8. 提供总结和 TODO 清单\n\n### 场景 2：集成到现有项目\n\n**用户**：\"根据这个 spec（粘贴内容）生成 API，集成到现有项目\"\n\n**执行**：\n1. 解析粘贴的 spec\n2. 检测现有项目结构\n3. 询问选择哪些 endpoints\n4. 检查文件冲突\n5. 生成新代码（避免覆盖已有文件）\n6. 更新 main.py 注册新 routers\n7. 更新测试\n8. 运行测试验证\n\n### 场景 3：只生成部分 endpoints\n\n**用户**：\"从 spec 里只生成 /users 和 /posts 相关的 API\"\n\n**执行**：\n1. 验证 spec\n2. 显示所有可用 endpoints\n3. 用户选择 /users 和 /posts\n4. 只为这两个资源生成代码\n5. 测试验证\n\n## 注意事项\n\n1. **认证/授权**：生成的代码**不包含**认证实现，只有 TODO 占位符\n2. **业务逻辑**：CRUD 操作是脚手架，需要用户补充业务逻辑\n3. **关系**：复杂的数据库关系需要用户手动调整\n4. **环境变量**：记得配置 `.env` 文件\n5. **生产部署**：生成的代码用于开发，生产环境需额外配置（如 Gunicorn、HTTPS、CORS 限制）\n\n## 资源文件\n\n- **references/type-mapping.md** - OpenAPI 到 Python/TypeScript 类型映射\n- **references/project-structure.md** - 推荐的项目结构\n- **references/fastapi-patterns.md** - FastAPI 最佳实践模式\n- **references/testing-patterns.md** - 测试模式和最佳实践\n- **assets/fastapi-template/** - FastAPI 项目基础模板\n- **assets/templates/** - Jinja2 代码生成模板\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:45:36.199Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full Stack Agents needing rapid FastAPI backend development with OpenAPI 3.x specifications.","zh":"非常适合需要快速开发FastAPI后端并使用OpenAPI 3.x规范的全栈代理。","ja":"FastAPIバックエンドの迅速な開発とOpenAPI 3.xの仕様を必要とするフルスタックエージェントに最適です。","ko":"FastAPI 백엔드의 빠른 개발과 OpenAPI 3.x 사양이 필요한 풀스택 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Full Stack que necesitan un desarrollo rápido de backend con FastAPI y especificaciones de OpenAPI 3.x.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Full Stack nécessitant un développement rapide de backend avec FastAPI et des spécifications OpenAPI 3.x.","de":"Perfekt für Full-Stack-Agents, die eine schnelle FastAPI-Backend-Entwicklung mit OpenAPI 3.x-Spezifikationen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Full Stack que precisam de desenvolvimento rápido de backend FastAPI com especificações OpenAPI 3.x.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Full Stack, которым требуется быстрое развитие бэкенда FastAPI с использованием спецификаций OpenAPI 3.x.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء كامل الحزمة الذين يحتاجون إلى تطوير خلفية سريع باستخدام مواصفات OpenAPI 3.x."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to automatically generate complete FastAPI backend scaffolding, including database models, API routes, and Next.js clients, directly from OpenAPI specifications using Python and validating specs with scripts like validate_spec.py.","zh":"赋予代理自动从OpenAPI规范中生成完整的FastAPI后端脚手架，包括数据库模型、API路由和Next.js客户端，并使用Python和脚本（如validate_spec.py）验证规范。","ja":"エージェントにOpenAPIの仕様からFastAPIバックエンドの完全なスケルトンを自動的に生成する能力を与え、データベースモデル、APIルート、Next.jsクライアントを含み、Pythonとスクリプト（例：validate_spec.py）を使用して仕様を検証します。","ko":"에이전트가 OpenAPI 사양에서 FastAPI 백엔드의 완전한 스켈레톤을 자동으로 생성하도록 하며, 데이터베이스 모델, API 라우트 및 Next.js 클라이언트를 포함하며, Python 및 스크립트(예: validate_spec.py)를 사용하여 사양을 검증합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar automáticamente la estructura completa del backend de FastAPI, incluidos modelos de base de datos, rutas de API y clientes de Next.js, directamente desde las especificaciones de OpenAPI utilizando Python y validando las especificaciones con scripts como validate_spec.py.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer automatiquement la structure complète du backend FastAPI, y compris les modèles de base de données, les routes API et les clients Next.js, directement à partir des spécifications OpenAPI en utilisant Python et en validant les spécifications avec des scripts comme validate_spec.py.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, automatisch die komplette FastAPI-Backend-Struktur zu generieren, einschließlich Datenbankmodellen, API-Routen und Next.js-Clients, direkt aus den OpenAPI-Spezifikationen mithilfe von Python und Validierung der Spezifikationen mit Skripten wie validate_spec.py.","pt":"Permite que os agentes gerem automaticamente toda a estrutura de backend do FastAPI, incluindo modelos de banco de dados, rotas de API e clientes Next.js, diretamente a partir de especificações OpenAPI usando Python e validando especificações com scripts como validate_spec.py.","ru":"Позволяет агентам автоматически генерировать полную структуру бэкенда FastAPI, включая модели баз данных, маршруты API и клиенты Next.js, напрямую из спецификаций OpenAPI с использованием Python и проверкой спецификаций с помощью скриптов, таких как validate_spec.py.","ar":"يمكن للوكلاء من خلالها توليد بنية خلفية كاملة تلقائيًا باستخدام FastAPI، بما في ذلك نماذج قواعد البيانات وطرق واجهة برمجة التطبيقات وعملاء Next.js، مباشرة من مواصفات OpenAPI باستخدام Python و التحقق من مواصفات باستخدام سكريبتات مثل validate_spec.py."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating FastAPI backend generation from OpenAPI specs","Generating database models and API routes","Creating Next.js clients for API interaction"],"zh":["从OpenAPI规范自动化FastAPI后端生成","生成数据库模型和API路由","为API交互创建Next.js客户端"],"ja":["OpenAPI仕様からFastAPIバックエンドを自動生成する","データベースモデルとAPIルートを生成する","APIとのやり取りのためにNext.jsクライアントを作成する"],"ko":["OpenAPI 사양에서 FastAPI 백엔드를 자동으로 생성하는 것","데이터베이스 모델 및 API 라우트 생성","API 상호 작용을 위한 Next.js 클라이언트 생성"],"es":["Automatización de la generación de backend de FastAPI a partir de especificaciones de OpenAPI","Generación de modelos de base de datos y rutas de API","Creación de clientes de Next.js para la interacción con la API"],"fr":["Automatisation de la génération de backend FastAPI à partir de spécifications OpenAPI","Génération de modèles de base de données et de routes API","Création de clients Next.js pour l''interaction avec l''API"],"de":["Automatisierung der FastAPI-Backend-Generierung aus OpenAPI-Spezifikationen","Generierung von Datenbankmodellen und API-Routen","Erstellung von Next.js-Clients für die API-Interaktion"],"pt":["Automatizar a geração de backend do FastAPI a partir de especificações OpenAPI","Gerar modelos de banco de dados e rotas de API","Criar clientes Next.js para interação com a API"],"ru":["Автоматизировать генерацию бэкенда FastAPI из спецификаций OpenAPI","Генерировать модели баз данных и маршруты API","Создавать клиенты Next.js для взаимодействия с API"],"ar":["تأتميت إنشاء خلفية FastAPI من مواصفات OpenAPI","إنشاء نماذج قواعد البيانات وطرق واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","إنشاء عملاء Next.js للتفاعل مع واجهة برمجة التطبيقات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires OpenAPI 3.x specification files (.yaml or .json)","Needs Python 3 environment for script execution","Limited to FastAPI and Next.js frameworks"],"zh":["需要OpenAPI 3.x规范文件(.yaml或.json)","需要Python 3环境来执行脚本","仅限于FastAPI和Next.js框架"],"ja":["OpenAPI 3.x仕様ファイル(.yamlまたは.json)が必要","スクリプトの実行にはPython 3環境が必要","FastAPIとNext.jsのフレームワークのみ"],"ko":["OpenAPI 3.x 사양 파일(.yaml 또는 .json) 필요","스크립트 실행을 위해 Python 3 환경 필요","FastAPI 및 Next.js 프레임워크만 해당"],"es":["Requiere archivos de especificación de OpenAPI 3.x (.yaml o .json)","Necesita un entorno de Python 3 para la ejecución de scripts","Limitado a los frameworks FastAPI y Next.js"],"fr":["Nécessite des fichiers de spécification OpenAPI 3.x (.yaml ou .json)","Nécessite un environnement Python 3 pour l''exécution des scripts","Limité aux frameworks FastAPI et Next.js"],"de":["Benötigt OpenAPI 3.x-Spezifikationsdateien (.yaml oder .json)","Benötigt eine Python 3-Umgebung für die Ausführung von Skripten","Begrenzt auf die Frameworks FastAPI und Next.js"],"pt":["Requer arquivos de especificação OpenAPI 3.x (.yaml ou .json)","Necessita de ambiente Python 3 para execução de scripts","Limitado aos quadros FastAPI e Next.js"],"ru":["Требует файлов спецификаций OpenAPI 3.x (.yaml или .json)","Требует среды Python 3 для выполнения скриптов","Ограничен фреймворками FastAPI и Next.js"],"ar":["يتطلب ملفات مواصفات OpenAPI 3.x (.yaml أو .json)","يحتاج إلى بيئة Python 3 لتنفيذ السكريبتات","محدود بإطارات FastAPI و Next.js"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('H2OSLabs/SynnovatorZero/spec-writer', 'community', 'H2OSLabs', 'SynnovatorZero', 'H2OSLabs/SynnovatorZero', 'spec-writer', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.411Z', '2026-02-18T03:45:06.206Z', NULL, '{"id":"H2OSLabs/SynnovatorZero/spec-writer","name":"spec-writer","description":{"zh":"Spec Writer 是一个技术指南，引导用户编写结构化的 SPEC.md 文件。它涵盖了 6 个核心领域，包括命令、测试、项目结构、代码风格、Git 工作流和边界","ja":"Spec Writer は、構造化された SPEC.md ファイルを書くための技術ガイドです。6 つのコアドメイン、つまりコマンド、テスト、プロジェクト構造、コードスタイル、Git ワークフロー、境界をカバーしています","ko":"Spec Writer 는 구조화 된 SPEC.md 파일을 작성하기 위한 기술 가이드입니다. 6 개의 코어 도메인, 즉 명령, 테스트, 프로젝트 구조, 코드 스타일, Git 워크 플로, 경계를 다룹니다","es":"Spec Writer es una herramienta que te guía a través de un flujo de trabajo de 4 etapas para escribir especificaciones técnicas estructuradas para agentes de codificación AI","fr":"Spec Writer est un outil qui vous guide à travers un flux de travail de 4 étapes pour rédiger des spécifications techniques structurées pour les agents de codage AI","de":"Spec Writer ist ein Tool, das Sie durch einen 4-stufigen Arbeitsablauf führt, um strukturierte technische Spezifikationen für AI-Coding-Agenten zu schreiben","pt":"O Escrivão de Especificações ajuda os desenvolvedores a criar especificações estruturadas para agentes de codificação AI","ru":"Спецификации-писатель помогает разработчикам создавать структурированные спецификации для агентов кодирования AI","ar":"كاتب المواصفات يساعد المطورين على إنشاء مواصفات منظمة للوكلاء البرمجيين الإصطناعي","en":"Synnovator Rebuild from Scratch"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Spec Writer 技术指南","ja":"Spec Writer 技術ガイド","ko":"Spec Writer 기술 가이드","es":"Escribe especificaciones técnicas con Spec Writer","fr":"Rédigez des spécifications techniques avec Spec Writer","de":"Schreiben Sie technische Spezifikationen mit Spec Writer","pt":"Escrivão de Especificações: Guia para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Спецификации-писатель: Руководство для разработчиков","ar":"كاتب المواصفات: دليل للمطورين","en":"spec-writer"},"description":{"zh":"Spec Writer 是一个技术指南，引导用户编写结构化的 SPEC.md 文件。它涵盖了 6 个核心领域，包括命令、测试、项目结构、代码风格、Git 工作流和边界","ja":"Spec Writer は、構造化された SPEC.md ファイルを書くための技術ガイドです。6 つのコアドメイン、つまりコマンド、テスト、プロジェクト構造、コードスタイル、Git ワークフロー、境界をカバーしています","ko":"Spec Writer 는 구조화 된 SPEC.md 파일을 작성하기 위한 기술 가이드입니다. 6 개의 코어 도메인, 즉 명령, 테스트, 프로젝트 구조, 코드 스타일, Git 워크 플로, 경계를 다룹니다","es":"Spec Writer es una herramienta que te guía a través de un flujo de trabajo de 4 etapas para escribir especificaciones técnicas estructuradas para agentes de ...","fr":"Spec Writer est un outil qui vous guide à travers un flux de travail de 4 étapes pour rédiger des spécifications techniques structurées pour les agents de co...","de":"Spec Writer ist ein Tool, das Sie durch einen 4-stufigen Arbeitsablauf führt, um strukturierte technische Spezifikationen für AI-Coding-Agenten zu schreiben","pt":"O Escrivão de Especificações ajuda os desenvolvedores a criar especificações estruturadas para agentes de codificação AI","ru":"Спецификации-писатель помогает разработчикам создавать структурированные спецификации для агентов кодирования AI","ar":"كاتب المواصفات يساعد المطورين على إنشاء مواصفات منظمة للوكلاء البرمجيين الإصطناعي","en":"Synnovator Rebuild from Scratch"},"definition":{"en":"Synnovator Rebuild from Scratch"},"features":{"zh":["4 阶段有门槛的工作流程","6 个核心领域","镜像用户语言","具体优于抽象"],"ja":["4 段階のゲート化されたワークフロー","6 つのコアドメイン","ユーザーの言語をミラーする","具体的なものを優先する"],"ko":["4 단계 게이트 化된 워크 플로","6 개의 코어 도메인","사용자의 언어를 미러링","구체적인 것을 우선"],"es":["Flujo de trabajo de 4 etapas","Estructura de SPEC.md para agentes de codificación AI","Compatibilidad con múltiples idiomas","Enfoque en la concreción sobre la abstracción","Guía para escribir especificaciones técnicas claras y concisas","Soporte para seis dominios core: Comandos, Pruebas, Estructura de proyecto, Estilo de código, Flujo de trabajo de Git y Límites"],"fr":["Flux de travail de 4 étapes","Structure de SPEC.md pour les agents de codage AI","Compatibilité avec plusieurs langues","Focus sur la concrétisation plutôt que l''abstraction","Guide pour rédiger des spécifications techniques claires et concises","Support pour six domaines core : Commandes, Tests, Structure de projet, Style de code, Flux de travail Git et Limites"],"de":["4-stufiger Arbeitsablauf","Struktur von SPEC.md für AI-Coding-Agenten","Unterstützung für mehrere Sprachen","Fokus auf Konkretion anstelle von Abstraktion","Anleitung zum Schreiben klarer und präziser technischer Spezifikationen","Unterstützung für sechs Kernbereiche: Befehle, Tests, Projektstruktur, Code-Stil, Git-Workflows und Grenzen"],"pt":["Fluxo de trabalho de 4 etapas","Cobertura de seis domínios principais","Compatibilidade com múltiplos idiomas","Regras concretas para escrita de especificações","Integração com agentes de codificação AI","Otimização para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["Работа в 4 этапа","Покрытие шести основных доменов","Поддержка нескольких языков","Конкретные правила для написания спецификаций","Интеграция с агентами кодирования AI","Оптимизация для разработчиков"],"ar":["عملية العمل المكونة من 4 مراحل","التغطية الست مجالات رئيسية","دعم اللغات المتعددة","القواعد المحددة لكتابة المواصفات","التكامل مع وكلاء البرمجة الإصطناعية","التحسين للمطورين"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Spec Writer","结构化 SPEC.md","AI 代码代理","技术指南","4 阶段工作流程","核心领域"],"ja":["Spec Writer","構造化された SPEC.md","AI コード エージェント","技術ガイド","4 段階のワークフロー","コアドメイン"],"ko":["Spec Writer","구조화 된 SPEC.md","AI 코드 에이전트","기술 가이드","4 단계 워크 플로","코어 도메인"],"es":["Spec Writer","especificaciones técnicas","agentes de codificación AI","desarrollo de software","flujo de trabajo","estructura de SPEC.md","compatibilidad con idiomas","concreción sobre abstracción"],"fr":["Spec Writer","spécifications techniques","agents de codage AI","développement de logiciels","flux de travail","structure de SPEC.md","compatibilité avec les langues","concrétisation plutôt que l''abstraction"],"de":["Spec Writer","technische Spezifikationen","AI-Coding-Agenten","Software-Entwicklung","Arbeitsablauf","Struktur von SPEC.md","Unterstützung für Sprachen","Konkretion anstelle von Abstraktion"],"pt":["Escrivão de Especificações","Agentes de codificação AI","Desenvolvimento de software","Especificação de software","Fluxo de trabalho","Desenvolvedores","Linguagem de programação","Inteligência artificial"],"ru":["Спецификации-писатель","Агенты кодирования AI","Разработка программного обеспечения","Спецификация программного обеспечения","Работа в потоке","Разработчики","Язык программирования","Искусственный интеллект"],"ar":["كاتب المواصفات","وكلاء البرمجة الإصطناعية","تطوير البرمجيات","مواصفات البرمجيات","عملية العمل","المطورين","لغة البرمجة","الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"H2OSLabs","repo":"SynnovatorZero","repoPath":"H2OSLabs/SynnovatorZero","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.411Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"spec-writer","description":"Guide structured specification writing for AI coding agents using a 4-stage gated workflow (Specify, Plan, Tasks, Implement) and a 6-domain framework (Commands, Testing, Project Structure, Code Style, Git Workflow, Boundaries). Produces a SPEC.md file that serves as a living reference for the project. Use when user mentions writing a spec, creating a SPEC.md, setting up project guidelines, onboarding an AI agent to a codebase, or asks for structured project specification. Trigger phrases include write a spec, create a SPEC.md, set up project guidelines, spec out this project, define project standards.","bodyPreview":"# Spec Writer\n\n## Overview\n\nGuide users through writing a structured SPEC.md for AI coding agents using a 4-stage gated workflow. The spec covers six core domains drawn from analysis of effective agent configurations: Commands, Testing, Project Structure, Code Style, Git Workflow, and Boundaries.\n\n**Core rule:** Mirror the user''s language. If they write in Chinese, respond in Chinese. If in English, respond in English. Never hardcode a language.\n\n**Key principle:** Concrete over abstract. A real","body":"# Spec Writer\n\n## Overview\n\nGuide users through writing a structured SPEC.md for AI coding agents using a 4-stage gated workflow. The spec covers six core domains drawn from analysis of effective agent configurations: Commands, Testing, Project Structure, Code Style, Git Workflow, and Boundaries.\n\n**Core rule:** Mirror the user''s language. If they write in Chinese, respond in Chinese. If in English, respond in English. Never hardcode a language.\n\n**Key principle:** Concrete over abstract. A real code snippet beats a paragraph of description. A runnable command beats a tool name. A specific file path beats \"see the docs.\"\n\n## When to Offer\n\nOffer this workflow when:\n- User says \"write a spec\", \"create a SPEC.md\", \"spec out this project\"\n- User wants to set up project guidelines or standards for an AI agent\n- User asks how to onboard an AI coding agent to their codebase\n- User mentions spec-driven development or structured project documentation\n- User wants to define boundaries/rules for an AI coding agent\n\n**Initial offer:** Explain the 4-stage workflow and ask if they want to proceed or work freeform. If they decline, work freeform. If they accept, proceed to Stage 1.\n\n## Stage 1: Specify (Vision Gathering)\n\n**Goal:** Understand what is being built, for whom, and why. No technical details yet.\n\n### Branching: Greenfield vs Existing\n\nDetermine which path applies:\n\n**Greenfield project (building from scratch):**\n1. Ask: What are you building? Who is it for? What problem does it solve?\n2. Ask: What does success look like? How will you know the project works?\n3. Ask: Any constraints or non-negotiables? (timeline, technology mandates, etc.)\n4. Draft a 2-3 sentence Vision statement and Success Criteria checklist\n5. Present for approval\n\n**Existing project (adding a spec to existing code):**\n1. Ask: What is this project? Point me to the codebase.\n2. Explore the codebase: read `package.json`/`pyproject.toml`/`Cargo.toml`, scan directory structure, read README if present\n3. Draft a Vision statement based on what exists\n4. Ask: Is this accurate? What''s missing or wrong?\n5. Present for approval\n\n### Stage 1 Gate\n\nPresent the Vision and Success Criteria. User must approve before advancing.\n\nIf user wants changes, iterate. Only proceed to Stage 2 when user explicitly approves.\n\n**Output so far:** Vision section + Success Criteria checklist.\n\n## Stage 2: Plan (Six Domain Framework)\n\n**Goal:** Systematically collect information for all six domains.\n\nRead [references/six-domains-checklist.md](references/six-domains-checklist.md) for the detailed checklist of what to collect, output formats, mistakes to avoid, and questions to ask for each domain.\n\n### Workflow\n\n1. **For each domain** (Commands, Testing, Project Structure, Code Style, Git Workflow, Boundaries), follow this loop:\n   - Ask the domain-specific questions from the checklist\n   - For existing projects: also probe the codebase (read configs, scan files, check for linters/formatters)\n   - Draft the domain section in the checklist''s output format\n   - Present for user review\n\n2. **Boundaries get special treatment:**\n   - Read [references/boundary-patterns.md](references/boundary-patterns.md) for project-type-specific examples\n   - Always produce all three tiers: Always, Ask First, Never\n   - The \"Never commit secrets\" rule is mandatory in every spec\n   - Adapt patterns to the specific project rather than copying generic lists\n\n3. **Tech Stack:** Also collect the full tech stack during this stage (language, framework, database, testing framework, package manager, versions).\n\n### Stage 2 Gate\n\nPresent a summary of all six domains plus the tech stack. User must approve before advancing.\n\nIf any domain is incomplete or wrong, iterate on that domain. Only proceed to Stage 3 when all six domains are approved.\n\n**Output so far:** Vision + Success Criteria + Tech Stack + all six domains in draft form.\n\n## Stage 3: Tasks (Decomposition and Scaffolding)\n\n**Goal:** Assemble the approved content into a SPEC.md file using the template scaffold.\n\nRead [references/spec-template.md](references/spec-template.md) for the output template.\n\n### Workflow\n\n1. Create a new file `SPEC.md` (or the user''s preferred filename/location) using the template scaffold\n2. Fill in each template section with the content approved in Stages 1-2\n3. For any optional sections (Architecture Notes, Version History), ask if the user wants them included\n4. Set Version History to `1.0 | [today''s date] | Initial specification`\n\n### Stage 3 Gate\n\nPresent the complete SPEC.md draft. User must approve the assembled document.\n\nKey review points to highlight:\n- Does the assembled document flow well as a whole?\n- Are there contradictions between sections?\n- Is anything missing that became obvious when seeing everything together?\n\nIterate until user approves.\n\n## Stage 4: Implement (Validation and Finalization)\n\n**Goal:** Validate completeness, finalize the spec, and establish it as the project''s living reference.\n\n### Workflow\n\n1. **Self-check:** Re-read the complete SPEC.md and verify:\n   - All six domains have substantive content (not placeholders)\n   - Boundaries has all three tiers\n   - Commands section has actual runnable commands with flags\n   - Code Style section has at least one real code snippet\n   - Success Criteria are measurable\n\n2. **Script validation:** Run the validation script:\n   ```bash\n   uv run python [skill-path]/scripts/validate_spec.py [spec-path]\n   ```\n   Replace `[skill-path]` with the path to this skill''s directory and `[spec-path]` with the SPEC.md file path.\n\n3. **Fix any failures:** If validation finds gaps, go back to the relevant section and fix it. Re-run until all checks pass.\n\n4. **Final presentation:** Show the user the validation results and the complete SPEC.md. Ask for final approval.\n\n### Stage 4 Gate\n\nUser gives final approval. The spec is done.\n\n## Post-Completion\n\nAfter the spec is approved:\n\n1. **Living document guidance:** Remind the user that SPEC.md is a living document:\n   - Update it when requirements change\n   - Update it when technical decisions are made\n   - Track changes in Version History\n   - Commit it to version control alongside code\n\n2. **Integration suggestions:**\n   - Place SPEC.md at the project root or in a `specs/` directory\n   - Reference it from CLAUDE.md or agents.md if applicable\n   - Consider adding the validation script to CI\n\n3. **Next steps:** Ask if the user wants to:\n   - Start implementing based on the spec\n   - Create task breakdowns from the spec\n   - Review an existing spec against this framework\n\n## Handling Deviations\n\n**User wants to skip stages:** Allow it, but warn that skipping Stage 2 (Plan) risks an incomplete spec. If they skip, note which domains weren''t covered.\n\n**User wants a partial spec:** Support single-domain mode — e.g., \"just help me define boundaries.\" Follow the Stage 2 workflow for that domain only, then validate just that section.\n\n**User has an existing SPEC.md to audit:** Run `validate_spec.py` on it first, then walk through any FAIL items using the six-domains checklist.\n\n**User is updating, not creating:** Read the existing SPEC.md, identify what changed, update the relevant sections, bump the version in Version History.\n\n## Quality Principles\n\n1. **Concrete over abstract:** A runnable command beats a tool name. A code snippet beats a style description. A file path beats \"see the docs.\"\n\n2. **Boundaries are non-negotiable:** Every spec must have all three tiers. \"Never commit secrets\" is always included. Generic boundaries (\"don''t break things\") are rejected — push for specifics.\n\n3. **Six domains are mandatory:** No spec is complete without all six. If the user insists on skipping one, note the gap explicitly in the spec.\n\n4. **The spec is for an AI agent, not a human:** Write for parsability. Use headers, lists, and code blocks. Avoid prose paragraphs where structured formats work better.\n\n5. **Medium freedom template:** The six domains are fixed scaffolding. Content within each domain is flexible and adapts to the project. Don''t force patterns that don''t fit.\n\n6. **Validate deterministically:** Always run the validation script. Human judgment catches semantic issues; the script catches structural ones. Both matter.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:45:06.206Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI coding agents requiring structured specification development, such as those using SPEC.md for configuration management.","zh":"非常适合需要结构化规范开发的AI编码智能体，例如使用SPEC.md进行配置管理的智能体。","ja":"SPEC.mdを使用した構成管理など、構造化された仕様開発を必要とするAIコーディングエージェントに最適です。","ko":"SPEC.md를 사용한 구성 관리와 같이 구조화된 사양 개발이 필요한 AI 코딩 에이전트에 이상적입니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de codificación de IA que requieren el desarrollo de especificaciones estructuradas, como aquellos que utilizan SPEC.md para la gestión de configuraciones.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de codage IA nécessitant un développement de spécifications structurées, tels que ceux utilisant SPEC.md pour la gestion de configuration.","de":"Ideal für AI-Coding-Agenten, die eine strukturierte Spezifikationsentwicklung erfordern, wie z.B. solche, die SPEC.md für die Konfigurationsverwaltung verwenden.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de codificação de IA que exigem desenvolvimento de especificação estruturada, como aqueles que usam SPEC.md para gerenciamento de configuração.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов кодирования ИИ, требующих разработки структурированной спецификации, таких как те, которые используют SPEC.md для управления конфигурацией.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الترميز الإصطناعي التي تتطلب تطوير مواصفات منظم، مثل تلك التي تستخدم SPEC.md لإدارة التكوين."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate comprehensive SPEC.md files using a 4-stage gated workflow, covering core domains like Commands, Testing, and Git Workflow, while mirroring the user''s language for seamless interaction.","zh":"通过4阶段门控工作流，使智能体能够生成全面的SPEC.md文件，涵盖命令、测试和Git工作流等核心领域，同时镜像用户语言以实现无缝交互。","ja":"4段階のゲート付きワークフローを使用して、コマンド、テスト、Gitワークフローなどのコアドメインをカバーし、ユーザーの言語をミラーリングしてシームレスなインタラクションを実現する包括的なSPEC.mdファイルの生成をエージェントに可能にします。","ko":"4단계 게이트 워크플로우를 사용하여 명령, 테스트, Git 워크플로우와 같은 핵심 도메인을 다루는 포괄적인 SPEC.md 파일을 생성하고 원활한 상호 작용을 위해 사용자의 언어를 미러링하도록 에이전트를 강화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar archivos SPEC.md completos utilizando un flujo de trabajo de 4 etapas, que cubre dominios básicos como Comandos, Pruebas y Flujo de trabajo de Git, al mismo tiempo que refleja el lenguaje del usuario para una interacción sin problemas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des fichiers SPEC.md complets en utilisant un flux de travail à 4 étapes, couvrant des domaines clés tels que les Commandes, les Tests et le Flux de travail Git, tout en mirroirant le langage de l''utilisateur pour une interaction sans accroc.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, umfassende SPEC.md-Dateien mit einem 4-Stufen-Workflow zu generieren, der Kernbereiche wie Befehle, Testen und Git-Workflow abdeckt, während gleichzeitig die Sprache des Benutzers für eine nahtlose Interaktion widerspiegelt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar arquivos SPEC.md abrangentes usando um fluxo de trabalho de 4 estágios, cobrindo domínios principais como Comandos, Testes e Fluxo de Trabalho do Git, ao mesmo tempo em que espelha a linguagem do usuário para interação sem problemas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать полные файлы SPEC.md, используя 4-этапный поток работ, покрывающий основные области, такие как Команды, Тестирование и Поток работы Git, а также отражая язык пользователя для бесперебойного взаимодействия.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إنشاء ملفات SPEC.md شاملة باستخدام تدفق عمل من 4 مراحل ، وتغطية المجالات الأساسية مثل الأوامر و الاختبار و تدفق العمل جيت ، مع تمكين镜ة لغة المستخدم من أجل التفاعل السلس."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating SPEC.md generation for AI agent configurations","Standardizing project structures through SPEC.md templates","Streamlining Git workflows with SPEC.md guidelines"],"zh":["自动化生成AI智能体配置的SPEC.md文件","通过SPEC.md模板标准化项目结构","使用SPEC.md指南简化Git工作流程"],"ja":["AIエージェント構成のためのSPEC.md生成の自動化","SPEC.mdテンプレートによるプロジェクト構造の標準化","SPEC.mdガイドラインによるGitワークフローの効率化"],"ko":["AI 에이전트 구성을 위한 SPEC.md 생성 자동화","SPEC.md 템플릿을 통한 프로젝트 구조 표준화","SPEC.md 지침으로 Git 워크플로우 간소화"],"es":["Automatizar la generación de SPEC.md para configuraciones de agentes de IA","Establecer estructuras de proyecto estándar a través de plantillas SPEC.md","Optimizar flujos de trabajo de Git con pautas SPEC.md"],"fr":["Automatiser la génération de SPEC.md pour les configurations d''agents IA","Normaliser les structures de projet via des modèles SPEC.md","Optimiser les flux de travail Git avec des directives SPEC.md"],"de":["Automatisieren der Erstellung von SPEC.md für AI-Agenten-Konfigurationen","Standardisieren von Projekstrukturen durch SPEC.md-Vorlagen","Optimieren von Git-Workflows mit SPEC.md-Richtlinien"],"pt":["Automatizar a geração de SPEC.md para configurações de agentes de IA","Padronizar estruturas de projeto por meio de modelos SPEC.md","Otimizar fluxos de trabalho do Git com diretrizes SPEC.md"],"ru":["Автоматизировать генерацию SPEC.md для конфигураций агентов ИИ","Стандартизировать структуры проектов с помощью шаблонов SPEC.md","Оптимизировать потоки работы Git с помощью руководств SPEC.md"],"ar":["توفير автомاتي لإنشاء SPEC.md لتنفيذ وكلاء الإصطناعي","تقييس هياكل المشروع من خلال قوالب SPEC.md","تسهيل تدفق العمل جيت باستخدام إرشادات SPEC.md"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of SPEC.md format","Language mirroring may require additional natural language processing capabilities"],"zh":["需要理解SPEC.md格式","语言镜像可能需要额外的自然语言处理能力"],"ja":["SPEC.md形式の理解が必要","言語ミラーリングには追加の自然言語処理能力が必要な場合がある"],"ko":["SPEC.md 형식에 대한 이해가 필요함","언어 미러링에는 추가 자연어 처리 기능이 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión del formato SPEC.md","La reflexión del lenguaje puede requerir capacidades adicionales de procesamiento de lenguaje natural"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension du format SPEC.md","Le mirroir du langage peut nécessiter des capacités de traitement du langage naturel supplémentaires"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis für das SPEC.md-Format","Die Sprachspiegelung kann zusätzliche Fähigkeiten zur Verarbeitung von natürlichen Sprachen erfordern"],"pt":["Exige compreensão do formato SPEC.md","A espelhamento da linguagem pode exigir capacidades adicionais de processamento de linguagem natural"],"ru":["Требует понимания формата SPEC.md","Зеркалирование языка может потребовать дополнительных возможностей обработки естественного языка"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم تنسيق SPEC.md","鏡像 اللغة قد يتطلب القدرات الإضافية لمعالجة اللغة الطبيعية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
