nfiguration des variables d''environnement","Déploiement en production avec Vercel"],"de":["Erstellung und Bereitstellung von LangChain.js-Retrieval-Agents","Integrierte Retrieval-Tools","Kompatibilität mit dem Vercel AI SDK","Konfiguration von Umgebungsvariablen","Bereitstellung in der Produktion mit Vercel"],"pt":["Utiliza LangGraph para recuperação de informações","Integração com Supabase para armazenamento de dados","Compatível com SDK de IA da Vercel","Fácil implantação com Vercel","Suporte a variáveis de ambiente"],"ru":["Использует LangGraph для поиска информации","Интегрируется с Supabase для хранения данных","Компатибелен с SDK ИИ Vercel","Легкая установка с Vercel","Поддержка переменных окружения"],"ar":["يستخدم LangGraph لاسترجاع المعلومات","التكامل مع Supabase لتخزين البيانات","متوافق مع SDK AI من Vercel","نشر سهل مع Vercel","دعم متغيرات البيئة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["LangChain.js","Supabase","Vercel AI SDK","LangGraph","vercel build --prod","AI","SEO"],"ja":["LangChain.js","Supabase","Vercel AI SDK","LangGraph","vercel build --prod","AI","SEO"],"ko":["LangChain.js","Supabase","Vercel AI SDK","LangGraph","vercel build --prod","AI","SEO"],"es":["LangChain.js","agente de recuperación","herramientas de recuperación","Vercel AI SDK","despliegue en producción","variables de entorno","aplicaciones de recuperación de información"],"fr":["LangChain.js","agent de récupération","outils de récupération","SDK Vercel AI","déploiement en production","variables d''environnement","applications de récupération d''informations"],"de":["LangChain.js","Retrieval-Agent","Retrieval-Tools","Vercel AI SDK","Bereitstellung in der Produktion","Umgebungsvariablen","Informationsabrufanwendungen"],"pt":["LangChain","LangGraph","Supabase","Vercel","SDK de IA","Agente de recuperação","Desenvolvimento de software","Inteligência artificial"],"ru":["LangChain","LangGraph","Supabase","Vercel","SDK ИИ","Агент поиска","Разработка программного обеспечения","Искусственный интеллект"],"ar":["LangChain","LangGraph","Supabase","Vercel","SDK AI","وكيل استرجاع","تطوير البرمجيات","الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"rebyteai-template","repo":"langchain-retrieval-agent","repoPath":"rebyteai-template/langchain-retrieval-agent","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.412Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"build-and-deploy","description":"Build and deploy this Next.js LangChain retrieval agent application with Supabase vector store. Use when building, deploying, setting up vector store, or preparing the project for production.","bodyPreview":"# Build and Deploy LangChain Retrieval Agent\n\n> **CRITICAL: For Vercel, you MUST use `vercel build --prod` then `vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod`.**\n> Do NOT use `vercel --prod` or `vercel deploy --prod` directly - these will fail due to Git author permission issues in VM environments.\n\n## Workflow\n\n### 1. Setup Environment Variables\n\n**Read `.env.example` to see all required variables:**\n\n```bash\ncat .env.example\n```\n\n**Create `.env` by reading values from current environment:**\n\nFor each varia","body":"# Build and Deploy LangChain Retrieval Agent\n\n> **CRITICAL: For Vercel, you MUST use `vercel build --prod` then `vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod`.**\n> Do NOT use `vercel --prod` or `vercel deploy --prod` directly - these will fail due to Git author permission issues in VM environments.\n\n## Workflow\n\n### 1. Setup Environment Variables\n\n**Read `.env.example` to see all required variables:**\n\n```bash\ncat .env.example\n```\n\n**Create `.env` by reading values from current environment:**\n\nFor each variable in `.env.example`, read the value from the current environment and write to `.env`. Example approach:\n\n```bash\n# Read .env.example and create .env with values from current environment\nwhile IFS= read -r line || [[ -n \"$line\" ]]; do\n  # Skip comments and empty lines\n  [[ \"$line\" =~ ^#.*$ || -z \"$line\" ]] && continue\n  # Extract variable name (before = sign)\n  var_name=$(echo \"$line\" | cut -d''='' -f1)\n  # Get value from environment\n  var_value=\"${!var_name}\"\n  # Write to .env\n  echo \"${var_name}=${var_value}\" >> .env\ndone < .env.example\n```\n\nOr manually inspect `.env.example` and create `.env` with the required values from environment variables.\n\n### 2. Install Dependencies\n\n```bash\nyarn install\n```\n\n### 3. Setup Supabase Vector Store\n\nGet the database connection URL from Supabase Dashboard:\n- Go to Settings → Database → Connection string → URI\n- Copy the URI and add it to `.env` as `SUPABASE_DB_URL`\n\n```bash\nyarn setup-db\n```\n\nThis creates the pgvector extension, documents table, and match_documents function in your Supabase project.\n\n### 4. Build\n\n```bash\nyarn build\n```\n\n### 5. Deploy\n\n**Vercel:**\n\nAll vercel CLI commands require `-t <token>` or `--token <token>` for authentication.\n\n```bash\n# Pull project settings (also links project, creates .vercel/project.json)\nvercel pull --yes -t $VERCEL_TOKEN\n\n# Push env vars to Vercel (first time only)\n# Must add to each environment separately\nwhile IFS=''='' read -r key value; do\n  [[ \"$key\" =~ ^#.*$ || -z \"$key\" || -z \"$value\" ]] && continue\n  for env in production preview development; do\n    printf ''%s'' \"$value\" | vercel env add \"$key\" $env -t $VERCEL_TOKEN\n  done\ndone < .env\n\n# Build locally for production\nvercel build --prod -t $VERCEL_TOKEN\n\n# Deploy prebuilt\nvercel deploy --prebuilt --prod --yes -t $VERCEL_TOKEN\n```\n\n**Netlify:**\n```bash\n# Import all env vars from .env (first time only)\nnetlify env:import .env\n\n# Deploy\nnetlify deploy --prod\n```\n\n## Critical Notes\n\n- **VERCEL PREBUILT MODE IS MANDATORY:** Always use `vercel build --prod` followed by `vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod`. Never use `vercel --prod` or `vercel deploy --prod` without `--prebuilt` flag.\n- **Supabase Required:** Need a Supabase project (free tier works)\n- **Vector Store Setup:** Run `yarn setup-db` to create tables automatically\n- **Environment Variables:** All values come from current environment - inspect `.env.example` for required variables\n- **OpenAI for Embeddings:** OPENAI_API_KEY is always required for vector embeddings\n- **No Dev Server:** Never run `yarn dev` in VM environment\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:48:08.526Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for LangChain.js agents needing streamlined deployment and retrieval capabilities powered by LangGraph and Supabase vector store.","zh":"适合需要简化部署和检索功能的 LangChain.js 代理，支持由 LangGraph 和 Supabase 向量存储提供的功能。","ja":"LangGraph と Supabase ベクトルストアによって提供される機能を使用してストリーミングされたデプロイとリトリーバル機能を必要とする LangChain.js エージェントに最適です。","ko":"LangGraph와 Supabase 벡터 저장소가 제공하는 기능을 사용하여 스트리밍된 배포 및检索 기능이 필요한 LangChain.js 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de LangChain.js que necesitan capacidades de implementación y recuperación simplificadas impulsadas por LangGraph y la tienda de vectores de Supabase.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents LangChain.js qui nécessitent des capacités de déploiement et de récupération simplifiées alimentées par LangGraph et le magasin de vecteurs Supabase.","de":"Perfekt für LangChain.js-Agents, die eine vereinfachte Bereitstellung und Wiederherstellungs-Funktionen benötigen, die von LangGraph und dem Supabase-Vektor-Speicher angetrieben werden.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes LangChain.js que necessitam de capacidades de implantação e recuperação simplificadas impulsionadas por LangGraph e Supabase vector store.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов LangChain.js, которым необходимы упрощенные возможности развертывания и извлечения, работающие на базе LangGraph и Supabase vector store.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء LangChain.js الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات نشر واسترجاع مبسطة مدعومة من LangGraph و Supabase vector store."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build and deploy retrieval tools using the Vercel AI SDK, leveraging environment variables and prebuilt deployments for seamless integration with Vercel, while avoiding Git author permission issues in VM environments.","zh":"赋予代理使用 Vercel AI SDK 构建和部署检索工具的能力，利用环境变量和预构建部署实现与 Vercel 的无缝集成，同时避免 VM 环境中的 Git 作者权限问题。","ja":"Vercel AI SDK を使用してエージェントがリトリーバツールを構築およびデプロイできるようにし、環境変数と事前ビルドのデプロイを使用して Vercel とのシームレスな統合を実現し、VM 環境での Git 著者権限の問題を回避します。","ko":"에이전트가 Vercel AI SDK를 사용하여 리트리버 툴을 구축 및 배포할 수 있게 하여 환경 변수 및 사전 구축 배포를 사용하여 Vercel과의无缝な統合을 구현하며, VM 환경에서의 Git 저자 권한 문제를 피합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear y implementar herramientas de recuperación utilizando el SDK de Vercel AI, aprovechando las variables de entorno y los despliegues preconstruidos para una integración sin problemas con Vercel, evitando problemas de permisos de autor de Git en entornos de VM.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer et de déployer des outils de récupération en utilisant le SDK Vercel AI, en exploitant les variables d''environnement et les déploiements préconstruits pour une intégration transparente avec Vercel, tout en évitant les problèmes de permissions d''auteur Git dans les environnements de VM.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Retrieval-Tools mit dem Vercel AI SDK zu erstellen und zu bereitstellen, wobei Umgebungsvariablen und vorkonfigurierte Bereitstellungen für eine nahtlose Integration mit Vercel genutzt werden, während Git-Autoren-Berechtigungsprobleme in VM-Umgebungen vermieden werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir e implantar ferramentas de recuperação usando o SDK de IA da Vercel, aproveitando variáveis de ambiente e implantações pré-construídas para integração perfeita com a Vercel, enquanto evita problemas de permissão de autor do Git em ambientes de VM.","ru":"Предоставляет агентам возможность создавать и развертывать инструменты для извлечения информации, используя SDK ИИ Vercel, который использует переменные окружения и предварительно подготовленные развертывания для бесшовной интеграции с Vercel, а также избегает проблем с разрешениями автора Git в средах виртуальных машин.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من بناء وأستخدام أدوات استرجاع باستخدام SDK الذكاء الاصطناعي من Vercel، واستخدام متغيرات البيئة والتركيبات المسبقة للدمج السلس مع Vercel، مع تجنب مشاكل صلاحيات مؤلف Git في بيئات الآلة الافتراضية."},"useCases":{"en":["Deploying LangChain.js agents with retrieval tools on Vercel","Configuring environment variables for LangGraph and Supabase vector store","Building prebuilt deployments for production-ready agent retrieval tools"],"zh":["在 Vercel 上部署带有检索工具的 LangChain.js 代理","为 LangGraph 和 Supabase 向量存储配置环境变量","为生产就绪的代理检索工具构建预构建部署"],"ja":["Vercel 上でリトリーバツールを使用した LangChain.js エージェントのデプロイ","LangGraph と Supabase ベクトルストアの環境変数の構成","本番環境向けのエージェントリトリーバツールの事前ビルドのデプロイ"],"ko":["Vercel에서 리트리버 툴을 사용한 LangChain.js 에이전트 배포","LangGraph와 Supabase 벡터 저장소의 환경 변수 구성","본番 환경을 위한 에이전트 리트리버 툴의 사전 구축 배포"],"es":["Implementar agentes de LangChain.js con herramientas de recuperación en Vercel","Configurar variables de entorno para LangGraph y la tienda de vectores de Supabase","Crear despliegues preconstruidos para herramientas de recuperación de agentes listas para producción"],"fr":["Déployer des agents LangChain.js avec des outils de récupération sur Vercel","Configurer les variables d''environnement pour LangGraph et le magasin de vecteurs Supabase","Créer des déploiements préconstruits pour des outils de récupération d''agents prêts pour la production"],"de":["Bereitstellen von LangChain.js-Agents mit Retrieval-Tools auf Vercel","Konfigurieren von Umgebungsvariablen für LangGraph und den Supabase-Vektor-Speicher","Erstellen von vorkonfigurierten Bereitstellungen für produktionsbereite Agenten-Retrieval-Tools"],"pt":["Implantando agentes LangChain.js com ferramentas de recuperação no Vercel","Configurando variáveis de ambiente para LangGraph e Supabase vector store","Construindo implantações pré-construídas para ferramentas de recuperação de agentes prontas para produção"],"ru":["Развертывание агентов LangChain.js с инструментами для извлечения информации в Vercel","Настройка переменных окружения для LangGraph и Supabase vector store","Создание предварительно подготовленных развертываний для инструментов извлечения информации, готовых к производству"],"ar":["نشر وكلاء LangChain.js مع أدوات استرجاع على Vercel","تكوين متغيرات البيئة ل LangGraph و Supabase vector store","بناء تركيبات مسبقة لادوات استرجاع الوكلاء جاهزة للإنتاج"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Vercel AI SDK and LangGraph setup","Must use `vercel build --prod` and `vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod` for successful deployment","Git author permission issues may arise in VM environments if not using prebuilt deployments"],"zh":["需要 Vercel AI SDK 和 LangGraph 设置","必须使用 `vercel build --prod` 和 `vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod` 进行成功的部署","如果不使用预构建部署，VM 环境中可能会出现 Git 作者权限问题"],"ja":["Vercel AI SDK と LangGraph の設定が必要","正常なデプロイを行うには `vercel build --prod` と `vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod` を使用する必要があります","事前ビルドのデプロイを使用しないと、VM 環境で Git 著者権限の問題が発生する可能性があります"],"ko":["Vercel AI SDK 및 LangGraph 설정이 필요합니다.","정상적인 배포를 위해 `vercel build --prod` 및 `vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod`를 사용해야 합니다.","사전 구축 배포를 사용하지 않으면 VM 환경에서 Git 저자 권한 문제가 발생할 수 있습니다."],"es":["Requiere configuración del SDK de Vercel AI y LangGraph","Debe utilizar `vercel build --prod` y `vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod` para un despliegue exitoso","Pueden surgir problemas de permisos de autor de Git en entornos de VM si no se utilizan despliegues preconstruidos"],"fr":["Nécessite la configuration du SDK Vercel AI et LangGraph","Doit utiliser `vercel build --prod` et `vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod` pour un déploiement réussi","Des problèmes de permissions d''auteur Git peuvent survenir dans les environnements de VM si les déploiements préconstruits ne sont pas utilisés"],"de":["Erfordert Vercel AI SDK- und LangGraph-Setup","Muss `vercel build --prod` und `vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod` für eine erfolgreiche Bereitstellung verwenden","Git-Autoren-Berechtigungsprobleme können in VM-Umgebungen auftreten, wenn keine vorkonfigurierten Bereitstellungen verwendet werden"],"pt":["Requer o SDK de IA da Vercel e configuração do LangGraph","Deve usar `vercel build --prod` e `vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod` para implantação bem-sucedida","Problemas de permissão de autor do Git podem surgir em ambientes de VM se não estiver usando implantações pré-construídas"],"ru":["Требует наличия SDK ИИ Vercel и настройки LangGraph","Необходимо использовать `vercel build --prod` и `vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod` для успешного развертывания","Проблемы с разрешениями автора Git могут возникнуть в средах виртуальных машин, если не используются предварительно подготовленные развертывания"],"ar":["يتطلب SDK الذكاء الاصطناعي من Vercel و إعداد LangGraph","يجب استخدام `vercel build --prod` و `vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod` لنشر ناجح","مشاكل صلاحيات مؤلف Git قد تنشأ في بيئات الآلة الافتراضية إذا لم يتم استخدام التطبيقات المسبقة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('gwpjp/Web3-Claude/web3-implementer', 'community', 'gwpjp', 'Web3-Claude', 'gwpjp/Web3-Claude', 'web3-implementer', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.412Z', '2026-02-18T03:47:57.212Z', NULL, '{"id":"gwpjp/Web3-Claude/web3-implementer","name":"web3-implementer","description":{"zh":"Web3实现专家负责所有区块链功能的实现，包括合约读写、ponder-indexer查询和调试数据流问题","ja":"Web3実装スペシャリストは、すべてのブロックチェーン機能の実装を担当します。合約の読み取り、合約の書き込み、ponder-indexerのクエリ、およびデータフローの問題のデバッグなどを含みます","ko":"Web3 구현 전문가는 모든 블록체인 기능의 구현을 담당합니다. 계약 읽기, 계약 쓰기, ponder-indexer 쿼리 및 데이터 흐름 문제 디버깅 등을 포함합니다","es":"El implementador Web3 es el agente principal de implementación de blockchain, responsable de orquestar la funcionalidad de blockchain","fr":"L''implémenteur Web3 est l''agent principal d''implémentation de blockchain, chargé d''orchestrer la fonctionnalité de blockchain","de":"Der Web3-Implementierer ist der primäre Blockchain-Implementierungsagent, verantwortlich für die Orchestrierung der Blockchain-Funktionalität","pt":"O Implementador Web3 é um agente de blockchain que gerencia funcionalidades de contrato e debugging, delegando tarefas a especialistas quando necessário.","ru":"Реализатор Web3 - это агент блокчейна, который управляет функциональностью контрактов и отладкой, делегируя задачи специалистам при необходимости.","ar":"مُطبق ويب3 هو وسيط سلاسل الكتل الذي يدير وظائف العقد والتصحيح، ويتولى تفويض المهام إلى الأخصائيين عند الحاجة.","en":"My generic claude settings"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Web3实现专家：区块链开发解决方案","ja":"Web3実装スペシャリスト：ブロックチェーン開発ソリューション","ko":"Web3 구현 전문가: 블록체인 개발 솔루션","es":"Implementador Web3: Experto en Blockchain","fr":"Implémenteur Web3 : Spécialiste de la Blockchain","de":"Web3-Implementierer: Blockchain-Experte","pt":"Implementador Web3: Especialista em Blockchain","ru":"Реализатор Web3: Специалист по блокчейну","ar":"مُطبق ويب3: خبير سلاسل الكتل","en":"web3-implementer"},"description":{"zh":"Web3实现专家负责所有区块链功能的实现，包括合约读写、ponder-indexer查询和调试数据流问题","ja":"Web3実装スペシャリストは、すべてのブロックチェーン機能の実装を担当します。合約の読み取り、合約の書き込み、ponder-indexerのクエリ、およびデータフローの問題のデバッグなどを含みます","ko":"Web3 구현 전문가는 모든 블록체인 기능의 구현을 담당합니다. 계약 읽기, 계약 쓰기, ponder-indexer 쿼리 및 데이터 흐름 문제 디버깅 등을 포함합니다","es":"El implementador Web3 es el agente principal de implementación de blockchain, responsable de orquestar la funcionalidad de blockchain","fr":"L''implémenteur Web3 est l''agent principal d''implémentation de blockchain, chargé d''orchestrer la fonctionnalité de blockchain","de":"Der Web3-Implementierer ist der primäre Blockchain-Implementierungsagent, verantwortlich für die Orchestrierung der Blockchain-Funktionalität","pt":"O Implementador Web3 é um agente de blockchain que gerencia funcionalidades de contrato e debugging, delegando tarefas a especialistas quando necessário.","ru":"Реализатор Web3 - это агент блокчейна, который управляет функциональностью контрактов и отладкой, делегируя задачи специалистам при необходимости.","ar":"مُطبق ويب3 هو وسيط سلاسل الكتل الذي يدير وظائف العقد والتصحيح، ويتولى تفويض المهام إلى الأخصائيين عند الحاجة.","en":"My generic claude settings"},"definition":{"en":"My generic claude settings"},"features":{"zh":["区块链功能实现","合约读写","ponder-indexer查询","数据流问题调试","多代理协调"],"ja":["ブロックチェーン機能の実装","合約の読み取りと書き込み","ponder-indexerのクエリ","データフローの問題のデバッグ","多エージェントの調整"],"ko":["블록체인 기능 구현","계약 읽기 및 쓰기","ponder-indexer 쿼리","데이터 흐름 문제 디버깅","다중 에이전트 조정"],"es":["Implementación de contrato de blockchain","Consulta de ponder-indexer","Depuración de flujo de datos","Orquestación de subagentes especializados","Implementación de esquemas de blockchain","Integración con react-query y wagmi"],"fr":["Implémentation de contrat de blockchain","Requête de ponder-indexer","Débogage du flux de données","Orchestration d''agents spécialisés","Implémentation de schémas de blockchain","Intégration avec react-query et wagmi"],"de":["Implementierung von Blockchain-Verträgen","Abfrage von Ponder-Indexer","Fehlerbehebung bei Datenflussproblemen","Orchestrierung von Spezialagenten","Implementierung von Blockchain-Schemata","Integration mit react-query und wagmi"],"pt":["Orquestração de funcionalidades de contrato","Gerenciamento de debugging de dados","Delegação de tarefas a especialistas","Integração com ponder-schema-specialist","Integração com wagmi-specialist","Integração com react-query-specialist"],"ru":["Организация функциональности контрактов","Управление отладкой данных","Делегирование задач специалистам","Интеграция с ponder-schema-specialist","Интеграция с wagmi-specialist","Интеграция с react-query-specialist"],"ar":["توجيه وظائف العقد","إدارة التصحيح البيانات","تفويض المهام إلى الأخصائيين","التكامل مع ponder-schema-specialist","التكامل مع wagmi-specialist","التكامل مع react-query-specialist"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Web3","区块链开发","区块链实现","合约读写","ponder-indexer","数据流问题调试"],"ja":["Web3","ブロックチェーン開発","ブロックチェーン実装","合約の読み取りと書き込み","ponder-indexer","データフローの問題のデバッグ"],"ko":["Web3","블록체인 개발","블록체인 구현","계약 읽기 및 쓰기","ponder-indexer","데이터 흐름 문제 디버깅"],"es":["web3","implementador web3","blockchain","desarrollo de blockchain","contratos inteligentes","ponder-indexer","react-query","wagmi"],"fr":["web3","implémenteur web3","blockchain","développement de blockchain","contrats intelligents","ponder-indexer","react-query","wagmi"],"de":["web3","web3-implementierer","blockchain","blockchain-entwicklung","smart contracts","ponder-indexer","react-query","wagmi"],"pt":["Implementador Web3","Blockchain","Contrato","Debugging","Ponder-schema-specialist","Wagmi-specialist","React-query-specialist","Desenvolvimento de blockchain"],"ru":["Реализатор Web3","Блокчейн","Контракт","Отладка","Ponder-schema-specialist","Wagmi-specialist","React-query-specialist","Разработка блокчейна"],"ar":["مُطبق ويب3","سلاسل الكتل","عقد","التصحيح","ponder-schema-specialist","wagmi-specialist","react-query-specialist","تطوير سلاسل الكتل"]}},"owner":"gwpjp","repo":"Web3-Claude","repoPath":"gwpjp/Web3-Claude","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.412Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"web3-implementer","description":"Primary agent for all blockchain and ponder-indexer functionality. Expert in wagmi hooks, @ponder/react, drizzle-style queries against ponder.schema.ts, and the two-layer hook architecture (ponder hooks + transform hooks). First point of contact for implementing reads, writes, data fetching, and debugging blockchain or ponder-indexer issues. Manages wagmi-specialist and react-query-specialist as sub-agents.","bodyPreview":"# Web3 Implementer\n\nYou are the **primary blockchain implementation agent** for this project. All blockchain functionality -- whether contract reads, contract writes, ponder-indexer queries, or debugging data flow issues -- routes through you first. You orchestrate `ponder-schema-specialist`, `wagmi-specialist`, and `react-query-specialist` as sub-agents when their deep expertise is needed.\n\n## Initialization\n\nWhen invoked:\n\n1. **For schema questions, delegate to `/ponder-schema-specialist`** --","body":"# Web3 Implementer\n\nYou are the **primary blockchain implementation agent** for this project. All blockchain functionality -- whether contract reads, contract writes, ponder-indexer queries, or debugging data flow issues -- routes through you first. You orchestrate `ponder-schema-specialist`, `wagmi-specialist`, and `react-query-specialist` as sub-agents when their deep expertise is needed.\n\n## Initialization\n\nWhen invoked:\n\n1. **For schema questions, delegate to `/ponder-schema-specialist`** -- it has a pre-compiled condensed reference of all ~70 tables, columns, types, indexes, and relations. Only read `src/services/ponder/ponder.schema.ts` directly if you need exact source verification or the specialist''s reference may be stale.\n2. **Read existing ponder hooks** -- `src/hooks/ponder/index.ts` to see what hooks already exist (avoid duplicating)\n3. Read `.claude/skills/web3-implementer/ponder-reference.md` for query patterns and hook catalog (supplementary)\n4. Read `.claude/skills/web3-implementer/hook-patterns.md` for hook creation templates\n5. If the task involves contract writes or transaction lifecycle, read `.claude/skills/wagmi-specialist/hook-reference.md`\n6. Read `.claude/docs/project-rules.md` for project conventions (address safety, number formatting, etc.)\n7. Read relevant source files before making any changes\n8. For protocol-level context, read `.claude/docs/PROTOCOL_SPECIFICATION.md`\n\n## Your Domain (Handle Yourself)\n\n- **Ponder hooks**: Creating, modifying, or debugging hooks in `src/hooks/ponder/`\n- **Transform hooks**: Creating, modifying, or debugging hooks in `src/hooks/blockchain/useGet*Live.ts`\n- **Contract read hooks**: Creating hooks in `src/hooks/blockchain/useGet*.ts`\n- **Contract write hooks**: Creating hooks in `src/hooks/blockchain/use[Action].ts`\n- **Schema queries**: Any work involving `ponder.schema.ts` or drizzle-style queries\n- **Data flow debugging**: When ponder or blockchain data isn''t showing up correctly\n- **Hook architecture decisions**: Which layer a hook belongs in, what data source to use\n\n## Sub-Agent Delegation\n\n| Situation                                                                               | Delegate To                 |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| Schema questions, table lookups, column types, relationship queries, index availability | `/ponder-schema-specialist` |\n| Complex transaction state machines, Safe wallet handling, gas estimation edge cases     | `/wagmi-specialist`         |\n| Complex cache invalidation strategies, staleTime/gcTime tuning, query key architecture  | `/react-query-specialist`   |\n| UI components, Common components, React patterns                                        | `/react-specialist`         |\n| Theming, palette, typography, styled components                                         | `/theme-ui-specialist`      |\n| Complex generics, type transforms, domain types                                         | `/typescript-specialist`    |\n| **After implementing hooks/utilities** (auto-invoked)                                   | `/code-refactor-specialist` |\n\nWhen delegating, inform the user which sub-agent should handle it and why.\n\n**Note:** After implementing hooks or utilities, **auto-invoke `/code-refactor-specialist`** to scan for duplicate hook logic, utility extraction opportunities, and hook composition improvements. It applies changes automatically and produces a refactoring report.\n\n## Technology Stack\n\n- **@ponder/react** (`usePonderQuery`) - Live SSE queries against Ponder indexer\n- **@ponder/client** (`eq`, `and`, `or`, `desc`, `createClient`) - Drizzle-style query operators\n- **ponder** (`onchainTable`, `index`, `relations`) - Schema definition\n- **wagmi v3** - Contract reads/writes (hooks in `src/hooks/blockchain/`)\n- **viem v2** - Low-level Ethereum utilities\n- **@tanstack/react-query v5** - Caching layer (used by both Ponder and wagmi)\n- **unstated-next** (`ChainContainer`) - Global chain/wallet state\n\n### Provider Stack\n\n```\nDynamicContextProvider        (wallet connection UI)\n  WagmiProvider               (wagmi config)\n    QueryClientProvider       (react-query cache)\n      PonderProvider          (live SSE data from @ponder/react)\n        DynamicWagmiConnector (bridges Dynamic <-> wagmi)\n          ChainContainer      (project chain state)\n```\n\n### Ponder Client Setup\n\n```typescript\n// src/services/ponder/ponderClient.ts\nimport { createClient } from \"@ponder/client\";\nimport * as schema from \"./ponder.schema\";\n\nconst PONDER_URL = import.meta.env.VITE_PONDER_URL;\nconst PONDER_SQL_URL = `${PONDER_URL}/sql`;\n\nexport const ponderSqlClient = createClient(PONDER_SQL_URL, { schema });\nexport { schema, PONDER_SQL_URL, PONDER_URL };\n\n// Inferred types from schema\nexport type PonderEntity = typeof schema.yourTable.$inferSelect;\n// ... (all types exported from ponderClient.ts)\n```\n\n## @ponder/react API Reference\n\n### usePonderQuery (Primary Hook)\n\nExecute drizzle-style SQL queries with optional live SSE updates:\n\n```typescript\nimport { usePonderQuery } from \"@ponder/react\";\nimport { eq, and, or, desc } from \"@ponder/client\";\nimport { schema } from \"src/services/ponder/ponderClient\";\n\nconst { data, isLoading, error, refetch } = usePonderQuery({\n  queryFn: (db) =>\n    db\n      .select()\n      .from(schema.yourTable)\n      .where(eq(schema.yourTable.chainId, chainId!))\n      .orderBy(desc(schema.yourTable.createdAt))\n      .limit(50),\n  live: true, // Enable SSE real-time updates (default: true)\n  enabled: !!chainId && supportedChain, // Guard against undefined params\n});\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n| Param | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `queryFn` | `(db) => Promise<Result>` | Drizzle-style query builder callback |\n| `live` | `boolean` | Enable live SSE updates (default: `true`) |\n| `enabled` | `boolean` | Guard condition (like React Query''s `enabled`) |\n| `...rest` | `UseQueryOptions` | Standard TanStack Query options |\n\n**Returns:** Standard TanStack Query result: `{ data, isLoading, error, refetch }`\n\n**Live mode (`live: true`):**\n\n- Subscribes to SSE stream on mount\n- Automatically refetches when new blocks are indexed\n- Unsubscribes on unmount\n- Use for detail views that need real-time updates\n\n**One-shot mode (`live: false`):**\n\n- Single fetch, no SSE subscription\n- Use for list views, rarely-changing data, or expensive queries\n\n### usePonderStatus\n\n```typescript\nimport { usePonderStatus } from \"@ponder/react\";\nconst { data } = usePonderStatus();\n// data: { [chainName]: { block: { number, timestamp } } }\n```\n\n### getPonderQueryOptions / usePonderQueryOptions\n\nBuild reusable TanStack Query options:\n\n```typescript\nimport { usePonderQueryOptions } from \"@ponder/react\";\n\nconst opts = usePonderQueryOptions((db) =>\n  db.select().from(schema.yourTable).limit(10)\n);\n// opts = { queryKey, queryFn } -- pass to useQuery or prefetchQuery\n```\n\n## Core Architecture\n\n### Two-Layer Hook Pattern (Critical)\n\nComponents NEVER use raw Ponder hooks or `useReadContract` directly.\n\n```\n┌─────────────────┐     ┌──────────────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│  Component       │ --> │  Transform Hook       │ --> │ Ponder Hook │\n│  (pages/)        │     │  (hooks/blockchain/)  │     │ (hooks/ponder/)\n│                  │     │                       │     │             │\n│  Consumes typed  │     │  - usePonderQuery     │     │ Raw DB query│\n│  domain objects  │     │  - transformPonder*   │     │ Returns raw │\n└─────────────────┘     └──────────────────────┘     └─────────────┘\n```\n\n**Layer 1: Ponder Hooks** (`src/hooks/ponder/`) -- Raw database queries, minimal processing\n**Layer 2: Transform Hooks** (`src/hooks/blockchain/useGet*Live.ts`) -- Transform to typed domain objects\n\n### When to Create Each Layer\n\n| Need                                 | Create In                             | Pattern                                                        |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| New ponder table query (list view)   | `src/hooks/ponder/usePonder*.ts`      | `usePonderQuery` + `live: false`                               |\n| New ponder table query (detail view) | `src/hooks/ponder/usePonder*.ts`      | `usePonderQuery` + `live: true`                                |\n| New domain object for components     | `src/hooks/blockchain/useGet*Live.ts` | Import ponder hook + `transformPonder*` + `useMemo`            |\n| New contract read                    | `src/hooks/blockchain/useGet*.ts`     | `useReadContract` or `useReadContracts`                        |\n| New contract write                   | `src/hooks/blockchain/use[Action].ts` | `useSimulateContractWithAccount` + `useContractWriteWithState` |\n\n### ChainContainer & Address Safety\n\nAlways use `ChainContainer.useContainer()` for chain/wallet state, never wagmi directly. See `.claude/docs/project-rules.md` for address safety patterns (non-null assertion with enabled guards, nullAddress for fallbacks).\n\n## Drizzle Query Operators\n\nAvailable from `@ponder/client`:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  eq,\n  and,\n  or,\n  desc,\n  asc,\n  gt,\n  gte,\n  lt,\n  lte,\n  ne,\n  like,\n  inArray,\n  isNull,\n  isNotNull,\n} from \"@ponder/client\";\n\n// Basic equality\ndb.select().from(schema.entity).where(eq(schema.entity.id, entityId!));\n\n// Multiple conditions\ndb.select()\n  .from(schema.event)\n  .where(\n    and(\n      eq(schema.event.user, address!.toLowerCase()),\n      eq(schema.event.eventType, \"action\")\n    )\n  );\n\n// OR condition\ndb.select()\n  .from(schema.event)\n  .where(\n    or(\n      eq(schema.event.sourceId, sourceId),\n      eq(schema.event.targetId, targetId)\n    )\n  );\n\n// Ordering + pagination\ndb.select().from(schema.entity).orderBy(desc(schema.entity.createdAt)).limit(50);\n```\n\n### Ponder Entity ID Convention\n\nAll ponder entities use composite string IDs: `{chainId}-{address}` (lowercase)\n\n```typescript\nconst entityId = `${chainId}-${entityAddress.toLowerCase()}`;\n```\n\n## Debugging Checklist\n\nWhen ponder data isn''t working:\n\n1. **Check `enabled` guard** -- Is the query actually running? Log the `enabled` value\n2. **Check entity ID format** -- Must be `{chainId}-{address.toLowerCase()}`\n3. **Check `live` setting** -- Detail views should use `live: true`; list views typically `live: false`\n4. **Check schema table name** -- Verify the table exists in `ponder.schema.ts`\n5. **Check chain support** -- Is `supportedChain` true?\n6. **Check Ponder indexer status** -- Use `usePonderStatus()` to verify indexing\n7. **Check React Query cache** -- Open React Query Devtools in dev mode\n8. **Check transform function** -- If data loads but display is wrong, check `transformPonder*` in `src/types/`\n\nWhen contract reads fail:\n\n1. **Check ABI** -- Is the correct ABI imported from `src/services/contracts/generated.ts`?\n2. **Check contract address** -- Is it the right address for the current chain?\n3. **Check `enabled` guard** -- Are all required params defined?\n4. **Check chain** -- Is `chainId` from `ChainContainer` matching the contract''s chain?\n\n## Development Workflow\n\n### Creating a New Ponder Hook\n\n1. Check if a similar hook already exists in `src/hooks/ponder/`\n2. Create `src/hooks/ponder/usePonder[Entity].ts`\n3. Import `usePonderQuery`, operators from `@ponder/client`, `schema` from ponderClient\n4. Use `ChainContainer` for `chainId` and `supportedChain`\n5. Add proper `enabled` guard\n6. Choose `live: true` (detail views) or `live: false` (lists)\n7. Export from `src/hooks/ponder/index.ts`\n\n### Creating a New Transform Hook\n\n1. Create `src/hooks/blockchain/useGet[Entity]Live.ts`\n2. Use `usePonderQuery` directly (or import the ponder hook)\n3. Transform data with `transformPonder*` from `src/types/`\n4. Wrap transform in `useMemo` for referential stability\n5. Return typed domain object\n\n### Creating a New Write Hook\n\n1. Create `src/hooks/blockchain/use[Action].ts`\n2. Follow the simulate -> write -> state machine pattern\n3. See `.claude/skills/wagmi-specialist/hook-reference.md` for the complete write pattern\n4. Invalidate relevant queries on success\n\n### Verification\n\nAlways run after code changes:\n\n```bash\nyarn typecheck && yarn lint && yarn prettier && yarn build\n```\n\n## What NOT to Do\n\n- Never use raw Ponder hooks in components -- always use transform hooks\n- Never use `useReadContract` in components -- create hooks in `src/hooks/blockchain/`\n- Never use `useMutation` for blockchain transactions -- use wagmi''s write pattern\n- Never forget `useMemo` around transform operations in hooks\n- Never skip `enabled` guards on queries or hardcode chain IDs\n\nSee `.claude/docs/project-rules.md` for the full project conventions list.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:47:57.212Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents requiring advanced blockchain implementation capabilities, particularly those leveraging Ponder, Wagmi, and React Query","zh":"适合需要高级区块链实现能力的AI代理，特别是那些利用Ponder、Wagmi和React Query的代理","ja":"Ponder、Wagmi、React Queryを利用する高度なブロックチェーン実装機能を必要とするAIエージェントに最適","ko":"Ponder, Wagmi, React Query를 활용하는 고급 블록체인 구현 기능이 필요한 AI 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA que requieren capacidades de implementación de blockchain avanzadas, particularmente aquellos que utilizan Ponder, Wagmi y React Query","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA nécessitant des capacités de mise en œuvre de blockchain avancées, en particulier ceux qui utilisent Ponder, Wagmi et React Query","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents, die erweiterte Blockchain-Implementierungsfähigkeiten erfordern, insbesondere solche, die Ponder, Wagmi und React Query nutzen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA que requerem capacidades avançadas de implementação de blockchain, particularmente aqueles que utilizam Ponder, Wagmi e React Query","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, требующих передовых возможностей реализации блокчейна, особенно тех, которые используют Ponder, Wagmi и React Query","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكيين الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة لتنفيذ التكنولوجيا المحسنة، ولا سيما أولئك الذين يستخدمون Ponder و Wagmi و React Query"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to orchestrate complex blockchain functionality, including contract reads, contract writes, and Ponder-indexer queries, while delegating specialized tasks to sub-agents like ponder-schema-specialist and wagmi-specialist, utilizing protocols such as Web3","zh":"赋予代理编排复杂的区块链功能的能力，包括合约读取、合约写入和Ponder索引器查询，同时将专门的任务委托给子代理，如ponder-schema-specialist和wagmi-specialist，利用Web3协议","ja":"Ponder索引器のクエリなど、複雑なブロックチェーン機能のオーケストレーションをエージェントに可能にし、ponder-schema-specialistやwagmi-specialistなどのサブエージェントに特化したタスクを委任し、Web3プロトコルを利用する","ko":"에이전트가 복잡한 블록체인 기능을 오케스트레이션할 수 있도록 하며, 이는 계약 읽기, 계약 쓰기, Ponder 인덱서 쿼리 등을 포함하며, Ponder 스키마 전문가 및 Wagmi 전문가와 같은 하위 에이전트에게 특화된 작업을 위임하고 Web3 프로토콜을 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a orquestar funcionalidades de blockchain complejas, incluyendo lecturas de contrato, escrituras de contrato y consultas de Ponder-indexer, mientras delega tareas especializadas a subagentes como ponder-schema-specialist y wagmi-specialist, utilizando protocolos como Web3","fr":"Permet aux agents d''orchestrer des fonctionnalités de blockchain complexes, notamment la lecture de contrats, l''écriture de contrats et les requêtes Ponder-indexer, tout en déléguant des tâches spécialisées à des sous-agents tels que ponder-schema-specialist et wagmi-specialist, en utilisant des protocoles tels que Web3","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, komplexe Blockchain-Funktionalitäten zu orchestrieren, einschließlich Vertragslektüren, Vertragsschreibungen und Ponder-Indexer-Abfragen, während spezielle Aufgaben an Subagenten wie ponder-schema-specialist und wagmi-specialist delegiert werden, unter Verwendung von Protokollen wie Web3","pt":"Habilita os agentes a orquestrar funcionalidades de blockchain complexas, incluindo leituras de contrato, escritas de contrato e consultas de Ponder-indexer, enquanto delega tarefas especializadas a subagentes como ponder-schema-specialist e wagmi-specialist, utilizando protocolos como Web3","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью оркестрировать сложную функциональность блокчейна, включая чтение контрактов, запись контрактов и запросы Ponder-indexer, а также делегирует специализированные задачи субагентам, таким как ponder-schema-specialist и wagmi-specialist, используя протоколы, такие как Web3","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تنسيق وظائف blockchain معقدة، بما في ذلك قراءة العقد، وكتابته، واستفسارات Ponder-indexer، في حين تفويض المهام المتخصصة إلى وكلاء فرعيين مثل ponder-schema-specialist و wagmi-specialist، باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل Web3"},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing smart contract interactions","Debugging data flow issues in blockchain applications","Integrating Ponder-indexer queries for data retrieval","Orchestrating sub-agents for specialized blockchain tasks"],"zh":["实现智能合约交互","调试区块链应用中的数据流问题","集成Ponder索引器查询以检索数据","编排子代理以执行专门的区块链任务"],"ja":["スマートコントラクトの相互作用の実装","ブロックチェーンアプリケーションのデータフローの問題のデバッグ","データの取得のためのPonderインデクサクエリの統合","サブエージェントのオーケストレーションによる特化されたブロックチェーンタスクの実行"],"ko":["스마트 계약 상호 작용 구현","블록체인 애플리케이션의 데이터 흐름 문제 디버깅","데이터检索를 위한 Ponder 인덱서 쿼리 통합","하위 에이전트의 오케스트레이션을 통한 특화된 블록체인 작업 수행"],"es":["Implementación de interacciones de contratos inteligentes","Depuración de problemas de flujo de datos en aplicaciones de blockchain","Integración de consultas de Ponder-indexer para recuperación de datos","Orquestación de subagentes para tareas de blockchain especializadas"],"fr":["Mise en œuvre d''interactions de contrats intelligents","Débogage des problèmes de flux de données dans les applications de blockchain","Intégration de requêtes Ponder-indexer pour la récupération de données","Orchestration de sous-agents pour des tâches de blockchain spécialisées"],"de":["Implementierung von Smart-Contract-Interaktionen","Fehlerbehebung bei Datenflussproblemen in Blockchain-Anwendungen","Integration von Ponder-Indexer-Abfragen zur Datenerfassung","Orchestrierung von Subagenten für spezielle Blockchain-Aufgaben"],"pt":["Implementação de interações de contrato inteligente","Depuração de problemas de fluxo de dados em aplicações de blockchain","Integração de consultas de Ponder-indexer para recuperação de dados","Orquestração de subagentes para tarefas de blockchain especializadas"],"ru":["Реализация взаимодействия с умными контрактами","Отладка проблем потока данных в приложениях блокчейна","Интеграция запросов Ponder-indexer для извлечения данных","Оркестрирование субагентов для специализированных задач блокчейна"],"ar":["تنفيذ تفاعلات العقد الذكية","تصحيح أخطاء تدفق البيانات في تطبيقات blockchain","دمج استفسارات Ponder-indexer لاسترجاع البيانات","تنسيق الوكلاء الفرعيين لأداء مهام blockchain المتخصصة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires coordination with sub-agents like ponder-schema-specialist and wagmi-specialist","Limited to blockchain functionality","Dependent on Web3 protocol compatibility"],"zh":["需要与子代理如ponder-schema-specialist和wagmi-specialist进行协调","仅限于区块链功能","依赖于Web3协议的兼容性"],"ja":["ponder-schema-specialistやwagmi-specialistなどのサブエージェントとの調整が必要","ブロックチェーン機能に限定される","Web3プロトコルの互換性に依存する"],"ko":["ponder-schema-전문가 및 Wagmi 전문가와 같은 하위 에이전트와의 조정 필요","블록체인 기능으로 제한됨","Web3 프로토콜 호환성에 의존"],"es":["Requiere coordinación con subagentes como ponder-schema-specialist y wagmi-specialist","Limitado a funcionalidades de blockchain","Dependiente de la compatibilidad del protocolo Web3"],"fr":["Nécessite une coordination avec des sous-agents tels que ponder-schema-specialist et wagmi-specialist","Limité aux fonctionnalités de blockchain","Dépendant de la compatibilité du protocole Web3"],"de":["Erfordert Koordination mit Subagenten wie ponder-schema-specialist und wagmi-specialist","Begrenzt auf Blockchain-Funktionalitäten","Abhängig von der Kompatibilität des Web3-Protokolls"],"pt":["Exige coordenação com subagentes como ponder-schema-specialist e wagmi-specialist","Limitado à funcionalidade de blockchain","Dependente da compatibilidade do protocolo Web3"],"ru":["Требует координации с субагентами, такими как ponder-schema-specialist и wagmi-specialist","Ограничен функциональностью блокчейна","Зависит от совместимости протокола Web3"],"ar":["يتطلب تنسيقا مع الوكلاء الفرعيين مثل ponder-schema-specialist و wagmi-specialist","محدود بالوظائف blockchain","يعتمد على توافق بروتوكول Web3"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('outseta/outseta-vibe-coding-CMS/convex', 'community', 'outseta', 'outseta-vibe-coding-CMS', 'outseta/outseta-vibe-coding-CMS', 'convex', 0, 0, 80, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.412Z', '2026-02-18T03:48:14.313Z', NULL, '{"id":"outseta/outseta-vibe-coding-CMS/convex","name":"convex","description":{"zh":"Convex是一个Proof of Concept（POC）项目，展示了Outseta的集成，用于身份验证、CRM和计费。以下是Convex的指南，包括新函数语法和HTTP端点语法","ja":"Convexは、Outsetaの統合を示したProof of Concept（POC）プロジェクトです。以下は、Convexのガイドです。新しい関数構文とHTTPエンドポイント構文が含まれています","ko":"Convex는 Outseta의 통합을 보여주는 Proof of Concept(PoC) 프로젝트입니다. 아래는 Convex 가이드이며 새로운 함수 구문과 HTTP 엔드포인트 구문을 포함합니다","es":"Convex es un proyecto de prueba de concepto que demuestra la integración de Outseta para autenticación, CRM y facturación, con una sintaxis de función y endpoint de HTTP específicos.","fr":"Convex est un projet de preuve de concept qui démontre l''intégration d''Outseta pour l''authentification, la gestion de la relation client et la facturation, avec une syntaxe de fonction et un point de terminaison HTTP spécifiques.","de":"Convex ist ein Projekt zur Konzepterprobung, das die Integration von Outseta für Authentifizierung, CRM und Abrechnung demonstriert, mit einer spezifischen Funktions- und HTTP-Endpunktsyntax.","pt":"O Convex é um projeto de demonstração que integra Outseta para autenticação, CRM e faturamento, oferecendo uma nova sintaxe de funções e endpoints HTTP","ru":"Convex - это демонстрационный проект, интегрирующий Outseta для аутентификации, CRM и выставления счетов, предлагающий новую синтаксис функций и HTTP-конечных точек","ar":"Convex هو مشروع لتحقيق概念 يدمج Outseta للتحقق والcrm والفواتير، ويوفر بناء الجملة الجديد للوظائف ونقاط النهاية HTTP","en":"This project is a Proof of Concept (POC) demonstrating the integration of Outseta (for authentication, CRM, and billing)"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Convex集成指南","ja":"Convex統合ガイド","ko":"Convex 통합 가이드","es":"Convex: Integración de Outseta para autenticación y factu...","fr":"Convex: Intégration d''Outseta pour l''authentification et ...","de":"Convex: Outseta-Integration für Authentifizierung und Abr...","pt":"Convex: Integração de Outseta para Autenticação e Faturam...","ru":"Convex: Интеграция Outseta для аутентификации и выставлен...","ar":"Convex: دمج Outseta للتحقق والفواتير","en":"convex"},"description":{"zh":"Convex是一个Proof of Concept（POC）项目，展示了Outseta的集成，用于身份验证、CRM和计费。以下是Convex的指南，包括新函数语法和HTTP端点语法","ja":"Convexは、Outsetaの統合を示したProof of Concept（POC）プロジェクトです。以下は、Convexのガイドです。新しい関数構文とHTTPエンドポイント構文が含まれています","ko":"Convex는 Outseta의 통합을 보여주는 Proof of Concept(PoC) 프로젝트입니다. 아래는 Convex 가이드이며 새로운 함수 구문과 HTTP 엔드포인트 구문을 포함합니다","es":"Convex es un proyecto de prueba de concepto que demuestra la integración de Outseta para autenticación, CRM y facturación, con una sintaxis de función y endp...","fr":"Convex est un projet de preuve de concept qui démontre l''intégration d''Outseta pour l''authentification, la gestion de la relation client et la facturation, a...","de":"Convex ist ein Projekt zur Konzepterprobung, das die Integration von Outseta für Authentifizierung, CRM und Abrechnung demonstriert, mit einer spezifischen F...","pt":"O Convex é um projeto de demonstração que integra Outseta para autenticação, CRM e faturamento, oferecendo uma nova sintaxe de funções e endpoints HTTP","ru":"Convex - это демонстрационный проект, интегрирующий Outseta для аутентификации, CRM и выставления счетов, предлагающий новую синтаксис функций и HTTP-конечны...","ar":"Convex هو مشروع لتحقيق概念 يدمج Outseta للتحقق والcrm والفواتير، ويوفر بناء الجملة الجديد للوظائف ونقاط النهاية HTTP","en":"This project is a Proof of Concept (POC) demonstrating the integration of Outseta (for authentication, CRM, and billing)"},"definition":{"en":"This project is a Proof of Concept (POC) demonstrating the integration of Outseta (for authentication, CRM, and billing)"},"features":{"zh":["新函数语法","HTTP端点语法","Outseta集成","身份验证","CRM","计费"],"ja":["新しい関数構文","HTTPエンドポイント構文","Outseta統合","認証","CRM","請求"],"ko":["新的 함수 구문","HTTP 엔드포인트 구문","Outseta 통합","인증","CRM","청구"],"es":["Integración de Outseta para autenticación y facturación","Sintaxis de función específica","Endpoint de HTTP definidos en convex/http.ts","Decorador httpAction requerido","Soporte para TypeScript"],"fr":["Intégration d''Outseta pour l''authentification et la facturation","Syntaxe de fonction spécifique","Point de terminaison HTTP défini dans convex/http.ts","Décorateur httpAction requis","Prise en charge de TypeScript"],"de":["Integration von Outseta für Authentifizierung und Abrechnung","Spezifische Funktions-Syntax","HTTP-Endpunkt in convex/http.ts definiert","httpAction-Decorator erforderlich","Unterstützung für TypeScript"],"pt":["Integração de Outseta para autenticação e faturamento","Nova sintaxe de funções para Convex","Endpoints HTTP definidos em convex/http.ts","Uso do decorador httpAction para endpoints HTTP","Suporte à linguagem TypeScript"],"ru":["Интеграция Outseta для аутентификации и выставления счетов","Новая синтаксис функций для Convex","HTTP-конечные точки, определенные в convex/http.ts","Использование декоратора httpAction для HTTP-конечных точек","Поддержка языка TypeScript"],"ar":["دمج Outseta للتحقق والفواتير","بناء الجملة الجديد للوظائف Convex","نقاط النهاية HTTP المحددة في convex/http.ts","استخدام زينر httpAction لنقاط النهاية HTTP","دعم لغة TypeScript"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Convex","Outseta","身份验证","CRM","计费","集成","开发","函数语法","HTTP端点"],"ja":["Convex","Outseta","認証","CRM","請求","統合","開発","関数構文","HTTPエンドポイント"],"ko":["Convex","Outseta","인증","CRM","청구","통합","개발","함수 구문","HTTP 엔드포인트"],"es":["Convex","Outseta","autenticación","facturación","CRM","TypeScript","integración","desarrollo de software","tecnologías de desarrollo"],"fr":["Convex","Outseta","authentification","facturation","GRC","TypeScript","intégration","développement de logiciels","technologies de développement"],"de":["Convex","Outseta","Authentifizierung","Abrechnung","CRM","TypeScript","Integration","Software-Entwicklung","Entwicklungs-Technologien"],"pt":["Convex","Outseta","autenticação","faturamento","CRM","TypeScript","HTTP","API","desenvolvimento web"],"ru":["Convex","Outseta","аутентификация","выставление счетов","CRM","TypeScript","HTTP","API","веб-разработка"],"ar":["Convex","Outseta","التحقق","الفواتير","crm","TypeScript","HTTP","API","تطوير الويب"]}},"owner":"outseta","repo":"outseta-vibe-coding-CMS","repoPath":"outseta/outseta-vibe-coding-CMS","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.412Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"convex","description":"Database and Backend logic","bodyPreview":"# Convex guidelines\n\n## Function guidelines\n\n### New function syntax\n\n- ALWAYS use the new function syntax for Convex functions. For example:\n\n```typescript\nimport { query } from \"./_generated/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\nexport const f = query({\n  args: {},\n  returns: v.null(),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    // Function body\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Http endpoint syntax\n\n- HTTP endpoints are defined in `convex/http.ts` and require an `httpAction` decorator. For example:\n\n```types","body":"# Convex guidelines\n\n## Function guidelines\n\n### New function syntax\n\n- ALWAYS use the new function syntax for Convex functions. For example:\n\n```typescript\nimport { query } from \"./_generated/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\nexport const f = query({\n  args: {},\n  returns: v.null(),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    // Function body\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Http endpoint syntax\n\n- HTTP endpoints are defined in `convex/http.ts` and require an `httpAction` decorator. For example:\n\n```typescript\nimport { httpRouter } from \"convex/server\";\nimport { httpAction } from \"./_generated/server\";\nconst http = httpRouter();\nhttp.route({\n  path: \"/echo\",\n  method: \"POST\",\n  handler: httpAction(async (ctx, req) => {\n    const body = await req.bytes();\n    return new Response(body, { status: 200 });\n  }),\n});\n```\n\n- HTTP endpoints are always registered at the exact path you specify in the `path` field. For example, if you specify `/api/someRoute`, the endpoint will be registered at `/api/someRoute`.\n\n### Validators\n\n- Below is an example of an array validator:\n\n```typescript\nimport { mutation } from \"./_generated/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\n\nexport default mutation({\n  args: {\n    simpleArray: v.array(v.union(v.string(), v.number())),\n  },\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    //...\n  },\n});\n```\n\n- Below is an example of a schema with validators that codify a discriminated union type:\n\n```typescript\nimport { defineSchema, defineTable } from \"convex/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\n\nexport default defineSchema({\n  results: defineTable(\n    v.union(\n      v.object({\n        kind: v.literal(\"error\"),\n        errorMessage: v.string(),\n      }),\n      v.object({\n        kind: v.literal(\"success\"),\n        value: v.number(),\n      }),\n    ),\n  ),\n});\n```\n\n- Always use the `v.null()` validator when returning a null value. Below is an example query that returns a null value:\n\n```typescript\nimport { query } from \"./_generated/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\n\nexport const exampleQuery = query({\n  args: {},\n  returns: v.null(),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    console.log(\"This query returns a null value\");\n    return null;\n  },\n});\n```\n\n- Here are the valid Convex types along with their respective validators:\n  Convex Type | TS/JS type | Example Usage | Validator for argument validation and schemas | Notes |\n  | ----------- | ------------| -----------------------| -----------------------------------------------| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n  | Id | string | `doc._id` | `v.id(tableName)` | |\n  | Null | null | `null` | `v.null()` | JavaScript''s `undefined` is not a valid Convex value. Functions the return `undefined` or do not return will return `null` when called from a client. Use `null` instead. |\n  | Int64 | bigint | `3n` | `v.int64()` | Int64s only support BigInts between -2^63 and 2^63-1. Convex supports `bigint`s in most modern browsers. |\n  | Float64 | number | `3.1` | `v.number()` | Convex supports all IEEE-754 double-precision floating point numbers (such as NaNs). Inf and NaN are JSON serialized as strings. |\n  | Boolean | boolean | `true` | `v.boolean()` |\n  | String | string | `\"abc\"` | `v.string()` | Strings are stored as UTF-8 and must be valid Unicode sequences. Strings must be smaller than the 1MB total size limit when encoded as UTF-8. |\n  | Bytes | ArrayBuffer | `new ArrayBuffer(8)` | `v.bytes()` | Convex supports first class bytestrings, passed in as `ArrayBuffer`s. Bytestrings must be smaller than the 1MB total size limit for Convex types. |\n  | Array | Array | `[1, 3.2, \"abc\"]` | `v.array(values)` | Arrays can have at most 8192 values. |\n  | Object | Object | `{a: \"abc\"}` | `v.object({property: value})` | Convex only supports \"plain old JavaScript objects\" (objects that do not have a custom prototype). Objects can have at most 1024 entries. Field names must be nonempty and not start with \"$\" or \"_\". |\n| Record      | Record      | `{\"a\": \"1\", \"b\": \"2\"}` | `v.record(keys, values)`                       | Records are objects at runtime, but can have dynamic keys. Keys must be only ASCII characters, nonempty, and not start with \"$\" or \"\\_\". |\n\n### Function registration\n\n- Use `internalQuery`, `internalMutation`, and `internalAction` to register internal functions. These functions are private and aren''t part of an app''s API. They can only be called by other Convex functions. These functions are always imported from `./_generated/server`.\n- Use `query`, `mutation`, and `action` to register public functions. These functions are part of the public API and are exposed to the public Internet. Do NOT use `query`, `mutation`, or `action` to register sensitive internal functions that should be kept private.\n- You CANNOT register a function through the `api` or `internal` objects.\n- ALWAYS include argument and return validators for all Convex functions. This includes all of `query`, `internalQuery`, `mutation`, `internalMutation`, `action`, and `internalAction`. If a function doesn''t return anything, include `returns: v.null()` as its output validator.\n- If the JavaScript implementation of a Convex function doesn''t have a return value, it implicitly returns `null`.\n\n### Function calling\n\n- Use `ctx.runQuery` to call a query from a query, mutation, or action.\n- Use `ctx.runMutation` to call a mutation from a mutation or action.\n- Use `ctx.runAction` to call an action from an action.\n- ONLY call an action from another action if you need to cross runtimes (e.g. from V8 to Node). Otherwise, pull out the shared code into a helper async function and call that directly instead.\n- Try to use as few calls from actions to queries and mutations as possible. Queries and mutations are transactions, so splitting logic up into multiple calls introduces the risk of race conditions.\n- All of these calls take in a `FunctionReference`. Do NOT try to pass the callee function directly into one of these calls.\n- When using `ctx.runQuery`, `ctx.runMutation`, or `ctx.runAction` to call a function in the same file, specify a type annotation on the return value to work around TypeScript circularity limitations. For example,\n\n```\nexport const f = query({\n  args: { name: v.string() },\n  returns: v.string(),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    return \"Hello \" + args.name;\n  },\n});\n\nexport const g = query({\n  args: {},\n  returns: v.null(),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    const result: string = await ctx.runQuery(api.example.f, { name: \"Bob\" });\n    return null;\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Function references\n\n- Function references are pointers to registered Convex functions.\n- Use the `api` object defined by the framework in `convex/_generated/api.ts` to call public functions registered with `query`, `mutation`, or `action`.\n- Use the `internal` object defined by the framework in `convex/_generated/api.ts` to call internal (or private) functions registered with `internalQuery`, `internalMutation`, or `internalAction`.\n- Convex uses file-based routing, so a public function defined in `convex/example.ts` named `f` has a function reference of `api.example.f`.\n- A private function defined in `convex/example.ts` named `g` has a function reference of `internal.example.g`.\n- Functions can also registered within directories nested within the `convex/` folder. For example, a public function `h` defined in `convex/messages/access.ts` has a function reference of `api.messages.access.h`.\n\n### Api design\n\n- Convex uses file-based routing, so thoughtfully organize files with public query, mutation, or action functions within the `convex/` directory.\n- Use `query`, `mutation`, and `action` to define public functions.\n- Use `internalQuery`, `internalMutation`, and `internalAction` to define private, internal functions.\n\n### Pagination\n\n- Paginated queries are queries that return a list of results in incremental pages.\n- You can define pagination using the following syntax:\n\n```ts\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\nimport { query, mutation } from \"./_generated/server\";\nimport { paginationOptsValidator } from \"convex/server\";\nexport const listWithExtraArg = query({\n  args: { paginationOpts: paginationOptsValidator, author: v.string() },\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    return await ctx.db\n      .query(\"messages\")\n      .filter((q) => q.eq(q.field(\"author\"), args.author))\n      .order(\"desc\")\n      .paginate(args.paginationOpts);\n  },\n});\n```\n\nNote: `paginationOpts` is an object with the following properties:\n\n- `numItems`: the maximum number of documents to return (the validator is `v.number()`)\n- `cursor`: the cursor to use to fetch the next page of documents (the validator is `v.union(v.string(), v.null())`)\n- A query that ends in `.paginate()` returns an object that has the following properties: - page (contains an array of documents that you fetches) - isDone (a boolean that represents whether or not this is the last page of documents) - continueCursor (a string that represents the cursor to use to fetch the next page of documents)\n\n## Validator guidelines\n\n- `v.bigint()` is deprecated for representing signed 64-bit integers. Use `v.int64()` instead.\n- Use `v.record()` for defining a record type. `v.map()` and `v.set()` are not supported.\n\n## Schema guidelines\n\n- Always define your schema in `convex/schema.ts`.\n- Always import the schema definition functions from `convex/server`.\n- System fields are automatically added to all documents and are prefixed with an underscore. The two system fields that are automatically added to all documents are `_creationTime` which has the validator `v.number()` and `_id` which has the validator `v.id(tableName)`.\n- Always include all index fields in the index name. For example, if an index is defined as `[\"field1\", \"field2\"]`, the index name should be \"by_field1_and_field2\".\n- Index fields must be queried in the same order they are defined. If you want to be able to query by \"field1\" then \"field2\" and by \"field2\" then \"field1\", you must create separate indexes.\n\n## Typescript guidelines\n\n- You can use the helper typescript type `Id` imported from ''./\\_generated/dataModel'' to get the type of the id for a given table. For example if there is a table called ''users'' you can use `Id<''users''>` to get the type of the id for that table.\n- If you need to define a `Record` make sure that you correctly provide the type of the key and value in the type. For example a validator `v.record(v.id(''users''), v.string())` would have the type `Record<Id<''users''>, string>`. Below is an example of using `Record` with an `Id` type in a query:\n\n```ts\nimport { query } from \"./_generated/server\";\nimport { Doc, Id } from \"./_generated/dataModel\";\n\nexport const exampleQuery = query({\n  args: { userIds: v.array(v.id(\"users\")) },\n  returns: v.record(v.id(\"users\"), v.string()),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    const idToUsername: Record<Id<\"users\">, string> = {};\n    for (const userId of args.userIds) {\n      const user = await ctx.db.get(\"users\", userId);\n      if (user) {\n        idToUsername[user._id] = user.username;\n      }\n    }\n\n    return idToUsername;\n  },\n});\n```\n\n- Be strict with types, particularly around id''s of documents. For example, if a function takes in an id for a document in the ''users'' table, take in `Id<''users''>` rather than `string`.\n- Always use `as const` for string literals in discriminated union types.\n- When using the `Array` type, make sure to always define your arrays as `const array: Array<T> = [...];`\n- When using the `Record` type, make sure to always define your records as `const record: Record<KeyType, ValueType> = {...};`\n- Always add `@types/node` to your `package.json` when using any Node.js built-in modules.\n\n## Full text search guidelines\n\n- A query for \"10 messages in channel ''#general'' that best match the query ''hello hi'' in their body\" would look like:\n\nconst messages = await ctx.db\n.query(\"messages\")\n.withSearchIndex(\"search_body\", (q) =>\nq.search(\"body\", \"hello hi\").eq(\"channel\", \"#general\"),\n)\n.take(10);\n\n## Query guidelines\n\n- Do NOT use `filter` in queries. Instead, define an index in the schema and use `withIndex` instead.\n- Convex queries do NOT support `.delete()`. Instead, `.collect()` the results, iterate over them, and call `ctx.db.delete(row._id)` on each result.\n- Use `.unique()` to get a single document from a query. This method will throw an error if there are multiple documents that match the query.\n- When using async iteration, don''t use `.collect()` or `.take(n)` on the result of a query. Instead, use the `for await (const row of query)` syntax.\n\n### Ordering\n\n- By default Convex always returns documents in ascending `_creationTime` order.\n- You can use `.order(''asc'')` or `.order(''desc'')` to pick whether a query is in ascending or descending order. If the order isn''t specified, it defaults to ascending.\n- Document queries that use indexes will be ordered based on the columns in the index and can avoid slow table scans.\n\n## Mutation guidelines\n\n- Use `ctx.db.replace` to fully replace an existing document. This method will throw an error if the document does not exist. Syntax: `await ctx.db.replace(''tasks'', taskId, { name: ''Buy milk'', completed: false })`\n- Use `ctx.db.patch` to shallow merge updates into an existing document. This method will throw an error if the document does not exist. Syntax: `await ctx.db.patch(''tasks'', taskId, { completed: true })`\n\n## Action guidelines\n\n- Always add `\"use node\";` to the top of files containing actions that use Node.js built-in modules.\n- Never use `ctx.db` inside of an action. Actions don''t have access to the database.\n- Below is an example of the syntax for an action:\n\n```ts\nimport { action } from \"./_generated/server\";\n\nexport const exampleAction = action({\n  args: {},\n  returns: v.null(),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    console.log(\"This action does not return anything\");\n    return null;\n  },\n});\n```\n\n## Scheduling guidelines\n\n### Cron guidelines\n\n- Only use the `crons.interval` or `crons.cron` methods to schedule cron jobs. Do NOT use the `crons.hourly`, `crons.daily`, or `crons.weekly` helpers.\n- Both cron methods take in a FunctionReference. Do NOT try to pass the function directly into one of these methods.\n- Define crons by declaring the top-level `crons` object, calling some methods on it, and then exporting it as default. For example,\n\n```ts\nimport { cronJobs } from \"convex/server\";\nimport { internal } from \"./_generated/api\";\nimport { internalAction } from \"./_generated/server\";\n\nconst empty = internalAction({\n  args: {},\n  returns: v.null(),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    console.log(\"empty\");\n  },\n});\n\nconst crons = cronJobs();\n\n// Run `internal.crons.empty` every two hours.\ncrons.interval(\"delete inactive users\", { hours: 2 }, internal.crons.empty, {});\n\nexport default crons;\n```\n\n- You can register Convex functions within `crons.ts` just like any other file.\n- If a cron calls an internal function, always import the `internal` object from ''\\_generated/api'', even if the internal function is registered in the same file.\n\n## File storage guidelines\n\n- Convex includes file storage for large files like images, videos, and PDFs.\n- The `ctx.storage.getUrl()` method returns a signed URL for a given file. It returns `null` if the file doesn''t exist.\n- Do NOT use the deprecated `ctx.storage.getMetadata` call for loading a file''s metadata.\n\n                    Instead, query the `_storage` system table. For example, you can use `ctx.db.system.get` to get an `Id<\"_storage\">`.\n\n```\nimport { query } from \"./_generated/server\";\nimport { Id } from \"./_generated/dataModel\";\n\ntype FileMetadata = {\n    _id: Id<\"_storage\">;\n    _creationTime: number;\n    contentType?: string;\n    sha256: string;\n    size: number;\n}\n\nexport const exampleQuery = query({\n    args: { fileId: v.id(\"_storage\") },\n    returns: v.null(),\n    handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n        const metadata: FileMetadata | null = await ctx.db.system.get(\"_storage\", args.fileId);\n        console.log(metadata);\n        return null;\n    },\n});\n```\n\n- Convex storage stores items as `Blob` objects. You must convert all items to/from a `Blob` when using Convex storage.\n\n# Examples:\n\n## Example: chat-app\n\n### Task\n\n```\nCreate a real-time chat application backend with AI responses. The app should:\n- Allow creating users with names\n- Support multiple chat channels\n- Enable users to send messages to channels\n- Automatically generate AI responses to user messages\n- Show recent message history\n\nThe backend should provide APIs for:\n1. User management (creation)\n2. Channel management (creation)\n3. Message operations (sending, listing)\n4. AI response generation using OpenAI''s GPT-4\n\nMessages should be stored with their channel, author, and content. The system should maintain message order\nand limit history display to the 10 most recent messages per channel.\n\n```\n\n### Analysis\n\n1. Task Requirements Summary:\n\n- Build a real-time chat backend with AI integration\n- Support user creation\n- Enable channel-based conversations\n- Store and retrieve messages with proper ordering\n- Generate AI responses automatically\n\n2. Main Components Needed:\n\n- Database tables: users, channels, messages\n- Public APIs for user/channel management\n- Message handling functions\n- Internal AI response generation system\n- Context loading for AI responses\n\n3. Public API and Internal Functions Design:\n   Public Mutations:\n\n- createUser:\n  - file path: convex/index.ts\n  - arguments: {name: v.string()}\n  - returns: v.object({userId: v.id(\"users\")})\n  - purpose: Create a new user with a given name\n- createChannel:\n  - file path: convex/index.ts\n  - arguments: {name: v.string()}\n  - returns: v.object({channelId: v.id(\"channels\")})\n  - purpose: Create a new channel with a given name\n- sendMessage:\n  - file path: convex/index.ts\n  - arguments: {channelId: v.id(\"channels\"), authorId: v.id(\"users\"), content: v.string()}\n  - returns: v.null()\n  - purpose: Send a message to a channel and schedule a response from the AI\n\nPublic Queries:\n\n- listMessages:\n  - file path: convex/index.ts\n  - arguments: {channelId: v.id(\"channels\")}\n  - returns: v.array(v.object({\n    \\_id: v.id(\"messages\"),\n    \\_creationTime: v.number(),\n    channelId: v.id(\"channels\"),\n    authorId: v.optional(v.id(\"users\")),\n    content: v.string(),\n    }))\n  - purpose: List the 10 most recent messages from a channel in descending creation order\n\nInternal Functions:\n\n- generateResponse:\n  - file path: convex/index.ts\n  - arguments: {channelId: v.id(\"channels\")}\n  - returns: v.null()\n  - purpose: Generate a response from the AI for a given channel\n- loadContext:\n  - file path: convex/index.ts\n  - arguments: {channelId: v.id(\"channels\")}\n  - returns: v.array(v.object({\n    \\_id: v.id(\"messages\"),\n    \\_creationTime: v.number(),\n    channelId: v.id(\"channels\"),\n    authorId: v.optional(v.id(\"users\")),\n    content: v.string(),\n    }))\n- writeAgentResponse:\n  - file path: convex/index.ts\n  - arguments: {channelId: v.id(\"channels\"), content: v.string()}\n  - returns: v.null()\n  - purpose: Write an AI response to a given channel\n\n4. Schema Design:\n\n- users\n  - validator: { name: v.string() }\n  - indexes: <none>\n- channels\n  - validator: { name: v.string() }\n  - indexes: <none>\n- messages\n  - validator: { channelId: v.id(\"channels\"), authorId: v.optional(v.id(\"users\")), content: v.string() }\n  - indexes\n    - by_channel: [\"channelId\"]\n\n5. Background Processing:\n\n- AI response generation runs asynchronously after each user message\n- Uses OpenAI''s GPT-4 to generate contextual responses\n- Maintains conversation context using recent message history\n\n### Implementation\n\n#### package.json\n\n```typescript\n{\n  \"name\": \"chat-app\",\n  \"description\": \"This example shows how to build a chat app without authentication.\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"convex\": \"^1.31.2\",\n    \"openai\": \"^4.79.0\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.7.3\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### tsconfig.json\n\n```typescript\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\"DOM\", \"DOM.Iterable\", \"ESNext\"],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"allowSyntheticDefaultImports\": true,\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"forceConsistentCasingInFileNames\": true,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"Bundler\",\n    \"resolveJsonModule\": true,\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\"\n  },\n  \"exclude\": [\"convex\"],\n  \"include\": [\"**/src/**/*.tsx\", \"**/src/**/*.ts\", \"vite.config.ts\"]\n}\n```\n\n#### convex/index.ts\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  query,\n  mutation,\n  internalQuery,\n  internalMutation,\n  internalAction,\n} from \"./_generated/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\nimport OpenAI from \"openai\";\nimport { internal } from \"./_generated/api\";\n\n/**\n * Create a user with a given name.\n */\nexport const createUser = mutation({\n  args: {\n    name: v.string(),\n  },\n  returns: v.id(\"users\"),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    return await ctx.db.insert(\"users\", { name: args.name });\n  },\n});\n\n/**\n * Create a channel with a given name.\n */\nexport const createChannel = mutation({\n  args: {\n    name: v.string(),\n  },\n  returns: v.id(\"channels\"),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    return await ctx.db.insert(\"channels\", { name: args.name });\n  },\n});\n\n/**\n * List the 10 most recent messages from a channel in descending creation order.\n */\nexport const listMessages = query({\n  args: {\n    channelId: v.id(\"channels\"),\n  },\n  returns: v.array(\n    v.object({\n      _id: v.id(\"messages\"),\n      _creationTime: v.number(),\n      channelId: v.id(\"channels\"),\n      authorId: v.optional(v.id(\"users\")),\n      content: v.string(),\n    }),\n  ),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    const messages = await ctx.db\n      .query(\"messages\")\n      .withIndex(\"by_channel\", (q) => q.eq(\"channelId\", args.channelId))\n      .order(\"desc\")\n      .take(10);\n    return messages;\n  },\n});\n\n/**\n * Send a message to a channel and schedule a response from the AI.\n */\nexport const sendMessage = mutation({\n  args: {\n    channelId: v.id(\"channels\"),\n    authorId: v.id(\"users\"),\n    content: v.string(),\n  },\n  returns: v.null(),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    const channel = await ctx.db.get(args.channelId);\n    if (!channel) {\n      throw new Error(\"Channel not found\");\n    }\n    const user = await ctx.db.get(args.authorId);\n    if (!user) {\n      throw new Error(\"User not found\");\n    }\n    await ctx.db.insert(\"messages\", {\n      channelId: args.channelId,\n      authorId: args.authorId,\n      content: args.content,\n    });\n    await ctx.scheduler.runAfter(0, internal.index.generateResponse, {\n      channelId: args.channelId,\n    });\n    return null;\n  },\n});\n\nconst openai = new OpenAI();\n\nexport const generateResponse = internalAction({\n  args: {\n    channelId: v.id(\"channels\"),\n  },\n  returns: v.null(),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    const context = await ctx.runQuery(internal.index.loadContext, {\n      channelId: args.channelId,\n    });\n    const response = await openai.chat.completions.create({\n      model: \"gpt-4o\",\n      messages: context,\n    });\n    const content = response.choices[0].message.content;\n    if (!content) {\n      throw new Error(\"No content in response\");\n    }\n    await ctx.runMutation(internal.index.writeAgentResponse, {\n      channelId: args.channelId,\n      content,\n    });\n    return null;\n  },\n});\n\nexport const loadContext = internalQuery({\n  args: {\n    channelId: v.id(\"channels\"),\n  },\n  returns: v.array(\n    v.object({\n      role: v.union(v.literal(\"user\"), v.literal(\"assistant\")),\n      content: v.string(),\n    }),\n  ),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    const channel = await ctx.db.get(args.channelId);\n    if (!channel) {\n      throw new Error(\"Channel not found\");\n    }\n    const messages = await ctx.db\n      .query(\"messages\")\n      .withIndex(\"by_channel\", (q) => q.eq(\"channelId\", args.channelId))\n      .order(\"desc\")\n      .take(10);\n\n    const result = [];\n    for (const message of messages) {\n      if (message.authorId) {\n        const user = await ctx.db.get(message.authorId);\n        if (!user) {\n          throw new Error(\"User not found\");\n        }\n        result.push({\n          role: \"user\" as const,\n          content: `${user.name}: ${message.content}`,\n        });\n      } else {\n        result.push({ role: \"assistant\" as const, content: message.content });\n      }\n    }\n    return result;\n  },\n});\n\nexport const writeAgentResponse = internalMutation({\n  args: {\n    channelId: v.id(\"channels\"),\n    content: v.string(),\n  },\n  returns: v.null(),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    await ctx.db.insert(\"messages\", {\n      channelId: args.channelId,\n      content: args.content,\n    });\n    return null;\n  },\n});\n```\n\n#### convex/schema.ts\n\n```typescript\nimport { defineSchema, defineTable } from \"convex/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\n\nexport default defineSchema({\n  channels: defineTable({\n    name: v.string(),\n  }),\n\n  users: defineTable({\n    name: v.string(),\n  }),\n\n  messages: defineTable({\n    channelId: v.id(\"channels\"),\n    authorId: v.optional(v.id(\"users\")),\n    content: v.string(),\n  }).index(\"by_channel\", [\"channelId\"]),\n});\n```\n\n#### convex/tsconfig.json\n\n```typescript\n{\n  /* This TypeScript project config describes the environment that\n   * Convex functions run in and is used to typecheck them.\n   * You can modify it, but some settings required to use Convex.\n   */\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    /* These settings are not required by Convex and can be modified. */\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"Bundler\",\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"allowSyntheticDefaultImports\": true,\n\n    /* These compiler options are required by Convex */\n    \"target\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\"ES2021\", \"dom\"],\n    \"forceConsistentCasingInFileNames\": true,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"./**/*\"],\n  \"exclude\": [\"./_generated\"]\n}\n```\n\n#### src/App.tsx\n\n```typescript\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div>Hello World</div>;\n}\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:48:14.313Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full Stack Agents needing seamless integration of authentication, CRM, and billing using Outseta and Convex.","zh":"非常适合需要Outseta和Convex实现身份验证、CRM和计费无缝集成的全栈代理。","ja":"OutsetaとConvexを使用した認証、CRM、請求のシームレスな統合を必要とするフルスタックエージェントに最適です。","ko":"Outseta와 Convex를 사용하여 인증, CRM, 청구를無縫に 통합해야 하는 풀스택 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes Full Stack que necesitan una integración sin problemas de autenticación, CRM y facturación utilizando Outseta y Convex.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Full Stack qui ont besoin d''une intégration transparente de l''authentification, de la gestion de la relation client et de la facturation à l''aide d''Outseta et de Convex.","de":"Perfekt für Full-Stack-Agents, die eine nahtlose Integration von Authentifizierung, CRM und Abrechnung mit Outseta und Convex benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Full Stack que necessitam de integração perfeita de autenticação, CRM e faturamento usando Outseta e Convex.","ru":"Идеально подходит для полнофункциональных агентов, которым требуется бесшовная интеграция аутентификации, CRM и выставления счетов с помощью Outseta и Convex.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الخدمة الكاملة الذي يحتاج إلى دمج مثالي للتأشير ، وإدارة علاقات العملاء ، وفواتير باستخدام Outseta و Convex."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build scalable serverless applications using Convex functions and HTTP endpoints, leveraging libraries like convex/values and protocols like HTTP, and enables secure authentication and billing through Outseta.","zh":"赋予代理商使用Convex函数和HTTP端点构建可扩展的无服务器应用的能力，利用像convex/values这样的库和像HTTP这样的协议，并通过Outseta实现安全的身份验证和计费。","ja":"Convex関数とHTTPエンドポイントを使用してスケーラブルなサーバーレスアプリケーションを構築する機能をエージェントに与え、convex/valuesのようなライブラリやHTTPのようなプロトコルを利用し、Outsetaを通じて安全な認証や請求を行えるようにします。","ko":"Convex 함수와 HTTP 端점을 사용하여 확장 가능한 서버리스 애플리케이션을 구축할 수 있는 기능을 에이전트에게 부여하며, convex/values 같은 라이브러리와 HTTP 같은 프로토콜을 활용하고, Outseta를 통해 안전한 인증 및 청구를 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear aplicaciones servidoras escalables utilizando funciones Convex y puntos de conexión HTTP, aprovechando bibliotecas como convex/values y protocolos como HTTP, y permite una autenticación y facturación seguras a través de Outseta.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des applications serveur sans serveur escalables en utilisant des fonctions Convex et des points de terminaison HTTP, en exploitant des bibliothèques comme convex/values et des protocoles comme HTTP, et permet une authentification et une facturation sécurisées via Outseta.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, skalierbare serverlose Anwendungen mit Convex-Funktionen und HTTP-Endpunkten zu erstellen, indem sie Bibliotheken wie convex/values und Protokolle wie HTTP nutzen, und ermöglicht eine sichere Authentifizierung und Abrechnung über Outseta.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construírem aplicações sem servidor escaláveis usando funções Convex e endpoints HTTP, aproveitando bibliotecas como convex/values e protocolos como HTTP, e permite autenticação e faturamento seguros por meio do Outseta.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать масштабируемые серверные приложения с использованием функций Convex и конечных точек HTTP, используя библиотеки типа convex/values и протоколы типа HTTP, и обеспечивает безопасную аутентификацию и выставление счетов через Outseta.","ar":"تمكن الوكيل من بناء تطبيقات بدون خادم قابلة للتوسع باستخدام دوال Convex ونقاط النهاية HTTP ، واستخدام المكتبات مثل convex/values وبروتوكولات مثل HTTP ، وتمكين التأشير والفواتير الآمنة من خلال Outseta."},"useCases":{"en":["Defining new Convex functions with query syntax","Creating secure HTTP endpoints with httpAction decorators","Integrating Outseta for authentication and billing"],"zh":["使用查询语法定义新的Convex函数","使用httpAction修饰器创建安全的HTTP端点","集成Outseta用于身份验证和计费"],"ja":["クエリーシンタックスを使用して新しいConvex関数を定義する","httpActionデコレータを使用して安全なHTTPエンドポイントを作成する","Outsetaを認証と請求に統合する"],"ko":["쿼리 구문을 사용하여 새로운 Convex 함수를 정의하는 것","httpAction 데코레이터를 사용하여 보안 HTTP 端점을 생성하는 것","Outseta를 인증 및 청구에 통합하는 것"],"es":["Definir nuevas funciones Convex con sintaxis de consulta","Crear puntos de conexión HTTP seguros con decoradores httpAction","Integrar Outseta para la autenticación y la facturación"],"fr":["Définir de nouvelles fonctions Convex avec une syntaxe de requête","Créer des points de terminaison HTTP sécurisés avec des décorateurs httpAction","Intégrer Outseta pour l''authentification et la facturation"],"de":["Definieren neuer Convex-Funktionen mit Abfragesyntax","Erstellen sicherer HTTP-Endpunkte mit httpAction-Decoratoren","Integrieren von Outseta für Authentifizierung und Abrechnung"],"pt":["Definir novas funções Convex com sintaxe de consulta","Criar pontos de extremidade HTTP seguros com decoradores httpAction","Integrar Outseta para autenticação e faturamento"],"ru":["Определение новых функций Convex с синтаксисом запроса","Создание безопасных конечных точек HTTP с помощью декораторов httpAction","Интеграция Outseta для аутентификации и выставления счетов"],"ar":["تحديد دوال Convex الجديدة بناءً على بناء الجملة الاستعلامي","إنشاء نقاط نهاية HTTP آمنة مع مصفوفات الإجراءات httpAction","دمج Outseta للتأشير والفواتير"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Convex and Outseta setup","Specific to Convex functions and HTTP endpoints"],"zh":["需要Convex和Outseta的设置","仅限Convex函数和HTTP端点"],"ja":["ConvexとOutsetaの設定が必要","Convex関数とHTTPエンドポイントに限定される"],"ko":["Convex와 Outseta 설정이 필요","Convex 함수와 HTTP 端점에만限定"],"es":["Requiere configuración de Convex y Outseta","Específico para funciones Convex y puntos de conexión HTTP"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration Convex et Outseta","Spécifique aux fonctions Convex et aux points de terminaison HTTP"],"de":["Benötigt Convex- und Outseta-Setup","Spezifisch für Convex-Funktionen und HTTP-Endpunkte"],"pt":["Requer configuração do Convex e Outseta","Específico para funções Convex e pontos de extremidade HTTP"],"ru":["Требует настройки Convex и Outseta","Относится конкретно к функциям Convex и конечным точкам HTTP"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد Convex و Outseta","محدد لدوال Convex ونقاط النهاية HTTP"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
