":"Lamport分布式系统是一种基于Swarm并行探测和密码学共识的分布式系统安全评估框架","ja":"Lamport分布システムは、スワームベースの並列探査と暗号論的コンセンサスに基づく分散システムの安全性評価フレームワークです","ko":"Lamport 분산 시스템은 Swarm 병렬 탐색 및 암호학적 합의를 기반으로 하는 분산 시스템 보안 평가 프레임워크입니다","es":"El marco de evaluación de seguridad de comportamiento adversario distribuido para LLM se basa en el trabajo de Leslie Lamport","fr":"Le cadre d''évaluation de sécurité de comportement adversaire distribué pour les LLM repose sur les travaux de Leslie Lamport","de":"Der Rahmen für die Bewertung von Sicherheitsverhalten in verteilten Systemen für LLM basiert auf der Arbeit von Leslie Lamport","pt":"O framework de sistemas distribuídos de Lamport fornece uma abordagem rigorosa para a segurança comportamental adversarial em LLMs","ru":"Фреймворк распределенных систем Лампорта обеспечивает строгий подход к поведенческой безопасности для LLM","ar":"إطار العمل لنظم لامبورت الموزعة يقدم نهجًا صارمًا لتقييم السلوك الأمني في المواد المعرفية الكبيرة","en":"Distributed adversarial behavioral security evaluation framework for LLMs - Swarm-based parallel probing with cryptographic consensus"},"definition":{"en":"Distributed adversarial behavioral security evaluation framework for LLMs - Swarm-based parallel probing with cryptographic consensus"},"features":{"zh":["Swarm并行探测","密码学共识","分布式系统安全评估","Logical Clocks","Paxos协议","TLA+形式规范"],"ja":["スワームベースの並列探査","暗号論的コンセンサス","分散システムの安全性評価","論理時計","Paxos协议","TLA+形式仕様"],"ko":["Swarm 병렬 탐색","암호학적 합의","분산 시스템 보안 평가","논리적 시계","Paxos协议","TLA+ 형식 규격"],"es":["Marco de evaluación de seguridad de comportamiento adversario","Sistemas distribuidos basados en el trabajo de Leslie Lamport","Consenso criptográfico","Pruebas paralelas basadas en enjambres","Especificación formal con TLA+","Relojes lógicos"],"fr":["Cadre d''évaluation de sécurité de comportement adversaire","Systèmes distribués basés sur les travaux de Leslie Lamport","Consensus cryptographique","Tests parallèles basés sur les essaims","Spécification formelle avec TLA+","Horloges logiques"],"de":["Rahmen für die Bewertung von Sicherheitsverhalten","Verteilte Systeme basierend auf der Arbeit von Leslie Lamport","Kryptographischer Konsens","Parallele Tests basierend auf Schwärmen","Formale Spezifikation mit TLA+","Logische Uhren"],"pt":["Enxame de sondagem paralela","Consenso criptográfico","Avaliação de segurança comportamental adversarial","Baseado em relógios lógicos de Lamport","Suporte a especificação formal com TLA+"],"ru":["Параллельное сканирование с использованием роев","Криптографический консенсус","Оценка поведенческой безопасности","Основан на логических часах Лампорта","Поддержка формальной спецификации с TLA+"],"ar":["تماسك سلوكي موزع","إجماع مشفر","تقييم أمني سلوكي","يعتمد على ساعات منطقية لامبورت","دعم مواصفات رسمية مع TLA+"]},"keywords":{"zh":["分布式系统","安全评估","Swarm并行探测","密码学共识","Lamport","Logical Clocks","Paxos协议","TLA+形式规范"],"ja":["分散システム","安全性評価","スワームベースの並列探査","暗号論的コンセンサス","Lamport","論理時計","Paxos协议","TLA+形式仕様"],"ko":["분산 시스템","보안 평가","Swarm 병렬 탐색","암호학적 합의","Lamport","논리적 시계","Paxos协议","TLA+ 형식 규격"],"es":["sistemas distribuidos","seguridad de comportamiento adversario","LLM","Leslie Lamport","consenso criptográfico","pruebas paralelas","TLA+","relojes lógicos","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["systèmes distribués","sécurité de comportement adversaire","LLM","Leslie Lamport","consensus cryptographique","tests parallèles","TLA+","horloges logiques","développement de logiciels"],"de":["verteilte Systeme","Sicherheitsverhalten","LLM","Leslie Lamport","kryptographischer Konsens","parallele Tests","TLA+","logische Uhren","Softwareentwicklung"],"pt":["sistemas distribuídos","segurança comportamental adversarial","LLMs","enxame de sondagem","consenso criptográfico","relógios lógicos","especificação formal","TLA+"],"ru":["распределенные системы","поведенческая безопасность","LLM","параллельное сканирование","криптографический консенсус","логические часы","формальная спецификация","TLA+"],"ar":["نظم موزعة","أمن سلوكي","مواد معرفية كبيرة","تماسك سلوكي","إجماع مشفر","ساعات منطقية","مواصفات رسمية","TLA+"]}},"owner":"copyleftdev","repo":"blsmesh","repoPath":"copyleftdev/blsmesh","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.412Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"lamport-distributed-systems","description":"Design distributed systems using Leslie Lamports rigorous approach. Emphasizes formal reasoning, logical time, consensus protocols, and state machine replication. Use when building systems where correctness under concurrency and partial failure is critical.","bodyPreview":"# Leslie Lamport Style Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nLeslie Lamport transformed distributed systems from ad-hoc engineering into a rigorous science. His work on logical clocks, consensus (Paxos), and formal specification (TLA+) provides the theoretical foundation for nearly every reliable distributed system built today. Turing Award winner (2013).\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\n> \"A distributed system is one in which the failure of a computer you didn''t even know existed can render your own computer unusable.\"\n\n> \"","body":"# Leslie Lamport Style Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nLeslie Lamport transformed distributed systems from ad-hoc engineering into a rigorous science. His work on logical clocks, consensus (Paxos), and formal specification (TLA+) provides the theoretical foundation for nearly every reliable distributed system built today. Turing Award winner (2013).\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\n> \"A distributed system is one in which the failure of a computer you didn''t even know existed can render your own computer unusable.\"\n\n> \"If you''re thinking without writing, you only think you''re thinking.\"\n\n> \"The way to be a good programmer is to write programs, not to learn languages.\"\n\n## Design Principles\n\n1. **Formal Specification First**: Write a precise specification before writing code. If you can''t specify it precisely, you don''t understand it.\n\n2. **Time is Relative**: There is no global clock in a distributed system. Use logical time (happens-before) to reason about ordering.\n\n3. **State Machine Replication**: Any deterministic service can be made fault-tolerant by replicating it as a state machine across multiple servers.\n\n4. **Safety and Liveness**: Separate what must always be true (safety) from what must eventually happen (liveness). Prove both.\n\n5. **Simplicity Through Rigor**: The clearest systems come from precise thinking. Formalism isn''t overhead—it''s the path to simplicity.\n\n## When Designing Systems\n\n### Always\n\n- Write a specification before implementation (TLA+, Alloy, or precise prose)\n- Define the safety properties: what bad things must never happen\n- Define the liveness properties: what good things must eventually happen\n- Reason about all possible interleavings of concurrent operations\n- Use logical timestamps when physical time isn''t reliable\n- Make system state explicit and transitions clear\n- Document invariants that must hold across all states\n\n### Never\n\n- Assume messages arrive in order (unless you''ve proven it)\n- Assume clocks are synchronized (they''re not)\n- Assume failures are independent (they''re often correlated)\n- Hand-wave about \"eventually\" without defining what guarantees that\n- Trust intuition for concurrent systems—prove it or test it exhaustively\n- Confuse the specification with the implementation\n\n### Prefer\n\n- State machines over ad-hoc event handling\n- Logical clocks over physical timestamps for ordering\n- Consensus protocols over optimistic concurrency for critical state\n- Explicit failure handling over implicit assumptions\n- Proved algorithms over clever heuristics\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n### Logical Clocks (Lamport Timestamps)\n\n```\nEach process maintains a counter C:\n1. Before any event, increment C\n2. When sending a message, include C\n3. When receiving a message with timestamp T, set C = max(C, T) + 1\n\nThis gives a partial ordering: if a → b, then C(a) < C(b)\n(But C(a) < C(b) does NOT imply a → b)\n```\n\n### The Happens-Before Relation (→)\n\n```\na → b (a happens before b) if:\n1. a and b are in the same process and a comes before b, OR\n2. a is a send and b is the corresponding receive, OR\n3. There exists c such that a → c and c → b (transitivity)\n\nIf neither a → b nor b → a, events are CONCURRENT.\n```\n\n### State Machine Replication\n\n```\nTo replicate a service:\n1. Model the service as a deterministic state machine\n2. Replicate the state machine across N servers\n3. Use consensus (Paxos/Raft) to agree on the sequence of inputs\n4. Each replica applies inputs in the same order → same state\n\nTolerates F failures with 2F+1 replicas.\n```\n\n### Paxos (Simplified)\n\n```\nThree roles: Proposers, Acceptors, Learners\n\nPhase 1 (Prepare):\n  Proposer sends PREPARE(n) to acceptors\n  Acceptor responds with highest-numbered proposal it accepted (if any)\n  \nPhase 2 (Accept):\n  If proposer receives majority responses:\n    Send ACCEPT(n, v) where v is highest-numbered value seen (or new value)\n  Acceptor accepts if it hasn''t promised to a higher proposal\n\nConsensus reached when majority accept the same (n, v).\n```\n\n## Mental Model\n\nLamport approaches distributed systems as a mathematician:\n\n1. **Define the problem precisely**: What are the inputs, outputs, and allowed behaviors?\n2. **Identify the invariants**: What must always be true?\n3. **Consider all interleavings**: What happens if events occur in any order?\n4. **Prove correctness**: Show that safety and liveness hold.\n5. **Then implement**: The code should be a straightforward translation of the spec.\n\n### The TLA+ Approach\n\n```\n1. Define the state space (all possible states)\n2. Define the initial state predicate\n3. Define the next-state relation (allowed transitions)\n4. Specify safety as invariants (always true)\n5. Specify liveness as temporal properties (eventually true)\n6. Model-check or prove that the spec satisfies properties\n```\n\n## Code Patterns\n\n### Implementing Logical Clocks\n\n```python\nclass LamportClock:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._time = 0\n    \n    def tick(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Increment before local event.\"\"\"\n        self._time += 1\n        return self._time\n    \n    def send_timestamp(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Get timestamp for outgoing message.\"\"\"\n        self._time += 1\n        return self._time\n    \n    def receive(self, msg_timestamp: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Update clock on message receipt.\"\"\"\n        self._time = max(self._time, msg_timestamp) + 1\n        return self._time\n```\n\n### Vector Clocks (for Causality Detection)\n\n```python\nclass VectorClock:\n    def __init__(self, node_id: str, num_nodes: int):\n        self._id = node_id\n        self._clock = {f\"node_{i}\": 0 for i in range(num_nodes)}\n    \n    def tick(self):\n        self._clock[self._id] += 1\n    \n    def send(self) -> dict:\n        self.tick()\n        return self._clock.copy()\n    \n    def receive(self, other: dict):\n        for node, time in other.items():\n            self._clock[node] = max(self._clock.get(node, 0), time)\n        self.tick()\n    \n    def happens_before(self, other: dict) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Returns True if self → other.\"\"\"\n        return all(self._clock[k] <= other.get(k, 0) for k in self._clock) \\\n           and any(self._clock[k] < other.get(k, 0) for k in self._clock)\n```\n\n## Warning Signs\n\nYou''re violating Lamport''s principles if:\n\n- You assume \"this will never happen in practice\" without proof\n- Your distributed algorithm works \"most of the time\"\n- You can''t write down the invariants your system maintains\n- You''re using wall-clock time for ordering in a distributed system\n- You haven''t considered what happens during network partitions\n- Your system has no formal specification\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n- For detailed philosophy, see [philosophy.md](philosophy.md)\n- For references (papers, talks), see [references.md](references.md)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:48:51.313Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents focusing on distributed systems security, such as Cursor and AutoGPT, needing advanced adversarial behavioral evaluation frameworks","zh":"适合专注于分布式系统安全的AI代理，例如Cursor和AutoGPT，需要高级对抗行为评估框架","ja":"分散システムのセキュリティに焦点を当てたAIエージェント、たとえばCursorやAutoGPTなどの、先進的な対抗的行動評価フレームワークを必要とするものに適しています","ko":"분산 시스템 보안에 중점을 둔 AI 에이전트, 즉 커서와 AutoGPT와 같은 고급 적대적 행동 평가 프레임워크가 필요한 경우에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA que se centran en la seguridad de sistemas distribuidos, como Cursor y AutoGPT, que necesitan marcos de evaluación de comportamiento adversario avanzados","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA axés sur la sécurité des systèmes distribués, tels que Cursor et AutoGPT, nécessitant des cadres d''évaluation de comportement adversaire avancés","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents, die sich auf die Sicherheit von verteilten Systemen konzentrieren, wie z.B. Cursor und AutoGPT, die erweiterte Frameworks für die Bewertung von adversarialen Verhaltensweisen benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA que se concentram em segurança de sistemas distribuídos, como Cursor e AutoGPT, necessitando de estruturas de avaliação de comportamento adversário avançadas","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, ориентированных на безопасность распределенных систем, таких как Cursor и AutoGPT, требующих продвинутых рамок оценки поведения противников","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكيل الذكي التي تركز على أمن الأنظمة الموزعة، مثل Cursor و AutoGPT، والتي تحتاج إلى إطارات تقييم سلوك معادي متقدم"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to conduct swarm-based parallel probing with cryptographic consensus, leveraging Leslie Lamport''s work on logical clocks and Paxos for robust distributed system security evaluation, utilizing protocols like TLA+ for formal specification","zh":"赋予代理进行基于群集的并行探测的能力，利用加密共识，利用莱斯利·兰波特关于逻辑时钟和Paxos的工作，用于强大的分布式系统安全评估，利用TLA+等协议进行正式规范","ja":"エージェントに、 крипトグラフィックコンセンサスを利用したスウォームベースの並列プロービングを行う能力を付与し、Leslie Lamportの論理時計とPaxosに関する研究を利用して、分散システムのセキュリティ評価を強化し、TLA+などのプロトコルを利用して正式な仕様を定義する","ko":"에이전트가 암호화 합의를 사용한 스웜 기반 병렬 탐색을 수행할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 강력한 분산 시스템 보안 평가를 انجام하고, 레슬리 램포트의 논리 시계 및 팩소스에 대한 연구를 활용하고, TLA+와 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 공식 사양을 정의합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar pruebas paralelas basadas en enjambres con consenso criptográfico, aprovechando el trabajo de Leslie Lamport sobre relojes lógicos y Paxos para una evaluación robusta de la seguridad de los sistemas distribuidos, utilizando protocolos como TLA+ para la especificación formal","fr":"Permet aux agents de réaliser des tests parallèles basés sur des essaims avec un consensus cryptographique, en exploitant le travail de Leslie Lamport sur les horloges logiques et Paxos pour une évaluation robuste de la sécurité des systèmes distribués, en utilisant des protocoles tels que TLA+ pour la spécification formelle","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, Schwarm-basierte parallele Sondierungen mit kryptographischem Konsens durchzuführen, indem es auf die Arbeit von Leslie Lamport über logische Uhren und Paxos für eine robuste Bewertung der Sicherheit von verteilten Systemen aufbaut, unter Nutzung von Protokollen wie TLA+ für die formale Spezifikation","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar sondagem paralela baseada em enxames com consenso criptográfico, aproveitando o trabalho de Leslie Lamport sobre relógios lógicos e Paxos para avaliação robusta de segurança de sistemas distribuídos, utilizando protocolos como TLA+ para especificação formal","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проводить параллельное исследование на основе роев с криптографическим консенсусом, используя работу Лесли Лампорта по логическим часам и Paxos для прочной оценки безопасности распределенных систем, используя протоколы như TLA+ для формальной спецификации","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إجراء اختبار موازٍ يستند إلى السرب مع إجماع التشفير، مستفيداً من عمل ليلى لامبورت حول الساعات المنطقية وبروتوكول باكسوس لتقييم أمن الأنظمة الموزعة بشكل قوي، باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل TLA+ للتحديد الشكلي"},"useCases":{"en":["Evaluating distributed system security through adversarial behavioral analysis","Conducting parallel probing with cryptographic consensus for enhanced system robustness","Implementing Lamport''s logical clocks for synchronized distributed system operations"],"zh":["通过对抗行为分析评估分布式系统的安全性","利用加密共识进行并行探测以增强系统的强壮性","实现兰波特的逻辑时钟以实现分布式系统的同步操作"],"ja":["対抗的行動分析による分散システムのセキュリティ評価","クリプトグラフィックコンセンサスを用いた並列プロービングによるシステムの頑健性の強化","ランポートの論理時計の実装による分散システムの同期操作"],"ko":["적대적 행동 분석을 통한 분산 시스템 보안 평가","암호화 합의를 사용한 병렬 프로빙을 통해 시스템의 강건성을 강화","랜포트의 논리 시계를 구현하여 분산 시스템의 동기화 작업을 수행"],"es":["Evaluación de la seguridad de los sistemas distribuidos a través del análisis de comportamiento adversario","Realización de pruebas paralelas con consenso criptográfico para una mayor robustez del sistema","Implementación de los relojes lógicos de Lamport para operaciones de sistemas distribuidos sincronizadas"],"fr":["Évaluation de la sécurité des systèmes distribués par l''analyse de comportement adversaire","Réalisation de tests parallèles avec un consensus cryptographique pour une robustesse accrue du système","Mise en œuvre des horloges logiques de Lamport pour des opérations de systèmes distribués synchronisées"],"de":["Bewertung der Sicherheit von verteilten Systemen durch Analyse von adversarialen Verhaltensweisen","Durchführung von parallelen Sondierungen mit kryptographischem Konsens für eine erhöhte Robustheit des Systems","Implementierung der logischen Uhren von Lamport für synchronisierte verteilte Systemoperationen"],"pt":["Avaliar a segurança de sistemas distribuídos por meio de análise de comportamento adversário","Realizar sondagem paralela com consenso criptográfico para robustez de sistema aprimorada","Implementar relógios lógicos de Lamport para operações de sistema distribuído sincronizadas"],"ru":["Оценка безопасности распределенных систем с помощью анализа поведения противников","Проведение параллельного исследования с криптографическим консенсусом для повышения прочности системы","Реализация логических часов Лампорта для синхронизированных операций распределенной системы"],"ar":["تقييم أمن الأنظمة الموزعة من خلال تحليل السلوك المعادي","إجراء اختبار موازٍ مع إجماع التشفير لتعزيز متانة النظام","تنفيذ ساعات منطقية لламبورت للتشغيل المتزامن لأنظمة موزعة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of distributed systems and cryptographic consensus protocols","Dependent on the implementation of TLA+ for formal specification and verification","May necessitate significant computational resources for swarm-based parallel probing"],"zh":["需要理解分布式系统和加密共识协议","依赖于TLA+的正式规范和验证的实现","可能需要大量的计算资源用于基于群集的并行探测"],"ja":["分散システムとクリプトグラフィックコンセンサスプロトコルの理解が必要","TLA+による正式な仕様と検証の実装に依存する","スウォームベースの並列プロービングのため、多大な計算リソースが必要になる可能性がある"],"ko":["분산 시스템 및 암호화 합의 프로토콜에 대한 이해가 필요","TLA+를 통한 공식 사양 및 검증의 구현에 의존","스웜 기반 병렬 프로빙을 위해大量의 컴퓨팅 리소스가 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los sistemas distribuidos y protocolos de consenso criptográficos","Depende de la implementación de TLA+ para la especificación y verificación formales","Puede necesitar recursos computacionales significativos para la prueba paralela basada en enjambres"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des systèmes distribués et des protocoles de consensus cryptographique","Dépend de la mise en œuvre de TLA+ pour la spécification et la vérification formelles","Peut nécessiter des ressources informatiques significatives pour les tests parallèles basés sur des essaims"],"de":["Erfordert ein Verständnis von verteilten Systemen und kryptographischen Konsensprotokollen","Hängt von der Implementierung von TLA+ für die formale Spezifikation und Überprüfung ab","Kann erhebliche Rechenressourcen für die Schwarm-basierte parallele Sondierung erfordern"],"pt":["Requer entendimento de sistemas distribuídos e protocolos de consenso criptográficos","Depende da implementação de TLA+ para especificação e verificação formais","Pode necessitar de recursos computacionais significativos para sondagem paralela baseada em enxames"],"ru":["Требует понимания распределенных систем и криптографических протоколов консенсуса","Зависит от реализации TLA+ для формальной спецификации и верификации","Может потребовать значительных вычислительных ресурсов для параллельного исследования на основе роев"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم الأنظمة الموزعة وبروتوكولات الإجماع التشفيري","يعتمد على تنفيذ TLA+ للتحديد الشكلي والتحقق","يمكن أن يتطلب موارد حسابية كبيرة للاختبار الموازي القائم على السرب"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('tkgally/je-dict-1/example-sentences', 'community', 'tkgally', 'je-dict-1', 'tkgally/je-dict-1', 'example-sentences', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.412Z', '2026-02-18T03:48:38.372Z', NULL, '{"id":"tkgally/je-dict-1/example-sentences","name":"example-sentences","description":{"zh":"本指南定义了日英词典中示例句子的标准，所有词条创建和修订活动必须遵循这些指南","ja":"本ガイドラインでは、日本語英語学習者辞書における例文の標準を定め、すべてのエントリ作成および修正活動はこれに従う必要があります","ko":"이 가이드라인은 일본어 영어 학습자 사전에서 예시 문장의 표준을 정의하며, 모든 항목 생성 및 수정 활동은 이에 따라야 합니다","es":"El skill ''example-sentences'' define los estándares para ejemplos de oraciones en diccionarios de japonés-inglés. Proporciona pautas para la creación y revisión de entradas","fr":"Le skill ''example-sentences'' définit les normes pour les exemples de phrases dans les dictionnaires japonais-anglais. Il fournit des lignes directrices pour la création et la révision des entrées","de":"Der Skill ''example-sentences'' definiert die Standards für Beispielsätze in Japanisch-Englisch-Wörterbüchern. Er bietet Richtlinien für die Erstellung und Überarbeitung von Einträgen","pt":"Este recurso define padrões para frases de exemplo em um dicionário de aprendizes de inglês-japonês, garantindo uma compreensão clara da língua.","ru":"Этот ресурс определяет стандарты для примеров предложений в японско-английском словаре, обеспечивая четкое понимание языка.","ar":"هذا الموارد يحدد معايير للجمل التوضيحية في قاموس لتعلم اللغة الإنجليزية-اليابانية، ويضمن فهمًا واضحًا للغة.","en":"In-progress Japanese-English learner''s dictionary"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"示例句子指南 - 学习日英词典","ja":"例文ガイドライン - 日本語英語学習者辞書","ko":"예시 문장 가이드라인 - 일본어 영어 학습자 사전","es":"Ejemplos de oraciones para diccionarios de japonés-inglés","fr":"Exemples de phrases pour dictionnaires japonais-anglais","de":"Beispielsätze für Japanisch-Englisch-Wörterbücher","pt":"Dicionário de Frases de Exemplo para Aprendizes de Inglês...","ru":"Словарь примеров предложений для изучающих японско-англий...","ar":"قاموس جمل примерية لتعلم اللغة الإنجليزية-اليابانية","en":"example-sentences"},"description":{"zh":"本指南定义了日英词典中示例句子的标准，所有词条创建和修订活动必须遵循这些指南","ja":"本ガイドラインでは、日本語英語学習者辞書における例文の標準を定め、すべてのエントリ作成および修正活動はこれに従う必要があります","ko":"이 가이드라인은 일본어 영어 학습자 사전에서 예시 문장의 표준을 정의하며, 모든 항목 생성 및 수정 활동은 이에 따라야 합니다","es":"El skill ''example-sentences'' define los estándares para ejemplos de oraciones en diccionarios de japonés-inglés. Proporciona pautas para la creación y revisi...","fr":"Le skill ''example-sentences'' définit les normes pour les exemples de phrases dans les dictionnaires japonais-anglais. Il fournit des lignes directrices pour ...","de":"Der Skill ''example-sentences'' definiert die Standards für Beispielsätze in Japanisch-Englisch-Wörterbüchern. Er bietet Richtlinien für die Erstellung und Übe...","pt":"Este recurso define padrões para frases de exemplo em um dicionário de aprendizes de inglês-japonês, garantindo uma compreensão clara da língua.","ru":"Этот ресурс определяет стандарты для примеров предложений в японско-английском словаре, обеспечивая четкое понимание языка.","ar":"هذا الموارد يحدد معايير للجمل التوضيحية في قاموس لتعلم اللغة الإنجليزية-اليابانية، ويضمن فهمًا واضحًا للغة.","en":"In-progress Japanese-English learner''s dictionary"},"definition":{"en":"In-progress Japanese-English learner''s dictionary"},"features":{"zh":["基本和核心级别每个词义至少5个示例句子","通用级别每个词义至少1个示例句子","示例句子用于说明词义的用法","示例句子必须遵循特定的格式和语法","示例句子用于提高词典的准确性和可用性"],"ja":["基本および核心レベルの各意味に少なくとも5つの例文","一般レベルの各意味に少なくとも1つの例文","例文は意味の使い方を示すために使用","例文は特定の形式と文法に従う必要がある","例文は辞書の正確性と使いやすさを向上させるために使用"],"ko":["기본 및 핵심 레벨의 각 의미에 최소 5개의 예시 문장","일반 레벨의 각 의미에 최소 1개의 예시 문장","예시 문장은 의미의 사용법을 보여주기 위해 사용","예시 문장은 특정 형식과 문법을 따라야 함","예시 문장은 사전의 정확성과 사용 편의성을 높이기 위해 사용"],"es":["Estándares para ejemplos de oraciones","Pautas para la creación de entradas","Revisión de entradas existentes","Minimo de 5 ejemplos de oraciones por sentido","Aplicación a los niveles básico y core"],"fr":["Normes pour les exemples de phrases","Lignes directrices pour la création d''entrées","Révision des entrées existantes","Minimum de 5 exemples de phrases par sens","Application aux niveaux de base et core"],"de":["Standards für Beispielsätze","Richtlinien für die Erstellung von Einträgen","Überarbeitung von bestehenden Einträgen","Mindestens 5 Beispielsätze pro Sinn","Anwendung auf die Grund- und Core-Ebenen"],"pt":["Padrões para frases de exemplo","Requisitos mínimos de exemplo por sentido","Tier básico e core com 5 exemplos por sentido","Tier geral com requisitos flexíveis","Melhoria da compreensão da língua"],"ru":["Стандарты для примеров предложений","Минимальные требования к примерам на смысл","Базовый и ядро уровней с 5 примерами на смысл","Общий уровень с гибкими требованиями","Улучшение понимания языка"],"ar":["معايير للجمل التوضيحية","متطلبات мінімية للجمل التوضيحية لكل معنی","المرتبة الأساسية والأساسية مع 5 جمل توضيحية لكل معنی","المرتبة العامة مع متطلبات مرنة","تحسين فهم اللغة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["日英词典","示例句子","词典创建","词典修订","语言学习","日本語","英語"],"ja":["日本語英語学習者辞書","例文","辞書作成","辞書修正","言語学習","日本語","英語"],"ko":["일본어 영어 학습자 사전","예시 문장","사전 생성","사전 수정","언어 학습","일본어","영어"],"es":["diccionarios de japonés-inglés","ejemplos de oraciones","creación de entradas","revisión de entradas","estándares lingüísticos","desarrollo de diccionarios"],"fr":["dictionnaires japonais-anglais","exemples de phrases","création d''entrées","révision d''entrées","normes linguistiques","développement de dictionnaires"],"de":["Japanisch-Englisch-Wörterbücher","Beispielsätze","Erstellung von Einträgen","Überarbeitung von Einträgen","Sprachstandards","Wörterbuchentwicklung"],"pt":["dicionário de frases de exemplo","aprendizes de inglês-japonês","padrões para frases de exemplo","requisitos mínimos de exemplo","tier básico e core","melhoria da compreensão da língua"],"ru":["словарь примеров предложений","изучающие японско-английский","стандарты для примеров предложений","минимальные требования к примерам","базовый и ядро уровней","улучшение понимания языка"],"ar":["قاموس الجمل التوضيحية","تعلم اللغة الإنجليزية-اليابانية","معايير للجمل التوضيحية","متطلبات мінімية للجمل التوضيحية","المرتبة الأساسية والأساسية","تحسين فهم اللغة"]}},"owner":"tkgally","repo":"je-dict-1","repoPath":"tkgally/je-dict-1","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.412Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"example-sentences","description":"Requirements for creating and revising example sentences in je-dict-1. Covers minimum counts, progressive length, vocabulary restrictions by tier, and quality standards.","bodyPreview":"# Example Sentence Guidelines\n\nThis skill defines the standards for example sentences across all dictionary entries. All entry-creation and revision activities must follow these guidelines.\n\n---\n\n## Minimum Example Counts by Tier\n\n### Basic and Core Tiers\n\nEvery sense of every entry in the basic and core tiers must have **at least 5 example sentences**.\n\n| Tier | Minimum Examples per Sense |\n|------|---------------------------|\n| Basic | 5 |\n| Core | 5 |\n\n### General Tier\n\nEvery sense of every e","body":"# Example Sentence Guidelines\n\nThis skill defines the standards for example sentences across all dictionary entries. All entry-creation and revision activities must follow these guidelines.\n\n---\n\n## Minimum Example Counts by Tier\n\n### Basic and Core Tiers\n\nEvery sense of every entry in the basic and core tiers must have **at least 5 example sentences**.\n\n| Tier | Minimum Examples per Sense |\n|------|---------------------------|\n| Basic | 5 |\n| Core | 5 |\n\n### General Tier\n\nEvery sense of every entry in the general tier must have **at least 3 example sentences**.\n\n| Tier | Minimum Examples per Sense |\n|------|---------------------------|\n| General | 3 |\n\n**Multi-sense entries:** The requirements apply per sense. An entry with 3 senses in the basic tier needs at least 15 examples total (5 per sense).\n\n---\n\n## Progressive Length Requirement\n\nExamples within each sense should progress from shorter to longer:\n\n1. **Example 1**: Short and simple - demonstrates the word clearly\n2. **Example 2**: Slightly longer - shows basic context\n3. **Example 3**: Medium length - natural usage with fuller context\n4. **Example 4** (basic/core): Longer sentence with more complex structure\n5. **Example 5** (basic/core): Longest - may consist of 2-3 short sentences or one longer sentence with relative clauses, compound structures, etc.\n\n**Key principle:** Early examples help learners recognize the word; later examples show how the word functions in natural, flowing Japanese.\n\n### Length Guidelines\n\n| Example | Target Length (Japanese) |\n|---------|-------------------------|\n| 1 | 5-15 characters |\n| 2 | 10-20 characters |\n| 3 | 15-30 characters |\n| 4 | 25-45 characters |\n| 5+ | 35-70 characters (or 2-3 short sentences) |\n\nThese are guidelines, not strict rules. Natural expression takes priority over hitting exact character counts.\n\n---\n\n## Vocabulary Restrictions by Tier\n\n### Basic Tier Entries\n\nFor entries in the **basic** vocabulary tier:\n\n| Examples | Vocabulary Restriction |\n|----------|----------------------|\n| 1-2 | **Basic tier only** - Use only words from the basic tier |\n| 3-5 | **Basic + Core tiers** - May use basic and core vocabulary |\n\n**Critical:** Basic tier examples must contain **no general-tier or unlisted vocabulary**. This ensures learners at the basic level can fully understand all examples without encountering unknown words.\n\n### Core Tier Entries\n\nFor entries in the **core** vocabulary tier:\n\n| Examples | Vocabulary Restriction |\n|----------|----------------------|\n| 1-2 | **Basic + Core tiers** - Use only basic or core vocabulary |\n| 3-5 | **No restriction** - May use any vocabulary |\n\n**Recommendation:** Even for unrestricted examples (3-5), avoid vocabulary that is not in the dictionary. Learners should be able to look up any unfamiliar word.\n\n### General Tier Entries\n\nFor entries in the **general** vocabulary tier:\n\n| Examples | Vocabulary Restriction |\n|----------|----------------------|\n| 1-3+ | **No restriction** - May use any vocabulary |\n\n**Recommendation:** Avoid obscure vocabulary not in the dictionary. Use common, natural expressions that learners are likely to encounter.\n\n---\n\n## Vocabulary Tier Verification\n\nWhen creating examples for basic and core tier entries, verify vocabulary tier compliance:\n\n```bash\n# Check if a word is in the dictionary and its tier\npython3 build/check_duplicate.py \"word\" \"reading\"\n```\n\nFor systematic verification during polishing:\n- Read the example sentence\n- Identify all content words (nouns, verbs, adjectives, adverbs)\n- Verify each word is in the appropriate tier\n- Replace non-compliant words with tier-appropriate alternatives\n\n**Common substitution patterns:**\n\n| Non-compliant | Basic alternative | Core alternative |\n|--------------|-------------------|------------------|\n| {購入|こうにゅう}する | {買|か}う | {買|か}う |\n| {使用|しよう}する | {使|つか}う | {使|つか}う |\n| {非常|ひじょう}に | とても | とても/{大変|たいへん} |\n| {困難|こんなん} | {難|むずか}しい | {難|むずか}しい |\n\n---\n\n## Sense Numbers Requirement\n\nEvery example **must** include a `sense_numbers` field linking it to the definition(s) it illustrates.\n\n```json\n\"examples\": [\n  {\n    \"id\": \"00001_word_ex1\",\n    \"japanese\": \"...\",\n    \"english\": \"...\",\n    \"sense_numbers\": [1],\n    \"has_audio\": false,\n    \"notes\": null\n  }\n]\n```\n\n### Rules\n\n- **Single-sense entries**: Use `[1]` for all examples\n- **Multi-sense entries**: Each example must specify which sense(s) it demonstrates\n- **Examples illustrating multiple senses**: Use `[1, 2]` format\n- **Must reference valid senses**: Numbers must match `sense_number` values in definitions\n\n### Distribution for Multi-Sense Entries\n\nFor entries with multiple senses in basic/core tiers:\n- Each sense needs at least 5 examples\n- Distribute examples to cover all senses adequately\n- Some examples may illustrate multiple senses (use `[1, 2]` notation)\n\n---\n\n## Quality Standards\n\n### Essential Requirements\n\n1. **Natural Japanese**: Examples should sound like something a native speaker would say\n2. **Clear context**: The usage should be understandable from the example\n3. **Complete furigana**: All kanji must have `{kanji|reading}` markup\n4. **Accurate translation**: English captures meaning without being overly literal\n\n### Content Quality\n\n1. **First example should be simple** - Demonstrate the word clearly without complexity\n2. **Progress to natural complexity** - Later examples show real-world usage\n3. **Include fixed phrases** - High-frequency collocations aid memory (at least one per sense)\n4. **Show grammatical connections** - Demonstrate how words connect with particles, etc.\n5. **Annotate non-obvious grammar** - Use `notes` field for explanations when needed\n\n### What to Demonstrate\n\nExamples should illustrate:\n- Common collocations and set phrases\n- Typical particle patterns (for verbs)\n- Predicate vs. modifier usage (for adjectives)\n- Register-appropriate contexts\n- Both literal and figurative meanings (if applicable)\n\n---\n\n## Example Format Reference\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"00396_taberu_ex1\",\n  \"japanese\": \"{朝|あさ}ごはんを{食|た}べる。\",\n  \"english\": \"To eat breakfast.\",\n  \"sense_numbers\": [1],\n  \"has_audio\": false,\n  \"notes\": null\n}\n```\n\n### ID Format\n\nPattern: `{entry_id}_ex{N}`\n\n- `entry_id`: The entry''s ID (e.g., `00396_taberu`)\n- `N`: Sequential number starting from 1\n\n### Fields\n\n| Field | Required | Description |\n|-------|----------|-------------|\n| `id` | Yes | Unique example ID |\n| `japanese` | Yes | Japanese sentence with furigana |\n| `english` | Yes | Natural English translation |\n| `sense_numbers` | Yes | Array of sense numbers illustrated |\n| `has_audio` | Yes | Boolean (usually `false`) |\n| `notes` | Yes | Explanatory note or `null` |\n\n---\n\n## Common Issues to Avoid\n\n1. **Adding inline links**: Do NOT add inline word links (⟦...⟧) when creating or revising examples. Links are added in a separate polishing step via `prompts/polish_add_inline_links.md`.\n2. **Missing furigana**: `お金が余った` instead of `お{金|かね}が{余|あま}った`\n3. **Overly literal translations**: \"As for me, I eat sushi\" instead of \"I eat sushi\"\n4. **Wrong sense_numbers**: Example linked to wrong definition\n5. **Unnatural constructions**: Grammatically correct but rarely used patterns\n6. **Vocabulary tier violations**: Using general-tier words in basic-tier examples 1-2\n7. **Insufficient examples**: Not meeting minimum counts per sense\n8. **No length progression**: All examples being similar length\n\n---\n\n## Polishing Checklist for Examples\n\nWhen reviewing or revising examples, verify:\n\n### Count and Distribution\n- [ ] Minimum examples per sense met (5 for basic/core, 3 for general)\n- [ ] All senses have adequate example coverage\n- [ ] Examples are properly distributed across senses\n\n### Progressive Length\n- [ ] Examples progress from shorter to longer within each sense\n- [ ] Final examples are substantially longer or multi-sentence\n\n### Vocabulary Restrictions\n- [ ] Basic tier: Examples 1-2 use only basic vocabulary\n- [ ] Basic tier: Examples 3-5 use only basic+core vocabulary\n- [ ] Core tier: Examples 1-2 use only basic+core vocabulary\n- [ ] No unlisted vocabulary in restricted examples\n\n### Quality\n- [ ] All examples sound natural\n- [ ] All kanji have complete furigana\n- [ ] Translations are accurate and natural\n- [ ] sense_numbers are correct for each example\n- [ ] At least one example shows a common collocation\n- [ ] Grammar patterns are demonstrated clearly\n\n### Format\n- [ ] IDs follow `{entry_id}_ex{N}` pattern\n- [ ] IDs are sequential (ex1, ex2, ex3...)\n- [ ] All required fields present\n- [ ] `has_audio` is accurate\n- [ ] `notes` field present (null if not needed)\n\n---\n\n## Adding Examples to Existing Entries\n\nWhen adding examples to bring an entry into compliance:\n\n1. **Read the existing entry** to understand current examples\n2. **Identify gaps**: Which senses need more examples? What lengths are missing?\n3. **Check vocabulary tier**: Determine what vocabulary can be used\n4. **Write new examples** following progressive length guidelines\n5. **Verify compliance** with all requirements\n6. **Update `modified` timestamp** in metadata\n\n### Example Addition Template\n\nFor a basic-tier entry with one sense needing 5 examples:\n\n```\nExample 1: [short, basic vocab only]\nExample 2: [short-medium, basic vocab only]\nExample 3: [medium, basic+core vocab]\nExample 4: [medium-long, basic+core vocab]\nExample 5: [long or multi-sentence, basic+core vocab]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary Table\n\n| Tier | Min Examples/Sense | Ex 1-2 Vocab | Ex 3+ Vocab |\n|------|-------------------|--------------|-------------|\n| Basic | 5 | Basic only | Basic + Core |\n| Core | 5 | Basic + Core | Any (prefer dictionary words) |\n| General | 3 | Any | Any (prefer dictionary words) |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:48:38.372Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Language Learning Agents needing comprehensive example sentence datasets for Japanese-English translation and dictionary entries.","zh":"非常适合需要全面例句数据集的日英翻译和词典条目的语言学习代理。","ja":"日本語英語翻訳と辞書エントリにための包括的な例文データセットを必要とする言語学習エージェントに最適です。","ko":"일본어-영어 번역 및 사전 항목을 위한 종합적인 예문 데이터 세트가 필요한 언어 학습 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Aprendizaje de Idiomas que necesitan conjuntos de datos de oraciones de ejemplo comprehensivos para la traducción japonés-inglés y entradas de diccionario.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Apprentissage de Langues ayant besoin de jeux de données d''exemples de phrases complets pour la traduction japonais-anglais et les entrées de dictionnaire.","de":"Perfekt für Sprachlernagenten, die umfassende Beispielsatz-Datenbanken für die japanisch-englische Übersetzung und Wörterbucheinträge benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Aprendizado de Línguas que necessitam de conjuntos de dados de frases de exemplo abrangentes para tradução japonês-inglês e entradas de dicionário.","ru":"Идеально для агентов по изучению языков, которым необходимы полные наборы примеровых предложений для японско-английского перевода и словарных статей.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تعلم اللغة التي تحتاج إلى مجموعات بيانات شاملة من الجمل التوضيحية لترجمة اللغة اليابانية إلى الإنجليزية ومواد قواميس"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create and revise dictionary entries with standardized example sentences, ensuring consistency across basic, core, and general tiers, with a minimum of 5 example sentences per sense for enhanced language understanding and generation capabilities using Tier-based guidelines.","zh":"赋予代理创建和修订词典条目以标准化例句的能力，确保基本、核心和一般层次的一致性，每个sense至少有5个例句，以提高语言理解和生成能力，使用分级指南。","ja":"エージェントが辞書エントリを作成・修正し、標準化された例文を使用できるようにし、基本、コア、一般の各層での一貫性を確保し、各senseに最低5つの例文を使用して、言語理解と生成能力を向上させるために、階層化ガイドラインを使用することを推奨します。","ko":"에이전트가 사전 항목을 생성 및 수정하고 표준화된 예문을 사용할 수 있도록 하여 기본, 핵심 및 일반 계층에서 일관성을 보장하고 각 감각에 최소 5개의 예문을 사용하여 언어 이해 및 생성 능력을 향상시키기 위해 계층화된 지침을 사용하는 것을 권장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear y revisar entradas de diccionario con oraciones de ejemplo estandarizadas, garantizando la consistencia en los niveles básico, central y general, con un mínimo de 5 oraciones de ejemplo por sentido para mejorar las capacidades de comprensión y generación del lenguaje utilizando pautas basadas en niveles.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer et de réviser des entrées de dictionnaire avec des phrases exemples standardisées, garantissant la cohérence à travers les niveaux de base, central et général, avec un minimum de 5 phrases exemples par sens pour améliorer les capacités de compréhension et de génération de langage en utilisant des lignes directrices basées sur les niveaux.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Wörterbucheinträge mit standardisierten Beispielsätzen zu erstellen und zu überarbeiten, wodurch Konsistenz über die grundlegenden, Kern- und allgemeinen Ebenen hinweg sichergestellt wird, mit einem Minimum von 5 Beispielsätzen pro Bedeutung für verbesserte Sprachverständnis- und Generierungsfähigkeiten unter Verwendung von ebenebasierten Richtlinien.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar e revisar entradas de dicionário com frases de exemplo padronizadas, garantindo consistência em níveis básico, central e geral, com um mínimo de 5 frases de exemplo por significado para capacidades de compreensão e geração de linguagem aprimoradas usando diretrizes baseadas em níveis.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать и редактировать словарные статьи с унифицированными примерами предложений, обеспечивая согласованность на базовом, ядре и общем уровнях, с минимальным количеством 5 примеров предложений на смысл для улучшения возможностей понимания и генерации языка с использованием руководств, основанных на уровнях.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إنشاء ومراجعة مدخلات القواميس بجمل توضيحية معيارية، ضامنًا الاتساق عبر المستويات الأساسية والأساسية والعامة، مع حد أدنى من 5 جمل توضيحية لكل معنى لتعزيز قدرات فهم اللغة وتوليدها باستخدام إرشادات قائمة على المستويات"},"useCases":{"en":["Generating example sentences for dictionary entries","Standardizing sentence formats across tiers","Enhancing language learning models with diverse example sentences"],"zh":["为词典条目生成例句","在各层次中标准化句子格式","使用多样化的例句增强语言学习模型"],"ja":["辞書エントリの例文を生成する","各層で文書の形式を標準化する","さまざまな例文を使用して言語学習モデルを強化する"],"ko":["사전 항목을 위한 예문을 생성하는 것","계층에서 문장 형식을 표준화하는 것","다양한 예문을 사용하여 언어 학습 모델을 강화하는 것"],"es":["Generar oraciones de ejemplo para entradas de diccionario","Estandarizar formatos de oraciones en diferentes niveles","Mejorar modelos de aprendizaje de lenguaje con oraciones de ejemplo diversas"],"fr":["Générer des phrases exemples pour les entrées de dictionnaire","Standardiser les formats de phrases à travers les niveaux","Améliorer les modèles d''apprentissage de langage avec des phrases exemples diverses"],"de":["Erzeugen von Beispielsätzen für Wörterbucheinträge","Standardisieren von Satzformaten über verschiedene Ebenen hinweg","Verbessern von Sprachlernmodellen mit verschiedenen Beispielsätzen"],"pt":["Geração de frases de exemplo para entradas de dicionário","Padronização de formatos de frases em diferentes níveis","Aprimoramento de modelos de aprendizado de línguas com frases de exemplo diversas"],"ru":["Генерация примеров предложений для словарных статей","Унификация форматов предложений на разных уровнях","Улучшение моделей изучения языков с помощью разнообразных примеров предложений"],"ar":["توليد جمل توضيحية لمدخلات القواميس","توحيد تنسيقات الجمل عبر المستويات","تحسين نماذج تعلم اللغة باستخدام جمل توضيحية متنوعة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to Tier-based minimum example counts","Limited to Japanese-English language pairs","Dictionary entry creation and revision activities must follow predefined guidelines"],"zh":["需要遵循分级的最低例句数量","仅限日英语言对","词典条目创建和修订活动必须遵循预定义的指南"],"ja":["階層化された最低の例文数に従う必要がある","日本語英語言語ペアに限定される","辞書エントリの作成・修正活動は、事前に定義されたガイドラインに従う必要がある"],"ko":["계층화된 최소 예문 수를 따라야 함","일본어-영어 언어 쌍으로 제한됨","사전 항목 생성 및 수정 활동은 사전에 정의된 지침을 따라야 함"],"es":["Requiere adherirse a los recuentos mínimos de ejemplo basados en niveles","Limitado a pares de idiomas japonés-inglés","Las actividades de creación y revisión de entradas de diccionario deben seguir pautas predefinidas"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion aux décomptes minimum d''exemples basés sur les niveaux","Limité aux paires de langues japonais-anglais","Les activités de création et de révision des entrées de dictionnaire doivent suivre des lignes directrices prédéfinies"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung der Mindestbeispielsätze basierend auf Ebenen","Begrenzt auf japanisch-englische Sprachpaare","Die Aktivitäten zur Erstellung und Überarbeitung von Wörterbucheinträgen müssen vorgegebenen Richtlinien folgen"],"pt":["Exige aderência a contagens mínimas de exemplos baseadas em níveis","Limitado a pares de línguas japonês-inglês","Atividades de criação e revisão de entradas de dicionário devem seguir diretrizes pré-definidas"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения минимальных количеств примеров, основанных на уровнях","Ограничен японско-английскими языковыми парами","Деятельность по созданию и редактированию словарных статей должна следовать предопределенным руководствам"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام بعدد الأمثلة الأدنى temel على المستويات","محدود للأزواج اللغوية اليابانية-الإنجليزية","يجب أن تتبع أنشطة إنشاء ومراجعة مدخلات القواميس إرشادات محددة مسبقًا"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
