ill ''manage-skills'' es una herramienta para administrar y auditar habilidades en VRP Toolkit. Permite comparar y validar habilidades para garantizar la ...","fr":"Le skill ''manage-skills'' est un outil pour gérer et auditer les compétences dans VRP Toolkit. Il permet de comparer et de valider les compétences pour garant...","de":"Der Skill ''manage-skills'' ist ein Tool zum Verwalten und Auditen von Fähigkeiten in VRP Toolkit. Es ermöglicht den Vergleich und die Überprüfung von Fähigkei...","pt":"O manage-skills é uma meta-habilidade para gerenciar e manter todas as habilidades do VRP Toolkit.","ru":"Manage-skills - это мета-навык для управления и обслуживания всех навыков VRP Toolkit.","ar":"manage-skills هو مهارة siêuية لادارة وصيانة جميع مهارات أداة VRP.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["审计技能目录","检查技能合规性","生成报告","同步技能状态","维护技能文档"],"ja":["スキルディレクトリの監査","スキルコンプライアンスの確認","レポートの生成","スキルステータスの同期","スキル文書のメンテナンス"],"ko":["스킬 디렉토리 감사","스킬 컴플라이언스 확인","리포트 생성","스킬 상태 동기화","스킬 문서 유지 보수"],"es":["Auditoría de habilidades","Validación de habilidades","Comparación de habilidades","Informe de habilidades","Mantenimiento de habilidades"],"fr":["Audit de compétences","Validation de compétences","Comparaison de compétences","Rapport de compétences","Maintenance de compétences"],"de":["Fähigkeitsaudit","Fähigkeitsvalidierung","Fähigkeitsvergleich","Fähigkeitsbericht","Fähigkeitswartung"],"pt":["Auditoria de habilidades","Validação de conformidade","Manutenção de habilidades","Relatórios de habilidades","Sincronização de habilidades"],"ru":["Аудит навыков","Проверка соответствия","Обслуживание навыков","Отчеты о навыках","Синхронизация навыков"],"ar":["تدقيق المهارات","التحقق من المطابقة","صيانة المهارات","تقارير المهارات","مزامنة المهارات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["VRP Toolkit","技能管理","元技能","审计技能","检查合规性","生成报告"],"ja":["VRP Toolkit","スキル管理","メタスキル","スキルの監査","コンプライアンスの確認","レポートの生成"],"ko":["VRP Toolkit","스킬 관리","메타 스킬","스킬 감사","컴플라이언스 확인","리포트 생성"],"es":["administración de habilidades","auditoría de habilidades","validación de habilidades","VRP Toolkit","desarrollo de habilidades","mantenimiento de habilidades"],"fr":["gestion de compétences","audit de compétences","validation de compétences","VRP Toolkit","développement de compétences","maintenance de compétences"],"de":["Fähigkeitsverwaltung","Fähigkeitsaudit","Fähigkeitsvalidierung","VRP Toolkit","Fähigkeitsentwicklung","Fähigkeitswartung"],"pt":["gerenciar habilidades VRP","auditoria de habilidades","validação de conformidade","manutenção de habilidades","relatórios de habilidades","sincronização de habilidades","VRP Toolkit"],"ru":["управлять навыками VRP","аудит навыков","проверка соответствия","обслуживание навыков","отчеты о навыках","синхронизация навыков","VRP Toolkit"],"ar":["إدارة المهارات VRP","تدقيق المهارات","التحقق من المطابقة","صيانة المهارات","تقارير المهارات","مزامنة المهارات","أداة VRP"]}},"owner":"dudusoar","repo":"VRP-Toolkit","repoPath":"dudusoar/VRP-Toolkit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.413Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"manage-skills","description":"Manage and maintain VRP Toolkit skills through compliance checking, audit tracking, and documentation synchronization. Use when (1) adding or modifying skills, (2) checking skill compliance with project standards, (3) auditing SKILLS.md vs skills directory consistency, (4) recording skill changes to SKILLS_LOG.md, or (5) performing periodic skill health checks. Ensures skills stay independent, under 500 lines, properly structured, and well-documented.","bodyPreview":"# Manage Skills\n\nMeta-skill for managing, auditing, and maintaining all VRP Toolkit skills.\n\n## Core Functions\n\n### 1. Audit Skills Directory\nCompare actual skills in `.claude/skills/` with SKILLS.md documentation.\n\n**Usage:**\n```bash\npython .claude/skills/manage-skills/scripts/audit_skills.py\n```\n\n**Reports:**\n- Skills in directory vs SKILLS.md\n- Missing from documentation\n- Missing from directory\n- Sync status\n\n### 2. Check Skill Compliance\nValidate skills against VRP Toolkit standards.\n\n**Usa","body":"# Manage Skills\n\nMeta-skill for managing, auditing, and maintaining all VRP Toolkit skills.\n\n## Core Functions\n\n### 1. Audit Skills Directory\nCompare actual skills in `.claude/skills/` with SKILLS.md documentation.\n\n**Usage:**\n```bash\npython .claude/skills/manage-skills/scripts/audit_skills.py\n```\n\n**Reports:**\n- Skills in directory vs SKILLS.md\n- Missing from documentation\n- Missing from directory\n- Sync status\n\n### 2. Check Skill Compliance\nValidate skills against VRP Toolkit standards.\n\n**Usage:**\n```bash\n# Check specific skill\npython .claude/skills/manage-skills/scripts/check_compliance.py skill-name\n\n# Check all skills\npython .claude/skills/manage-skills/scripts/check_compliance.py --all\n```\n\n**Checks:**\n- **Independence**: Skill doesn''t embed other skills'' content\n- **Size**: SKILL.md ≤ 500 lines (body, excluding frontmatter)\n- **Structure**: Required files present, no prohibited files\n- **Frontmatter**: Valid YAML with name and description\n- **References**: All reference files mentioned in SKILL.md\n\nSee [compliance_checklist.md](references/compliance_checklist.md) for detailed standards.\n\n### 3. Update SKILLS.md Index\nSync skills documentation in SKILLS.md with actual skills.\n\n**When:**\n- After adding new skill\n- After removing skill\n- After significantly modifying skill description\n\n**See:** [update_procedures.md](references/update_procedures.md) → Section 1\n\n### 4. Record Changes in SKILLS_LOG.md\nLog all skill modifications for tracking and history.\n\n**When:**\n- After any skill change (add/update/remove/rename/split/merge)\n\n**Template:**\n```markdown\n## YYYY-MM-DD - [Action]: [skill-name]\n**Action:** [Added/Updated/Removed/Renamed/Split/Merged]\n**Reason:** [Why this change was made]\n**Changes:**\n- [Specific change 1]\n- [Specific change 2]\n**Compliance Notes:** [Any compliance issues addressed]\n**Impact:** [How this affects other skills or workflows]\n```\n\n**See:** [update_procedures.md](references/update_procedures.md) → Section 2\n\n## Workflow Patterns\n\n### Pattern A: Add New Skill\n```\n1. Create skill using skill-creator\n2. Run: audit_skills.py\n   → Check if new skill appears in directory\n3. Update SKILLS.md skills index (Section 1)\n4. Record in SKILLS_LOG.md\n5. Run: check_compliance.py skill-name\n   → Verify new skill is compliant\n```\n\n### Pattern B: Modify Existing Skill\n```\n1. Make changes to skill\n2. Run: check_compliance.py skill-name\n   → Check for violations (size, independence, etc.)\n3. If issues found, fix them\n4. Update SKILLS.md description if needed\n5. Record changes in SKILLS_LOG.md\n```\n\n### Pattern C: Periodic Audit\n```\n1. Run: audit_skills.py\n   → Check directory vs SKILLS.md sync\n2. Run: check_compliance.py --all\n   → Check all skills for compliance\n3. Review warnings and errors\n4. Plan fixes or improvements\n5. Update SKILLS_LOG.md with findings\n```\n\n### Pattern D: Fix Compliance Issues\n\n**Size Violation (>500 lines):**\n```\n1. Identify extractable sections\n2. Move to references/ or create new skill\n3. Update SKILL.md references\n4. Re-run check_compliance.py\n5. Record in SKILLS_LOG.md\n```\n\n**Independence Violation:**\n```\n1. Find embedded content from other skills\n2. Replace with reference: \"See [skill-name] for...\"\n3. Re-run check_compliance.py\n4. Record in SKILLS_LOG.md\n```\n\nSee [update_procedures.md](references/update_procedures.md) for detailed procedures on:\n- Renaming skills\n- Splitting large skills\n- Merging similar skills\n- Archiving deprecated skills\n\n## Integration with Other Skills\n\n**Works with:**\n- **skill-creator** - Use to create new skills before managing them\n- **update-migration-log** - Similar logging pattern for migrations\n- **update-task-board** - Similar documentation sync pattern\n\n**DO NOT embed workflows from these skills** - Reference them instead.\n\n## Compliance Standards Quick Reference\n\n```yaml\nIndependence:\n  ✓ Can reference other skills: \"See [skill-name] for...\"\n  ✗ Cannot embed workflows from other skills\n\nSize:\n  ✓ SKILL.md ≤ 500 lines (excluding frontmatter)\n  ⚠ Warning at 400 lines\n  ✗ Error at 500 lines\n\nStructure:\n  ✓ Required: SKILL.md with valid frontmatter\n  ✓ Optional: scripts/, references/, assets/\n  ✗ Prohibited: README.md, CHANGELOG.md, etc.\n\nFrontmatter:\n  ✓ Required fields: name, description\n  ✓ Description: 50-200 words with use cases\n  ✗ Extra fields discouraged\n\nReferences:\n  ✓ All refs linked from SKILL.md\n  ✓ Max 1 level deep (no nested dirs)\n  ⚠ Warning if ref >500 lines\n```\n\nFull details: [compliance_checklist.md](references/compliance_checklist.md)\n\n## Files in This Skill\n\n```\nmanage-skills/\n├── SKILL.md                          # This file\n├── scripts/\n│   ├── audit_skills.py              # Directory vs CLAUDE.md audit\n│   └── check_compliance.py          # Compliance validation\n├── references/\n│   ├── compliance_checklist.md      # Detailed compliance standards\n│   └── update_procedures.md         # Step-by-step update procedures\n└── assets/\n    └── SKILLS_LOG_template.md       # Template for SKILLS_LOG.md\n```\n\n## Tips\n\n1. **Run audit after adding skills** - Catches missing documentation immediately\n2. **Check compliance before packaging** - Prevents distribution of non-compliant skills\n3. **Keep SKILLS_LOG.md updated** - Provides history for troubleshooting\n4. **Review warnings seriously** - They often indicate real issues\n5. **Split before 500 lines** - Easier to split at 400 than fix at 600\n\n## Limitations\n\n- Does not automatically fix compliance issues (manual fixes required)\n- Cannot detect semantic overlap between skills (manual review needed)\n- Windows encoding issues with emoji in scripts (uses ASCII fallback)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:51:48.007Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing advanced skill management and auditing capabilities, particularly those utilizing Python and VRP Toolkit standards.","zh":"非常适合需要高级技能管理和审计能力的AI代理，特别是那些使用Python和VRP Toolkit标准的代理。","ja":"PythonとVRP Toolkitの標準を使用するAIエージェントに適しています。高度なスキル管理と監査機能が必要なエージェントに最適です。","ko":"파이썬과 VRP Toolkit 표준을 사용하는 AI 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 고급 스킬 관리 및 감사 기능이 필요한 에이전트에게 이상적입니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que necesitan gestión y auditoría de habilidades avanzadas, particularmente aquellos que utilizan Python y estándares de VRP Toolkit.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA nécessitant une gestion et une audit de compétences avancées, en particulier ceux utilisant Python et les normes VRP Toolkit.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die erweiterte Fähigkeitsmanagement- und Auditfunktionen benötigen, insbesondere solche, die Python und VRP-Toolkit-Standards verwenden.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que necessitam de gerenciamento e auditoria de habilidades avançadas, particularmente aqueles que utilizam Python e padrões do VRP Toolkit.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности управления и аудита навыков, особенно тех, кто использует Python и стандарты VRP Toolkit.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة وتحليل مهارات متقدمة، خاصة أولئك الذين يستخدمون بايثون ومعايير VRP Toolkit."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to efficiently manage and maintain skills by auditing the skills directory, checking skill compliance against VRP Toolkit standards, and generating detailed reports on sync status, missing skills, and validation results using Python scripts like `audit_skills.py`.","zh":"使代理能够通过审计技能目录、检查技能是否符合VRP Toolkit标准以及使用Python脚本（如`audit_skills.py`）生成同步状态、缺失技能和验证结果的详细报告来高效地管理和维护技能。","ja":"エージェントがスキルディレクトリの監査、VRP Toolkitの標準へのスキルコンプライアンスのチェック、およびPythonスクリプト（例：`audit_skills.py`）を使用した同期ステータス、不足しているスキル、検証結果の詳細レポートの生成を行うことで、スキルを効率的に管理および維持できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 스킬 디렉토리의 감사를 통해, VRP Toolkit 표준에 대한 스킬 컴플라이언스의 확인, 및 파이썬 스크립트(`audit_skills.py`와 같은)를 사용한 동기화 상태, 결손 스킬 및 검증 결과의 상세한 보고서 생성을 통해 스킬을 효율적으로 관리하고 유지할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes gestionar y mantener habilidades de manera eficiente mediante la auditoría del directorio de habilidades, la comprobación de la conformidad de las habilidades con los estándares de VRP Toolkit y la generación de informes detallados sobre el estado de sincronización, habilidades que faltan y resultados de validación utilizando scripts de Python como `audit_skills.py`.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer et de maintenir les compétences de manière efficace en auditant le répertoire de compétences, en vérifiant la conformité des compétences aux normes VRP Toolkit et en générant des rapports détaillés sur l''état de synchronisation, les compétences manquantes et les résultats de validation en utilisant des scripts Python comme `audit_skills.py`.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, Fähigkeiten effizient zu verwalten und zu warten, indem sie das Verzeichnis der Fähigkeiten auditen, die Konformität der Fähigkeiten mit den VRP-Toolkit-Standards überprüfen und detaillierte Berichte über den Synchronisierungsstatus, fehlende Fähigkeiten und Validierungsergebnisse unter Verwendung von Python-Skripten wie `audit_skills.py` erstellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar e manter habilidades de forma eficiente, auditando o diretório de habilidades, verificando a conformidade das habilidades com os padrões do VRP Toolkit e gerando relatórios detalhados sobre o status de sincronização, habilidades ausentes e resultados de validação usando scripts Python como `audit_skills.py`.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью эффективно управлять и поддерживать навыки, проводя аудит каталога навыков, проверяя соответствие навыков стандартам VRP Toolkit и генерируя подробные отчеты о статусе синхронизации, отсутствующих навыках и результатах проверки с помощью скриптов Python, таких как `audit_skills.py`.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إدارة المهارات وتحديثها بفعالية من خلال مراجعة دليل المهارات، ومراجعة مطابقة المهارات لمعايير VRP Toolkit، وتوليد تقارير مفصلة حول حالة المزامنة والمهارات المفقودة ونتائج التحقق باستخدام نصوص بايثون مثل `audit_skills.py`."},"useCases":{"en":["Auditing skills directories for consistency with documentation","Validating skills against VRP Toolkit standards for compliance","Generating reports on skill sync status and missing skills"],"zh":["审计技能目录以确保与文档的一致性","验证技能以确保符合VRP Toolkit标准","生成同步状态和缺失技能的报告"],"ja":["ドキュメントとの整合性を確保するためにスキルディレクトリを監査する","VRP Toolkitの標準へのコンプライアンスを確保するためにスキルを検証する","同期ステータスと不足しているスキルのレポートを生成する"],"ko":["문서와의 일관성을 보장하기 위해 스킬 디렉토리를 감사한다","VRP Toolkit 표준에 대한 컴플라이언스를 보장하기 위해 스킬을 검증한다","동기화 상태와 결손 스킬에 대한 보고서를 생성한다"],"es":["Auditoría de directorios de habilidades para la coherencia con la documentación","Validación de habilidades contra estándares de VRP Toolkit para la conformidad","Generación de informes sobre el estado de sincronización de habilidades y habilidades que faltan"],"fr":["Audit des répertoires de compétences pour la cohérence avec la documentation","Validation des compétences contre les normes VRP Toolkit pour la conformité","Génération de rapports sur l''état de synchronisation des compétences et des compétences manquantes"],"de":["Auditing von Fähigkeitsverzeichnissen für die Konsistenz mit der Dokumentation","Validierung von Fähigkeiten gegen VRP-Toolkit-Standards für die Konformität","Erstellung von Berichten über den Synchronisierungsstatus von Fähigkeiten und fehlenden Fähigkeiten"],"pt":["Auditar diretórios de habilidades para consistência com a documentação","Validar habilidades contra padrões do VRP Toolkit para conformidade","Gerar relatórios sobre status de sincronização de habilidades e habilidades ausentes"],"ru":["Провести аудит каталогов навыков на соответствие документации","Проверить навыки на соответствие стандартам VRP Toolkit для соблюдения требований","Генерировать отчеты о статусе синхронизации навыков и отсутствующих навыках"],"ar":["مراجعة دلائل المهارات للتأكد من الاتساق مع الوثائق","التحقق من المهارات مقابل معايير VRP Toolkit للامتثال","توليد تقارير حول حالة مزامنة المهارات والمهارات المفقودة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python environment","Specific to VRP Toolkit skills and standards","Needs access to `.claude/skills/` directory and SKILLS.md documentation"],"zh":["需要Python环境","仅适用于VRP Toolkit技能和标准","需要访问`.claude/skills/`目录和SKILLS.md文档"],"ja":["Python環境が必要","VRP Toolkitのスキルと標準にのみ適用されます","`.claude/skills/`ディレクトリとSKILLS.mdドキュメントへのアクセスが必要"],"ko":["파이썬 환경이 필요합니다","VRP Toolkit의 스킬과 표준에만 적용됩니다","`.claude/skills/` 디렉토리와 SKILLS.md 문서에 대한 액세스가 필요합니다"],"es":["Requiere un entorno Python","Específico para habilidades y estándares de VRP Toolkit","Necesita acceso al directorio `.claude/skills/` y a la documentación SKILLS.md"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Python","Spécifique aux compétences et aux normes VRP Toolkit","Nécessite l''accès au répertoire `.claude/skills/` et à la documentation SKILLS.md"],"de":["Benötigt eine Python-Umgebung","Spezifisch für Fähigkeiten und VRP-Toolkit-Standards","Benötigt Zugriff auf das Verzeichnis `.claude/skills/` und die Dokumentation SKILLS.md"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Python","Específico para habilidades e padrões do VRP Toolkit","Necessita de acesso ao diretório `.claude/skills/` e à documentação SKILLS.md"],"ru":["Требуется среда Python","Относится конкретно к навыкам и стандартам VRP Toolkit","Требуется доступ к каталогу `.claude/skills/` и документации SKILLS.md"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة بايثون","محدد لمهارات ومعايير VRP Toolkit","يحتاج إلى الوصول إلى دليل `.claude/skills/` وتوثيق SKILLS.md"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Light-Brands/planetary-party/brainstorming', 'community', 'Light-Brands', 'planetary-party', 'Light-Brands/planetary-party', 'brainstorming', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.413Z', '2026-02-18T03:51:46.911Z', NULL, '{"id":"Light-Brands/planetary-party/brainstorming","name":"brainstorming","description":{"zh":"头脑风暴技能通过协同设计和开发，帮助您将粗糙的想法转化为完整的设计。","ja":"ブレインストーミングスキルは共同設計と開発を通じて、粗いアイデアを完成した設計に変換するのに役立ちます。","ko":"브레인스토밍 스킬은 협동 설계 및 개발을 통해粗은 아이디어를 완성된 설계로 변환하는 데 도움이 됩니다.","es":"El brainstorming es una técnica para desarrollar ideas a través del diálogo y la exploración de alternativas","fr":"Le brainstorming est une technique pour développer des idées à travers le dialogue et l''exploration d''alternatives","de":"Brainstorming ist eine Technik, um Ideen durch Dialog und alternative Exploration zu entwickeln","pt":"O brainstorming é uma técnica de desenvolvimento de ideias que envolve diálogo colaborativo para explorar alternativas e validar incrementos","ru":"Брейнсторминг - это техника разработки идей, которая включает в себя сотрудничество для изучения альтернатив и проверки","ar":"إطلاق الأفكار هو تقنية لتطوير الأفكار التي تتضمن حوارا تعاونيا لاستكشاف البدائل والتحقق من الصحة","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"头脑风暴技能：协同设计和开发","ja":"ブレインストーミングスキル：共同設計と開発","ko":"브레인스토밍 스킬: 협동 설계 및 개발","es":"Generación de ideas: de conceptos a diseños","fr":"Brainstorming: de l''idée au design","de":"Ideenfindung: von der Idee zum Design","pt":"Brainstorming: Desenvolvimento de Ideias","ru":"Брейнсторминг: Разработка Идей","ar":"إطلاق الأفكار: تطوير الأفكار","en":"brainstorming"},"description":{"zh":"头脑风暴技能通过协同设计和开发，帮助您将粗糙的想法转化为完整的设计。","ja":"ブレインストーミングスキルは共同設計と開発を通じて、粗いアイデアを完成した設計に変換するのに役立ちます。","ko":"브레인스토밍 스킬은 협동 설계 및 개발을 통해粗은 아이디어를 완성된 설계로 변환하는 데 도움이 됩니다.","es":"El brainstorming es una técnica para desarrollar ideas a través del diálogo y la exploración de alternativas","fr":"Le brainstorming est une technique pour développer des idées à travers le dialogue et l''exploration d''alternatives","de":"Brainstorming ist eine Technik, um Ideen durch Dialog und alternative Exploration zu entwickeln","pt":"O brainstorming é uma técnica de desenvolvimento de ideias que envolve diálogo colaborativo para explorar alternativas e validar incrementos","ru":"Брейнсторминг - это техника разработки идей, которая включает в себя сотрудничество для изучения альтернатив и проверки","ar":"إطلاق الأفكار هو تقنية لتطوير الأفكار التي تتضمن حوارا تعاونيا لاستكشاف البدائل والتحقق من الصحة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["协同设计","自然对话","上下文理解","替代方案探索","逐步验证"],"ja":["共同設計","自然な対話","コンテキスト理解","代替案の探索","段階的な検証"],"ko":["협동 설계","자연적인 대화","컨텍스트 이해","대안 탐색","점진적인 검증"],"es":["Diálogo colaborativo","Exploración de alternativas","Validación incremental","Desarrollo de ideas","Toma de decisiones informadas"],"fr":["Dialogue collaboratif","Exploration d''alternatives","Validation incrémentale","Développement d''idées","Prise de décisions éclairées"],"de":["Kollaborativer Dialog","Alternative Exploration","Inkrementale Validierung","Ideenentwicklung","Informierte Entscheidungsfindung"],"pt":["Diálogo colaborativo natural","Exploração de alternativas","Validação incremental","Desenvolvimento de designs completos","Tomada de decisões informadas"],"ru":["Естественное сотрудничество","Изучение альтернатив","Проверка на соответствие","Разработка полноценных дизайнов","Принятие обоснованных решений"],"ar":["حوار تعاوني طبيعي","استكشاف البدائل","التحقق من الصحة بالتدريج","تطوير تصاميم كاملة","اتخاذ قرارات مدروسة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["头脑风暴","协同设计","自然对话","开发过程","设计思维","软件开发","产品设计"],"ja":["ブレインストーミング","共同設計","自然な対話","開発プロセス","デザイン思考","ソフトウェア開発","製品設計"],"ko":["브레인스토밍","협동 설계","자연적인 대화","개발 프로세스","디자인 사고","소프트웨어 개발","제품 설계"],"es":["brainstorming","generación de ideas","desarrollo de ideas","colaboración","toma de decisiones","diseño de productos","innovación"],"fr":["brainstorming","génération d''idées","développement d''idées","collaboration","prise de décisions","conception de produits","innovation"],"de":["brainstorming","ideenfindung","ideenentwicklung","kollaboration","entscheidungsfindung","produktentwicklung","innovation"],"pt":["brainstorming","desenvolvimento de ideias","diálogo colaborativo","design de produtos","tomada de decisões","inovação","criatividade","resolução de problemas"],"ru":["брейнсторминг","разработка идей","сотрудничество","дизайн продукции","принятие решений","инновации","креативность","решение проблем"],"ar":["إطلاق الأفكار","تطوير الأفكار","حوار تعاوني","تصميم المنتجات","اتخاذ القرارات","الابتكار","الابداع","حل المشكلات"]}},"owner":"Light-Brands","repo":"planetary-party","repoPath":"Light-Brands/planetary-party","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.413Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"brainstorming","description":"Use when rough ideas need design before code or multiple approaches","version":"0.2.0","bodyPreview":"<objective>\nTurn rough ideas into fully-formed designs through natural collaborative dialogue. Understand the context, explore alternatives, validate incrementally.\n\nCore principle: Ask questions to understand, present options to explore, validate\nsections to refine. </objective>\n\n<when-to-use>\nUse brainstorming when you have a rough idea but unclear implementation, multiple approaches exist and you need to choose, requirements are fuzzy or incomplete, or design decisions need validation before","body":"<objective>\nTurn rough ideas into fully-formed designs through natural collaborative dialogue. Understand the context, explore alternatives, validate incrementally.\n\nCore principle: Ask questions to understand, present options to explore, validate\nsections to refine. </objective>\n\n<when-to-use>\nUse brainstorming when you have a rough idea but unclear implementation, multiple approaches exist and you need to choose, requirements are fuzzy or incomplete, or design decisions need validation before coding.\n\nSkip for clear mechanical tasks with obvious solutions, well-defined requirements with\nstandard implementations, or simple bug fixes. </when-to-use>\n\n<understanding-context>\nExplore the current project state. Check existing files, documentation, recent commits. Understand what''s already built.\n\nAsk questions one at a time to refine the idea. Use multiple choice when possible -\neasier to answer than open-ended. Focus on understanding purpose (what problem does this\nsolve?), constraints (what limits the solution?), and success criteria (how do we know\nit works?).\n\nOne question per message. If a topic needs more exploration, break it into multiple\nquestions. Don''t overwhelm with a list of questions. </understanding-context>\n\n<exploring-alternatives>\nPropose different approaches with their tradeoffs. Present conversationally, showing all options first before making a recommendation.\n\nExample pattern: \"I see three main approaches:\n\n1. Direct integration - Fast to implement but creates coupling. Good if this is\n   temporary.\n\n2. Event-driven - More flexible, better separation, but adds complexity. Worth it if\n   we''ll extend this.\n\n3. Separate service - Maximum isolation, easier to scale, but operational overhead.\n   Overkill unless we need independent scaling.\n\nI''d recommend #2 (event-driven) because the requirements suggest we''ll add features\nhere, and the loose coupling will make that easier. What do you think?\"\n\nPresent options before recommendation. LLMs process information sequentially - showing\noptions first lets them fully consider each alternative before being influenced by a\nrecommendation. The recommendation comes after all options have been presented.\n\nMake a clear recommendation - pick one approach and explain why it fits best. Don''t\nhedge or suggest combining approaches.\n\nAvoid defaulting to hybrid approaches. Hybrid solutions are rarely the right answer.\nThey often combine the complexity of multiple approaches without clear benefits. Only\nsuggest a hybrid if there''s a specific, compelling reason why a pure approach won''t\nwork.\n\nStructure alternatives clearly - each option should be distinct with clear tradeoffs. If\noptions are too similar, you haven''t explored the design space enough.\n\nExplain the choice criteria - make explicit what factors led to your recommendation\n(simplicity, performance, maintainability, etc.). This helps validate whether the\nrecommendation aligns with priorities.\n\nLet the human partner react after your recommendation. They may have constraints or\npriorities you didn''t consider. </exploring-alternatives>\n\n<presenting-design>\nOnce you understand what you''re building, present the design in small, manageable sections covering architecture and component structure, data flow and state management, error handling and edge cases, and testing approach.\n\nAsk after each section whether it looks right. Be ready to go back and clarify if\nsomething doesn''t make sense.\n\nThis incremental validation catches misunderstandings early before you''ve written a\ncomplete design document. </presenting-design>\n\n<after-validation>\nWrite the validated design to docs/plans/[topic]-design.md. Keep it concise and focused on decisions and rationale, not implementation details.\n\nCommit the design document to git so it''s tracked with the project.\n\nIf continuing to implementation, ask whether to proceed. Set up an isolated workspace\nfor development (git worktree or feature branch). Create a detailed implementation plan\nbreaking the design into concrete tasks. </after-validation>\n\n<key-principles>\nOne question at a time. Don''t list multiple questions. Ask one, get an answer, ask the next.\n\nMultiple choice preferred. \"Should we use events or direct calls?\" is easier than \"How\nshould components communicate?\"\n\nYAGNI ruthlessly. Remove unnecessary features from designs. Build what''s needed, not\nwhat might be needed someday.\n\nExplore alternatives always. Present multiple approaches before settling on one. This\nsurfaces tradeoffs. Choose one clear recommendation - avoid defaulting to hybrid\napproaches which rarely solve the problem well.\n\nIncremental validation. Present design in sections, validate each before continuing.\nDon''t write a complete design then ask for feedback - you might be heading the wrong\ndirection.\n\nBe flexible. When something doesn''t make sense to your partner, go back and clarify.\nDon''t defend the design, refine it. </key-principles>\n\n<common-pitfalls>\nDon''t ask many questions at once. Don''t present a complete design without incremental validation. Don''t skip exploring alternatives. Don''t add features beyond stated requirements. Don''t continue with a design that confuses your partner - go back and clarify first.\n</common-pitfalls>\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:51:46.911Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Conversational Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT needing advanced collaborative dialogue capabilities for design refinement","zh":"适用于 Claude Code 和 AutoGPT 等对话式代理，需要高级协作对话功能来完善设计","ja":"Claude Code や AutoGPT などの会話エージェントに適し、高度な共同対話機能を必要とする設計の洗練化に役立ちます","ko":"클라우드 코드와 오토지피티 같은 대화형 에이전트에 적합하며, 고급 협업 대화 기능을 통해 설계를 정교화하는 데 필요합니다","es":"Ideal para Agentes Conversacionales como Claude Code y AutoGPT que necesitan capacidades de diálogo colaborativo avanzadas para el refinamiento de diseños","fr":"Idéal pour les agents conversationnels comme Claude Code et AutoGPT nécessitant des capacités de dialogue collaboratif avancées pour l''affinement de conception","de":"Ideal für Konversationsagenten wie Claude Code und AutoGPT, die erweiterte kollaborative Dialogfunktionen für die Feinabstimmung von Designs benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Conversação como Claude Code e AutoGPT que necessitam de capacidades de diálogo colaborativo avançadas para refinar projetos","ru":"Идеально для разговорных агентов, таких как Claude Code и AutoGPT, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности сотрудничества в диалоге для совершенствования дизайна","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المحادثين مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT الذين يحتاجون إلى قابليات حوار تعاوني متقدم لتحسين التصميم"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to facilitate natural collaborative dialogue through iterative questioning, presenting options, and validating sections to refine designs, leveraging core principles of contextual understanding and incremental validation, utilizing protocols like natural language processing and human-computer interaction","zh":"能够赋予代理实现自然协作对话的能力，通过迭代提问、呈现选项和验证部分来完善设计，利用上下文理解和逐步验证的核心原则，利用自然语言处理和人机交互等协议","ja":"エージェントが自然な共同対話を促進できるようにし、設計を洗練化するために反復質問、選択肢の提示、セクションの検証を行い、文脈理解と逐次検証の基本原則を利用し、自然言語処理や人間コンピュータ相互作用などのプロトコルを利用する","ko":"에이전트가 자연스러운 협업 대화를 촉진할 수 있도록 하여, 설계를 정교화하기 위해 반복적인 질문, 선택지 제시, 섹션 검증을 수행하며, 문맥 이해와 점진적 검증의 핵심 원리를 활용하고, 자연어 처리와 인간-컴퓨터 상호작용 등 프로토콜을 활용함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a facilitar un diálogo colaborativo natural a través de la pregunta iterativa, la presentación de opciones y la validación de secciones para perfilar diseños, aprovechando los principios básicos de la comprensión contextual y la validación incremental, utilizando protocolos como el procesamiento de lenguaje natural y la interacción humano-computadora","fr":"Permet aux agents de faciliter un dialogue collaboratif naturel à travers des questions itératives, la présentation d''options et la validation de sections pour affiner les conceptions, en exploitant les principes fondamentaux de la compréhension contextuelle et de la validation incrémentale, en utilisant des protocoles tels que le traitement automatique des langues et l''interaction homme-ordinateur","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, ein natürliches kollaboratives Gespräch durch iterative Fragestellung, Darstellung von Optionen und Validierung von Abschnitten zur Feinabstimmung von Entwürfen zu erleichtern, indem es die grundlegenden Prinzipien des kontextuellen Verständnisses und der inkrementellen Validierung nutzt und Protokolle wie die natürliche Sprachverarbeitung und die Mensch-Computer-Interaktion verwendet","pt":"Habilita os agentes a facilitar diálogos colaborativos naturais por meio de questionamento iterativo, apresentação de opções e validação de seções para refinar projetos, aproveitando princípios fundamentais de compreensão contextual e validação incremental, utilizando protocolos como processamento de linguagem natural e interação homem-computador","ru":"Позволяет агентам облегчить естественный сотрудничество в диалоге посредством итеративных вопросов, представления вариантов и проверки разделов для усовершенствования дизайна, используя основные принципы контекстного понимания и пошаговой проверки, используя протоколы, такие как обработка естественного языка и взаимодействие человека с компьютером","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تسهيل الحوار التعاوني الطبيعي من خلال أسئلة متكررة وعرض خيارات وتصديق أقسام لتحسين التصميم، مستفيدا من المبادئ الأساسية للفهم السياقي والتحقق المتزايد، باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل معالجة اللغة الطبيعية وتفاعل الإنسان والحاسوب"},"useCases":{"en":["Refining rough ideas into fully-formed designs","Exploring alternative approaches to implementation","Validating design decisions through incremental refinement"],"zh":["将粗略的想法完善为完整的设计","探索实现的替代方法","通过逐步完善验证设计决策"],"ja":["あやふやなアイデアを完全な設計に洗練化する","実装の代替アプローチを探る","インクリメンタルな洗練化を通じて設計上の決定を検証する"],"ko":["거친 아이디어를 완전한 설계로 정교화하는 것","구현의 대체 방법을 탐색하는 것","점진적인 정교화를 통해 설계 결정의 검증"],"es":["Perfeccionar ideas rudimentarias en diseños completamente formados","Explorar enfoques alternativos para la implementación","Validar las decisiones de diseño a través de la refinación incremental"],"fr":["Affiner les idées rudimentaires en conceptions complètement formées","Explorer des approches alternatives pour la mise en œuvre","Valider les décisions de conception à travers l''affinement incrémental"],"de":["Rohideen in vollständig ausgebildete Entwürfe verfeinern","Alternative Ansätze für die Implementierung erkunden","Entscheidungen zum Entwurf durch inkrementelle Feinabstimmung validieren"],"pt":["Refinamento de ideias vagas em projetos completamente formados","Exploração de abordagens alternativas para implementação","Validação de decisões de projeto por meio de refinamento incremental"],"ru":["Уточнение неясных идей в полностью сформированные проекты","Изучение альтернативных подходов к реализации","Проверка решений по дизайну посредством пошагового усовершенствования"],"ar":["تحسين الأفكار الغامضة إلى تصاميم كاملة","استكشاف نهج بديلة للتطبيق","تحقق من قرارات التصميم من خلال تحسين تدريجي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires clear initial idea or objective","May not be effective with completely undefined or overly broad topics","Dependent on agent''s ability to understand context and ask relevant questions"],"zh":["需要清晰的初始想法或目标","可能不适用于完全未定义或过于宽泛的主题","依赖于代理理解上下文和提出相关问题的能力"],"ja":["明確な初期アイデアまたは目標が必要","完全に定義されていない、または幅広いテーマでは効果的ではない可能性がある","エージェントのコンテキストを理解し、関連する質問を提示する能力に依存する"],"ko":["명확한 초기 아이디어 또는 목적이 필요","완전히 정의되지 않은 또는 너무 넓은 주제에서는 효과적이지 않을 수 있음","에이전트의 문맥을 이해하고 관련된 질문을 제시하는 능력에 의존"],"es":["Requiere una idea o objetivo claro inicial","Puede no ser eficaz con temas completamente indefinidos o demasiado amplios","Depende de la capacidad del agente para comprender el contexto y formular preguntas relevantes"],"fr":["Nécessite une idée ou un objectif clair initial","Peut ne pas être efficace avec des sujets complètement indéfinis ou trop larges","Dépend de la capacité de l''agent à comprendre le contexte et à poser des questions pertinentes"],"de":["Benötigt eine klare anfängliche Idee oder ein Ziel","Kann bei völlig unklaren oder zu weit gefassten Themen nicht wirksam sein","Hängt von der Fähigkeit des Agents ab, den Kontext zu verstehen und relevante Fragen zu stellen"],"pt":["Exige ideia ou objetivo inicial claro","Pode não ser eficaz com tópicos completamente indefinidos ou excessivamente amplos","Depende da capacidade do agente de entender o contexto e fazer perguntas relevantes"],"ru":["Требует четкой первоначальной идеи или цели","Может быть неэффективным с полностью неопределенными или чрезмерно широкими темами","Зависит от способности агента понимать контекст и задавать соответствующие вопросы"],"ar":["يتطلب فكرة أو هدفًا أوليًا واضحًا","قد لا يكون فعالًا مع مواضيع غير محددة تمامًا أو واسعة جدًا","يعتمد على قدرة الوكيل على فهم السياق وطرح الأسئلة ذات الصلة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
