utomatisieren, bevor Pull-Anfragen erstellt werden"],"pt":["Validar código antes do deploy para staging ou produção","Revisar implementações de recursos principais para problemas de qualidade","Testar e verificar código para prontidão para produção","Automatizar processos de validação antes de criar solicitações de pull"],"ru":["Проверять код перед развертыванием в staging или производство","Проверять основные реализации функций на наличие проблем качества","Тестировать и проверять код на готовность к производству","Автоматизировать процессы валидации перед созданием запросов на принятие"],"ar":["التحقق من صحة الكود قبل النشر إلى مرحلة الاستجابة أو الإنتاج","مراجعة تنفيذ الميزات الرئيسية للعثور على مشاكل الجودة","اختبار وفحص الكود لجاهزيته للإنتاج","تأتمة عمليات التحقق قبل إنشاء طلبات السحب"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Node.js 20+ and TypeScript 5.2.2","Specific to Project Conductor''s architecture"],"zh":["需要 Node.js 20+ 和 TypeScript 5.2.2","特定于 Project Conductor 的架构"],"ja":["Node.js 20+ と TypeScript 5.2.2 が必要","Project Conductor のアーキテクチャに特有"],"ko":["노드 js 20 이상과 타입스크립트 5.2.2가 필요","프로젝트 콘덕터의 아키텍처에 특정"],"es":["Requiere Node.js 20+ y TypeScript 5.2.2","Específico para la arquitectura de Project Conductor"],"fr":["Nécessite Node.js 20+ et TypeScript 5.2.2","Spécifique à l''architecture de Project Conductor"],"de":["Benötigt Node.js 20+ und TypeScript 5.2.2","Spezifisch für die Architektur von Project Conductor"],"pt":["Requer Node.js 20+ e TypeScript 5.2.2","Específico para a arquitetura do Project Conductor"],"ru":["Требуется Node.js 20+ и TypeScript 5.2.2","Специфичен для архитектуры Project Conductor"],"ar":["يتطلب Node.js 20+ و TypeScript 5.2.2","محدد لهندسة مشروع Conductor"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('faroukBakari/trader-pro/implementation-reasoning', 'community', 'faroukBakari', 'trader-pro', 'faroukBakari/trader-pro', 'implementation-reasoning', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.413Z', '2026-02-18T03:54:09.456Z', NULL, '{"id":"faroukBakari/trader-pro/implementation-reasoning","name":"implementation-reasoning","description":{"zh":"实现推理AI代理专注于实用编码问题，避免陷入架构设计探索。其核心原则是代理决定如何改变代码，而不是决定什么是正确的设计。","ja":"実装推論AIエージェントは実践的なコード問題に焦点を当て、設計の探索に陥ることを避けます。設計が決定されていない場合、エージェントは事前条件を欠如しており、自己解決するのではなくエスカレーションすべきです。","ko":"구현推론 AI 에이전트는 실제 코드 문제에 집중하여 설계 탐색에 빠지는 것을 피합니다. 설계가 확정되지 않은 경우 에이전트는 사전 조건을 결여하고 있으므로 스스로 해결하는 대신 에스컬레이션해야 합니다.","es":"La implementación de razonamiento es una habilidad que ayuda a los agentes a enfocarse en preocupaciones de codificación prácticas para la API de trading","fr":"La mise en œuvre de la raison est une compétence qui aide les agents à se concentrer sur des préoccupations de codage pratiques pour l''API de trading","de":"Das Implementierungsraisonnement ist eine Fähigkeit, die Agenten hilft, sich auf praktische Codierungsbedenken für die Trading-API zu konzentrieren","pt":"A implementação de raciocínio é uma habilidade que ajuda desenvolvedores a se concentrar em preocupações de codificação práticas, evitando complicações de design. Ela fornece pré-portais de raciocínio, pontos de verificação de materialização e protocolos anti-espiral","ru":"Реализация рассуждений - это навык, который помогает разработчикам сосредоточиться на практических проблемах кодирования, избегая сложностей дизайна. Она предоставляет предварительные ворота рассуждений, контрольные точки материализации и анти-спиральные протоколы","ar":"تنفيذ المنطق هو مهارة تساعد المطورين على التركيز على проблемы الت코يد العملية، وتجنب تعقيدات التصميم. توفر بوابات منطقية مسبقة، نقاط فحص مادي، وبروتوكولات مضادة للدورة","en":"trading-api"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"实现推理：优化代码变更的AI代理","ja":"実装推論：コード変更の最適化AIエージェント","ko":"구현推論: 코드 변경 최적화 AI 에이전트","es":"Implementación de razonamiento para API de trading","fr":"Mise en œuvre de la raison pour l''API de trading","de":"Implementierungsraisonnement für Trading-API","pt":"Implementação de Raciocínio: Otimização de Código","ru":"Реализация рассуждений: оптимизация кода","ar":"تنفيذ المنطق: تحسين الكود","en":"implementation-reasoning"},"description":{"zh":"实现推理AI代理专注于实用编码问题，避免陷入架构设计探索。其核心原则是代理决定如何改变代码，而不是决定什么是正确的设计。","ja":"実装推論AIエージェントは実践的なコード問題に焦点を当て、設計の探索に陥ることを避けます。設計が決定されていない場合、エージェントは事前条件を欠如しており、自己解決するのではなくエスカレーションすべきです。","ko":"구현推론 AI 에이전트는 실제 코드 문제에 집중하여 설계 탐색에 빠지는 것을 피합니다. 설계가 확정되지 않은 경우 에이전트는 사전 조건을 결여하고 있으므로 스스로 해결하는 대신 에스컬레이션해야 합니다.","es":"La implementación de razonamiento es una habilidad que ayuda a los agentes a enfocarse en preocupaciones de codificación prácticas para la API de trading","fr":"La mise en œuvre de la raison est une compétence qui aide les agents à se concentrer sur des préoccupations de codage pratiques pour l''API de trading","de":"Das Implementierungsraisonnement ist eine Fähigkeit, die Agenten hilft, sich auf praktische Codierungsbedenken für die Trading-API zu konzentrieren","pt":"A implementação de raciocínio é uma habilidade que ajuda desenvolvedores a se concentrar em preocupações de codificação práticas, evitando complicações de de...","ru":"Реализация рассуждений - это навык, который помогает разработчикам сосредоточиться на практических проблемах кодирования, избегая сложностей дизайна. Она пре...","ar":"تنفيذ المنطق هو مهارة تساعد المطورين على التركيز على проблемы الت코يد العملية، وتجنب تعقيدات التصميم. توفر بوابات منطقية مسبقة، نقاط فحص مادي، وبروتوكولات مضا...","en":"trading-api"},"definition":{"en":"trading-api"},"features":{"zh":["预推理门槛","物化检查点","反螺旋协议","核心原则"],"ja":["事前推論ゲート","実体化チェックポイント","反螺旋プロトコル","コア原則"],"ko":["사전 推論 게이트","물화 체크 포인트","반 나선 프로토콜","코어 원칙"],"es":["Evita la exploración de diseños arquitectónicos","Proporciona puertas de pre-razonamiento","Incluye puntos de control de materialización","Protocolos anti-espiral","Enfocamiento en preocupaciones de codificación prácticas","Toma de decisiones para cambiar el código"],"fr":["Évite l''exploration de conceptions architecturales","Fournit des portes de pré-raisonnement","Inclut des points de contrôle de matérialisation","Protocoles anti-tourbillon","Concentration sur des préoccupations de codage pratiques","Prise de décision pour modifier le code"],"de":["Verhindert die Exploration von Architekturdesigns","Bietet Vor-Gründe-Schleusen","Enthält Materialisierungs-Checkpoints","Anti-Spiral-Protokolle","Fokussierung auf praktische Codierungsbedenken","Entscheidungen zur Änderung des Codes"],"pt":["Pré-portais de raciocínio","Pontos de verificação de materialização","Protocolos anti-espiral","Otimização de código","Evitação de complicações de design"],"ru":["Предварительные ворота рассуждений","Контрольные точки материализации","Анти-спиральные протоколы","Оптимизация кода","Избежание сложностей дизайна"],"ar":["بوابات منطقية مسبقة","نقاط فحص مادي","بروتوكولات مضادة للدورة","تحسين الكود","تجنب تعقيدات التصميم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["实现推理","AI代理","代码变更","实用编码问题","架构设计探索","预推理门槛","物化检查点","反螺旋协议"],"ja":["実装推論","AIエージェント","コード変更","実践的なコード問題","設計の探索","事前推論ゲート","実体化チェックポイント","反螺旋プロトコル"],"ko":["구현推론","AI 에이전트","코드 변경","실제 코드 문제","설계 탐색","사전 推論 게이트","물화 체크 포인트","반 나선 프로토콜"],"es":["implementación de razonamiento","API de trading","preocupaciones de codificación prácticas","diseño arquitectónico","agentes de implementación","desarrollo de software","ingeniería de software","principios de diseño","patrones de diseño"],"fr":["mise en œuvre de la raison","API de trading","préoccupations de codage pratiques","conception architecturale","agents de mise en œuvre","développement de logiciels","ingénierie de logiciels","principes de conception","modèles de conception"],"de":["Implementierungsraisonnement","Trading-API","praktische Codierungsbedenken","Architekturdesign","Implementierungsagenten","Software-Entwicklung","Software-Ingenieurwesen","Entwurfsprinzipien","Entwurfsmuster"],"pt":["implementação de raciocínio","otimização de código","desenvolvimento de software","codificação prática","evitação de complicações de design","pré-portais de raciocínio","pontos de verificação de materialização"],"ru":["реализация рассуждений","оптимизация кода","разработка программного обеспечения","практическая кодировка","избежание сложностей дизайна","предварительные ворота рассуждений","контрольные точки материализации"],"ar":["تنفيذ المنطق","تحسين الكود","تطوير البرمجيات","الت코يد العملي","تجنب تعقيدات التصميم","بوابات منطقية مسبقة","نقاط فحص مادي"]}},"owner":"faroukBakari","repo":"trader-pro","repoPath":"faroukBakari/trader-pro","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.413Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"implementation-reasoning","description":"Reasoning guardrails preventing design-spiral in implementation. Load when planning implementation or detecting drift","bodyPreview":"# Implementation Reasoning\n\nGuardrails that keep implementation-focused agents reasoning about **practical coding concerns** instead of spiraling into **architectural design exploration**. Provides pre-reasoning gates, materialization checkpoints, and anti-spiral protocols.\n\n**Core principle**: An implementation agent reasons to decide *how to change code* — not *what the right design is*. If the design isn''t settled, the agent lacks a prerequisite and should escalate, not self-solve.\n\n---\n\n## W","body":"# Implementation Reasoning\n\nGuardrails that keep implementation-focused agents reasoning about **practical coding concerns** instead of spiraling into **architectural design exploration**. Provides pre-reasoning gates, materialization checkpoints, and anti-spiral protocols.\n\n**Core principle**: An implementation agent reasons to decide *how to change code* — not *what the right design is*. If the design isn''t settled, the agent lacks a prerequisite and should escalate, not self-solve.\n\n---\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Before entering a planning or analysis phase in a build workflow\n- When a reasoning chain exceeds 3 deliberation steps on the same decision\n- When reasoning starts branching into \"what if\" scenarios about architecture\n- When you notice yourself weighing design alternatives rather than sequencing code changes\n- As a continuous background check during Phase 1 (Discovery) and Phase 2 (Planning)\n\n---\n\n## Methodology\n\n### Phase 1: Pre-Reasoning Gate (Before Thinking)\n\nBefore entering any extended reasoning, answer these **3 materialization questions**:\n\n```\n1. What file(s) will I change?     → Must name concrete paths\n2. What function/class is affected? → Must name specific symbols\n3. What does \"done\" look like?      → Must describe observable outcome (test passes, type checks, behavior change)\n```\n\n**Decision:**\n\n| Result | Action |\n|--------|--------|\n| All 3 answered concretely | Proceed — reasoning is grounded |\n| 1-2 answers are \"TBD\" or vague | Investigate (search/read) to ground them — max 4 tool calls |\n| All 3 are abstract (\"refactor the service layer\", \"fix the mapping\") | **STOP** — prerequisite missing. Escalate: the solution design is insufficiently specified |\n\n### Phase 2: Reasoning Boundary Patrol (During Thinking)\n\nApply these **5 tripwires** continuously during reasoning. If any triggers, execute the prescribed action immediately.\n\n#### Tripwire 1: Design Alternative Detection\n\n**Signal**: You''re comparing 2+ architectural approaches (\"should enrichment happen before or after conversion?\", \"should I add a method to X or Y?\")\n\n**Action**: STOP. This is a design question. Summarize the alternatives in 2-3 sentences and escalate to advisor. Do not pick one.\n\n**Template**:\n```\n⚠️ DESIGN QUESTION DETECTED — not in my scope.\n\nAlternatives identified:\n- Option A: [brief]\n- Option B: [brief]\n\nTrade-off axis: [what makes this hard to decide]\n\n→ Recommend switching to advisor to resolve this design choice before proceeding.\n```\n\n#### Tripwire 2: Speculative Branching\n\n**Signal**: Reasoning contains \"what if...\", \"after reconnection...\", \"in the case where...\", \"edge case when...\" creating hypothetical scenarios beyond the immediate scope.\n\n**Action**: Tag the branch as \"out of scope for this implementation pass\" and continue with the mainline case. Note the edge case for the advisor to evaluate.\n\n**Rule**: An implementation plan covers the **primary path**. Edge cases and failure modes are design concerns unless explicitly scoped in.\n\n#### Tripwire 3: Unbounded Root Cause Exploration\n\n**Signal**: You''ve identified the proximate cause but keep digging into underlying causes (\"the real issue is...\", \"but this is caused by...\", \"which stems from...\").\n\n**Action**: After identifying **one clear root cause**, STOP exploring deeper. If the fix for that cause is clear → plan the fix. If not → the root cause analysis needs advisor-level investigation.\n\n**Budget**: Max 2 cause-depth levels. Beyond that = investigation scope.\n\n#### Tripwire 4: Materialization Failure\n\n**Signal**: After 4+ reasoning steps, you still can''t name *specific files and functions* to change.\n\n**Action**: The problem is insufficiently understood for implementation. Produce what you know as a structured handoff:\n\n```\n📋 IMPLEMENTATION BLOCKED — insufficient specification\n\nWhat I know:\n- [concrete findings so far]\n\nWhat I need to start coding:\n- [specific missing information]\n\n→ Switch to advisor to complete the solution specification.\n```\n\n#### Tripwire 5: Scope Expansion\n\n**Signal**: Your reasoning is adding tasks beyond the original scope (\"I should also fix...\", \"while I''m here...\", \"this also affects...\").\n\n**Action**: Note the expansion in a \"follow-up\" list. Do NOT fold it into the current plan. Apply drift-guard if the expansion is significant.\n\n### Phase 3: Reasoning Shape Enforcement (How to Think)\n\nWhen implementation reasoning IS warranted, enforce this shape:\n\n#### The \"File → Function → Diff\" Funnel\n\n```\nLevel 1: Which files? (paths)\n  └─ Level 2: Which functions/classes in those files? (symbols)\n       └─ Level 3: What changes to those symbols? (pseudo-diff)\n            └─ Level 4: What tests verify the changes? (test names)\n```\n\nEach level MUST complete before the next begins. Do not jump to Level 3 (designing the change) without Level 1-2 (grounding where it happens).\n\n#### Reasoning Verb Filter\n\nUse these verbs in implementation reasoning:\n\n| ✅ Implementation verbs | ❌ Design verbs (escalation signals) |\n|--------------------------|--------------------------------------|\n| Modify, Add, Remove, Rename | Evaluate, Compare, Weigh, Assess |\n| Call, Import, Inject, Wire | Should, Could, Might, Perhaps |\n| Test, Assert, Mock, Stub | Consider, Explore, Investigate |\n| Extract, Inline, Move | Architect, Design, Restructure |\n\nIf your reasoning is dominated by ❌ verbs → you''re doing design work, not implementation planning.\n\n#### Incremental Step Sizing\n\nEach planned step must be:\n- **Implementable** in a single subagent invocation (1-3 files)\n- **Verifiable** with a concrete check (test, type-check, grep)\n- **Independent** enough to commit if subsequent steps fail\n\nIf a step can''t meet all three → decompose further or escalate the design complexity.\n\n> **Why this matters**: Benchmark data (Feb 2026) shows first-attempt success drops from ~70-80% on simple tasks to ~25-40% on compound plans. Verification at each step is not overhead — it''s the difference between 40% and 80% success. See `plan-implement` skill § \"Plan Execution Model\" for the full odds table and checkpoint protocol.\n\n### Phase 4: Convergence Protocol\n\n| Checkpoint | Threshold | Action |\n|------------|-----------|--------|\n| **Soft gate** | 3 reasoning steps without a concrete file/function reference | Ground: search codebase for evidence |\n| **Medium gate** | 5 reasoning steps total on same topic | Produce intermediate plan draft as-is with gaps marked |\n| **Hard gate** | 8 reasoning steps total on same topic | STOP reasoning. Output: what''s decided + what''s blocked + recommended next step |\n\n---\n\n## Templates\n\n### Implementation-Ready Reasoning Template\n\n```\nSCOPE: [1-sentence description of the change]\n\nFILES:\n- [path/to/file1.py] → modify [FunctionName]: [what changes]\n- [path/to/file2.py] → add [NewFunction]: [what it does]\n\nDEPENDENCIES: [what must be true before this works]\n\nVERIFICATION:\n- [ ] Test: [test_name] passes\n- [ ] Type check: clean\n- [ ] Behavior: [observable outcome]\n\nBLOCKED BY: [nothing / list specific missing info]\n```\n\n### Design Escalation Template\n\n```\n⚠️ DESIGN DECISION NEEDED — escalating to advisor\n\nContext: [what I was trying to plan]\n\nDecision needed: [the specific design question]\n  - Option A: [brief + known pro/con]\n  - Option B: [brief + known pro/con]\n\nImpact on implementation: [what changes depending on the answer]\n\nMy coding concerns: [practical constraints I''ve noticed — e.g., \"Option A requires modifying a\n  generated file\", \"Option B adds a new dependency\"]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n| Anti-Pattern | Signal | Fix |\n|--------------|--------|-----|\n| **Design masquerading as planning** | \"The architecture should...\" | Tripwire 1 — escalate design questions |\n| **Infinite root cause chaining** | \"But the real problem is...\" | Tripwire 3 — max 2 cause levels |\n| **Speculative edge case spiraling** | \"What about reconnection...\" | Tripwire 2 — note and continue mainline |\n| **Abstract planning** | Steps with no file paths | Phase 1 gate — all 3 materialization Qs required |\n| **Boiling the ocean** | 10+ step plans touching 8+ files | Incremental sizing — cap at 1-3 files per step |\n| **Reasoning without acting** | Extended thinking with no tool calls | Convergence Protocol — hard gate at 8 steps |\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n| Source | Key Contribution |\n|--------|------------------|\n| Wei et al. (2022) — Chain-of-Thought | Structured intermediate steps improve complex task accuracy |\n| Yao et al. (2023) — Tree of Thoughts | Structured exploration + self-evaluation + backtracking |\n| Anthropic (2025) — Building Effective Agents | \"Ground truth from environment at each step\"; stopping conditions |\n| Anthropic (2025) — Think Tool | Inter-action reasoning: 54% improvement on policy-heavy tasks |\n| Kojima et al. (2022) — Zero-shot CoT | Minimal triggers improve accuracy; specificity correlates with depth |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:54:09.456Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for coding-focused AI Agents like Claude Code or AutoGPT that require practical implementation reasoning for trading API integrations.","zh":"适合于像 Claude Code 或 AutoGPT 这样的面向编码的 AI Agent，它们需要实用实现推理来进行交易 API 集成。","ja":"Claude Code や AutoGPT のようなコーディングに焦点を当てた AI エージェントに適しています。これらはトレーディング API 統合の実用的実装の推論を必要とします。","ko":"Claude Code 또는 AutoGPT와 같은 코딩 중심의 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다. 이러한 에이전트는 거래 API 통합을 위한 실용적인 구현 推論을 필요로 합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA enfocados en codificación como Claude Code o AutoGPT que requieren razonamiento de implementación práctica para integraciones de API de trading.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''IA axés sur la codification comme Claude Code ou AutoGPT qui nécessitent un raisonnement d''implémentation pratique pour les intégrations d''API de trading.","de":"Ideal für kodiervorientierte KI-Agenten wie Claude Code oder AutoGPT, die praktisches Implementierungsverständnis für Trading-API-Integrationen erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA focados em codificação, como Claude Code ou AutoGPT, que requerem implementação prática de raciocínio para integrações de API de negociação.","ru":"Идеально подходит для кодирующих агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code или AutoGPT, которые требуют практической реализации рассуждений для интеграций с торговой API.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذي يركز على الكود مثل Claude Code أو AutoGPT الذي يتطلب تنفيذًا عمليًا للreasoning لدمج واجهة برمجة التطبيقات التجارية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to reason about practical coding concerns, providing pre-reasoning gates, materialization checkpoints, and anti-spiral protocols to prevent architectural design exploration, ensuring focused implementation decisions using protocols like trading-api.","zh":"赋予代理实体关于实用编码问题的推理能力，提供预推理门、物化检查点和反螺旋协议，以防止架构设计探索，确保使用类似 trading-api 的协议进行专注的实现决策。","ja":"実用的コーディングに関する推論をエージェントに可能にし、事前推論ゲート、物質化チェックポイント、反スパイラルプロトコルを提供してアーキテクチャ設計の探索を防ぎ、trading-api のようなプロトコルを使用した集中した実装の決定を保証します。","ko":"에이전트가 실제 코딩 문제에 대해 推論할 수 있도록 하며, 사전 推論 게이트, 물질화 체크 포인트 및 반스파이럴 프로토콜을 제공하여 아키텍처 설계 탐색을 방지하고, trading-api와 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 집중적인 구현 결정을 보장합니다.","es":"Empodera a los agentes para razonar sobre preocupaciones de codificación práctica, proporcionando puertas de pre-razonamiento, puntos de control de materialización y protocolos anti-espiral para evitar la exploración del diseño arquitectónico, garantizando decisiones de implementación enfocadas que utilizan protocolos como trading-api.","fr":"Permet aux agents de raisonner sur des préoccupations de codification pratiques, en fournissant des portes de pré-raisonnement, des points de contrôle de matérialisation et des protocoles anti-spirale pour éviter l''exploration de la conception architecturale, en garantissant des décisions d''implémentation ciblées en utilisant des protocoles tels que trading-api.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, über praktische Kodierungsbedenken nachzudenken, indem es Vor-Überlegungs-Tore, Materialisierungs-Prüfpunkte und Anti-Spiral-Protokolle zur Vermeidung der architektonischen Design-Exploration bereitstellt, um fokussierte Implementierungsentscheidungen unter Verwendung von Protokollen wie trading-api sicherzustellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a raciocinarem sobre preocupações de codificação prática, fornecendo portas de pré-raciocínio, pontos de verificação de materialização e protocolos anti-espiral para prevenir a exploração de design arquitetônico, garantindo decisões de implementação focadas usando protocolos como trading-api.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью рассуждать о практических кодировочных проблемах, предоставляя ворота предрассуждения, контрольные точки материализации и антиспиральные протоколы для предотвращения архитектурного проектирования, обеспечивая сосредоточенные решения реализации с использованием протоколов, таких как trading-api.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على التفكير في مشاكل الكود العملي، وتوفير بوابات التفكير المسبق، و نقاط فحص التمثيل، و بروتوكولات مضادة للدوامات لمنع استكشاف التصميم المعماري، وضمان اتخاذ قرارات التركيب المتخصصة باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل trading-api."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing trading API integrations with guardrails","Debugging implementation-focused coding concerns","Escalating design uncertainties to prevent self-solving"],"zh":["使用防护栏实现交易 API 集成","调试面向实现的编码问题","升级设计不确定性以防止自我解决"],"ja":["ガードレールを使用したトレーディング API 統合の実装","実装に焦点を当てたコーディングに関する問題のデバッグ","自己解決を防ぐために設計の不確実性をエスカレートする"],"ko":["가드레일을 사용한 거래 API 통합 구현","구현 중심의 코딩 문제 디버깅","자체 해결을 방지하기 위해 설계 불확실성을 강화"],"es":["Implementar integraciones de API de trading con guardias","Depurar preocupaciones de codificación enfocadas en la implementación","Escalando incertidumbres de diseño para evitar la auto-resolución"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des intégrations d''API de trading avec des garde-fous","Déboguer des préoccupations de codification axées sur l''implémentation","Élever des incertitudes de conception pour éviter l''auto-résolution"],"de":["Implementierung von Trading-API-Integrationen mit Schutzmechanismen","Fehlerbehebung von implementierungsorientierten Kodierungsbedenken","Eskalation von Design-Uncertainties, um Selbstlösung zu vermeiden"],"pt":["Implementação de integrações de API de negociação com guardrails","Depuração de preocupações de codificação focadas na implementação","Escalada de incertezas de design para prevenir a autossolução"],"ru":["Реализация интеграций с торговой API с ограничителями","Отладка кодировочных проблем, ориентированных на реализацию","Эскалация неопределенностей проектирования для предотвращения саморешения"],"ar":["تنفيذ دمج واجهة برمجة التطبيقات التجارية مع الحاجز","تصحيح الأخطاء في مشاكل الكود التي تركز على التنفيذ","تسريع عدم اليقين في التصميم لمنع الحل الذاتي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires settled design prerequisites","Limited to implementation-focused reasoning, not architectural design"],"zh":["需要已解决的设计前提","仅限于实现重点的推理，不是架构设计"],"ja":["解決された設計の前提が必要","実装に焦点を当てた推論に限定され、アーキテクチャ設計ではありません"],"ko":["정리된 설계 전제가 필요","구현 중심의 推論에만 한정되어 있으며, 아키텍처 설계는 아닙니다"],"es":["Requiere requisitos de diseño asentados","Limitado a razonamiento enfocado en la implementación, no en el diseño arquitectónico"],"fr":["Nécessite des prérequis de conception établis","Limité au raisonnement axé sur l''implémentation, et non sur la conception architecturale"],"de":["Benötigt abgeschlossene Design-Voraussetzungen","Begrenzt auf implementierungsorientiertes Verständnis, nicht auf architektonisches Design"],"pt":["Requer pré-requisitos de design estabelecidos","Limitado à razão de implementação, não ao design arquitetônico"],"ru":["Требует установленных предварительных требований к проектированию","Ограничен рассуждениями реализации, а не архитектурного проектирования"],"ar":["يتطلب مسبقات التصميم المستقرة","محدود بالreasoning التنفيذ، وليس التصميم المعماري"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
