:"Guides de développement Python pour établir la cohérence et les meilleures pratiques","de":"Richtlinien für die Python-Entwicklung, um Konsistenz und beste Praktiken sicherzustellen","pt":"Estabeleça consistência e melhores práticas para desenvolvimento Python com padrões modernos e segurança de tipos","ru":"Установите последовательность и лучшие практики для разработки на Python с современными шаблонами и безопасностью типов","ar":"قم بتثبيت الاتساق وأفضل الممارسات لتطوير بايثون مع الأنماط الحديثة وأمان النوع","en":"Setup for claude code"},"definition":{"en":"Setup for claude code"},"features":{"zh":["现代Python 3.12+模式","类型安全和Pydantic v2模型","FastAPI和异步/等待编程","代码格式化和排序导入","项目组织和测试"],"ja":["モダンPython 3.12+パターン","型安全性とPydantic v2モデル","FastAPIと非同期/待機プログラミング","コードフォーマットとソートインポート","プロジェクト組織とテスト"],"ko":["모ダン 파이썬 3.12+ 패턴","타입 안전성과 Pydantic v2 모델","FastAPI와 비동기/대기 프로그래밍","코드 형식과 정렬导入","프로젝트 조직과 테스트"],"es":["Patrones modernos de Python 3.12+","Seguridad de tipos con Pydantic v2","Pruebas y organización de proyectos","Uso de FastAPI y async/await","Formato de código con ruff"],"fr":["Modèles Python 3.12+ modernes","Sécurité de types avec Pydantic v2","Tests et organisation de projets","Utilisation de FastAPI et async/await","Formatage de code avec ruff"],"de":["Moderne Python-3.12+-Muster","Typsicherheit mit Pydantic v2","Tests und Projektorganisation","Verwendung von FastAPI und async/await","Code-Formatierung mit ruff"],"pt":["Padrões modernos de Python 3.12+","Segurança de tipos com Pydantic v2","Testes e organização de projetos","Uso de FastAPI e async/await","Formatação de código com ruff"],"ru":["Современные шаблоны Python 3.12+","Безопасность типов с Pydantic v2","Тестирование и организация проектов","Использование FastAPI и async/await","Форматирование кода с ruff"],"ar":["أنماط بايثون الحديثة 3.12+","أمان النوع مع Pydantic v2","الاختبارات وتنظيم المشاريع","استخدام FastAPI و async/await","تنسيق الكود مع ruff"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Python开发","现代Python","类型安全","FastAPI","异步编程","代码格式化","项目组织","测试","Pydantic"],"ja":["Python開発","モダンPython","型安全性","FastAPI","非同期プログラミング","コードフォーマット","プロジェクト組織","テスト","Pydantic"],"ko":["파이썬 개발","모다ン 파이썬","타입 안전성","FastAPI","비동기 프로그래밍","코드 형식","프로젝트 조직","테스트","Pydantic"],"es":["desarrollo de python","python 3.12+","seguridad de tipos","pruebas de python","organización de proyectos","fastapi","async/await","ruff"],"fr":["développement python","python 3.12+","sécurité de types","tests python","organisation de projets","fastapi","async/await","ruff"],"de":["python-entwicklung","python 3.12+","typsicherheit","python-tests","projektorganisation","fastapi","async/await","ruff"],"pt":["desenvolvimento python","padrões python","segurança de tipos","testes python","organização de projetos","FastAPI","async/await","ruff"],"ru":["разработка на python","шаблоны python","безопасность типов","тестирование python","организация проектов","FastAPI","async/await","ruff"],"ar":["تطوير بايثون","أنماط بايثون","أمان النوع","اختبارات بايثون","تنظيم المشاريع","FastAPI","async/await","ruff"]}},"owner":"NmBoyd","repo":"claude_setup","repoPath":"NmBoyd/claude_setup","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.414Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"python-dev-guidelines","description":"Python development guidelines for modern Python projects. Use when creating Python modules, classes, functions, scripts, or working with type hints, pytest, packaging (pip/poetry), virtual environments, async/await, data classes, or Python best practices. Covers project structure, typing, testing patterns, error handling, logging, and Pythonic idioms.","bodyPreview":"# Python Development Guidelines\n\n## Purpose\n\nEstablish consistency and best practices for Python development, covering modern Python 3.12+ patterns, type safety, testing, and project organization.\n\n---\n\n## Standards Overview\n\n| Category | Standard |\n|----------|----------|\n| **Python** | 3.12+, FastAPI, async/await preferred |\n| **Formatting** | ruff (96-char lines, double quotes, sorted imports) |\n| **Typing** | Strict (Pydantic v2 models preferred); `from __future__ import annotations` |\n| **N","body":"# Python Development Guidelines\n\n## Purpose\n\nEstablish consistency and best practices for Python development, covering modern Python 3.12+ patterns, type safety, testing, and project organization.\n\n---\n\n## Standards Overview\n\n| Category | Standard |\n|----------|----------|\n| **Python** | 3.12+, FastAPI, async/await preferred |\n| **Formatting** | ruff (96-char lines, double quotes, sorted imports) |\n| **Typing** | Strict (Pydantic v2 models preferred); `from __future__ import annotations` |\n| **Naming** | `snake_case` (functions/variables), `PascalCase` (classes), `SCREAMING_SNAKE` (constants) |\n| **Error Handling** | Typed exceptions; context managers for resources |\n| **Documentation** | Google-style docstrings for public functions/classes |\n| **Testing** | Separate test files matching source file patterns |\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nAutomatically activates when working on:\n- Creating or modifying Python files (`.py`)\n- Writing classes, functions, or modules\n- Setting up Python projects (pyproject.toml, setup.py)\n- Writing tests with pytest\n- Working with type hints and mypy\n- Async/await patterns with FastAPI\n- Package management (pip, poetry, conda)\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### New Python Project Checklist\n\n- [ ] **Python version**: 3.12+ specified in `.python-version`\n- [ ] **Project structure**: src layout or flat layout\n- [ ] **pyproject.toml**: Modern packaging config with ruff\n- [ ] **Type hints**: Strict typing with `from __future__ import annotations`\n- [ ] **Tests**: pytest with fixtures, matching source patterns\n- [ ] **Linting**: ruff (96-char lines, double quotes, sorted imports)\n- [ ] **Virtual env**: venv, poetry, or conda\n- [ ] **Documentation**: Google-style docstrings\n- [ ] **Exceptions**: Hierarchical exceptions in `exceptions.py`\n\n### New Module Checklist\n\n- [ ] `from __future__ import annotations` at top\n- [ ] Module docstring (Google-style)\n- [ ] Type hints on all public functions\n- [ ] `__all__` export list (if applicable)\n- [ ] Unit tests in `tests/` mirror structure\n- [ ] Error handling with typed exceptions from `exceptions.py`\n\n---\n\n## Project Structure\n\n### Recommended Layout (src-layout)\n\n```\nproject/\n├── src/\n│   └── mypackage/\n│       ├── __init__.py\n│       ├── exceptions.py     # Hierarchical typed exceptions\n│       ├── core/\n│       │   ├── __init__.py\n│       │   └── module.py\n│       ├── utils/\n│       │   ├── __init__.py\n│       │   └── helpers.py\n│       └── py.typed          # PEP 561 marker\n├── tests/\n│   ├── conftest.py           # Shared fixtures\n│   ├── test_core/\n│   │   └── test_module.py    # Mirrors src/mypackage/core/module.py\n│   └── test_utils/\n│       └── test_helpers.py   # Mirrors src/mypackage/utils/helpers.py\n├── pyproject.toml\n├── ruff.toml                 # ruff config (96-char, double quotes)\n├── README.md\n└── .python-version           # 3.12+\n```\n\n### Alternative: Flat Layout (smaller projects)\n\n```\nproject/\n├── mypackage/\n│   ├── __init__.py\n│   └── module.py\n├── tests/\n│   └── test_module.py\n├── pyproject.toml\n└── README.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## Core Principles (7 Key Rules)\n\n### 1. Type Everything Public (Strict Typing)\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations  # Always at top of file\n\n# ❌ NEVER: Untyped public functions\ndef process_data(data):\n    return data.upper()\n\n# ✅ ALWAYS: Full type annotations\ndef process_data(data: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Process input data.\n\n    Args:\n        data: The input string to process.\n\n    Returns:\n        The processed uppercase string.\n    \"\"\"\n    return data.upper()\n```\n\n### 2. Use Pydantic v2 for Data Models (Preferred)\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, EmailStr, Field\n\n# ✅ Pydantic v2 for validation (preferred)\nclass UserCreate(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"User creation model with validation.\"\"\"\n\n    name: str = Field(..., min_length=1, max_length=100)\n    email: EmailStr\n\nclass UserResponse(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"User response model.\"\"\"\n\n    id: int\n    name: str\n    email: str\n\n# For simple internal data without validation, dataclasses are acceptable\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass\nclass InternalConfig:\n    timeout: int = 30\n    retries: int = 3\n```\n\n### 3. Handle Errors with Typed Hierarchical Exceptions\n\n```python\n# exceptions.py - Define hierarchical typed exceptions\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\n\nclass AppError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for application errors.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, message: str) -> None:\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(message)\n\n\nclass ValidationError(AppError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when validation fails.\"\"\"\n\n    pass\n\n\nclass NotFoundError(AppError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when resource not found.\"\"\"\n\n    pass\n\n\nclass DatabaseError(AppError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when database operation fails.\"\"\"\n\n    pass\n\n\n# Usage - catch specific exceptions, not general Exception\nfrom mypackage.exceptions import ValidationError, NotFoundError\n\nasync def get_user(user_id: int) -> User:\n    \"\"\"Get user by ID.\n\n    Args:\n        user_id: The user''s unique identifier.\n\n    Returns:\n        The user object.\n\n    Raises:\n        NotFoundError: If user does not exist.\n    \"\"\"\n    user = await db.find(user_id)\n    if not user:\n        raise NotFoundError(f\"User {user_id} not found\")\n    return user\n```\n\n### 4. Use Context Managers for Resources\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager, contextmanager\n\n# ❌ NEVER: Manual resource management\nf = open(\"file.txt\")\ndata = f.read()\nf.close()\n\n# ✅ ALWAYS: Context managers\nwith open(\"file.txt\") as f:\n    data = f.read()\n\n# ✅ Sync context manager\n@contextmanager\ndef database_transaction():\n    \"\"\"Manage database transaction with automatic cleanup.\"\"\"\n    conn = get_connection()\n    try:\n        yield conn\n        conn.commit()\n    except Exception:\n        conn.rollback()\n        raise\n    finally:\n        conn.close()\n\n# ✅ Async - use try/finally to ensure cleanup\n@asynccontextmanager\nasync def async_db_session():\n    \"\"\"Manage async database session with cleanup.\"\"\"\n    session = await create_session()\n    try:\n        yield session\n        await session.commit()\n    except Exception:\n        await session.rollback()\n        raise\n    finally:\n        await session.close()\n```\n\n### 5. Prefer Composition Over Inheritance\n\n```python\n# ❌ Avoid deep inheritance\nclass Animal: ...\nclass Mammal(Animal): ...\nclass Dog(Mammal): ...\n\n# ✅ Prefer composition and protocols\nfrom typing import Protocol\n\nclass Walker(Protocol):\n    def walk(self) -> None: ...\n\nclass Dog:\n    def __init__(self, legs: int = 4):\n        self.legs = legs\n\n    def walk(self) -> None:\n        print(f\"Walking on {self.legs} legs\")\n```\n\n### 6. Use Logging, Not Print\n\n```python\nimport logging\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n# ❌ NEVER\nprint(f\"Processing {item}\")\n\n# ✅ ALWAYS\nlogger.info(\"Processing %s\", item)\nlogger.error(\"Failed to process\", exc_info=True)\n```\n\n### 7. Write Testable Code\n\n```python\n# ❌ Hard to test: hidden dependencies\ndef send_email(user_id: int) -> None:\n    user = database.get_user(user_id)  # Hidden dependency\n    smtp.send(user.email, \"Hello\")      # Hidden dependency\n\n# ✅ Easy to test: explicit dependencies\ndef send_email(\n    user: User,\n    email_sender: EmailSender\n) -> None:\n    email_sender.send(user.email, \"Hello\")\n```\n\n---\n\n## Type Hints Quick Reference\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nfrom typing import TypeVar, Generic\nfrom collections.abc import Callable\n\n# Basic types (Python 3.12+)\nvalues: list[int] = [1, 2, 3]\nmapping: dict[str, int] = {\"a\": 1}\nvalue: str | None = None  # Union syntax\n\n# Callable and Generics\nhandler: Callable[[int, str], bool]\nT = TypeVar(\"T\")\n\nclass Container(Generic[T]):\n    def __init__(self, value: T) -> None:\n        self.value = value\n```\n\n---\n\n## Testing Patterns\n\n```python\n# tests/test_user_service.py - mirrors src/mypackage/services/user_service.py\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport pytest\nfrom mypackage.services import UserService\nfrom mypackage.exceptions import ValidationError\n\nclass TestUserService:\n    \"\"\"Tests for UserService.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_create_user_success(self, mock_database):\n        \"\"\"Should create user with valid data.\"\"\"\n        service = UserService(mock_database)\n        user = service.create(name=\"Test\", email=\"test@example.com\")\n        assert user.name == \"Test\"\n\n    def test_create_user_invalid_email_raises(self, mock_database):\n        \"\"\"Should raise ValidationError for invalid email.\"\"\"\n        service = UserService(mock_database)\n        with pytest.raises(ValidationError, match=\"invalid email\"):\n            service.create(name=\"Test\", email=\"not-an-email\")\n```\n\n---\n\n## Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n❌ Mutable default arguments (`def foo(items=[])`)\n❌ Bare `except:` clauses - catch specific exceptions\n❌ Catching general `Exception` - use typed exceptions\n❌ `from module import *`\n❌ Global mutable state\n❌ Ignoring type checker errors\n❌ print() instead of logging\n❌ String concatenation in loops (use join)\n❌ Not using `if __name__ == \"__main__\":`\n❌ Missing `from __future__ import annotations`\n\n---\n\n## Async Patterns (FastAPI Preferred)\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, status\nfrom mypackage.exceptions import ValidationError\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n# ✅ FastAPI endpoint with proper error handling\n@app.post(\"/users\", response_model=UserResponse, status_code=status.HTTP_201_CREATED)\nasync def create_user(user: UserCreate) -> UserResponse:\n    \"\"\"Create a new user.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return await user_service.create(user)\n    except ValidationError as e:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=str(e)) from e\n\n# ✅ Async error handling with exception chaining (from e)\nasync def process_data(data: dict) -> Result:\n    \"\"\"Process data with proper exception handling.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return await do_processing(data)\n    except KeyError as e:\n        raise ValidationError(f\"Missing required field: {e}\") from e\n\n# ✅ Concurrent operations\nasync def process_items(items: list[str]) -> list[dict]:\n    return await asyncio.gather(*[fetch_data(item) for item in items])\n```\n\n---\n\n## Resource Files\n\n### [style-guide.md](resources/style-guide.md)\nGoogle Python Style Guide + PEP 8 practices, naming, docstrings, imports\n\n<!-- ### [project-setup.md](resources/project-setup.md)\npyproject.toml, poetry, pip, virtual environments\n\n### [typing-guide.md](resources/typing-guide.md)\nAdvanced type hints, generics, protocols, mypy configuration\n\n### [testing-patterns.md](resources/testing-patterns.md)\npytest fixtures, mocking, parameterization, coverage\n\n### [async-patterns.md](resources/async-patterns.md)\nasyncio, aiohttp, async context managers\n\n### [packaging.md](resources/packaging.md)\nBuilding packages, publishing to PyPI, versioning -->\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **cpp-dev-guidelines** - C++ development patterns\n- **error-tracking** - Sentry integration for Python\n- **skill-developer** - Creating and managing skills\n\n---\n\n**Skill Status**: COMPLETE ✅\n**Line Count**: < 450 ✅\n**Progressive Disclosure**: Resource files for details ✅\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:55:47.345Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Python Development Agents needing strict type safety and modern Python 3.12+ patterns","zh":"非常适合需要严格类型安全和现代Python 3.12+模式的Python开发代理","ja":"Python 3.12+の厳格な型安全性とモダンなパターンを必要とするPython開発エージェントに最適","ko":"엄격한 타입 안전성과 현대적인 Python 3.12+ 패턴이 필요한 Python 개발 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo de Python que necesitan una seguridad de tipo estricta y patrones de Python 3.12+ modernos","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement Python ayant besoin d''une sécurité de type stricte et de modèles Python 3.12+ modernes","de":"Perfekt für Python-Entwicklungsagenten, die eine strikte Typsicherheit und moderne Python-3.12+-Muster benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Python que necessitam de segurança de tipo estrita e padrões Python 3.12+ modernos","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки Python, требующих строгой безопасности типов и современных шаблонов Python 3.12+","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير بايثون الذي يحتاج إلى سلامة نوع صارمة وأنماط بايثون 3.12+ الحديثة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce consistency and best practices in Python development using ruff for formatting, Pydantic v2 models for typing, and async/await for asynchronous programming, ensuring high-quality code with FastAPI","zh":"赋予代理人使用ruff进行格式化、Pydantic v2模型进行类型检查和async/await进行异步编程的能力，确保使用FastAPI的高质量代码","ja":"ruffによるフォーマット、Pydantic v2モデルによる型チェック、async/awaitによる非同期プログラミングを使用して、高品質のコードをFastAPIで保証するエージェントの能力を付与","ko":"ruff를 사용한 형식화, Pydantic v2 모델을 사용한 타입 검사 및 async/await를 사용한 비동기 프로그래밍을 통해 FastAPI에서 높은 품질의 코드를 보장하는 에이전트의 능력을 부여","es":"Habilita a los agentes para hacer cumplir la coherencia y las mejores prácticas en el desarrollo de Python utilizando ruff para el formato, modelos Pydantic v2 para la tipificación y async/await para la programación asíncrona, garantizando un código de alta calidad con FastAPI","fr":"Permet aux agents d''assurer la cohérence et les meilleures pratiques dans le développement Python en utilisant ruff pour la mise en forme, les modèles Pydantic v2 pour la typage et async/await pour la programmation asynchrone, garantissant un code de haute qualité avec FastAPI","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Konsistenz und Best Practices in der Python-Entwicklung durchzusetzen, indem sie ruff für die Formatierung, Pydantic-v2-Modelle für die Typisierung und async/await für die asynchrone Programmierung verwenden, um einen hochwertigen Code mit FastAPI sicherzustellen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a impor consistência e as melhores práticas no desenvolvimento Python, utilizando ruff para formatação, modelos Pydantic v2 para digitação e async/await para programação assíncrona, garantindo um código de alta qualidade com FastAPI","ru":"Позволяет агентам обеспечивать согласованность и лучшие практики в разработке Python, используя ruff для форматирования, модели Pydantic v2 для типизации и async/await для асинхронного программирования, гарантируя высококачественный код с FastAPI","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من فرض الاتساق وأفضل الممارسات في تطوير بايثون باستخدام ruff للتنسيق ونماذج Pydantic v2 للتنميط وasync/await للبرمجة غير المتزامنة، مما يضمن 코드 عالي الجودة مع FastAPI"},"useCases":{"en":["Enforcing strict type safety with Pydantic v2 models","Formatting code with ruff for consistency","Setting up modern Python 3.12+ projects with async/await and FastAPI"],"zh":["使用Pydantic v2模型强制执行严格的类型安全性","使用ruff进行代码格式化以保持一致性","使用async/await和FastAPI设置现代Python 3.12+项目"],"ja":["Pydantic v2モデルを使用して厳格な型安全性を強制する","ruffを使用してコードのフォーマットを一貫性を持たせる","async/awaitとFastAPIを使用してモダンなPython 3.12+プロジェクトを設定する"],"ko":["Pydantic v2 모델을 사용하여 엄격한 타입 안전성을 강제执行","ruff를 사용하여 코드 형식화를 일관성 있게 유지","async/await와 FastAPI를 사용하여 현대적인 Python 3.12+ 프로젝트를 설정"],"es":["Hacer cumplir la seguridad de tipo estricta con modelos Pydantic v2","Formato de código con ruff para la coherencia","Configuración de proyectos Python 3.12+ modernos con async/await y FastAPI"],"fr":["Assurer la sécurité de type stricte avec des modèles Pydantic v2","Mise en forme du code avec ruff pour la cohérence","Configuration de projets Python 3.12+ modernes avec async/await et FastAPI"],"de":["Durchsetzen der strikten Typsicherheit mit Pydantic-v2-Modellen","Formatierung von Code mit ruff für die Konsistenz","Einrichtung moderner Python-3.12+-Projekte mit async/await und FastAPI"],"pt":["Impor segurança de tipo estrita com modelos Pydantic v2","Formatar código com ruff para consistência","Configurar projetos Python 3.12+ modernos com async/await e FastAPI"],"ru":["Обеспечить строгую безопасность типов с помощью моделей Pydantic v2","Форматировать код с помощью ruff для согласованности","Настроить современные проекты Python 3.12+ с async/await и FastAPI"],"ar":["فرض سلامة النوع الصارمة باستخدام نماذج Pydantic v2","تنسيق الكود باستخدام ruff للاتساق","إعداد مشاريع بايثون 3.12+ الحديثة مع async/await و FastAPI"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python 3.12+","Limited to FastAPI framework","Requires ruff and Pydantic v2 for formatting and typing respectively"],"zh":["需要Python 3.12+","仅限FastAPI框架","需要ruff和Pydantic v2进行格式化和类型检查"],"ja":["Python 3.12+が必要","FastAPIフレームワークのみ","フォーマットと型チェックのためにruffとPydantic v2が必要"],"ko":["Python 3.12+가 필요","FastAPI 프레임워크만 해당","형식화 및 타입 검사를 위해 ruff 및 Pydantic v2가 필요"],"es":["Requiere Python 3.12+","Limitado al marco de FastAPI","Requiere ruff y Pydantic v2 para formato y tipificación respectivamente"],"fr":["Nécessite Python 3.12+","Limité au framework FastAPI","Nécessite ruff et Pydantic v2 pour la mise en forme et la typage respectivement"],"de":["Benötigt Python 3.12+","Begrenzt auf das FastAPI-Framework","Benötigt ruff und Pydantic v2 für die Formatierung und die Typisierung jeweils"],"pt":["Exige Python 3.12+","Limitado ao framework FastAPI","Exige ruff e Pydantic v2 para formatação e digitação, respectivamente"],"ru":["Требует Python 3.12+","Ограничен фреймворком FastAPI","Требует ruff и Pydantic v2 для форматирования и типизации соответственно"],"ar":["يتطلب بايثون 3.12+","محدود بإطار FastAPI","يتطلب ruff و Pydantic v2 للتنسيق والتنميط على التوالي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
