ass sur rivsprod01","Compatibilité avec les modèles d''URL relative","Sécurité et protection de l''application web"],"de":["Implementierung von Webanwendungen hinter einem Apache-Reverse-Proxy","Verwendung relativer URLs im Frontend-Code","Konfiguration von ProxyPass auf rivsprod01","Kompatibilität mit relativen URL-Mustern","Sicherheit und Schutz der Webanwendung"],"pt":["Uso de URLs relativas","Configuração de ProxyPass no Apache","Implantação de aplicações web em rivsprod01","Compatibilidade com padrões de URL relativa","Otimização do desempenho com proxy reverso"],"ru":["Использование относительных URL","Настройка ProxyPass в Apache","Развертывание веб-приложений на rivsprod01","Совместимость с относительными шаблонами URL","Оптимизация производительности с обратным прокси"],"ar":["استخدام URLs النسبية","التكوين ProxyPass في Apache","تثبيت تطبيقات الويب في rivsprod01","التوافق مع أنماط URL النسبية","تحسين الأداء مع وكيل الويب العكسي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["反向代理部署","Apache反向代理服务器","Web应用程序部署","相对URL","ProxyPass配置","前端代码兼容性"],"ja":["リバースプロキシ配置","Apacheリバースプロキシサーバー","Webアプリケーションの配置","相対URL","ProxyPass構成","フロントエンドコードの互換性"],"ko":["역방향 프록시 배포","Apache 역방향 프록시 서버","웹 애플리케이션 배포","상대 URL","ProxyPass 구성","프론트엔드 코드 호환성"],"es":["proxy inverso","apache","deploy","desarrollo web","seguridad","url relativa","proxy pass","rivsprod01","implementación de aplicaciones web"],"fr":["proxy inverse","apache","déploiement","développement web","sécurité","url relative","proxy pass","rivsprod01","implémentation d''applications web"],"de":["reverse-proxy","apache","implementierung","webentwicklung","sicherheit","relative url","proxy pass","rivsprod01","webanwendungsimplementierung"],"pt":["proxy reverso","apache","urls relativas","proxy pass","desenvolvimento web","implantação de aplicações","rivsprod01","otimização de desempenho"],"ru":["обратный прокси","apache","относительные url","proxy pass","веб-разработка","развертывание приложений","rivsprod01","оптимизация производительности"],"ar":["وكيل الويب العكسي","apache","urls نسبية","proxy pass","تطوير الويب","تثبيت تطبيقات","rivsprod01","تحسين الأداء"]}},"owner":"lawless-m","repo":"Gwen","repoPath":"lawless-m/Gwen","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.414Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Reverse Proxy Deployment","description":"Deploy web applications behind Apache reverse proxy on rivsprod01 with relative URLs and proper path configuration","bodyPreview":"# Reverse Proxy Deployment\n\nGuide for deploying web applications behind the Apache reverse proxy on rivsprod01 (dw.ramsden-international.com). Covers frontend relative URL patterns and Apache ProxyPass configuration.\n\n## Instructions\n\nWhen deploying a web application that will be accessed through the reverse proxy:\n\n1. **Use Relative URLs**: Frontend code must use relative URLs (not absolute localhost URLs) to work behind the proxy\n2. **Configure ProxyPass on rivsprod01**: Create Apache config i","body":"# Reverse Proxy Deployment\n\nGuide for deploying web applications behind the Apache reverse proxy on rivsprod01 (dw.ramsden-international.com). Covers frontend relative URL patterns and Apache ProxyPass configuration.\n\n## Instructions\n\nWhen deploying a web application that will be accessed through the reverse proxy:\n\n1. **Use Relative URLs**: Frontend code must use relative URLs (not absolute localhost URLs) to work behind the proxy\n2. **Configure ProxyPass on rivsprod01**: Create Apache config in `/etc/apache2/proxy-conf.d/` with proper path stripping\n3. **Order Matters**: More specific paths must come before general paths in Apache config\n4. **Test Locally First**: Verify services are accessible from rivsprod01 before configuring proxy\n5. **Use Trailing Slashes**: Both source and target URLs need trailing slashes for path stripping to work\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1: Deploy Web Application with API Backend\n\n```\nUser: I have a web app with frontend on port 9273 and API on port 8765. Deploy it behind the proxy at /myapp/\n\nClaude: I''ll set up your application for reverse proxy deployment:\n\n1. **Update Frontend URLs**: Change API calls to use relative URLs\n   - Before: `fetch(''http://localhost:8765/api/status'')`\n   - After: `fetch(''api/status'')`  // Relative to current path\n\n2. **Create Apache Config**: SSH to rivsprod01 and create `/etc/apache2/proxy-conf.d/myapp.conf`\n   - API path: `/myapp/api/` → backend on port 8765\n   - Frontend path: `/myapp/` → frontend on port 9273\n   - API location must come FIRST (more specific)\n\n3. **Reload Apache**: `sudo systemctl reload apache2`\n\n[Provides implementation using the ProxyPass Configuration pattern below]\n```\n\n### Example 2: Frontend Uses Absolute URLs\n\n```\nUser: My frontend has `fetch(''http://localhost:3000/api/data'')` hardcoded. How do I make it work behind a proxy?\n\nClaude: Absolute URLs won''t work behind a reverse proxy. You need to update the frontend to use relative URLs:\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Best: Use relative URLs** - `fetch(''api/data'')` - works anywhere\n2. **Alternative: Use base path** - Store base path in config, prepend to all API calls\n3. **Hidden input method** - Store proxy path in HTML, read in JavaScript\n\nFor option 1 (recommended):\n- Replace all `http://localhost:3000/api/` with `api/`\n- The browser resolves relative to current page path\n- If page is at `/myapp/`, API call goes to `/myapp/api/`\n\n[Shows the Relative URL Pattern implementation below]\n```\n\n### Example 3: Multiple Services on Same Machine\n\n```\nUser: I have 3 services running on ports 8001, 8002, 8003. Deploy all at /service1/, /service2/, /service3/\n\nClaude: I''ll configure all three services in a single Apache config file:\n\n1. **Create single config file**: `/etc/apache2/proxy-conf.d/services.conf`\n2. **Add ProxyPass for each**: More specific paths first (doesn''t matter here since no overlap)\n3. **Each service gets clean URLs**: Paths are stripped before forwarding\n4. **Reload once**: All services go live together\n\n[Provides implementation using the Multi-Service Configuration pattern below]\n```\n\n### Example 4: API Calls Return 404\n\n```\nUser: My frontend loads but API calls return 404. Frontend is at /rabbit/, API should be at /rabbit/api/\n\nClaude: The issue is likely ProxyPass configuration. Let me check:\n\n1. **Verify services are reachable**: From rivsprod01, can you curl the backend directly?\n   - `curl http://10.99.0.3:8765/status` should work\n\n2. **Check ProxyPass order**: API location must come BEFORE frontend location\n   - Wrong order: frontend `/rabbit/` catches `/rabbit/api/` requests\n   - Right order: API `/rabbit/api/` catches first, then frontend `/rabbit/`\n\n3. **Verify trailing slashes**: Both paths need trailing slashes for stripping\n   - `ProxyPass /rabbit/api/ http://10.99.0.3:8765/`\n   - Without trailing slash, path isn''t stripped properly\n\n[Shows debugging steps from Troubleshooting section below]\n```\n\n---\n\n# Reference Implementation Details\n\nThe sections below contain proven working configurations from production deployments.\n\n**Reference Files in This Folder**:\n- `rabbit.conf` - Example Apache config from Invoice OCR deployment\n\n## Relative URL Pattern\n\n**Purpose**: Make frontend work behind any reverse proxy path without hardcoding URLs\n\n### HTML Method (Recommended for Simple Cases)\n\n```html\n<!-- Hidden input stores the API base path -->\n<input type=\"hidden\" id=\"serverUrl\" value=\"api\">\n\n<script>\nfunction getServerUrl() {\n    return document.getElementById(''serverUrl'').value.trim();\n}\n\n// Use in fetch calls\nasync function checkStatus() {\n    const res = await fetch(`${getServerUrl()}/status`);\n    const data = await res.json();\n    // ...\n}\n</script>\n```\n\n**Key Points**:\n- Value is `\"api\"` (relative) not `\"http://localhost:8765\"` (absolute)\n- Browser resolves `api/status` relative to current page\n- If page is at `https://example.com/rabbit/`, request goes to `https://example.com/rabbit/api/status`\n- Proxy strips `/rabbit/` and forwards to backend\n\n### JavaScript Config Method (For Complex Applications)\n\n```javascript\n// config.js\nconst CONFIG = {\n    API_BASE: ''api'',  // Relative to current path\n    WS_BASE: ''ws''     // WebSocket endpoint if needed\n};\n\n// Use throughout app\nfetch(`${CONFIG.API_BASE}/endpoint`)\n```\n\n**When to use**:\n- Multiple API endpoints\n- Different base paths for dev/staging/prod\n- Need to change paths without editing HTML\n\n## ProxyPass Configuration Pattern\n\n**Purpose**: Configure Apache to forward requests from public path to internal service\n\n### Basic Single-Service Configuration\n\n**File**: `/etc/apache2/proxy-conf.d/myservice.conf`\n\n```apache\n# Single service on custom path\nProxyPass /myservice/ http://10.99.0.3:8080/\nProxyPassReverse /myservice/ http://10.99.0.3:8080/\n```\n\n**Key Points**:\n- Simple ProxyPass directives (no `<Location>` blocks needed)\n- Trailing slashes on both source and target strip the path prefix\n- Request to `/myservice/page` becomes `/page` at backend\n- `ProxyPassReverse` rewrites response headers (redirects, etc.)\n\n### API + Frontend Configuration\n\n**File**: `/etc/apache2/proxy-conf.d/service-with-api.conf`\n\n```apache\n# Backend API - Must come FIRST (more specific path)\nProxyPass /rabbit/api/ http://10.99.0.3:8765/\nProxyPassReverse /rabbit/api/ http://10.99.0.3:8765/\n\n# Frontend - Comes SECOND (less specific path)\nProxyPass /rabbit/ http://10.99.0.3:9273/\nProxyPassReverse /rabbit/ http://10.99.0.3:9273/\n```\n\n**Key Points**:\n- API location MUST be listed first (more specific)\n- If frontend is listed first, it catches API requests → 404\n- Both locations strip their prefix before forwarding\n- Request flow:\n  - `GET /rabbit/api/status` → matches first rule → `GET /status` to port 8765\n  - `GET /rabbit/index.html` → matches second rule → `GET /index.html` to port 9273\n\n### Large File Upload Configuration\n\n```apache\n# Service that handles file uploads (PDFs, images, etc.)\nProxyPass /uploads/ http://10.99.0.3:7000/\nProxyPassReverse /uploads/ http://10.99.0.3:7000/\n\n# Important for large PDF uploads\n<Location /uploads/>\n    ProxyPass http://10.99.0.3:7000/\n    ProxyPassReverse http://10.99.0.3:7000/\n\n    # Allow 50MB uploads\n    LimitRequestBody 52428800\n</Location>\n```\n\n**When to use**:\n- File upload services\n- PDF/image processing\n- Any endpoint that receives large request bodies\n\n## Multi-Service Configuration Pattern\n\n**Purpose**: Deploy multiple independent services in one config file\n\n**File**: `/etc/apache2/proxy-conf.d/all-services.conf`\n\n```apache\n# Service 1: API Gateway\nProxyPass /api/ http://10.99.0.3:8001/\nProxyPassReverse /api/ http://10.99.0.3:8001/\n\n# Service 2: Admin Dashboard\nProxyPass /admin/ http://10.99.0.3:8002/\nProxyPassReverse /admin/ http://10.99.0.3:8002/\n\n# Service 3: Public Website\nProxyPass /site/ http://10.99.0.3:8003/\nProxyPassReverse /site/ http://10.99.0.3:8003/\n```\n\n**Key Points**:\n- Each service is completely independent\n- Order doesn''t matter if paths don''t overlap\n- All go live together when Apache reloads\n- Can comment out individual services to disable temporarily\n\n## Deployment Workflow\n\n**Standard deployment process for new service:**\n\n### 1. Verify Local Service Accessibility\n\n```bash\n# From local machine where service runs\ncurl http://10.99.0.3:8765/status  # Test your port\n\n# From rivsprod01 (SSH in)\nssh rivsprod01 \"curl -s http://10.99.0.3:8765/status\"\n```\n\n**Expected**: JSON response or HTML, not connection refused\n\n### 2. Create Apache Configuration\n\n```bash\n# SSH to rivsprod01\nssh rivsprod01\n\n# Create config file (as root or with sudo)\nsudo nano /etc/apache2/proxy-conf.d/myservice.conf\n\n# Add ProxyPass configuration (see patterns above)\n\n# Verify syntax (optional, but recommended)\n# apache2ctl configtest   # May not be available\n# Just proceed to reload if command not found\n```\n\n### 3. Reload Apache\n\n```bash\nsudo systemctl reload apache2\n\n# Verify Apache is still running\nsudo systemctl status apache2\n```\n\n### 4. Test Public Access\n\n```bash\n# From any machine\ncurl https://dw.ramsden-international.com/myservice/\n\n# Or open in browser\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### 404 Not Found - Service Works Locally\n\n**Cause**: ProxyPass configuration issue\n\n**Diagnostic Steps**:\n1. Verify service is accessible from rivsprod01:\n   ```bash\n   ssh rivsprod01 \"curl -s http://10.99.0.3:PORT/endpoint\"\n   ```\n\n2. Check Apache config order:\n   ```bash\n   ssh rivsprod01 \"cat /etc/apache2/proxy-conf.d/myservice.conf\"\n   ```\n   - API paths must come before frontend paths\n   - Verify trailing slashes on both source and target\n\n3. Check Apache error logs:\n   ```bash\n   ssh rivsprod01 \"sudo tail -50 /var/log/apache2/error.log | grep myservice\"\n   ```\n\n**Solution**:\n- Fix ProxyPass order (more specific first)\n- Add missing trailing slashes\n- Reload Apache: `sudo systemctl reload apache2`\n\n### 404 on API Calls, Frontend Works\n\n**Cause**: Frontend path is catching API requests\n\n**Example of Wrong Configuration**:\n```apache\n# WRONG - Frontend catches everything\nProxyPass /app/ http://10.99.0.3:9000/\nProxyPass /app/api/ http://10.99.0.3:8000/\n```\n\n**Solution - Put API First**:\n```apache\n# CORRECT - API catches specific path first\nProxyPass /app/api/ http://10.99.0.3:8000/\nProxyPass /app/ http://10.99.0.3:9000/\n```\n\n### Connection Refused from rivsprod01\n\n**Cause**: Service not listening on accessible IP\n\n**Diagnostic**:\n```bash\n# On machine running service\nnetstat -tlnp | grep PORT\n# or\nss -tlnp | grep PORT\n```\n\n**Look for**:\n- `127.0.0.1:PORT` - Only listening on localhost (wrong)\n- `10.99.0.3:PORT` - Listening on network IP (correct)\n- `0.0.0.0:PORT` - Listening on all interfaces (also correct)\n\n**Solution**: Configure service to bind to `0.0.0.0` or specific IP `10.99.0.3`\n\n### Service Stops Working After Apache Reload\n\n**Cause**: Configuration syntax error\n\n**Diagnostic**:\n```bash\nssh rivsprod01 \"sudo systemctl status apache2\"\n```\n\n**Solution**:\n1. Check for typos in ProxyPass URLs\n2. Verify no missing quotes or slashes\n3. Look at error log: `sudo tail /var/log/apache2/error.log`\n4. Fix config and reload again\n\n### CORS Errors in Browser Console\n\n**Cause**: Backend not configured for CORS, or wrong origin\n\n**Solution (Backend)**: Enable CORS in your service\n\n```python\n# FastAPI example\nfrom fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware\n\napp.add_middleware(\n    CORSMiddleware,\n    allow_origins=[\"*\"],  # Or specific domain\n    allow_credentials=True,\n    allow_methods=[\"*\"],\n    allow_headers=[\"*\"],\n)\n```\n\n**Note**: Proxy handles forwarding; backend sees requests from proxy IP, not client\n\n## IP Addresses Reference\n\n| Hostname | IP Address | Purpose |\n|----------|-----------|---------|\n| rivsprod01 | 10.99.0.2 | Reverse proxy server (Apache) |\n| pogs (local) | 10.99.0.3 | Development machine running services |\n\n**Service Configuration**:\n- Services should bind to `10.99.0.3` or `0.0.0.0` to be accessible from rivsprod01\n- Use `http://10.99.0.3:PORT` in ProxyPass target URLs\n- Never use `localhost` or `127.0.0.1` in ProxyPass targets\n\n## File Locations on rivsprod01\n\n| Path | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `/etc/apache2/proxy-conf.d/*.conf` | Proxy configurations (add yours here) |\n| `/etc/apache2/sites-available/default-ssl.conf` | Main SSL site config (includes proxy-conf.d) |\n| `/var/log/apache2/error.log` | Apache error log |\n| `/var/log/apache2/access.log` | Access log (if needed) |\n\n**Important**: Configs in `/etc/apache2/proxy-conf.d/` are automatically included by the SSL site configuration.\n\n## Best Practices Summary\n\n1. **Always use relative URLs** in frontend code for proxy compatibility\n2. **Test service accessibility** from rivsprod01 before configuring proxy\n3. **Put specific paths first** in Apache config (API before frontend)\n4. **Use trailing slashes** on both ProxyPass source and target for path stripping\n5. **Reload Apache** after config changes: `sudo systemctl reload apache2`\n6. **Keep configs organized** - one file per application or related service group\n7. **Document your paths** - add comments explaining what each ProxyPass does\n8. **Test both frontend and API** after deployment to verify routing\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:57:58.748Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Web Development Agents needing advanced reverse proxy configuration capabilities for secure web application deployment.","zh":"非常适合需要高级反向代理配置能力的Web开发代理，以便安全地部署Web应用程序。","ja":"Web開発エージェントが高度なリバースプロキシ構成機能を必要とする場合に最適です。セキュアなWebアプリケーションの展開を可能にします。","ko":"고급 리버스 프록시 구성 기능을 필요로 하는 웹 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 보안적인 웹 애플리케이션 배포를 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo web que necesitan capacidades de configuración de proxy inverso avanzadas para la implementación segura de aplicaciones web.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement Web ayant besoin de fonctionnalités de configuration de proxy inversé avancées pour le déploiement sécurisé d''applications Web.","de":"Perfekt für Webentwicklungsagenten, die erweiterte Konfigurationsfunktionen für Reverse-Proxy benötigen, um Webanwendungen sicher bereitzustellen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Web que necessitam de capacidades de configuração de proxy reverso avançadas para implantação de aplicações web seguras.","ru":"Идеально для агентов веб-разработки, которым требуются расширенные возможности конфигурации обратного прокси для безопасного развертывания веб-приложений.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير الويب الذي يحتاج إلى إمكانيات تكوين بروكسي عكسي متقدمة لتنفيذ تطبيقات الويب بشكل آمن."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to deploy web applications behind the Apache reverse proxy, leveraging relative URL patterns and Apache ProxyPass configuration for secure and efficient routing, utilizing protocols like HTTP and HTTPS.","zh":"赋予代理部署Web应用程序在Apache反向代理后面的能力，利用相对URL模式和Apache ProxyPass配置实现安全高效的路由，使用HTTP和HTTPS等协议。","ja":"エージェントがApacheのリバースプロキシの後にWebアプリケーションを展開する能力を提供します。相対的なURLパターンとApache ProxyPass構成を利用して、セキュアで効率的なルーティングを実現します。HTTPやHTTPSなどのプロトコルを使用します。","ko":"에이전트가 웹 애플리케이션을 아파치 리버스 프록시 뒤에 배포하는 능력을 제공합니다. 상대적인 URL 패턴과 아파치 ProxyPass 구성이 활용되어 보안하고 효율적인 라우팅을 실현합니다. HTTP와 HTTPS 같은 프로토콜을 사용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar aplicaciones web detrás del proxy inverso de Apache, aprovechando patrones de URL relativos y la configuración de Apache ProxyPass para un enrutamiento seguro y eficiente, utilizando protocolos como HTTP y HTTPS.","fr":"Permet aux agents de déployer des applications Web derrière le proxy inversé Apache, en exploitant des modèles d''URL relatifs et la configuration Apache ProxyPass pour un routage sécurisé et efficace, en utilisant des protocoles comme HTTP et HTTPS.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Webanwendungen hinter dem Apache-Reverse-Proxy zu bereitstellen, indem relative URL-Muster und die Apache-ProxyPass-Konfiguration für sichere und effiziente Weiterleitung genutzt werden, unter Verwendung von Protokollen wie HTTP und HTTPS.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implantar aplicações web atrás do proxy reverso do Apache, aproveitando padrões de URL relativos e configuração do Apache ProxyPass para roteamento seguro e eficiente, utilizando protocolos como HTTP e HTTPS.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью развертывать веб-приложения за обратным прокси Apache, используя относительные шаблоны URL и конфигурацию Apache ProxyPass для безопасного и эффективного маршрутизации, используя протоколы như HTTP и HTTPS.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على نشر تطبيقات الويب خلف بروكسي عكسي Apache، مستفيداً من أنماط URL النسبية وتكوين Apache ProxyPass من أجل التوجيه الآمن والفعال، واستخدام بروتوكولات مثل HTTP وHTTPS."},"useCases":{"en":["Configuring Apache ProxyPass for secure web application routing","Deploying web applications with relative URL patterns","Troubleshooting reverse proxy issues on rivsprod01"],"zh":["为安全的Web应用程序路由配置Apache ProxyPass","使用相对URL模式部署Web应用程序","在rivsprod01上解决反向代理问题"],"ja":["セキュアなWebアプリケーションのルーティングのためにApache ProxyPassを構成する","相対的なURLパターンを使用してWebアプリケーションを展開する","rivsprod01でのリバースプロキシの問題をトラブルシューティングする"],"ko":["보안적인 웹 애플리케이션 라우팅을 위한 아파치 ProxyPass 구성","상대적인 URL 패턴을 사용하여 웹 애플리케이션을 배포하는 것","rivsprod01에서의 리버스 프록시 문제를 해결하는 것"],"es":["Configuración de Apache ProxyPass para el enrutamiento seguro de aplicaciones web","Implementación de aplicaciones web con patrones de URL relativos","Solución de problemas de proxy inverso en rivsprod01"],"fr":["Configuration d''Apache ProxyPass pour le routage sécurisé d''applications Web","Déploiement d''applications Web avec des modèles d''URL relatifs","Dépannage des problèmes de proxy inversé sur rivsprod01"],"de":["Konfiguration von Apache ProxyPass für sicheres Webanwendungs-Weiterleiten","Bereitstellung von Webanwendungen mit relativen URL-Mustern","Fehlerbehebung bei Reverse-Proxy-Problemen auf rivsprod01"],"pt":["Configurando Apache ProxyPass para roteamento de aplicações web seguro","Implantando aplicações web com padrões de URL relativos","Solucionando problemas de proxy reverso no rivsprod01"],"ru":["Настройка Apache ProxyPass для безопасного маршрутизации веб-приложений","Развертывание веб-приложений с относительными шаблонами URL","Устранение неполадок обратного прокси на rivsprod01"],"ar":["تكوين Apache ProxyPass لتنفيذ تطبيقات الويب بشكل آمن","نشر تطبيقات الويب باستخدام أنماط URL النسبية","معالجة مشاكل بروكسي عكسي على rivsprod01"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Apache configuration access","Specific to rivsprod01 (dw.ramsden-international.com) environment"],"zh":["需要Apache配置访问权限","仅限于rivsprod01（dw.ramsden-international.com）环境"],"ja":["Apache構成へのアクセス権が必要","rivsprod01（dw.ramsden-international.com）環境に特有"],"ko":["아파치 구성 접근 권한이 필요함","rivsprod01（dw.ramsden-international.com）환경에 특화"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la configuración de Apache","Específico del entorno rivsprod01 (dw.ramsden-international.com)"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à la configuration d''Apache","Spécifique à l''environnement rivsprod01 (dw.ramsden-international.com)"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Apache-Konfiguration","Spezifisch für die Umgebung rivsprod01 (dw.ramsden-international.com)"],"pt":["Requer acesso à configuração do Apache","Específico para ambiente rivsprod01 (dw.ramsden-international.com)"],"ru":["Требует доступа к конфигурации Apache","Специфичен для среды rivsprod01 (dw.ramsden-international.com)"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى تكوين Apache","محدد للبيئة rivsprod01 (dw.ramsden-international.com)"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('mrfansi/shlink/mobile-design', 'community', 'mrfansi', 'shlink', 'mrfansi/shlink', 'mobile-design', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.414Z', '2026-02-18T03:58:14.113Z', NULL, '{"id":"mrfansi/shlink/mobile-design","name":"mobile-design","description":{"zh":"移动设计系统是一种基于移动设备的设计原则，注重触摸式操作、电池寿命、平台兼容性和离线能力","ja":"モバイルデザインシステムは、モバイルデバイスを基盤とした設計原則であり、タッチ操作、バッテリー寿命、プラットフォーム互換性、オフライン機能に焦点を当てたものです","ko":"모바일 디자인 시스템은 모바일 장치를 기반으로 하는 설계 원칙으로, 터치 스타일, 배터리 수명, 플랫폼 호환성, 오프라인 기능에 중점을 둔 것입니다","es":"El diseño móvil se centra en la experiencia del usuario en dispositivos móviles, considerando factores como la interacción táctil y la eficiencia energética","fr":"La conception mobile se concentre sur l''expérience utilisateur sur les appareils mobiles, en tenant compte de facteurs tels que l''interaction tactile et l''efficacité énergétique","de":"Das Mobile-Design konzentriert sich auf die Benutzererfahrung auf mobilen Geräten, wobei Faktoren wie Touch-Interaktion und Energieeffizienz berücksichtigt werden","pt":"O design móvel é uma abordagem de desenvolvimento que prioriza a experiência do usuário em dispositivos móveis, considerando as limitações e oportunidades da plataforma","ru":"Мобильный дизайн - это подход к разработке, который отдает приоритет опыту пользователя на мобильных устройствах, учитывая ограничения и возможности платформы","ar":"تصميم الهاتف المحمول هو نهج في التطوير يؤثر على تجربة المستخدم على أجهزة الهاتف المحمول، مع مراعاة القيود والفرص للمنصة","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"移动设计系统开发","ja":"モバイルデザインシステム開発","ko":"모바일 디자인 시스템 개발","es":"Diseño Móvil: Principios y Mejores Prácticas","fr":"Conception Mobile: Principes et Bonnes Pratiques","de":"Mobile-Design: Prinzipien und Best Practices","pt":"Desenvolvimento de Design Móvel","ru":"Мобильный дизайн","ar":"تصميم الهاتف المحمول","en":"mobile-design"},"description":{"zh":"移动设计系统是一种基于移动设备的设计原则，注重触摸式操作、电池寿命、平台兼容性和离线能力","ja":"モバイルデザインシステムは、モバイルデバイスを基盤とした設計原則であり、タッチ操作、バッテリー寿命、プラットフォーム互換性、オフライン機能に焦点を当てたものです","ko":"모바일 디자인 시스템은 모바일 장치를 기반으로 하는 설계 원칙으로, 터치 스타일, 배터리 수명, 플랫폼 호환성, 오프라인 기능에 중점을 둔 것입니다","es":"El diseño móvil se centra en la experiencia del usuario en dispositivos móviles, considerando factores como la interacción táctil y la eficiencia energética","fr":"La conception mobile se concentre sur l''expérience utilisateur sur les appareils mobiles, en tenant compte de facteurs tels que l''interaction tactile et l''ef...","de":"Das Mobile-Design konzentriert sich auf die Benutzererfahrung auf mobilen Geräten, wobei Faktoren wie Touch-Interaktion und Energieeffizienz berücksichtigt w...","pt":"O design móvel é uma abordagem de desenvolvimento que prioriza a experiência do usuário em dispositivos móveis, considerando as limitações e oportunidades da...","ru":"Мобильный дизайн - это подход к разработке, который отдает приоритет опыту пользователя на мобильных устройствах, учитывая ограничения и возможности платформы","ar":"تصميم الهاتف المحمول هو نهج في التطوير يؤثر على تجربة المستخدم على أجهزة الهاتف المحمول، مع مراعاة القيود والفرص للمنصة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["触摸式操作","电池寿命优化","平台兼容性","离线能力","移动设备优化"],"ja":["タッチ操作","バッテリー寿命の最適化","プラットフォーム互換性","オフライン機能","モバイルデバイス最適化"],"ko":["터치 스타일","배터리 수명 최적화","플랫폼 호환성","오프라인 기능","모바일 장치 최적화"],"es":["Enfoque touch-first","Conciencia de batería","Respeto a la plataforma","Capacidad offline","Validación de la experiencia del usuario"],"fr":["Approche touch-first","Prise en compte de la batterie","Respect de la plateforme","Capacité hors ligne","Validation de l''expérience utilisateur"],"de":["Touch-first-Ansatz","Batteriebewusstsein","Plattformrespekt","Offline-Fähigkeit","Validierung der Benutzererfahrung"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de UX móvel","Considerações de plataforma","Otimização para dispositivos móveis","Desenvolvimento de aplicativos móveis","Testes de usabilidade"],"ru":["Разработка мобильного UX","Учет платформы","Оптимизация для мобильных устройств","Разработка мобильных приложений","Тестирование удобства использования"],"ar":["تطوير UX الموبايل","الاعتبارات المنصة","تحسين أداء الأجهزة المحمولة","تطوير تطبيقات الهاتف المحمول","اختبارات سهولة الاستخدام"]},"keywords":{"zh":["移动设计系统","移动应用开发","触摸式操作","电池寿命优化","平台兼容性","离线能力"],"ja":["モバイルデザインシステム","モバイルアプリ開発","タッチ操作","バッテリー寿命の最適化","プラットフォーム互換性","オフライン機能"],"ko":["모바일 디자인 시스템","모바일 애플리케이션 개발","터치 스타일","배터리 수명 최적화","플랫폼 호환성","오프라인 기능"],"es":["diseño móvil","experiencia del usuario","interacción táctil","eficiencia energética","desarrollo móvil","principios de diseño"],"fr":["conception mobile","expérience utilisateur","interaction tactile","efficacité énergétique","développement mobile","principes de conception"],"de":["Mobile-Design","Benutzererfahrung","Touch-Interaktion","Energieeffizienz","mobile Entwicklung","Designprinzipien"],"pt":["desenvolvimento móvel","design de UX","plataforma móvel","aplicativos móveis","testes de usabilidade","otimização para dispositivos móveis"],"ru":["мобильная разработка","дизайн UX","мобильная платформа","мобильные приложения","тестирование удобства использования","оптимизация для мобильных устройств"],"ar":["التطوير الموبايل","تصميم UX","المنصة الموبايل","تطبيقات الهاتف المحمول","اختبارات سهولة الاستخدام","تحسين أداء الأجهزة المحمولة"]}},"owner":"mrfansi","repo":"shlink","repoPath":"mrfansi/shlink","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.414Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"mobile-design","description":"Mobile-first design thinking and decision-making for iOS and Android apps. Touch interaction, performance patterns, platform conventions. Teaches principles, not fixed values. Use when building React Native, Flutter, or native mobile apps.","bodyPreview":"# Mobile Design System\n\n> **Philosophy:** Touch-first. Battery-conscious. Platform-respectful. Offline-capable.\n> **Core Principle:** Mobile is NOT a small desktop. THINK mobile constraints, ASK platform choice.\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 Runtime Scripts\n\n**Execute these for validation (don''t read, just run):**\n\n| Script | Purpose | Usage |\n|--------|---------|-------|\n| `scripts/mobile_audit.py` | Mobile UX & Touch Audit | `python scripts/mobile_audit.py <project_path>` |\n\n---\n\n## 🔴 MANDATORY: Read Reference","body":"# Mobile Design System\n\n> **Philosophy:** Touch-first. Battery-conscious. Platform-respectful. Offline-capable.\n> **Core Principle:** Mobile is NOT a small desktop. THINK mobile constraints, ASK platform choice.\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 Runtime Scripts\n\n**Execute these for validation (don''t read, just run):**\n\n| Script | Purpose | Usage |\n|--------|---------|-------|\n| `scripts/mobile_audit.py` | Mobile UX & Touch Audit | `python scripts/mobile_audit.py <project_path>` |\n\n---\n\n## 🔴 MANDATORY: Read Reference Files Before Working!\n\n**⛔ DO NOT start development until you read the relevant files:**\n\n### Universal (Always Read)\n\n| File | Content | Status |\n|------|---------|--------|\n| **[mobile-design-thinking.md](mobile-design-thinking.md)** | **⚠️ ANTI-MEMORIZATION: Forces thinking, prevents AI defaults** | **⬜ CRITICAL FIRST** |\n| **[touch-psychology.md](touch-psychology.md)** | **Fitts'' Law, gestures, haptics, thumb zone** | **⬜ CRITICAL** |\n| **[mobile-performance.md](mobile-performance.md)** | **RN/Flutter performance, 60fps, memory** | **⬜ CRITICAL** |\n| **[mobile-backend.md](mobile-backend.md)** | **Push notifications, offline sync, mobile API** | **⬜ CRITICAL** |\n| **[mobile-testing.md](mobile-testing.md)** | **Testing pyramid, E2E, platform-specific** | **⬜ CRITICAL** |\n| **[mobile-debugging.md](mobile-debugging.md)** | **Native vs JS debugging, Flipper, Logcat** | **⬜ CRITICAL** |\n| [mobile-navigation.md](mobile-navigation.md) | Tab/Stack/Drawer, deep linking | ⬜ Read |\n| [mobile-typography.md](mobile-typography.md) | System fonts, Dynamic Type, a11y | ⬜ Read |\n| [mobile-color-system.md](mobile-color-system.md) | OLED, dark mode, battery-aware | ⬜ Read |\n| [decision-trees.md](decision-trees.md) | Framework/state/storage selection | ⬜ Read |\n\n> 🧠 **mobile-design-thinking.md is PRIORITY!** This file ensures AI thinks instead of using memorized patterns.\n\n### Platform-Specific (Read Based on Target)\n\n| Platform | File | Content | When to Read |\n|----------|------|---------|--------------|\n| **iOS** | [platform-ios.md](platform-ios.md) | Human Interface Guidelines, SF Pro, SwiftUI patterns | Building for iPhone/iPad |\n| **Android** | [platform-android.md](platform-android.md) | Material Design 3, Roboto, Compose patterns | Building for Android |\n| **Cross-Platform** | Both above | Platform divergence points | React Native / Flutter |\n\n> 🔴 **If building for iOS → Read platform-ios.md FIRST!**\n> 🔴 **If building for Android → Read platform-android.md FIRST!**\n> 🔴 **If cross-platform → Read BOTH and apply conditional platform logic!**\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ CRITICAL: ASK BEFORE ASSUMING (MANDATORY)\n\n> **STOP! If the user''s request is open-ended, DO NOT default to your favorites.**\n\n### You MUST Ask If Not Specified:\n\n| Aspect | Ask | Why |\n|--------|-----|-----|\n| **Platform** | \"iOS, Android, or both?\" | Affects EVERY design decision |\n| **Framework** | \"React Native, Flutter, or native?\" | Determines patterns and tools |\n| **Navigation** | \"Tab bar, drawer, or stack-based?\" | Core UX decision |\n| **State** | \"What state management? (Zustand/Redux/Riverpod/BLoC?)\" | Architecture foundation |\n| **Offline** | \"Does this need to work offline?\" | Affects data strategy |\n| **Target devices** | \"Phone only, or tablet support?\" | Layout complexity |\n\n### ⛔ AI MOBILE ANTI-PATTERNS (YASAK LİSTESİ)\n\n> 🚫 **These are AI default tendencies that MUST be avoided!**\n\n#### Performance Sins\n\n| ❌ NEVER DO | Why It''s Wrong | ✅ ALWAYS DO |\n|-------------|----------------|--------------|\n| **ScrollView for long lists** | Renders ALL items, memory explodes | Use `FlatList` / `FlashList` / `ListView.builder` |\n| **Inline renderItem function** | New function every render, all items re-render | `useCallback` + `React.memo` |\n| **Missing keyExtractor** | Index-based keys cause bugs on reorder | Unique, stable ID from data |\n| **Skip getItemLayout** | Async layout = janky scroll | Provide when items have fixed height |\n| **setState() everywhere** | Unnecessary widget rebuilds | Targeted state, `const` constructors |\n| **Native driver: false** | Animations blocked by JS thread | `useNativeDriver: true` always |\n| **console.log in production** | Blocks JS thread severely | Remove before release build |\n| **Skip React.memo/const** | Every item re-renders on any change | Memoize list items ALWAYS |\n\n#### Touch/UX Sins\n\n| ❌ NEVER DO | Why It''s Wrong | ✅ ALWAYS DO |\n|-------------|----------------|--------------|\n| **Touch target < 44px** | Impossible to tap accurately, frustrating | Minimum 44pt (iOS) / 48dp (Android) |\n| **Spacing < 8px between targets** | Accidental taps on neighbors | Minimum 8-12px gap |\n| **Gesture-only interactions** | Motor impaired users excluded | Always provide button alternative |\n| **No loading state** | User thinks app crashed | ALWAYS show loading feedback |\n| **No error state** | User stuck, no recovery path | Show error with retry option |\n| **No offline handling** | Crash/block when network lost | Graceful degradation, cached data |\n| **Ignore platform conventions** | Users confused, muscle memory broken | iOS feels iOS, Android feels Android |\n\n#### Security Sins\n\n| ❌ NEVER DO | Why It''s Wrong | ✅ ALWAYS DO |\n|-------------|----------------|--------------|\n| **Token in AsyncStorage** | Easily accessible, stolen on rooted device | `SecureStore` / `Keychain` / `EncryptedSharedPreferences` |\n| **Hardcode API keys** | Reverse engineered from APK/IPA | Environment variables, secure storage |\n| **Skip SSL pinning** | MITM attacks possible | Pin certificates in production |\n| **Log sensitive data** | Logs can be extracted | Never log tokens, passwords, PII |\n\n#### Architecture Sins\n\n| ❌ NEVER DO | Why It''s Wrong | ✅ ALWAYS DO |\n|-------------|----------------|--------------|\n| **Business logic in UI** | Untestable, unmaintainable | Service layer separation |\n| **Global state for everything** | Unnecessary re-renders, complexity | Local state default, lift when needed |\n| **Deep linking as afterthought** | Notifications, shares broken | Plan deep links from day one |\n| **Skip dispose/cleanup** | Memory leaks, zombie listeners | Clean up subscriptions, timers |\n\n---\n\n## 📱 Platform Decision Matrix\n\n### When to Unify vs Diverge\n\n```\n                    UNIFY (same on both)          DIVERGE (platform-specific)\n                    ───────────────────           ──────────────────────────\nBusiness Logic      ✅ Always                     -\nData Layer          ✅ Always                     -\nCore Features       ✅ Always                     -\n                    \nNavigation          -                             ✅ iOS: edge swipe, Android: back button\nGestures            -                             ✅ Platform-native feel\nIcons               -                             ✅ SF Symbols vs Material Icons\nDate Pickers        -                             ✅ Native pickers feel right\nModals/Sheets       -                             ✅ iOS: bottom sheet vs Android: dialog\nTypography          -                             ✅ SF Pro vs Roboto (or custom)\nError Dialogs       -                             ✅ Platform conventions for alerts\n```\n\n### Quick Reference: Platform Defaults\n\n| Element | iOS | Android |\n|---------|-----|---------|\n| **Primary Font** | SF Pro / SF Compact | Roboto |\n| **Min Touch Target** | 44pt × 44pt | 48dp × 48dp |\n| **Back Navigation** | Edge swipe left | System back button/gesture |\n| **Bottom Tab Icons** | SF Symbols | Material Symbols |\n| **Action Sheet** | UIActionSheet from bottom | Bottom Sheet / Dialog |\n| **Progress** | Spinner | Linear progress (Material) |\n| **Pull to Refresh** | Native UIRefreshControl | SwipeRefreshLayout |\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Mobile UX Psychology (Quick Reference)\n\n### Fitts'' Law for Touch\n\n```\nDesktop: Cursor is precise (1px)\nMobile:  Finger is imprecise (~7mm contact area)\n\n→ Touch targets MUST be 44-48px minimum\n→ Important actions in THUMB ZONE (bottom of screen)\n→ Destructive actions AWAY from easy reach\n```\n\n### Thumb Zone (One-Handed Usage)\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────┐\n│      HARD TO REACH          │ ← Navigation, menu, back\n│        (stretch)            │\n├─────────────────────────────┤\n│      OK TO REACH            │ ← Secondary actions\n│       (natural)             │\n├─────────────────────────────┤\n│      EASY TO REACH          │ ← PRIMARY CTAs, tab bar\n│    (thumb''s natural arc)    │ ← Main content interaction\n└─────────────────────────────┘\n        [  HOME  ]\n```\n\n### Mobile-Specific Cognitive Load\n\n| Desktop | Mobile Difference |\n|---------|-------------------|\n| Multiple windows | ONE task at a time |\n| Keyboard shortcuts | Touch gestures |\n| Hover states | NO hover (tap or nothing) |\n| Large viewport | Limited space, scroll vertical |\n| Stable attention | Interrupted constantly |\n\nFor deep dive: [touch-psychology.md](touch-psychology.md)\n\n---\n\n## ⚡ Performance Principles (Quick Reference)\n\n### React Native Critical Rules\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ CORRECT: Memoized renderItem + React.memo wrapper\nconst ListItem = React.memo(({ item }: { item: Item }) => (\n  <View style={styles.item}>\n    <Text>{item.title}</Text>\n  </View>\n));\n\nconst renderItem = useCallback(\n  ({ item }: { item: Item }) => <ListItem item={item} />,\n  []\n);\n\n// ✅ CORRECT: FlatList with all optimizations\n<FlatList\n  data={items}\n  renderItem={renderItem}\n  keyExtractor={(item) => item.id}  // Stable ID, NOT index\n  getItemLayout={(data, index) => ({\n    length: ITEM_HEIGHT,\n    offset: ITEM_HEIGHT * index,\n    index,\n  })}\n  removeClippedSubviews={true}\n  maxToRenderPerBatch={10}\n  windowSize={5}\n/>\n```\n\n### Flutter Critical Rules\n\n```dart\n// ✅ CORRECT: const constructors prevent rebuilds\nclass MyWidget extends StatelessWidget {\n  const MyWidget({super.key}); // CONST!\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return const Column( // CONST!\n      children: [\n        Text(''Static content''),\n        MyConstantWidget(),\n      ],\n    );\n  }\n}\n\n// ✅ CORRECT: Targeted state with ValueListenableBuilder\nValueListenableBuilder<int>(\n  valueListenable: counter,\n  builder: (context, value, child) => Text(''$value''),\n  child: const ExpensiveWidget(), // Won''t rebuild!\n)\n```\n\n### Animation Performance\n\n```\nGPU-accelerated (FAST):     CPU-bound (SLOW):\n├── transform               ├── width, height\n├── opacity                 ├── top, left, right, bottom\n└── (use these ONLY)        ├── margin, padding\n                            └── (AVOID animating these)\n```\n\nFor complete guide: [mobile-performance.md](mobile-performance.md)\n\n---\n\n## 📝 CHECKPOINT (MANDATORY Before Any Mobile Work)\n\n> **Before writing ANY mobile code, you MUST complete this checkpoint:**\n\n```\n🧠 CHECKPOINT:\n\nPlatform:   [ iOS / Android / Both ]\nFramework:  [ React Native / Flutter / SwiftUI / Kotlin ]\nFiles Read: [ List the skill files you''ve read ]\n\n3 Principles I Will Apply:\n1. _______________\n2. _______________\n3. _______________\n\nAnti-Patterns I Will Avoid:\n1. _______________\n2. _______________\n```\n\n**Example:**\n```\n🧠 CHECKPOINT:\n\nPlatform:   iOS + Android (Cross-platform)\nFramework:  React Native + Expo\nFiles Read: touch-psychology.md, mobile-performance.md, platform-ios.md, platform-android.md\n\n3 Principles I Will Apply:\n1. FlatList with React.memo + useCallback for all lists\n2. 48px touch targets, thumb zone for primary CTAs\n3. Platform-specific navigation (edge swipe iOS, back button Android)\n\nAnti-Patterns I Will Avoid:\n1. ScrollView for lists → FlatList\n2. Inline renderItem → Memoized\n3. AsyncStorage for tokens → SecureStore\n```\n\n> 🔴 **Can''t fill the checkpoint? → GO BACK AND READ THE SKILL FILES.**\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 Framework Decision Tree\n\n```\nWHAT ARE YOU BUILDING?\n        │\n        ├── Need OTA updates + rapid iteration + web team\n        │   └── ✅ React Native + Expo\n        │\n        ├── Need pixel-perfect custom UI + performance critical\n        │   └── ✅ Flutter\n        │\n        ├── Deep native features + single platform focus\n        │   ├── iOS only → SwiftUI\n        │   └── Android only → Kotlin + Jetpack Compose\n        │\n        ├── Existing RN codebase + new features\n        │   └── ✅ React Native (bare workflow)\n        │\n        └── Enterprise + existing Flutter codebase\n            └── ✅ Flutter\n```\n\nFor complete decision trees: [decision-trees.md](decision-trees.md)\n\n---\n\n## 📋 Pre-Development Checklist\n\n### Before Starting ANY Mobile Project\n\n- [ ] **Platform confirmed?** (iOS / Android / Both)\n- [ ] **Framework chosen?** (RN / Flutter / Native)\n- [ ] **Navigation pattern decided?** (Tabs / Stack / Drawer)\n- [ ] **State management selected?** (Zustand / Redux / Riverpod / BLoC)\n- [ ] **Offline requirements known?**\n- [ ] **Deep linking planned from day one?**\n- [ ] **Target devices defined?** (Phone / Tablet / Both)\n\n### Before Every Screen\n\n- [ ] **Touch targets ≥ 44-48px?**\n- [ ] **Primary CTA in thumb zone?**\n- [ ] **Loading state exists?**\n- [ ] **Error state with retry exists?**\n- [ ] **Offline handling considered?**\n- [ ] **Platform conventions followed?**\n\n### Before Release\n\n- [ ] **console.log removed?**\n- [ ] **SecureStore for sensitive data?**\n- [ ] **SSL pinning enabled?**\n- [ ] **Lists optimized (memo, keyExtractor)?**\n- [ ] **Memory cleanup on unmount?**\n- [ ] **Tested on low-end devices?**\n- [ ] **Accessibility labels on all interactive elements?**\n\n---\n\n## 📚 Reference Files\n\nFor deeper guidance on specific areas:\n\n| File | When to Use |\n|------|-------------|\n| [mobile-design-thinking.md](mobile-design-thinking.md) | **FIRST! Anti-memorization, forces context-based thinking** |\n| [touch-psychology.md](touch-psychology.md) | Understanding touch interaction, Fitts'' Law, gesture design |\n| [mobile-performance.md](mobile-performance.md) | Optimizing RN/Flutter, 60fps, memory/battery |\n| [platform-ios.md](platform-ios.md) | iOS-specific design, HIG compliance |\n| [platform-android.md](platform-android.md) | Android-specific design, Material Design 3 |\n| [mobile-navigation.md](mobile-navigation.md) | Navigation patterns, deep linking |\n| [mobile-typography.md](mobile-typography.md) | Type scale, system fonts, accessibility |\n| [mobile-color-system.md](mobile-color-system.md) | OLED optimization, dark mode, battery |\n| [decision-trees.md](decision-trees.md) | Framework, state, storage decisions |\n\n---\n\n> **Remember:** Mobile users are impatient, interrupted, and using imprecise fingers on small screens. Design for the WORST conditions: bad network, one hand, bright sun, low battery. If it works there, it works everywhere.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:58:14.113Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for UI/UX Agents needing touch-first, battery-conscious, and platform-respectful mobile design capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要触摸优先、电池节能和尊重平台的移动设计能力的 UI/UX 代理。","ja":"UI/UX エージェントがタッチファースト、バッテリー意識、プラットフォームに配慮したモバイルデザイン能力を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"터치 우선, 배터리 절약, 플랫폼을尊重하는 모바일 디자인 능력이 필요한 UI/UX 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de UI/UX que necesitan capacidades de diseño móvil de primera generación, conscientes de la batería y respetuosas con la plataforma.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents UI/UX ayant besoin de capacités de conception mobile de première génération, conscientes de la batterie et respectueuses de la plateforme.","de":"Perfekt für UI/UX-Agents, die touch-first-, batteriebewusste und plattformrespektierende Mobile-Designfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de UI/UX que precisam de capacidades de design móvel touch-first, conscientes da bateria e respeitosas com a plataforma.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов UI/UX, которым требуются возможности мобильного дизайна, ориентированные на сенсорный ввод, экономичные в отношении батареи и уважительные к платформе.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء UI/UX الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات تصميم الهاتف المحمول التي تتمحور حول اللمس أولاً وتوفير الطاقة واحترام المنصة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design mobile interfaces with Python scripts for validation, such as executing mobile UX and touch audits using scripts like `mobile_audit.py`, and respecting platform choices to ensure seamless user experiences.","zh":"赋予代理设计移动接口的能力，使用 Python 脚本进行验证，例如使用 `mobile_audit.py` 等脚本执行移动 UX 和触摸审计，并尊重平台选择以确保无缝的用户体验。","ja":"エージェントが Python スクリプトを使用してモバイル インターフェイスを設計することを可能にし、たとえば、`mobile_audit.py` などのスクリプトを使用してモバイル UX とタッチの監査を実行し、プラットフォームの選択を尊重してシームレスなユーザー エクスペリエンスを確保する。","ko":"에이전트가 모바일 인터페이스를 설계할 수 있도록 Python 스크립트를 사용하여 검증할 수 있도록 하며, 예를 들어 `mobile_audit.py`와 같은 스크립트를 사용하여 모바일 UX와 터치 감사 등을 수행하고, 플랫폼 선택을尊重하여 무결점의 사용자 경험을 보장합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes diseñar interfaces móviles con scripts de Python para la validación, como la ejecución de auditorías de UX y touch móviles utilizando scripts como `mobile_audit.py`, y respetar las opciones de plataforma para garantizar experiencias de usuario sin problemas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir des interfaces mobiles avec des scripts Python pour la validation, tels que l''exécution d''audits UX et touch mobiles à l''aide de scripts comme `mobile_audit.py`, et respecter les choix de plateforme pour assurer des expériences utilisateur sans problème.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, mobile Schnittstellen mit Python-Skripten für die Validierung zu entwerfen, wie z.B. die Ausführung von mobilen UX- und Touch-Audits unter Verwendung von Skripten wie `mobile_audit.py`, und respektiert Plattformauswahlen, um eine nahtlose Benutzererfahrung zu gewährleisten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar interfaces móveis com scripts Python para validação, como executar auditorias de UX e toque móvel usando scripts como `mobile_audit.py`, e respeitando as escolhas de plataforma para garantir experiências de usuário sem interrupções.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать мобильные интерфейсы с помощью скриптов Python для валидации, таких как выполнение аудитов мобильного UX и сенсорных аудитов с помощью скриптов типа `mobile_audit.py`, и уважение выбора платформы для обеспечения бесперебойного пользовательского опыта.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تصميم واجهات الهاتف المحمول باستخدام نصوص برمجة بايثون للتحقق، مثل تشغيل تدقيق UX و لمس الهاتف المحمول باستخدام نصوص مثل `mobile_audit.py`، واحترام خيارات المنصة لضمان تجربة مستخدم دون انقطاع."},"useCases":{"en":["Validating mobile UX and touch interactions using `scripts/mobile_audit.py`","Designing battery-conscious and offline-capable mobile applications","Developing platform-respectful mobile interfaces for diverse user bases"],"zh":["使用 `scripts/mobile_audit.py` 验证移动 UX 和触摸交互","设计电池节能和离线能力的移动应用程序","为多样化的用户群体开发尊重平台的移动接口"],"ja":["`scripts/mobile_audit.py` を使用してモバイル UX とタッチの相互作用を検証する","バッテリー意識とオフライン対応のモバイル アプリケーションを設計する","多様なユーザー ベースのためのプラットフォームに配慮したモバイル インターフェイスを開発する"],"ko":["`scripts/mobile_audit.py`를 사용하여 모바일 UX와 터치 상호작용을 검증하는 것","배터리 절약과 오프라인 기능을 갖춘 모바일 애플리케이션을 설계하는 것","다양한 사용자 기반이 위한 플랫폼을尊重하는 모바일 인터페이스를 개발하는 것"],"es":["Validar las interacciones de UX y touch móviles utilizando `scripts/mobile_audit.py`","Diseñar aplicaciones móviles conscientes de la batería y capaces de funcionar sin conexión","Desarrollar interfaces móviles respetuosas con la plataforma para bases de usuarios diversas"],"fr":["Valider les interactions UX et touch mobiles à l''aide de `scripts/mobile_audit.py`","Concevoir des applications mobiles conscientes de la batterie et capables de fonctionner hors ligne","Développer des interfaces mobiles respectueuses de la plateforme pour des bases d''utilisateurs diverses"],"de":["Validieren von mobilen UX- und Touch-Interaktionen unter Verwendung von `scripts/mobile_audit.py`","Entwerfen von batteriebewussten und offline-fähigen mobilen Anwendungen","Entwickeln von plattformrespektierenden mobilen Schnittstellen für diverse Benutzerbasen"],"pt":["Validar interações de UX e toque móvel usando `scripts/mobile_audit.py`","Projetar aplicações móveis conscientes da bateria e capazes de funcionar offline","Desenvolver interfaces móveis respeitosas com a plataforma para bases de usuários diversas"],"ru":["Проверять взаимодействия мобильного UX и сенсорные взаимодействия с помощью `scripts/mobile_audit.py`","Проектировать мобильные приложения, экономичные в отношении батареи и способные работать в автономном режиме","Разрабатывать мобильные интерфейсы, уважительные к платформе, для разнообразных пользовательских баз"],"ar":["التحقق من التفاعلات UX و اللمس للهاتف المحمول باستخدام `scripts/mobile_audit.py`","تصميم تطبيقات الهاتف المحمول التي توفير الطاقة وقادرة على العمل بدون اتصال","تطوير واجهات الهاتف المحمول التي تحترم المنصة لأسس مستخدمين متنوعة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python environment for script execution","Limited to mobile design principles and audits, not a full-fledged design tool"],"zh":["需要 Python 环境来执行脚本","仅限于移动设计原则和审计，不是一个成熟的设计工具"],"ja":["スクリプトの実行には Python 環境が必要","モバイル デザインの原則と監査のみに限定され、完全なデザイン ツールではありません"],"ko":["스크립트 실행을 위해 Python 환경이 필요함","모바일 디자인 원칙과 감사에만 국한되어 있으며, 완전한 디자인 툴은 아님"],"es":["Requiere un entorno de Python para la ejecución de scripts","Limitado a principios de diseño móvil y auditorías, no es una herramienta de diseño completa"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Python pour l''exécution de scripts","Limité aux principes de conception mobile et aux audits, et non à une outil de conception complet"],"de":["Benötigt eine Python-Umgebung für die 