的、平台尊重的和离线功能的设计哲学","ja":"モバイルデザインシステムは、タッチファースト、バッテリー意識、プラットフォーム尊重、オフライン可能な設計哲学です","ko":"모바일 디자인 시스템은 터치 우선, 배터리 효율, 플랫폼 존중, 오프라인 기능을 갖춘 디자인 철학입니다","es":"El diseño móvil se centra en la creación de experiencias de usuario óptimas para dispositivos móviles, considerando factores como la batería y la conexión a ...","fr":"La conception mobile se concentre sur la création d''expériences utilisateur optimales pour les appareils mobiles, en tenant compte de facteurs tels que la ba...","de":"Das mobile Design konzentriert sich auf die Erstellung optimaler Benutzererfahrungen für mobile Geräte, unter Berücksichtigung von Faktoren wie Batterie und ...","pt":"O design móvel é uma abordagem que prioriza a experiência do usuário em dispositivos móveis, considerando restrições e escolhas de plataforma","ru":"Мобильный дизайн - это подход, который отдает приоритет пользовательскому опыту на мобильных устройствах, учитывая ограничения и выбор платформы","ar":"تصميم الجوال هو نهج ي ưu tiên تجربة المستخدم على أجهزة الجوال، مع مراعاة القيود والخيارات المنصبة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["触摸优先设计","电池节能","平台尊重","离线功能","移动设备特性优化"],"ja":["タッチファースト設計","バッテリー節約","プラットフォーム尊重","オフライン機能","モバイルデバイス特性最適化"],"ko":["터치 우선 디자인","배터리 효율","플랫폼 존중","오프라인 기능","모바일 디바이스 특성 최적화"],"es":["Enfoque en la experiencia del usuario","Diseño para dispositivos móviles","Consideración de la batería y la conexión a Internet","Principios de diseño para una experiencia óptima","Herramientas y scripts para la validación del diseño"],"fr":["Focus sur l''expérience utilisateur","Conception pour les appareils mobiles","Prise en compte de la batterie et de la connexion Internet","Principes de conception pour une expérience optimale","Outils et scripts pour la validation de la conception"],"de":["Fokus auf die Benutzererfahrung","Design für mobile Geräte","Berücksichtigung von Batterie und Internetverbindung","Designprinzipien für eine optimale Erfahrung","Werkzeuge und Skripte für die Validierung des Designs"],"pt":["Abordagem touch-first","Otimização de bateria","Funcionalidade offline","Respeito às restrições de plataforma","Execução de scripts de validação"],"ru":["Ориентация на сенсорный интерфейс","Оптимизация батареи","Функциональность offline","Учет ограничений платформы","Выполнение скриптов валидации"],"ar":["نهج اللمس أولاً","تحسين البطارية","الوظائف دون اتصال","احترام قيود المنصة","تشغيل سكريبتات التحقق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["移动设计系统","触摸优先设计","电池节能","平台尊重","离线功能","移动设备特性优化","移动应用程序设计"],"ja":["モバイルデザインシステム","タッチファースト設計","バッテリー節約","プラットフォーム尊重","オフライン機能","モバイルデバイス特性最適化","モバイルアプリケーションデザイン"],"ko":["모바일 디자인 시스템","터치 우선 디자인","배터리 효율","플랫폼 존중","오프라인 기능","모바일 디바이스 특성 최적화","모바일 애플리케이션 디자인"],"es":["diseño móvil","experiencia del usuario","dispositivos móviles","batería","conexión a Internet","principios de diseño","validación del diseño"],"fr":["conception mobile","expérience utilisateur","appareils mobiles","batterie","connexion Internet","principes de conception","validation de la conception"],"de":["mobiles Design","Benutzererfahrung","mobile Geräte","Batterie","Internetverbindung","Designprinzipien","Validierung des Designs"],"pt":["design móvel","experiência do usuário","otimização de bateria","funcionalidade offline","desenvolvimento de aplicativos móveis","design de interface do usuário"],"ru":["мобильный дизайн","пользовательский опыт","оптимизация батареи","функциональность offline","разработка мобильных приложений","дизайн пользовательского интерфейса"],"ar":["تصميم الجوال","تجربة المستخدم","تحسين البطارية","الوظائف دون اتصال","تطوير تطبيقات الجوال","تصميم واجهة المستخدم"]}},"owner":"maskelog","repo":"Daegu_bus_flutter_app","repoPath":"maskelog/Daegu_bus_flutter_app","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.414Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"mobile-design","description":"Mobile-first design thinking and decision-making for iOS and Android apps. Touch interaction, performance patterns, platform conventions. Teaches principles, not fixed values. Use when building React Native, Flutter, or native mobile apps.","bodyPreview":"# Mobile Design System\n\n> **Philosophy:** Touch-first. Battery-conscious. Platform-respectful. Offline-capable.\n> **Core Principle:** Mobile is NOT a small desktop. THINK mobile constraints, ASK platform choice.\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 Runtime Scripts\n\n**Execute these for validation (don''t read, just run):**\n\n| Script | Purpose | Usage |\n|--------|---------|-------|\n| `scripts/mobile_audit.py` | Mobile UX & Touch Audit | `python scripts/mobile_audit.py <project_path>` |\n\n---\n\n## 🔴 MANDATORY: Read Reference","body":"# Mobile Design System\n\n> **Philosophy:** Touch-first. Battery-conscious. Platform-respectful. Offline-capable.\n> **Core Principle:** Mobile is NOT a small desktop. THINK mobile constraints, ASK platform choice.\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 Runtime Scripts\n\n**Execute these for validation (don''t read, just run):**\n\n| Script | Purpose | Usage |\n|--------|---------|-------|\n| `scripts/mobile_audit.py` | Mobile UX & Touch Audit | `python scripts/mobile_audit.py <project_path>` |\n\n---\n\n## 🔴 MANDATORY: Read Reference Files Before Working!\n\n**⛔ DO NOT start development until you read the relevant files:**\n\n### Universal (Always Read)\n\n| File | Content | Status |\n|------|---------|--------|\n| **[mobile-design-thinking.md](mobile-design-thinking.md)** | **⚠️ ANTI-MEMORIZATION: Forces thinking, prevents AI defaults** | **⬜ CRITICAL FIRST** |\n| **[touch-psychology.md](touch-psychology.md)** | **Fitts'' Law, gestures, haptics, thumb zone** | **⬜ CRITICAL** |\n| **[mobile-performance.md](mobile-performance.md)** | **RN/Flutter performance, 60fps, memory** | **⬜ CRITICAL** |\n| **[mobile-backend.md](mobile-backend.md)** | **Push notifications, offline sync, mobile API** | **⬜ CRITICAL** |\n| **[mobile-testing.md](mobile-testing.md)** | **Testing pyramid, E2E, platform-specific** | **⬜ CRITICAL** |\n| **[mobile-debugging.md](mobile-debugging.md)** | **Native vs JS debugging, Flipper, Logcat** | **⬜ CRITICAL** |\n| [mobile-navigation.md](mobile-navigation.md) | Tab/Stack/Drawer, deep linking | ⬜ Read |\n| [mobile-typography.md](mobile-typography.md) | System fonts, Dynamic Type, a11y | ⬜ Read |\n| [mobile-color-system.md](mobile-color-system.md) | OLED, dark mode, battery-aware | ⬜ Read |\n| [decision-trees.md](decision-trees.md) | Framework/state/storage selection | ⬜ Read |\n\n> 🧠 **mobile-design-thinking.md is PRIORITY!** This file ensures AI thinks instead of using memorized patterns.\n\n### Platform-Specific (Read Based on Target)\n\n| Platform | File | Content | When to Read |\n|----------|------|---------|--------------|\n| **iOS** | [platform-ios.md](platform-ios.md) | Human Interface Guidelines, SF Pro, SwiftUI patterns | Building for iPhone/iPad |\n| **Android** | [platform-android.md](platform-android.md) | Material Design 3, Roboto, Compose patterns | Building for Android |\n| **Cross-Platform** | Both above | Platform divergence points | React Native / Flutter |\n\n> 🔴 **If building for iOS → Read platform-ios.md FIRST!**\n> 🔴 **If building for Android → Read platform-android.md FIRST!**\n> 🔴 **If cross-platform → Read BOTH and apply conditional platform logic!**\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ CRITICAL: ASK BEFORE ASSUMING (MANDATORY)\n\n> **STOP! If the user''s request is open-ended, DO NOT default to your favorites.**\n\n### You MUST Ask If Not Specified:\n\n| Aspect | Ask | Why |\n|--------|-----|-----|\n| **Platform** | \"iOS, Android, or both?\" | Affects EVERY design decision |\n| **Framework** | \"React Native, Flutter, or native?\" | Determines patterns and tools |\n| **Navigation** | \"Tab bar, drawer, or stack-based?\" | Core UX decision |\n| **State** | \"What state management? (Zustand/Redux/Riverpod/BLoC?)\" | Architecture foundation |\n| **Offline** | \"Does this need to work offline?\" | Affects data strategy |\n| **Target devices** | \"Phone only, or tablet support?\" | Layout complexity |\n\n### ⛔ AI MOBILE ANTI-PATTERNS (YASAK LİSTESİ)\n\n> 🚫 **These are AI default tendencies that MUST be avoided!**\n\n#### Performance Sins\n\n| ❌ NEVER DO | Why It''s Wrong | ✅ ALWAYS DO |\n|-------------|----------------|--------------|\n| **ScrollView for long lists** | Renders ALL items, memory explodes | Use `FlatList` / `FlashList` / `ListView.builder` |\n| **Inline renderItem function** | New function every render, all items re-render | `useCallback` + `React.memo` |\n| **Missing keyExtractor** | Index-based keys cause bugs on reorder | Unique, stable ID from data |\n| **Skip getItemLayout** | Async layout = janky scroll | Provide when items have fixed height |\n| **setState() everywhere** | Unnecessary widget rebuilds | Targeted state, `const` constructors |\n| **Native driver: false** | Animations blocked by JS thread | `useNativeDriver: true` always |\n| **console.log in production** | Blocks JS thread severely | Remove before release build |\n| **Skip React.memo/const** | Every item re-renders on any change | Memoize list items ALWAYS |\n\n#### Touch/UX Sins\n\n| ❌ NEVER DO | Why It''s Wrong | ✅ ALWAYS DO |\n|-------------|----------------|--------------|\n| **Touch target < 44px** | Impossible to tap accurately, frustrating | Minimum 44pt (iOS) / 48dp (Android) |\n| **Spacing < 8px between targets** | Accidental taps on neighbors | Minimum 8-12px gap |\n| **Gesture-only interactions** | Motor impaired users excluded | Always provide button alternative |\n| **No loading state** | User thinks app crashed | ALWAYS show loading feedback |\n| **No error state** | User stuck, no recovery path | Show error with retry option |\n| **No offline handling** | Crash/block when network lost | Graceful degradation, cached data |\n| **Ignore platform conventions** | Users confused, muscle memory broken | iOS feels iOS, Android feels Android |\n\n#### Security Sins\n\n| ❌ NEVER DO | Why It''s Wrong | ✅ ALWAYS DO |\n|-------------|----------------|--------------|\n| **Token in AsyncStorage** | Easily accessible, stolen on rooted device | `SecureStore` / `Keychain` / `EncryptedSharedPreferences` |\n| **Hardcode API keys** | Reverse engineered from APK/IPA | Environment variables, secure storage |\n| **Skip SSL pinning** | MITM attacks possible | Pin certificates in production |\n| **Log sensitive data** | Logs can be extracted | Never log tokens, passwords, PII |\n\n#### Architecture Sins\n\n| ❌ NEVER DO | Why It''s Wrong | ✅ ALWAYS DO |\n|-------------|----------------|--------------|\n| **Business logic in UI** | Untestable, unmaintainable | Service layer separation |\n| **Global state for everything** | Unnecessary re-renders, complexity | Local state default, lift when needed |\n| **Deep linking as afterthought** | Notifications, shares broken | Plan deep links from day one |\n| **Skip dispose/cleanup** | Memory leaks, zombie listeners | Clean up subscriptions, timers |\n\n---\n\n## 📱 Platform Decision Matrix\n\n### When to Unify vs Diverge\n\n```\n                    UNIFY (same on both)          DIVERGE (platform-specific)\n                    ───────────────────           ──────────────────────────\nBusiness Logic      ✅ Always                     -\nData Layer          ✅ Always                     -\nCore Features       ✅ Always                     -\n                    \nNavigation          -                             ✅ iOS: edge swipe, Android: back button\nGestures            -                             ✅ Platform-native feel\nIcons               -                             ✅ SF Symbols vs Material Icons\nDate Pickers        -                             ✅ Native pickers feel right\nModals/Sheets       -                             ✅ iOS: bottom sheet vs Android: dialog\nTypography          -                             ✅ SF Pro vs Roboto (or custom)\nError Dialogs       -                             ✅ Platform conventions for alerts\n```\n\n### Quick Reference: Platform Defaults\n\n| Element | iOS | Android |\n|---------|-----|---------|\n| **Primary Font** | SF Pro / SF Compact | Roboto |\n| **Min Touch Target** | 44pt × 44pt | 48dp × 48dp |\n| **Back Navigation** | Edge swipe left | System back button/gesture |\n| **Bottom Tab Icons** | SF Symbols | Material Symbols |\n| **Action Sheet** | UIActionSheet from bottom | Bottom Sheet / Dialog |\n| **Progress** | Spinner | Linear progress (Material) |\n| **Pull to Refresh** | Native UIRefreshControl | SwipeRefreshLayout |\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Mobile UX Psychology (Quick Reference)\n\n### Fitts'' Law for Touch\n\n```\nDesktop: Cursor is precise (1px)\nMobile:  Finger is imprecise (~7mm contact area)\n\n→ Touch targets MUST be 44-48px minimum\n→ Important actions in THUMB ZONE (bottom of screen)\n→ Destructive actions AWAY from easy reach\n```\n\n### Thumb Zone (One-Handed Usage)\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────┐\n│      HARD TO REACH          │ ← Navigation, menu, back\n│        (stretch)            │\n├─────────────────────────────┤\n│      OK TO REACH            │ ← Secondary actions\n│       (natural)             │\n├─────────────────────────────┤\n│      EASY TO REACH          │ ← PRIMARY CTAs, tab bar\n│    (thumb''s natural arc)    │ ← Main content interaction\n└─────────────────────────────┘\n        [  HOME  ]\n```\n\n### Mobile-Specific Cognitive Load\n\n| Desktop | Mobile Difference |\n|---------|-------------------|\n| Multiple windows | ONE task at a time |\n| Keyboard shortcuts | Touch gestures |\n| Hover states | NO hover (tap or nothing) |\n| Large viewport | Limited space, scroll vertical |\n| Stable attention | Interrupted constantly |\n\nFor deep dive: [touch-psychology.md](touch-psychology.md)\n\n---\n\n## ⚡ Performance Principles (Quick Reference)\n\n### React Native Critical Rules\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ CORRECT: Memoized renderItem + React.memo wrapper\nconst ListItem = React.memo(({ item }: { item: Item }) => (\n  <View style={styles.item}>\n    <Text>{item.title}</Text>\n  </View>\n));\n\nconst renderItem = useCallback(\n  ({ item }: { item: Item }) => <ListItem item={item} />,\n  []\n);\n\n// ✅ CORRECT: FlatList with all optimizations\n<FlatList\n  data={items}\n  renderItem={renderItem}\n  keyExtractor={(item) => item.id}  // Stable ID, NOT index\n  getItemLayout={(data, index) => ({\n    length: ITEM_HEIGHT,\n    offset: ITEM_HEIGHT * index,\n    index,\n  })}\n  removeClippedSubviews={true}\n  maxToRenderPerBatch={10}\n  windowSize={5}\n/>\n```\n\n### Flutter Critical Rules\n\n```dart\n// ✅ CORRECT: const constructors prevent rebuilds\nclass MyWidget extends StatelessWidget {\n  const MyWidget({super.key}); // CONST!\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return const Column( // CONST!\n      children: [\n        Text(''Static content''),\n        MyConstantWidget(),\n      ],\n    );\n  }\n}\n\n// ✅ CORRECT: Targeted state with ValueListenableBuilder\nValueListenableBuilder<int>(\n  valueListenable: counter,\n  builder: (context, value, child) => Text(''$value''),\n  child: const ExpensiveWidget(), // Won''t rebuild!\n)\n```\n\n### Animation Performance\n\n```\nGPU-accelerated (FAST):     CPU-bound (SLOW):\n├── transform               ├── width, height\n├── opacity                 ├── top, left, right, bottom\n└── (use these ONLY)        ├── margin, padding\n                            └── (AVOID animating these)\n```\n\nFor complete guide: [mobile-performance.md](mobile-performance.md)\n\n---\n\n## 📝 CHECKPOINT (MANDATORY Before Any Mobile Work)\n\n> **Before writing ANY mobile code, you MUST complete this checkpoint:**\n\n```\n🧠 CHECKPOINT:\n\nPlatform:   [ iOS / Android / Both ]\nFramework:  [ React Native / Flutter / SwiftUI / Kotlin ]\nFiles Read: [ List the skill files you''ve read ]\n\n3 Principles I Will Apply:\n1. _______________\n2. _______________\n3. _______________\n\nAnti-Patterns I Will Avoid:\n1. _______________\n2. _______________\n```\n\n**Example:**\n```\n🧠 CHECKPOINT:\n\nPlatform:   iOS + Android (Cross-platform)\nFramework:  React Native + Expo\nFiles Read: touch-psychology.md, mobile-performance.md, platform-ios.md, platform-android.md\n\n3 Principles I Will Apply:\n1. FlatList with React.memo + useCallback for all lists\n2. 48px touch targets, thumb zone for primary CTAs\n3. Platform-specific navigation (edge swipe iOS, back button Android)\n\nAnti-Patterns I Will Avoid:\n1. ScrollView for lists → FlatList\n2. Inline renderItem → Memoized\n3. AsyncStorage for tokens → SecureStore\n```\n\n> 🔴 **Can''t fill the checkpoint? → GO BACK AND READ THE SKILL FILES.**\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 Framework Decision Tree\n\n```\nWHAT ARE YOU BUILDING?\n        │\n        ├── Need OTA updates + rapid iteration + web team\n        │   └── ✅ React Native + Expo\n        │\n        ├── Need pixel-perfect custom UI + performance critical\n        │   └── ✅ Flutter\n        │\n        ├── Deep native features + single platform focus\n        │   ├── iOS only → SwiftUI\n        │   └── Android only → Kotlin + Jetpack Compose\n        │\n        ├── Existing RN codebase + new features\n        │   └── ✅ React Native (bare workflow)\n        │\n        └── Enterprise + existing Flutter codebase\n            └── ✅ Flutter\n```\n\nFor complete decision trees: [decision-trees.md](decision-trees.md)\n\n---\n\n## 📋 Pre-Development Checklist\n\n### Before Starting ANY Mobile Project\n\n- [ ] **Platform confirmed?** (iOS / Android / Both)\n- [ ] **Framework chosen?** (RN / Flutter / Native)\n- [ ] **Navigation pattern decided?** (Tabs / Stack / Drawer)\n- [ ] **State management selected?** (Zustand / Redux / Riverpod / BLoC)\n- [ ] **Offline requirements known?**\n- [ ] **Deep linking planned from day one?**\n- [ ] **Target devices defined?** (Phone / Tablet / Both)\n\n### Before Every Screen\n\n- [ ] **Touch targets ≥ 44-48px?**\n- [ ] **Primary CTA in thumb zone?**\n- [ ] **Loading state exists?**\n- [ ] **Error state with retry exists?**\n- [ ] **Offline handling considered?**\n- [ ] **Platform conventions followed?**\n\n### Before Release\n\n- [ ] **console.log removed?**\n- [ ] **SecureStore for sensitive data?**\n- [ ] **SSL pinning enabled?**\n- [ ] **Lists optimized (memo, keyExtractor)?**\n- [ ] **Memory cleanup on unmount?**\n- [ ] **Tested on low-end devices?**\n- [ ] **Accessibility labels on all interactive elements?**\n\n---\n\n## 📚 Reference Files\n\nFor deeper guidance on specific areas:\n\n| File | When to Use |\n|------|-------------|\n| [mobile-design-thinking.md](mobile-design-thinking.md) | **FIRST! Anti-memorization, forces context-based thinking** |\n| [touch-psychology.md](touch-psychology.md) | Understanding touch interaction, Fitts'' Law, gesture design |\n| [mobile-performance.md](mobile-performance.md) | Optimizing RN/Flutter, 60fps, memory/battery |\n| [platform-ios.md](platform-ios.md) | iOS-specific design, HIG compliance |\n| [platform-android.md](platform-android.md) | Android-specific design, Material Design 3 |\n| [mobile-navigation.md](mobile-navigation.md) | Navigation patterns, deep linking |\n| [mobile-typography.md](mobile-typography.md) | Type scale, system fonts, accessibility |\n| [mobile-color-system.md](mobile-color-system.md) | OLED optimization, dark mode, battery |\n| [decision-trees.md](decision-trees.md) | Framework, state, storage decisions |\n\n---\n\n> **Remember:** Mobile users are impatient, interrupted, and using imprecise fingers on small screens. Design for the WORST conditions: bad network, one hand, bright sun, low battery. If it works there, it works everywhere.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:58:07.092Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Interface Agents requiring touch-first, battery-conscious, and platform-respectful mobile design capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要触摸优先、电池节能和平台尊重的移动设计能力的接口代理。","ja":"タッチ優先、バッテリー意識、プラットフォーム尊重のモバイル設計能力を必要とするインターフェースエージェントに適しています。","ko":"터치 우선, 배터리 의식, 플랫폼 존중의 모바일 디자인 능력이 필요한 인터페이스 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Interfaz que requieren capacidades de diseño móvil de primera generación, conscientes de la batería y respetuosas con la plataforma.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents d''Interface nécessitant des capacités de conception mobile de première génération, conscientes de la batterie et respectueuses de la plateforme.","de":"Ideal für Interface-Agents, die touch-first, batteriebewusste und plattformrespektierende Mobile-Designfunktionen erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Interface que exigem capacidades de design móvel touch-first, conscientes da bateria e respeitosas com a plataforma.","ru":"Идеально для Интерфейсных Агентов, требующих тактильных, экономящих батарею и уважающих платформу мобильных возможностей проектирования.","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة يتطلب قدرات تصميم الهاتف المحمول التي تتم أولاً باللمس ووتيريت الحفاظ على البطارية والاحترام منصة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design mobile interfaces with Python scripts for validation, such as executing mobile UX and touch audits using scripts like `mobile_audit.py`, and respecting platform choices for offline-capable designs.","zh":"赋予代理设计移动接口的能力，使用Python脚本进行验证，例如使用`mobile_audit.py`等脚本执行移动UX和触摸审计，并尊重平台选择以实现离线功能的设计。","ja":"エージェントにPythonスクリプトを使用してモバイルインターフェイスを設計する能力を与え、`mobile_audit.py`などのスクリプトを使用してモバイルUXとタッチの監査を実行し、オフライン対応設計のためのプラットフォーム選択を尊重する。","ko":"에이전트가 모바일 인터페이스를 설계할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 Python 스크립트를 사용하여 검증을 수행할 수 있도록 하며, `mobile_audit.py`와 같은 스크립트를 사용하여 모바일 UX 및 터치 감사를 수행하고, 오프라인 기능을 지원하는 디자인을 위한 플랫폼 선택을 존중합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes diseñar interfaces móviles con scripts de Python para la validación, como la ejecución de auditorías de experiencia del usuario móvil y de interacción táctil mediante scripts como `mobile_audit.py`, y respetando las opciones de plataforma para diseños capaces de funcionar sin conexión.","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir des interfaces mobiles avec des scripts Python pour la validation, tels que l''exécution d''audits d''expérience utilisateur mobile et d''interactions tactiles à l''aide de scripts comme `mobile_audit.py`, et en respectant les choix de plateforme pour des conceptions capables de fonctionner hors ligne.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, mobile Schnittstellen mit Python-Skripten für die Validierung zu entwerfen, wie z.B. die Ausführung von mobilen UX- und Touch-Audits mithilfe von Skripten wie `mobile_audit.py`, und unter Berücksichtigung der Plattformwahl für offline-fähige Designs.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetarem interfaces móveis com scripts Python para validação, como a execução de auditorias de UX móvel e interações por toque usando scripts como `mobile_audit.py`, e respeitando as escolhas de plataforma para designs capazes de funcionar offline.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать мобильные интерфейсы с помощью скриптов Python для валидации, таких как выполнение аудитов мобильного UX и тактильных аудитов с помощью скриптов như `mobile_audit.py`, и уважая выбор платформы для проектов, способных работать в автономном режиме.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على تصميم واجهات الهاتف المحمول باستخدام البرامج النصية لغة بايثون للتحقق، مثل تنفيذ عمليات التدقيق لخبرة المستخدم للهاتف المحمول وتفاعلات اللمس باستخدام البرامج النصية مثل `mobile_audit.py`، والاحترام لاختيارات المنصة لتصاميم قادرة على العمل دون اتصال"},"useCases":{"en":["Validating mobile UX and touch interactions","Auditing mobile design for platform respectfulness","Designing offline-capable mobile interfaces"],"zh":["验证移动UX和触摸交互","审计移动设计的平台尊重性","设计离线功能的移动接口"],"ja":["モバイルUXとタッチの相互作用を検証する","モバイル設計のプラットフォーム尊重性を監査する","オフライン機能を備えたモバイルインターフェイスを設計する"],"ko":["모바일 UX 및 터치 상호 작용을 검증하는 것","모바일 디자인의 플랫폼 존중성을 감사하는 것","오프라인 기능을 지원하는 모바일 인터페이스를 설계하는 것"],"es":["Validar la experiencia del usuario móvil y las interacciones táctiles","Auditar el diseño móvil para la respetabilidad de la plataforma","Diseñar interfaces móviles capaces de funcionar sin conexión"],"fr":["Valider l''expérience utilisateur mobile et les interactions tactiles","Auditer la conception mobile pour le respect de la plateforme","Concevoir des interfaces mobiles capables de fonctionner hors ligne"],"de":["Überprüfen der mobilen Benutzeroberfläche und der Touch-Interaktionen","Prüfen des mobilen Designs auf Plattform-Respektierbarkeit","Entwerfen von offline-fähigen mobilen Schnittstellen"],"pt":["Validação da experiência do usuário móvel e interações por toque","Auditoria do design móvel para respeito à plataforma","Projeto de interfaces móveis capazes de funcionar offline"],"ru":["Валидация мобильного UX и тактильных взаимодействий","Аудит мобильного дизайна для уважения платформы","Проектирование мобильных интерфейсов, способных работать в автономном режиме"],"ar":["التحقق من تجربة المستخدم للهاتف المحمول وتفاعلات اللمس","فحص تصميم الهاتف المحمول لاحترام المنصة","تصميم واجهات الهاتف المحمول القادرة على العمل دون اتصال"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python environment for script execution","Platform-specific design considerations needed"],"zh":["需要Python环境来执行脚本","需要平台特定的设计考虑"],"ja":["スクリプトの実行にはPython環境が必要","プラットフォーム固有の設計の考慮が必要"],"ko":["스크립트 실행을 위해 Python 환경이 필요","플랫폼 특정 디자인 고려가 필요"],"es":["Se requiere un entorno de Python para la ejecución de scripts","Se necesitan consideraciones de diseño específicas de la plataforma"],"fr":["Un environnement Python est requis pour l''exécution de scripts","Des considérations de conception spécifiques à la plateforme sont nécessaires"],"de":["Ein Python-Umgebung ist für die Skriptausführung erforderlich","Plattform-spezifische Design-Überlegungen sind erforderlich"],"pt":["Exige ambiente Python para execução de scripts","Considerações de design específicas da plataforma necessárias"],"ru":["Требует среды Python для выполнения скриптов","Необходимы платформо-специфические соображения по проектированию"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة بايثون لتنفيذ البرامج النصية","مطلوب اعتبارات التصميم الخاصة بالمنصة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('hoanghd218/learn-revit-api-vibe-coding-2026-english/research', 'community', 'hoanghd218', 'learn-revit-api-vibe-coding-2026-english', 'hoanghd218/learn-revit-api-vibe-coding-2026-english', 'research', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.415Z', '2026-02-18T03:59:06.581Z', NULL, '{"id":"hoanghd218/learn-revit-api-vibe-coding-2026-english/research","name":"research","description":{"zh":"研究技能是一种高效的研究方法，遵循YAGNI、KISS和DRY原则，用于快速准确地获取信息","ja":"研究スキルは、YAGNI、KISS、DRY原則に基づく効率的な研究方法で、迅速かつ正確に情報を取得するために使用されます","ko":"연구 스킬은 YAGNI, KISS, DRY 원칙을 따르는 효율적인 연구 방법으로 빠르고 정확하게 정보를 얻기 위해 사용됩니다","es":"Investigación sistemática y eficiente, siguiendo principios de YAGNI, KISS y DRY para desarrolladores","fr":"Recherche systématique et efficace, suivant les principes YAGNI, KISS et DRY pour les développeurs","de":"Systematische und effiziente Recherche, folgend den Prinzipien YAGNI, KISS und DRY für Entwickler","pt":"A Research Skill é uma metodologia estruturada para pesquisa técnica, focada em princípios de desenvolvimento como YAGNI, KISS e DRY. Ela guia o usuário desde a definição do escopo até uma busca sistemática de informações, garantindo resultados concisos e relevantes.","ru":"Research Skill — это структурированная методология технического исследования, основанная на принципах разработки YAGNI, KISS и DRY. Она направляет пользователя от определения области до систематического поиска информации, обеспечивая точные и релевантные результаты.","ar":"Research Skill هي منهجية منظمة للبحث التقني، تركز على مبادئ التطوير مثل YAGNI وKISS وDRY. تقود المستخدم من تحديد النطاق إلى البحث المنهجي عن المعلومات، مما يضمن نتائج موجزة وذات صلة.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"研究技能：高效研究方法","ja":"リサーチスキル：効率的な研究方法","ko":"연구 스킬: 효율적인 연구 방법","es":"Investigación Efectiva","fr":"Recherche Efficient","de":"Effektive Recherche","pt":"Research Skill: Metodologia de Pesquisa Técnica para Devs","ru":"Research Skill: Методология технического исследования для...","ar":"Research Skill: منهجية البحث التقني للمطورين","en":"research"},"description":{"zh":"研究技能是一种高效的研究方法，遵循YAGNI、KISS和DRY原则，用于快速准确地获取信息","ja":"研究スキルは、YAGNI、KISS、DRY原則に基づく効率的な研究方法で、迅速かつ正確に情報を取得するために使用されます","ko":"연구 스킬은 YAGNI, KISS, DRY 원칙을 따르는 효율적인 연구 방법으로 빠르고 정확하게 정보를 얻기 위해 사용됩니다","es":"Investigación sistemática y eficiente, siguiendo principios de YAGNI, KISS y DRY para desarrolladores","fr":"Recherche systématique et efficace, suivant les principes YAGNI, KISS et DRY pour les développeurs","de":"Systematische und effiziente Recherche, folgend den Prinzipien YAGNI, KISS und DRY für Entwickler","pt":"A Research Skill é uma metodologia estruturada para pesquisa técnica, focada em princípios de desenvolvimento como YAGNI, KISS e DRY. Ela guia o usuário desd...","ru":"Research Skill — это структурированная методология технического исследования, основанная на принципах разработки YAGNI, KISS и DRY. Она направляет пользовате...","ar":"Research Skill هي منهجية منظمة للبحث التقني، تركز على مبادئ التطوير مثل YAGNI وKISS وDRY. تقود المستخدم من تحديد النطاق إلى البحث المنهجي عن المعلومات، مما ي...","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["遵循YAGNI、KISS和DRY原则","快速定义研究范围","确定关键术语和概念","设定信息获取的深度和范围","评估信息来源的可靠性"],"ja":["YAGNI、KISS、DRY原則に基づく","研究範囲の迅速な定義","重要な用語と概念の特定","情報取得の深度と範囲の設定","情報源の信頼性の評価"],"ko":["YAGNI, KISS, DRY 원칙을 따름","연구 범위의 빠른 정의","중요한 용어와 개념의 식별","정보 획득의 깊이와 범위 설정","정보 출처의 신뢰성 평가"],"es":["Definición del alcance de la investigación","Identificación de términos y conceptos clave","Determinación de los requisitos de actualidad","Establecimiento de criterios de evaluación para fuentes","Configuración de límites para la profundidad de la investigación"],"fr":["Définition de la portée de la recherche","Identification des termes et des concepts clés","Détermination des exigences de mise à jour","Établissement de critères d''évaluation pour les sources","Configuration des limites pour la profondeur de la recherche"],"de":["Definition des Forschungsumfangs","Identifizierung von Schlüsselbegriffen und -konzepten","Festlegung der Aktualitätsanforderungen","Festlegung von Bewertungskriterien für Quellen","Konfiguration der Grenzen für die Recherchetiefe"],"pt":["Definição de Escopo: Identificação de termos-chave e conceitos para investigação.","Princípios de Desenvolvimento: Adesão estrita a YAGNI, KISS e DRY.","Critérios de Avaliação: Estabelecimento de métricas para qualidade e recência das fontes.","Busca Sistemática: Metodologia faseada para coleta de informações.","Resultados Concisos: Comunicação direta, honesta e técnica dos achados."],"ru":["Определение области: Выявление ключевых терминов и концепций для исследования.","Принципы разработки: Строгое соблюдение YAGNI, KISS и DRY.","Критерии оценки: Установление метрик для качества и актуальности источников.","Систематический поиск: Поэтапная методология сбора информации.","Лаконичные результаты: Прямое, честное и техническое представление выводов."],"ar":["تحديد النطاق: تحديد المصطلحات والمفاهيم الرئيسية للتحقيق.","مبادئ التطوير: الالتزام الصارم بمبادئ YAGNI وKISS وDRY.","معايير التقييم: وضع مقاييس لجودة وحداثة المصادر.","بحث منهجي: منهجية مرحلية لجمع المعلومات.","نتائج موجزة: توصيل النتائج بطريقة مباشرة وصادقة وتقنية."]},"keywords":{"zh":["研究技能","高效研究","YAGNI","KISS","DRY","研究方法","信息获取","开发效率"],"ja":["研究スキル","効率的な研究","YAGNI","KISS","DRY","研究方法","情報取得","開発効率"],"ko":["연구 스킬","효율적인 연구","YAGNI","KISS","DRY","연구 방법","정보 획득","개발 효율성"],"es":["investigación sistemática","YAGNI","KISS","DRY","desarrollo de software","recherche eficiente","análisis de información","evaluación de fuentes"],"fr":["recherche systématique","YAGNI","KISS","DRY","développement de logiciels","recherche efficace","analyse d''informations","évaluation de sources"],"de":["systematische Recherche","YAGNI","KISS","DRY","Softwareentwicklung","effiziente Recherche","Informationsanalyse","Quellenbewertung"],"pt":["metodologia pesquisa técnica","princípios YAGNI KISS DRY","definição escopo desenvolvimento","busca sistemática informação","pesquisa para desenvolvedores","avaliação fontes técnicas","pesquisa concisa desenvolvimento"],"ru":["методология технического исследования","принципы YAGNI KISS DRY","определение области разработки","систематический поиск информации","исследование для разработчиков","оценка технических источников","лаконичное исследование разработки"],"ar":["منهجية البحث التقني","مبادئ YAGNI KISS DRY","تحديد نطاق التطوير","بحث منهجي عن المعلومات","بحث للمطورين","تقييم المصادر التقنية","بحث موجز للتطوير"]}},"owner":"hoanghd218","repo":"learn-revit-api-vibe-coding-2026-english","repoPath":"hoanghd218/learn-revit-api-vibe-coding-2026-english","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.415Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"research","description":"Research technical solutions, analyze architectures, gather requirements thoroughly. Use for technology evaluation, best practices research, solution design, scalability/security/maintainability analysis.","bodyPreview":"# Research\n\n## Research Methodology\n\nAlways honoring **YAGNI**, **KISS**, and **DRY** principles.\n**Be honest, be brutal, straight to the point, and be concise.**\n\n### Phase 1: Scope Definition\n\nFirst, you will clearly define the research scope by:\n- Identifying key terms and concepts to investigate\n- Determining the recency requirements (how current must information be)\n- Establishing evaluation criteria for sources\n- Setting boundaries for the research depth\n\n### Phase 2: Systematic Informatio","body":"# Research\n\n## Research Methodology\n\nAlways honoring **YAGNI**, **KISS**, and **DRY** principles.\n**Be honest, be brutal, straight to the point, and be concise.**\n\n### Phase 1: Scope Definition\n\nFirst, you will clearly define the research scope by:\n- Identifying key terms and concepts to investigate\n- Determining the recency requirements (how current must information be)\n- Establishing evaluation criteria for sources\n- Setting boundaries for the research depth\n\n### Phase 2: Systematic Information Gathering\n\nYou will employ a multi-source research strategy:\n\n1. **Search Strategy**:\n   - **Gemini Toggle**: Check `.claude/.ck.json` (or `~/.claude/.ck.json`) for `skills.research.useGemini` (default: `true`). If `false`, skip Gemini and use WebSearch.\n   - **Gemini Model**: Read from `.claude/.ck.json`: `gemini.model` (default: `gemini-3.0-flash`)\n   - If `useGemini` is enabled and `gemini` bash command is available, execute `gemini -y -m <gemini.model> \"...your search prompt...\"` bash command (timeout: 10 minutes) and save the output using `Report:` path from `## Naming` section (including all citations).\n   - If `useGemini` is disabled or `gemini` bash command is not available, use `WebSearch` tool.\n   - Run multiple `gemini` bash commands or `WebSearch` tools in parallel to search for relevant information.\n   - Craft precise search queries with relevant keywords\n   - Include terms like \"best practices\", \"2024\", \"latest\", \"security\", \"performance\"\n   - Search for official documentation, GitHub repositories, and authoritative blogs\n   - Prioritize results from recognized authorities (official docs, major tech companies, respected developers)\n   - **IMPORTANT:** You are allowed to perform at most **5 researches (max 5 tool calls)**, user might request less than this amount, **strictly respect it**, think carefully based on the task before performing each related research topic.\n\n2. **Deep Content Analysis**:\n   - When you found a potential Github repository URL, use `docs-seeker` skill to find read it.\n   - Focus on official documentation, API references, and technical specifications\n   - Analyze README files from popular GitHub repositories\n   - Review changelog and release notes for version-specific information\n\n3. **Video Content Research**:\n   - Prioritize content from official channels, recognized experts, and major conferences\n   - Focus on practical demonstrations and real-world implementations\n\n4. **Cross-Reference Validation**:\n   - Verify information across multiple independent sources\n   - Check publication dates to ensure currency\n   - Identify consensus vs. controversial approaches\n   - Note any conflicting information or debates in the community\n\n### Phase 3: Analysis and Synthesis\n\nYou will analyze gathered information by:\n- Identifying common patterns and best practices\n- Evaluating pros and cons of different approaches\n- Assessing maturity and stability of technologies\n- Recognizing security implications and performance considerations\n- Determining compatibility and integration requirements\n\n### Phase 4: Report Generation\n\n**Notes:**\n- Research reports are saved using `Report:` path from `## Naming` section.\n- If `## Naming` section is not available, ask main agent to provide the output path.\n\nYou will create a comprehensive markdown report with the following structure:\n\n```markdown\n# Research Report: [Topic]\n\n## Executive Summary\n[2-3 paragraph overview of key findings and recommendations]\n\n## Research Methodology\n- Sources consulted: [number]\n- Date range of materials: [earliest to most recent]\n- Key search terms used: [list]\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### 1. Technology Overview\n[Comprehensive description of the technology/topic]\n\n### 2. Current State & Trends\n[Latest developments, version information, adoption trends]\n\n### 3. Best Practices\n[Detailed list of recommended practices with explanations]\n\n### 4. Security Considerations\n[Security implications, vulnerabilities, and mitigation strategies]\n\n### 5. Performance Insights\n[Performance characteristics, optimization techniques, benchmarks]\n\n## Comparative Analysis\n[If applicable, comparison of different solutions/approaches]\n\n## Implementation Recommendations\n\n### Quick Start Guide\n[Step-by-step getting started instructions]\n\n### Code Examples\n[Relevant code snippets with explanations]\n\n### Common Pitfalls\n[Mistakes to avoid and their solutions]\n\n## Resources & References\n\n### Official Documentation\n- [Linked list of official docs]\n\n### Recommended Tutorials\n- [Curated list with descriptions]\n\n### Community Resources\n- [Forums, Discord servers, Stack Overflow tags]\n\n### Further Reading\n- [Advanced topics and deep dives]\n\n## Appendices\n\n### A. Glossary\n[Technical terms and definitions]\n\n### B. Version Compatibility Matrix\n[If applicable]\n\n### C. Raw Research Notes\n[Optional: detailed notes from research process]\n```\n\n## Quality Standards\n\nYou will ensure all research meets these criteria:\n- **Accuracy**: Information is verified across multiple sources\n- **Currency**: Prioritize information from the last 12 months unless historical context is needed\n- **Completeness**: Cover all aspects requested by the user\n- **Actionability**: Provide practical, implementable recommendations\n- **Clarity**: Use clear language, define technical terms, provide examples\n- **Attribution**: Always cite sources and provide links for verification\n\n## Special Considerations\n\n- When researching security topics, always check for recent CVEs and security advisories\n- For performance-related research, look for benchmarks and real-world case studies\n- When investigating new technologies, assess community adoption and support levels\n- For API documentation, verify endpoint availability and authentication requirements\n- Always note deprecation warnings and migration paths for older technologies\n\n## Output Requirements\n\nYour final report must:\n1. Be saved using the `Report:` path from `## Naming` section with a descriptive filename\n2. Include a timestamp of when the research was conducted\n3. Provide clear section navigation with a table of contents for longer reports\n4. Use code blocks with appropriate syntax highlighting\n5. Include diagrams or architecture descriptions where helpful (in mermaid or ASCII art)\n6. Conclude with specific, actionable next steps\n\n**IMPORTANT:** Sacrifice grammar for the sake of concision when writing reports.\n**IMPORTANT:** In reports, list any unresolved questions at the end, if any.\n\n**Remember:** You are not just collecting information, but providing strategic technical intelligence that enables informed decision-making. Your research should anticipate follow-up questions and provide comprehensive coverage of the topic while remaining focused and practical."},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:59:06.581Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Information Retrieval Agents needing structured research capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要结构化研究能力的信息检索代理。","ja":"構造化された研究機能を必要とする情報検索エージェントに最適です。","ko":"구조화된 연구 기능이 필요한 정보 검색 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de recuperación de información que necesitan capacidades de investigación estructuradas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de récupération d''informations nécessitant des capacités de recherche structurées.","de":"Ideal für Informationsabrufagenten, die strukturierte Recherchefähigkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Recuperação de Informações que necessitam de capacidades de pesquisa estruturadas.","ru":"Идеально для агентов поиска информации, требующих структурированных исследовательских возможностей.","ar":"مثالي لعميل استرجاع المعلومات الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات بحثية منظمة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to systematically gather information using YAGNI, KISS, and DRY principles, evaluating sources based on recency requirements and predefined criteria, and analyzing data with concise and honest insights.","zh":"赋予代理人使用YAGNI、KISS和DRY原则系统地收集信息的能力，根据最新要求和预定义标准评估信息源，并以简洁和诚实的见解分析数据。","ja":"YAGNI、KISS、DRY原則を使用して、エージェントが体系的に情報を収集し、最新要件と事前定義された基準に基づいて情報源を評価し、データを簡潔かつ誠実な洞察で分析する能力を付与します。","ko":"YAGNI, KISS, DRY 원칙을 사용하여 에이전트가 체계적으로 정보를 수집하고 최신 요구 사항 및 사전 정의된 기준에 따라 정보 출처를 평가하고 데이터를 간결하고 진실된 통찰력으로 분석할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a recopilar sistemáticamente información utilizando los principios YAGNI, KISS y DRY, evaluando fuentes en función de los requisitos de actualidad y los criterios predefinidos, y analizando datos con información concisa y honesta.","fr":"Permet aux agents de rassembler systématiquement des informations en utilisant les principes YAGNI, KISS et DRY, en évaluant les sources en fonction des exigences de récence et des critères prédéfinis, et en analysant les données avec des informations concises et honnêtes.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Informationen systematisch unter Verwendung der Prinzipien YAGNI, KISS und DRY zu sammeln, Quellen basierend auf Aktualitätsanforderungen und vordefinierten Kriterien zu bewerten und Daten mit präzisen und ehrlichen Erkenntnissen zu analysieren.","pt":"Permite que os agentes colem informações de forma sistemática, utilizando os princípios YAGNI, KISS e DRY, avaliando fontes com base em requisitos de recência e critérios pré-definidos, e analisando dados com insights concisos e honestos.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью систематически собирать информацию, используя принципы YAGNI, KISS и DRY, оценивая источники на основе требований к актуальности и предопределенных критериев, и анализируя данные с краткими и честными идеями.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من جمع المعلومات بشكل منهجي باستخدام مبادئ YAGNI و KISS و DRY ، وتقييم المصادر بناءً على متطلبات الحداثة والمعايير المحددة مسبقًا ، وتحليل البيانات بأفكار موجزة و صادقة."},"useCases":{"en":["Defining research scope for key terms and concepts","Evaluating source credibility based on recency and relevance","Conducting systematic information analysis for informed decision-making"],"zh":["定义关键词和概念的研究范围","根据最新性和相关性评估信息源的可信度","进行系统化的信息分析以进行明智的决策"],"ja":["重要な用語や概念の研究範囲を定義する","最新性や関連性に基づいて情報源の信頼性を評価する","情報に基づいた意思決定を行うための体系的な情報分析を実施する"],"ko":["주요 용어 및 개념의 연구 범위를 정의하는 것","최신성 및 관련성에 따라 정보 출처의 신뢰성을 평가하는 것","정보에 आध안한 의사 결정에 대한 체계적인 정보 분석을 수행하는 것"],"es":["Definir el alcance de la investigación para términos y conceptos clave","Evaluar la credibilidad de las fuentes en función de la actualidad y la relevancia","Realizar un análisis sistemático de la información para la toma de decisiones informadas"],"fr":["Définir la portée de la recherche pour les termes et les concepts clés","Évaluer la crédibilité des sources en fonction de la récence et de la pertinence","Effectuer une analyse systématique de l''information pour une prise de décision éclairée"],"de":["Definieren des Forschungsumfangs für Schlüsselbegriffe und -konzepte","Bewerten der Quellen auf Basis von Aktualität und Relevanz","Durchführen einer systematischen Informationsanalyse für eine fundierte Entscheidungsfindung"],"pt":["Definir o escopo da pesquisa para termos e conceitos-chave","Avaliar a credibilidade da fonte com base na recência e relevância","Realizar análise sistemática de informações para tomada de decisões informadas"],"ru":["Определение области исследования для ключевых терминов и понятий","Оценка достоверности источника на основе актуальности и релевантности","Проведение систематического анализа информации для принятия обоснованных решений"],"ar":["تحديد نطاق البحث لمصطلحات ومفاهيم رئيسية","تقييم مصداقية المصدر بناءً على الحداثة والأهمية","إجراء تحليل منهجي للمعلومات لاتخاذ قرارات مستنيرة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires clear definition of research scope and boundaries","Dependent on quality and availability of source information"],"zh":["需要清晰地定义研究范围和边界","依赖于信息源的质量和可用性"],"ja":["研究範囲と境界を明確に定義する必要がある","情報源の品質や入手可能性に依存する"],"ko":["연구 범위 및 경계를 명확하게 정의해야 함","정보 출처의 품질 및 가용성에 의존함"],"es":["Requiere una definición clara del alcance y los límites de la investigación","Depende de la calidad y la disponibilidad de la información de las fuentes"],"fr":["Nécessite une définition claire de la portée et des limites de la recherche","Dépend de la qualité et de la disponibilité de l''information des sources"],"de":["Benötigt eine klare Definition des Forschungsumfangs und der -grenzen","Hängt von der Qualität und Verfügbarkeit der Quelleninformation ab"],"pt":["Requer definição clara do escopo e limites da pesquisa","Depende da qualidade e disponibilidade das informações da fonte"],"ru":["Требует четкого определения области и границ исследования","Зависит от качества и доступности информации источника"],"ar":["يتطلب تعريفًا واضحًا لنطاق البحث وحدوده","يعتمد على جودة ومتاحة للمعلومات من المصدر"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
