ords completion state and changed files in analysisContext. Use during implementation.","bodyPreview":"# Implementation Runner\n\n## Inputs\n- `analysisContext.request.userMessage`\n- `analysisContext.decisions.skillChain`\n- `analysisContext.repo.openFiles`\n- `analysisContext.artifacts.contextDocPath` (if present)\n\n## Procedure\n1. Check requirements and context.\n2. Define change scope and implement.\n3. Record changed files and key change summary.\n4. Update implementation completion in `analysisContext`.\n\n## Output (patch)\n```yaml\nsignals.implementationComplete: true\nrepo.changedFiles:\n  - src/...\nnot","body":"# Implementation Runner\n\n## Inputs\n- `analysisContext.request.userMessage`\n- `analysisContext.decisions.skillChain`\n- `analysisContext.repo.openFiles`\n- `analysisContext.artifacts.contextDocPath` (if present)\n\n## Procedure\n1. Check requirements and context.\n2. Define change scope and implement.\n3. Record changed files and key change summary.\n4. Update implementation completion in `analysisContext`.\n\n## Output (patch)\n```yaml\nsignals.implementationComplete: true\nrepo.changedFiles:\n  - src/...\nnotes:\n  - \"implementation: complete, changed_files=3\"\n```\n\n## Rules\n- Do not call other skills/subagents.\n- If failed or deferred, record the reason in `notes`.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:59:52.369Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Analysis Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT requiring automated implementation of code changes.","zh":"适用于 Claude Code 和 AutoGPT 等代码分析代理，需要自动实现代码更改。","ja":"Claude Code や AutoGPT などのコード分析エージェントに適しており、コードの変更を自動的に実装する必要があります。","ko":"Claude Code 및 AutoGPT와 같은 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합하며 자동으로 코드 변경을 구현하는 것이 필요합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de análisis de código como Claude Code y AutoGPT que requieren implementación automatizada de cambios de código.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''analyse de code tels que Claude Code et AutoGPT nécessitant une mise en œuvre automatique des modifications de code.","de":"Ideal für Code-Analyse-Agenten wie Claude Code und AutoGPT, die eine automatisierte Implementierung von Code-Änderungen erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Análise de Código como Claude Code e AutoGPT que exigem implementação automatizada de alterações de código.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа кода, таких как Claude Code и AutoGPT, требующих автоматизированной реализации изменений кода.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل الشفرة مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT الذين يحتاجون إلى تنفيذ تلقائي لتغييرات الشفرة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to define change scope, implement modifications, and record changes to files, utilizing YAML outputs for signals like implementation completion and updating analysis contexts with changed files and summaries, leveraging `analysisContext` and file system interactions.","zh":"赋予代理定义更改范围、实现修改、记录文件更改的能力，利用 YAML 输出来发送信号，例如实现完成和更新分析上下文，包括更改的文件和摘要，利用 `analysisContext` 和文件系统交互。","ja":"エージェントに変更の範囲を定義し、変更を実施し、ファイルの変更を記録する能力を与え、YAML 出力を使用してシグナルを送信します。たとえば、実装の完了や分析コンテキストの更新など、変更されたファイルやサマリーを含む `analysisContext` とファイルシステムの相互作用を利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 변경 범위를 정의하고 수정을 구현하며 파일 변경을 기록할 수 있도록 하며 YAML 출력을 사용하여 신호를 보냅니다. 예를 들어 구현이 완료되거나 분석 컨텍스트가 업데이트되는 경우와 같이 변경된 파일 및 요약을 포함하여 `analysisContext`와 파일 시스템 상호 작용을 利用합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a definir el alcance de los cambios, implementar modificaciones y registrar los cambios en los archivos, utilizando salidas YAML para señales como la finalización de la implementación y la actualización de los contextos de análisis con archivos y resúmenes modificados, aprovechando `analysisContext` y las interacciones con el sistema de archivos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de définir la portée des modifications, de mettre en œuvre des modifications et d''enregistrer les modifications apportées aux fichiers, en utilisant des sorties YAML pour des signaux tels que l''achèvement de la mise en œuvre et la mise à jour des contextes d''analyse avec les fichiers et les résumés modifiés, en exploitant `analysisContext` et les interactions avec le système de fichiers.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, den Änderungsumfang zu definieren, Änderungen zu implementieren und Änderungen an Dateien zu protokollieren, indem YAML-Ausgaben für Signale wie die Implementierungsvollendung und die Aktualisierung der Analysekontexte mit geänderten Dateien und Zusammenfassungen verwendet werden, wobei `analysisContext` und Dateisysteminteraktionen genutzt werden.","pt":"Permite que os agentes definam o escopo da alteração, implementem modificações e registrem alterações em arquivos, utilizando saídas YAML para sinais como conclusão da implementação e atualização de contextos de análise com arquivos alterados e resumos, aproveitando `analysisContext` e interações com o sistema de arquivos.","ru":"Позволяет агентам определять объем изменений, реализовывать модификации и регистрировать изменения файлов, используя выходные данные YAML для сигналов, таких как завершение реализации и обновление контекстов анализа с измененными файлами и сводками, используя `analysisContext` и взаимодействия с файловой системой.","ar":"يمكن للعميل تحديد نطاق التغيير وتنفيذ التعديلات وتسجيل التغييرات على الملفات، باستخدام مخرجات YAML لإشارات مثل استكمال التنفيذ وتحديث سياقات التحليل مع الملفات المعدلة والملخصات، والاستفادة من `analysisContext` وتفاعلات نظام الملفات."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating code updates based on user messages and skill chain decisions","Generating change summaries for code reviews","Updating repository files and tracking changes"],"zh":["基于用户消息和技能链决策自动执行代码更新","为代码审查生成更改摘要","更新存储库文件并跟踪更改"],"ja":["ユーザーのメッセージやスキルチェーンの決定に基づいてコードの自動更新を実施する","コードレビューのための変更のサマリーを生成する","リポジトリのファイルを更新し、変更を追跡する"],"ko":["사용자 메시지 및 스킬 체인 결정에 따라 코드 업데이트를 자동으로 수행하는 것","코드 리뷰를 위한 변경 요약을 생성하는 것","저장소 파일을 업데이트하고 변경 사항을 추적하는 것"],"es":["Automatizar actualizaciones de código en función de los mensajes de los usuarios y las decisiones de la cadena de habilidades","Generar resúmenes de cambios para revisiones de código","Actualizar archivos del repositorio y realizar un seguimiento de los cambios"],"fr":["Automatiser les mises à jour de code en fonction des messages des utilisateurs et des décisions de la chaîne de compétences","Générer des résumés de modifications pour les examens de code","Mettre à jour les fichiers du référentiel et suivre les modifications"],"de":["Automatisieren von Code-Aktualisierungen basierend auf Benutzernachrichten und Skill-Chain-Entscheidungen","Erstellen von Änderungszusammenfassungen für Code-Überprüfungen","Aktualisieren von Repository-Dateien und Nachverfolgen von Änderungen"],"pt":["Automatizar atualizações de código com base em mensagens de usuário e decisões de cadeia de habilidades","Gerar resumos de alterações para revisões de código","Atualizar arquivos de repositório e rastrear alterações"],"ru":["Автоматизация обновлений кода на основе сообщений пользователя и решений цепочки навыков","Генерация сводок изменений для обзоров кода","Обновление файлов репозитория и отслеживание изменений"],"ar":["تحديث الشفرة تلقائيًا بناءً على رسائل المستخدم وعمليات اتخاذ القرارات في سلسلة المهارات","توليد ملخصات التغييرات لاستعراض الشفرة","تحديث ملفات المستودع وتتبع التغييرات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to `analysisContext` and repository files","Dependent on the presence of `analysisContext.artifacts.contextDocPath` for certain operations"],"zh":["需要访问 `analysisContext` 和存储库文件","某些操作依赖于 `analysisContext.artifacts.contextDocPath` 的存在"],"ja":["`analysisContext` とリポジトリのファイルへのアクセスが必要","一部の操作は `analysisContext.artifacts.contextDocPath` の存在に依存しています"],"ko":["`analysisContext` 및 리포지토리 파일에 대한 액세스가 필요합니다","일부 작업은 `analysisContext.artifacts.contextDocPath`가存在하는지 여부에 따라 달라집니다"],"es":["Requiere acceso a `analysisContext` y archivos del repositorio","Depende de la presencia de `analysisContext.artifacts.contextDocPath` para ciertas operaciones"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès à `analysisContext` et aux fichiers du référentiel","Dépend de la présence de `analysisContext.artifacts.contextDocPath` pour certaines opérations"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf `analysisContext` und Repository-Dateien","Hängt von der Anwesenheit von `analysisContext.artifacts.contextDocPath` für bestimmte Operationen ab"],"pt":["Exige acesso a `analysisContext` e arquivos de repositório","Depende da presença de `analysisContext.artifacts.contextDocPath` para certas operações"],"ru":["Требует доступа к `analysisContext` и файлам репозитория","Зависит от наличия `analysisContext.artifacts.contextDocPath` для определенных операций"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى `analysisContext` وملفات المستودع","يعتمد على وجود `analysisContext.artifacts.contextDocPath` لبعض العمليات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('eyepyon/car/erc4337-privacy-wallet', 'community', 'eyepyon', 'car', 'eyepyon/car', 'erc4337-privacy-wallet', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.415Z', '2026-02-18T03:59:53.601Z', NULL, '{"id":"eyepyon/car/erc4337-privacy-wallet","name":"erc4337-privacy-wallet","description":{"zh":"ERC-4337, ","ja":"ERC-4337","ko":"ERC-4337 ","es":"Esta habilidad proporciona soporte integral para desarrollar billeteras de privacidad ERC-4337 con características de protección de datos","fr":"Cette compétence fournit un support complet pour développer des portefeuilles de confidentialité ERC-4337 avec des fonctionnalités de protection des données","de":"Diese Fähigkeit bietet umfassende Unterstützung für die Entwicklung von ERC-4337-Privatsphären-Wallets mit Datenschutzfunktionen","pt":"A Carteira de Privacidade ERC-4337 fornece suporte abrangente para desenvolver carteiras de abstração de contas com recursos de privacidade","ru":"Кошелек ERC-4337 с защитой приватности обеспечивает комплексную поддержку для разработки кошельков с абстракцией учетных записей","ar":"محفظة الخصوصية ERC-4337 توفر دعمًا شاملًا لتطوير محفظة تجريد الحسابات مع ميزات الخصوصية","en":"for hackathon"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"ERC-4337 ","ja":"ERC-4337","ko":"ERC-4337 ","es":"Billetera de privacidad ERC-4337 para desarrolladores","fr":"Portefeuille de confidentialité ERC-4337 pour les dévelop...","de":"ERC-4337-Privatsphären-Wallet für Entwickler","pt":"Carteira de Privacidade ERC-4337 para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Кошелек ERC-4337 с защитой приватности для разработчиков","ar":"محفظة الخصوصية ERC-4337 للمطورين","en":"erc4337-privacy-wallet"},"description":{"zh":"ERC-4337, ","ja":"ERC-4337","ko":"ERC-4337 ","es":"Esta habilidad proporciona soporte integral para desarrollar billeteras de privacidad ERC-4337 con características de protección de datos","fr":"Cette compétence fournit un support complet pour développer des portefeuilles de confidentialité ERC-4337 avec des fonctionnalités de protection des données","de":"Diese Fähigkeit bietet umfassende Unterstützung für die Entwicklung von ERC-4337-Privatsphären-Wallets mit Datenschutzfunktionen","pt":"A Carteira de Privacidade ERC-4337 fornece suporte abrangente para desenvolver carteiras de abstração de contas com recursos de privacidade","ru":"Кошелек ERC-4337 с защитой приватности обеспечивает комплексную поддержку для разработки кошельков с абстракцией учетных записей","ar":"محفظة الخصوصية ERC-4337 توفر دعمًا شاملًا لتطوير محفظة تجريد الحسابات مع ميزات الخصوصية","en":"for hackathon"},"definition":{"en":"for hackathon"},"features":{"zh":["ERC-4337","","","ERC-4337"],"ja":["ERC-4337","","","ERC-4337"],"ko":["ERC-4337","","","ERC-4337"],"es":["Plantillas de contrato inteligente","Herramientas de validación de privacidad","Marco de pruebas de seguridad","Mejores prácticas de seguridad","Soporte para casos de uso de identidad de vehículos"],"fr":["Modèles de contrat intelligents","Outils de validation de la confidentialité","Cadre de tests de sécurité","Meilleures pratiques de sécurité","Prise en charge des cas d''utilisation d''identité de véhicules"],"de":["Smart-Contract-Vorlagen","Werkzeuge zur Überprüfung der Privatsphäre","Sicherheitstestrahmen","Sicherheitsbest Practices","Unterstützung für Fahrzeugidentitätsanwendungsfälle"],"pt":["Suporte a abstração de contas","Recursos de privacidade","Validação de privacidade","Melhores práticas de segurança","Modelos de contrato inteligente"],"ru":["Поддержка абстракции учетных записей","Функции приватности","Проверка приватности","Лучшие практики безопасности","Шаблоны умных контрактов"],"ar":["دعم تجريد الحسابات","ميزات الخصوصية","التحقق من الخصوصية","أفضل الممارسات الأمنية","قوالب العقد الذكي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["ERC-4337","","ERC-4337","","","ERC-4337"],"ja":["ERC-4337","","ERC-4337","","","ERC-4337"],"ko":["ERC-4337","","ERC-4337","","","ERC-4337"],"es":["ERC-4337","billetera de privacidad","desarrollo de billeteras","protección de datos","identidad de vehículos","contrato inteligente","seguridad blockchain"],"fr":["ERC-4337","portefeuille de confidentialité","développement de portefeuilles","protection des données","identité de véhicules","contrat intelligent","sécurité blockchain"],"de":["ERC-4337","Privatsphären-Wallet","Wallet-Entwicklung","Datenschutz","Fahrzeugidentität","Smart-Contract","Blockchain-Sicherheit"],"pt":["Carteira de Privacidade ERC-4337","Desenvolvimento de carteiras","Abstração de contas","Privacidade","Segurança","Contratos inteligentes"],"ru":["Кошелек ERC-4337 с защитой приватности","Разработка кошельков","Абстракция учетных записей","Приватность","Безопасность","Умные контракты"],"ar":["محفظة الخصوصية ERC-4337","تطوير المحفظة","تجريد الحسابات","الخصوصية","الأمان","العقود الذكية"]}},"owner":"eyepyon","repo":"car","repoPath":"eyepyon/car","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.415Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"erc4337-privacy-wallet","description":"Privacy-preserving ERC-4337 wallet development for vehicle identity and sensitive data protection. Use when implementing ERC-4337 account abstraction wallets that handle sensitive information (vehicle license plates, biometric data, personal IDs) requiring on-chain privacy. Triggers on requests like implement ERC-4337 wallet for vehicle, create privacy-protected account abstraction, build wallet with vehicle number privacy, develop ERC-4337 with ZK proof integration, or any smart contract wallet development requiring commitment schemes, deterministic address generation, and sensitive data protection.","bodyPreview":"# ERC-4337 Privacy-Protected Wallet\n\n## Overview\n\nThis skill provides comprehensive support for developing ERC-4337 compliant Account Abstraction wallets with privacy-preserving features, specifically designed for vehicle identity and other sensitive data use cases. It combines smart contract templates, testing frameworks, privacy validation tools, and security best practices to enable the secure implementation of wallets that protect user privacy while maintaining on-chain functionality.\n\n**Key","body":"# ERC-4337 Privacy-Protected Wallet\n\n## Overview\n\nThis skill provides comprehensive support for developing ERC-4337 compliant Account Abstraction wallets with privacy-preserving features, specifically designed for vehicle identity and other sensitive data use cases. It combines smart contract templates, testing frameworks, privacy validation tools, and security best practices to enable the secure implementation of wallets that protect user privacy while maintaining on-chain functionality.\n\n**Key Capabilities:**\n- Privacy-protected smart contract templates (PrivacyProtectedAccount, AccountFactory, VehicleRegistry)\n- Commitment scheme implementation for sensitive data (vehicle plates, personal info)\n- Deterministic address generation using CREATE2\n- Comprehensive test suites with privacy verification\n- Automated privacy validation tooling\n- Security and compliance checklists\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nInvoke this skill when you encounter requests involving:\n\n- **Vehicle Identity Wallets**: \"Create a wallet from vehicle license plate information\"\n- **ERC-4337 Implementation**: \"Implement account abstraction for privacy-protected accounts\"\n- **Sensitive Data Protection**: \"Build wallet that hides user''s personal identification\"\n- **Deterministic Address Generation**: \"Generate predictable wallet addresses from private data\"\n- **ZK Proof Integration**: \"Add zero-knowledge proof verification to ERC-4337 wallet\"\n- **Privacy Auditing**: \"Validate that my smart contract doesn''t leak sensitive information\"\n\n## Quick Start Guide\n\n### 1. Understand the Requirements\n\nAsk the user these key questions:\n- What sensitive data needs protection? (vehicle plate, biometric, etc.)\n- Is deterministic address generation required?\n- Are ZK proofs needed, or is commitment hashing sufficient?\n- What is the target blockchain/testnet?\n\n### 2. Set Up the Project\n\n```bash\n# Copy contract templates\ncp -r assets/contracts/* ./contracts/\n\n# Install dependencies\ncd contracts\nnpm install\n\n# Compile contracts\nnpm run compile\n```\n\n### 3. Customize for Your Use Case\n\n**For vehicle-based wallets:**\n```solidity\n// Off-chain: Compute vehicle commitment\nconst plateNumber = \"ABC-1234\";\nconst userSalt = ethers.id(\"user-secret-entropy\");\nconst commitment = ethers.keccak256(\n    ethers.solidityPacked([\"string\", \"bytes32\"], [plateNumber, userSalt])\n);\n\n// Deploy account with commitment\nconst account = await factory.createAccount(\n    ownerAddress,\n    commitment,\n    12345  // deployment salt\n);\n```\n\n**For biometric/other sensitive data:**\n```solidity\n// Replace plateNumber with your sensitive data\nconst biometricHash = computeHash(biometricData);\nconst commitment = ethers.keccak256(\n    ethers.solidityPacked([\"bytes32\", \"bytes32\"], [biometricHash, userSalt])\n);\n```\n\n### 4. Run Privacy Validation\n\n```bash\n# Validate that contracts don''t leak sensitive data\npython scripts/validate_privacy.py contracts/PrivacyProtectedAccount.sol\n```\n\n### 5. Run Tests\n\n```bash\n# Run comprehensive test suite\nnpm test\n\n# Run specific test file\nnpx hardhat test tests/PrivacyProtectedAccount.test.ts\n```\n\n## Core Components\n\n### 1. PrivacyProtectedAccount\n\nThe main account contract that implements ERC-4337''s `IAccount` interface with privacy features.\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Stores only commitment (hash) of sensitive data, never raw values\n- Deterministic address generation via CREATE2\n- ERC-4337 compliant UserOperation validation\n- Owner-based access control\n- Batch transaction execution\n\n**Usage:**\n```solidity\n// Deploy via factory\nconst account = await factory.createAccount(owner, vehicleCommitment, salt);\n\n// Verify ownership without revealing data\nconst isValid = await account.verifyVehicleOwnership(plateNumber, userSalt);\n\n// Execute transaction\nawait account.execute(targetAddress, value, calldata);\n```\n\n**Privacy Guarantee:**\n- Vehicle commitment is stored as `bytes32` hash\n- Raw plate number never touches blockchain\n- Verification is view-only (off-chain safe)\n\n### 2. AccountFactory\n\nFactory contract for deploying PrivacyProtectedAccount instances with deterministic addresses.\n\n**Key Features:**\n- CREATE2-based deterministic deployment\n- Counterfactual address computation\n- Batch account creation\n- Cross-chain address consistency\n\n**Usage:**\n```solidity\n// Compute address before deployment\nconst predictedAddress = await factory.getAddress(owner, commitment, salt);\n\n// Deploy account\nconst account = await factory.createAccount(owner, commitment, salt);\n\n// Address matches prediction\nassert(accountAddress === predictedAddress);\n```\n\n**Use Cases:**\n- Receive funds before account creation\n- Consistent addresses across multiple chains\n- Privacy-preserving wallet generation\n\n### 3. VehicleRegistry\n\nOptional registry contract for managing vehicle-to-wallet mappings with privacy.\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Maps commitments to wallet addresses\n- Authorized verifier system\n- Selective disclosure support\n- Batch registration\n\n**Usage:**\n```solidity\n// Register vehicle with commitment only\nawait registry.registerVehicle(commitment, walletAddress, metadataHash);\n\n// Verify registration (authorized only)\nconst isRegistered = await registry.verifyVehicleRegistration(commitment);\n\n// Update commitment (ownership transfer)\nawait registry.updateVehicleCommitment(oldCommitment, newCommitment);\n```\n\n## Implementation Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Define Privacy Model\n\nDetermine what needs privacy protection:\n\n**Example - Vehicle Wallet:**\n```\nSensitive: License plate number\nPublic: Wallet address, transaction history\nCommitment: keccak256(plateNumber + salt)\n```\n\n**Example - Biometric Wallet:**\n```\nSensitive: Fingerprint hash\nPublic: Wallet address\nCommitment: keccak256(fingerprintHash + salt)\n```\n\n### Step 2: Generate Commitment Off-Chain\n\n**CRITICAL: Never pass raw sensitive data to blockchain functions.**\n\n```javascript\n// Frontend/Backend - OFF-CHAIN computation\nimport { ethers } from ''ethers'';\n\nfunction generateCommitment(sensitiveData, userSecret) {\n    // Generate cryptographically secure salt\n    const salt = ethers.keccak256(\n        ethers.solidityPacked(\n            [''string'', ''uint256'', ''address''],\n            [userSecret, Date.now(), userAddress]\n        )\n    );\n\n    // Compute commitment\n    const commitment = ethers.keccak256(\n        ethers.solidityPacked([''string'', ''bytes32''], [sensitiveData, salt])\n    );\n\n    return { commitment, salt };\n}\n\n// Usage\nconst { commitment, salt } = generateCommitment(licensePlate, userSecret);\n// Store salt securely off-chain!\n// Send only commitment to blockchain\n```\n\n### Step 3: Deploy Account\n\n```javascript\n// Connect to factory\nconst factory = await ethers.getContractAt(''AccountFactory'', factoryAddress);\n\n// Optional: Predict address first\nconst predictedAddress = await factory.getAddress(\n    ownerAddress,\n    commitment,\n    deploymentSalt\n);\nconsole.log(''Account will be deployed at:'', predictedAddress);\n\n// Deploy account\nconst tx = await factory.createAccount(ownerAddress, commitment, deploymentSalt);\nawait tx.wait();\n\nconsole.log(''Account deployed at:'', predictedAddress);\n```\n\n### Step 4: Create and Submit UserOperation\n\n```javascript\nimport { ethers } from ''ethers'';\n\n// Build UserOperation\nconst userOp = {\n    sender: accountAddress,\n    nonce: await account.getNonce(),\n    initCode: ''0x'',  // Empty if account exists\n    callData: account.interface.encodeFunctionData(''execute'', [\n        targetAddress,\n        value,\n        data\n    ]),\n    accountGasLimits: ethers.solidityPacked(\n        [''uint128'', ''uint128''],\n        [verificationGasLimit, callGasLimit]\n    ),\n    preVerificationGas,\n    gasFees: ethers.solidityPacked(\n        [''uint128'', ''uint128''],\n        [maxPriorityFeePerGas, maxFeePerGas]\n    ),\n    paymasterAndData: ''0x'',  // Or paymaster address + data\n    signature: ''0x''  // Will be filled after signing\n};\n\n// Sign UserOperation\nconst userOpHash = await account.getUserOpHash(userOp);\nconst signature = await owner.signMessage(ethers.getBytes(userOpHash));\nuserOp.signature = signature;\n\n// Submit to bundler\nawait bundler.sendUserOperation(userOp);\n```\n\n### Step 5: Verify Privacy Protection\n\n```bash\n# Run automated privacy validation\npython scripts/validate_privacy.py contracts/YourContract.sol\n\n# Expected output:\n# ✅ PRIVACY VALIDATION PASSED\n# No privacy violations detected.\n```\n\n## Privacy Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Basic Commitment\n\n```solidity\n// Off-chain\nconst commitment = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(sensitiveData, salt));\n\n// On-chain\nbytes32 public dataCommitment;\n\nfunction initialize(bytes32 _commitment) external {\n    dataCommitment = _commitment;\n}\n\nfunction verify(string memory data, bytes32 salt) external view returns (bool) {\n    return keccak256(abi.encodePacked(data, salt)) == dataCommitment;\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Multi-Attribute Commitment\n\n```solidity\n// For vehicles with multiple attributes\nstruct VehicleData {\n    string plateNumber;\n    string model;\n    uint256 year;\n}\n\n// Off-chain\nconst commitment = keccak256(abi.encode(\n    vehicleData.plateNumber,\n    vehicleData.model,\n    vehicleData.year,\n    salt\n));\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: ZK Proof Integration\n\nFor advanced privacy (see `references/privacy-patterns.md` for full examples):\n\n```solidity\n// Verify ZK proof instead of revealing data\nfunction _validateSignature(\n    PackedUserOperation calldata userOp,\n    bytes32 userOpHash\n) internal override returns (uint256) {\n    (bytes memory proof, bytes memory publicInputs) =\n        abi.decode(userOp.signature, (bytes, bytes));\n\n    require(zkVerifier.verify(proof, publicInputs), \"Invalid proof\");\n    return SIG_VALIDATION_SUCCESS;\n}\n```\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Privacy Tests\n\n```typescript\ndescribe(\"Privacy Protection\", () => {\n    it(\"should not store raw sensitive data\", async () => {\n        // Verify storage doesn''t contain plate number\n        for (let i = 0; i < 20; i++) {\n            const storage = await ethers.provider.getStorage(account.address, i);\n            expect(storage).to.not.include(ethers.hexlify(ethers.toUtf8Bytes(plateNumber)));\n        }\n    });\n\n    it(\"should verify with correct preimage\", async () => {\n        const isValid = await account.verifyVehicleOwnership(plateNumber, salt);\n        expect(isValid).to.be.true;\n    });\n\n    it(\"should reject wrong preimage\", async () => {\n        const isValid = await account.verifyVehicleOwnership(\"WRONG-PLATE\", salt);\n        expect(isValid).to.be.false;\n    });\n});\n```\n\n### ERC-4337 Tests\n\n```typescript\ndescribe(\"UserOperation Validation\", () => {\n    it(\"should validate correct signature\", async () => {\n        const userOp = buildUserOp({ sender: account.address });\n        const userOpHash = await entryPoint.getUserOpHash(userOp);\n        userOp.signature = await owner.signMessage(ethers.getBytes(userOpHash));\n\n        await expect(entryPoint.handleOps([userOp], bundler.address))\n            .to.not.be.reverted;\n    });\n});\n```\n\n## Security Checklist\n\nBefore deploying to mainnet, verify:\n\n- [ ] Run privacy validation: `python scripts/validate_privacy.py`\n- [ ] All tests passing: `npm test`\n- [ ] No raw sensitive data in storage or events\n- [ ] Commitment generation uses strong salt (≥256 bits entropy)\n- [ ] Verification functions are `view` or `pure`\n- [ ] Access control properly implemented\n- [ ] EntryPoint address is correct\n- [ ] Contracts verified on Etherscan\n- [ ] Professional security audit completed\n\nSee `references/security-checklist.md` for complete checklist.\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n### ❌ Storing Raw Sensitive Data\n\n```solidity\n// NEVER DO THIS\ncontract BadExample {\n    string public licensePlate;  // Publicly visible!\n}\n```\n\n### ✅ Correct Approach\n\n```solidity\n// DO THIS\ncontract GoodExample {\n    bytes32 public vehicleCommitment;  // Only hash stored\n}\n```\n\n### ❌ Weak Salt Generation\n\n```solidity\n// WEAK - predictable\nbytes32 salt = bytes32(block.timestamp);\n```\n\n### ✅ Strong Salt\n\n```solidity\n// STRONG - unique per user with high entropy\nbytes32 salt = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\n    userSecret,\n    block.timestamp,\n    block.prevrandao,\n    msg.sender\n));\n```\n\n### ❌ Exposing Data in Events\n\n```solidity\n// NEVER DO THIS\nevent VehicleRegistered(string plateNumber);\n```\n\n### ✅ Events with Commitments\n\n```solidity\n// DO THIS\nevent VehicleRegistered(bytes32 indexed commitment);\n```\n\n## Advanced Topics\n\n### ZK-SNARK Integration\n\nFor zero-knowledge proof integration, see `references/privacy-patterns.md` section on ZK proofs.\n\n**High-level flow:**\n1. Generate ZK circuit for vehicle ownership\n2. Prove knowledge of plate number without revealing it\n3. Verify proof on-chain in `_validateSignature()`\n\n### Cross-Chain Deployment\n\n```bash\n# Deploy to multiple networks with same addresses\nnpx hardhat run scripts/deploy.ts --network sepolia\nnpx hardhat run scripts/deploy.ts --network polygonAmoy\n\n# Addresses match due to CREATE2 determinism\n```\n\n### Gasless Transactions with Paymaster\n\n```javascript\n// Add paymaster to UserOperation\nuserOp.paymasterAndData = ethers.solidityPacked(\n    [''address'', ''bytes''],\n    [paymasterAddress, paymasterData]\n);\n\n// User doesn''t pay gas - paymaster sponsors it\n```\n\n## Resources\n\n### Bundled Resources\n\n- **`assets/contracts/`**: Production-ready contract templates\n  - `PrivacyProtectedAccount.sol` - Main account contract\n  - `AccountFactory.sol` - Deterministic factory\n  - `VehicleRegistry.sol` - Optional registry\n  - `package.json`, `hardhat.config.ts` - Project setup\n\n- **`assets/tests/`**: Comprehensive test suites\n  - Privacy protection tests\n  - ERC-4337 compliance tests\n  - Gas optimization tests\n\n- **`scripts/validate_privacy.py`**: Automated privacy validation tool\n  - Scans for sensitive data leaks\n  - Validates commitment patterns\n  - Checks event safety\n\n- **`references/`**: In-depth documentation\n  - `erc4337-architecture.md` - ERC-4337 deep dive\n  - `privacy-patterns.md` - Privacy implementation patterns\n  - `security-checklist.md` - Comprehensive security guide\n\n### External Resources\n\n- [ERC-4337 Specification](https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-4337)\n- [Account Abstraction Docs](https://docs.erc4337.io/)\n- [MynaWallet Reference](https://github.com/MynaWallet/monorepo)\n- [Toyota MON](https://www.toyota-blockchain-lab.org/)\n- [OpenZeppelin Contracts](https://docs.openzeppelin.com/contracts/)\n\n## Support and Troubleshooting\n\n### Common Issues\n\n**Issue: Gas estimation fails**\n```\nSolution: Ensure account has sufficient deposit in EntryPoint\nawait account.addDeposit({ value: ethers.parseEther(\"0.1\") });\n```\n\n**Issue: Signature validation fails**\n```\nSolution: Check that userOpHash is computed correctly\nconst userOpHash = await entryPoint.getUserOpHash(userOp);\n```\n\n**Issue: Privacy validation fails**\n```\nSolution: Review reported violations and fix\n- Remove string storage for sensitive data\n- Make verification functions view/pure\n- Use commitments instead of raw data\n```\n\n### Getting Help\n\n1. Check `references/` for detailed documentation\n2. Review test files for usage examples\n3. Run privacy validation for security issues\n4. Consult ERC-4337 documentation for protocol questions\n\n## 参考文献\n- [ETHGlobalTokyo上位チーム勝手に解説 Myna](https://zenn.dev/kozayupapa/scraps/782815787c5c33)\n- [a42inc/ETHGlobalTokyo2023](https://github.com/a42inc/ETHGlobalTokyo2023)\n- [マイナンバーカードの公開鍵からSmartAccountのアドレスを一意に導出する方法 Study](https://zenn.dev/kozayupapa/articles/b0025b213ed39f)\n- [マイナンバーカードで署名をするところを動かしてみよう:ERC-4337 (AccountAbstraction)](https://zenn.dev/kozayupapa/articles/3347b360712b12)\n- [MynaWallet/monorepo](https://github.com/MynaWallet/monorepo)\n- [【Account Abstraction】UserOperation周りの具体的な実装について](https://zenn.dev/pokena/articles/84e243cf91a2cf)\n- [マイナウォレットメモ](https://zenn.dev/pokena/scraps/c8d8189a1c6cb9)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:59:53.601Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Ethereum-based AI Agents requiring secure and private wallet implementations with ERC-4337 compliance.","zh":"适用于需要安全和私有钱包实现的以太坊基于人工智能代理，符合ERC-4337标准。","ja":"EthereumベースのAIエージェントが、セキュアでプライベートなウォレット実装とERC-4337に準拠したものに適しています。","ko":"ERC-4337 규격을 준수하는 보안 및 사적 지갑 구현이 필요한 이더리움 기반 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA basados en Ethereum que requieren implementaciones de billeteras seguras y privadas con cumplimiento de ERC-4337.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''IA basés sur Ethereum nécessitant des mises en œuvre de portefeuilles sécurisés et privés conformes à la norme ERC-4337.","de":"Ideal für auf Ethereum basierende KI-Agents, die sichere und private Wallet-Implementierungen mit ERC-4337-Konformität erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA baseados em Ethereum que exigem implementações de carteira seguras e privadas com conformidade ERC-4337.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ на основе Ethereum, требующих безопасных и частных реализаций кошелька с соблюдением ERC-4337.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الإيثرียม المستند إلى وكيل الإيثرียม الذي يتطلب تطبيقات محفظة آمنة وخاصة مع امتثال ERC-4337."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to develop Account Abstraction wallets with privacy-preserving features, utilizing smart contract templates, testing frameworks, and security best practices to protect user privacy while maintaining on-chain functionality, specifically with ERC-4337 protocol and privacy validation tools.","zh":"赋予代理开发具有隐私保护功能的账户抽象钱包的能力，利用智能合约模板、测试框架和安全最佳实践保护用户隐私，同时保持链上功能，特别是使用ERC-4337协议和隐私验证工具。","ja":"スマートコントラクトテンプレート、テストフレームワーク、セキュリティベストプラクティスを使用して、プライバシを保護しながらオンチェーン機能を維持する、プライバシ保護機能を備えたアカウント抽象化ウォレットを開発するエージェントの能力を提供する、特にERC-4337プロトコルとプライバシ検証ツールを使用。","ko":"스마트 계약 템플릿, 테스트 프레임워크 및 보안最佳实践을 사용하여 프라이버시를 보호하면서 온체인 기능을 유지하는 프라이버시 보호 기능을 갖춘 계정 추상화 월렛을 개발할 수 있는 에이전트의 능력을 부여하며, 특히 ERC-4337 프로토콜 및 프라이버시 검증 도구를 사용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes desarrollar billeteras de abstracción de cuentas con características de preservación de la privacidad, utilizando plantillas de contratos inteligentes, marcos de prueba y mejores prácticas de seguridad para proteger la privacidad del usuario mientras mantiene la funcionalidad en la cadena, específicamente con el protocolo ERC-4337 y herramientas de validación de privacidad.","fr":"Permet aux agents de développer des portefeuilles d''abstraction de comptes avec des fonctionnalités de préservation de la vie privée, en utilisant des modèles de contrats intelligents, des cadres de test et des meilleures pratiques de sécurité pour protéger la vie privée de l''utilisateur tout en maintenant la fonctionnalité sur la chaîne, spécifiquement avec le protocole ERC-4337 et des outils de validation de la vie privée.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Kontenabstraktions-Wallets mit privatsphärenschützenden Funktionen zu entwickeln, indem es intelligente Vertragsvorlagen, Testframeworks und Sicherheitsbest Practices zur Schutz der Benutzerprivatsphäre bei gleichzeitiger Aufrechterhaltung der Funktionalität in der Chain nutzt, speziell mit dem ERC-4337-Protokoll und Privatsphärenvalidierungstools.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a desenvolver carteiras de Abstração de Conta com recursos de preservação da privacidade, utilizando modelos de contrato inteligente, estruturas de teste e melhores práticas de segurança para proteger a privacidade do usuário enquanto mantém a funcionalidade na cadeia, especificamente com o protocolo ERC-4337 e ferramentas de validação de privacidade.","ru":"Позволяет агентам разрабатывать кошельки абстракции учетной записи с функциями сохранения конфиденциальности, используя шаблоны умных контрактов, фреймворки тестирования и лучшие практики безопасности для защиты конфиденциальности пользователя при сохранении функциональности в цепочке, в частности с протоколом ERC-4337 и инструментами проверки конфиденциальности.","ar":"يتمكن الوكلاء من تطوير محافظ الت 抽象 الحساب مع الميزات الحافظة للخصوصية، باستخدام قوالب العقد الذكي، وأطر الاختبار، وأفضل الممارسات الأمنية لحماية خصوصية المستخدم مع الحفاظ على الوظائف في السلسلة، على وجه التحديد مع بروتوكول ERC-4337 وأدوات التحقق من الخصوصية."},"useCases":{"en":["Developing secure and private wallets for vehicle identity and sensitive data use cases","Implementing ERC-4337 compliant Account Abstraction wallets with smart contract templates","Validating privacy features in Ethereum-based wallets using specialized tools"],"zh":["为车辆身份和敏感数据使用场景开发安全和私有的钱包","使用智能合约模板实现符合ERC-4337的账户抽象化钱包","使用专用工具验证以太坊基于钱包的隐私功能"],"ja":["車両のアイデンティティや機密データの使用事例向けにセキュアでプライベートなウォレットを開発する","スマートコントラクトテンプレートを使用してERC-4337に準拠したアカウント抽象化ウォレットを実装する","専用ツールを使用してEthereumベースのウォレットのプライバシ機能を検証する"],"ko":["차량 식별 및 민감한 데이터 사용 사례를 위한 보안 및 사적 지갑 개발","스마트 계약 템플릿을 사용하여 ERC-4337 규격의 계정 추상화 월렛 구현","전용 도구를 사용하여 이더리움 기반 월렛의 프라이버시 기능 검증"],"es":["Desarrollar billeteras seguras y privadas para casos de uso de identidad de vehículos y datos sensibles","Implementar billeteras de abstracción de cuentas compatibles con ERC-4337 con plantillas de contratos inteligentes","Validar características de privacidad en billeteras basadas en Ethereum utilizando herramientas especializadas"],"fr":["Développer des portefeuilles sécurisés et privés pour les cas d''utilisation d''identité de véhicules et de données sensibles","Mettre en œuvre des portefeuilles d''abstraction de comptes conformes à la norme ERC-4337 avec des modèles de contrats intelligents","Valider les fonctionnalités de vie privée dans les portefeuilles basés sur Ethereum en utilisant des outils spécialisés"],"de":["Sichere und private Wallets für Fahrzeugidentitäts- und sensible Datenanwendungsfälle entwickeln","ERC-4337-konforme Kontenabstraktions-Wallets mit intelligenten Vertragsvorlagen implementieren","Privatsphärenfunktionen in Ethereum-basierten Wallets mithilfe spezieller Tools validieren"],"pt":["Desenvolver carteiras seguras e privadas para casos de uso de identidade de veículo e dados sensíveis","Implementar carteiras de Abstração de Conta compatíveis com ERC-4337 com modelos de contrato inteligente","Validar recursos de privacidade em carteiras baseadas em Ethereum usando ferramentas especializadas"],"ru":["Разрабатывать безопасные и частные кошельки для случаев использования идентификатора транспортного средства и конфиденциальных данных","Реализовывать кошельки абстракции учетной записи, совместимые с ERC-4337, с шаблонами умного контракта","Проверять функции конфиденциальности в кошельках на основе Ethereum с помощью специализированных инструментов"],"ar":["تطوير محافظ آمنة وخاصة لحالات استخدام هوية السيارة والبيانات الحساسة","تنفيذ محافظ 抽象 الحساب المتوافقة مع ERC-4337 باستخدام قوالب العقد الذكي","التحقق من ميزات الخصوصية في محافظ الإيثرียม باستخدام أدوات متخصصة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of Ethereum smart contracts and ERC-4337 protocol","Limited to Ethereum-based applications","Dependent on specific testing frameworks and security best practices"],"zh":["需要以太坊智能合约和ERC-4337协议的知识","仅限以太坊基于应用","依赖于特定的测试框架和安全最佳实践"],"ja":["EthereumスマートコントラクトとERC-4337プロトコルの知識が必要","Ethereumベースのアプリケーションに限定される","特定のテストフレームワークとセキュリティベストプラクティスに依存する"],"ko":["이더리움 스마트 계약 및 ERC-4337 프로토콜에 대한 지식 필요","이더리움 기반 응용 프로그램으로 제한됨","특정 테스트 프레임워크 및 보안最佳实践에 의존"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de contratos inteligentes de Ethereum y protocolo ERC-4337","Limitado a aplicaciones basadas en Ethereum","Dependiente de marcos de prueba y mejores prácticas de seguridad específicos"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance des contrats intelligents Ethereum et du protocole ERC-4337","Limité aux applications basées sur Ethereum","Dépendant de cadres de test et de meilleures pratiques de sécurité spécifiques"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse von Ethereum-Smart-Contracts und ERC-4337-Protokoll","Begrenzt auf Ethereum-basierte Anwendungen","Abhängig von bestimmten Testframeworks und Sicherheitsbest Practices"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento de contratos inteligentes do Ethereum e protocolo ERC-4337","Limitado a aplicações baseadas em Ethereum","Dependente de estruturas de teste específicas e melhores práticas de segurança"],"ru":["Требует знания умных контрактов Ethereum и протокола ERC-4337","Ограничен для приложений на основе Ethereum","Зависит от конкретных фреймворков тестирования и лучших практик безопасности"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة العقود الذكية الإيثرียม وبروتوكول ERC-4337","محدود للتطبيقات المستندة إلى الإيثرียม","يعتمد على أطر الاختبار المحددة وأفضل الممارسات الأمنية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Light-Brands/planetary-party-html/brainstorming', 'community', 'Light-Brands', 'planetary-party-html', 'Light-Brands/planetary-party-html', 'brainstorming', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.415Z', '2026-02-18T03:59:43.489Z', NULL, '{"id":"Light-Brands/planetary-party-html/brainstorming","name":"brainstorming","description":{"zh":"头脑风暴是一种将粗略想法转化为成熟设计的方法，通过自然的协作对话来实现。它帮助开发者了解上下文，探索替代方案，逐步验证设计决策","ja":"ブレーンストーミングは、自然なコラボレーションの対話を通じて、アイデアを完成した設計に変える方法です。コンテキストを理解し、代替案を探り、段階的に検証することで設計決定を助けることを目指しています","ko":"브레인스토밍은 자연적인 협력 대화를 통해 粗略한 아이디어를 완성된 설계로 만드는 방법입니다. 컨텍스트를 이해하고 대안을 탐색하며 점진적으로 검증하여 설계 결정에 도움을 줍니다","es":"La técnica de lluvia de ideas permite a los desarrolladores convertir ideas rough en diseños completamente formados a través del diálogo colaborativo natural","fr":"La technique de remue-méninges permet aux développeurs de convertir les idées rough en conceptions complètement formées grâce au dialogue collaboratif naturel","de":"Die Brainstorming-Technik ermöglicht es Entwicklern, grobe Ideen in vollständig ausgearbeitete Entwürfe durch natürlichen kollaborativen Dialog umzuwandeln","pt":"O brainstorming é uma técnica para desenvolver ideias em design através do diálogo colaborativo natural","ru":"Мозговой штурм - это техника для разработки идей в дизайне посредством естественного сотрудничества","ar":"العصف الذهني هو تقنية لتنمية الأفكار في التصميم من خلال الحوار التعاوني الطبيعي","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"头脑风暴：将粗略想法转化为成熟设计","ja":"ブレーンストーミング：アイデアを完成した設計に","ko":"브레인스토밍: الخام 아이디어를 완성된 설계로","es":"Técnica de lluvia de ideas para desarrolladores","fr":"Technique de remue-méninges pour les développeurs","de":"Brainstorming-Technik für Entwickler","pt":"Brainstorming: Desenvolva Ideias em Design","ru":"Мозговой штурм: Разработка идей в дизайне","ar":"العصف الذهني: تنمية الأفكار في التصميم","en":"brainstorming"},"description":{"zh":"头脑风暴是一种将粗略想法转化为成熟设计的方法，通过自然的协作对话来实现。它帮助开发者了解上下文，探索替代方案，逐步验证设计决策","ja":"ブレーンストーミングは、自然なコラボレーションの対話を通じて、アイデアを完成した設計に変える方法です。コンテキストを理解し、代替案を探り、段階的に検証することで設計決定を助けることを目指しています","ko":"브레인스토밍은 자연적인 협력 대화를 통해 粗略한 아이디어를 완성된 설계로 만드는 방법입니다. 컨텍스트를 이해하고 대안을 탐색하며 점진적으로 검증하여 설계 결정에 도움을 줍니다","es":"La técnica de lluvia de ideas permite a los desarrolladores convertir ideas rough en diseños completamente formados a través del diálogo colaborativo natural","fr":"La technique de remue-méninges permet aux développeurs de convertir les idées rough en conceptions complètement formées grâce au dialogue collaboratif naturel","de":"Die Brainstorming-Technik ermöglicht es Entwicklern, grobe Ideen in vollständig ausgearbeitete Entwürfe durch natürlichen kollaborativen Dialog umzuwandeln","pt":"O brainstorming é uma técnica para desenvolver ideias em design através do diálogo colaborativo natural","ru":"Мозговой штурм - это техника для разработки идей в дизайне посредством естественного сотрудничества","ar":"العصف الذهني هو تقنية لتنمية الأفكار في التصميم من خلال الحوار التعاوني الطبيعي","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["自然协作对话","上下文理解","替代方案探索","逐步验证","设计决策支持"],"ja":["自然なコラボレーションの対話","コンテキストの理解","代替案の探索","段階的な検証","設計決定の支援"],"ko":["자연적인 협력 대화","컨텍스트 이해","대안 탐색","점진적인 검증","설계 결정 지원"],"es":["Generación de ideas y soluciones","Diálogo colaborativo natural","Validación incremental de ideas","Exploración de alternativas","Refinamiento de diseños"],"fr":["Génération d''idées et de solutions","Dialogue collaboratif naturel","Validation incrémentale des idées","Exploration d''alternatives","Affinement de conceptions"],"de":["Erzeugung von Ideen und Lösungen","Natürlicher kollaborativer Dialog","Inkrementale Validierung von Ideen","Erkundung von Alternativen","Verfeinerung von Entwürfen"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de ideias em design","Diálogo colaborativo natural","Exploração de alternativas","Validação incremental","Refinamento de designs"],"ru":["Разработка идей в дизайне","Естественное сотрудничество","Изучение альтернатив","Постепенная проверка","Уточнение дизайнов"],"ar":["تنمية الأفكار في التصميم","حوار تعاوني طبيعي","استكشاف البدائل","التحقق المتدرج","تحسين التصاميم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["头脑风暴","协作设计","自然对话","设计决策","开发方法","软件开发","产品设计"],"ja":["ブレーンストーミング","コラボレーションデザイン","自然な対話","設計決定","開発方法","ソフトウェア開発","プロダクトデザイン"],"ko":["브레인스토밍","협력 설계","자연적인 대화","설계 결정","개발 방법","소프트웨어 개발","제품 디자인"],"es":["lluvia de ideas","desarrollo de software","colaboración en equipo","generación de ideas","diseño de soluciones","validación incremental"],"fr":["remue-méninges","développement de logiciels","collaboration d''équipe","génération d''idées","conception de solutions","validation incrémentale"],"de":["Brainstorming","Software-Entwicklung","Team-Kollaboration","Erzeugung von Ideen","Entwurf von Lösungen","inkrementale Validierung"],"pt":["brainstorming","desenvolvimento de ideias","design","diálogo colaborativo","validação incremental","refinamento de designs","técnica de design","criatividade em design"],"ru":["мозговой штурм","разработка идей","дизайн","естественное сотрудничество","постепенная проверка","уточнение дизайнов","техника дизайна","креативность в дизайне"],"ar":["العصف الذهني","تنمية الأفكار","التصميم","الحوار التعاوني","التحقق المتدرج","تحسين التصاميم","تقنية التصميم","الابتكار في التصميم"]}},"owner":"Light-Brands","repo":"planetary-party-html","repoPath":"Light-Brands/planetary-party-html","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.415Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"brainstorming","description":"Use when rough ideas need design before code or multiple approaches","version":"0.2.0","bodyPreview":"<objective>\nTurn rough ideas into fully-formed designs through natural collaborative dialogue. Understand the context, explore alternatives, validate incrementally.\n\nCore principle: Ask questions to understand, present options to explore, validate\nsections to refine. </objective>\n\n<when-to-use>\nUse brainstorming when you have a rough idea but unclear implementation, multiple approaches exist and you need to choose, requirements are fuzzy or incomplete, or design decisions need validation before","body":"<objective>\nTurn rough ideas into fully-formed designs through natural collaborative dialogue. Understand the context, explore alternatives, validate incrementally.\n\nCore principle: Ask questions to understand, present options to explore, validate\nsections to refine. </objective>\n\n<when-to-use>\nUse brainstorming when you have a rough idea but unclear implementation, multiple approaches exist and you need to choose, requirements are fuzzy or incomplete, or design decisions need validation before coding.\n\nSkip for clear mechanical tasks with obvious solutions, well-defined requirements with\nstandard implementations, or simple bug fixes. </when-to-use>\n\n<understanding-context>\nExplore the current project state. Check existing files, documentation, recent commits. Understand what''s already built.\n\nAsk questions one at a time to refine the idea. Use multiple choice when possible -\neasier to answer than open-ended. Focus on understanding purpose (what problem does this\nsolve?), constraints (what limits the solution?), and success criteria (how do we know\nit works?).\n\nOne question per message. If a topic needs more exploration, break it into multiple\nquestions. Don''t overwhelm with a list of questions. </understanding-context>\n\n<exploring-alternatives>\nPropose different approaches with their tradeoffs. Present conversationally, showing all options first before making a recommendation.\n\nExample pattern: \"I see three main approaches:\n\n1. Direct integration - Fast to implement but creates coupling. Good if this is\n   temporary.\n\n2. Event-driven - More flexible, better separation, but adds complexity. Worth it if\n   we''ll extend this.\n\n3. Separate service - Maximum isolation, easier to scale, but operational overhead.\n   Overkill unless we need independent scaling.\n\nI''d recommend #2 (event-driven) because the requirements suggest we''ll add features\nhere, and the loose coupling will make that easier. What do you think?\"\n\nPresent options before recommendation. LLMs process information sequentially - showing\noptions first lets them fully consider each alternative before being influenced by a\nrecommendation. The recommendation comes after all options have been presented.\n\nMake a clear recommendation - pick one approach and explain why it fits best. Don''t\nhedge or suggest combining approaches.\n\nAvoid defaulting to hybrid approaches. Hybrid solutions are rarely the right answer.\nThey often combine the complexity of multiple approaches without clear benefits. Only\nsuggest a hybrid if there''s a specific, compelling reason why a pure approach won''t\nwork.\n\nStructure alternatives clearly - each option should be distinct with clear tradeoffs. If\noptions are too similar, you haven''t explored the design space enough.\n\nExplain the choice criteria - make explicit what factors led to your recommendation\n(simplicity, performance, maintainability, etc.). This helps validate whether the\nrecommendation aligns with priorities.\n\nLet the human partner react after your recommendation. They may have constraints or\npriorities you didn''t consider. </exploring-alternatives>\n\n<presenting-design>\nOnce you understand what you''re building, present the design in small, manageable sections covering architecture and component structure, data flow and state management, error handling and edge cases, and testing approach.\n\nAsk after each section whether it looks right. Be ready to go back and clarify if\nsomething doesn''t make sense.\n\nThis incremental validation catches misunderstandings early before you''ve written a\ncomplete design document. </presenting-design>\n\n<after-validation>\nWrite the validated design to docs/plans/[topic]-design.md. Keep it concise and focused on decisions and rationale, not implementation details.\n\nCommit the design document to git so it''s tracked with the project.\n\nIf continuing to implementation, ask whether to proceed. Set up an isolated workspace\nfor development (git worktree or feature branch). Create a detailed implementation plan\nbreaking the design into concrete tasks. </after-validation>\n\n<key-principles>\nOne question at a time. Don''t list multiple questions. Ask one, get an answer, ask the next.\n\nMultiple choice preferred. \"Should we use events or direct calls?\" is easier than \"How\nshould components communicate?\"\n\nYAGNI ruthlessly. Remove unnecessary features from designs. Build what''s needed, not\nwhat might be needed someday.\n\nExplore alternatives always. Present multiple approaches before settling on one. This\nsurfaces tradeoffs. Choose one clear recommendation - avoid defaulting to hybrid\napproaches which rarely solve the problem well.\n\nIncremental validation. Present design in sections, validate each before continuing.\nDon''t write a complete design then ask for feedback - you might be heading the wrong\ndirection.\n\nBe flexible. When something doesn''t make sense to your partner, go back and clarify.\nDon''t defend the design, refine it. </key-principles>\n\n<common-pitfalls>\nDon''t ask many questions at once. Don''t present a complete design without incremental validation. Don''t skip exploring alternatives. Don''t add features beyond stated requirements. Don''t continue with a design that confuses your partner - go back and clarify first.\n</common-pitfalls>\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T03:59:43.489Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Conversational Agents like Claude Code and LangChain needing collaborative dialogue for design refinement","zh":"适合于需要协作对话来进行设计完善的对话式代理，如Claude Code和LangChain","ja":"Claude CodeやLangChainのような、設計の洗練のために共同の対話を必要とする会話エージェントに適しています","ko":"클라우드 코드나 랭체인과 같은 협력적 대화를 통해 설계를 정제해야 하는 대화형 에이전트에게 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes de conversación como Claude Code y LangChain que necesitan diálogo colaborativo para el refinamiento del diseño","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de conversation comme Claude Code et LangChain nécessitant un dialogue collaboratif pour l''affinement de la conception","de":"Ideal für Konversationsagenten wie Claude Code und LangChain, die ein kollaboratives Dialog für die Feinabstimmung von Designs benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Conversação como Claude Code e LangChain que necessitam de diálogo colaborativo para refinar projetos","ru":"Идеально для разговорных агентов, таких как Claude Code и LangChain, требующих совместного диалога для усовершенствования конструкции","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المحادثين مثل Claude Code و LangChain الذين يحتاجون إلى حوار تعاوني لتحسين التصميم"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to facilitate natural collaborative dialogue, presenting options to explore and validating sections to refine through incremental understanding, utilizing context exploration and alternative analysis protocols","zh":"赋予代理以促进自然的协作对话的能力，提出选项以探索，并通过增量理解来验证部分，从而完善设计，利用上下文探索和替代分析协议","ja":"エージェントに自然な共同の対話を促進する能力を与え、探索するための選択肢を提示し、段階的な理解を通じて設計を洗練し、コンテキストの探索と代替分析プロトコルを利用する","ko":"에이전트가 자연스러운 협력적 대화를 촉진할 수 있도록 하며, 탐색할 수 있는 옵션을 제시하고, 점진적인 이해를 통해 부분을 검증하여 설계를 정제하고, 문맥 탐색 및 대체 분석 프로토콜을 활용함으로써","es":"Permite a los agentes facilitar un diálogo colaborativo natural, presentando opciones para explorar y validando secciones para refinar a través de la comprensión incremental, utilizando protocolos de exploración de contexto y análisis alternativo","fr":"Permet aux agents de faciliter un dialogue collaboratif naturel, en présentant des options à explorer et en validant les sections à affiner par le biais d''une compréhension incrémentale, en utilisant des protocoles d''exploration de contexte et d''analyse alternative","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, ein natürliches kollaboratives Dialog zu erleichtern, indem Optionen zur Erforschung präsentiert und Abschnitte zur Feinabstimmung durch inkrementelles Verständnis validiert werden, unter Nutzung von Kontext-Erforschungs- und alternativen Analyseprotokollen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a facilitar diálogos colaborativos naturais, apresentando opções para explorar e validando seções para refinar por meio da compreensão incremental, utilizando protocolos de exploração de contexto e análise alternativa","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью облегчить естественный совместный диалог, предлагая варианты для изучения и проверки разделов для усовершенствования посредством пошагового понимания, используя протоколы исследования контекста и альтернативного анализа","ar":"يتمكن الوكلاء من تسهيل حوار تعاوني طبيعي، مع تقديم خيارات لاستكشافها وتصديق أقسام لتحسينها من خلال الفهم المتزايد، باستخدام بروتوكولات استكشاف السياق والتحليل البديل"},"useCases":{"en":["Refining rough ideas into fully-formed designs","Exploring multiple implementation approaches","Validating design decisions through iterative questioning"],"zh":["将粗略的想法完善为完整的设计","探索多种实现方法","通过迭代式提问验证设计决策"],"ja":["粗いアイデアを完全な設計に洗練する","複数の実装アプローチを探る","イテレーションによる質問を通じて設計の決定を検証する"],"ko":["조잡한 아이디어를 완전한 설계로 정제하는 것","다양한 구현 방식을 탐색하는 것","반복적인 질문을 통해 설계 결정을 검증하는 것"],"es":["Perfeccionar ideas rudimentarias en diseños completamente formados","Explorar múltiples enfoques de implementación","Validar decisiones de diseño a través de preguntas iterativas"],"fr":["Affiner les idées rudimentaires en conceptions entièrement formées","Explorer plusieurs approches d''implémentation","Valider les décisions de conception par le biais de questions itératives"],"de":["Rohideen in vollständig ausgebildete Designs verfeinern","Mehrere Implementierungsansätze erforschen","Entscheidungen über das Design durch iterative Fragestellungen validieren"],"pt":["Refinar ideias grosseiras em projetos completamente formados","Explorar várias abordagens de implementação","Validar decisões de projeto por meio de questionamento iterativo"],"ru":["Усовершенствовать грубые идеи в полностью сформированные конструкции","Изучить несколько подходов к реализации","Проверить решения по проектированию посредством итеративного вопроса"],"ar":["تحسين الأفكار الخشنة إلى تصاميم完全 متكشفة","استكشاف مناهج متعددة للتطبيق","تصديق قرارات التصميم من خلال الاستفهام التكراري"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires natural language understanding capabilities","Dependent on quality of initial ideas and context provided"],"zh":["需要自然语言理解能力","依赖于初始想法和提供的上下文的质量"],"ja":["自然言語の理解能力が必要","初期のアイデアと提供されたコンテキストの品質に依存する"],"ko":["자연어 이해 능력이 필요함","초기 아이디어와 제공된 문맥의 품질에 의존함"],"es":["Requiere capacidades de comprensión del lenguaje natural","Depende de la calidad de las ideas iniciales y del contexto proporcionado"],"fr":["Nécessite des capacités de compréhension du langage naturel","Dépend de la qualité des idées initiales et du contexte fourni"],"de":["Benötigt Fähigkeiten zur Verständigung in natürlicher Sprache","Hängt von der Qualität der anfänglichen Ideen und des bereitgestellten Kontexts ab"],"pt":["Exige capacidades de compreensão de linguagem natural","Depende da qualidade das ideias iniciais e do contexto fornecido"],"ru":["Требует возможностей понимания естественного языка","Зависит от качества первоначальных идей и предоставленного контекста"],"ar":["يتطلب قدرات فهم اللغة الطبيعية","يعتمد على جودة الأفكار الأولى والسياق المقدّم"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('pipecat-ai/pipecat/code-review', 'community', 'pipecat-ai', 'pipecat', 'pipecat-ai/pipecat', 'code-review', 0, 0, 35, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.415Z', '2026-02-18T04:00:25.788Z', NULL, '{"id":"pipecat-ai/pipecat/code-review","name":"code-review","description":{"zh":"代码审查是一种AI驱动的代码评审框架，帮助开发人员提高代码质量和开发效率","ja":"コードレビューは、開発者がコードの品質と開発効率を向上させるのに役立つAI駆動のコードレビューフレームワークです","ko":"코드 리뷰는 개발자가 코드 품질과 개발 효율을 향상시키는 데 도움이 되는 AI 기반 코드 리뷰 프레임워크입니다","es":"El skill de revisión de código es una herramienta fundamental para garantizar la calidad del código en proyectos de AI conversacional","fr":"Le skill de révision de code est un outil essentiel pour garantir la qualité du code dans les projets d''IA conversationnelle","de":"Das Code-Review-Skill ist ein grundlegendes Tool, um die Code-Qualität in konversationellen KI-Projekten sicherzustellen","pt":"O framework de código aberto para AI conversacional e multimodal permite revisões de código eficazes. Aprenda como utilizar essa ferramenta.","ru":"Открытый фреймворк для разговорного ИИ и мультимодального взаимодействия позволяет проводить эффективные обзоры кода. Узнайте, как использовать эту инструмент.","ar":"الإطار المفتوح للم源ة الاصطناعية المحادثية ومتعددة الوضعيات يسمح بمراجعات الكود الفعالة. تعلم كيفية استخدام هذه الأداة.","en":"Open Source framework for voice and multimodal conversational AI"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"代码审查：AI驱动的代码评审框架","ja":"コードレビュー：AI駆動のコードレビューフレームワーク","ko":"코드 리뷰: AI 기반 코드 리뷰 프레임워크","es":"Revisión de código para AI conversacional","fr":"Révision de code pour l''IA conversationnelle","de":"Code-Review für konversationelle KI","pt":"Revisão de Código para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Обзор Код для Разработчиков","ar":"مراجعة الكود لمطوري البرمجيات","en":"code-review"},"description":{"zh":"代码审查是一种AI驱动的代码评审框架，帮助开发人员提高代码质量和开发效率","ja":"コードレビューは、開発者がコードの品質と開発効率を向上させるのに役立つAI駆動のコードレビューフレームワークです","ko":"코드 리뷰는 개발자가 코드 품질과 개발 효율을 향상시키는 데 도움이 되는 AI 기반 코드 리뷰 프레임워크입니다","es":"El skill de revisión de código es una herramienta fundamental para garantizar la calidad del código en proyectos de AI conversacional","fr":"Le skill de révision de code est un outil essentiel pour garantir la qualité du code dans les projets d''IA conversationnelle","de":"Das Code-Review-Skill ist ein grundlegendes Tool, um die Code-Qualität in konversationellen KI-Projekten sicherzustellen","pt":"O framework de código aberto para AI conversacional e multimodal permite revisões de código eficazes. Aprenda como utilizar essa ferramenta.","ru":"Открытый фреймворк для разговорного ИИ и мультимодального взаимодействия позволяет проводить эффективные обзоры кода. Узнайте, как использовать эту инструмент.","ar":"الإطار المفتوح للم源ة الاصطناعية المحادثية ومتعددة الوضعيات يسمح بمراجعات الكود الفعالة. تعلم كيفية استخدام هذه الأداة.","en":"Open Source framework for voice and multimodal conversational AI"},"definition":{"en":"Open Source framework for voice and multimodal conversational AI"},"features":{"zh":["AI驱动的代码评审","自动化代码审查","代码质量提高","开发效率提升","支持多种编程语言"],"ja":["AI駆動のコードレビュー","自動化コード審査","コードの品質向上","開発効率の向上","複数のプログラミング言語をサポート"],"ko":["AI 기반 코드 리뷰","자동 코드审查","코드 품질 향상","개발 효율성 향상","다중 프로그래밍 언어 지원"],"es":["Análisis de código para detectar errores","Mejora de la calidad del código","Optimización del rendimiento","Seguimiento de los estándares de codificación","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["Analyse de code pour détecter les erreurs","Amélioration de la qualité du code","Optimisation des performances","Suivi des normes de codage","Intégration avec les outils de développement"],"de":["Code-Analyse zur Fehlererkennung","Verbesserung der Code-Qualität","Leistungsoptimierung","Einhaltung der Codierungsstandards","Integration mit Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["Análise de código-fonte","Verificação de erros","Otimização de desempenho","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento","Suporte a múltiplos linguagens de programação"],"ru":["Анализ исходного кода","Проверка ошибок","Оптимизация производительности","Интеграция с инструментами разработки","Поддержка нескольких языков программирования"],"ar":["تحليل الكود المصدري","التحقق من الأخطاء","تحسين الأداء","التكامل مع أدوات التطوير","دعم لغات برمجة متعددة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码审查","AI代码评审","代码质量","开发效率","自动化代码审查","代码审查工具"],"ja":["コードレビュー","AIコードレビュー","コードの品質","開発効率","自動化コード審査","コードレビューツール"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","AI 코드 리뷰","코드 품질","개발 효율성","자동 코드审查","코드 리뷰 도구"],"es":["revisión de código","AI conversacional","desarrollo de software","calidad del código","análisis de código","mejora del rendimiento"],"fr":["révision de code","IA conversationnelle","développement de logiciels","qualité du code","analyse de code","amélioration des performances"],"de":["Code-Review","konversationelle KI","Software-Entwicklung","Code-Qualität","Code-Analyse","Leistungsverbesserung"],"pt":["revisão de código","desenvolvimento de software","ai conversacional","multimodal","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","análise de código","otimização de desempenho"],"ru":["обзор кода","разработка программного обеспечения","разговорный ИИ","мультимодальный","инструменты разработки","анализ кода","оптимизация производительности"],"ar":["مراجعة الكود","تطوير البرمجيات","المصدرة الاصطناعية المحادثية","متعددة الوضعيات","أدوات التطوير","تحليل الكود","تحسين الأداء"]}},"owner":"pipecat-ai","repo":"pipecat","repoPath":"pipecat-ai/pipecat","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.415Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"code-review","description":"Automated code review for pull requests using multiple specialized agents","bodyPreview":"Provide a code review for the given pull request.\n\n**Agent assumptions (applies to all agents and subagents):**\n\n- All tools are functional and will work without error. Do not test tools or make exploratory calls. Make sure this is clear to every subagent that is launched.\n- Only call a tool if it is required to complete the task. Every tool call should have a clear purpose.\n\nTo do this, follow these steps precisely:\n\n1. Launch a haiku agent to check if any of the following are true:\n   - The pu","body":"Provide a code review for the given pull request.\n\n**Agent assumptions (applies to all agents and subagents):**\n\n- All tools are functional and will work without error. Do not test tools or make exploratory calls. Make sure this is clear to every subagent that is launched.\n- Only call a tool if it is required to complete the task. Every tool call should have a clear purpose.\n\nTo do this, follow these steps precisely:\n\n1. Launch a haiku agent to check if any of the following are true:\n   - The pull request is closed\n   - The pull request is a draft\n   - The pull request does not need code review (e.g. automated PR, trivial change that is obviously correct)\n   - Claude has already commented on this PR (check `gh pr view <PR> --comments` for comments left by claude)\n\n   If any condition is true, stop and do not proceed.\n\nNote: Still review Claude generated PR''s.\n\n2. Launch a haiku agent to return a list of file paths (not their contents) for all relevant CLAUDE.md files including:\n   - The root CLAUDE.md file, if it exists\n   - Any CLAUDE.md files in directories containing files modified by the pull request\n\n3. Launch a sonnet agent to view the pull request and return a summary of the changes\n\n4. Launch 4 agents in parallel to independently review the changes. Each agent should return the list of issues, where each issue includes a description and the reason it was flagged (e.g. \"CLAUDE.md adherence\", \"bug\"). The agents should do the following:\n\n   Agents 1 + 2: CLAUDE.md compliance sonnet agents\n   Audit changes for CLAUDE.md compliance in parallel. Note: When evaluating CLAUDE.md compliance for a file, you should only consider CLAUDE.md files that share a file path with the file or parents.\n\n   Agent 3: Opus bug agent (parallel subagent with agent 4)\n   Scan for obvious bugs. Focus only on the diff itself without reading extra context. Flag only significant bugs; ignore nitpicks and likely false positives. Do not flag issues that you cannot validate without looking at context outside of the git diff.\n\n   Agent 4: Opus bug agent (parallel subagent with agent 3)\n   Look for problems that exist in the introduced code. This could be security issues, incorrect logic, etc. Only look for issues that fall within the changed code.\n\n   **CRITICAL: We only want HIGH SIGNAL issues.** Flag issues where:\n   - The code will fail to compile or parse (syntax errors, type errors, missing imports, unresolved references)\n   - The code will definitely produce wrong results regardless of inputs (clear logic errors)\n   - Clear, unambiguous CLAUDE.md violations where you can quote the exact rule being broken\n\n   Do NOT flag:\n   - Code style or quality concerns\n   - Potential issues that depend on specific inputs or state\n   - Subjective suggestions or improvements\n\n   If you are not certain an issue is real, do not flag it. False positives erode trust and waste reviewer time.\n\n   In addition to the above, each subagent should be told the PR title and description. This will help provide context regarding the author''s intent.\n\n5. For each issue found in the previous step by agents 3 and 4, launch parallel subagents to validate the issue. These subagents should get the PR title and description along with a description of the issue. The agent''s job is to review the issue to validate that the stated issue is truly an issue with high confidence. For example, if an issue such as \"variable is not defined\" was flagged, the subagent''s job would be to validate that is actually true in the code. Another example would be CLAUDE.md issues. The agent should validate that the CLAUDE.md rule that was violated is scoped for this file and is actually violated. Use Opus subagents for bugs and logic issues, and sonnet agents for CLAUDE.md violations.\n\n6. Filter out any issues that were not validated in step 5. This step will give us our list of high signal issues for our review.\n\n7. If issues were found, skip to step 8 to post comments.\n\n   If NO issues were found, post a summary comment using `gh pr comment` (if `--comment` argument is provided):\n   \"No issues found. Checked for bugs and CLAUDE.md compliance.\"\n\n8. Create a list of all comments that you plan on leaving. This is only for you to make sure you are comfortable with the comments. Do not post this list anywhere.\n\n9. Post inline comments for each issue using `gh pr review` with inline comments. For each comment:\n   - Provide a brief description of the issue\n   - For small, self-contained fixes, include a committable suggestion block\n   - For larger fixes (6+ lines, structural changes, or changes spanning multiple locations), describe the issue and suggested fix without a suggestion block\n   - Never post a committable suggestion UNLESS committing the suggestion fixes the issue entirely. If follow up steps are required, do not leave a committable suggestion.\n\n   **IMPORTANT: Only post ONE comment per unique issue. Do not post duplicate comments.**\n\nUse this list when evaluating issues in Steps 4 and 5 (these are false positives, do NOT flag):\n\n- Pre-existing issues\n- Something that appears to be a bug but is actually correct\n- Pedantic nitpicks that a senior engineer would not flag\n- Issues that a linter will catch (do not run the linter to verify)\n- General code quality concerns (e.g., lack of test coverage, general security issues) unless explicitly required in CLAUDE.md\n- Issues mentioned in CLAUDE.md but explicitly silenced in the code (e.g., via a lint ignore comment)\n\nNotes:\n\n- Use gh CLI to interact with GitHub (e.g., fetch pull requests, create comments). Do not use web fetch.\n- Create a todo list before starting.\n- You must cite and link each issue in inline comments (e.g., if referring to a CLAUDE.md, include a link to it).\n- If no issues are found, post a comment with the following format:\n\n---\n\n## Code review\n\nNo issues found. Checked for bugs and CLAUDE.md compliance.\n\n---\n\n- When linking to code in inline comments, follow the following format precisely, otherwise the Markdown preview won''t render correctly: `https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/blob/FULL_SHA/path/to/file.py#L10-L15`\n  - Requires full git sha\n  - You must provide the full sha. Commands like `https://github.com/owner/repo/blob/$(git rev-parse HEAD)/foo/bar` will not work, since your comment will be directly rendered in Markdown.\n  - Repo name must match the repo you''re code reviewing\n  - # sign after the file name\n  - Line range format is L[start]-L[end]\n  - Provide at least 1 line of context before and after, centered on the line you are commenting about (eg. if you are commenting about lines 5-6, you should link to `L4-7`)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:00:25.788Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing advanced code analysis and review capabilities for open-source frameworks and multimodal conversational AI projects.","zh":"非常适合需要高级代码分析和审查能力的AI代理，尤其是用于开源框架和多模态对话式AI项目。","ja":"高度なコード分析およびレビュー機能を必要とするAIエージェントに最適で、オープンソースフレームワークやマルチモーダル会話AIプロジェクトに適しています。","ko":"고급 코드 분석 및 리뷰 기능이 필요한 AI 에이전트에게 적합하며, 오픈 소스 프레임워크 및 멀티모달 대화형 AI 프로젝트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que necesitan capacidades de análisis y revisión de código avanzadas para frameworks de código abierto y proyectos de IA conversacional multimodal.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA nécessitant des capacités d''analyse et de révision de code avancées pour les frameworks de code source ouvert et les projets d''IA conversationnelle multimodale.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die erweiterte Code-Analyse- und Überprüfungsfunktionen für Open-Source-Frameworks und multimodale Conversational-AI-Projekte benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de análise e revisão de código para estruturas de código aberto e projetos de IA conversacional multimodal.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, которым необходимы расширенные возможности анализа и проверки кода для проектов с открытым исходным кодом и мульти-модальной разговорной ИИ.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذي يحتاج إلى قدرات متقدمة لتحليل ومراجعة الشفرة لمشاريع الإطار المفتوح والمشاريع الذكية المتعددة الأنماط"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform thorough code reviews for pull requests, utilizing tools for checking code quality, syntax, and best practices, with a focus on conversational AI and multimodal interactions.","zh":"赋予代理执行全面代码审查的能力，利用工具检查代码质量、语法和最佳实践，重点关注对话式AI和多模态交互。","ja":"エージェントにプルリクエストの徹底的なコードレビューを実行する能力を付与し、コードの品質、構文、ベストプラクティスをチェックするツールを利用し、会話AIやマルチモーダルインタラクションに焦点を当てています。","ko":"에이전트가 プル リクエスト에 대한 철저한 코드 리뷰를 수행 할 수 있는 기능을 부여하며, 코드 품질, 구문 및 모범 사례를 확인하는 도구를 사용하여 대화형 AI 및 멀티모달 상호 작용에 중점을 둡니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar revisiones de código exhaustivas para solicitudes de incorporación, utilizando herramientas para comprobar la calidad del código, la sintaxis y las mejores prácticas, con un enfoque en IA conversacional y interacciones multimodales.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''effectuer des révisions de code approfondies pour les demandes d''intégration, en utilisant des outils pour vérifier la qualité du code, la syntaxe et les meilleures pratiques, avec un focus sur l''IA conversationnelle et les interactions multimodales.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, gründliche Code-Reviews für Pull-Requests durchzuführen, indem Tools zur Überprüfung der Code-Qualität, Syntax und Best Practices verwendet werden, mit Fokus auf Conversational-AI und multimodale Interaktionen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar revisões de código aprofundadas para solicitações de pull, utilizando ferramentas para verificar a qualidade do código, a sintaxe e as melhores práticas, com foco em IA conversacional e interações multimodais.","ru":"Позволяет агентам выполнять тщательные проверки кода для запросов на слияние, используя инструменты для контроля качества кода, синтаксиса и лучших практик, с фокусом на разговорной ИИ и мульти-модальных взаимодействиях.","ar":"تمكن الوكيل من إجراء مراجعات شاملة للشفرة لطلبات السحب، باستخدام أدوات للتحقق من جودة الشفرة والتركيب والأساليب المثلى، مع التركيز على الذكاء الاصطناعي المتكلم والتفاعلات متعددة الأنماط"},"useCases":{"en":["Reviewing pull requests for open-source conversational AI frameworks","Analyzing code quality and syntax for multimodal interactions","Debugging issues in voice and conversational AI projects"],"zh":["审查开源对话式AI框架的拉取请求","分析多模态交互的代码质量和语法","调试语音和对话式AI项目中的问题"],"ja":["オープンソース会話AIフレームワークのプルリクエストをレビューする","マルチモーダルインタラクションのコード品質と構文を分析する","音声および会話AIプロジェクトの問題をデバッグする"],"ko":["오픈 소스 대화형 AI 프레임워크의 풀 리クエ스트를 리뷰하는 것","멀티모달 상호 작용의 코드 품질 및 구문을 분석","음성 및 대화형 AI 프로젝트의 문제를 디버깅"],"es":["Revisar solicitudes de incorporación para frameworks de IA conversacional de código abierto","Analizar la calidad del código y la sintaxis para interacciones multimodales","Depurar problemas en proyectos de voz y IA conversacional"],"fr":["Réviser les demandes d''intégration pour les frameworks d''IA conversationnelle de code source ouvert","Analyser la qualité du code et la syntaxe pour les interactions multimodales","Déboguer les problèmes dans les projets de voix et d''IA conversationnelle"],"de":["Überprüfen von Pull-Requests für Open-Source-Conversational-AI-Frameworks","Analysieren der Code-Qualität und Syntax für multimodale Interaktionen","Beheben von Problemen in Sprach- und Conversational-AI-Projekten"],"pt":["Revisão de solicitações de pull para estruturas de IA conversacional de código aberto","Análise da qualidade do código e sintaxe para interações multimodais","Depuração de problemas em projetos de IA conversacional e voz"],"ru":["Проверка запросов на слияние для проектов с открытым исходным кодом разговорной ИИ","Анализ качества кода и синтаксиса для мульти-модальных взаимодействий","Отладка проблем в проектах разговорной ИИ и голоса"],"ar":["مراجعةطلبات السحب لمشاريع الإطار المفتوح للذكاء الاصطناعي المتكلم","تحليل جودة الشفرة والتركيب للتفاعلات متعددة الأنماط","تصحيح الأخطاء في مشاريع الذكاء الاصطناعي المتكلم والصوت"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires functional tools and services for code review","Assumes error-free tool operation","Limited to specific open-source frameworks and conversational AI projects"],"zh":["需要功能性工具和服务来进行代码审查","假设工具操作无误","仅限于特定的开源框架和对话式AI项目"],"ja":["コードレビューを行うための機能的なツールとサービスが必要","ツールの動作がエラー-freeであると仮定","特定のオープンソースフレームワークおよび会話AIプロジェクトに限定"],"ko":["코드 리뷰를 수행하기 위한 기능적인 도구 및 서비스가 필요","도구 작동이 오류가 없다고 가정","특정 오픈 소스 프레임워크 및 대화형 AI 프로젝트에 한정"],"es":["Requiere herramientas y servicios funcionales para la revisión de código","Supone una operación de herramientas sin errores","Limitado a frameworks de código abierto y proyectos de IA conversacional específicos"],"fr":["Nécessite des outils et services fonctionnels pour la révision de code","Suppose une opération d''outils sans erreurs","Limité à des frameworks de code source ouvert et des projets d''IA conversationnelle spécifiques"],"de":["Benötigt funktionale Tools und Dienste für die Code-Überprüfung","Geht von einer fehlerfreien Tool-Operation aus","Begrenzt auf bestimmte Open-Source-Frameworks und Conversational-AI-Projekte"],"pt":["Exige ferramentas e serviços funcionais para revisão de código","Pressupõe operação de ferramentas sem erros","Limitado a estruturas de código aberto e projetos de IA conversacional específicos"],"ru":["Требует функциональных инструментов и услуг для проверки кода","Предполагает бесперебойную работу инструментов","Ограничен конкретными проектами с открытым исходным кодом и разговорной ИИ"],"ar":["يتطلب أدوات وخدمات وظيفية لمراجعة الشفرة","يفترض تشغيل أدوات بدون أخطاء","محدود بمشاريع الإطار المفتوح والذكاء الاصطناعي المتكلم الخاصة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}'