","ar":"تقييم أنظمة الوكلاء","en":"evaluation"},"description":{"zh":"该技能专注于为AI代理系统构建评估框架。它提供了专门的方法来评估动态决策、非确定性运行且通常没有单一正确答案的代理系统，与传统软件评估截然不同。","ja":"このスキルは、AIエージェントシステムの評価フレームワークの構築に焦点を当てています。動的な意思決定を行い、実行ごとに非決定的で、単一の正解がないエージェントを評価するための専門的な方法を提供します。","ko":"이 스킬은 AI 에이전트 시스템을 위한 평가 프레임워크 구축에 중점을 둡니다. 동적 의사 결정을 내리고, 실행마다 비결정적이며, 단일 정답이 없는 에이전트를 평가하기 위한 전문 방법론을 제공합니다.","es":"La evaluación de sistemas de agentes requiere enfoques diferentes a los de software tradicional. Los agentes toman decisiones dinámicas y no determinísticas.","fr":"L''évaluation de systèmes d''agents nécessite des approches différentes de celles du logiciel traditionnel. Les agents prennent des décisions dynamiques et non...","de":"Die Bewertung von Agentsystemen erfordert andere Ansätze als die traditionelle Software. Agenten treffen dynamische und nicht deterministische Entscheidungen.","pt":"A avaliação de sistemas de agentes requer abordagens diferentes das tradicionais. Aprenda a construir estruturas de avaliação eficazes.","ru":"Оценка систем агентов требует разных подходов, чем традиционные. Узнайте, как строить эффективные структуры оценки.","ar":"تقييم أنظمة الوكلاء يتطلب نهجًا مختلفًا عن التقليدية. تعلم كيف تبني هياكل تقييم فعالة.","en":"Getting Skills Together to Learn from the Best"},"definition":{"en":"Getting Skills Together to Learn from the Best"},"features":{"zh":["专为动态决策的代理系统设计","处理运行间的非确定性差异","适用于缺乏单一正确答案的开放式任务","提供与传统软件不同的评估方法","构建全面的评估框架","衡量代理在复杂环境中的适应性"],"ja":["動的的意思決定を行うエージェントシステム専用設計","実行間の非決定論的差異の処理","単一の正解がないオープンエンドタスクに対応","従来のソフトウェア評価とは異なる手法を提供","包括的な評価フレームワークの構築","複雑な環境におけるエージェントの適応性の測定"],"ko":["동적 의사 결정 에이전트 시스템 전용 설계","실행 간 비결정적 차이 처리","단일 정답이 없는 개방형 작업 지원","기존 소프트웨어 평가와 다른 방법론 제공","포괄적인 평가 프레임워크 구축","복잡한 환경에서 에이전트 적응성 측정"],"es":["Enfoques personalizados para la evaluación de sistemas de agentes","Toma de decisiones dinámicas y no determinísticas","Evaluación de la performance de agentes","Frameworks de evaluación para sistemas de agentes","Análisis de la complejidad de los sistemas de agentes"],"fr":["Approches sur mesure pour l''évaluation de systèmes d''agents","Prise de décision dynamique et non déterministe","Évaluation de la performance des agents","Frameworks d''évaluation pour les systèmes d''agents","Analyse de la complexité des systèmes d''agents"],"de":["Maßgeschneiderte Ansätze für die Bewertung von Agentsystemen","Dynamische und nicht deterministische Entscheidungsfindung","Bewertung der Leistung von Agenten","Bewertungsframeworks für Agentsysteme","Analyse der Komplexität von Agentsystemen"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de estruturas de avaliação","Avaliação de sistemas de agentes","Abordagens não tradicionais de avaliação","Consideração de decisões dinâmicas","Avaliação de desempenho em sistemas de agentes","Construção de frameworks de avaliação personalizados"],"ru":["Разработка структур оценки","Оценка систем агентов","Нетрадиционные подходы к оценке","Учет динамических решений","Оценка производительности в системах агентов","Создание индивидуальных фреймворков оценки"],"ar":["طور هياكل تقييم","تقييم أنظمة الوكلاء","نهج غير تقليدية للتقيم","الاعتبار القرارات الديناميكية","تقييم الأداء في أنظمة الوكلاء","بناء إطارات تقييم مخصصة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI代理评估","代理系统评估框架","动态决策评估","非确定性AI测试","构建代理评估","LLM代理评估方法","多智能体系统评估","开放式任务评估"],"ja":["AIエージェント評価","エージェントシステム評価フレームワーク","動的的意思決定評価","非決定論的AIテスト","エージェント評価構築","LLMエージェント評価手法","マルチエージェントシステム評価","オープンエンドタスク評価"],"ko":["AI 에이전트 평가","에이전트 시스템 평가 프레임워크","동적 의사 결정 평가","비결정적 AI 테스트","에이전트 평가 구축","LLM 에이전트 평가 방법","다중 에이전트 시스템 평가","개방형 작업 평가"],"es":["evaluación de sistemas de agentes","agentes inteligentes","sistemas de agentes","evaluación de la performance","frameworks de evaluación","toma de decisiones dinámicas","complejidad de los sistemas de agentes","desarrollo de agentes"],"fr":["évaluation de systèmes d''agents","agents intelligents","systèmes d''agents","évaluation de la performance","frameworks d''évaluation","prise de décision dynamique","complexité des systèmes d''agents","développement d''agents"],"de":["Bewertung von Agentsystemen","intelligente Agenten","Agentsysteme","Bewertung der Leistung","Bewertungsframeworks","dynamische Entscheidungsfindung","Komplexität von Agentsystemen","Entwicklung von Agenten"],"pt":["avaliação de sistemas de agentes","desenvolvimento de estruturas de avaliação","sistemas de agentes","avaliação de desempenho","frameworks de avaliação","agentes inteligentes","sistemas dinâmicos","tomada de decisões","aprendizado de máquina"],"ru":["оценка систем агентов","разработка структур оценки","системы агентов","оценка производительности","фреймворки оценки","интеллектуальные агенты","динамические системы","принятие решений","машинное обучение"],"ar":["تقييم أنظمة الوكلاء","طور هياكل تقييم","أنظمة الوكلاء","تقييم الأداء","إطارات تقييم","وكلاء ذكاء اصطناعي","أنظمة ديناميكية","اتخاذ القرارات","تعلم الآلة"]}},"owner":"boisenoise","repo":"skills-collections","repoPath":"boisenoise/skills-collections","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.415Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"evaluation","description":"Build evaluation frameworks for agent systems","bodyPreview":"## When to Use This Skill\n\nBuild evaluation frameworks for agent systems\n\nUse this skill when working with build evaluation frameworks for agent systems.\n# Evaluation Methods for Agent Systems\n\nEvaluation of agent systems requires different approaches than traditional software or even standard language model applications. Agents make dynamic decisions, are non-deterministic between runs, and often lack single correct answers. Effective evaluation must account for these characteristics while prov","body":"## When to Use This Skill\n\nBuild evaluation frameworks for agent systems\n\nUse this skill when working with build evaluation frameworks for agent systems.\n# Evaluation Methods for Agent Systems\n\nEvaluation of agent systems requires different approaches than traditional software or even standard language model applications. Agents make dynamic decisions, are non-deterministic between runs, and often lack single correct answers. Effective evaluation must account for these characteristics while providing actionable feedback. A robust evaluation framework enables continuous improvement, catches regressions, and validates that context engineering choices achieve intended effects.\n\n## When to Activate\n\nActivate this skill when:\n- Testing agent performance systematically\n- Validating context engineering choices\n- Measuring improvements over time\n- Catching regressions before deployment\n- Building quality gates for agent pipelines\n- Comparing different agent configurations\n- Evaluating production systems continuously\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nAgent evaluation requires outcome-focused approaches that account for non-determinism and multiple valid paths. Multi-dimensional rubrics capture various quality aspects: factual accuracy, completeness, citation accuracy, source quality, and tool efficiency. LLM-as-judge provides scalable evaluation while human evaluation catches edge cases.\n\nThe key insight is that agents may find alternative paths to goals—the evaluation should judge whether they achieve right outcomes while following reasonable processes.\n\n**Performance Drivers: The 95% Finding**\nResearch on the BrowseComp evaluation (which tests browsing agents'' ability to locate hard-to-find information) found that three factors explain 95% of performance variance:\n\n| Factor | Variance Explained | Implication |\n|--------|-------------------|-------------|\n| Token usage | 80% | More tokens = better performance |\n| Number of tool calls | ~10% | More exploration helps |\n| Model choice | ~5% | Better models multiply efficiency |\n\nThis finding has significant implications for evaluation design:\n- **Token budgets matter**: Evaluate agents with realistic token budgets, not unlimited resources\n- **Model upgrades beat token increases**: Upgrading to Claude Sonnet 4.5 or GPT-5.2 provides larger gains than doubling token budgets on previous versions\n- **Multi-agent validation**: The finding validates architectures that distribute work across agents with separate context windows\n\n## Detailed Topics\n\n### Evaluation Challenges\n\n**Non-Determinism and Multiple Valid Paths**\nAgents may take completely different valid paths to reach goals. One agent might search three sources while another searches ten. They might use different tools to find the same answer. Traditional evaluations that check for specific steps fail in this context.\n\nThe solution is outcome-focused evaluation that judges whether agents achieve right outcomes while following reasonable processes.\n\n**Context-Dependent Failures**\nAgent failures often depend on context in subtle ways. An agent might succeed on simple queries but fail on complex ones. It might work well with one tool set but fail with another. Failures may emerge only after extended interaction when context accumulates.\n\nEvaluation must cover a range of complexity levels and test extended interactions, not just isolated queries.\n\n**Composite Quality Dimensions**\nAgent quality is not a single dimension. It includes factual accuracy, completeness, coherence, tool efficiency, and process quality. An agent might score high on accuracy but low in efficiency, or vice versa.\n\nEvaluation rubrics must capture multiple dimensions with appropriate weighting for the use case.\n\n### Evaluation Rubric Design\n\n**Multi-Dimensional Rubric**\nEffective rubrics cover key dimensions with descriptive levels:\n\nFactual accuracy: Claims match ground truth (excellent to failed)\n\nCompleteness: Output covers requested aspects (excellent to failed)\n\nCitation accuracy: Citations match claimed sources (excellent to failed)\n\nSource quality: Uses appropriate primary sources (excellent to failed)\n\nTool efficiency: Uses right tools reasonable number of times (excellent to failed)\n\n**Rubric Scoring**\nConvert dimension assessments to numeric scores (0.0 to 1.0) with appropriate weighting. Calculate weighted overall scores. Determine passing threshold based on use case requirements.\n\n### Evaluation Methodologies\n\n**LLM-as-Judge**\nLLM-based evaluation scales to large test sets and provides consistent judgments. The key is designing effective evaluation prompts that capture the dimensions of interest.\n\nProvide clear task description, agent output, ground truth (if available), evaluation scale with level descriptions, and request structured judgment.\n\n**Human Evaluation**\nHuman evaluation catches what automation misses. Humans notice hallucinated answers on unusual queries, system failures, and subtle biases that automated evaluation misses.\n\nEffective human evaluation covers edge cases, samples systematically, tracks patterns, and provides contextual understanding.\n\n**End-State Evaluation**\nFor agents that mutate persistent state, end-state evaluation focuses on whether the final state matches expectations rather than how the agent got there.\n\n### Test Set Design\n\n**Sample Selection**\nStart with small samples during development. Early in agent development, changes have dramatic impacts because there is abundant low-hanging fruit. Small test sets reveal large effects.\n\nSample from real usage patterns. Add known edge cases. Ensure coverage across complexity levels.\n\n**Complexity Stratification**\nTest sets should span complexity levels: simple (single tool call), medium (multiple tool calls), complex (many tool calls, significant ambiguity), and very complex (extended interaction, deep reasoning).\n\n### Context Engineering Evaluation\n\n**Testing Context Strategies**\nContext engineering choices should be validated through systematic evaluation. Run agents with different context strategies on the same test set. Compare quality scores, token usage, and efficiency metrics.\n\n**Degradation Testing**\nTest how context degradation affects performance by running agents at different context sizes. Identify performance cliffs where context becomes problematic. Establish safe operating limits.\n\n### Continuous Evaluation\n\n**Evaluation Pipeline**\nBuild evaluation pipelines that run automatically on agent changes. Track results over time. Compare versions to identify improvements or regressions.\n\n**Monitoring Production**\nTrack evaluation metrics in production by sampling interactions and evaluating randomly. Set alerts for quality drops. Maintain dashboards for trend analysis.\n\n## Practical Guidance\n\n### Building Evaluation Frameworks\n\n1. Define quality dimensions relevant to your use case\n2. Create rubrics with clear, actionable level descriptions\n3. Build test sets from real usage patterns and edge cases\n4. Implement automated evaluation pipelines\n5. Establish baseline metrics before making changes\n6. Run evaluations on all significant changes\n7. Track metrics over time for trend analysis\n8. Supplement automated evaluation with human review\n\n### Avoiding Evaluation Pitfalls\n\nOverfitting to specific paths: Evaluate outcomes, not specific steps.\nIgnoring edge cases: Include diverse test scenarios.\nSingle-metric obsession: Use multi-dimensional rubrics.\nNeglecting context effects: Test with realistic context sizes.\nSkipping human evaluation: Automated evaluation misses subtle issues.\n\n## Examples\n\n**Example 1: Simple Evaluation**\n```python\ndef evaluate_agent_response(response, expected):\n    rubric = load_rubric()\n    scores = {}\n    for dimension, config in rubric.items():\n        scores[dimension] = assess_dimension(response, expected, dimension)\n    overall = weighted_average(scores, config[\"weights\"])\n    return {\"passed\": overall >= 0.7, \"scores\": scores}\n```\n\n**Example 2: Test Set Structure**\n\nTest sets should span multiple complexity levels to ensure comprehensive evaluation:\n\n```python\ntest_set = [\n    {\n        \"name\": \"simple_lookup\",\n        \"input\": \"What is the capital of France?\",\n        \"expected\": {\"type\": \"fact\", \"answer\": \"Paris\"},\n        \"complexity\": \"simple\",\n        \"description\": \"Single tool call, factual lookup\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"medium_query\",\n        \"input\": \"Compare the revenue of Apple and Microsoft last quarter\",\n        \"complexity\": \"medium\",\n        \"description\": \"Multiple tool calls, comparison logic\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"multi_step_reasoning\",\n        \"input\": \"Analyze sales data from Q1-Q4 and create a summary report with trends\",\n        \"complexity\": \"complex\",\n        \"description\": \"Many tool calls, aggregation, analysis\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"research_synthesis\",\n        \"input\": \"Research emerging AI technologies, evaluate their potential impact, and recommend adoption strategy\",\n        \"complexity\": \"very_complex\",\n        \"description\": \"Extended interaction, deep reasoning, synthesis\"\n    }\n]\n```\n\n## Guidelines\n\n1. Use multi-dimensional rubrics, not single metrics\n2. Evaluate outcomes, not specific execution paths\n3. Cover complexity levels from simple to complex\n4. Test with realistic context sizes and histories\n5. Run evaluations continuously, not just before release\n6. Supplement LLM evaluation with human review\n7. Track metrics over time for trend detection\n8. Set clear pass/fail thresholds based on use case\n\n## Integration\n\nThis skill connects to all other skills as a cross-cutting concern:\n\n- context-fundamentals - Evaluating context usage\n- context-degradation - Detecting degradation\n- context-optimization - Measuring optimization effectiveness\n- multi-agent-patterns - Evaluating coordination\n- tool-design - Evaluating tool effectiveness\n- memory-systems - Evaluating memory quality\n\n## References\n\nInternal reference:\n- [Metrics Reference](./references/metrics.md) - Detailed evaluation metrics and implementation\n\n## References\n\nInternal skills:\n- All other skills connect to evaluation for quality measurement\n\nExternal resources:\n- LLM evaluation benchmarks\n- Agent evaluation research papers\n- Production monitoring practices\n\n---\n\n## Skill Metadata\n\n**Created**: 2025-12-20\n**Last Updated**: 2025-12-20\n**Author**: Agent Skills for Context Engineering Contributors\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:04:50.418Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Advanced AI Agents requiring dynamic evaluation frameworks for agent systems","zh":"适合需要动态评估框架的高级 AI 代理系统","ja":"高度なAIエージェントが動的評価フレームワークを必要とする場合に最適","ko":"동적 평가 프레임워크가 필요한 고급 AI 에이전트 시스템에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de IA Avanzados que requieren marcos de evaluación dinámicos para sistemas de agentes","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents IA Avancés nécessitant des cadres d''évaluation dynamiques pour les systèmes d''agents","de":"Perfekt für fortgeschrittene KI-Agents, die dynamische Bewertungsrahmen für Agentsysteme erfordern","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA Avançados que exigem estruturas de avaliação dinâmicas para sistemas de agentes","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых агентов ИИ, требующих динамических рамок оценки для систем агентов","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكلاء الذكية المتقدمة التي تتطلب إطارات تقييم ديناميكية لأنظمة الوكلاء"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build evaluation frameworks using non-deterministic and dynamic decision-making approaches, accounting for agent systems'' unique characteristics and leveraging protocols such as evaluation methodologies for multi-run assessments","zh":"赋予代理能力，使用非确定性和动态决策方法建立评估框架，考虑代理系统的独特特征，并利用评估方法等协议进行多次运行的评估","ja":"エージェントは、非決定性および動的意思決定アプローチを使用して評価フレームワークを構築することを可能にし、エージェントシステムの独自の特性を考慮し、評価方法などのプロトコルを使用して複数実行の評価を実行する","ko":"에이전트에게 비결정적이고 동적인 의사결정 접근 방식을 사용하여 평가 프레임워크를 구축할 수 있게 하여, 에이전트 시스템의 고유한 특성을 고려하고 다중 실행 평가를 위한 평가 방법론과 같은 프로토콜을 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a construir marcos de evaluación utilizando enfoques de toma de decisiones no deterministas y dinámicos, teniendo en cuenta las características únicas de los sistemas de agentes y aprovechando protocolos como metodologías de evaluación para evaluaciones de varias ejecuciones","fr":"Permet aux agents de construire des cadres d''évaluation en utilisant des approches de prise de décision non déterministes et dynamiques, en tenant compte des caractéristiques uniques des systèmes d''agents et en exploitant des protocoles tels que des méthodologies d''évaluation pour des évaluations multi-exécutions","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Bewertungsrahmen unter Verwendung nicht-deterministischer und dynamischer Entscheidungsansätze zu erstellen, wobei die einzigartigen Merkmale der Agentsysteme berücksichtigt und Protokolle wie Bewertungsmethoden für Multi-Lauf-Bewertungen genutzt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir estruturas de avaliação utilizando abordagens de tomada de decisão não determinísticas e dinâmicas, considerando as características únicas dos sistemas de agentes e utilizando protocolos como metodologias de avaliação para avaliações de várias execuções","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать рамки оценки с использованием неопределенных и динамических подходов к принятию решений, учитывая уникальные характеристики систем агентов и используя протоколы, такие как методологии оценки для многоходовых оценок","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من بناء إطارات تقييم باستخدام مناهج غير محددة وديناميكية لاتخاذ القرارات، مع考虑 الخصائص الفريدة لأنظمة الوكلاء وتطبيق بروتوكولات مثل منهجيات التقييم للتقييمات متعددة التشغيل"},"useCases":{"en":["Building evaluation frameworks for agent systems","Assessing dynamic decision-making in agent systems","Developing non-deterministic evaluation methods"],"zh":["为代理系统构建评估框架","评估代理系统中的动态决策","开发非确定性评估方法"],"ja":["エージェントシステムの評価フレームワークを構築する","エージェントシステムの動的意思決定を評価する","非決定性評価方法を開発する"],"ko":["에이전트 시스템을 위한 평가 프레임워크 구축","에이전트 시스템의 동적 의사결정 평가","비결정적 평가 방법 개발"],"es":["Construir marcos de evaluación para sistemas de agentes","Evaluar la toma de decisiones dinámica en sistemas de agentes","Desarrollar métodos de evaluación no deterministas"],"fr":["Construire des cadres d''évaluation pour les systèmes d''agents","Évaluer la prise de décision dynamique dans les systèmes d''agents","Développer des méthodes d''évaluation non déterministes"],"de":["Bewertungsrahmen für Agentsysteme erstellen","Dynamische Entscheidungsfindung in Agentsystemen bewerten","Nicht-deterministische Bewertungsmethoden entwickeln"],"pt":["Construção de estruturas de avaliação para sistemas de agentes","Avaliação de tomada de decisão dinâmica em sistemas de agentes","Desenvolvimento de métodos de avaliação não determinísticos"],"ru":["Создание рамок оценки для систем агентов","Оценка динамического принятия решений в системах агентов","Разработка неопределенных методов оценки"],"ar":["بناء إطارات تقييم لأنظمة الوكلاء","تقييم اتخاذ القرارات الديناميكي في أنظمة الوكلاء","تطوير أساليب تقييم غير محددة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of agent systems'' complexities","May need customization for specific agent systems"],"zh":["需要了解代理系统的复杂性","可能需要为特定代理系统进行定制"],"ja":["エージェントシステムの複雑性を理解する必要がある","特定のエージェントシステムに合わせてカスタマイズする必要があるかもしれない"],"ko":["에이전트 시스템의 복잡성을 이해해야 함","특정 에이전트 시스템에 맞게 커스터마이징이 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de las complejidades de los sistemas de agentes","Puede necesitar personalización para sistemas de agentes específicos"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des complexités des systèmes d''agents","Peut nécessiter une personnalisation pour des systèmes d''agents spécifiques"],"de":["Benötigt das Verständnis der Komplexitäten von Agentsystemen","Kann eine Anpassung für spezifische Agentsysteme erfordern"],"pt":["Exige compreensão das complexidades dos sistemas de agentes","Pode necessitar de personalização para sistemas de agentes específicos"],"ru":["Требует понимания сложностей систем агентов","Может потребовать настройки для конкретных систем агентов"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا للتعقيدات لأنظمة الوكلاء","يمكن أن يحتاج إلى تخصيص لأنظمة وكلاء محددة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
