s con networkx","Exportación de artefactos de grafo para Neo4j/Gephi","Creación de un grafo de co-cambio de archivos","Cálculo de la similitud de Jaccard"],"fr":["Analyse des risques de propriétaires","Création d''un graphe bipartite de personnes et de fichiers","Détection de communautés avec networkx","Exportation d''artefacts de graphe pour Neo4j/Gephi","Création d''un graphe de co-changement de fichiers","Calcul de la similarité de Jaccard"],"de":["Analyse von Eigentumsrisiken","Erstellung eines bipartiten Graphen von Personen und Dateien","Community-Erkennung mit networkx","Export von Graph-Artefakten für Neo4j/Gephi","Erstellung eines Datei-Co-Change-Graphen","Berechnung der Jaccard-Ähnlichkeit"],"pt":["Constrói um grafo bipartido de pessoas e arquivos","Calcula o risco de propriedade","Exporta artefatos de grafo para Neo4j/Gephi","Constroi um grafo de co-mudança de arquivos","Ignora commits grandes e barulhentos"],"ru":["Постройте двудольный граф людей и файлов","Вычислите риск собственности","Экспортируйте графические артефакты в Neo4j/Gephi","Постройте граф совместных изменений файлов","Игнорируйте большие и шумные коммиты"],"ar":["ابني مخططًا ثنائي القسم للأشخاص والملفات","حسابي مخاطر الملكية","استخراج مكونات المخطط ل Neo4j/Gephi","ابني مخططًا لتغيير الملفات المشترك","تجاهل التعديلات الكبيرة والصاخبة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["安全所有权地图","AI代理安全风险","文件共改变图","Python 3","networkx","Neo4j","Gephi","代码安全性","安全风险计算"],"ja":["セキュリティ所有権マップ","AIエージェントのセキュリティリスク","ファイルの共通変更グラフ","Python 3","networkx","Neo4j","Gephi","コードのセキュリティ","セキュリティリスク計算"],"ko":["보안 소유권 맵","AI 에이전트의 보안 위험","파일의 공통 변경 그래프","Python 3","networkx","Neo4j","Gephi","코드의 보안","보안 위험 계산"],"es":["seguridad de propietarios","análisis de riesgos","grafo bipartito","networkx","Neo4j","Gephi","desarrollo de software","seguridad de proyectos","ingeniería de software"],"fr":["sécurité de propriétaires","analyse des risques","graphe bipartite","networkx","Neo4j","Gephi","développement de logiciels","sécurité de projets","ingénierie de logiciels"],"de":["Sicherheitseigentum","Risikoanalyse","bipartiter Graph","networkx","Neo4j","Gephi","Softwareentwicklung","Projektsicherheit","Softwareingenieurwesen"],"pt":["segurança de desenvolvimento","propriedade de código","grafo bipartido","risco de propriedade","Neo4j","Gephi"],"ru":["безопасность разработки","собственность кода","двудольный граф","риск собственности","Neo4j","Gephi"],"ar":["أمان التطوير","ملكية الشفرة","مخطط ثنائي القسم","مخاطر الملكية","Neo4j","Gephi"]}},"owner":"PipeOpsHQ","repo":"agent-sdk-go","repoPath":"PipeOpsHQ/agent-sdk-go","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.415Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"security-ownership-map","description":"Analyze git repositories to build a security ownership topology (people-to-file), compute bus factor and sensitive-code ownership, and export CSV/JSON for graph databases and visualization. Trigger only when the user explicitly wants a security-oriented ownership or bus-factor analysis grounded in git history (for example: orphaned sensitive code, security maintainers, CODEOWNERS reality checks for risk, sensitive hotspots, or ownership clusters). Do not trigger for general maintainer lists or non-security ownership questions.","bodyPreview":"# Security Ownership Map\n\n## Overview\n\nBuild a bipartite graph of people and files from git history, then compute ownership risk and export graph artifacts for Neo4j/Gephi. Also build a file co-change graph (Jaccard similarity on shared commits) to cluster files by how they move together while ignoring large, noisy commits.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Python 3\n- `networkx` (required; community detection is enabled by default)\n\nInstall with:\n\n```bash\npip install networkx\n```\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Scope the re","body":"# Security Ownership Map\n\n## Overview\n\nBuild a bipartite graph of people and files from git history, then compute ownership risk and export graph artifacts for Neo4j/Gephi. Also build a file co-change graph (Jaccard similarity on shared commits) to cluster files by how they move together while ignoring large, noisy commits.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Python 3\n- `networkx` (required; community detection is enabled by default)\n\nInstall with:\n\n```bash\npip install networkx\n```\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Scope the repo and time window (optional `--since/--until`).\n2. Decide sensitivity rules (use defaults or provide a CSV config).\n3. Build the ownership map with `scripts/run_ownership_map.py` (co-change graph is on by default; use `--cochange-max-files` to ignore supernode commits).\n4. Communities are computed by default; graphml output is optional (`--graphml`).\n5. Query the outputs with `scripts/query_ownership.py` for bounded JSON slices.\n6. Persist and visualize (see `references/neo4j-import.md`).\n\nBy default, the co-change graph ignores common “glue” files (lockfiles, `.github/*`, editor config) so clusters reflect actual code movement instead of shared infra edits. Override with `--cochange-exclude` or `--no-default-cochange-excludes`. Dependabot commits are excluded by default; override with `--no-default-author-excludes` or add patterns via `--author-exclude-regex`.\n\nIf you want to exclude Linux build glue like `Kbuild` from co-change clustering, pass:\n\n```bash\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/run_ownership_map.py \\\n  --repo /path/to/linux \\\n  --out ownership-map-out \\\n  --cochange-exclude \"**/Kbuild\"\n```\n\n## Quick start\n\nRun from the repo root:\n\n```bash\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/run_ownership_map.py \\\n  --repo . \\\n  --out ownership-map-out \\\n  --since \"12 months ago\" \\\n  --emit-commits\n```\n\nDefaults: author identity, author date, and merge commits excluded. Use `--identity committer`, `--date-field committer`, or `--include-merges` if needed.\n\nExample (override co-change excludes):\n\n```bash\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/run_ownership_map.py \\\n  --repo . \\\n  --out ownership-map-out \\\n  --cochange-exclude \"**/Cargo.lock\" \\\n  --cochange-exclude \"**/.github/**\" \\\n  --no-default-cochange-excludes\n```\n\nCommunities are computed by default. To disable:\n\n```bash\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/run_ownership_map.py \\\n  --repo . \\\n  --out ownership-map-out \\\n  --no-communities\n```\n\n## Sensitivity rules\n\nBy default, the script flags common auth/crypto/secret paths. Override by providing a CSV file:\n\n```\n# pattern,tag,weight\n**/auth/**,auth,1.0\n**/crypto/**,crypto,1.0\n**/*.pem,secrets,1.0\n```\n\nUse it with `--sensitive-config path/to/sensitive.csv`.\n\n## Output artifacts\n\n`ownership-map-out/` contains:\n\n- `people.csv` (nodes: people)\n- `files.csv` (nodes: files)\n- `edges.csv` (edges: touches)\n- `cochange_edges.csv` (file-to-file co-change edges with Jaccard weight; omitted with `--no-cochange`)\n- `summary.json` (security ownership findings)\n- `commits.jsonl` (optional, if `--emit-commits`)\n- `communities.json` (computed by default from co-change edges when available; includes `maintainers` per community; disable with `--no-communities`)\n- `cochange.graph.json` (NetworkX node-link JSON with `community_id` + `community_maintainers`; falls back to `ownership.graph.json` if no co-change edges)\n- `ownership.graphml` / `cochange.graphml` (optional, if `--graphml`)\n\n`people.csv` includes timezone detection based on author commit offsets: `primary_tz_offset`, `primary_tz_minutes`, and `timezone_offsets`.\n\n## LLM query helper\n\nUse `scripts/query_ownership.py` to return small, JSON-bounded slices without loading the full graph into context.\n\nExamples:\n\n```bash\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/query_ownership.py --data-dir ownership-map-out people --limit 10\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/query_ownership.py --data-dir ownership-map-out files --tag auth --bus-factor-max 1\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/query_ownership.py --data-dir ownership-map-out person --person alice@corp --limit 10\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/query_ownership.py --data-dir ownership-map-out file --file crypto/tls\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/query_ownership.py --data-dir ownership-map-out cochange --file crypto/tls --limit 10\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/query_ownership.py --data-dir ownership-map-out summary --section orphaned_sensitive_code\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/query_ownership.py --data-dir ownership-map-out community --id 3\n```\n\nUse `--community-top-owners 5` (default) to control how many maintainers are stored per community.\n\n## Basic security queries\n\nRun these to answer common security ownership questions with bounded output:\n\n```bash\n# Orphaned sensitive code (stale + low bus factor)\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/query_ownership.py --data-dir ownership-map-out summary --section orphaned_sensitive_code\n\n# Hidden owners for sensitive tags\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/query_ownership.py --data-dir ownership-map-out summary --section hidden_owners\n\n# Sensitive hotspots with low bus factor\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/query_ownership.py --data-dir ownership-map-out summary --section bus_factor_hotspots\n\n# Auth/crypto files with bus factor <= 1\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/query_ownership.py --data-dir ownership-map-out files --tag auth --bus-factor-max 1\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/query_ownership.py --data-dir ownership-map-out files --tag crypto --bus-factor-max 1\n\n# Who is touching sensitive code the most\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/query_ownership.py --data-dir ownership-map-out people --sort sensitive_touches --limit 10\n\n# Co-change neighbors (cluster hints for ownership drift)\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/query_ownership.py --data-dir ownership-map-out cochange --file path/to/file --min-jaccard 0.05 --limit 20\n\n# Community maintainers (for a cluster)\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/query_ownership.py --data-dir ownership-map-out community --id 3\n\n# Monthly maintainers for the community containing a file\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/community_maintainers.py \\\n  --data-dir ownership-map-out \\\n  --file network/card.c \\\n  --since 2025-01-01 \\\n  --top 5\n\n# Quarterly buckets instead of monthly\npython skills/skills/security-ownership-map/scripts/community_maintainers.py \\\n  --data-dir ownership-map-out \\\n  --file network/card.c \\\n  --since 2025-01-01 \\\n  --bucket quarter \\\n  --top 5\n```\n\nNotes:\n- Touches default to one authored commit (not per-file). Use `--touch-mode file` to count per-file touches.\n- Use `--window-days 90` or `--weight recency --half-life-days 180` to smooth churn.\n- Filter bots with `--ignore-author-regex ''(bot|dependabot)''`.\n- Use `--min-share 0.1` to show stable maintainers only.\n- Use `--bucket quarter` for calendar quarter groupings.\n- Use `--identity committer` or `--date-field committer` to switch from author attribution.\n- Use `--include-merges` to include merge commits (excluded by default).\n\n### Summary format (default)\n\nUse this structure, add fields if needed:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"orphaned_sensitive_code\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"crypto/tls/handshake.rs\",\n      \"last_security_touch\": \"2023-03-12T18:10:04+00:00\",\n      \"bus_factor\": 1\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hidden_owners\": [\n    {\n      \"person\": \"alice@corp\",\n      \"controls\": \"63% of auth code\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Graph persistence\n\nUse `references/neo4j-import.md` when you need to load the CSVs into Neo4j. It includes constraints, import Cypher, and visualization tips.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `bus_factor_hotspots` in `summary.json` lists sensitive files with low bus factor; `orphaned_sensitive_code` is the stale subset.\n- If `git log` is too large, narrow with `--since` or `--until`.\n- Compare `summary.json` against CODEOWNERS to highlight ownership drift.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:05:00.556Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Security Analysis Agents needing advanced graph-based ownership risk assessment and visualization capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级图形化所有权风险评估和可视化能力的安全分析代理。","ja":"セキュリティ分析エージェントが高度なグラフベースの所有権リスク評価と可視化機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 그래프 기반 소유권 위험 평가 및 시각화 기능이 필요한 보안 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de análisis de seguridad que necesitan una evaluación y visualización de riesgos de propiedad avanzadas basadas en gráficos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de sécurité nécessitant une évaluation et une visualisation de risques de propriété avancées basées sur des graphiques.","de":"Perfekt für Sicherheitsanalyse-Agents, die erweiterte graphbasierte Eigentumsrisikobewertung und Visualisierungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfect for Security Analysis Agents needing advanced graph-based ownership risk assessment and visualization capabilities.","ru":"Perfect for Security Analysis Agents needing advanced graph-based ownership risk assessment and visualization capabilities.","ar":"Perfect for Security Analysis Agents needing advanced graph-based ownership risk assessment and visualization capabilities."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to compute ownership risk and export graph artifacts for Neo4j/Gephi, utilizing Python 3 and the networkx library to build bipartite graphs of people and files from git history, and file co-change graphs using Jaccard similarity.","zh":"赋予代理计算所有权风险并导出图形制品以供Neo4j/Gephi使用，利用Python 3和networkx库从git历史记录中构建人和文件的二分图，以及使用Jaccard相似度的文件共同更改图。","ja":"エージェントが所有権リスクを計算し、Neo4j/Gephi用のグラフアーティファクトをエクスポートできるようにし、Python 3とnetworkxライブラリを使用してGit履歴から人物とファイルの二部グラフを構築し、Jaccard類似度を使用したファイル共同変更グラフを構築します。","ko":"에이전트가 소유권 위험을 계산하고 Neo4j/Gephi 용 그래프 아티팩트를 내보낼 수 있도록 하며, Python 3 및 networkx 라이브러리를 사용하여 Git 기록에서 사람과 파일의 이분 그래프를 구축하고, Jaccard 유사성을 사용한 파일 공통 변경 그래프를 구축합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes calcular el riesgo de propiedad y exportar artefactos de gráficos para Neo4j/Gephi, utilizando Python 3 y la biblioteca networkx para construir gráficos bipartitos de personas y archivos a partir del historial de git, y gráficos de coincidencia de archivos utilizando la similitud de Jaccard.","fr":"Permet aux agents de calculer le risque de propriété et d''exporter des artefacts de graphiques pour Neo4j/Gephi, en utilisant Python 3 et la bibliothèque networkx pour construire des graphiques bipartites de personnes et de fichiers à partir de l''historique de git, et des graphiques de co-changement de fichiers en utilisant la similarité de Jaccard.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, das Eigentumsrisiko zu berechnen und Graph-Artefakte für Neo4j/Gephi zu exportieren, indem Python 3 und die networkx-Bibliothek verwendet werden, um bipartite Graphen von Personen und Dateien aus der Git-Historie zu erstellen und Datei-Co-Change-Graphen unter Verwendung der Jaccard-Ähnlichkeit.","pt":"Empowers agents to compute ownership risk and export graph artifacts for Neo4j/Gephi, utilizing Python 3 and the networkx library to build bipartite graphs of people and files from git history, and file co-change graphs using Jaccard similarity.","ru":"Empowers agents to compute ownership risk and export graph artifacts for Neo4j/Gephi, utilizing Python 3 and the networkx library to build bipartite graphs of people and files from git history, and file co-change graphs using Jaccard similarity.","ar":"Empowers agents to compute ownership risk and export graph artifacts for Neo4j/Gephi, utilizing Python 3 and the networkx library to build bipartite graphs of people and files from git history, and file co-change graphs using Jaccard similarity."},"useCases":{"en":["Analyzing git history to identify ownership risks","Building file co-change graphs to cluster related files","Visualizing security ownership maps in Neo4j or Gephi"],"zh":["分析Git历史记录以识别所有权风险","构建文件共同更改图以聚类相关文件","在Neo4j或Gephi中可视化安全所有权映射"],"ja":["所有権リスクを特定するためのGit履歴の分析","関連ファイルのクラスタリングのためのファイル共同変更グラフの構築","Neo4jまたはGephiでのセキュリティ所有権マップの可視化"],"ko":["소유권 위험을 식별하기 위한 Git 기록 분석","관련 파일을 클러스터링하기 위한 파일 공통 변경 그래프 구축","Neo4j 또는 Gephi에서 보안 소유권 맵 시각화"],"es":["Análisis del historial de git para identificar riesgos de propiedad","Construcción de gráficos de coincidencia de archivos para agrupar archivos relacionados","Visualización de mapas de propiedad de seguridad en Neo4j o Gephi"],"fr":["Analyse de l''historique de git pour identifier les risques de propriété","Construction de graphiques de co-changement de fichiers pour regrouper des fichiers liés","Visualisation de cartes de propriété de sécurité dans Neo4j ou Gephi"],"de":["Analyse der Git-Historie zur Identifizierung von Eigentumsrisiken","Erstellung von Datei-Co-Change-Graphen zur Gruppierung von verwandten Dateien","Visualisierung von Sicherheitseigentums-Karten in Neo4j oder Gephi"],"pt":["Analyzing git history to identify ownership risks","Building file co-change graphs to cluster related files","Visualizing security ownership maps in Neo4j or Gephi"],"ru":["Analyzing git history to identify ownership risks","Building file co-change graphs to cluster related files","Visualizing security ownership maps in Neo4j or Gephi"],"ar":["Analyzing git history to identify ownership risks","Building file co-change graphs to cluster related files","Visualizing security ownership maps in Neo4j or Gephi"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python 3","Dependent on networkx library","Limited to analyzing git history"],"zh":["需要Python 3","依赖于networkx库","仅限分析Git历史记录"],"ja":["Python 3が必要","networkxライブラリに依存","Git履歴の分析のみ"],"ko":["Python 3 필요","networkx 라이브러리에 의존","Git 기록 분석만 제한"],"es":["Requiere Python 3","Dependiente de la biblioteca networkx","Limitado al análisis del historial de git"],"fr":["Nécessite Python 3","Dépend de la bibliothèque networkx","Limité à l''analyse de l''historique de git"],"de":["Benötigt Python 3","Abhängig von der networkx-Bibliothek","Begrenzt auf die Analyse der Git-Historie"],"pt":["Requires Python 3","Dependent on networkx library","Limited to analyzing git history"],"ru":["Requires Python 3","Dependent on networkx library","Limited to analyzing git history"],"ar":["Requires Python 3","Dependent on networkx library","Limited to analyzing git history"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
