matisés exhaustifs","Suit les principes de la phase rouge de TDD","Capture le comportement attendu","Couvre les cas de bordure avant la mise en œuvre","Améliore les compétences de test et de développement","Intègre avec des plateformes de développement comme openclaw et claudecode"],"de":["Erstellt umfassende automatisierte Tests","Folgt den Grundsätzen der roten Phase von TDD","Erfasst das erwartete Verhalten","Deckt Randfälle vor der Implementierung ab","Verbessert die Test- und Entwicklungsfähigkeiten","Integriert mit Entwicklungsumgebungen wie openclaw und claudecode"],"pt":["Escrita de testes abrangentes de falha","Seguimento dos princípios da fase vermelha do TDD","Cobertura de casos de bordo antes da implementação","Geração de testes que definem o comportamento esperado","Integração com o agente test-automator"],"ru":["Написание комплексных тестов на отказ","Следование принципам красного этапа TDD","Покрытие граничных случаев до реализации","Генерация тестов, определяющих ожидаемое поведение","Интеграция с агентом test-automator"],"ar":["كتابة الاختبارات الشاملة للفشل","اتباع مبادئ الطور الأحمر من TDD","التغطية الحالات الحدية قبل التنفيذ","توليد الاختبارات التي تعرف السلوك المتوقع","التكامل مع وكيل test-automator"]},"keywords":{"zh":["TDD 工作流","失败测试","红色阶段","预期行为","代码质量","可靠性","边界情况测试"],"ja":["TDD ワークフロー","失敗テスト","レッドフェーズ","期待する動作","コードの品質","信頼性","境界状況のテスト"],"ko":["TDD 워크플로우","실패 테스트","레드 단계","예상 동작","코드 품질","신뢰성","경계 상황 테스트"],"es":["TDD","pruebas automatizadas","desarrollo de software","fase roja de TDD","pruebas exhaustivas","casos de borde","openclaw","claudecode"],"fr":["TDD","tests automatisés","développement de logiciels","phase rouge de TDD","tests exhaustifs","cas de bordure","openclaw","claudecode"],"de":["TDD","automatisierte Tests","Softwareentwicklung","rote Phase von TDD","umfassende Tests","Randfälle","openclaw","claudecode"],"pt":["TDD","Test-Driven Development","Fase Vermelha","Testes de Falha","Desenvolvimento de Software","Testes Automatizados"],"ru":["TDD","Test-Driven Development","Красный Этап","Тесты На Отказ","Разработка Программного Обеспечения","Автоматизированное Тестирование"],"ar":["TDD","التطوير الموجه بالاختبار","الطور الأحمر","الاختبارات الفاشلة","تطوير البرمجيات","الاختبارات الآلية"]}},"owner":"YPYT1","repo":"All-skills","repoPath":"YPYT1/All-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.417Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"tdd-workflows-tdd-red","description":"Generate failing tests for the TDD red phase to define expected behavior and edge cases.","bodyPreview":"Write comprehensive failing tests following TDD red phase principles.\n\n[Extended thinking: Generates failing tests that properly define expected behavior using test-automator agent.]\n\n## Use this skill when\n\n- Starting the TDD red phase for new behavior\n- You need failing tests that capture expected behavior\n- You want edge case coverage before implementation\n\n## Do not use this skill when\n\n- You are in the green or refactor phase\n- You only need performance benchmarks\n- Tests must run against p","body":"Write comprehensive failing tests following TDD red phase principles.\n\n[Extended thinking: Generates failing tests that properly define expected behavior using test-automator agent.]\n\n## Use this skill when\n\n- Starting the TDD red phase for new behavior\n- You need failing tests that capture expected behavior\n- You want edge case coverage before implementation\n\n## Do not use this skill when\n\n- You are in the green or refactor phase\n- You only need performance benchmarks\n- Tests must run against production systems\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Identify behaviors, constraints, and edge cases.\n2. Generate failing tests that define expected outcomes.\n3. Ensure failures are due to missing behavior, not setup errors.\n4. Document how to run tests and verify failures.\n\n## Safety\n\n- Keep test data isolated and avoid production environments.\n- Avoid flaky external dependencies in the red phase.\n\n## Role\n\nGenerate failing tests using Task tool with subagent_type=\"unit-testing::test-automator\".\n\n## Prompt Template\n\n\"Generate comprehensive FAILING tests for: $ARGUMENTS\n\n## Core Requirements\n\n1. **Test Structure**\n   - Framework-appropriate setup (Jest/pytest/JUnit/Go/RSpec)\n   - Arrange-Act-Assert pattern\n   - should_X_when_Y naming convention\n   - Isolated fixtures with no interdependencies\n\n2. **Behavior Coverage**\n   - Happy path scenarios\n   - Edge cases (empty, null, boundary values)\n   - Error handling and exceptions\n   - Concurrent access (if applicable)\n\n3. **Failure Verification**\n   - Tests MUST fail when run\n   - Failures for RIGHT reasons (not syntax/import errors)\n   - Meaningful diagnostic error messages\n   - No cascading failures\n\n4. **Test Categories**\n   - Unit: Isolated component behavior\n   - Integration: Component interaction\n   - Contract: API/interface contracts\n   - Property: Mathematical invariants\n\n## Framework Patterns\n\n**JavaScript/TypeScript (Jest/Vitest)**\n- Mock dependencies with `vi.fn()` or `jest.fn()`\n- Use `@testing-library` for React components\n- Property tests with `fast-check`\n\n**Python (pytest)**\n- Fixtures with appropriate scopes\n- Parametrize for multiple test cases\n- Hypothesis for property-based tests\n\n**Go**\n- Table-driven tests with subtests\n- `t.Parallel()` for parallel execution\n- Use `testify/assert` for cleaner assertions\n\n**Ruby (RSpec)**\n- `let` for lazy loading, `let!` for eager\n- Contexts for different scenarios\n- Shared examples for common behavior\n\n## Quality Checklist\n\n- Readable test names documenting intent\n- One behavior per test\n- No implementation leakage\n- Meaningful test data (not ''foo''/''bar'')\n- Tests serve as living documentation\n\n## Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n- Tests passing immediately\n- Testing implementation vs behavior\n- Complex setup code\n- Multiple responsibilities per test\n- Brittle tests tied to specifics\n\n## Edge Case Categories\n\n- **Null/Empty**: undefined, null, empty string/array/object\n- **Boundaries**: min/max values, single element, capacity limits\n- **Special Cases**: Unicode, whitespace, special characters\n- **State**: Invalid transitions, concurrent modifications\n- **Errors**: Network failures, timeouts, permissions\n\n## Output Requirements\n\n- Complete test files with imports\n- Documentation of test purpose\n- Commands to run and verify failures\n- Metrics: test count, coverage areas\n- Next steps for green phase\"\n\n## Validation\n\nAfter generation:\n1. Run tests - confirm they fail\n2. Verify helpful failure messages\n3. Check test independence\n4. Ensure comprehensive coverage\n\n## Example (Minimal)\n\n```typescript\n// auth.service.test.ts\ndescribe(''AuthService'', () => {\n  let authService: AuthService;\n  let mockUserRepo: jest.Mocked<UserRepository>;\n\n  beforeEach(() => {\n    mockUserRepo = { findByEmail: jest.fn() } as any;\n    authService = new AuthService(mockUserRepo);\n  });\n\n  it(''should_return_token_when_valid_credentials'', async () => {\n    const user = { id: ''1'', email: ''test@example.com'', passwordHash: ''hashed'' };\n    mockUserRepo.findByEmail.mockResolvedValue(user);\n\n    const result = await authService.authenticate(''test@example.com'', ''pass'');\n\n    expect(result.success).toBe(true);\n    expect(result.token).toBeDefined();\n  });\n\n  it(''should_fail_when_user_not_found'', async () => {\n    mockUserRepo.findByEmail.mockResolvedValue(null);\n\n    const result = await authService.authenticate(''none@example.com'', ''pass'');\n\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false);\n    expect(result.error).toBe(''INVALID_CREDENTIALS'');\n  });\n});\n```\n\nTest requirements: $ARGUMENTS\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:09:40.906Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Test-Driven Development Agents needing automated test generation for the red phase.","zh":"非常适合需要自动化测试生成的测试驱动开发代理，特别是在红色阶段。","ja":"テスト駆動開発エージェントが赤いフェーズの自動テスト生成を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"자동화된 테스트 생성이 필요한 테스트 주도 개발 에이전트에게 적합하며, 특히 적색 단계에서 vậy.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas que necesitan generación automática de pruebas para la fase roja.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement piloté par les tests nécessitant une génération automatisée de tests pour la phase rouge.","de":"Perfekt für Test-Driven-Development-Agents, die eine automatisierte Testgenerierung für die rote Phase benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes que necessitam de geração automática de testes para a fase vermelha.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, управляемой тестированием, которым требуется автоматическая генерация тестов для красной фазы.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء التطويين القائمين على الاختبار الذين يحتاجون إلى توليد اختبارات آلي في مرحلة الحمرة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write comprehensive failing tests following TDD red phase principles, utilizing test-automator agents for edge case coverage and defining expected behavior, all while integrating with platforms like OpenClaw and ClaudeCode.","zh":"赋予代理编写全面性失败测试的能力，遵循TDD红色阶段的原则，利用测试自动化代理来覆盖边缘情况，并定义预期行为，同时与OpenClaw和ClaudeCode等平台集成。","ja":"TDDの赤いフェーズの原則に従って包括的な失敗テストを記述するエージェントの能力を提供し、エッジケースのカバレッジのためにテスト自動化エージェントを利用し、期待される動作を定義し、OpenClawやClaudeCodeなどのプラットフォームと統合します。","ko":"TDD 적색 단계 원칙에 따라 포괄적인 실패 테스트를 작성할 수 있는 에이전트의 능력을 제공하며, 테스트 자동화 에이전트를 사용하여 에지 케이스 커버리지와 예상 동작을 정의하며, OpenClaw 및 ClaudeCode와 같은 플랫폼과 통합합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a escribir pruebas exhaustivas con fallos siguiendo los principios de la fase roja de TDD, utilizando agentes automatizadores de pruebas para la cobertura de casos límite y definiendo el comportamiento esperado, todo mientras se integra con plataformas como OpenClaw y ClaudeCode.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''écrire des tests complets avec des erreurs en suivant les principes de la phase rouge de TDD, en utilisant des agents automatisés de test pour la couverture des cas limites et en définissant le comportement attendu, le tout en s''intégrant avec des plateformes comme OpenClaw et ClaudeCode.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, umfassende fehlerhafte Tests zu schreiben, die den Grundsätzen der roten Phase von TDD folgen, indem Testautomatisierungsagenten für den Schutz von Randfällen und die Definition des erwarteten Verhaltens verwendet werden, all dies bei der Integration mit Plattformen wie OpenClaw und ClaudeCode.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a escreverem testes abrangentes com falha, seguindo os princípios da fase vermelha do TDD, utilizando agentes automatizadores de testes para cobertura de casos extremos e definindo o comportamento esperado, tudo isso integrado a plataformas como OpenClaw e ClaudeCode.","ru":"Позволяет агентам писать полные тесты с неудачей, следуя принципам красной фазы TDD, используя агентов-автоматизаторов тестов для покрытия граничных случаев и определения ожидаемого поведения, все это интегрируется с платформами типа OpenClaw и ClaudeCode.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من كتابة اختبارات شاملة مع فشل، اتباعًا لمبادئ مرحلة الحمرة في التطوير القائم على الاختبار، مستخدمين وكلاء آليين لاختبارات لتغطية الحالات القصوى وتحديد السلوك المتوقع، مع كل ذلك المتكامل مع منصات مثل OpenClaw وClaudeCode."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating test generation for new behavior","Generating failing tests for edge case coverage","Defining expected behavior before implementation"],"zh":["为新行为自动化测试生成","为边缘情况覆盖生成失败测试","在实施之前定义预期行为"],"ja":["新しい動作の自動テスト生成","エッジケースのカバレッジのための失敗テストの生成","実装前に期待される動作を定義"],"ko":["새로운 동작을 위한 자동화된 테스트 생성","에지 케이스 커버리지에 대한 실패 테스트 생성","구현之前에 예상되는 동작을 정의"],"es":["Automatización de la generación de pruebas para nuevo comportamiento","Generación de pruebas con fallos para la cobertura de casos límite","Definir el comportamiento esperado antes de la implementación"],"fr":["Automatisation de la génération de tests pour un nouveau comportement","Génération de tests avec des erreurs pour la couverture des cas limites","Définition du comportement attendu avant la mise en œuvre"],"de":["Automatisierung der Testgenerierung für neues Verhalten","Generierung fehlerhafter Tests für den Schutz von Randfällen","Definition des erwarteten Verhaltens vor der Implementierung"],"pt":["Automatizar a geração de testes para novo comportamento","Gerar testes com falha para cobertura de casos extremos","Definir comportamento esperado antes da implementação"],"ru":["Автоматизировать генерацию тестов для нового поведения","Генерировать тесты с неудачей для покрытия граничных случаев","Определить ожидаемое поведение до реализации"],"ar":["آليَة توليد الاختبارات للتصرّف الجديد","إنتاج اختبارات الفشل لتغطية الحالات القصوى","تحديد السلوك المتوقع قبل التنفيذ"]},"limitations":{"en":["Only applicable during the TDD red phase","Not suitable for performance benchmarks","Tests must not run against production environments"],"zh":["仅适用于TDD红色阶段","不适用于性能基准测试","测试不得在生产环境中运行"],"ja":["TDDの赤いフェーズでのみ適用可能","パフォーマンスベンチマークには不向き","テストは運用環境で実行できません"],"ko":["TDD 적색 단계에서만 적용 가능","성능 벤치마크에는 부적합","테스트는 프로덕션 환경에서 실행할 수 없음"],"es":[" Solo aplicable durante la fase roja de TDD","No es adecuado para pruebas de rendimiento","Las pruebas no deben ejecutarse en entornos de producción"],"fr":["N''est applicable que pendant la phase rouge de TDD","N''est pas adapté pour les tests de performance","Les tests ne doivent pas être exécutés dans des environnements de production"],"de":["Nur während der roten Phase von TDD anwendbar","Nicht geeignet für Leistungstests","Tests dürfen nicht in Produktionsumgebungen ausgeführt werden"],"pt":["Apenas aplicável durante a fase vermelha do TDD","Não adequado para benchmarks de desempenho","Os testes não devem ser executados em ambientes de produção"],"ru":["Применимо только во время красной фазы TDD","Не подходит для тестирования производительности","Тесты не должны запускаться в производственных средах"],"ar":["مطبّق فقط خلال مرحلة الحمرة من التطوير القائم على الاختبار","غير مناسب لاختبارات الأداء","لا يجب تشغيل الاختبارات في بيئات الإنتاج"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/context-compression', 'community', 'majiayu000', 'claude-skill-registry', 'majiayu000/claude-skill-registry', 'context-compression', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.417Z', '2026-02-18T04:10:36.521Z', NULL, '{"id":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/context-compression","name":"context-compression","description":{"es":"La compresión de contexto es una estrategia para optimizar el rendimiento de los agentes. Reduce los tokens y mejora la eficiencia en las sesiones de agente","fr":"La compression de contexte est une stratégie pour optimiser les performances des agents. Elle réduit les tokens et améliore l''efficacité dans les sessions d''agent","de":"Die Kontextkomprimierung ist eine Strategie zur Optimierung der Leistung von Agenten. Sie reduziert die Token und verbessert die Effizienz in den Agentsitzungen","pt":"A compressão de contexto é uma técnica para reduzir a quantidade de tokens em agentes de conversação, melhorando o desempenho e a eficiência","ru":"Сжатие контекста - это техника, которая уменьшает количество токенов в агентах разговора, улучшая производительность и эффективность","ar":"ضغط السياق هو تقنية لتقليل عدد الرموز في وكلاء المحادثة، مما يحسن الأداء والكفاءة","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"seo":{"title":{"es":"Compresión de contexto para desarrolladores","fr":"Compression de contexte pour développeurs","de":"Kontextkomprimierung für Entwickler","pt":"Compressão de Contexto: Otimização de Tokens","ru":"Сжатие контекста: оптимизация токенов","ar":"ضغط السياق: تحسين الرموز","en":"context-compression"},"description":{"es":"La compresión de contexto es una estrategia para optimizar el rendimiento de los agentes. Reduce los tokens y mejora la eficiencia en las sesiones de agente","fr":"La compression de contexte est une stratégie pour optimiser les performances des agents. Elle réduit les tokens et améliore l''efficacité dans les sessions d''...","de":"Die Kontextkomprimierung ist eine Strategie zur Optimierung der Leistung von Agenten. Sie reduziert die Token und verbessert die Effizienz in den Agentsitzungen","pt":"A compressão de contexto é uma técnica para reduzir a quantidade de tokens em agentes de conversação, melhorando o desempenho e a eficiência","ru":"Сжатие контекста - это техника, которая уменьшает количество токенов в агентах разговора, улучшая производительность и эффективность","ar":"ضغط السياق هو تقنية لتقليل عدد الرموز في وكلاء المحادثة، مما يحسن الأداء والكفاءة","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"es":["Reducción de tokens en las sesiones de agente","Mejora de la eficiencia en las sesiones de agente","Optimización del rendimiento de los agentes","Reducir los costos de re-fecthing"," Mejora de la experiencia del usuario","Compatibilidad con código abierto"],"fr":["Réduction des tokens dans les sessions d''agent","Amélioration de l''efficacité dans les sessions d''agent","Optimisation des performances des agents","Réduction des coûts de re-fecthing","Amélioration de l''expérience utilisateur","Compatibilité avec le code ouvert"],"de":["Reduzierung der Token in den Agentsitzungen","Verbesserung der Effizienz in den Agentsitzungen","Optimierung der Leistung von Agenten","Reduzierung der Kosten für das erneute Fetchen","Verbesserung der Benutzererfahrung","Kompatibilität mit Open-Source-Code"],"pt":["Otimização de tokens","Redução de custos de re-fetching","Melhoria do desempenho em agentes de conversação","Compatibilidade com limites de janela de contexto","Integração com codebases"],"ru":["Оптимизация токенов","Уменьшение затрат на повторную загрузку","Улучшение производительности в агентах разговора","Совместимость с ограничениями контекстного окна","Интеграция с кодовыми базами"],"ar":["تحسين الرموز","تقليل تكاليف إعادة التحميل","تحسين الأداء في وكلاء المحادثة","التوافق مع حدود نافذة السياق","التكامل مع قواعد البيانات"]},"keywords":{"es":["compresión de contexto","optimización de agentes","reducción de tokens","eficiencia en sesiones de agente","desarrollo de software","tecnologías de inteligencia artificial","desarrollo de chatbots","optimización de rendimiento"],"fr":["compression de contexte","optimisation d''agents","réduction de tokens","efficacité dans les sessions d''agent","développement de logiciels","technologies d''intelligence artificielle","développement de chatbots","optimisation de performances"],"de":["Kontextkomprimierung","Optimierung von Agenten","Reduzierung von Token","Effizienz in Agentsitzungen","Softwareentwicklung","Künstliche-Intelligenz-Technologien","Chatbot-Entwicklung","Leistungsoptimierung"],"pt":["compressão de contexto","otimização de tokens","agentes de conversação","desempenho","eficiência","codebases","limites de janela de contexto"],"ru":["сжатие контекста","оптимизация токенов","агенты разговора","производительность","эффективность","кодовые базы","ограничения контекстного окна"],"ar":["ضغط السياق","تحسين الرموز","وكلاء المحادثة","الأداء","الكفاءة","قواعد البيانات","حدود نافذة السياق"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.417Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"context-compression","description":"This skill should be used when the user asks to compress context, summarize conversation history, implement compaction, reduce token usage, or mentions context compression, structured summarization, tokens-per-task optimization, or long-running agent sessions exceeding context limits.","bodyPreview":"# Context Compression Strategies\n\nWhen agent sessions generate millions of tokens of conversation history, compression becomes mandatory. The naive approach is aggressive compression to minimize tokens per request. The correct optimization target is tokens per task: total tokens consumed to complete a task, including re-fetching costs when compression loses critical information.\n\n## When to Activate\n\nActivate this skill when:\n- Agent sessions exceed context window limits\n- Codebases exceed conte","body":"# Context Compression Strategies\n\nWhen agent sessions generate millions of tokens of conversation history, compression becomes mandatory. The naive approach is aggressive compression to minimize tokens per request. The correct optimization target is tokens per task: total tokens consumed to complete a task, including re-fetching costs when compression loses critical information.\n\n## When to Activate\n\nActivate this skill when:\n- Agent sessions exceed context window limits\n- Codebases exceed context windows (5M+ token systems)\n- Designing conversation summarization strategies\n- Debugging cases where agents \"forget\" what files they modified\n- Building evaluation frameworks for compression quality\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nContext compression trades token savings against information loss. Three production-ready approaches exist:\n\n1. **Anchored Iterative Summarization**: Maintain structured, persistent summaries with explicit sections for session intent, file modifications, decisions, and next steps. When compression triggers, summarize only the newly-truncated span and merge with the existing summary. Structure forces preservation by dedicating sections to specific information types.\n\n2. **Opaque Compression**: Produce compressed representations optimized for reconstruction fidelity. Achieves highest compression ratios (99%+) but sacrifices interpretability. Cannot verify what was preserved.\n\n3. **Regenerative Full Summary**: Generate detailed structured summaries on each compression. Produces readable output but may lose details across repeated compression cycles due to full regeneration rather than incremental merging.\n\nThe critical insight: structure forces preservation. Dedicated sections act as checklists that the summarizer must populate, preventing silent information drift.\n\n## Detailed Topics\n\n### Why Tokens-Per-Task Matters\n\nTraditional compression metrics target tokens-per-request. This is the wrong optimization. When compression loses critical details like file paths or error messages, the agent must re-fetch information, re-explore approaches, and waste tokens recovering context.\n\nThe right metric is tokens-per-task: total tokens consumed from task start to completion. A compression strategy saving 0.5% more tokens but causing 20% more re-fetching costs more overall.\n\n### The Artifact Trail Problem\n\nArtifact trail integrity is the weakest dimension across all compression methods, scoring 2.2-2.5 out of 5.0 in evaluations. Even structured summarization with explicit file sections struggles to maintain complete file tracking across long sessions.\n\nCoding agents need to know:\n- Which files were created\n- Which files were modified and what changed\n- Which files were read but not changed\n- Function names, variable names, error messages\n\nThis problem likely requires specialized handling beyond general summarization: a separate artifact index or explicit file-state tracking in agent scaffolding.\n\n### Structured Summary Sections\n\nEffective structured summaries include explicit sections:\n\n```markdown\n## Session Intent\n[What the user is trying to accomplish]\n\n## Files Modified\n- auth.controller.ts: Fixed JWT token generation\n- config/redis.ts: Updated connection pooling\n- tests/auth.test.ts: Added mock setup for new config\n\n## Decisions Made\n- Using Redis connection pool instead of per-request connections\n- Retry logic with exponential backoff for transient failures\n\n## Current State\n- 14 tests passing, 2 failing\n- Remaining: mock setup for session service tests\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Fix remaining test failures\n2. Run full test suite\n3. Update documentation\n```\n\nThis structure prevents silent loss of file paths or decisions because each section must be explicitly addressed.\n\n### Compression Trigger Strategies\n\nWhen to trigger compression matters as much as how to compress:\n\n| Strategy | Trigger Point | Trade-off |\n|----------|---------------|-----------|\n| Fixed threshold | 70-80% context utilization | Simple but may compress too early |\n| Sliding window | Keep last N turns + summary | Predictable context size |\n| Importance-based | Compress low-relevance sections first | Complex but preserves signal |\n| Task-boundary | Compress at logical task completions | Clean summaries but unpredictable timing |\n\nThe sliding window approach with structured summaries provides the best balance of predictability and quality for most coding agent use cases.\n\n### Probe-Based Evaluation\n\nTraditional metrics like ROUGE or embedding similarity fail to capture functional compression quality. A summary may score high on lexical overlap while missing the one file path the agent needs.\n\nProbe-based evaluation directly measures functional quality by asking questions after compression:\n\n| Probe Type | What It Tests | Example Question |\n|------------|---------------|------------------|\n| Recall | Factual retention | \"What was the original error message?\" |\n| Artifact | File tracking | \"Which files have we modified?\" |\n| Continuation | Task planning | \"What should we do next?\" |\n| Decision | Reasoning chain | \"What did we decide about the Redis issue?\" |\n\nIf compression preserved the right information, the agent answers correctly. If not, it guesses or hallucinates.\n\n### Evaluation Dimensions\n\nSix dimensions capture compression quality for coding agents:\n\n1. **Accuracy**: Are technical details correct? File paths, function names, error codes.\n2. **Context Awareness**: Does the response reflect current conversation state?\n3. **Artifact Trail**: Does the agent know which files were read or modified?\n4. **Completeness**: Does the response address all parts of the question?\n5. **Continuity**: Can work continue without re-fetching information?\n6. **Instruction Following**: Does the response respect stated constraints?\n\nAccuracy shows the largest variation between compression methods (0.6 point gap). Artifact trail is universally weak (2.2-2.5 range).\n\n## Practical Guidance\n\n### Three-Phase Compression Workflow\n\nFor large codebases or agent systems exceeding context windows, apply compression through three phases:\n\n1. **Research Phase**: Produce a research document from architecture diagrams, documentation, and key interfaces. Compress exploration into a structured analysis of components and dependencies. Output: single research document.\n\n2. **Planning Phase**: Convert research into implementation specification with function signatures, type definitions, and data flow. A 5M token codebase compresses to approximately 2,000 words of specification.\n\n3. **Implementation Phase**: Execute against the specification. Context remains focused on the spec rather than raw codebase exploration.\n\n### Using Example Artifacts as Seeds\n\nWhen provided with a manual migration example or reference PR, use it as a template to understand the target pattern. The example reveals constraints that static analysis cannot surface: which invariants must hold, which services break on changes, and what a clean migration looks like.\n\nThis is particularly important when the agent cannot distinguish essential complexity (business requirements) from accidental complexity (legacy workarounds). The example artifact encodes that distinction.\n\n### Implementing Anchored Iterative Summarization\n\n1. Define explicit summary sections matching your agent''s needs\n2. On first compression trigger, summarize truncated history into sections\n3. On subsequent compressions, summarize only new truncated content\n4. Merge new summary into existing sections rather than regenerating\n5. Track which information came from which compression cycle for debugging\n\n### When to Use Each Approach\n\n**Use anchored iterative summarization when:**\n- Sessions are long-running (100+ messages)\n- File tracking matters (coding, debugging)\n- You need to verify what was preserved\n\n**Use opaque compression when:**\n- Maximum token savings required\n- Sessions are relatively short\n- Re-fetching costs are low\n\n**Use regenerative summaries when:**\n- Summary interpretability is critical\n- Sessions have clear phase boundaries\n- Full context review is acceptable on each compression\n\n### Compression Ratio Considerations\n\n| Method | Compression Ratio | Quality Score | Trade-off |\n|--------|-------------------|---------------|-----------|\n| Anchored Iterative | 98.6% | 3.70 | Best quality, slightly less compression |\n| Regenerative | 98.7% | 3.44 | Good quality, moderate compression |\n| Opaque | 99.3% | 3.35 | Best compression, quality loss |\n\nThe 0.7% additional tokens retained by structured summarization buys 0.35 quality points. For any task where re-fetching costs matter, this trade-off favors structured approaches.\n\n## Examples\n\n**Example 1: Debugging Session Compression**\n\nOriginal context (89,000 tokens, 178 messages):\n- 401 error on /api/auth/login endpoint\n- Traced through auth controller, middleware, session store\n- Found stale Redis connection\n- Fixed connection pooling, added retry logic\n- 14 tests passing, 2 failing\n\nStructured summary after compression:\n\n```markdown\n## Session Intent\nDebug 401 Unauthorized error on /api/auth/login despite valid credentials.\n\n## Root Cause\nStale Redis connection in session store. JWT generated correctly but session could not be persisted.\n\n## Files Modified\n- auth.controller.ts: No changes (read only)\n- middleware/cors.ts: No changes (examined)\n- config/redis.ts: Fixed connection pooling configuration\n- services/session.service.ts: Added retry logic for transient failures\n- tests/auth.test.ts: Updated mock setup\n\n## Test Status\n14 passing, 2 failing (mock setup issues)\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Fix remaining test failures (mock session service)\n2. Run full test suite\n3. Deploy to staging\n```\n\n**Example 2: Probe Response Quality**\n\nAfter compression, asking \"What was the original error?\":\n\nGood response (structured summarization):\n> \"The original error was a 401 Unauthorized response from the /api/auth/login endpoint. Users received this error with valid credentials. Root cause was stale Redis connection in session store.\"\n\nPoor response (aggressive compression):\n> \"We were debugging an authentication issue. The login was failing. We fixed some configuration problems.\"\n\nThe structured response preserves endpoint, error code, and root cause. The aggressive response loses all technical detail.\n\n## Guidelines\n\n1. Optimize for tokens-per-task, not tokens-per-request\n2. Use structured summaries with explicit sections for file tracking\n3. Trigger compression at 70-80% context utilization\n4. Implement incremental merging rather than full regeneration\n5. Test compression quality with probe-based evaluation\n6. Track artifact trail separately if file tracking is critical\n7. Accept slightly lower compression ratios for better quality retention\n8. Monitor re-fetching frequency as a compression quality signal\n\n## Integration\n\nThis skill connects to several others in the collection:\n\n- context-degradation - Compression is a mitigation strategy for degradation\n- context-optimization - Compression is one optimization technique among many\n- evaluation - Probe-based evaluation applies to compression testing\n- memory-systems - Compression relates to scratchpad and summary memory patterns\n\n## References\n\nInternal reference:\n- [Evaluation Framework Reference](./references/evaluation-framework.md) - Detailed probe types and scoring rubrics\n\nRelated skills in this collection:\n- context-degradation - Understanding what compression prevents\n- context-optimization - Broader optimization strategies\n- evaluation - Building evaluation frameworks\n\nExternal resources:\n- Factory Research: Evaluating Context Compression for AI Agents (December 2025)\n- Research on LLM-as-judge evaluation methodology (Zheng et al., 2023)\n- Netflix Engineering: \"The Infinite Software Crisis\" - Three-phase workflow and context compression at scale (AI Summit 2025)\n\n---\n\n## Skill Metadata\n\n**Created**: 2025-12-22\n**Last Updated**: 2025-12-26\n**Author**: Agent Skills for Context Engineering Contributors\n**Version**: 1.1.0\n\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:10:36.521Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Conversational Agents like Claude Code, AutoGPT, and LangChain requiring efficient context compression to handle large conversation histories.","zh":"适用于像 Claude Code、AutoGPT 和 LangChain 这样的对话式代理，需要高效的上下文压缩来处理大型对话历史。","ja":"Claude Code、AutoGPT、LangChain などの会話エージェントに適しており、大規模な会話履歴を扱うための効率的なコンテキスト圧縮が必要です。","ko":"클라우드 코드, 오토 GPT, 랭체인과 같은 대화형 에이전트에 적합하며, 대규모 대화 기록을 처리하기 위한 효율적인 문맥 압축이 필요합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de conversación como Claude Code, AutoGPT y LangChain que requieren una compresión de contexto eficiente para manejar historias de conversación grandes.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de conversation tels que Claude Code, AutoGPT et LangChain nécessitant une compression de contexte efficace pour gérer de grandes histoires de conversation.","de":"Ideal für Konversationsagenten wie Claude Code, AutoGPT und LangChain, die eine effiziente Kontextkomprimierung benötigen, um große Konversationshistorien zu verarbeiten.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de conversação como Claude Code, AutoGPT e LangChain que exigem compressão de contexto eficiente para lidar com grandes históricos de conversa.","ru":"Идеально подходит для разговорных агентов, таких как Claude Code, AutoGPT и LangChain, требующих эффективного сжатия контекста для обработки больших историй разговоров.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكلاء مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT و LangChain التي تتطلب ضغط سياق فعال للتعامل مع تاريخ حوار طويل."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to optimize tokens per task by leveraging advanced compression strategies, minimizing re-fetching costs and maximizing information retention, all while navigating context window limits and codebase constraints.","zh":"通过利用高级压缩策略来优化每个任务的令牌数，最大限度地减少重新获取成本并最大限度地保留信息，同时在上下文窗口限制和代码库约束范围内进行导航。","ja":"高度な圧縮戦略を利用して、タスクごとのトークン数を最適化し、再取得コストを最小限に抑え、情報の保持を最大化する，同时にコンテキストウィンドウの制限やコードベースの制約の中でナビゲートします。","ko":"고급 압축 전략을 활용하여 각 작업의 토큰 수를 최적화하고, 재조회 비용을 최소화하고 정보 보존을 최대화하며,同時에 문맥 창 제한과 코드베이스 제약 범위 내에서 탐색합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes optimizar los tokens por tarea mediante estrategias de compresión avanzadas, minimizando los costos de recuperación y maximizando la retención de información, todo mientras navega por los límites de la ventana de contexto y las restricciones del código.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''optimiser les jetons par tâche en exploitant des stratégies de compression avancées, en minimisant les coûts de réactualisation et en maximisant la rétention d''informations, le tout en naviguant dans les limites de la fenêtre de contexte et les contraintes du codebase.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, Token pro Aufgabe durch fortschrittliche Komprimierungsstrategien zu optimieren, die Abrufkosten zu minimieren und die Informationsretention zu maximieren, während sie innerhalb der Kontextfensterlimits und Codebase-Einschränkungen navigieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a otimizar tokens por tarefa, aproveitando estratégias de compressão avançadas, minimizando custos de re-recuperação e maximizando a retenção de informações, tudo isso enquanto navega pelos limites da janela de contexto e restrições de codebase.","ru":"Позволяет агентам оптимизировать токены на задачу, используя передовые стратегии сжатия, минимизируя затраты на повторную выборку и максимизируя сохранение информации, все это при навигации по пределам контекстного окна и ограничениям кодовой базы.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من تحسين الرموز لكل مهمة من خلال الاستفادة من استراتيجيات الضغط المتقدمة، وتقليل تكاليف إعادة الاسترجاع وتحقيق أقصى استفادة من الحفظ المعلوماتي، وكل ذلك أثناء التنقل في حدود نافذة السياق وقيود قاعدة الشفرة."},"useCases":{"en":["Compressing extensive conversation histories to reduce token counts","Optimizing agent performance by balancing compression and information loss","Streamlining codebases by applying context compression to large datasets"],"zh":["压缩大量对话历史以减少令牌数","通过平衡压缩和信息损失来优化代理性能","通过将上下文压缩应用于大型数据集来简化代码库"],"ja":["大量の会話履歴を圧縮してトークン数を削減する","圧縮と情報損失のバランスをとってエージェントの性能を最適化する","大規模なデータセットにコンテキスト圧縮を適用してコードベースを簡素化する"],"ko":["대규모 대화 기록을 압축하여 토큰 수를 줄임","압축과 정보 손실의 균형을 맞추어 에이전트 성능을 최적화함","대규모 데이터셋에 문맥 압축을 적용하여 코드베이스를 간소화함"],"es":["Comprimir historias de conversación extensas para reducir el recuento de tokens","Optimizar el rendimiento del agente equilibrando la compresión y la pérdida de información","Racionalizar los codebases aplicando la compresión de contexto a grandes conjuntos de datos"],"fr":["Compresser des histoires de conversation extensives pour réduire le nombre de jetons","Optimiser les performances de l''agent en équilibrant la compression et la perte d''informations","Rationaliser les codebases en appliquant la compression de contexte à de grands ensembles de données"],"de":["Umfangreiche Konversationshistorien komprimieren, um die Tokenanzahl zu reduzieren","Die Leistung des Agents optimieren, indem Komprimierung und Informationsverlust ausbalanciert werden","Codebases rationalisieren, indem die Kontextkomprimierung auf große Datensätze angewendet wird"],"pt":["Comprimir históricos de conversa extensos para reduzir a contagem de tokens","Otimizar o desempenho do agente, equilibrando a compressão e a perda de informações","Otimizar codebases aplicando a compressão de contexto a grandes conjuntos de dados"],"ru":["Сжимать обширные истории разговоров, чтобы уменьшить количество токенов","Оптимизировать производительность агента, балансируя сжатие и потерю информации","Оптимизировать кодовые базы, применяя сжатие контекста к большим наборам данных"],"ar":["ضغط تاريخ حوار طويل لتقليل عدد الرموز","تحسين أداء العميل من خلال موازنة الضغط وفقدان المعلومات","تبسيط قواعد الشفرة بتطبيق ضغط السياق على مجموعات بيانات كبيرة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires careful calibration to avoid critical information loss","May not be suitable for extremely short conversation histories or small codebases","Agent sessions must exceed context window limits to fully benefit from this skill"],"zh":["需要仔细校准以避免关键信息损失","可能不适合非常短的对话历史或小型代码库","代理会话必须超过上下文窗口限制才能充分受益于此技能"],"ja":["重要な情報の損失を避けるために、慎重な調整が必要","非常に短い会話履歴や小規模なコードベースには適さない可能性がある","エージェントのセッションは、コンテキストウィンドウの制限を超える必要があり、このスキルから十分に利益を得る"],"ko":["중요한 정보 손실을 피하기 위해慎重한 조정이 필요함","非常히 짧은 대화 기록이나 작은 코드베이스에는 적합하지 않을 수 있음","에이전트 세션은 문맥 창 제한을 초과해야 하며, 이 기술에서 충분히 이익을 얻음"],"es":["Requiere una calibración cuidadosa para evitar la pérdida crítica de información","Puede no ser adecuado para historias de conversación extremadamente cortas o codebases pequeños","Las sesiones del agente deben superar los límites de la ventana de contexto para beneficiarse completamente de esta habilidad"],"fr":["Nécessite une calibration soigneuse pour éviter la perte critique d''informations","Peut ne pas convenir pour des histoires de conversation extrêmement courtes ou des codebases petits","Les sessions de l''agent doivent dépasser les limites de la fenêtre de contexte pour bénéficier pleinement de cette compétence"],"de":["Benötigt eine sorgfältige Kalibrierung, um einen kritischen Informationsverlust zu vermeiden","Kann nicht geeignet sein für extrem kurze Konversationshistorien oder kleine Codebases","Die Sitzungen des Agents müssen die Kontextfensterlimits überschreiten, um sich vollständig von dieser Fähigkeit zu profitieren"],"pt":["Exige calibração cuidadosa para evitar perda crítica de informações","Pode não ser adequado para históricos de conversa extremamente curtos ou codebases pequenas","As sessões do agente devem exceder os limites da janela de contexto para aproveitar completamente essa habilidade"],"ru":["Требует тщательной калибровки, чтобы избежать критической потери информации","Может быть не подходящим для очень коротких историй разговоров или небольших кодовых баз","Сессии агента должны превышать пределы контекстного окна, чтобы полностью воспользоваться этим навыком"],"ar":["يتطلب تعديلاً دقيقاً لتجنب فقدان المعلومات الحرج","قد لا يكون مناسبًا لتاريخ حوار قصير جداً أو قواعد شفرة صغيرة","يجب أن تتجاوز جلسات العميل حدود نافذة السياق للاستفادة الكاملة من هذه المهارة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
