ion"},"description":{"zh":"上下文压缩技术用于优化对话历史记录，减少任务完成时间","ja":"コンテキスト圧縮技術は会話履歴を最適化してタスク完了時間を短縮する","ko":"컨텍스트 압축 기술은 대화 기록을 최적화하여 작업 완료 시간을 단축","es":"La compresión de contexto permite a los agentes AI resolver problemas complejos de manera sistemática","fr":"La compression de contexte permet aux agents IA de résoudre des problèmes complexes de manière systématique","de":"Die Kontextkomprimierung ermöglicht es KI-Agenten, komplexe Probleme systematisch zu lösen","pt":"A compressão de contexto é uma técnica para otimizar tokens em sessões de agentes, melhorando a eficiência em desenvolvimento full-stack e resolução de probl...","ru":"Сжатие контекста - это техника для оптимизации токенов в сессиях агентов, улучшающая эффективность в полном цикле разработки и решении сложных проблем","ar":"ضغط السياق هو تقنية لتحسين الرموز في جلسات الوكيل، مما يحسن الكفاءة في التطوير الكامل وحل المشكلات المعقدة","en":"Empower agents with professional capabilities in specific fields (such as full-stack development, complex logic planning, multimedia processing, etc.) throug..."},"definition":{"en":"Empower agents with professional capabilities in specific fields (such as full-stack development, complex logic planning, multimedia processing, etc.) through modular Skills definitions, allowing agents to solve complex problems systematically like human experts."},"features":{"zh":["优化对话历史记录","减少任务完成时间","支持多种开发语言","提高代码复用率","简化开发流程"],"ja":["会話履歴の最適化","タスク完了時間の短縮","複数の開発言語をサポート","コードの再利用性の向上","開発プロセスの簡素化"],"ko":["대화 기록 최적화","작업 완료 시간 단축","다중 개발 언어 지원","코드 재사용성 향상","개발 프로세스 간소화"],"es":["Reducir tokens por solicitud","Optimizar la compresión de contexto","Resolver problemas complejos de manera sistemática","Mejorar la eficiencia de los agentes AI","Reducir costos de re-fetching"],"fr":["Réduire les tokens par requête","Optimiser la compression de contexte","Résoudre des problèmes complexes de manière systématique","Améliorer l''efficacité des agents IA","Réduire les coûts de re-fetching"],"de":["Token pro Anfrage reduzieren","Kontextkomprimierung optimieren","Komplexe Probleme systematisch lösen","Effizienz von KI-Agenten verbessern","Re-fetching-Kosten reduzieren"],"pt":["Otimização de tokens em sessões de agentes","Melhoria da eficiência em desenvolvimento full-stack","Resolução de problemas complexos de forma sistemática","Redução de custos de re-fetching","Melhoria da experiência do usuário"],"ru":["Оптимизация токенов в сессиях агентов","Улучшение эффективности в полном цикле разработки","Решение сложных проблем систематическим образом","Снижение затрат на повторную загрузку","Улучшение пользовательского опыта"],"ar":["تحسين الرموز في جلسات الوكيل","تحسين الكفاءة في التطوير الكامل","حل المشكلات المعقدة بطريقة منهجية","تخفيض تكاليف إعادة التحميل","تحسين تجربة المستخدم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["上下文压缩","对话历史记录","任务完成时间","开发语言","代码复用","开发流程","会话管理"],"ja":["コンテキスト圧縮","会話履歴","タスク完了時間","開発言語","コード再利用","開発プロセス","セッション管理"],"ko":["컨텍스트 압축","대화 기록","작업 완료 시간","개발 언어","코드 재사용","개발 프로세스","세션 관리"],"es":["compresión de contexto","agentes AI","optimización de tokens","resolución de problemas complejos","eficiencia de agentes AI","reducción de costos","desarrollo de IA","tecnologías de compresión"],"fr":["compression de contexte","agents IA","optimisation de tokens","résolution de problèmes complexes","efficacité des agents IA","réduction de coûts","développement d''IA","technologies de compression"],"de":["Kontextkomprimierung","KI-Agenten","Token-Optimierung","Lösung komplexer Probleme","Effizienz von KI-Agenten","Kostenreduzierung","KI-Entwicklung","Komprimierungstechnologien"],"pt":["compressão de contexto","otimização de tokens","desenvolvimento full-stack","resolução de problemas complexos","eficiência em desenvolvimento","tecnologia de compressão"],"ru":["сжатие контекста","оптимизация токенов","полный цикл разработки","решение сложных проблем","эффективность в разработке","технология сжатия"],"ar":["ضغط السياق","تحسين الرموز","التطوير الكامل","حل المشكلات المعقدة","الكفاءة في التطوير","تكنولوجيا الضغط"]}},"owner":"guanyang","repo":"antigravity-skills","repoPath":"guanyang/antigravity-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.417Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"context-compression","description":"This skill should be used when the user asks to compress context, summarize conversation history, implement compaction, reduce token usage, or mentions context compression, structured summarization, tokens-per-task optimization, or long-running agent sessions exceeding context limits.","bodyPreview":"# Context Compression Strategies\n\nWhen agent sessions generate millions of tokens of conversation history, compression becomes mandatory. The naive approach is aggressive compression to minimize tokens per request. The correct optimization target is tokens per task: total tokens consumed to complete a task, including re-fetching costs when compression loses critical information.\n\n## When to Activate\n\nActivate this skill when:\n- Agent sessions exceed context window limits\n- Codebases exceed conte","body":"# Context Compression Strategies\n\nWhen agent sessions generate millions of tokens of conversation history, compression becomes mandatory. The naive approach is aggressive compression to minimize tokens per request. The correct optimization target is tokens per task: total tokens consumed to complete a task, including re-fetching costs when compression loses critical information.\n\n## When to Activate\n\nActivate this skill when:\n- Agent sessions exceed context window limits\n- Codebases exceed context windows (5M+ token systems)\n- Designing conversation summarization strategies\n- Debugging cases where agents \"forget\" what files they modified\n- Building evaluation frameworks for compression quality\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nContext compression trades token savings against information loss. Three production-ready approaches exist:\n\n1. **Anchored Iterative Summarization**: Maintain structured, persistent summaries with explicit sections for session intent, file modifications, decisions, and next steps. When compression triggers, summarize only the newly-truncated span and merge with the existing summary. Structure forces preservation by dedicating sections to specific information types.\n\n2. **Opaque Compression**: Produce compressed representations optimized for reconstruction fidelity. Achieves highest compression ratios (99%+) but sacrifices interpretability. Cannot verify what was preserved.\n\n3. **Regenerative Full Summary**: Generate detailed structured summaries on each compression. Produces readable output but may lose details across repeated compression cycles due to full regeneration rather than incremental merging.\n\nThe critical insight: structure forces preservation. Dedicated sections act as checklists that the summarizer must populate, preventing silent information drift.\n\n## Detailed Topics\n\n### Why Tokens-Per-Task Matters\n\nTraditional compression metrics target tokens-per-request. This is the wrong optimization. When compression loses critical details like file paths or error messages, the agent must re-fetch information, re-explore approaches, and waste tokens recovering context.\n\nThe right metric is tokens-per-task: total tokens consumed from task start to completion. A compression strategy saving 0.5% more tokens but causing 20% more re-fetching costs more overall.\n\n### The Artifact Trail Problem\n\nArtifact trail integrity is the weakest dimension across all compression methods, scoring 2.2-2.5 out of 5.0 in evaluations. Even structured summarization with explicit file sections struggles to maintain complete file tracking across long sessions.\n\nCoding agents need to know:\n- Which files were created\n- Which files were modified and what changed\n- Which files were read but not changed\n- Function names, variable names, error messages\n\nThis problem likely requires specialized handling beyond general summarization: a separate artifact index or explicit file-state tracking in agent scaffolding.\n\n### Structured Summary Sections\n\nEffective structured summaries include explicit sections:\n\n```markdown\n## Session Intent\n[What the user is trying to accomplish]\n\n## Files Modified\n- auth.controller.ts: Fixed JWT token generation\n- config/redis.ts: Updated connection pooling\n- tests/auth.test.ts: Added mock setup for new config\n\n## Decisions Made\n- Using Redis connection pool instead of per-request connections\n- Retry logic with exponential backoff for transient failures\n\n## Current State\n- 14 tests passing, 2 failing\n- Remaining: mock setup for session service tests\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Fix remaining test failures\n2. Run full test suite\n3. Update documentation\n```\n\nThis structure prevents silent loss of file paths or decisions because each section must be explicitly addressed.\n\n### Compression Trigger Strategies\n\nWhen to trigger compression matters as much as how to compress:\n\n| Strategy | Trigger Point | Trade-off |\n|----------|---------------|-----------|\n| Fixed threshold | 70-80% context utilization | Simple but may compress too early |\n| Sliding window | Keep last N turns + summary | Predictable context size |\n| Importance-based | Compress low-relevance sections first | Complex but preserves signal |\n| Task-boundary | Compress at logical task completions | Clean summaries but unpredictable timing |\n\nThe sliding window approach with structured summaries provides the best balance of predictability and quality for most coding agent use cases.\n\n### Probe-Based Evaluation\n\nTraditional metrics like ROUGE or embedding similarity fail to capture functional compression quality. A summary may score high on lexical overlap while missing the one file path the agent needs.\n\nProbe-based evaluation directly measures functional quality by asking questions after compression:\n\n| Probe Type | What It Tests | Example Question |\n|------------|---------------|------------------|\n| Recall | Factual retention | \"What was the original error message?\" |\n| Artifact | File tracking | \"Which files have we modified?\" |\n| Continuation | Task planning | \"What should we do next?\" |\n| Decision | Reasoning chain | \"What did we decide about the Redis issue?\" |\n\nIf compression preserved the right information, the agent answers correctly. If not, it guesses or hallucinates.\n\n### Evaluation Dimensions\n\nSix dimensions capture compression quality for coding agents:\n\n1. **Accuracy**: Are technical details correct? File paths, function names, error codes.\n2. **Context Awareness**: Does the response reflect current conversation state?\n3. **Artifact Trail**: Does the agent know which files were read or modified?\n4. **Completeness**: Does the response address all parts of the question?\n5. **Continuity**: Can work continue without re-fetching information?\n6. **Instruction Following**: Does the response respect stated constraints?\n\nAccuracy shows the largest variation between compression methods (0.6 point gap). Artifact trail is universally weak (2.2-2.5 range).\n\n## Practical Guidance\n\n### Three-Phase Compression Workflow\n\nFor large codebases or agent systems exceeding context windows, apply compression through three phases:\n\n1. **Research Phase**: Produce a research document from architecture diagrams, documentation, and key interfaces. Compress exploration into a structured analysis of components and dependencies. Output: single research document.\n\n2. **Planning Phase**: Convert research into implementation specification with function signatures, type definitions, and data flow. A 5M token codebase compresses to approximately 2,000 words of specification.\n\n3. **Implementation Phase**: Execute against the specification. Context remains focused on the spec rather than raw codebase exploration.\n\n### Using Example Artifacts as Seeds\n\nWhen provided with a manual migration example or reference PR, use it as a template to understand the target pattern. The example reveals constraints that static analysis cannot surface: which invariants must hold, which services break on changes, and what a clean migration looks like.\n\nThis is particularly important when the agent cannot distinguish essential complexity (business requirements) from accidental complexity (legacy workarounds). The example artifact encodes that distinction.\n\n### Implementing Anchored Iterative Summarization\n\n1. Define explicit summary sections matching your agent''s needs\n2. On first compression trigger, summarize truncated history into sections\n3. On subsequent compressions, summarize only new truncated content\n4. Merge new summary into existing sections rather than regenerating\n5. Track which information came from which compression cycle for debugging\n\n### When to Use Each Approach\n\n**Use anchored iterative summarization when:**\n- Sessions are long-running (100+ messages)\n- File tracking matters (coding, debugging)\n- You need to verify what was preserved\n\n**Use opaque compression when:**\n- Maximum token savings required\n- Sessions are relatively short\n- Re-fetching costs are low\n\n**Use regenerative summaries when:**\n- Summary interpretability is critical\n- Sessions have clear phase boundaries\n- Full context review is acceptable on each compression\n\n### Compression Ratio Considerations\n\n| Method | Compression Ratio | Quality Score | Trade-off |\n|--------|-------------------|---------------|-----------|\n| Anchored Iterative | 98.6% | 3.70 | Best quality, slightly less compression |\n| Regenerative | 98.7% | 3.44 | Good quality, moderate compression |\n| Opaque | 99.3% | 3.35 | Best compression, quality loss |\n\nThe 0.7% additional tokens retained by structured summarization buys 0.35 quality points. For any task where re-fetching costs matter, this trade-off favors structured approaches.\n\n## Examples\n\n**Example 1: Debugging Session Compression**\n\nOriginal context (89,000 tokens, 178 messages):\n- 401 error on /api/auth/login endpoint\n- Traced through auth controller, middleware, session store\n- Found stale Redis connection\n- Fixed connection pooling, added retry logic\n- 14 tests passing, 2 failing\n\nStructured summary after compression:\n\n```markdown\n## Session Intent\nDebug 401 Unauthorized error on /api/auth/login despite valid credentials.\n\n## Root Cause\nStale Redis connection in session store. JWT generated correctly but session could not be persisted.\n\n## Files Modified\n- auth.controller.ts: No changes (read only)\n- middleware/cors.ts: No changes (examined)\n- config/redis.ts: Fixed connection pooling configuration\n- services/session.service.ts: Added retry logic for transient failures\n- tests/auth.test.ts: Updated mock setup\n\n## Test Status\n14 passing, 2 failing (mock setup issues)\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Fix remaining test failures (mock session service)\n2. Run full test suite\n3. Deploy to staging\n```\n\n**Example 2: Probe Response Quality**\n\nAfter compression, asking \"What was the original error?\":\n\nGood response (structured summarization):\n> \"The original error was a 401 Unauthorized response from the /api/auth/login endpoint. Users received this error with valid credentials. Root cause was stale Redis connection in session store.\"\n\nPoor response (aggressive compression):\n> \"We were debugging an authentication issue. The login was failing. We fixed some configuration problems.\"\n\nThe structured response preserves endpoint, error code, and root cause. The aggressive response loses all technical detail.\n\n## Guidelines\n\n1. Optimize for tokens-per-task, not tokens-per-request\n2. Use structured summaries with explicit sections for file tracking\n3. Trigger compression at 70-80% context utilization\n4. Implement incremental merging rather than full regeneration\n5. Test compression quality with probe-based evaluation\n6. Track artifact trail separately if file tracking is critical\n7. Accept slightly lower compression ratios for better quality retention\n8. Monitor re-fetching frequency as a compression quality signal\n\n## Integration\n\nThis skill connects to several others in the collection:\n\n- context-degradation - Compression is a mitigation strategy for degradation\n- context-optimization - Compression is one optimization technique among many\n- evaluation - Probe-based evaluation applies to compression testing\n- memory-systems - Compression relates to scratchpad and summary memory patterns\n\n## References\n\nInternal reference:\n- [Evaluation Framework Reference](./references/evaluation-framework.md) - Detailed probe types and scoring rubrics\n\nRelated skills in this collection:\n- context-degradation - Understanding what compression prevents\n- context-optimization - Broader optimization strategies\n- evaluation - Building evaluation frameworks\n\nExternal resources:\n- Factory Research: Evaluating Context Compression for AI Agents (December 2025)\n- Research on LLM-as-judge evaluation methodology (Zheng et al., 2023)\n- Netflix Engineering: \"The Infinite Software Crisis\" - Three-phase workflow and context compression at scale (AI Summit 2025)\n\n---\n\n## Skill Metadata\n\n**Created**: 2025-12-22\n**Last Updated**: 2025-12-26\n**Author**: Agent Skills for Context Engineering Contributors\n**Version**: 1.1.0\n\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:10:02.785Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Advanced AI Agents needing efficient conversation history management through context-compression strategies.","zh":"非常适合需要高效对话历史管理的高级 AI 代理，通过上下文压缩策略实现。","ja":"高度の会話履歴管理が必要な高度な AI エージェントに適しています。コンテキスト圧縮戦略を通じて効率を高めます。","ko":"효율적인 대화 기록 관리가 필요한 고급 AI 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 문맥 압축 전략을 통해 효율성을 높입니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA avanzados que necesitan una gestión eficiente del historial de conversación a través de estrategias de compresión de contexto.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''IA avancés ayant besoin d''une gestion efficace de l''historique de conversation grâce à des stratégies de compression de contexte.","de":"Perfekt für erweiterte KI-Agents, die eine effiziente Konversationshistorienverwaltung durch Kontextkomprimierungsstrategien benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA Avançados que necessitam de gerenciamento eficiente do histórico de conversas por meio de estratégias de compressão de contexto.","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых агентов ИИ, которым требуется эффективное управление историей разговора посредством стратегий сжатия контекста.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المتقدم الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة فعالة لتاريخ المحادثة من خلال استراتيجيات الضغط السياقي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to optimize tokens per task, including re-fetching costs when compression loses critical information, utilizing modular skills definitions for systematic problem-solving in fields like full-stack development and complex logic planning.","zh":"赋予代理优化每项任务的令牌数量的能力，包括在压缩丢失关键信息时重新获取成本，利用模块化技能定义进行系统化问题解决，如全栈开发和复杂逻辑规划等领域。","ja":"エージェントにタスクごとのトークン数を最適化する能力を与え、圧縮によって重要な情報が失われた場合の再取得コストを含むことができます。モジュラーなスキル定義を使用して、フルスタック開発や複雑なロジック計画などの分野で体系的な問題解決を行うことができます。","ko":"에이전트에게 각 작업의 토큰 수를 최적화하는 능력을 부여하며, 압축으로 인해 중요한 정보가 손실된 경우 다시 가져오는 비용을 포함하여, 모듈러한 기술 정의를 사용하여 풀스택 개발이나 복잡한 논리 계획 등의 분야에서 체계적인 문제 해결을 할 수 있습니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes optimizar los tokens por tarea, incluyendo los costos de reobtención cuando la compresión pierde información crítica, utilizando definiciones de habilidades modulares para la resolución sistemática de problemas en campos como el desarrollo full-stack y la planificación de lógica compleja.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''optimiser les jetons par tâche, y compris les coûts de ré-obtention lorsque la compression perd des informations critiques, en utilisant des définitions de compétences modulaires pour la résolution systématique de problèmes dans des domaines tels que le développement full-stack et la planification de la logique complexe.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, Token pro Aufgabe zu optimieren, einschließlich der Kosten für die erneute Abrufung, wenn die Komprimierung kritische Informationen verliert, unter Verwendung modularer Fertigkeitsdefinitionen für die systematische Problemlösung in Bereichen wie Full-Stack-Entwicklung und komplexe Logikplanung.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a otimizar tokens por tarefa, incluindo custos de re-recuperação quando a compressão perde informações críticas, utilizando definições de habilidades modulares para resolução sistemática de problemas em campos como desenvolvimento full-stack e planejamento de lógica complexa.","ru":"Позволяет агентам оптимизировать токены на задачу, включая затраты на повторную выборку, когда сжатие теряет критическую информацию, используя модульные определения навыков для системного решения проблем в таких областях, как полнофункциональное веб-разработка и планирование сложной логики.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تحسين الرموز لكل مهمة، بما في ذلك التكاليف الناشئة عن إعادة استرداد المعلومات عند فقدان الضغط للمعلومات الحيوية، باستخدام تعريفات المهارات الموديولرية لحل المشكلات بشكل منهجي في مجالات مثل التطوير الكامل والتنظيم المنطقي المعقد."},"useCases":{"en":["Compressing large conversation histories to minimize tokens per request","Optimizing agent sessions to reduce context window limits","Implementing token compression to improve task completion efficiency"],"zh":["压缩大型对话历史以最小化每个请求的令牌数量","优化代理会话以减少上下文窗口限制","实现令牌压缩以提高任务完成效率"],"ja":["大きな会話履歴を圧縮して、各リクエストのトークン数を最小限に抑える","エージェントセッションを最適化してコンテキストウィンドウの制限を減らす","トークン圧縮を実装してタスク完了の効率を向上させる"],"ko":["대형 대화 기록을 압축하여 요청당 토큰 수를 최소화하는 것","에이전트 세션을 최적화하여 문맥 창 제한을 줄이는 것","토큰 압축을 구현하여 작업 완료 효율을 향상시키는 것"],"es":["Comprimir historiales de conversación grandes para minimizar los tokens por solicitud","Optimizar sesiones de agentes para reducir los límites de la ventana de contexto","Implementar la compresión de tokens para mejorar la eficiencia de finalización de tareas"],"fr":["Compresser les historiques de conversation importants pour minimiser les jetons par demande","Optimiser les sessions d''agents pour réduire les limites de la fenêtre de contexte","Mettre en œuvre la compression de jetons pour améliorer l''efficacité d''achèvement des tâches"],"de":["Große Konversationshistorien komprimieren, um die Token pro Anfrage zu minimieren","Agentensitzungen optimieren, um die Kontextfensterlimits zu reduzieren","Token-Komprimierung implementieren, um die Aufgabenerfüllungseffizienz zu verbessern"],"pt":["Comprimir históricos de conversas grandes para minimizar tokens por solicitação","Otimizar sessões de agente para reduzir os limites da janela de contexto","Implementar compressão de tokens para melhorar a eficiência de conclusão de tarefas"],"ru":["Сжатие больших историй разговоров для минимизации токенов на запрос","Оптимизация сессий агента для снижения пределов окна контекста","Реализация сжатия токенов для提高 эффективности выполнения задач"],"ar":["ضغط تاريخ المحادثات الكبيرة لتقليل الرموز لكل طلب","تحسين جلسات الوكيل لتقليل حدود نافذة السياق","تنفيذ ضغط الرموز لتحسين كفاءة إكمال المهام"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires agent sessions to exceed context window limits","Codebases need to exceed context limits for optimal usage","May lose critical information if aggressive compression is applied"],"zh":["需要代理会话超过上下文窗口限制","代码库需要超过上下文限制以获得最佳使用效果","如果采用激进的压缩，可能会丢失关键信息"],"ja":["エージェントセッションがコンテキストウィンドウの制限を超える必要がある","コードベースがコンテキストの制限を超える必要があるため、最適な使用が可能になる","激しい圧縮を適用した場合、重要な情報が失われる可能性がある"],"ko":["에이전트 세션이 문맥 창 제한을 초과해야 함","코드베이스가 문맥 제한을 초과해야 최적의 사용이 가능함","攻击적인 압축을 적용하면 중요한 정보가 손실될 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere que las sesiones del agente superen los límites de la ventana de contexto","Los codebases necesitan superar los límites de contexto para un uso óptimo","Puede perder información crítica si se aplica una compresión agresiva"],"fr":["Nécessite que les sessions d''agent dépassent les limites de la fenêtre de contexte","Les codebases doivent dépasser les limites de contexte pour une utilisation optimale","Peut perdre des informations critiques si une compression agressive est appliquée"],"de":["Benötigt, dass die Agentensitzungen die Kontextfensterlimits überschreiten","Codebases müssen die Kontextlimits überschreiten, um eine optimale Nutzung zu gewährleisten","Kann kritische Informationen verlieren, wenn eine aggressive Komprimierung angewendet wird"],"pt":["Requer que as sessões do agente excedam os limites da janela de contexto","As bases de código precisam exceder os limites de contexto para uso ótimo","Pode perder informações críticas se a compressão agressiva for aplicada"],"ru":["Требует, чтобы сессии агента превышали пределы окна контекста","Кодовые базы должны превышать пределы контекста для оптимального использования","Может потерять критическую информацию, если применяется агрессивное сжатие"],"ar":["يتطلب أن تتجاوز جلسات الوكيل حدود نافذة السياق","تحتاج قواعد البيانات إلى تجاوز حدود السياق للاستخدام الأمثل","قد تفقد المعلومات الحيوية إذا تم تطبيق ضغط قوي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/seo-audit', 'community', 'majiayu000', 'claude-skill-registry', 'majiayu000/claude-skill-registry', 'seo-audit', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.417Z', '2026-02-18T04:09:52.982Z', NULL, '{"id":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/seo-audit","name":"seo-audit","description":{"zh":"SEO 审计是为了识别网站的 SEO 问题，并提供可行的优化建议，以提高搜索引擎性能","ja":"SEO オーディットは、ウェブサイトの SEO 問題を特定し、検索エンジン性能を向上させるための実行可能な最適化提案を提供する","ko":"SEO 감사는 웹사이트의 SEO 문제를 식별하고, 검색 엔진 성능을 향상시키기 위한 실행 가능한 최적화 제안을 제공하는 것을 목표로 합니다","es":"El análisis de SEO identifica problemas y proporciona recomendaciones para mejorar el rendimiento de búsqueda orgánica","fr":"L''audit SEO identifie les problèmes et fournit des recommandations pour améliorer les performances de recherche organique","de":"Das SEO-Audit identifiziert Probleme und liefert Empfehlungen zur Verbesserung der organischen Suchleistung","pt":"A análise de SEO é um processo que identifica problemas de otimização de busca e fornece recomendações para melhorar o desempenho de busca orgânica.","ru":"Аудит SEO - это процесс, который выявляет проблемы с оптимизацией поиска и предоставляет рекомендации для улучшения производительности поиска.","ar":"فحص تحسين محركات البحث هو عملية تحدد مشاكل تحسين بحث و توفر توصيات لتحسين أداء البحث العضوي.","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"SEO 审计：优化搜索引擎性能","ja":"SEO オーディット：検索エンジン性能の最適化","ko":"SEO 감사: 검색 엔진 성능 최적화","es":"Análisis de SEO: mejora el rendimiento de búsqueda","fr":"Audit SEO: améliorez les performances de recherche","de":"SEO-Audit: Verbesserung der Suchleistung","pt":"Análise de SEO: Otimização de Desempenho de Busca","ru":"Аудит SEO: Оптимизация Производительности Поиска","ar":"فحص تحسين محركات البحث: تحسين أداء البحث","en":"seo-audit"},"description":{"zh":"SEO 审计是为了识别网站的 SEO 问题，并提供可行的优化建议，以提高搜索引擎性能","ja":"SEO オーディットは、ウェブサイトの SEO 問題を特定し、検索エンジン性能を向上させるための実行可能な最適化提案を提供する","ko":"SEO 감사는 웹사이트의 SEO 문제를 식별하고, 검색 엔진 성능을 향상시키기 위한 실행 가능한 최적화 제안을 제공하는 것을 목표로 합니다","es":"El análisis de SEO identifica problemas y proporciona recomendaciones para mejorar el rendimiento de búsqueda orgánica","fr":"L''audit SEO identifie les problèmes et fournit des recommandations pour améliorer les performances de recherche organique","de":"Das SEO-Audit identifiziert Probleme und liefert Empfehlungen zur Verbesserung der organischen Suchleistung","pt":"A análise de SEO é um processo que identifica problemas de otimização de busca e fornece recomendações para melhorar o desempenho de busca orgânica.","ru":"Аудит SEO - это процесс, который выявляет проблемы с оптимизацией поиска и предоставляет рекомендации для улучшения производительности поиска.","ar":"فحص تحسين محركات البحث هو عملية تحدد مشاكل تحسين بحث و توفر توصيات لتحسين أداء البحث العضوي.","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"zh":["识别 SEO 问题","提供可行的优化建议","提高搜索引擎排名","提高网站性能","专业的 SEO 审计报告"],"ja":["SEO 問題の特定","実行可能な最適化提案の提供","検索エンジンランキングの向上","ウェブサイトパフォーマンスの向上","専門的な SEO オーディットレポート"],"ko":["SEO 문제 식별","실행 가능한 최적화 제안 제공","검색 엔진 순위 향상","웹사이트 성능 향상","전문적인 SEO 감사 보고서"],"es":["Identificación de problemas de SEO","Análisis de contexto de sitio web","Recomendaciones para mejorar el rendimiento de búsqueda","Análisis de marketing de producto","Optimización de contenido","Mejora de la experiencia del usuario"],"fr":["Identification des problèmes de SEO","Analyse du contexte du site web","Recommandations pour améliorer les performances de recherche","Analyse de marketing de produit","Optimisation du contenu","Amélioration de l''expérience utilisateur"],"de":["Identifizierung von SEO-Problemen","Analyse des Kontexts der Website","Empfehlungen zur Verbesserung der Suchleistung","Analyse des Produktmarketings","Optimierung des Inhalts","Verbesserung der Benutzererfahrung"],"pt":["Identificação de problemas de SEO","Análise de desempenho de busca","Recomendações para melhorar o desempenho","Otimização de conteúdo","Análise de links"],"ru":["Выявление проблем с SEO","Анализ производительности поиска","Рекомендации для улучшения производительности","Оптимизация контента","Анализ ссылок"],"ar":["تحديد مشاكل تحسين محركات البحث","تحليل أداء البحث","توصيات لتحسين الأداء","تحسين المحتوى","تحليل الروابط"]},"keywords":{"zh":["SEO 审计","搜索引擎优化","网站优化","搜索引擎排名","网站性能","SEO 问题","优化建议","专业 SEO 审计"],"ja":["SEO オーディット","検索エンジン最適化","ウェブサイト最適化","検索エンジンランキング","ウェブサイトパフォーマンス","SEO 問題","最適化提案","専門的な SEO オーディット"],"ko":["SEO 감사","검색 엔진 최적화","웹사이트 최적화","검색 엔진 순위","웹사이트 성능","SEO 문제","최적화 제안","전문적인 SEO 감사"],"es":["análisis de SEO","optimización de búsqueda","mejora del rendimiento de búsqueda","marketing de producto","optimización de contenido","experiencia del usuario","SEO técnico","audit de SEO"],"fr":["audit SEO","optimisation de recherche","amélioration des performances de recherche","marketing de produit","optimisation du contenu","expérience utilisateur","SEO technique","analyse de SEO"],"de":["SEO-Audit","Suchmaschinenoptimierung","Verbesserung der Suchleistung","Produktmarketing","Inhaltsoptimierung","Benutzererfahrung","technisches SEO","SEO-Analyse"],"pt":["análise de SEO","otimização de busca","desempenho de busca orgânica","recomendações de SEO","análise de links","otimização de conteúdo"],"ru":["аудит SEO","оптимизация поиска","производительность поиска","рекомендации SEO","анализ ссылок","оптимизация контента"],"ar":["فحص تحسين محركات البحث","تحسين بحث","أداء البحث العضوي","توصيات تحسين محركات البحث","تحليل الروابط","تحسين المحتوى"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.417Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"seo-audit","description":"When the user wants to audit, review, or diagnose SEO issues on their site. Also use when the user mentions SEO audit, technical SEO, why am I not ranking, SEO issues, on-page SEO, meta tags review, or SEO health check. For building pages at scale to target keywords, see programmatic-seo. For adding structured data, see schema-markup.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# SEO Audit\n\nYou are an expert in search engine optimization. Your goal is to identify SEO issues and provide actionable recommendations to improve organic search performance.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore auditing, understand:\n\n1. **Site Context**\n   - What type of site? (Sa","body":"# SEO Audit\n\nYou are an expert in search engine optimization. Your goal is to identify SEO issues and provide actionable recommendations to improve organic search performance.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore auditing, understand:\n\n1. **Site Context**\n   - What type of site? (SaaS, e-commerce, blog, etc.)\n   - What''s the primary business goal for SEO?\n   - What keywords/topics are priorities?\n\n2. **Current State**\n   - Any known issues or concerns?\n   - Current organic traffic level?\n   - Recent changes or migrations?\n\n3. **Scope**\n   - Full site audit or specific pages?\n   - Technical + on-page, or one focus area?\n   - Access to Search Console / analytics?\n\n---\n\n## Audit Framework\n\n### Priority Order\n1. **Crawlability & Indexation** (can Google find and index it?)\n2. **Technical Foundations** (is the site fast and functional?)\n3. **On-Page Optimization** (is content optimized?)\n4. **Content Quality** (does it deserve to rank?)\n5. **Authority & Links** (does it have credibility?)\n\n---\n\n## Technical SEO Audit\n\n### Crawlability\n\n**Robots.txt**\n- Check for unintentional blocks\n- Verify important pages allowed\n- Check sitemap reference\n\n**XML Sitemap**\n- Exists and accessible\n- Submitted to Search Console\n- Contains only canonical, indexable URLs\n- Updated regularly\n- Proper formatting\n\n**Site Architecture**\n- Important pages within 3 clicks of homepage\n- Logical hierarchy\n- Internal linking structure\n- No orphan pages\n\n**Crawl Budget Issues** (for large sites)\n- Parameterized URLs under control\n- Faceted navigation handled properly\n- Infinite scroll with pagination fallback\n- Session IDs not in URLs\n\n### Indexation\n\n**Index Status**\n- site:domain.com check\n- Search Console coverage report\n- Compare indexed vs. expected\n\n**Indexation Issues**\n- Noindex tags on important pages\n- Canonicals pointing wrong direction\n- Redirect chains/loops\n- Soft 404s\n- Duplicate content without canonicals\n\n**Canonicalization**\n- All pages have canonical tags\n- Self-referencing canonicals on unique pages\n- HTTP → HTTPS canonicals\n- www vs. non-www consistency\n- Trailing slash consistency\n\n### Site Speed & Core Web Vitals\n\n**Core Web Vitals**\n- LCP (Largest Contentful Paint): < 2.5s\n- INP (Interaction to Next Paint): < 200ms\n- CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift): < 0.1\n\n**Speed Factors**\n- Server response time (TTFB)\n- Image optimization\n- JavaScript execution\n- CSS delivery\n- Caching headers\n- CDN usage\n- Font loading\n\n**Tools**\n- PageSpeed Insights\n- WebPageTest\n- Chrome DevTools\n- Search Console Core Web Vitals report\n\n### Mobile-Friendliness\n\n- Responsive design (not separate m. site)\n- Tap target sizes\n- Viewport configured\n- No horizontal scroll\n- Same content as desktop\n- Mobile-first indexing readiness\n\n### Security & HTTPS\n\n- HTTPS across entire site\n- Valid SSL certificate\n- No mixed content\n- HTTP → HTTPS redirects\n- HSTS header (bonus)\n\n### URL Structure\n\n- Readable, descriptive URLs\n- Keywords in URLs where natural\n- Consistent structure\n- No unnecessary parameters\n- Lowercase and hyphen-separated\n\n---\n\n## On-Page SEO Audit\n\n### Title Tags\n\n**Check for:**\n- Unique titles for each page\n- Primary keyword near beginning\n- 50-60 characters (visible in SERP)\n- Compelling and click-worthy\n- Brand name placement (end, usually)\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Duplicate titles\n- Too long (truncated)\n- Too short (wasted opportunity)\n- Keyword stuffing\n- Missing entirely\n\n### Meta Descriptions\n\n**Check for:**\n- Unique descriptions per page\n- 150-160 characters\n- Includes primary keyword\n- Clear value proposition\n- Call to action\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Duplicate descriptions\n- Auto-generated garbage\n- Too long/short\n- No compelling reason to click\n\n### Heading Structure\n\n**Check for:**\n- One H1 per page\n- H1 contains primary keyword\n- Logical hierarchy (H1 → H2 → H3)\n- Headings describe content\n- Not just for styling\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Multiple H1s\n- Skip levels (H1 → H3)\n- Headings used for styling only\n- No H1 on page\n\n### Content Optimization\n\n**Primary Page Content**\n- Keyword in first 100 words\n- Related keywords naturally used\n- Sufficient depth/length for topic\n- Answers search intent\n- Better than competitors\n\n**Thin Content Issues**\n- Pages with little unique content\n- Tag/category pages with no value\n- Doorway pages\n- Duplicate or near-duplicate content\n\n### Image Optimization\n\n**Check for:**\n- Descriptive file names\n- Alt text on all images\n- Alt text describes image\n- Compressed file sizes\n- Modern formats (WebP)\n- Lazy loading implemented\n- Responsive images\n\n### Internal Linking\n\n**Check for:**\n- Important pages well-linked\n- Descriptive anchor text\n- Logical link relationships\n- No broken internal links\n- Reasonable link count per page\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Orphan pages (no internal links)\n- Over-optimized anchor text\n- Important pages buried\n- Excessive footer/sidebar links\n\n### Keyword Targeting\n\n**Per Page**\n- Clear primary keyword target\n- Title, H1, URL aligned\n- Content satisfies search intent\n- Not competing with other pages (cannibalization)\n\n**Site-Wide**\n- Keyword mapping document\n- No major gaps in coverage\n- No keyword cannibalization\n- Logical topical clusters\n\n---\n\n## Content Quality Assessment\n\n### E-E-A-T Signals\n\n**Experience**\n- First-hand experience demonstrated\n- Original insights/data\n- Real examples and case studies\n\n**Expertise**\n- Author credentials visible\n- Accurate, detailed information\n- Properly sourced claims\n\n**Authoritativeness**\n- Recognized in the space\n- Cited by others\n- Industry credentials\n\n**Trustworthiness**\n- Accurate information\n- Transparent about business\n- Contact information available\n- Privacy policy, terms\n- Secure site (HTTPS)\n\n### Content Depth\n\n- Comprehensive coverage of topic\n- Answers follow-up questions\n- Better than top-ranking competitors\n- Updated and current\n\n### User Engagement Signals\n\n- Time on page\n- Bounce rate in context\n- Pages per session\n- Return visits\n\n---\n\n## Common Issues by Site Type\n\n### SaaS/Product Sites\n- Product pages lack content depth\n- Blog not integrated with product pages\n- Missing comparison/alternative pages\n- Feature pages thin on content\n- No glossary/educational content\n\n### E-commerce\n- Thin category pages\n- Duplicate product descriptions\n- Missing product schema\n- Faceted navigation creating duplicates\n- Out-of-stock pages mishandled\n\n### Content/Blog Sites\n- Outdated content not refreshed\n- Keyword cannibalization\n- No topical clustering\n- Poor internal linking\n- Missing author pages\n\n### Local Business\n- Inconsistent NAP\n- Missing local schema\n- No Google Business Profile optimization\n- Missing location pages\n- No local content\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\n### Audit Report Structure\n\n**Executive Summary**\n- Overall health assessment\n- Top 3-5 priority issues\n- Quick wins identified\n\n**Technical SEO Findings**\nFor each issue:\n- **Issue**: What''s wrong\n- **Impact**: SEO impact (High/Medium/Low)\n- **Evidence**: How you found it\n- **Fix**: Specific recommendation\n- **Priority**: 1-5 or High/Medium/Low\n\n**On-Page SEO Findings**\nSame format as above\n\n**Content Findings**\nSame format as above\n\n**Prioritized Action Plan**\n1. Critical fixes (blocking indexation/ranking)\n2. High-impact improvements\n3. Quick wins (easy, immediate benefit)\n4. Long-term recommendations\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n- [AI Writing Detection](references/ai-writing-detection.md): Common AI writing patterns to avoid (em dashes, overused phrases, filler words)\n- [AEO & GEO Patterns](references/aeo-geo-patterns.md): Content patterns optimized for answer engines and AI citation\n\n---\n\n## Tools Referenced\n\n**Free Tools**\n- Google Search Console (essential)\n- Google PageSpeed Insights\n- Bing Webmaster Tools\n- Rich Results Test\n- Mobile-Friendly Test\n- Schema Validator\n\n**Paid Tools** (if available)\n- Screaming Frog\n- Ahrefs / Semrush\n- Sitebulb\n- ContentKing\n\n---\n\n## Task-Specific Questions\n\n1. What pages/keywords matter most?\n2. Do you have Search Console access?\n3. Any recent changes or migrations?\n4. Who are your top organic competitors?\n5. What''s your current organic traffic baseline?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **programmatic-seo**: For building SEO pages at scale\n- **schema-markup**: For implementing structured data\n- **page-cro**: For optimizing pages for conversion (not just ranking)\n- **analytics-tracking**: For measuring SEO performance\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:09:52.982Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Digital Marketing Agents needing advanced SEO analysis and optimization capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级SEO分析和优化能力的数字营销代理。","ja":"デジタルマーケティングエージェントが高度なSEO分析および最適化機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 SEO 분석 및 최적화 기능이 필요한 디지털 마케팅 에이전트에게 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de marketing digital que necesitan un análisis y capacidades de optimización de SEO avanzadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de marketing numérique ayant besoin d''une analyse et de capacités d''optimisation de SEO avancées.","de":"Perfekt für digitale Marketing-Agenten, die erweiterte SEO-Analyse- und Optimierungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Marketing Digital que precisam de análise e capacidades de otimização de SEO avançadas.","ru":"Идеально для цифровых маркетинговых агентов, которым требуются продвинутые возможности анализа и оптимизации SEO.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء التسويقيين الرقميين الذين يحتاجون إلى تحليل متقدم وقدرات تحسين SEO."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to identify SEO issues and provide actionable recommendations to improve organic search performance, leveraging product marketing context and site-specific analysis through files like `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`.","zh":"使代理能够识别SEO问题，并提供可执行的建议以提高有机搜索性能，利用产品营销背景和通过文件（如`.claude/product-marketing-context.md`）的站点特定分析。","ja":"エージェントがSEOの問題を特定し、有機検索のパフォーマンスを改善するための実行可能な推奨事項を提供できるようにし、`.claude/product-marketing-context.md`などのファイルを介した製品マーケティングのコンテキストとサイト固有の分析を利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 SEO 문제를 식별하고 유기적 검색 성능을 개선하기 위한 실행 가능한 권장 사항을 제공할 수 있도록 하며, `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`와 같은 파일을 통해 제품 마케팅 컨텍스트 및 사이트 특정 분석을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a identificar problemas de SEO y proporcionar recomendaciones con acciones para mejorar el rendimiento de la búsqueda orgánica, utilizando el contexto de marketing de productos y el análisis específico del sitio a través de archivos como `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''identifier les problèmes de SEO et de fournir des recommandations avec des actions pour améliorer les performances de recherche organique, en exploitant le contexte de marketing de produits et l''analyse spécifique au site via des fichiers tels que `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, SEO-Probleme zu identifizieren und handhabbare Empfehlungen zur Verbesserung der organischen Suchleistung zu geben, indem sie den Produktmarketing-Kontext und die standortspezifische Analyse über Dateien wie `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a identificar problemas de SEO e fornecer recomendações práticas para melhorar o desempenho de busca orgânica, utilizando o contexto de marketing de produtos e análise específica do site por meio de arquivos como `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выявлять проблемы SEO и предоставлять действенные рекомендации для улучшения результатов органической поисковой системы, используя контекст маркетинга продукта и анализ конкретного сайта через файлы типа `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تحديد مشاكل SEO وتقديم توصيات قابلة للتنفيذ لتحسين أداء البحث العضوي، مستخدمين سياق تسويق المنتج والتحليل المحدد للموقع من خلال ملفات مثل `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`."},"useCases":{"en":["Analyzing site context for optimization","Generating actionable SEO reports","Identifying organic search performance issues"],"zh":["优化的站点背景分析","生成可执行的SEO报告","识别有机搜索性能问题"],"ja":["最適化のサイトコンテキスト分析","実行可能なSEOレポートの生成","有機検索パフォーマンスの問題の特定"],"ko":["최적화 사이트 컨텍스트 분석","실행 가능한 SEO 보고서 생성","유기적 검색 성능 문제 식별"],"es":["Análisis del contexto del sitio para la optimización","Generación de informes de SEO con acciones","Identificación de problemas de rendimiento de búsqueda orgánica"],"fr":["Analyse du contexte du site pour l''optimisation","Génération de rapports SEO avec des actions","Identification des problèmes de performances de recherche organique"],"de":["Analyse des Standortkontexts für die Optimierung","Erzeugung von SEO-Berichten mit Handlungen","Identifizierung von Problemen mit der organischen Suchleistung"],"pt":["Analisar o contexto do site para otimização","Gerar relatórios de SEO práticos","Identificar problemas de desempenho de busca orgânica"],"ru":["Анализ контекста сайта для оптимизации","Генерация практических отчетов SEO","Выявление проблем результатов органической поисковой системы"],"ar":["تحليل سياق الموقع لتحسين الأداء","توليد تقارير SEO قابلة للتنفيذ","تحديد مشاكل أداء البحث العضوي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to site context information","Needs product marketing context file for optimal analysis"],"zh":["需要访问站点背景信息","需要产品营销背景文件以实现最佳分析"],"ja":["サイトコンテキスト情報へのアクセスが必要","最適な分析を行うには製品マーケティングコンテキストファイルが必要"],"ko":["사이트 컨텍스트 정보에 액세스해야 함","최적의 분석을 수행하려면 제품 마케팅 컨텍스트 파일이 필요함"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la información del contexto del sitio","Necesita un archivo de contexto de marketing de productos para un análisis óptimo"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à l''information du contexte du site","A besoin d''un fichier de contexte de marketing de produits pour une analyse optimale"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Standortkontext-Informationen","Benötigt eine Datei mit Produktmarketing-Kontext für eine optimale Analyse"],"pt":["Requer acesso às informações de contexto do site","Necessita de arquivo de contexto de marketing de produtos para análise ótima"],"ru":["Требует доступа к информации контекста сайта","Нуждается в файле контекста маркетинга продукта для оптимального анализа"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى معلومات سياق الموقع","يحتاج إلى ملف سياق تسويق المنتج لتحليل مثالي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
