markdown","GitHub-flavored markdown: Auszeichnungssprache für Dokumentation","Tutorials: Anleitungen für Anfänger","Dokumentation organisiert: Klar strukturiert und leicht verständlich"],"pt":["Organização de documentação com o framework Diátaxis","Uso de GitHub-flavored markdown","Renderização com Astro Starlight","Tutoriais para iniciantes","Explicação e referência detalhadas","Suporte à documentação sistemática"],"ru":["Организация документации с помощью фреймворка Diátaxis","Использование GitHub-flavored markdown","Рендеринг с Astro Starlight","Учебные пособия для начинающих","Подробное объяснение и справка","Поддержка систематической документации"],"ar":["تنظيم التوثيق باستخدام إطار Diátaxis","استخدام GitHub-flavored markdown","ترميز Astro Starlight","دروس للمبتدئين","شرح ومرجع مفصل","دعم التوثيق المنهجي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["项目文档","Diátaxis框架","文档组织","教程","如何","参考","解释","GitHub风格的Markdown","Astro Starlight"],"ja":["プロジェクトドキュメント","Diátaxisフレームワーク","ドキュメント整理","チュートリアル","ハウツー","リファレンス","解説","GitHub風のMarkdown","Astro Starlight"],"ko":["프로젝트 문서","Diátaxis 프레임워크","문서 구성","튜토리얼","방법","참조","설명","GitHub 스타일의 Markdown","Astro Starlight"],"es":["documentación técnica","Diátaxis","Astro Starlight","GitHub-flavored markdown","desarrollo de software","guías para desarrolladores","tutoriales para principiantes"],"fr":["documentation technique","Diátaxis","Astro Starlight","GitHub-flavored markdown","développement de logiciels","guides pour développeurs","tutoriels pour débutants"],"de":["technische Dokumentation","Diátaxis","Astro Starlight","GitHub-flavored markdown","Software-Entwicklung","Anleitungen für Entwickler","Tutorials für Anfänger"],"pt":["documentação de projeto","diátaxis","astro starlight","github flavored markdown","tutoriais para desenvolvedores","explicação técnica","referência de projeto","desenvolvimento de software","organização de documentação"],"ru":["документация проекта","диатаксис","астро старлайт","гитхаб флейворд маркдаун","учебные пособия для разработчиков","техническое объяснение","справка по проекту","разработка программного обеспечения","организация документации"],"ar":["توثيق المشروع","دياتاكسيس","أسترو ستارلايت","جيثب فلavored ماركداون","دروس للمطورين","شرح تقني","مرجع المشروع","تطوير البرمجيات","تنظيم التوثيق"]}},"owner":"maxfraieho","repo":"garden-seedling","repoPath":"maxfraieho/garden-seedling","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.417Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"documentation","description":"Documentation Brief description for SEO and navigation","bodyPreview":"### Documentation\n\nThe documentation for this project is available in the `docs/` directory. It uses GitHub-flavored markdown with Astro Starlight for rendering and follows the Diátaxis framework for systematic documentation.\n\n## Diátaxis Framework\n\nDocumentation must be organized into four distinct types, each serving a specific purpose:\n\n### 1. Tutorials (Learning-Oriented)\n**Purpose**: Guide beginners through achieving a specific outcome to build confidence.\n\n- Start with what the user will b","body":"### Documentation\n\nThe documentation for this project is available in the `docs/` directory. It uses GitHub-flavored markdown with Astro Starlight for rendering and follows the Diátaxis framework for systematic documentation.\n\n## Diátaxis Framework\n\nDocumentation must be organized into four distinct types, each serving a specific purpose:\n\n### 1. Tutorials (Learning-Oriented)\n**Purpose**: Guide beginners through achieving a specific outcome to build confidence.\n\n- Start with what the user will build or achieve\n- Provide a clear, step-by-step path from start to finish\n- Include concrete examples and working code\n- Assume minimal prior knowledge\n- Focus on the happy path (avoid edge cases and alternatives)\n- End with a working result the user can see and use\n- Use imperative mood: \"Create a file\", \"Run the command\"\n\n**Avoid**: Explaining concepts in depth, multiple options, troubleshooting\n\n### 2. How-to Guides (Goal-Oriented)\n**Purpose**: Show how to solve a specific real-world problem or accomplish a particular task.\n\n- Title format: \"How to [accomplish specific goal]\"\n- Assume the user knows the basics\n- Focus on practical steps to solve one problem\n- Include necessary context but stay focused\n- Show multiple approaches only when genuinely useful\n- End when the goal is achieved\n- Use imperative mood: \"Configure the setting\", \"Add the following\"\n\n**Avoid**: Teaching fundamentals, explaining every detail, being exhaustive\n\n### 3. Reference (Information-Oriented)\n**Purpose**: Provide accurate, complete technical descriptions of the system.\n\n- Organized by structure (CLI commands, configuration options, API endpoints)\n- Comprehensive and authoritative\n- Consistent format across all entries\n- Technical accuracy is paramount\n- Include all parameters, options, and return values\n- Use descriptive mood: \"The command accepts\", \"Returns a string\"\n- Minimal narrative or explanation\n\n**Avoid**: Instructions, tutorials, opinions on usage\n\n### 4. Explanation (Understanding-Oriented)\n**Purpose**: Clarify and illuminate topics to deepen understanding.\n\n- Discuss why things are the way they are\n- Explain design decisions and tradeoffs\n- Provide context and background\n- Connect concepts to help form mental models\n- Discuss alternatives and their implications\n- Use indicative mood: \"This approach provides\", \"The engine uses\"\n\n**Avoid**: Step-by-step instructions, exhaustive reference material\n\n## General Style Guidelines\n\n- **Tone**: Neutral, technical, not promotional\n- **Voice**: Avoid \"we\", \"our\", \"us\" (use \"the tool\", \"this command\")\n- **Headings**: Use markdown heading syntax, not bold text as headings\n- **Lists**: Avoid long bullet point lists; prefer prose with structure\n- **Code samples**: Minimal and focused; exclude optional fields unless relevant\n- **Language tag**: Use `aw` for agentic workflow snippets with YAML frontmatter\n\n**Example workflow code block**:\n```aw wrap\non: push\n# Your workflow steps here\n```\n\n## GitHub-Flavored Markdown Syntax\n\nDocumentation files use GitHub-flavored markdown with Astro Starlight for rendering. Key syntax elements:\n\n### Frontmatter\nEvery documentation page must have frontmatter:\n```markdown\ntitle: Page Title\ndescription: Brief description for SEO and navigation\n```\n\n### GitHub Alerts\nUse GitHub''s alert syntax for notes, tips, warnings, and cautions:\n```markdown\n> [!NOTE]\n> Important information the reader should notice.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Helpful advice for the reader.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Warning about potential issues or pitfalls.\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Critical warning about dangerous operations.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Key information users need to know.\n```\n\n### Code Blocks\n- Use syntax highlighting with language tags\n- Add `title` attribute for file names: ` ```yaml title=\".github/workflows/example.yml\" `\n- Use `aw` language for agentic workflow files with YAML frontmatter\n- Add `wrap` for line wrapping: ` ```aw wrap `\n\n### Links\n- Internal links: Use relative paths between documentation pages\n- External links: Open in new tab automatically\n- Link text: Use descriptive text, avoid \"click here\"\n\n### Tabs\nUse tabs for showing alternatives (e.g., different languages, platforms):\n```markdown\nimport { Tabs, TabItem } from ''@astrojs/starlight/components'';\n\n<Tabs>\n  <TabItem label=\"npm\">\n    ```bash\n    npm install package\n    ```\n  </TabItem>\n  <TabItem label=\"yarn\">\n    ```bash\n    yarn add package\n    ```\n  </TabItem>\n</Tabs>\n```\n\n### Cards\nUse cards for navigation or highlighting multiple options:\n```markdown\nimport { Card, CardGrid } from ''@astrojs/starlight/components'';\n\n<CardGrid>\n  <Card title=\"Getting Started\" icon=\"rocket\">\n    Quick introduction to the basics.\n  </Card>\n  <Card title=\"Advanced Usage\" icon=\"setting\">\n    Deep dive into advanced features.\n  </Card>\n</CardGrid>\n```\n\n**Remember**: Keep components minimal. Prefer standard markdown when possible.\n\n## Content to Avoid\n\n- \"Key Features\" sections\n- Marketing language or selling points\n- Excessive bullet points (prefer structured prose)\n- Overly verbose examples with all optional parameters\n- Mixing documentation types (e.g., tutorials that become reference)\n\n## Avoiding Documentation Bloat\n\nDocumentation bloat reduces clarity and makes content harder to navigate. Common types of bloat include:\n\n### Types of Documentation Bloat\n\n1. **Duplicate content**: Same information repeated in different sections\n2. **Excessive bullet points**: Long lists that could be condensed into prose or tables\n3. **Redundant examples**: Multiple examples showing the same concept\n4. **Verbose descriptions**: Overly wordy explanations that could be more concise\n5. **Repetitive structure**: The same \"What it does\" / \"Why it''s valuable\" pattern overused\n\n### Writing Concise Documentation\n\nWhen editing documentation, focus on:\n\n**Consolidate bullet points**: \n- Convert long bullet lists into concise prose or tables\n- Remove redundant points that say the same thing differently\n\n**Eliminate duplicates**:\n- Remove repeated information\n- Consolidate similar sections\n\n**Condense verbose text**:\n- Make descriptions more direct and concise\n- Remove filler words and phrases\n- Keep technical accuracy while reducing word count\n\n**Standardize structure**:\n- Reduce repetitive \"What it does\" / \"Why it''s valuable\" patterns\n- Use varied, natural language\n\n**Simplify code samples**:\n- Remove unnecessary complexity from code examples\n- Focus on demonstrating the core concept clearly\n- Eliminate boilerplate or setup code unless essential for understanding\n- Keep examples minimal yet complete\n- Use realistic but simple scenarios\n\n### Example: Before and After\n\n**Before (Bloated)**:\n```markdown\n### Tool Name\nDescription of the tool.\n\n- **What it does**: This tool does X, Y, and Z\n- **Why it''s valuable**: It''s valuable because A, B, and C\n- **How to use**: You use it by doing steps 1, 2, 3, 4, 5\n- **When to use**: Use it when you need X\n- **Benefits**: Gets you benefit A, benefit B, benefit C\n- **Learn more**: [Link](url)\n```\n\n**After (Concise)**:\n```markdown\n### Tool Name\nDescription of the tool that does X, Y, and Z to achieve A, B, and C.\n\nUse it when you need X by following steps 1-5. [Learn more](url)\n```\n\n### Documentation Quality Guidelines\n\n1. **Preserve meaning**: Never lose important information\n2. **Be surgical**: Make precise edits, don''t rewrite everything\n3. **Maintain tone**: Keep the neutral, technical tone\n4. **Test locally**: Verify links and formatting are still correct\n\n## Structure by File Type\n\n- **Getting Started**: Tutorial format\n- **How-to Guides**: Goal-oriented, one task per guide\n- **CLI Reference**: Reference format, complete command documentation\n- **Concepts**: Explanation format, building understanding\n- **API Reference**: Reference format, complete API documentation\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:11:35.106Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Technical Writing Agents needing structured documentation capabilities using GitHub-flavored markdown and the Diátaxis framework.","zh":"非常适合需要使用 GitHub 风格 markdown 和 Diátaxis 框架进行结构化文档编写的技术写作代理。","ja":"GitHub フレーバーの Markdown と Diátaxis フレームワークを使用した構造化ドキュメント機能を必要とするテクニカルライティングエージェントに最適です。","ko":"GitHub風 마크다운과 Diátaxis 프레임워크를 사용한 구조화된 문서 기능이 필요한 기술 작성 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de escritura técnica que necesitan capacidades de documentación estructurada utilizando el markdown con sintaxis de GitHub y el marco Diátaxis.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de rédaction technique ayant besoin de capacités de documentation structurée utilisant le markdown de style GitHub et le cadre Diátaxis.","de":"Perfekt für technische Redaktionsagenten, die strukturierte Dokumentationsfähigkeiten unter Verwendung von GitHub-Flavored Markdown und dem Diátaxis-Framework benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Escrita Técnica que necessitam de capacidades de documentação estruturada utilizando markdown com sabor GitHub e o framework Diátaxis.","ru":"Идеально для технических писателей, которым необходимы структурированные возможности документации с использованием markdown от GitHub и фреймворка Diátaxis.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء النصوص الفنية الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات توثيقية منظمة باستخدام تنسيق ماركداون المُحسَّن من جيت هاب وإطار دياتاكسيس."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create systematic documentation with tutorials, guides, and reference materials, utilizing Astro Starlight for rendering and following the Diátaxis framework for organization, including tutorials, guides, and reference materials in Markdown format.","zh":"能够让代理创建系统化的文档，包括教程、指南和参考材料，利用 Astro Starlight 进行渲染，并遵循 Diátaxis 框架进行组织，包括 Markdown 格式的教程、指南和参考材料。","ja":"エージェントが、Astro Starlight を使用したレンダリングと、組織構造として Diátaxis フレームワークを使用した、体系的なドキュメントを作成できるようにします。ドキュメントには、チュートリアル、ガイド、リファレンス資料など、Markdown 形式の資料が含まれます。","ko":"에이전트가 체계적인 문서를 생성할 수 있도록 해줍니다. 튜토리얼, 가이드, 참조 자료 등을 Astro Starlight를 사용하여 렌더링하고, Diátaxis 프레임워크를 사용하여 구성합니다. 문서에는 Markdown 형식의 튜토리얼, 가이드, 참조 자료가 포함됩니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear documentación sistemática con tutoriales, guías y materiales de referencia, utilizando Astro Starlight para el renderizado y siguiendo el marco Diátaxis para la organización, incluyendo tutoriales, guías y materiales de referencia en formato Markdown.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer une documentation systématique avec des tutoriels, des guides et des documents de référence, en utilisant Astro Starlight pour le rendu et en suivant le cadre Diátaxis pour l''organisation, y compris des tutoriels, des guides et des documents de référence au format Markdown.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, systematische Dokumentation mit Tutorials, Anleitungen und Referenzmaterialien zu erstellen, unter Verwendung von Astro Starlight für das Rendering und unter Einhaltung des Diátaxis-Frameworks für die Organisation, einschließlich Tutorials, Anleitungen und Referenzmaterialien im Markdown-Format.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar documentação sistemática com tutoriais, guias e materiais de referência, utilizando Astro Starlight para renderização e seguindo o framework Diátaxis para organização, incluindo tutoriais, guias e materiais de referência no formato Markdown.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать системную документацию с учебными пособиями, руководствами и справочными материалами, используя Astro Starlight для рендеринга и следуя фреймворку Diátaxis для организации, включая учебные пособия, руководства и справочные материалы в формате Markdown.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إنشاء توثيق منهجي مع دروس تعليمية ودلائل ومواد مرجعية، باستخدام إضاءة أسترو للتصيير والالتزام بإطار دياتاكسيس للتنظيم، بما في ذلك دروس تعليمية ودلائل ومواد مرجعية بصيغة ماركداون."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating tutorial content for beginner users","Creating technical guides for advanced users","Organizing reference materials using the Diátaxis framework"],"zh":["为初学者用户生成教程内容","为高级用户创建技术指南","使用 Diátaxis 框架组织参考材料"],"ja":["初心者ユーザー向けのチュートリアルコンテンツを生成する","上級ユーザー向けのテクニカルガイドを作成する","Diátaxis フレームワークを使用してリファレンス資料を整理する"],"ko":["초보 사용자를 위한 튜토리얼 내용 생성","고급 사용자를 위한 기술 가이드 작성","Diátaxis 프레임워크를 사용한 참조 자료 구성"],"es":["Generar contenido de tutorial para usuarios principiantes","Crear guías técnicas para usuarios avanzados","Organizar materiales de referencia utilizando el marco Diátaxis"],"fr":["Générer du contenu de tutoriel pour les utilisateurs débutants","Créer des guides techniques pour les utilisateurs avancés","Organiser des documents de référence en utilisant le cadre Diátaxis"],"de":["Erstellen von Tutorial-Inhalten für Anfänger","Erstellen von technischen Anleitungen für fortgeschrittene Benutzer","Organisieren von Referenzmaterialien mit dem Diátaxis-Framework"],"pt":["Gerar conteúdo de tutorial para usuários iniciantes","Criar guias técnicos para usuários avançados","Organizar materiais de referência usando o framework Diátaxis"],"ru":["Генерировать содержимое учебных пособий для начинающих пользователей","Создавать технические руководства для опытных пользователей","Организовывать справочные материалы с использованием фреймворка Diátaxis"],"ar":["Generating tutorial content for beginner users","إنشاء دلائل فنية لمستخدمين متقدمين","تنظيم مواد مرجعية باستخدام إطار دياتاكسيس"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of GitHub-flavored markdown","Limited to the Diátaxis framework for documentation structure","Astro Starlight required for rendering"],"zh":["需要了解 GitHub 风格 markdown","仅限于 Diátaxis 框架进行文档结构","需要 Astro Starlight 进行渲染"],"ja":["GitHub フレーバーの Markdown の知識が必要","ドキュメント構造は Diátaxis フレームワークに限定される","Astro Starlight がレンダリングに必要"],"ko":["GitHub風 마크다운에 대한 지식이 필요","문서 구조는 Diátaxis 프레임워크로 제한","Astro Starlight가 렌더링에 필요"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento del markdown con sintaxis de GitHub","Limitado al marco Diátaxis para la estructura de la documentación","Se requiere Astro Starlight para el renderizado"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance du markdown de style GitHub","Limité au cadre Diátaxis pour la structure de la documentation","Astro Starlight requis pour le rendu"],"de":["Erfordert Kenntnisse in GitHub-Flavored Markdown","Beschränkt auf das Diátaxis-Framework für die Dokumentationsstruktur","Astro Starlight wird für das Rendering benötigt"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento de markdown com sabor GitHub","Limitado ao framework Diátaxis para estrutura de documentação","Astro Starlight necessário para renderização"],"ru":["Требуется знание markdown от GitHub","Ограничен фреймворком Diátaxis для структуры документации","Требуется Astro Starlight для рендеринга"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة تنسيق ماركداون المُحسَّن من جيت هاب","محدود بإطار دياتاكسيس لهيكل التوثيق","يتطلب إضاءة أسترو للتصيير"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/documentation', 'community', 'majiayu000', 'claude-skill-registry', 'majiayu000/claude-skill-registry', 'documentation', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.417Z', '2026-02-18T04:11:28.118Z', NULL, '{"id":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/documentation","name":"documentation","description":{"zh":"本项目的文档使用Diátaxis框架组织，包括教程、如何、参考和解释等内容，帮助开发者快速理解项目","ja":"本プロジェクトのドキュメントはDiátaxisフレームワークを使用して組織されており、チュートリアル、HOWTO、リファレンス、解説などが含まれています","ko":"이 프로젝트의 문서는 Diátaxis 프레임워크를 사용하여 구성되어 있으며 튜토리얼, HOWTO, 참조 및 설명 등이 포함되어 있습니다","es":"La documentación técnica utiliza el marco Diátaxis y Astro Starlight para guiar a los desarrolladores. Ofrece tutoriales, explicaciones y referencias para una documentación efectiva.","fr":"La documentation technique utilise le cadre Diátaxis et Astro Starlight pour guider les développeurs. Elle propose des tutoriels, des explications et des références pour une documentation efficace.","de":"Die technische Dokumentation nutzt den Diátaxis-Rahmen und Astro Starlight, um Entwickler zu unterstützen. Sie bietet Tutorien, Erklärungen und Referenzen für eine effektive Dokumentation.","pt":"A documentação do projeto é organizada de acordo com o framework Diátaxis, com tutoriais, conceitos e referências","ru":"Документация проекта организована в соответствии с фреймворком Diátaxis, с учебными пособиями, концепциями и ссылками","ar":"توثيق المشروع منظمة وفق إطار Diátaxis، مع التutorials والمفاهيم والمراجع","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"文档和Diátaxis框架指南","ja":"ドキュメントとDiátaxisフレームワークガイド","ko":"문서 및 Diátaxis 프레임워크 가이드","es":"Documentación técnica: Diátaxis Framework y Astro Starlight","fr":"Documentation technique : Diátaxis Framework et Astro Sta...","de":"Technische Dokumentation: Diátaxis Framework und Astro St...","pt":"Documentação Técnica: Guia de Início Rápido","ru":"Техническая документация: Быстрый старт","ar":"توثيق تقني: دليل البداية السريعة","en":"documentation"},"description":{"zh":"本项目的文档使用Diátaxis框架组织，包括教程、如何、参考和解释等内容，帮助开发者快速理解项目","ja":"本プロジェクトのドキュメントはDiátaxisフレームワークを使用して組織されており、チュートリアル、HOWTO、リファレンス、解説などが含まれています","ko":"이 프로젝트의 문서는 Diátaxis 프레임워크를 사용하여 구성되어 있으며 튜토리얼, HOWTO, 참조 및 설명 등이 포함되어 있습니다","es":"La documentación técnica utiliza el marco Diátaxis y Astro Starlight para guiar a los desarrolladores. Ofrece tutoriales, explicaciones y referencias para un...","fr":"La documentation technique utilise le cadre Diátaxis et Astro Starlight pour guider les développeurs. Elle propose des tutoriels, des explications et des réf...","de":"Die technische Dokumentation nutzt den Diátaxis-Rahmen und Astro Starlight, um Entwickler zu unterstützen. Sie bietet Tutorien, Erklärungen und Referenzen fü...","pt":"A documentação do projeto é organizada de acordo com o framework Diátaxis, com tutoriais, conceitos e referências","ru":"Документация проекта организована в соответствии с фреймворком Diátaxis, с учебными пособиями, концепциями и ссылками","ar":"توثيق المشروع منظمة وفق إطار Diátaxis، مع التutorials والمفاهيم والمراجع","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"zh":["教程（学习导向）","如何（问题导向）","参考（信息导向）","解释（理解导向）","使用GitHub-flavored markdown","使用Astro Starlight渲染"],"ja":["チュートリアル（学習指向）","HOWTO（問題指向）","リファレンス（情報指向）","解説（理解指向）","GitHub-flavored markdownを使用","Astro Starlightを使用してレンダリング"],"ko":["튜토리얼（학습 지향）","HOWTO（문제 지향）","참조（정보 지향）","설명（이해 지향）","GitHub-flavored markdown 사용","Astro Starlight로 렌더링"],"es":["Marco Diátaxis para documentación sistemática","Astro Starlight para renderizado de markdown","Tutoriales para principiantes","Explicaciones detalladas","Referencias para desarrolladores avanzados"],"fr":["Cadre Diátaxis pour documentation systématique","Astro Starlight pour rendu de markdown","Tutoriels pour débutants","Explications détaillées","Références pour développeurs avancés"],"de":["Diátaxis-Rahmen für systematische Dokumentation","Astro Starlight für Markdown-Rendering","Tutorien für Anfänger","Detaillierte Erklärungen","Referenzen für erfahrene Entwickler"],"pt":["Tutoriais para iniciantes","Conceitos e explicações técnicas","Referências para desenvolvedores","Organização de acordo com o framework Diátaxis","Uso de GitHub-flavored markdown com Astro Starlight"],"ru":["Учебные пособия для начинающих","Концепции и технические объяснения","Ссылки для разработчиков","Организация в соответствии с фреймворком Diátaxis","Использование GitHub-flavored markdown с Astro Starlight"],"ar":["التutorials للمبتدئين","المفاهيم والشروحات الفنية","المراجع للمطورين","التنظيم وفق إطار Diátaxis","استخدام GitHub-flavored markdown مع Astro Starlight"]},"keywords":{"zh":["文档","Diátaxis框架","教程","如何","参考","解释","GitHub-flavored markdown","Astro Starlight"],"ja":["ドキュメント","Diátaxisフレームワーク","チュートリアル","HOWTO","リファレンス","解説","GitHub-flavored markdown","Astro Starlight"],"ko":["문서","Diátaxis 프레임워크","튜토리얼","HOWTO","참조","설명","GitHub-flavored markdown","Astro Starlight"],"es":["documentación técnica","Diátaxis Framework","Astro Starlight","tutoriales para desarrolladores","explicaciones técnicas","referencias para programadores"],"fr":["documentation technique","Diátaxis Framework","Astro Starlight","tutoriels pour développeurs","explications techniques","références pour programmeurs"],"de":["technische Dokumentation","Diátaxis-Rahmen","Astro Starlight","Tutorien für Entwickler","technische Erklärungen","Referenzen für Programmierer"],"pt":["documentação técnica","tutoriais","conceitos","referências","Diátaxis","GitHub-flavored markdown","Astro Starlight","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["техническая документация","учебные пособия","концепции","ссылки","Diátaxis","GitHub-flavored markdown","Astro Starlight","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["توثيق تقني","التutorials","المفاهيم","المراجع","Diátaxis","GitHub-flavored markdown","Astro Starlight","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.417Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"documentation","description":"Documentation Brief description for SEO and navigation","bodyPreview":"### Documentation\n\nThe documentation for this project is available in the `docs/` directory. It uses GitHub-flavored markdown with Astro Starlight for rendering and follows the Diátaxis framework for systematic documentation.\n\n## Diátaxis Framework\n\nDocumentation must be organized into four distinct types, each serving a specific purpose:\n\n### 1. Tutorials (Learning-Oriented)\n**Purpose**: Guide beginners through achieving a specific outcome to build confidence.\n\n- Start with what the user will b","body":"### Documentation\n\nThe documentation for this project is available in the `docs/` directory. It uses GitHub-flavored markdown with Astro Starlight for rendering and follows the Diátaxis framework for systematic documentation.\n\n## Diátaxis Framework\n\nDocumentation must be organized into four distinct types, each serving a specific purpose:\n\n### 1. Tutorials (Learning-Oriented)\n**Purpose**: Guide beginners through achieving a specific outcome to build confidence.\n\n- Start with what the user will build or achieve\n- Provide a clear, step-by-step path from start to finish\n- Include concrete examples and working code\n- Assume minimal prior knowledge\n- Focus on the happy path (avoid edge cases and alternatives)\n- End with a working result the user can see and use\n- Use imperative mood: \"Create a file\", \"Run the command\"\n\n**Avoid**: Explaining concepts in depth, multiple options, troubleshooting\n\n### 2. How-to Guides (Goal-Oriented)\n**Purpose**: Show how to solve a specific real-world problem or accomplish a particular task.\n\n- Title format: \"How to [accomplish specific goal]\"\n- Assume the user knows the basics\n- Focus on practical steps to solve one problem\n- Include necessary context but stay focused\n- Show multiple approaches only when genuinely useful\n- End when the goal is achieved\n- Use imperative mood: \"Configure the setting\", \"Add the following\"\n\n**Avoid**: Teaching fundamentals, explaining every detail, being exhaustive\n\n### 3. Reference (Information-Oriented)\n**Purpose**: Provide accurate, complete technical descriptions of the system.\n\n- Organized by structure (CLI commands, configuration options, API endpoints)\n- Comprehensive and authoritative\n- Consistent format across all entries\n- Technical accuracy is paramount\n- Include all parameters, options, and return values\n- Use descriptive mood: \"The command accepts\", \"Returns a string\"\n- Minimal narrative or explanation\n\n**Avoid**: Instructions, tutorials, opinions on usage\n\n### 4. Explanation (Understanding-Oriented)\n**Purpose**: Clarify and illuminate topics to deepen understanding.\n\n- Discuss why things are the way they are\n- Explain design decisions and tradeoffs\n- Provide context and background\n- Connect concepts to help form mental models\n- Discuss alternatives and their implications\n- Use indicative mood: \"This approach provides\", \"The engine uses\"\n\n**Avoid**: Step-by-step instructions, exhaustive reference material\n\n## General Style Guidelines\n\n- **Tone**: Neutral, technical, not promotional\n- **Voice**: Avoid \"we\", \"our\", \"us\" (use \"the tool\", \"this command\")\n- **Headings**: Use markdown heading syntax, not bold text as headings\n- **Lists**: Avoid long bullet point lists; prefer prose with structure\n- **Code samples**: Minimal and focused; exclude optional fields unless relevant\n- **Language tag**: Use `aw` for agentic workflow snippets with YAML frontmatter\n\n**Example workflow code block**:\n```aw wrap\non: push\n# Your workflow steps here\n```\n\n## GitHub-Flavored Markdown Syntax\n\nDocumentation files use GitHub-flavored markdown with Astro Starlight for rendering. Key syntax elements:\n\n### Frontmatter\nEvery documentation page must have frontmatter:\n```markdown\ntitle: Page Title\ndescription: Brief description for SEO and navigation\n```\n\n### GitHub Alerts\nUse GitHub''s alert syntax for notes, tips, warnings, and cautions:\n```markdown\n> [!NOTE]\n> Important information the reader should notice.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Helpful advice for the reader.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Warning about potential issues or pitfalls.\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Critical warning about dangerous operations.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Key information users need to know.\n```\n\n### Code Blocks\n- Use syntax highlighting with language tags\n- Add `title` attribute for file names: ` ```yaml title=\".github/workflows/example.yml\" `\n- Use `aw` language for agentic workflow files with YAML frontmatter\n- Add `wrap` for line wrapping: ` ```aw wrap `\n\n### Links\n- Internal links: Use relative paths between documentation pages\n- External links: Open in new tab automatically\n- Link text: Use descriptive text, avoid \"click here\"\n\n### Tabs\nUse tabs for showing alternatives (e.g., different languages, platforms):\n```markdown\nimport { Tabs, TabItem } from ''@astrojs/starlight/components'';\n\n<Tabs>\n  <TabItem label=\"npm\">\n    ```bash\n    npm install package\n    ```\n  </TabItem>\n  <TabItem label=\"yarn\">\n    ```bash\n    yarn add package\n    ```\n  </TabItem>\n</Tabs>\n```\n\n### Cards\nUse cards for navigation or highlighting multiple options:\n```markdown\nimport { Card, CardGrid } from ''@astrojs/starlight/components'';\n\n<CardGrid>\n  <Card title=\"Getting Started\" icon=\"rocket\">\n    Quick introduction to the basics.\n  </Card>\n  <Card title=\"Advanced Usage\" icon=\"setting\">\n    Deep dive into advanced features.\n  </Card>\n</CardGrid>\n```\n\n**Remember**: Keep components minimal. Prefer standard markdown when possible.\n\n## Content to Avoid\n\n- \"Key Features\" sections\n- Marketing language or selling points\n- Excessive bullet points (prefer structured prose)\n- Overly verbose examples with all optional parameters\n- Mixing documentation types (e.g., tutorials that become reference)\n\n## Avoiding Documentation Bloat\n\nDocumentation bloat reduces clarity and makes content harder to navigate. Common types of bloat include:\n\n### Types of Documentation Bloat\n\n1. **Duplicate content**: Same information repeated in different sections\n2. **Excessive bullet points**: Long lists that could be condensed into prose or tables\n3. **Redundant examples**: Multiple examples showing the same concept\n4. **Verbose descriptions**: Overly wordy explanations that could be more concise\n5. **Repetitive structure**: The same \"What it does\" / \"Why it''s valuable\" pattern overused\n\n### Writing Concise Documentation\n\nWhen editing documentation, focus on:\n\n**Consolidate bullet points**: \n- Convert long bullet lists into concise prose or tables\n- Remove redundant points that say the same thing differently\n\n**Eliminate duplicates**:\n- Remove repeated information\n- Consolidate similar sections\n\n**Condense verbose text**:\n- Make descriptions more direct and concise\n- Remove filler words and phrases\n- Keep technical accuracy while reducing word count\n\n**Standardize structure**:\n- Reduce repetitive \"What it does\" / \"Why it''s valuable\" patterns\n- Use varied, natural language\n\n**Simplify code samples**:\n- Remove unnecessary complexity from code examples\n- Focus on demonstrating the core concept clearly\n- Eliminate boilerplate or setup code unless essential for understanding\n- Keep examples minimal yet complete\n- Use realistic but simple scenarios\n\n### Example: Before and After\n\n**Before (Bloated)**:\n```markdown\n### Tool Name\nDescription of the tool.\n\n- **What it does**: This tool does X, Y, and Z\n- **Why it''s valuable**: It''s valuable because A, B, and C\n- **How to use**: You use it by doing steps 1, 2, 3, 4, 5\n- **When to use**: Use it when you need X\n- **Benefits**: Gets you benefit A, benefit B, benefit C\n- **Learn more**: [Link](url)\n```\n\n**After (Concise)**:\n```markdown\n### Tool Name\nDescription of the tool that does X, Y, and Z to achieve A, B, and C.\n\nUse it when you need X by following steps 1-5. [Learn more](url)\n```\n\n### Documentation Quality Guidelines\n\n1. **Preserve meaning**: Never lose important information\n2. **Be surgical**: Make precise edits, don''t rewrite everything\n3. **Maintain tone**: Keep the neutral, technical tone\n4. **Test locally**: Verify links and formatting are still correct\n\n## Structure by File Type\n\n- **Getting Started**: Tutorial format\n- **How-to Guides**: Goal-oriented, one task per guide\n- **CLI Reference**: Reference format, complete command documentation\n- **Concepts**: Explanation format, building understanding\n- **API Reference**: Reference format, complete API documentation\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:11:28.118Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing systematic and organized documentation capabilities using GitHub-flavored markdown and the Diátaxis framework.","zh":"非常适合需要系统化和组织化文档能力的 AI 代理，使用 GitHub 风格的 markdown 和 Diátaxis 框架。","ja":"GitHub 風のマークダウンと Diátaxis フレームワークを使用した体系的で組織化されたドキュメント機能を必要とする AI エージェントに最適です。","ko":"GitHub风格의 markdown와 Diátaxis 프레임워크를 사용한 체계적이고 조직화된 문서 기능을 필요한 AI 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que necesitan capacidades de documentación sistemáticas y organizadas utilizando markdown con sabor a GitHub y el marco Diátaxis.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA ayant besoin de capacités de documentation systématiques et organisées utilisant markdown à saveur GitHub et le cadre Diátaxis.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die systematische und organisierte Dokumentationsfunktionen mit GitHub-geschmacktem Markdown und dem Diátaxis-Framework benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que necessitam de capacidades de documentação sistemáticas e organizadas usando markdown com sabor GitHub e o framework Diátaxis.","ru":"Идеально для ИИ-агентов, которым необходимы системные и организованные возможности документации, использующие markdown с вкусом GitHub и фреймворк Diátaxis.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذي يحتاج إلى إمكانيات توثيقية منظمة ومتماسكة باستخدام markdown ذو نكهة جيت هاب و إطار دياتاكسيس."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create comprehensive documentation with tutorials, guides, and reference materials using Astro Starlight for rendering, following the Diátaxis framework for systematic organization, and supporting GitHub-flavored markdown for content creation.","zh":"赋予代理创建综合文档的能力，包括教程、指南和参考资料，使用 Astro Starlight 渲染，遵循 Diátaxis 框架进行系统化组织，并支持 GitHub 风格的 markdown 进行内容创建。","ja":"Astro Starlight を使用したレンダリングを行い、Diátaxis フレームワークに従った体系的な組織化を行い、GitHub 風のマークダウンを使用したコンテンツ作成をサポートすることで、教程、ガイド、参考資料を含む包括的なドキュメントを作成するエージェントの能力を提供します。","ko":"Astro Starlight를 사용한 렌더링을 수행하고 Diátaxis 프레임워크에 따라 체계적인 조직화를 수행하고 GitHub风格의 markdown를 사용한 컨텐츠 생성을 지원하여 튜토리얼, 가이드, 참조 자료 등을 포함한 포괄적인 문서를 생성하는 에이전트의 능력을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear documentación integral con tutoriales, guías y materiales de referencia utilizando Astro Starlight para la representación, siguiendo el marco Diátaxis para la organización sistemática y admitiendo markdown con sabor a GitHub para la creación de contenido.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer une documentation complète avec des didacticiels, des guides et des documents de référence en utilisant Astro Starlight pour le rendu, en suivant le cadre Diátaxis pour l''organisation systématique et en prenant en charge le markdown à saveur GitHub pour la création de contenu.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, umfassende Dokumentationen mit Tutorien, Anleitungen und Referenzmaterialien zu erstellen, indem Astro Starlight für die Darstellung verwendet wird, dem Diátaxis-Framework für die systematische Organisation gefolgt wird und GitHub-geschmacktes Markdown für die Inhaltserschaffung unterstützt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar documentação abrangente com tutoriais, guias e materiais de referência usando Astro Starlight para renderização, seguindo o framework Diátaxis para organização sistemática e suportando markdown com sabor GitHub para criação de conteúdo.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать всестороннюю документацию с учебными пособиями, руководствами и справочными материалами, используя Astro Starlight для рендеринга, следуя фреймворку Diátaxis для системной организации и поддерживая markdown с вкусом GitHub для создания контента.","ar":"تمكن العميل من إنشاء توثيق شامل مع دروس ومرشدين ومواد مرجعية باستخدام إسترو ستار لايت للتقديم، متبوعًا بتشغيل إطار دياتاكسيس للتنظيم المنهجي ودعم markdown ذو نكهة جيت هاب لإنشاء المحتوى."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating tutorial content for beginner users","Creating reference materials for advanced users","Organizing documentation into tutorials, guides, and reference sections"],"zh":["为初学者用户生成教程内容","为高级用户创建参考资料","将文档组织成教程、指南和参考部分"],"ja":["初心者ユーザー向けのチュートリアルコンテンツを生成する","上級ユーザー向けの参考資料を作成する","ドキュメントをチュートリアル、ガイド、参考セクションに整理する"],"ko":["초급 사용자를 위한 튜토리얼 컨텐츠 생성","고급 사용자를 위한 참조 자료 생성","문서를 튜토리얼, 가이드, 참조 섹션으로 조직화"],"es":["Generar contenido de tutorial para usuarios principiantes","Crear materiales de referencia para usuarios avanzados","Organizar la documentación en secciones de tutoriales, guías y referencias"],"fr":["Générer du contenu de didacticiel pour les utilisateurs débutants","Créer des documents de référence pour les utilisateurs avancés","Organiser la documentation en sections de didacticiels, de guides et de références"],"de":["Tutorialinhalte für Anfängerbenutzer generieren","Referenzmaterialien für fortgeschrittene Benutzer erstellen","Dokumentation in Tutorien-, Anleitungs- und Referenzabschnitte organisieren"],"pt":["Gerar conteúdo de tutorial para usuários iniciantes","Criar materiais de referência para usuários avançados","Organizar documentação em tutoriais, guias e seções de referência"],"ru":["Генерировать контент учебных пособий для начинающих пользователей","Создавать справочные материалы для опытных пользователей","Организовывать документацию в учебные пособия, руководства и разделы справки"],"ar":["إنشاء محتوى دروسي لمستخدمي المبتدئين","إنشاء مواد مرجعية لمستخدمي المحترفين","تنظيم التوثيق في دروس ومرشدين وأقسام مرجعية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires GitHub-flavored markdown compatibility","Limited to Astro Starlight for rendering","Follows the Diátaxis framework for documentation organization"],"zh":["需要 GitHub 风格的 markdown 兼容性","仅限 Astro Starlight 渲染","遵循 Diátaxis 框架进行文档组织"],"ja":["GitHub 風のマークダウンとの互換性が必要","Astro Starlight のレンダリングのみ","ドキュメントの組織化に Diátaxis フレームワークを使用"],"ko":["GitHub风格의 markdown와의 호환성이 필요","Astro Starlight의 렌더링만","문서의 조직화에 Diátaxis 프레임워크 사용"],"es":["Requiere compatibilidad con markdown con sabor a GitHub","Limitado a Astro Starlight para la representación","Sigue el marco Diátaxis para la organización de la documentación"],"fr":["Nécessite la compatibilité avec le markdown à saveur GitHub","Limité à Astro Starlight pour le rendu","Suit le cadre Diátaxis pour l''organisation de la documentation"],"de":["Benötigt Kompatibilität mit GitHub-geschmacktem Markdown","Begrenzt auf Astro Starlight für die Darstellung","Folgt dem Diátaxis-Framework für die Dokumentationsorganisation"],"pt":["Requer compatibilidade com markdown com sabor GitHub","Limitado ao Astro Starlight para renderização","Segue o framework Diátaxis para organização de documentação"],"ru":["Требует совместимости с markdown с вкусом GitHub","Ограничен Astro Starlight для рендеринга","Следует фреймворку Diátaxis для организации документации"],"ar":["يتطلب توافقًا مع markdown ذو نكهة جيت هاب","محدود ب إسترو ستار لايت للتقديم","يتابع إطار دياتاكسيس لتنظيم التوثيق"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('maxfraieho/garden-bloom/documentation', 'community', 'maxfraieho', 'garden-bloom', 'maxfraieho/garden-bloom', 'documentation', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.417Z', '2026-02-18T04:11:53.232Z', NULL, '{"id":"maxfraieho/garden-bloom/documentation","name":"documentation","description":{"zh":"本项目的文档使用GitHub风格的Markdown和Astro Starlight渲染，遵循Diátaxis框架进行系统化文档管理。","ja":"このプロジェクトのドキュメントは、GitHub風のMarkdownとAstro Starlightを使用してレンダリングされ、Diátaxisフレームワークに従って体系的に管理されています。","ko":"이 프로젝트의 문서는 GitHub 스타일의 Markdown과 Astro Starlight를 사용하여 렌더링되며, Diátaxis 프레임워크에 따라 시스템적으로 문서가 관리됩니다.","es":"La documentación del proyecto utiliza Diátaxis, un framework para documentación sistemática, y se encuentra en el directorio docs/","fr":"La documentation du projet utilise Diátaxis, un framework pour documentation systématique, et se trouve dans le répertoire docs/","de":"Die Projektdokumentation verwendet Diátaxis, ein Framework für systematische Dokumentation, und befindet sich im Verzeichnis docs/","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"文档和Diátaxis框架指南","ja":"ドキュメントとDiátaxisフレームワークガイド","ko":"문서 및 Diátaxis 프레임워크 가이드","es":"Documentación de Proyecto con Diátaxis","fr":"Documentation de Projet avec Diátaxis","de":"Projektdokumentation mit Diátaxis","en":"documentation"},"description":{"zh":"本项目的文档使用GitHub风格的Markdown和Astro Starlight渲染，遵循Diátaxis框架进行系统化文档管理。","ja":"このプロジェクトのドキュメントは、GitHub風のMarkdownとAstro Starlightを使用してレンダリングされ、Diátaxisフレームワークに従って体系的に管理されています。","ko":"이 프로젝트의 문서는 GitHub 스타일의 Markdown과 Astro Starlight를 사용하여 렌더링되며, Diátaxis 프레임워크에 따라 시스템적으로 문서가 관리됩니다.","es":"La documentación del proyecto utiliza Diátaxis, un framework para documentación sistemática, y se encuentra en el directorio docs/","fr":"La documentation du projet utilise Diátaxis, un framework pour documentation systématique, et se trouve dans le répertoire docs/","de":"Die Projektdokumentation verwendet Diátaxis, ein Framework für systematische Dokumentation, und befindet sich im Verzeichnis docs/","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["教程（学习导向）","如何（操作指南）","参考（技术文档）","解释（背景介绍）","使用GitHub风格的Markdown","Astro Starlight渲染"],"ja":["チュートリアル（学習向け）","方法（操作ガイド）","リファレンス（技術文書）","説明（背景紹介）","GitHub風のMarkdownを使用","Astro Starlightレンダリング"],"ko":["튜토리얼（학습 지향）","방법（操作 가이드）","참조（기술 문서）","설명（배경 소개）","GitHub 스타일의 Markdown 사용","Astro Starlight 렌더링"],"es":["Documentación sistemática con Diátaxis","Tutoriales para principiantes","Uso de GitHub-flavored markdown","Renderizado con Astro Starlight","Organización en cuatro tipos de contenido"],"fr":["Documentation systématique avec Diátaxis","Tutoriels pour débutants","Utilisation de GitHub-flavored markdown","Renderisation avec Astro Starlight","Organisation en quatre types de contenu"],"de":["Systematische Dokumentation mit Diátaxis","Tutorien für Anfänger","Verwendung von GitHub-flavored markdown","Renderung mit Astro Starlight","Organisation in vier Inhaltstypen"]},"keywords":{"zh":["文档管理","Diátaxis框架","GitHub风格的Markdown","Astro Starlight","教程","如何","参考","解释"],"ja":["ドキュメント管理","Diátaxisフレームワーク","GitHub風のMarkdown","Astro Starlight","チュートリアル","方法","リファレンス","説明"],"ko":["문서 관리","Diátaxis 프레임워크","GitHub 스타일의 Markdown","Astro Starlight","튜토리얼","방법","참조","설명"],"es":["documentación de proyecto","Diátaxis","GitHub-flavored markdown","Astro Starlight","documentación sistemática","tutoriales para principiantes","desarrollo de software","documentación de código"],"fr":["documentation de projet","Diátaxis","GitHub-flavored markdown","Astro Starlight","documentation systématique","tutoriels pour débutants","développement de logiciel","documentation de code"],"de":["Projektdokumentation","Diátaxis","GitHub-flavored markdown","Astro Starlight","systematische Dokumentation","Tutorien für Anfänger","Softwareentwicklung","Codedokumentation"]}},"owner":"maxfraieho","repo":"garden-bloom","repoPath":"maxfraieho/garden-bloom","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.417Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"documentation","description":"Documentation Brief description for SEO and navigation","bodyPreview":"### Documentation\n\nThe documentation for this project is available in the `docs/` directory. It uses GitHub-flavored markdown with Astro Starlight for rendering and follows the Diátaxis framework for systematic documentation.\n\n## Diátaxis Framework\n\nDocumentation must be organized into four distinct types, each serving a specific purpose:\n\n### 1. Tutorials (Learning-Oriented)\n**Purpose**: Guide beginners through achieving a specific outcome to build confidence.\n\n- Start with what the user will b","body":"### Documentation\n\nThe documentation for this project is available in the `docs/` directory. It uses GitHub-flavored markdown with Astro Starlight for rendering and follows the Diátaxis framework for systematic documentation.\n\n## Diátaxis Framework\n\nDocumentation must be organized into four distinct types, each serving a specific purpose:\n\n### 1. Tutorials (Learning-Oriented)\n**Purpose**: Guide beginners through achieving a specific outcome to build confidence.\n\n- Start with what the user will build or achieve\n- Provide a clear, step-by-step path from start to finish\n- Include concrete examples and working code\n- Assume minimal prior knowledge\n- Focus on the happy path (avoid edge cases and alternatives)\n- End with a working result the user can see and use\n- Use imperative mood: \"Create a file\", \"Run the command\"\n\n**Avoid**: Explaining concepts in depth, multiple options, troubleshooting\n\n### 2. How-to Guides (Goal-Oriented)\n**Purpose**: Show how to solve a specific real-world problem or accomplish a particular task.\n\n- Title format: \"How to [accomplish specific goal]\"\n- Assume the user knows the basics\n- Focus on practical steps to solve one problem\n- Include necessary context but stay focused\n- Show multiple approaches only when genuinely useful\n- End when the goal is achieved\n- Use imperative mood: \"Configure the setting\", \"Add the following\"\n\n**Avoid**: Teaching fundamentals, explaining every detail, being exhaustive\n\n### 3. Reference (Information-Oriented)\n**Purpose**: Provide accurate, complete technical descriptions of the system.\n\n- Organized by structure (CLI commands, configuration options, API endpoints)\n- Comprehensive and authoritative\n- Consistent format across all entries\n- Technical accuracy is paramount\n- Include all parameters, options, and return values\n- Use descriptive mood: \"The command accepts\", \"Returns a string\"\n- Minimal narrative or explanation\n\n**Avoid**: Instructions, tutorials, opinions on usage\n\n### 4. Explanation (Understanding-Oriented)\n**Purpose**: Clarify and illuminate topics to deepen understanding.\n\n- Discuss why things are the way they are\n- Explain design decisions and tradeoffs\n- Provide context and background\n- Connect concepts to help form mental models\n- Discuss alternatives and their implications\n- Use indicative mood: \"This approach provides\", \"The engine uses\"\n\n**Avoid**: Step-by-step instructions, exhaustive reference material\n\n## General Style Guidelines\n\n- **Tone**: Neutral, technical, not promotional\n- **Voice**: Avoid \"we\", \"our\", \"us\" (use \"the tool\", \"this command\")\n- **Headings**: Use markdown heading syntax, not bold text as headings\n- **Lists**: Avoid long bullet point lists; prefer prose with structure\n- **Code samples**: Minimal and focused; exclude optional fields unless relevant\n- **Language tag**: Use `aw` for agentic workflow snippets with YAML frontmatter\n\n**Example workflow code block**:\n```aw wrap\non: push\n# Your workflow steps here\n```\n\n## GitHub-Flavored Markdown Syntax\n\nDocumentation files use GitHub-flavored markdown with Astro Starlight for rendering. Key syntax elements:\n\n### Frontmatter\nEvery documentation page must have frontmatter:\n```markdown\ntitle: Page Title\ndescription: Brief description for SEO and navigation\n```\n\n### GitHub Alerts\nUse GitHub''s alert syntax for notes, tips, warnings, and cautions:\n```markdown\n> [!NOTE]\n> Important information the reader should notice.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Helpful advice for the reader.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Warning about potential issues or pitfalls.\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Critical warning about dangerous operations.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Key information users need to know.\n```\n\n### Code Blocks\n- Use syntax highlighting with language tags\n- Add `title` attribute for file names: ` ```yaml title=\".github/workflows/example.yml\" `\n- Use `aw` language for agentic workflow files with YAML frontmatter\n- Add `wrap` for line wrapping: ` ```aw wrap `\n\n### Links\n- Internal links: Use relative paths between documentation pages\n- External links: Open in new tab automatically\n- Link text: Use descriptive text, avoid \"click here\"\n\n### Tabs\nUse tabs for showing alternatives (e.g., different languages, platforms):\n```markdown\nimport { Tabs, TabItem } from ''@astrojs/starlight/components'';\n\n<Tabs>\n  <TabItem label=\"npm\">\n    ```bash\n    npm install package\n    ```\n  </TabItem>\n  <TabItem label=\"yarn\">\n    ```bash\n    yarn add package\n    ```\n  </TabItem>\n</Tabs>\n```\n\n### Cards\nUse cards for navigation or highlighting multiple options:\n```markdown\nimport { Card, CardGrid } from ''@astrojs/starlight/components'';\n\n<CardGrid>\n  <Card title=\"Getting Started\" icon=\"rocket\">\n    Quick introduction to the basics.\n  </Card>\n  <Card title=\"Advanced Usage\" icon=\"setting\">\n    Deep dive into advanced features.\n  </Card>\n</CardGrid>\n```\n\n**Remember**: Keep components minimal. Prefer standard markdown when possible.\n\n## Content to Avoid\n\n- \"Key Features\" sections\n- Marketing language or selling points\n- Excessive bullet points (prefer structured prose)\n- Overly verbose examples with all optional parameters\n- Mixing documentation types (e.g., tutorials that become reference)\n\n## Avoiding Documentation Bloat\n\nDocumentation bloat reduces clarity and makes content harder to navigate. Common types of bloat include:\n\n### Types of Documentation Bloat\n\n1. **Duplicate content**: Same information repeated in different sections\n2. **Excessive bullet points**: Long lists that could be condensed into prose or tables\n3. **Redundant examples**: Multiple examples showing the same concept\n4. **Verbose descriptions**: Overly wordy explanations that could be more concise\n5. **Repetitive structure**: The same \"What it does\" / \"Why it''s valuable\" pattern overused\n\n### Writing Concise Documentation\n\nWhen editing documentation, focus on:\n\n**Consolidate bullet points**: \n- Convert long bullet lists into concise prose or tables\n- Remove redundant points that say the same thing differently\n\n**Eliminate duplicates**:\n- Remove repeated information\n- Consolidate similar sections\n\n**Condense verbose text**:\n- Make descriptions more direct and concise\n- Remove filler words and phrases\n- Keep technical accuracy while reducing word count\n\n**Standardize structure**:\n- Reduce repetitive \"What it does\" / \"Why it''s valuable\" patterns\n- Use varied, natural language\n\n**Simplify code samples**:\n- Remove unnecessary complexity from code examples\n- Focus on demonstrating the core concept clearly\n- Eliminate boilerplate or setup code unless essential for understanding\n- Keep examples minimal yet complete\n- Use realistic but simple scenarios\n\n### Example: Before and After\n\n**Before (Bloated)**:\n```markdown\n### Tool Name\nDescription of the tool.\n\n- **What it does**: This tool does X, Y, and Z\n- **Why it''s valuable**: It''s valuable because A, B, and C\n- **How to use**: You use it by doing steps 1, 2, 3, 4, 5\n- **When to use**: Use it when you need X\n- **Benefits**: Gets you benefit A, benefit B, benefit C\n- **Learn more**: [Link](url)\n```\n\n**After (Concise)**:\n```markdown\n### Tool Name\nDescription of the tool that does X, Y, and Z to achieve A, B, and C.\n\nUse it when you need X by following steps 1-5. [Learn more](url)\n```\n\n### Documentation Quality Guidelines\n\n1. **Preserve meaning**: Never lose important information\n2. **Be surgical**: Make precise edits, don''t rewrite everything\n3. **Maintain tone**: Keep the neutral, technical tone\n4. **Test locally**: Verify links and formatting are still correct\n\n## Structure by File Type\n\n- **Getting Started**: Tutorial format\n- **How-to Guides**: Goal-oriented, one task per guide\n- **CLI Reference**: Reference format, complete command documentation\n- **Concepts**: Explanation format, building understanding\n- **API Reference**: Reference format, complete API documentation\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:11:53.232Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Developer Agents requiring systematic and structured documentation using GitHub-flavored markdown and the Diátaxis framework.","zh":"适用于需要使用GitHub风格标记语言和Diátaxis框架进行系统化和结构化文档的开发者代理。","ja":"GitHub風マークダウンとDiátaxisフレームワークを使用した体系的で構造化されたドキュメントを必要とする開発者エージェントに最適です。","ko":"GitHub风格 마크다운과 Diátaxis 프레임워크를 사용하여 체계적이고 구조화된 문서가 필요한 개발자 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Desarrollador que requieren documentación sistemática y estructurada utilizando markdown con sabor a GitHub y el marco Diátaxis.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement nécessitant une documentation systématique et structurée utilisant markdown à saveur GitHub et le framework Diátaxis.","de":"Ideal für Entwickleragenten, die systematische und strukturierte Dokumentationen unter Verwendung von GitHub-geschmacktem Markdown und dem Diátaxis-Framework benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvedores que requerem documentação sistemática e estruturada usando markdown com sabor GitHub e o framework Diátaxis.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработчиков, требующих систематической и структурированной документации, использующих markdown с вкусом GitHub и фреймворк Diátaxis.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المطورين الذين يحتاجون إلى توثيق منهجي ومنظم باستخدام markdown ذو نكهة GitHub و إطار Diátaxis."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create and manage tutorials, guides, and references using Astro Starlight for rendering, following the Diátaxis framework for organized documentation, and leveraging markdown for content creation.","zh":"赋予代理创建和管理教程、指南和参考文档的能力，使用Astro Starlight进行渲染，遵循Diátaxis框架进行组织化文档，并利用标记语言进行内容创建。","ja":"Astro Starlightを使用したレンダリング、Diátaxisフレームワークに従った組織化されたドキュメント、そしてマークダウンを使用したコンテンツ作成により、エージェントがチュートリアル、ガイド、リファレンスを生成および管理できるようにします。","ko":"Astro Starlight를 사용한 렌더링, Diátaxis 프레임워크를 따르는 조직화된 문서, 그리고 마크다운을 사용한 콘텐츠 생성을 통해 에이전트가 튜토리얼, 가이드, 참조를 생성 및 관리할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear y gestionar tutoriales, guías y referencias utilizando Astro Starlight para la representación, siguiendo el marco Diátaxis para la documentación organizada y aprovechando markdown para la creación de contenido.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer et de gérer des didacticiels, des guides et des références en utilisant Astro Starlight pour le rendu, en suivant le framework Diátaxis pour une documentation organisée et en exploitant markdown pour la création de contenu.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Tutorien, Anleitungen und Referenzen zu erstellen und zu verwalten, indem Astro Starlight für die Darstellung verwendet wird, dem Diátaxis-Framework für eine organisierte Dokumentation folgt und Markdown für die Inhaltserschaffung nutzt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar e gerenciar tutoriais, guias e referências usando Astro Starlight para renderização, seguindo o framework Diátaxis para documentação organizada e aproveitando markdown para criação de conteúdo.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать и управлять уроками, руководствами и справочными материалами, используя Astro Starlight для рендеринга, следуя фреймворку Diátaxis для организованной документации и используя markdown для созд