 engineered, approved, packaged, and delivered across our global endpoint estate."},"features":{"zh":["GitHub Actions 工作流","Docker Compose 容器编排","代码质量检查","自动化测试","CI/CD 管道"],"ja":["GitHub Actions ワークフロー","Docker Compose コンテナ オーケストレーション","コード品質チェック","自動テスト","CI/CD パイプライン"],"ko":["GitHub Actions 작업 흐름","Docker Compose 컨테이너 오케스트레이션","코드 품질 검사","자동 테스트","CI/CD 파이프라인"],"es":["Patrones de CI/CD con GitHub Actions","Orquestación de contenedores con Docker Compose y Kubernetes","Calidad del código con pre-commit hooks y CI enforcement","Cobertura de código ≥90%","Tolerancia cero warnings en linting"],"fr":["Modèles de CI/CD avec GitHub Actions","Orchestration de conteneurs avec Docker Compose et Kubernetes","Qualité du code avec des hooks pre-commit et une mise en œuvre de CI","Couverture de code ≥90%","Tolérance zéro avertissements en linting"],"de":["CI/CD-Muster mit GitHub Actions","Container-Orchestrierung mit Docker Compose und Kubernetes","Code-Qualität mit Pre-Commit-Hooks und CI-Enforcement","Code-Coverage ≥90%","Null-Toleranz für Warnungen im Linting"],"pt":["Padrões de CI/CD com GitHub Actions","Orquestração de contêineres com Docker Compose e Kubernetes","Portas de qualidade com hooks de pré-compilação e aplicação de CI","Cobertura de código ≥90%","Tolerância zero para warnings de linting"],"ru":["Шаблоны CI/CD с GitHub Actions","Оркестрация контейнеров с Docker Compose и Kubernetes","Качественные ворота с хуками предкомпиляции и применением CI","Покрытие кода ≥90%","Нулевая терпимость к предупреждениям linting"],"ar":["أنماط CI/CD مع GitHub Actions","أوركسترا الحاويات مع Docker Compose و Kubernetes","بوابات الجودة مع hooks ما قبل الترجمة وتنفيذ CI","التغطية الكودية ≥90%","التحمل صفر للتحذيرات من linting"]},"keywords":{"zh":["DevOps","CI/CD","EUCORA","GitHub Actions","Docker Compose","代码质量","自动化测试"],"ja":["DevOps","CI/CD","EUCORA","GitHub Actions","Docker Compose","コード品質","自動テスト"],"ko":["DevOps","CI/CD","EUCORA","GitHub Actions","Docker Compose","코드 품질","자동 테스트"],"es":["DevOps","CI/CD","orquestación de contenedores","EUCORA","GitHub Actions","Kubernetes","calidad del código","cobertura de código","linting"],"fr":["DevOps","CI/CD","orchestration de conteneurs","EUCORA","GitHub Actions","Kubernetes","qualité du code","couverture de code","linting"],"de":["DevOps","CI/CD","Container-Orchestrierung","EUCORA","GitHub Actions","Kubernetes","Code-Qualität","Code-Coverage","Linting"],"pt":["DevOps","CI/CD","EUCORA","GitHub Actions","Docker Compose","Kubernetes","orquestração de contêineres","padrões de engenharia de software"],"ru":["DevOps","CI/CD","EUCORA","GitHub Actions","Docker Compose","Kubernetes","оркестрация контейнеров","шаблоны разработки программного обеспечения"],"ar":["DevOps","CI/CD","EUCORA","GitHub Actions","Docker Compose","Kubernetes","أوركسترا الحاويات","نماذج هندسة البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"buildworksai","repo":"EUCORA","repoPath":"buildworksai/EUCORA","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.418Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"devops-cicd","description":"DevOps and CI/CD patterns for EUCORA including GitHub Actions workflows, Docker Compose orchestration, quality gates, and pre-commit hooks. Use when creating pipelines, configuring containers, or implementing quality enforcement.","bodyPreview":"# DevOps & CI/CD Patterns\n\nCI/CD and container orchestration patterns for the EUCORA platform.\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Technology | Pattern |\n|------------|---------|\n| CI/CD | GitHub Actions |\n| Containers | Docker Compose (dev), Kubernetes (prod) |\n| Quality Gates | Pre-commit hooks + CI enforcement |\n| Coverage | ≥90% enforced |\n| Linting | Zero warnings tolerance |\n\n---\n\n## GitHub Actions Workflows\n\n### Workflow Structure\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/code-quality.yml\nname: Code Quality","body":"# DevOps & CI/CD Patterns\n\nCI/CD and container orchestration patterns for the EUCORA platform.\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Technology | Pattern |\n|------------|---------|\n| CI/CD | GitHub Actions |\n| Containers | Docker Compose (dev), Kubernetes (prod) |\n| Quality Gates | Pre-commit hooks + CI enforcement |\n| Coverage | ≥90% enforced |\n| Linting | Zero warnings tolerance |\n\n---\n\n## GitHub Actions Workflows\n\n### Workflow Structure\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/code-quality.yml\nname: Code Quality\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main, develop]\n  pull_request:\n    branches: [main]\n\njobs:\n  backend-tests:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n\n    services:\n      postgres:\n        image: postgres:16\n        env:\n          POSTGRES_DB: test_db\n          POSTGRES_USER: test\n          POSTGRES_PASSWORD: test\n        ports:\n          - 5432:5432\n        options: >-\n          --health-cmd pg_isready\n          --health-interval 10s\n          --health-timeout 5s\n          --health-retries 5\n\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n      - name: Set up Python\n        uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n        with:\n          python-version: ''3.12''\n          cache: ''pip''\n\n      - name: Install dependencies\n        run: pip install -r requirements.txt\n\n      - name: Run tests with coverage\n        run: pytest --cov --cov-fail-under=90 --cov-report=xml\n        env:\n          DATABASE_URL: postgres://test:test@localhost:5432/test_db\n\n      - name: Upload coverage\n        uses: codecov/codecov-action@v4\n        with:\n          files: coverage.xml\n          fail_ci_if_error: true\n\n  frontend-tests:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n      - name: Set up Node\n        uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: ''20''\n          cache: ''npm''\n          cache-dependency-path: frontend/package-lock.json\n\n      - name: Install dependencies\n        run: npm ci\n        working-directory: frontend\n\n      - name: TypeScript check\n        run: npx tsc --noEmit\n        working-directory: frontend\n\n      - name: ESLint (zero warnings)\n        run: npm run lint -- --max-warnings 0\n        working-directory: frontend\n\n      - name: Run tests\n        run: npm test -- --coverage\n        working-directory: frontend\n```\n\n### Quality Gate Enforcement\n\n```yaml\n# Quality gate job - blocks merge if failed\nquality-gate:\n  runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n  needs: [backend-tests, frontend-tests, security-scan]\n\n  steps:\n    - name: Check all jobs passed\n      run: |\n        echo \"All quality gates passed ✅\"\n        echo \"- Backend tests: ${{ needs.backend-tests.result }}\"\n        echo \"- Frontend tests: ${{ needs.frontend-tests.result }}\"\n        echo \"- Security scan: ${{ needs.security-scan.result }}\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Docker Compose\n\n### Development Configuration\n\n```yaml\n# docker-compose.dev.yml\nversion: ''3.8''\n\nservices:\n  web:\n    build:\n      context: .\n      dockerfile: Dockerfile.dev\n    ports:\n      - \"8000:8000\"\n    volumes:\n      - ./backend:/app\n      - static_volume:/app/staticfiles\n    environment:\n      - DEBUG=True\n      - DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@db:5432/eucora\n      - REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379/0\n    depends_on:\n      db:\n        condition: service_healthy\n      redis:\n        condition: service_healthy\n    healthcheck:\n      test: [\"CMD\", \"curl\", \"-f\", \"http://localhost:8000/health/\"]\n      interval: 30s\n      timeout: 10s\n      retries: 3\n\n  db:\n    image: postgres:16\n    volumes:\n      - postgres_data:/var/lib/postgresql/data\n    environment:\n      POSTGRES_DB: eucora\n      POSTGRES_USER: user\n      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: pass\n    healthcheck:\n      test: [\"CMD-SHELL\", \"pg_isready -U user -d eucora\"]\n      interval: 10s\n      timeout: 5s\n      retries: 5\n\n  redis:\n    image: redis:7-alpine\n    healthcheck:\n      test: [\"CMD\", \"redis-cli\", \"ping\"]\n      interval: 10s\n      timeout: 5s\n      retries: 3\n\n  celery-worker:\n    build:\n      context: .\n      dockerfile: Dockerfile.dev\n    command: celery -A config worker -l info\n    volumes:\n      - ./backend:/app\n    environment:\n      - DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@db:5432/eucora\n      - REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379/0\n    depends_on:\n      - web\n      - redis\n\n  celery-beat:\n    build:\n      context: .\n      dockerfile: Dockerfile.dev\n    command: celery -A config beat -l info\n    volumes:\n      - ./backend:/app\n    depends_on:\n      - celery-worker\n    deploy:\n      replicas: 1  # Singleton pattern\n\nvolumes:\n  postgres_data:\n  static_volume:\n```\n\n### Production Configuration\n\n```yaml\n# docker-compose.prod.yml\nversion: ''3.8''\n\nservices:\n  web:\n    image: eucora/backend:${TAG:-latest}\n    deploy:\n      replicas: 3\n      resources:\n        limits:\n          cpus: ''1''\n          memory: 1G\n        reservations:\n          cpus: ''0.5''\n          memory: 512M\n      update_config:\n        parallelism: 1\n        delay: 10s\n        failure_action: rollback\n    healthcheck:\n      test: [\"CMD\", \"curl\", \"-f\", \"http://localhost:8000/health/\"]\n      interval: 30s\n      timeout: 10s\n      retries: 3\n      start_period: 40s\n```\n\n---\n\n## Pre-Commit Hooks\n\n### Configuration\n\n```yaml\n# .pre-commit-config.yaml\nrepos:\n  # Python\n  - repo: https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff-pre-commit\n    rev: v0.3.0\n    hooks:\n      - id: ruff\n        args: [--fix]\n      - id: ruff-format\n\n  - repo: https://github.com/pre-commit/mirrors-mypy\n    rev: v1.8.0\n    hooks:\n      - id: mypy\n        additional_dependencies: [types-all]\n\n  # JavaScript/TypeScript\n  - repo: https://github.com/pre-commit/mirrors-eslint\n    rev: v8.56.0\n    hooks:\n      - id: eslint\n        args: [--max-warnings, ''0'']\n        files: \\.[jt]sx?$\n\n  # Security\n  - repo: https://github.com/Yelp/detect-secrets\n    rev: v1.4.0\n    hooks:\n      - id: detect-secrets\n        args: [''--baseline'', ''.secrets.baseline'']\n\n  # General\n  - repo: https://github.com/pre-commit/pre-commit-hooks\n    rev: v4.5.0\n    hooks:\n      - id: trailing-whitespace\n      - id: end-of-file-fixer\n      - id: check-yaml\n      - id: check-json\n      - id: check-merge-conflict\n      - id: no-commit-to-branch\n        args: [--branch, main]\n```\n\n### Installation\n\n```bash\n# Install pre-commit\npip install pre-commit\n\n# Install hooks\npre-commit install\n\n# Run on all files\npre-commit run --all-files\n```\n\n---\n\n## Dockerfile Patterns\n\n### Multi-Stage Build\n\n```dockerfile\n# Dockerfile\n# Stage 1: Build\nFROM python:3.12-slim as builder\n\nWORKDIR /app\n\nCOPY requirements.txt .\nRUN pip wheel --no-cache-dir --no-deps --wheel-dir /wheels -r requirements.txt\n\n# Stage 2: Production\nFROM python:3.12-slim\n\nENV PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \\\n    PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1\n\nWORKDIR /app\n\n# Install system deps\nRUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \\\n    libpq5 \\\n    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*\n\n# Install Python deps\nCOPY --from=builder /wheels /wheels\nRUN pip install --no-cache /wheels/*\n\n# Copy app\nCOPY backend/ .\n\n# Create non-root user\nRUN adduser --disabled-password --gecos '''' appuser\nUSER appuser\n\nEXPOSE 8000\n\nCMD [\"gunicorn\", \"config.wsgi:application\", \"--bind\", \"0.0.0.0:8000\", \"--workers\", \"4\"]\n```\n\n### Development Dockerfile\n\n```dockerfile\n# Dockerfile.dev\nFROM python:3.12-slim\n\nENV PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \\\n    PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1\n\nWORKDIR /app\n\n# Install system deps\nRUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \\\n    libpq-dev gcc curl \\\n    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*\n\nCOPY requirements.txt requirements-dev.txt ./\nRUN pip install -r requirements-dev.txt\n\nEXPOSE 8000\n\nCMD [\"python\", \"manage.py\", \"runserver\", \"0.0.0.0:8000\"]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Quality Gates Checklist\n\n### CI Pipeline Must Enforce\n\n```\n☐ Backend tests pass (pytest)\n☐ Frontend tests pass (vitest)\n☐ Coverage ≥90% (pytest-cov, vitest --coverage)\n☐ TypeScript check passes (tsc --noEmit)\n☐ ESLint zero warnings (--max-warnings 0)\n☐ Python linting passes (ruff)\n☐ Security scan passes (trivy, detect-secrets)\n☐ SPDX compliance check passes\n```\n\n### Pre-Commit Must Block\n\n```\n☐ Trailing whitespace\n☐ Merge conflicts\n☐ Invalid YAML/JSON\n☐ Secrets in code\n☐ Direct commits to main\n☐ Type errors (mypy)\n☐ Linting errors (ruff, eslint)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Commands Reference\n\n```bash\n# Docker Compose\ndocker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml up -d\ndocker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml logs -f web\ndocker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml exec web python manage.py migrate\ndocker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml down -v\n\n# Pre-commit\npre-commit install\npre-commit run --all-files\npre-commit autoupdate\n\n# Testing with coverage\npytest --cov --cov-fail-under=90 --cov-report=html\nnpm test -- --coverage\n\n# Build and push\ndocker build -t eucora/backend:latest .\ndocker push eucora/backend:latest\n```\n\n---\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n| ❌ FORBIDDEN | ✅ CORRECT |\n|--------------|------------|\n| Skipping CI checks | All checks must pass |\n| Coverage < 90% | Enforce ≥90% in CI |\n| `--no-verify` commits | Pre-commit hooks mandatory |\n| Secrets in Dockerfile | Use build args or vault |\n| Root user in container | Create non-root user |\n| No health checks | Always define health checks |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:13:55.476Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents specializing in automation and deployment, such as AutoGPT and LangChain, seeking to streamline DevOps and CI/CD pipelines.","zh":"适用于专门从事自动化和部署的AI代理，例如AutoGPT和LangChain，旨在简化DevOps和CI/CD流水线。","ja":"自動化とデプロイを専門とするAIエージェント、たとえばAutoGPTとLangChainに適しています。DevOpsとCI/CDパイプラインを効率化することを目指しています。","ko":"자동화 및 배포에 특화된 AI 에이전트(AutoGPT 및 LangChain 등)에 적합합니다. DevOps 및 CI/CD 파이프라인을 간소화하려는 경우에 사용됩니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA que se especializan en automatización y despliegue, como AutoGPT y LangChain, que buscan optimizar las tuberías de DevOps y CI/CD.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA spécialisés dans l''automatisation et le déploiement, tels que AutoGPT et LangChain, qui cherchent à rationaliser les pipelines DevOps et CI/CD.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents, die auf Automatisierung und Bereitstellung spezialisiert sind, wie z.B. AutoGPT und LangChain, die DevOps- und CI/CD-Pipelines optimieren möchten.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA especializados em automação e implantação, como AutoGPT e LangChain, que buscam otimizar os pipelines de DevOps e CI/CD.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, специализирующихся на автоматизации и развертывании, таких как AutoGPT и LangChain, стремящихся оптимизировать конвейеры DevOps и CI/CD.","ar":"متوافق بشكل مثالي مع وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المتخصصين في الأتمتة والتشغيل، مثل AutoGPT و LangChain، الذين يسعون إلى简历 أنابيب DevOps و CI/CD."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to orchestrate containerized applications using Docker Compose and Kubernetes, enforcing quality gates through pre-commit hooks and CI enforcement, while maintaining zero warnings tolerance and ≥90% code coverage through GitHub Actions workflows.","zh":"赋予代理使用Docker Compose和Kubernetes编排容器化应用的能力，通过预提交钩子和CI强制执行执行质量门控，同时通过GitHub Actions工作流维持零警告容忍度和≥90%的代码覆盖率。","ja":"Docker ComposeとKubernetesを使用してコンテナ化されたアプリケーションをオーケストレーションする機能をエージェントに与え、事前コミットフックとCIによる強制実行を通じて品質ゲートを施行し、GitHub Actionsワークフローを通じてゼロ警告容認度と≥90%のコードカバレッジを維持します。","ko":"Docker Compose 및 Kubernetes를 사용하여 컨테이너화된 애플리케이션을 오케스트레이션할 수 있는 기능을 에이전트에 제공하며,事前 커밋 훅 및 CI 강제 실행을 통해 품질 게이트를 시행同时 GitHub Actions 워크플로우를 통해 0 警告 허용 및 ≥90% 코드 커버리지를 유지합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a orquestar aplicaciones contenerizadas utilizando Docker Compose y Kubernetes, aplicando puertas de calidad a través de ganchos pre-compromiso y cumplimiento de CI, manteniendo al mismo tiempo una tolerancia de cero advertencias y una cobertura de código ≥90% a través de flujos de trabajo de GitHub Actions.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''orchestrer des applications conteneurisées en utilisant Docker Compose et Kubernetes, en appliquant des portes de qualité via des crochets pré-engagement et un respect de la CI, tout en maintenant une tolérance zéro avertissements et une couverture de code ≥90% via des flux de travail GitHub Actions.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, containerisierte Anwendungen mithilfe von Docker Compose und Kubernetes zu orchestrieren, Qualitätstoren durch Vorcommit-Hooks und CI-Einhaltung durchzusetzen, während gleichzeitig eine Null-Warnung-Toleranz und eine Codeabdeckung von ≥90% durch GitHub-Actions-Workflows aufrechterhalten wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a orquestrar aplicações contenerizadas usando Docker Compose e Kubernetes, aplicando portais de qualidade por meio de ganchos pré-compromisso e execução de CI, mantendo tolerância zero de avisos e cobertura de código ≥90% por meio de fluxos de trabalho do GitHub Actions.","ru":"Позволяет агентам оркестрировать контейнеризированные приложения с помощью Docker Compose и Kubernetes, применяя ворота качества через хуки предкоммита и принудительное выполнение CI, сохраняя толерантность к нулевым предупреждениям и покрытие кода ≥90% посредством рабочих процессов GitHub Actions.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من أوركسترا التطبيقات المُحكمة باستخدام Docker Compose و Kubernetes، وتنفيذ بوابات الجودة من خلال Hooks ما قبل الالتزام وتنفيذ CI، مع الحفاظ على تسامح الصفر لتحذيرات وغطاء الرمز ≥90% من خلال سير عمل GitHub Actions."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating code quality checks with GitHub Actions","Deploying containerized applications to Kubernetes clusters","Enforcing consistent coding standards through pre-commit hooks and linting"],"zh":["使用GitHub Actions自动执行代码质量检查","将容器化应用程序部署到Kubernetes集群","通过预提交钩子和linting强制执行一致的编码标准"],"ja":["GitHub Actionsを使用してコード品質チェックを自動化する","コンテナ化されたアプリケーションをKubernetesクラスターにデプロイする","事前コミットフックとlintingを通じて一貫したコーディング規約を施行する"],"ko":["GitHub Actions를 사용하여 코드 품질 체크를 자동화하는 것","컨테이너화된 애플리케이션을 Kubernetes 클러스터에 배포하는 것","事前 커밋 훅 및 린팅을 통해 일관된 코딩 표준을 시행하는 것"],"es":["Automatizar controles de calidad de código con GitHub Actions","Implementar aplicaciones contenerizadas en clústeres de Kubernetes","Aplicar normas de codificación coherentes a través de ganchos pre-compromiso y linting"],"fr":["Automatiser les contrôles de qualité de code avec GitHub Actions","Déployer des applications conteneurisées sur des clusters Kubernetes","Appliquer des normes de codage cohérentes via des crochets pré-engagement et un linter"],"de":["Automatisieren von Codequalitätsprüfungen mit GitHub Actions","Bereitstellen containerisierter Anwendungen in Kubernetes-Clustern","Durchsetzen konsistenter Codierungsstandards durch Vorcommit-Hooks und Linting"],"pt":["Automatizar verificações de qualidade de código com GitHub Actions","Implantar aplicações contenerizadas em clusters Kubernetes","Aplicar padrões de codificação consistentes por meio de ganchos pré-compromisso e linting"],"ru":["Автоматизировать проверки качества кода с помощью GitHub Actions","Развертывать контейнеризированные приложения в кластерах Kubernetes","Применять последовательные стандарты кодирования через хуки предкоммита и линтинг"],"ar":["أتمتة فحص جودة الرمز مع GitHub Actions","نشر التطبيقات المُحكمة في مجاميع Kubernetes","تطبيق معايير الترميز الثابتة من خلال Hooks ما قبل الالتزام والتنميط"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires GitHub repository access","Limited to Docker Compose for development environments","Kubernetes required for production environments"],"zh":["需要GitHub仓库访问权限","仅限Docker Compose用于开发环境","生产环境需要Kubernetes"],"ja":["GitHubリポジトリへのアクセスが必要","開発環境ではDocker Composeのみに限定される","本稼働環境ではKubernetesが必要"],"ko":["GitHub 리포지토리 액세스가 필요함","개발 환경에서는 Docker Compose만 사용 가능","운영 환경에서는 Kubernetes가 필요"],"es":["Requiere acceso al repositorio de GitHub","Limitado a Docker Compose para entornos de desarrollo","Se requiere Kubernetes para entornos de producción"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au référentiel GitHub","Limité à Docker Compose pour les environnements de développement","Kubernetes est requis pour les environnements de production"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf das GitHub-Repository","Begrenzt auf Docker Compose für Entwicklungsumgebungen","Kubernetes wird für Produktionsumgebungen benötigt"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao repositório do GitHub","Limitado ao Docker Compose para ambientes de desenvolvimento","Kubernetes é necessário para ambientes de produção"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к репозиторию GitHub","Ограничен до Docker Compose для сред разработки","Kubernetes необходим для производственных сред"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى مستودع GitHub","محدود إلى Docker Compose لبيئات التطوير","يُطلب Kubernetes لبيئات الإنتاج"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('parasharcuraj/project-marlin/project-marlin', 'community', 'parasharcuraj', 'project-marlin', 'parasharcuraj/project-marlin', 'project-marlin', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.418Z', '2026-02-18T04:14:21.293Z', NULL, '{"id":"parasharcuraj/project-marlin/project-marlin","name":"project-marlin","description":{"zh":"Project Marlin 是一个评估 AI 生成的 Python 代码更改的项目，通过迭代评估和比较代码更改","ja":"Project Marlin は、AI 生成の Python コードの変更を評価するプロジェクトで、反復的な評価と比較を行う","ko":"Project Marlin은 AI 생성 Python 코드 변경을 평가하는 프로젝트로 코드 변경을 반복적으로 평가하고 비교한다","es":"Project Marlin es un proyecto que evalúa cambios de código Python generados por IA en repositorios de GitHub reales","fr":"Project Marlin est un projet qui évalue les modifications de code Python générées par l''IA sur des dépôts GitHub réels","de":"Project Marlin ist ein Projekt, das Änderungen von Python-Code generiert durch KI in realen GitHub-Repositorys bewertet","pt":"O Project Marlin é um projeto que avalia alterações de código Python geradas por IA em repositórios GitHub reais","ru":"Project Marlin — проект, оценивающий изменения кода Python, сгенерированные ИИ, в реальных репозиториях GitHub","ar":"مشروع مارلين هو مشروع يقيم التغييرات في код بايثون الذي يتم توليده بواسطة الذكاء الاصطناعي في مستودعات جيت هاب الحقيقية","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Project Marlin 工作流指南","ja":"Project Marlin ワークフロー ガイド","ko":"Project Marlin 워크플로우 가이드","es":"Guía de flujo de trabajo de Project Marlin","fr":"Guide de workflow de Project Marlin","de":"Project Marlin Workflow-Leitfaden","pt":"Guia de Fluxo de Trabalho do Project Marlin","ru":"Руководство по рабочему процессу Project Marlin","ar":"دليل تدفق عمل مشروع مارلين","en":"project-marlin"},"description":{"zh":"Project Marlin 是一个评估 AI 生成的 Python 代码更改的项目，通过迭代评估和比较代码更改","ja":"Project Marlin は、AI 生成の Python コードの変更を評価するプロジェクトで、反復的な評価と比較を行う","ko":"Project Marlin은 AI 생성 Python 코드 변경을 평가하는 프로젝트로 코드 변경을 반복적으로 평가하고 비교한다","es":"Project Marlin es un proyecto que evalúa cambios de código Python generados por IA en repositorios de GitHub reales","fr":"Project Marlin est un projet qui évalue les modifications de code Python générées par l''IA sur des dépôts GitHub réels","de":"Project Marlin ist ein Projekt, das Änderungen von Python-Code generiert durch KI in realen GitHub-Repositorys bewertet","pt":"O Project Marlin é um projeto que avalia alterações de código Python geradas por IA em repositórios GitHub reais","ru":"Project Marlin — проект, оценивающий изменения кода Python, сгенерированные ИИ, в реальных репозиториях GitHub","ar":"مشروع مارلين هو مشروع يقيم التغييرات في код بايثون الذي يتم توليده بواسطة الذكاء الاصطناعي في مستودعات جيت هاب الحقيقية","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["评估 AI 生成的 Python 代码更改","迭代评估和比较代码更改","评估和比较两种模型输出","需要至少 3 次迭代","需要自行评估和理由"],"ja":["AI 生成の Python コードの変更を評価","反復的な評価と比較","2 つのモデル出力を評価と比較","少なくとも 3 回の反復が必要","自ら評価と理由を付ける必要がある"],"ko":["AI 생성 Python 코드 변경 평가","반복적인 평가와 비교","두 가지 모델 출력 평가와 비교","최소 3회의 반복 필요","자신의 평가와 이유 필요"],"es":["Evaluación de cambios de código Python generados por IA","Revisión y comparación de dos salidas de modelo","Iteración a través de un mínimo de 3 turnos","Calificación y justificación de las respuestas","Uso de GitHub para evaluar cambios en repositorios reales"],"fr":["Évaluation des modifications de code Python générées par l''IA","Révision et comparaison de deux sorties de modèle","Itération à travers un minimum de 3 tours","Notation et justification des réponses","Utilisation de GitHub pour évaluer les modifications dans des dépôts réels"],"de":["Bewertung von Änderungen von Python-Code generiert durch KI","Überprüfung und Vergleich von zwei Modellausgaben","Iterierung über ein Minimum von 3 Runden","Bewertung und Rechtfertigung der Antworten","Verwendung von GitHub zur Bewertung von Änderungen in realen Repositorys"],"pt":["Avaliação de alterações de código Python geradas por IA","Comparação de dois modelos de saída","Iteração mínima de 3 turnos","Avaliação e justificativa das respostas","Uso de repositórios GitHub reais","Desenvolvimento de habilidades de avaliação de código"],"ru":["Оценка изменений кода Python, сгенерированных ИИ","Сравнение двух моделей вывода","Минимальная итерация 3 ходов","Оценка и обоснование ответов","Использование реальных репозиториев GitHub","Развитие навыков оценки кода"],"ar":["تقييم التغييرات في код بايثون الذي يتم توليده بواسطة الذكاء الاصطناعي","مقارنة بين نموذجين للخرج","تكرار حداقل 3 مرات","تقييم والتبرير للردود","استخدام مستودعات جيت هاب الحقيقية","تنمية مهارات تقييم الكود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Project Marlin","AI 代码评估","Python 代码更改","代码评估","AI 生成代码","代码比较"],"ja":["Project Marlin","AI コード評価","Python コードの変更","コード評価","AI 生成コード","コード比較"],"ko":["Project Marlin","AI 코드 평가","Python 코드 변경","코드 평가","AI 생성 코드","코드 비교"],"es":["Project Marlin","evaluación de código","código Python","IA","GitHub","desarrollo de software","ingeniería de software","evaluación de cambios"],"fr":["Project Marlin","évaluation de code","code Python","IA","GitHub","développement de logiciels","ingénierie de logiciels","évaluation de modifications"],"de":["Project Marlin","Code-Bewertung","Python-Code","KI","GitHub","Software-Entwicklung","Software-Ingenieurwesen","Änderungsbewertung"],"pt":["Project Marlin","Avaliação de código Python","IA","GitHub","Desenvolvimento de software","Avaliação de modelo","Iteração de modelo","Técnica de avaliação de código"],"ru":["Project Marlin","Оценка кода Python","ИИ","GitHub","Разработка программного обеспечения","Оценка модели","Итерация модели","Техника оценки кода"],"ar":["مشروع مارلين","تقييم код بايثون","الذكاء الاصطناعي","جيت هاب","تطوير البرمجيات","تقييم النموذج","تكرار النموذج","تقنية تقييم الكود"]}},"owner":"parasharcuraj","repo":"project-marlin","repoPath":"parasharcuraj/project-marlin","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.418Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"project-marlin","description":"Guide for Project Marlin workflow - evaluating AI-generated Python code changes on real repositories. Use when working on Marlin tasks including PR selection, prompt preparation, CLI execution with 3 turns, comparing Option A vs Option B outputs, rating and justifying responses.","bodyPreview":"# Project Marlin Workflow Guide\n\n## What Is Project Marlin?\n\nA project where you evaluate AI-generated Python code changes on real GitHub repositories. You:\n- Write prompts to guide the model\n- Review and compare two model outputs (Option A vs Option B)\n- Iterate across **minimum 3 turns** (required)\n- Rate and justify which response is better\n- All reasoning must be YOUR OWN (no external LLMs)\n\n## The 6-Step Workflow\n\n| Step | Purpose | Platform |\n|------|---------|----------|\n| 1. Assessment |","body":"# Project Marlin Workflow Guide\n\n## What Is Project Marlin?\n\nA project where you evaluate AI-generated Python code changes on real GitHub repositories. You:\n- Write prompts to guide the model\n- Review and compare two model outputs (Option A vs Option B)\n- Iterate across **minimum 3 turns** (required)\n- Rate and justify which response is better\n- All reasoning must be YOUR OWN (no external LLMs)\n\n## The 6-Step Workflow\n\n| Step | Purpose | Platform |\n|------|---------|----------|\n| 1. Assessment | Qualify to participate (one-time) | Marlin-Expert_Assessment-2 |\n| 2. PR Selection | Choose meaningful, non-trivial PR | Marlin-PR-Selection |\n| 3. Prompt Preparation | Plan work, write prompts for 3 turns | Marlin-Prompt-Prep |\n| 4. CLI Setup | Configure tools (one-time) | Provider Platform |\n| 5. PR Creation | Execute 3 turns, compare A vs B, rate & justify | CLI |\n| 6. Submission | Finalize and submit | Marlin-Prompt-Review V2 |\n\n**Steps must be completed sequentially. No skipping.**\n\n## Critical Rules (MUST FOLLOW)\n\n| Rule | Details |\n|------|---------|\n| **No external LLMs** | All reasoning, prompts, evaluations must be yours |\n| **No role-based prompting** | Never write \"You are a senior engineer...\" |\n| **No PR references** | Write prompts as if PR doesn''t exist yet |\n| **Minimum 3 turns** | Each must be intentional and justified |\n| **Never checkout PR branch** | Use pre-PR baseline state only (from approval email) |\n| **Match scope to PR** | Don''t over-scope - if PR has no tests, don''t add tests |\n| **No embedded code in prompts** | Describe behavior and outcomes, not code |\n| **DIFF before justifying** | Always compare A vs B before writing anything |\n\n## What You Must Prepare (Step 3)\n\n### 1. Repository and PR Context\n- What the repository does\n- What the PR is intended to change or fix\n- Why that change is necessary\n- Focus on **behavior and impact**, not implementation history\n\n### 2. Task Approach\n- **Current behavior**: How code works now\n- **Expected behavior**: How it should work after changes\n- **Files/functions/components** involved\n- **Dependencies or interactions** affected\n- **Edge cases** (concrete and verifiable, not hypothetical)\n- **Tests** to add/update and what they validate\n- **Acceptance criteria**: When is the task complete?\n\n### 3. Prompt Definition\n- Self-contained (understandable without additional context)\n- Clear, objective, structured instructions\n- No conversational language\n- No role-based prompting\n- **Describes what needs to be done, not how with code**\n\n### 4. Effort and Complexity\n- Why the PR is non-trivial\n- Number of files, logic complexity, component interactions\n- Edge cases requiring careful handling\n\n## Good Prompt Example\n\n```\nUpdate Gaphor''s property editor to clearly separate model-level and\ndiagram-level behavior for UML Dependency elements. Add a dedicated\nproperty page for Dependency model objects that shows Source and Target\nwhen selected from the model tree. Refactor the existing Dependency\ndiagram item editor into a separate item-specific page with updated\nidentifiers. Add support for the UML isFinalSpecialization attribute\non classifiers and expose it through a toggle in the classifier property\neditor using proper transaction handling. Update the GTK UI definitions\nwhere needed and add unit tests to verify both Dependency property\nvisibility and classifier specialization updates. The changes should\nfollow the UML specification and leave the code production ready.\n```\n\n**Why this works:**\n- Names exact components and behaviors\n- Outcomes you can actually verify\n- Reads like a real GitHub issue\n- Thinks about production (transaction handling, spec compliance)\n- Sounds like a person wrote it (domain-specific language)\n\n## Bad Prompt Example\n\n```\nYou are a senior software engineer. Please change dict[''key''] to\ndict.get(''key'') on line 45 of handler.py and also fix the PR issues.\n```\n\n**Why this fails:**\n- Role-based prompting (\"You are...\")\n- Embedded code (specific line changes)\n- References existing PR\n- Vague (\"fix the PR issues\")\n\n## Turn Structure\n\n### Each turn requires:\n1. **NEW prompt** (different work from previous turns)\n2. **Option A and Option B** outputs to compare\n3. **Rating** (A1-B1 scale)\n4. **Justification** with real code details (files, lines, behavior)\n\n### Turn Progression (divide PR scope into 3 parts):\n\n| Turn | Focus | Example |\n|------|-------|---------|\n| 1 | Core feature implementation | Create main class/function |\n| 2 | Supporting code OR tests | Add example script, helpers |\n| 3 | Integration OR edge cases | Update related components |\n\n### Before Each Turn''s Prompt:\n1. Review what previous turn accomplished\n2. Check what''s still missing from PR scope\n3. Write prompt for **ONLY the remaining work**\n\n**Iterations must be intentional and justified. Re-running prompts without clear reasoning is strongly discouraged.**\n\n## Rating Scale\n\n| Rating | Meaning | When to Use |\n|--------|---------|-------------|\n| **A1** | A clearly superior | B incorrect, useless, or no meaningful changes |\n| **A2** | A significantly better | B incorrect, incomplete, unsafe, or unnecessarily complex |\n| **A3** | A better overall | A follows instructions more accurately, more consistent |\n| **A4/B4** | Effectively equivalent | Minor differences (formatting, docs). Selection still required |\n| **B3** | B better overall | B follows instructions more accurately, more consistent |\n| **B2** | B significantly better | A incorrect, incomplete, unsafe, or unnecessarily complex |\n| **B1** | B clearly superior | A incorrect, useless, or no meaningful changes |\n\n## Rating Evaluation Criteria (8 Axes)\n\nWhen comparing Option A vs Option B, evaluate across these 8 axes:\n\n| Axis | What to Evaluate |\n|------|------------------|\n| **1. Overall Preference** | Which response better fulfills the prompt requirements |\n| **2. Logic and Correctness** | Code produces correct results, handles edge cases, no bugs |\n| **3. Naming and Clarity** | Variable/function names are descriptive and consistent |\n| **4. Organization and Modularity** | Code structure, separation of concerns, reusability |\n| **5. Interface Design** | API design, function signatures, parameter handling |\n| **6. Error Handling and Robustness** | Exception handling, input validation, failure modes |\n| **7. Comments and Documentation** | Docstrings, inline comments where needed, clarity |\n| **8. Review/Merge Readiness** | Production-ready, follows project conventions, complete |\n\n### Axis Rating Options\n\nFor each axis, select one:\n- **A is better** - Option A is superior on this axis\n- **B is better** - Option B is superior on this axis\n- **N/A** - Implementations are identical on this axis (only use when code is truly the same)\n\n### Required Justification Fields\n\n| Field | Purpose |\n|-------|---------|\n| **Model A Pros** | Specific strengths of Option A with code references |\n| **Model A Cons** | Specific weaknesses of Option A with code references |\n| **Model B Pros** | Specific strengths of Option B with code references |\n| **Model B Cons** | Specific weaknesses of Option B with code references |\n| **Overall Preference Justification** | Why you selected your overall rating (A1-B1) |\n\n### Evaluation Rules\n\n1. **DIFF first** - Always compare outputs before rating any axis\n2. **Cite real code** - Reference actual files, lines, variable names\n3. **No ties** - You must select A or B even if differences are minor\n4. **Consistency** - Axis ratings must support your overall selection\n5. **No fabrication** - Only cite differences that actually exist\n6. **Justification-Rating Alignment** - If you identify quality issues in written Pros/Cons, the relevant axes CANNOT be N/A. Your written justification and axis ratings must match.\n\n## Evaluation Process\n\n```\n1. Receive Option A and Option B\n              ↓\n2. DIFF them FIRST - are they identical or different?\n              ↓\n       ┌──────┴──────┐\n   IDENTICAL      DIFFERENT\n       ↓             ↓\n   Most axes      Rate each axis\n   = N/A          based on REAL\n   (see below)    differences only\n              ↓\n3. Ensure ratings SUPPORT your selection\n              ↓\n4. Write justification citing REAL code details\n```\n\n### If Outputs Are IDENTICAL:\n- Mark most/all axes as **N/A**\n- Only rate axes with actual differences (e.g., test names)\n- **NEVER invent differences that don''t exist**\n- Selection: A4/B4 (Effectively equivalent)\n\n## Justification Requirements\n\n**Pros/Cons MUST:**\n- Reference concrete details (files, logic, behavior)\n- Clearly support your rating\n- Explain strengths AND weaknesses of BOTH responses\n- Be as thorough as possible\n\n**AVOID:**\n- Subjective statements (\"looks cleaner\", \"seems better\")\n- Generic statements without specific evidence\n- Citing issues that don''t actually exist in the code\n\n**Tip:** If ratings differ across axes, add 1-2 sentence justification for each outlier (e.g., \"Correct but poor modularity due to duplicated parsing logic.\")\n\n## Common Mistakes (Cause Rejection)\n\n| Mistake | Result |\n|---------|--------|\n| Embedded code in prompts | Unclear scope, rejection |\n| Repeating work across turns | No code changes, rejection |\n| Citing non-existent differences | Immediate rejection |\n| Rating identical code differently | Rejection |\n| Ratings contradict selection/tradeoffs | Required fixes, rejection |\n| **Written issues but all axes N/A** | Inconsistency between justification and ratings, rejection |\n| Over-scoped plans | Required rewrite, rejection |\n| **Prompt cohesion issues** | Turns don''t logically connect or build on each other, rejection |\n| Vague justifications | Required rewrites, rejection |\n| Describing PR instead of instructing | Rejection |\n| Fabricated analysis | Immediate rejection |\n| Ignoring blocking issues | Weakened reasoning, rejection |\n| No reviewable code (binary/errors) | Rejection |\n| Output doesn''t follow instructions | Rejection |\n| Not addressing reviewer feedback | Rejection |\n| LLM-generated content indicators | Rejection |\n\nSee [references/mistakes.md](references/mistakes.md) for detailed examples (13 documented mistakes).\n\n## Pre-Submission Checklist\n\n**Before EACH turn:**\n- [ ] Does this turn request NEW work (not done in previous turns)?\n- [ ] Did I DIFF Option A and Option B before writing justifications?\n- [ ] Does every cited difference ACTUALLY EXIST in the code?\n- [ ] If code is identical, are most axes marked N/A?\n- [ ] Do my axis ratings SUPPORT my overall selection?\n- [ ] Do my ratings MATCH my stated tradeoffs?\n- [ ] If I wrote Pros/Cons identifying issues, are relevant axes rated (not N/A)?\n- [ ] Is there actual code to review (not binary files/errors)?\n- [ ] Does the output actually follow the prompt instructions?\n- [ ] Did I acknowledge any blocking issues in both outputs?\n- [ ] Is my analysis based on REAL code, not fabricated claims?\n\n**Before final submission:**\n- [ ] Does my plan scope match the actual PR scope?\n- [ ] Are all 3 turns complete with proper evaluations?\n- [ ] Is my prompt an INSTRUCTION (not a description of PR)?\n- [ ] No embedded code in prompts?\n- [ ] No role-based prompting?\n- [ ] No PR references in prompts?\n- [ ] No LLM-generated content indicators?\n- [ ] Did I address ALL reviewer feedback?\n- [ ] Final line-by-line review of all modified files?\n\n## Key Definitions\n\n| Term | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| **EC** | Expert Contributor (you) |\n| **Turn** | One execution cycle: prompt → review outputs → decide |\n| **Option A/B** | Two model outputs to compare per turn |\n| **Baseline Repository** | Pre-PR codebase state |\n| **Blocking Issue** | Problem making result unacceptable |\n| **N/A** | Rating when implementations are identical on that axis |\n\n## Writing Style (Pass AI Detection)\n\nUse clear, simple language. Short sentences. Active voice.\n\nBanned: em dashes, \"delve\", \"craft\", \"utilize\", \"groundbreaking\", \"pivotal\", \"however\", \"furthermore\", \"in conclusion\"\n\nGood: \"Response A adds null checks in handler.py at line 45.\"\nBad: \"Response A crafts an elegant solution that delves into error handling.\"\n\nSee [Writing Style Guide](references/writing-style.md) for full list.\n\n## Additional References\n\n- [Detailed Workflow](references/workflow.md)\n- [Complete Evaluation Guide](references/evaluation.md)\n- [Common Mistakes & Rejection Feedback](references/mistakes.md)\n- [Prompt Writing Guide](references/prompts.md)\n- [Writing Style Guide](references/writing-style.md)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T04:14:21.293Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing advanced Python code analysis and comparison capabilities on real GitHub repositories.","zh":"非常适合需要高级Python代码分析和比较能力的代码审查代理，特别是在真实的GitHub仓库中。","ja":"GitHubリポジトリで高度なPythonコード分析および比較機能を必要とするコードレビューエージェントに最適です。","ko":"진짜 GitHub 저장소에서 고급 Python 코드 분석 및 비교 기능이 필요한 코드 리뷰 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de revisión de código que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de análisis y comparación de código Python en repositorios de GitHub reales.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de révision de code nécessitant des capacités avancées d''analyse et de comparaison de code Python sur des dépôts GitHub réels.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agents, die erweiterte Python-Code-Analyse- und Vergleichsfunktionen in realen GitHub-Repositorys benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de análise e comparação de código Python em repositórios reais do GitHub.","ru":"Идеально подходит для Агентов проверки кода, которым требуются расширенные возможности анализа и сравнения кода Python на реальных репозиториях GitHub.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء مراجعة التعليمات البرمجية الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة لتحليل ومقارنة كود بايثون على مستودعات جيت هاب الحقيقية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to evaluate AI-generated Python code changes, iterate across multiple turns, and rate model outputs using GitHub repositories and Python code comparison protocols, while ensuring all reasoning is based on their own internal logic without relying on external LLMs.","zh":"赋予代理评估AI生成的Python代码更改、跨多个回合迭代并使用GitHub仓库和Python代码比较协议对模型输出进行评分的能力，同时确保所有推理都基于其自身的内部逻辑，而不依赖外部LLM。","ja":"エージェントがGitHubリポジトリとPythonコード比較プロトコルを使用してAI生成のPythonコードの変更を評価し、複数のターンにわたって反復処理し、モデル出力を評価する能力を与えます。また、すべての推論は内部ロジックに基づいており、外部LLMに依存しません。","ko":"에이전트가 GitHub 저장소와 Python 코드 비교 프로토콜을 사용하여 AI 생성 Python 코드 변경을 평가하고 여러 번의 반복을 통해 모델 출력을 평가할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다. 또한 모든 추론은 내부 논리에 기반하여 외부 LLM에 의존하지 않습니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a evaluar cambios de código Python generados por IA, iterar a lo largo de múltiples turnos y calificar las salidas del modelo utilizando protocolos de comparación de código Python y repositorios de GitHub, garantizando que toda la lógica de razonamiento se base en su propia lógica interna sin depender de LLM externos.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''évaluer les modifications de code Python générées par l''IA, d''itérer sur plusieurs tours et de noter les sorties du modèle en utilisant des protocoles de comparaison de code Python et des dépôts GitHub, en garantissant que toute la logique de raisonnement est basée sur leur propre logique interne sans s''appuyer sur des LLM externes.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Änderungen am Python-Code, der von KI generiert wurde, zu bewerten, über mehrere Runden zu iterieren und die Modellausgaben unter Verwendung von Python-Code-Vergleichsprotokollen und GitHub-Repositorys zu bewerten, während sichergestellt wird, dass die gesamte Argumentationslogik auf ihrer eigenen internen Logik basiert, ohne auf externe LLMs zurückzugreifen.","pt":"Capacita os agentes a avaliar alterações de código Python geradas por IA, iterar em múltiplos turnos e classificar as saídas do modelo usando repositórios do GitHub e protocolos de comparação de código Python, garantindo que todo o raciocínio seja baseado em sua própria lógica interna sem depender de LLMs externos.","ru":"Позволяет агентам оценивать изменения в коде Python, сгенерированные ИИ, выполнять итерации в несколько ходов и оценивать выходные данные модели с использованием репозиториев GitHub и протоколов сравнения кода Python, обеспечивая при этом, что все рассуждения основаны на их собственной внутренней логике без reliance на внешние LLM.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من تقييم تغييرات كود بايثون المُنشأة بواسطة الذكاء الاصطناعي، والتكرار عبر عدة أدوار، وتقييم مخرجات النماذج باستخدام مستودعات جيت هاب وبروتوكولات مقارنة كود بايثون، مع ضمان أن يكون كل التفكير قائمًا على منطقهم الداخلي الخاص دون الاعتماد على نماذج اللغة الكبيرة (LLMs) الخارجية."},"useCases":{"en":["Evaluating AI-generated Python code changes on GitHub repositories","Comparing model outputs for code improvement","Iterating across multiple turns for refined code review"],"zh":["在GitHub仓库中评估AI生成的Python代码更改","比较模型输出以改进代码","跨多个回合迭代以完善代码审查"],"ja":["GitHubリポジトリでAI生成のPythonコードの変更を評価する","コード改善のためのモデル出力の比較","コードレビューのための複数のターンにわたる反復"],"ko":["GitHub 저장소에서 AI 생성 Python 코드 변경을 평가하는 것","코드 개선을 위한 모델 출력 비교","코드 리뷰를 위한 여러 번의 반복"],"es":["Evaluación de cambios de código Python generados por IA en repositorios de GitHub","Comparación de salidas de modelo para la mejora del código","Iteración a lo largo de múltiples turnos para una revisión de código refinada"],"fr":["Évaluation des modifications de code Python générées par l''IA sur des dépôts GitHub","Comparaison des sorties de modèle pour l''amélioration du code","Itération sur plusieurs tours pour une révision de code raffinée"],"de":["Bewertung von Änderungen am Python-Code, der von KI in GitHub-Repositorys generiert wurde","Vergleich von Modellausgaben zur Verbesserung des Codes","Iteration über mehrere Runden für eine verfeinerte Code-Überprüfung"],"pt":["Avaliação de alterações de código Python geradas por IA em repositórios do GitHub","Comparação de saídas de modelo para melhoria de código","Iteração em múltiplos turnos para uma revisão de código refinada"],"ru":["Оценка сгенерированных ИИ изменений кода Python в репозиториях GitHub","Сравнение выходных данных модели для улучшения кода","Итерация в несколько ходов для уточненного обзора кода"],"ar":["تقييم تغييرات كود بايثون المُنشأة بواسطة الذكاء الاصطناعي على مستودعات جيت هاب","مقارنة مخرجات النماذج لتحسين التعليمات البرمجية","التكرار عبر عدة أدوار لمراجعة تعليمات برمجية مُحسنة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires minimum 3 turns for iteration","Limited to Python code analysis","No external LLMs allowed for reasoning"],"zh":["需要至少3个回合来迭代","仅限Python代码分析","不允许使用外部LLM进行推理"],"ja":["反復処理には少なくとも3つのターンが必要","Pythonコード分析のみ","推論に外部LLMを使用することは許可されません"],"ko":["반복에는 최소 3개의 턴이 필요합니다","Python 코드 분석만 가능합니다","추론에 외부 LLM을 사용하는 것은 허용되지 않습니다"],"es":["Requiere un mínimo de 3 turnos para la iteración","Limitado al análisis de código Python","No se permiten LLM externos para el razonamiento"],"fr":["Nécessite un minimum de 3 tours pour l''itération","Limité à l''analyse de code Python","Aucun LLM externe n''est autorisé pour le raisonnement"],"de":["Erfordert mindestens 3 Runden für die Iteration","Beschränkt auf die Analyse von Python-Code","Keine externen LLMs für die Argumentation erlaubt"],"pt":["Requer no mínimo 3 turnos para iteração","Limitado à análise de código Python","Não é permitido o uso de LLMs externos para raciocínio"],"ru":["Требуется минимум 3 хода для итерации","Ограничено анализом кода Python","Запрещено использование внешних LLM для рассуждений"],"ar":["يتطلب 3 أدوار كحد أدنى للتكرار","مقتصر على تحليل كود بايثون","غير مسموح باستخدام نماذج اللغة الكبيرة (LLMs) الخارجية للتفكير"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('agentset-ai/agentset/baseline-ui', 'community', 'agentset-ai', 'agentset', 'agentset-ai/agentset', 'baseline-ui', 0, 0, 35, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.418Z', '2026-02-18T04:14:37.012Z', NULL, '{"id":"agentset-ai/agentset/baseline-ui","name":"baseline-ui","description":{"zh":"Baseline UI 是一个开源平台，提供标准化 UI 基线，确保一致的设计风格和开发效率","ja":"Baseline UI はオープンソースのプラットフォームであり、標準化 UI ベースラインを提供し、一貫したデザインスタイルと開発効率を保証する","ko":"Baseline UI는 오픈소스 플랫폼으로 표준화 UI 베이스라인을 제공하여 일관된 디자인 스타일과 개발 효율성을 보장한다","es":"Baseline UI es una herramienta de código abierto que establece un estándar de interfaz de usuario para prevenir la degradación de la interfaz generada por IA. Utiliza Tailwind CSS y otras tecnologías para garantizar la consistencia y calidad de las interfaces de usuario.","fr":"Baseline UI est un outil open-source qui établit un standard d''interface utilisateur pour prévenir la dégradation de l''interface générée par l''IA. Il utilise Tailwind CSS et d''autres technologies pour assurer la cohérence et la qualité des interfaces utilisateur.","de":"Baseline UI ist ein Open-Source-Tool, das einen Benutzeroberflächen-Standard für die Vermeidung von IA-generierten Benutzeroberflächen-Abfällen festlegt. Es verwendet Tailwind CSS und andere Technologien, um die Konsistenz und Qualität von Benutzeroberflächen zu gewährleisten.","pt":"Baseline UI é uma ferramenta que impõe um padrão de interface para prevenir problemas de consistência em interfaces geradas por AI. Ela oferece uma forma de garantir que o código seja consistente e fácil de manter","ru":"Baseline UI — это инструмент, который накладывает стандартный интерфейс для предотвращения проблем согласованности в интерфейсах, сгенерированных ИИ. Он предоставляет способ гарантировать, что код будет согласованным и легким в обслуживании","ar":"Baseline UI هي أداة تفرض معياراً لواجهة المستخدم لمنع مشاكل في الاتساق في واجهات المستخدم التي تم إنشاؤها بواسطة الذكاء الاصطناعي. إنها توفر وسيلة لضمان أن يكون الكود متسقًا وسهل الصيانة","en":"The open-source RAG platform: built-in citations, deep research, 22+ file formats, partitions, MCP server, and more."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Baseline UI - 标准化 UI 基线","ja":"Baseline UI - 標準化 UI ベースライン","ko":"Baseline UI - 표준화 UI 베이스라인","es":"Baseline UI: Estándar de interfaz de usuario para desarro...","fr":"Baseline UI: Standard d''interface utilisateur pour les dé...","de":"Baseline UI: Benutzeroberflächen-Standard für Entwickler","pt":"Baseline UI: Padronização de Interface para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Baseline UI: Стандартизация Интерфейса для Разработчиков","ar":"Baseline UI: معايير واجهة المستخدم لل مطورين","en":"baseline-ui"},"description":{"zh":"Baseline UI 是一个开源平台，提供标准化 UI 基线，确保一致的设计风格和开发效率","ja":"Baseline UI はオープンソースのプラットフォームであり、標準化 UI ベースラインを提供し、一貫したデザインスタイルと開発効率を保証する","ko":"Baseline UI는 오픈소스 플랫폼으로 표준화 UI 베이스라인을 제공하여 일관된 디자인 스타일과 개발 효율성을 보장한다","es":"Baseline UI es una herramienta de código abierto que establece un estándar de interfaz de usuario para prevenir la degradación de la interfaz generada por IA...","fr":"Baseline UI est un outil open-source qui établit un standard d''interface utilisateur pour prévenir la dégradation de l''interface générée par l''IA. Il utilise...","de":"Baseline UI ist ein Open-Source-Tool, das einen Benutzeroberflächen-Standard für die Vermeidung von IA-generierten Benutzeroberflächen-Abfällen festlegt. Es ...","pt":"Baseline UI é uma ferramenta que impõe um padrão de interface para prevenir problemas de consistência em interfaces geradas por AI. Ela oferece uma forma de ...","ru":"Baseline UI — это инструмент, который накладывает стандартный интерфейс для предотвращения проблем согласованности в интерфейсах, сгенерированных ИИ. Он пред...","ar":"Baseline UI هي أداة تفرض معياراً لواجهة المستخدم لمنع مشاكل في الاتساق في واجهات المستخدم التي تم إنشاؤها بواسطة الذكاء الاصطناعي. إنها توفر